helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0108.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0108.xhp\" name=\"Help\"\>Help\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0108.xhp	0	help	par_id3153990				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:HelpMenu\"\>The Help menu allows you to start and control the $[officename] Help system.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0108.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399				0	en-ZA	$[officename] Help				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0108.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:HelpIndex\"\>Opens the main page of the $[officename] Help for the current application.\</ahelp\> You can scroll through the Help pages and you can search for index terms or any text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0108.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064A				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id1619006\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_helpindex.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1619006\"\>icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0108.xhp	0	help	par_idN10667				0	en-ZA	%PRODUCTNAME Help				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0108.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154898				0	en-ZA	Support				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0108.xhp	0	help	par_id3157909				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:HelpSupport\"\>Shows information on how to get support.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0108.xhp	0	help	hd_id2926419				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/online_update.xhp\"\>Check for Updates\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0108.xhp	0	help	par_id2783898				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enable an Internet connection for %PRODUCTNAME. If you need a Proxy, check the %PRODUCTNAME Proxy settings in \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Internet. Then choose Check for Updates to check for the availability of a newer version of your office suite.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0108.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A6				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>This menu command is visible for the evaluation version of %PRODUCTNAME. Choose to open the Purchase %PRODUCTNAME Wizard.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0108.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153881				0	en-ZA	About $[officename]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0108.xhp	0	help	par_id3144510				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:About\"\>Displays general program information such as version number and copyrights.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0209.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Hyperlink Bar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0209.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154094				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0209.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink Bar\"\>Hyperlink Bar\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0209.xhp	0	help	par_id3159201				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OFA_HYPERLINK_DLG\"\>Use the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\> Bar to create and edit the hyperlinks in your documents, and to enter criteria for searches using the available Internet search engines.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0209.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136				0	en-ZA	You can open and close the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\> Bar in \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Java Platform Support				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153089				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0650.xhp\" name=\"Java Platform Support\"\>Java Platform Support\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3152363				0	en-ZA	$[officename] supports the Java platform for running applications and components based on the JavaBeans architecture.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	en-ZA	For $[officename] to support the Java platform, you must install the Java 2 Runtime Environment software. When you installed $[officename], you automatically received the option to install these files if they were not yet installed. You can also install these files now if required.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	en-ZA	The Java platform support needs to be activated under $[officename] to run Java applications.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	en-ZA	Activate Java platform support by choosing \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/java.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - Java\"\>$[officename] - Java\</link\>\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id9116183				0	en-ZA	Before you can use a JDBC driver, you need to add its class path. Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME- Java, and click the Class Path button. After you add the path information, restart %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3153822				0	en-ZA	Your modifications at the \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - Java\</emph\> tab page will be used even if the Java Virtual Machine (JVM, a virtual machine for the Java platform) already has been started. After modifications to the ClassPath you must restart $[officename]. The same is true for modifications under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Internet - Proxy\</emph\>. Only the two boxes "Http Proxy" and "Ftp Proxy" and their ports don't require a restart, they will be evaluated when you click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Glossaries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
