helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	hd_id0810200911433792				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/schart/main0202.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Bar\"\>Formatting Bar\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200911433835				0	en-ZA	The Formatting Bar is shown when a chart is set to edit mode. Double-click a chart to enter edit mode. Click outside the chart to leave edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200911433878				0	en-ZA	You can edit the formatting of a chart using the controls and icons on the Formatting Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	hd_id0810200902300436				0	en-ZA	Select Chart Element				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200902300479				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select the element from the chart that you want to format. The element gets selected in the chart preview. Click Format Selection to open the properties dialogue for the selected element.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	hd_id0810200902300555				0	en-ZA	Format Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200902300539				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the properties dialogue for the selected element.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	hd_id0810200902300545				0	en-ZA	Chart Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200902300594				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the Chart Type dialogue.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	hd_id0810200902300537				0	en-ZA	Chart Data Table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200902300699				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the Data Table dialogue where you can edit the chart data.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	hd_id0810200902300672				0	en-ZA	Horizontal Grid On/Off				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200902300630				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The Horizontal Grid On/Off icon on the Formatting bar toggles the visibility of the grid display for the Y axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	hd_id0810200902300738				0	en-ZA	Legend On/Off				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	par_id081020090230076				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>To show or hide a legend, click Legend On/Off on the Formatting bar.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	hd_id0810200902300785				0	en-ZA	Scale Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200902300784				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Rescales the text in the chart when you change the size of the chart.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	hd_id081020090230087				0	en-ZA	Automatic Layout				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200902300834				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Moves all chart elements to their default positions inside the current chart. This function does not alter the chart type or any other attributes other than the position of elements.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Charts in $[officename]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148664				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>charts; overview\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>HowTos for charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148664				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"chart_main\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/main0000.xhp\" name=\"Charts in $[officename]\"\>Using Charts in %PRODUCTNAME\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685	2			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"chart\"\>$[officename] lets you present data graphically in a chart, so that you can visually compare data series and view trends in the data. You can insert charts into spreadsheets, text documents, drawings, and presentations. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153143				0	en-ZA	Chart Data				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id5181432				0	en-ZA	Charts can be based on the following data:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id7787102				0	en-ZA	Spreadsheet values from Calc cell ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id7929929				0	en-ZA	Cell values from a Writer table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id4727011				0	en-ZA	Values that you enter in the Chart Data Table dialogue (you can create these charts in Writer, Draw, or Impress, and you can copy and paste them also to Calc)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id76601				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Creates a chart in the current document. To use a continuous range of cells as the data source for your chart, click inside the cell range, and then choose this command. Alternatively, select some cells and choose this command to create a chart of the selected cells.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	hd_id5345011				0	en-ZA	To insert a chart				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	hd_id5631580				0	en-ZA	To edit a chart				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id7911008				0	en-ZA	Click a chart to edit the object properties:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id9844660				0	en-ZA	Size and position on the current page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id8039796				0	en-ZA	Alignment, text wrap, outer borders, and more.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id7986693				0	en-ZA	Double-click a chart to enter the chart edit mode:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id2350840				0	en-ZA	Chart data values (for charts with own data).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id3776055				0	en-ZA	Chart type, axes, titles, walls, grid, and more.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id8442335				0	en-ZA	Double-click a chart element in chart edit mode:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id4194769				0	en-ZA	Double-click an axis to edit the scale, type, colour, and more.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id8644672				0	en-ZA	Double-click a data point to select and edit the data series to which the data point belongs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id6574907				0	en-ZA	With a data series selected, click, then double-click a single data point to edit the properties of this data point (for example, a single bar in a bar chart).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id1019200902360575				0	en-ZA	Double-click the legend to select and edit the legend. Click, then double-click a symbol in the selected legend to edit the associated data series.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id7528916				0	en-ZA	Double-click any other chart element, or click the element and open the Format menu, to edit the properties.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id8420667				0	en-ZA	Click outside the chart to leave the current edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id4923856				0	en-ZA	To print a chart in high quality, you can export the chart to a PDF file and print that file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200912061033				0	en-ZA	In chart edit mode, you see the \<link href=\"text/schart/main0202.xhp\"\>Formatting Bar\</link\> for charts near the upper border of the document. The Drawing Bar for charts appears near the lower border of the document. The Drawing Bar shows a subset of the icons from the \<link href=\"text/simpress/main0210.xhp\"\>Drawing\</link\> toolbar of Draw and Impress.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200902080452				0	en-ZA	You can right-click an element of a chart to open the context menu. The context menu offers many commands to format the selected element.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id081020090354489				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Formats the selected title.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
