helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017	2			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:OnlineAutoFormat\"\>Automatically formats the document while you type. To set the formatting options, choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>\<emph\> Options\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Options \</emph\>tab.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	en-ZA	You can use AutoCorrect to format text documents and plain ASCII text files, but not characters that you have manually formatted. Automatic \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040100.xhp\" name=\"word completion\"\>word completion\</link\> only occurs after you type a word for the second time in a document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
