helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147340				0	en-ZA	Open Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148999				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NAVIGATOR_LISTBOX\"\>Lists the names of all open text documents. To view the contents of a document in the Navigator window, select the name of the document in the list. The current document displayed in the Navigator is indicated by the word "active" after its name in the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149025				0	en-ZA	You can also right-click an item in the Navigator, choose \<emph\>Display\</emph\>, and then click the document that you want to view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Insert Bookmark				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	bm_id4974211				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>bookmarks;inserting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147506				0	en-ZA	Insert Bookmark				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149806	2			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"textmarkeein\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertBookmark\"\>Inserts a bookmark at the cursor position. You can then use the Navigator to quickly jump to the marked location at a later time.\</ahelp\> In an HTML document, bookmarks are converted to anchors that you can jump to from a hyperlink. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153677	3			0	en-ZA	To jump to a specific bookmark, press F5 to open the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\>, click the plus sign (+) next to the\<emph\> Bookmark\</emph\> entry, and then double-click the bookmark.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151308				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>You can also right-click the \<emph\>Page Number\</emph\> field at the left end of the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\> at the bottom of the document window, and then choose the bookmark that you want to jump to.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154188				0	en-ZA	Bookmarks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:COMBOBOX:DLG_INSERT_BOOKMARK:CB_BOOKMARK\"\>Type the name of the bookmark that you want to create. The lower list contains all of the bookmarks in the current document. To delete a bookmark, select it in the list, and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149483				0	en-ZA	You cannot use the following characters in a bookmark name: / \\ @ : * ? " ; , . #				2002-02-02 02:02:02
