helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04220000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Header				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04220000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146320				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04220000.xhp\" name=\"Header\"\>Header\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04220000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145827				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertPageHeader\"\>Adds or removes a header from the page style that you select in the submenu. The header is added to all of the pages that use the same page style.\</ahelp\> In a new document, only the "Default" page style is listed. Other page styles are added to the list after you apply them in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04220000.xhp	0	help	par_id2326425				0	en-ZA	The headers are visible only when you view the document in print layout (enable \<emph\>View - Print Layout\</emph\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04220000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150570				0	en-ZA	A tick mark is displayed in front of the page styles that have headers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04220000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153921				0	en-ZA	To remove a header, choose \<emph\>Insert - Header\</emph\>, and then select the page style containing the header. The header is removed from all of the pages that use this page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04220000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150761				0	en-ZA	To add or remove headers from all of the page styles that are in use in the document, choose \<emph\>Insert - Header - All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04220000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	en-ZA	To format a header, choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05040300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Page - Header\"\>\<emph\>Format - Page - Header\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Nonprinting Characters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154507				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"Nonprinting Characters\"\>Nonprinting Characters\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154646				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ControlCodes\"\>Shows nonprinting characters in your text, such as paragraph marks, line breaks, tab stops, and spaces.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145410				0	en-ZA	When you delete a paragraph mark, the paragraph that is merged takes on the formatting of the paragraph that the cursor is in.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147511				0	en-ZA	To specify which nonprinting characters are displayed, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040600.xhp\" name=\"Writer - Formatting Aids\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</link\>\</emph\>, and then select the options that you want in the \<emph\>Display of\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03140000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Hidden Paragraphs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155959				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03140000.xhp\" name=\"Hidden Paragraphs\"\>Hidden Paragraphs\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150251				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowHiddenParagraphs\"\>Shows or hides hidden paragraphs.\</ahelp\> This option only affects the screen display of hidden paragraphs, and not the printing of hidden paragraphs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3157875				0	en-ZA	To enable this feature, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040600.xhp\" name=\"Writer - Formatting Aids\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</link\>\</emph\>, and ensure that the \<emph\>Hidden paragraphs\</emph\> check box in the \<emph\>Display of\</emph\> area is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154501				0	en-ZA	Use the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"field command\"\>field command\</link\> "Hidden Paragraph" to assign a \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"condition\"\>condition\</link\> that must be met to hide a paragraph. If the condition is not met, the paragraph is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3083451				0	en-ZA	When you hide a paragraph, footnotes and frames that are anchored to characters in the paragraph are also hidden.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154643				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"tabelletext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:TableDialog\"\>Specifies the properties of the selected table, for example, name, alignment, spacing, column width, borders, and background.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
