helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mm_seladdblo.xhp	0	help	par_idN10559				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Excludes country or regional information from the address block.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mm_seladdblo.xhp	0	help	par_idN1055C				0	en-ZA	Always include country/region				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mm_seladdblo.xhp	0	help	par_idN10560				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Includes country or regional information in the address block.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mm_seladdblo.xhp	0	help	par_idN10563				0	en-ZA	Only include country/region if it is not:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mm_seladdblo.xhp	0	help	par_idN10567				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Only includes country or regional information in the address block if the value differs from the value that you enter in the text box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mm_seladdblo.xhp	0	help	par_idN10651				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the country/region string that shall not be printed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mm_seladdblo.xhp	0	help	par_idN1056A				0	en-ZA	New				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mm_seladdblo.xhp	0	help	par_idN1056E				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/mm_newaddblo.xhp\"\>New Address Block\</link\> dialogue where you can define a new address block layout.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mm_seladdblo.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057F				0	en-ZA	Edit				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mm_seladdblo.xhp	0	help	par_idN10583				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/mm_newaddblo.xhp\"\>New Address Block\</link\> dialogue where you can edit the selected address block layout.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mm_seladdblo.xhp	0	help	par_idN10594				0	en-ZA	Delete				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mm_seladdblo.xhp	0	help	par_idN10598				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Deletes the selected address block layout.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Insert Manual Break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145827				0	en-ZA	Insert Manual Break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147176				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"umbruch\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertBreak\"\>Inserts a manual line break, column break or a page break at the current cursor position.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151176				0	en-ZA	Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420				0	en-ZA	Select the type of break that you want to insert.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154097				0	en-ZA	Line Break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149805				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_BREAK:RB_LINE\"\>Ends the current line, and moves the text found to the right of the cursor to the next line, without creating a new paragraph.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149685				0	en-ZA	You can also insert a line break by pressing Shift+Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148566				0	en-ZA	Column Break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155182				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_BREAK:RB_COL\"\>Inserts a manual column break (in a multiple column layout), and moves the text found to the right of the cursor to the beginning of the next \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05040500.xhp\" name=\"column\"\>column\</link\>. A manual column break is indicated by a nonprinting border at the top of the new column.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149487				0	en-ZA	Page Break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149102				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_BREAK:RB_PAGE\"\>Inserts a manual page break, and moves the text found to the right of the cursor to the beginning of the next page. The inserted page break is indicated by a nonprinting border at the top of the new page.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145758	13			0	en-ZA	You can also insert a page break by pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter. However, if you want to assign the following page a different Page Style, you must use the menu command to insert the manual page break.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149175				0	en-ZA	Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156275				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_BREAK:LB_COLL\"\>Select the page style for the page that follows the manual page break.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145782				0	en-ZA	Change page number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155917				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:DLG_BREAK:CB_PAGENUM\"\>Assigns the page number that you specify to the page that follows the manual page break. This option is only available if you assign a different page style to the page that follows manual page break.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151384				0	en-ZA	Page number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150700				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:DLG_BREAK:ED_PAGENUM\"\>Enter the new page number for the page that follows the manual page break.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150554				0	en-ZA	To display manual breaks, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Nonprinting Characters\"\>\<emph\>View - Nonprinting Characters\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Special Tags				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154106				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>tags; in $[officename] Writer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>$[officename] Writer; special HTML tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML;special tags for fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fields;HTML import and export\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>time fields;HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>date fields;HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>DocInformation fields\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154106				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090007.xhp\" name=\"Special Tags\"\>Special Tags\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3153669				0	en-ZA	When you save a document that contains fields as an HTML document, $[officename] automatically converts date, time, and DocInformation fields to special HTML tags. The field contents are inserted between the opening and closing HTML tags of the converted fields. These special HTML tags do not correspond to standard HTML tags.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3152960				0	en-ZA	$[officename] Writer fields are identified by the <SDFIELD> tag in an HTML document. The field type, the format, and the name of the special field are included in the opening HTML tag. The format of a field tag that is recognised by an HTML filter depends on the field type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154570				0	en-ZA	Date and Time Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149696				0	en-ZA	For "Date" and "Time" fields, the TYPE parameter equals DATETIME. The format of the date or the time is specified by the SDNUM parameter, for example, DD:MM:YY for dates, or HH:MM:SS for time.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155183				0	en-ZA	For fixed date and time fields, the date or the time is specified by the SDVAL parameter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149485				0	en-ZA	Examples of date and time special HTML tags that are recognised by $[officename] as fields are shown in the following table:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3151257				0	en-ZA	Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3148970				0	en-ZA	$[officename] Tag				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147102				0	en-ZA	Date is fixed				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3153634				0	en-ZA	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDVAL="35843,4239988426" SDNUM="1031;1031;DD/MM/YY">17/02/98</SDFIELD>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155137				0	en-ZA	Date is variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3156275				0	en-ZA	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDNUM="1031;1031;DD/MM/YY">17/02/98</SDFIELD>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3145774				0	en-ZA	Time is fixed				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155915				0	en-ZA	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDVAL="35843,4240335648" SDNUM="1031;1031;HH:MM:SS">10:10:36</SDFIELD>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3150110				0	en-ZA	Time is variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155862				0	en-ZA	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDNUM="1031;1031;HH:MM:SS">10:10:36</SDFIELD>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147409				0	en-ZA	DocInformation Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147487				0	en-ZA	For DocInformation fields, the TYPE parameter equals DOCINFO. The SUBTYPE parameter displays the specific field type, for example, for the "Created" DocInformation field, SUBTYPE=CREATE. For date and time DocInformation fields, the FORMAT parameter equals DATE or TIME, and the SDNUM parameter indicates the number format that is used. The SDFIXED parameter indicates if the content of the DocInformation field is fixed or not.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147501				0	en-ZA	The contents of a fixed date or time field are equal to the SDVAL parameter, otherwise the contents are equal to the text found between the SDFIELD HTML tags.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149562				0	en-ZA	Examples of DocInformation special HTML tags that are recognised by $[officename] as fields are shown in the following table:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147738				0	en-ZA	Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3146334				0	en-ZA	$[officename] Tag				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149846				0	en-ZA	Description (fixed content)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3148863				0	en-ZA	<SDFIELD TYPE=DOCINFO SUBTYPE=COMMENT SDFIXED>Description</SDFIELD>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3151083				0	en-ZA	Creation date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3153298				0	en-ZA	<SDFIELD TYPE=DOCINFO SUBTYPE=CREATE FORMAT=DATE SDNUM="1031;1031;QQ YY">1. Quarter 98</SDFIELD>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3150175				0	en-ZA	Creation time (fixed content)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3156134				0	en-ZA	<SDFIELD TYPE=DOCINFO SUBTYPE=CREATE FORMAT=TIME SDVAL="0" SDNUM="1031;1031;HH:MM:SS AM/PM" SDFIXED>03:58:35 PM</SDFIELD>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155077				0	en-ZA	Modification date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3154330				0	en-ZA	<SDFIELD TYPE=DOCINFO SUBTYPE=CHANGE FORMAT=DATE SDNUM="1031;1031;NN DD MMM, YY">Mo 23 Feb, 98</SDFIELD>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149879				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05060900.xhp\" name=\"Options\"\>Options\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	par_id3149708				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FRM_ADD\"\>Specifies properties for the selected object, graphic or frame.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151183				0	en-ZA	Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	par_id3147568				0	en-ZA	Specifies the name of the selected item, and associated links.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151178				0	en-ZA	Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	par_id3147510				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FRM_ADD:ED_NAME\"\>Enter a name for the selected item.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	par_id3154565				0	en-ZA	Assign an object, graphic or frame a meaningful name, so that you can quickly locate it afterwards in long documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153674				0	en-ZA	Alternative text (floating frames, graphics, and objects only)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	par_id3150977				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FRM_ADD:ED_ALT_NAME\"\>Enter the text to display in a web browser when the selected item is unavailable. Alternate text is also used to assist people with disabilities.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155903				0	en-ZA	Previous link				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	par_id3154192				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_FRM_ADD_LB_PREV\"\>Displays the item (object, graphic, or frame) that comes before the current item in a linked sequence. To add or change the previous link, select a name from the list. If you are linking frames, the current frame and the target frame must be empty.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159198				0	en-ZA	Next link				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	par_id3149485				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_FRM_ADD_LB_NEXT\"\>Displays the item (object, graphic, or frame) that comes after the current item in a linked sequence. To add or change the next link, select a name from the list. If you are a linking frames, the target frame must be empty.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143280				0	en-ZA	Protect				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	par_id3154834				0	en-ZA	Specifies protection options for the selected item.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149820				0	en-ZA	Protect Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	par_id3149105				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_FRM_ADD:CB_PROTECT_CONTENT\"\>Prevents changes to the contents of the selected item.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	par_id3147099				0	en-ZA	You can still copy the contents of the selected item.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148979				0	en-ZA	Protect Position				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	par_id3147225				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_FRM_ADD:CB_PROTECT_FRAME\"\>Locks the position of the selected item in the current document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153629				0	en-ZA	Protect Size				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_FRM_ADD:CB_PROTECT_SIZE\"\>Locks the size of the selected item.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152770				0	en-ZA	Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	par_id3155137				0	en-ZA	Specifies print and text options for the selected item.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	en-ZA	Editable in read-only document (frames only)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	par_id3149167				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_FRM_ADD:CB_EDIT_IN_READONLY\"\>Allows you to edit the contents of a frame in a document that is read-only (write-protected).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156269				0	en-ZA	Print				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	par_id3151028				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_FRM_ADD:CB_PRINT_FRAME\"\>Includes the selected item when you print the document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145776				0	en-ZA	Text flow				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	par_id3151374	32			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_FRM_ADD_LB_TEXTFLOW\"\>Specifies the preferred text flow direction in a frame. To use the default text flow settings for the page, select \<emph\>Use superordinate object settings \</emph\>from the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060900.xhp	0	help	par_id3150689				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05040200.xhp\" name=\"Text direction\"\>Text direction\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Edit Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150493				0	en-ZA	Edit Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151184				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"feldbefehltext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FieldDialog\"\>Opens a dialogue where you can edit the properties of a field. Click in front of a field, and then choose this command.\</ahelp\> In the dialogue, you can use the arrow buttons to move to the previous or the next field. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151168				0	en-ZA	You can also double-click a field in your document to open the field for editing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153668				0	en-ZA	To change the view between field names and field contents in your document, choose \<emph\>View - Fields\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149106	59			0	en-ZA	If you select a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#dde\" name=\"DDE\"\>DDE\</link\> link in your document, and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Fields, \</emph\>the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02180000.xhp\" name=\"Edit Links\"\>\<emph\>Edit Links\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149036				0	en-ZA	If you click in front of a "sender" type field, and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>, the \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010100.xhp\" name=\"User data\"\>\<emph\>User data\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145765				0	en-ZA	Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155142				0	en-ZA	Lists the type of field that you are editing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151371				0	en-ZA	The following dialogue elements are only visible when the corresponding field type is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150687				0	en-ZA	Select				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150700				0	en-ZA	Lists the field options, for example, "fixed". If you want, you can click another option for the selected field type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155854				0	en-ZA	Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147409				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKNUMFORMAT\"\>Select the format for the contents of the field. For date, time, and user-defined fields, you can also click "Additional formats" in the list, and then choose a different format.\</ahelp\> The formats that are available depend on the type of field that you are editing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149556				0	en-ZA	Offset				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145256				0	en-ZA	Displays the offset for the selected field type, for example, for "Next Page," "Page Numbers" or "Previous Page". You can enter a new offset value which will be added to the displayed page number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id5081637				0	en-ZA	If you want to change the actual page number and not the displayed number, do not use the \<emph\>Offset\</emph\> value. To change page numbers, read the \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagenumbers.xhp\" name=\"Page Numbers\"\>\<emph\>Page Numbers\</emph\>\</link\> guide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145269				0	en-ZA	Level				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150559				0	en-ZA	Change the defined values and outline levels for the "Chapter" field type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147744				0	en-ZA	Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149834				0	en-ZA	Displays the name of a field variable. If you want, you can enter a new name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148844				0	en-ZA	Value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148857				0	en-ZA	Displays the current value of the field variable. If you want, you can enter a new value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153306				0	en-ZA	Condition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156124				0	en-ZA	Displays the condition that must be met for the field to be activated. If you want, you can enter a new \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"condition\"\>condition\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156103				0	en-ZA	Then, Else				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155073				0	en-ZA	Change the field contents that are displayed depending on whether the field condition is met or not.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154326				0	en-ZA	Reference				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154339				0	en-ZA	Insert or modify the reference text for the selected field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148785				0	en-ZA	Macro name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	en-ZA	Displays the name of the macro assigned to the selected field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150097				0	en-ZA	Placeholder				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150027				0	en-ZA	Displays the placeholder text of the selected field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150041				0	en-ZA	Insert Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126				0	en-ZA	Displays the text that is linked to a condition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153140				0	en-ZA	Formula				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154624				0	en-ZA	Displays the formula of a formula field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150658				0	en-ZA	Database selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150671				0	en-ZA	Select a registered database that you want to insert the selected field from. You can also change the table or query that the selected field refers to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154025				0	en-ZA	Record number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154039	39			0	en-ZA	Displays the database record number that is inserted when the condition specified for the "Any record" field type is met. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
