helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id0902200804290272				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Lists the available fields for the field type selected in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list. To insert a field, click the field, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149956				0	en-ZA	For the "Created", "Modified", and "Last printed" field types, you can include the author, date, and time of the corresponding operation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id0902200804290382				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click the format that you want to apply to the selected field, or click "Additional formats" to define a custom format.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149608				0	en-ZA	Fixed content				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_FLD_DOKINF:CB_DOKINFFIXEDCONTENT\"\>Inserts the field as static content, that is, the field cannot be updated.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155554				0	en-ZA	Fields with fixed content are only evaluated when you create a new document from a template that contains such a field. For example, a date field with fixed content inserts the date that a new document was created from the template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Frame				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151189				0	en-ZA	Frame				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"rahm\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertFrame\"\>Inserts a frame that you can use to create a layout of one or more columns of text and objects.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153678				0	en-ZA	To edit a frame, click the border to select it, and then choose \<emph\>Format - Frame/Object\</emph\>. You can also resize or move a selected frame using special \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04130100.xhp\" name=\"shortcut keys\"\>shortcut keys\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152952				0	en-ZA	To delete a frame, click the border of the frame, and then press Delete.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151311				0	en-ZA	If you see small red arrows at the beginning and the end of text in frame, use the arrow keys to scroll through the remaining text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	en-ZA	In the preview area of the \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> dialogue, the frame is represented by a green rectangle, and the reference area by a red rectangle.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149694				0	en-ZA	You can also preview the effects when you change the frame anchor to "As Character". The "Baseline" is drawn in red, "Character" is the font height, and "line" is the height of the line, including the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149107				0	en-ZA	Icon on the Insert toolbar:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148970				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"syrahmentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertFrameInteract\"\>Draws a frame where you drag in the document. Click the arrow next to the icon to select the number of columns for the frame.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120224.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Entries (index of tables)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120224.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147406				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120224.xhp\" name=\"Entries (index of tables)\"\>Entries (index of tables)\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120224.xhp	0	help	par_id3146318	2			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"eintraege\"\>Specify the format for the entries in an Index of Tables. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120224.xhp	0	help	par_id3150020				0	en-ZA	An Index of Tables only has one index level.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040501.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040501.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149871				0	en-ZA	Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040501.xhp	0	help	par_id3148569				0	en-ZA	Specifies the number of columns and the column layout for the section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040501.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390				0	en-ZA	Sections follow the text flow behaviour of the page they are inserted into.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040501.xhp	0	help	par_id3083448				0	en-ZA	For example, if you insert a section that uses a two-column layout into a page style that uses a four-column layout, the two-column layout is nested inside one of the four columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040501.xhp	0	help	par_id3155625				0	en-ZA	You can also nest sections, that is, you can insert a section into another section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
