helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Outline Numbering				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154561				0	en-ZA	Outline Numbering				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145246				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"kapnum\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ChapterNumberingDialog\"\>Specifies the number format and the hierarchy for chapter numbering in the current document.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150934				0	en-ZA	Outline numbering is linked to paragraph styles. By default, the "Heading" paragraph styles (1-10) are assigned to the corresponding outline number levels (1-10). If you want, you can assign different paragraph styles to the outline number level.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id8237250				0	en-ZA	If you want numbered headings, use the \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\> menu command to assign numbering to a paragraph style. Do not use the Numbering icon on the Formatting toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147567	55			0	en-ZA	To highlight the screen display of outline numbers, choose \<emph\>View -\</emph\>\<emph\>Field Shadings\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151168				0	en-ZA	Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147512				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OUTLINE_FORM\"\>Saves or loads an outline number format. A saved outline number format is available to all text documents.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150979				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Format\</emph\> button is only available for outline numbering. For numbered or bulleted list styles, modify the Numbering Styles of the paragraphs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154572				0	en-ZA	Untitled 1 - 9				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150350				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NUM_OUTL_NAMED_NUMS\"\>Select the predefined numbering style that you want to assign to the selected outline level.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153675				0	en-ZA	Save As				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NUM_OUTL_NUM_SAVEAS\"\>Opens a dialogue where you can save the current settings for the selected outline level. You can then load these settings from another document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149689				0	en-ZA	Save As				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154200				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_NUM_NAMES:LB_FORM\"\>Click a numbering style in the list, and then enter a name for the style. The numbers correspond to the outline level that the styles are assigned to.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05120200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Optimal Width				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05120200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149500				0	en-ZA	Optimal Width				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05120200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149050				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"spaltenbreitetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SetOptimalColumnWidth\"\>Automatically adjusts column widths to match the contents of the cells.\</ahelp\> Changing the width of a column does not affect the width of the other columns in the table. The width of the table cannot exceed the page width.\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05120200.xhp	0	help	par_id5611743				0	en-ZA	The change affects only selected cells. You can adjust multiple cells next to each other if you select the cells together.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Condition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154656				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>styles; conditional\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>conditional styles\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154656				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05130100.xhp\" name=\"Condition\"\>Condition\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154766				0	en-ZA	Define conditions for conditional styles here.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151391				0	en-ZA	Conditional styles are paragraph styles that have different properties depending on the context. Once defined, you cannot change the conditional properties of a conditional style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149349				0	en-ZA	$[officename] applies the paragraph properties of conditional styles as follows (the bold terms correspond to the titles of dialogue fields): If a paragraph formatted with a conditional style is in a \<emph\>Context\</emph\> that has an \<emph\>Applied Style\</emph\> linked to it, then the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> from that condition is used. If no style is linked to the \<emph\>Context\</emph\>, then the attributes defined in the conditional style apply. The following example illustrates this relationship:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149883				0	en-ZA	Open a blank text document and write a short business letter with a header (\<emph\>Format\</emph\> - \<emph\>Page\</emph\> - \<emph\>Header\</emph\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148768				0	en-ZA	Define a new Paragraph Style by choosing \<emph\>New\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, and selecting all the paragraph properties that you want for your business letter in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> dialogue. Name this style "Business letter".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153723				0	en-ZA	Then click the \<emph\>Condition\</emph\> tab and select the \<emph\>Conditional style\</emph\> field to define the new Paragraph Style as a conditional style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154647				0	en-ZA	In \<emph\>Context\</emph\>, select the header entry and under \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> select the style for the header in your business letter; for example, the default Paragraph Style "Header". You also can select your own style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150760				0	en-ZA	You can apply the Paragraph Style to the context by double-clicking the selected entry in the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> list box or by using \<emph\>Apply\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149753				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the Paragraph Style dialogue, and then format all paragraphs in your business letter, including the header, with the new "Business letter" conditional Paragraph Style. (When you click in the header, you may need to display \<item type=\"literal\"\>All Styles\</item\> or \<item type=\"literal\"\>Custom Styles\</item\> in the style list to use the new business letter style.)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145412				0	en-ZA	The header text now has the attributes you specified in the Header Paragraph Style, while the other parts of the document have the attributes defined in the business letter conditional Paragraph Style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154473				0	en-ZA	The "Text body" Style was created as a conditional style. Therefore, any styles you derive from it can be used as conditional styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151321				0	en-ZA	The Paragraph Style applied to the context is used when exporting to other formats (RTF, HTML, and so on).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152952				0	en-ZA	Conditional style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150974				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_CONDCOLL:CB_CONDITION\"\>Check this box to define a new style as a conditional style.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153672				0	en-ZA	Context				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147530				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_COND_COLL_TABLIST\"\>Here you can see the $[officename] predefined contexts, including outline levels 1 to 10, numbering/bullets levels 1 to 10, table header, table contents, section, border, footnote, header and footer.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155896				0	en-ZA	Applied Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149689				0	en-ZA	Here you can see the list of all Paragraph Styles applied to a context.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154194				0	en-ZA	Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159195				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_CONDCOLL:LB_STYLE\"\>A list of all Paragraph Styles which can be assigned to a context is contained in the list box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149306				0	en-ZA	Remove				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151335				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:TP_CONDCOLL:PB_REMOVE\"\>Click here to remove the current context assigned to the selected style.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149483				0	en-ZA	Assign				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154829				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:TP_CONDCOLL:PB_ASSIGN\"\>Click \<emph\>Assign\</emph\> to apply the \<emph\>selected Paragraph Style\</emph\> to the defined \<emph\>context\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\01160300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Create AutoAbstract				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\01160300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148570				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/01160300.xhp\" name=\"Create AutoAbstract\"\>Create AutoAbstract\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\01160300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149286	2			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"autoabstracttext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:CreateAbstract\"\>Copies the headings and a number of subsequent paragraphs in the active document to a new AutoAbstract text document. An AutoAbstract is useful for obtaining an overview of long documents.\</ahelp\> You can specify the number of outline levels as well as the number of paragraphs displayed therein. All levels and paragraphs under the respective settings are hidden. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\01160300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147516				0	en-ZA	Included Outline Levels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\01160300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149804				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:DLG_INSERT_ABSTRACT:NF_LEVEL\"\>Enter the extent of the outline levels to be copied to the new document.\</ahelp\> For example, if you choose 4 levels, all paragraphs formatted with Heading 1 to Heading 4 are included, along with the number of subsequent paragraphs specified in \<emph\>Subpoints per Level\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\01160300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151316				0	en-ZA	Subpoints per Level				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\01160300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:DLG_INSERT_ABSTRACT:NF_PARA\"\>Specify the maximum number of consecutive paragraphs to be included in the AutoAbstract document after each heading.\</ahelp\> All of the paragraphs up to the maximum defined are included until the next paragraph with a Heading Style is reached.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06210000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Links				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06210000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155962				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06210000.xhp\" name=\"Links\"\>Links\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06210000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149499				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:UpdateAllLinks\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Updates the links in the current document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05100400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Unprotect				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05100400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149052				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05100400.xhp\" name=\"Unprotect\"\>Unprotect\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05100400.xhp	0	help	par_id3083450				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:UnsetCellsReadOnly\"\>Removes the cell protection for all selected cells in the current table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05100400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154558	3			0	en-ZA	To remove the protection from several tables at once, select the tables, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+T. To remove the protection from all of the tables in a document, click anywhere in the document, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+T.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05100400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150765				0	en-ZA	You can also remove cell protection from a table in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02130000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Edit Bibliography Entry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434				0	en-ZA	Edit Bibliography Entry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145253				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"litvz\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:AuthoritiesEntryDialog\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Edits the selected bibliography entry.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147340				0	en-ZA	Entry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155961				0	en-ZA	Short name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154657				0	en-ZA	Displays the abbreviation for the bibliography entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148837				0	en-ZA	Author, Title				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152741				0	en-ZA	Displays the author and title information contained in the bibliography entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150214				0	en-ZA	Modify				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154766	11			0	en-ZA	Applies the changes that you made, and then closes the \<emph\>Edit Bibliography Entry \</emph\>dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146968				0	en-ZA	Close				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166468				0	en-ZA	Closes the dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147299				0	en-ZA	New				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151389				0	en-ZA	Opens the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120229.xhp\" name=\"Define Bibliography Entry\"\>Define Bibliography Entry\</link\> dialogue, where you can create a new entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150534				0	en-ZA	Edit				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155620	17			0	en-ZA	Opens the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120229.xhp\" name=\"Define Bibliography Entry\"\>Define Bibliography Entry\</link\> dialogue, where  you can edit the current entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154560				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_literature.xhp\" name=\"Tips for working with bibliography entries\"\>Tips for working with bibliography entries\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Caption				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147173				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"Caption\"\>Caption\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149288	2			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"beschrifttext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_CAPTION\"\>Adds a numbered caption to a selected graphic, table, frame, text frame, or drawing object.\</ahelp\> You can also access this command by right-clicking the item that you want to add the caption to. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154098				0	en-ZA	Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149804				0	en-ZA	Set the caption options for the current selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153533				0	en-ZA	Category				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154574	6			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:COMBOBOX:DLG_CAPTION:BOX_CATEGORY\"\>Select the caption category, or type a name to create a new category. The category text appears before the caption number in the caption label. Each predefined caption category is formatted with a paragraph style of the same name. \</ahelp\> For example, the "Illustration" caption category is formatted with the "Illustration" paragraph style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153675				0	en-ZA	Numbering				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152962				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_CAPTION:BOX_FORMAT\"\>Select the type of numbering that you want to use in the caption.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155893				0	en-ZA	Caption				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149688				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:DLG_CAPTION:EDT_TEXT\"\>Type the text that you want to appear after the caption number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068A				0	en-ZA	Separator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10690				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter optional text characters to appear between the number and the caption text.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154199				0	en-ZA	Position				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149486				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_CAPTION:BOX_POS\"\>Adds the caption above or below the selected item. This option is only available for some objects.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149043				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04060100.xhp\" name=\"Options\"\>Options\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10744				0	en-ZA	AutoCaption				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074A				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the Caption dialogue. It has the same information as the dialogue you get by menu %PRODUCTNAME Writer - AutoCaption in the Options dialogue box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Insert Section				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154108				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"bereicheinfuegen\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Section\"\>Insert Section\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"bereich\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"FN_INSERT_COLUMN_SECTION\"\>Inserts a text section at the cursor position in the document. You can also select a block of text and then choose this command to create a section. You can use sections to insert blocks of text from other documents, to apply custom column layouts, or to protect or to hide blocks of text if a condition is met.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152955				0	en-ZA	You can insert an entire document in a section, or a named section from another. You can also insert a section as a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#dde\" name=\"DDE\"\>DDE\</link\> link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149684				0	en-ZA	To edit a section, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02170000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Sections\"\>\<emph\>Format - Sections\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155183	6			0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Insert Section \</emph\>dialogue contains the following tabs:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151257				0	en-ZA	Insert				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149102				0	en-ZA	Inserts the section that you defined at the current cursor position in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Printer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154104				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04070300.xhp\"\>Printer\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153531				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_ENV_PRT\"\>Set the print options for the envelope.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3152960				0	en-ZA	Consult the documentation that came with your printer for setting up the printer for envelopes. Depending on the printer model, envelopes may have to be placed left, right, in the middle, and either face up or face down.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153665				0	en-ZA	Horizontal left				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154564				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"ITM_HOR_LEFT\"\>Feeds the envelope horizontally from the left edge of the printer tray.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155898				0	en-ZA	Horizontal centre				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149694				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"ITM_HOR_CNTR\"\>Feeds the envelope horizontally from the centre of the printer tray.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155174				0	en-ZA	Horizontal right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3143273				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"ITM_HOR_RGHT\"\>Feeds the envelope horizontally from the right edge of the printer tray.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149488				0	en-ZA	Vertical left				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149823				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"ITM_VER_LEFT\"\>Feeds the envelope vertically from the left edge of the printer tray.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151260				0	en-ZA	Vertical centre				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3148968				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"ITM_VER_CNTR\"\>Feeds the envelope vertically from the centre of the printer tray.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153633				0	en-ZA	Vertical right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149037				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"ITM_VER_RGHT\"\>Feeds the envelope vertically from the right edge of the printer tray.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152773				0	en-ZA	Print from top				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145763				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:TP_ENV_PRT:BTN_TOP\"\>Feeds the envelope with the print side face up in the printer tray.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155146				0	en-ZA	Print from bottom				2002-02-02 02:02:02
