helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145244				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PVIEW_ZOOM_LB\"\>Determines the zoom level of the page preview.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\10070000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Page Preview: Multiple Pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\10070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147171				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/10070000.xhp\" name=\"Page Preview: Multiple Pages\"\>Page Preview: Multiple Pages\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\10070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148771				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:PreviewZoom\"\>Defines the number of pages displayed on screen. Click the arrow next to the icon to open a grid to select the number of pages to be displayed as rows and columns in the preview.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\10070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152738				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3152744\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_showmultiplepages.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152744\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\10070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149805				0	en-ZA	Page Preview: Multiple Pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\10070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154573	5			0	en-ZA	After clicking the \<emph\>Page Preview: Multiple Pages\</emph\> icon, the\<emph\> Multiple pages\</emph\> dialogue opens. Use the two spin buttons to set the number of pages to be displayed. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\10070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	en-ZA	Rows				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\10070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149483				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:DLG_PAGEPREVIEW_ZOOM:ED_ROW\"\>Defines the number of rows of pages.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\10070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143274				0	en-ZA	Columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\10070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149102				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:DLG_PAGEPREVIEW_ZOOM:ED_COL\"\>Defines the number of pages shown in columns.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\10070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149822				0	en-ZA	The settings you choose in the dialogue can also be set using the mouse: Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Page Preview: Multiple Pages\</emph\> icon. Now move the mouse over the desired number of rows and columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\04090000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Insert Rows				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\04090000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154838				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>tables; inserting rows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; inserting in tables, using icon\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\04090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154838				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Rows\"\>Insert Rows\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\04090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147407				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertRows\"\>Inserts one or more rows in the table, below the selection. You can insert more than one row by opening the dialogue (choose \<emph\>Table - Insert - Rows\</emph\>), or by selecting more than one row before clicking the icon.\</ahelp\> The second method inserts rows of the same height as the originally selected rows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\04090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151180				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3151189\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_insertrows.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151189\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\04090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	en-ZA	Insert Row				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18030200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Time				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18030200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147174				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>time fields;inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fields;inserting time\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18030200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147174				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/18030200.xhp\" name=\"Time\"\>Time\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18030200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152896				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertTimeField\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Inserts the current time as a field.\</ahelp\> The time is taken directly from the system settings of your operating system. A fixed time format is applied, which cannot be updated by using the F9 function key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18030200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177				0	en-ZA	To assign a different time format, or adapt the actual time data, select \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and make the desired changes in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>\<emph\>Fields\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue. Additionally, you can modify the format of an inserted time field at any time by choosing \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02140000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Fields\"\>\<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\04220000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Table: Fixed				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\04220000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151187				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/04220000.xhp\" name=\"Table: Fixed\"\>Table: Fixed\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\04220000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151174				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:TableModeFix\" visibility=\"visible\"\>If this mode is active, changes to a line and/or column affect only the neighbouring lines or columns in question.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\04220000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	en-ZA	\<image src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_tablemodefix.png\" id=\"img_id3155903\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155903\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\04220000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155066				0	en-ZA	Table: Fixed				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Combined Display				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151186				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/08080000.xhp\" name=\"Combined Display\"\>Combined Display\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151172				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:StatusBarFunc\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Displays current information about the active document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156375				0	en-ZA	When the cursor is in a named section, the section name appears. When the cursor is in a table, the name of the table cell appears. The size of the object is shown when you edit frames or drawing objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145416				0	en-ZA	When the cursor is positioned within text, you can double-click this field to open the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>\<emph\>Fields\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue. In this dialogue, you can define a field to be inserted in your document at the current cursor position. When the cursor is positioned in a table, a double-click in this field will call the \<emph\>Table Format\</emph\> dialogue. Depending on the object selected, you can call up a dialogue to edit a section, a graphic object, a floating frame, an OLE object, direct numbering or the position and size of a drawing object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\06090000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Insert Unnumbered Entry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\06090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154505				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/06090000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Unnumbered Entry\"\>Insert Unnumbered Entry\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\06090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148775				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertNeutralParagraph\"\>Inserts a paragraph without numbering. The existing numbering will not be affected.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\06090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156377				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3156384\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_insertneutralparagraph.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156384\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\06090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156381				0	en-ZA	Insert Unnumbered Entry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18130000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Direct Cursor On/Off				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18130000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147167				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>direct cursor; restriction\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147167				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/18130000.xhp\" name=\"Direct Cursor On/Off\"\>Direct Cursor On/Off\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152896				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShadowCursor\"\>Activates or deactivates the direct cursor.\</ahelp\> You can specify the behaviour of the direct cursor by choosing \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040600.xhp\" name=\"Text Document - Formatting Aids\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</link\>\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147508				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3154840\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_shadowcursor.png\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154840\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151310				0	en-ZA	Direct Cursor On/Off				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154570				0	en-ZA	The direct cursor allows you to click in any blank area of a page to place text, images, tables, frames, and other objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155902				0	en-ZA	If you place the direct cursor approximately in the middle between the left and the right margin of a page or a table cell, the text you insert will be centred. Similarly, text is right-aligned when the direct cursor is placed on the right margin.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151255				0	en-ZA	The AutoCorrect tool automatically removes empty paragraphs, tabs, and spaces that are inserted by the direct cursor. If you want to use the direct cursor, then disable the AutoCorrect tool.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148982				0	en-ZA	The direct cursor sets tabs to position the cursor. If you change the tabs later. the position of the text on the page may change as well.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\19020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Insert Footer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\19020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145829				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/19020000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Footer\"\>Insert Footer\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\19020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148768				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"FN_INSERT_FOOTER\"\>Displays the footer of an HTML document if footers are enabled on the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05040400.xhp\" name=\"Format - Page - Footer\"\>\<emph\>Format - Page - Footer\</emph\>\</link\> tab page.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\06140000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Restart Numbering				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\06140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147171				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/06140000.xhp\" name=\"Restart Numbering\"\>Restart Numbering\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\06140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145249				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:NumberingStart\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Restarts the text numbering.\</ahelp\> This is only visible when the cursor is positioned within numbered or bulleted text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\06140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145082				0	en-ZA	\<image src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_numberingstart.png\" id=\"img_id3145089\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145089\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
