helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Merging and Splitting Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147240				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>cells; merging/splitting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; merging cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell merges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>splitting cells;by menu command\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>merging;cells\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id6618243				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"table_cellmerge\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_cellmerge.xhp\" name=\"Merging and Splitting Cells\"\>Merging and Splitting Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id1211890				0	en-ZA	You can select adjacent cells, then merge them into a single cell. Conversely, you can take a large cell and divide it into individual cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id3463850				0	en-ZA	To Merge Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id5708792				0	en-ZA	Select the adjacent cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id6301461				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Table - Merge Cells\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id9156468				0	en-ZA	To Split Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3415936				0	en-ZA	Place the cursor in the cell to be split.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id4044312				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Table - Split Cells\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id634174				0	en-ZA	A dialogue allows you to split the cell into two or more cells, horizontally or vertically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Using Captions 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147691				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>inserting; captions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>captions; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;captions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects; captioning\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; labelling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames; labelling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>charts; labelling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text frames; labelling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>draw objects; inserting captions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>legends, see also captions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150537				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"captions\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions.xhp\" name=\"Using Captions\"\>Using Captions\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153156				0	en-ZA	In text documents, you can add continuously numbered captions to graphics, tables, frames, and drawing objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153172				0	en-ZA	You can edit the text and the number ranges for different types of captions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153186				0	en-ZA	When you add a caption to a picture or to an object, the object and the caption text are placed together in a new frame. When you add a caption to a table, the caption text is inserted as a paragraph next to the table. When you add a caption to a frame, the caption text is added to the text inside the frame, either before or after the existing text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_idN10713				0	en-ZA	To move both the object and the caption, drag the frame that contains these items. To update the caption numbering after you move the frame, press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155541				0	en-ZA	To define a caption proceed as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3155567				0	en-ZA	Select the item that you want to add a caption to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3155586				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Caption\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147765				0	en-ZA	Select the options that you want, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>. If you want, you can also enter different text in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Category\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, for example \<item type=\"literal\"\>Figure\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	en-ZA	You can edit caption text directly in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147271				0	en-ZA	A caption is formatted with the paragraph style that matches the name of the caption category. For example, if you insert a "Table" caption, the "Table" paragraph style is applied to the caption text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3145671				0	en-ZA	$[officename] can automatically add a caption when you insert an object, graphic, frame, or table. Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - AutoCaption\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Numbering and Numbering Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155174				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>numbering; manually/by styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>manual numbering in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraph styles;numbering\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155174	30			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"using_numbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Numbering and Numbering Styles\"\>Numbering and Numbering Styles\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149818				0	en-ZA	You can apply numbering to a paragraph manually or with a paragraph style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id6140629				0	en-ZA	To Apply Numbering Manually				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155866				0	en-ZA	To apply numbering manually, click in the paragraph, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering On/Off\</item\>         \<emph/\>icon on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3153405				0	en-ZA	You cannot apply manual numbering to paragraphs that are listed under "Special Styles" in the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN10711				0	en-ZA	When you press Enter in a numbered or bulleted list, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> automatically numbers the next paragraph. To remove the numbering or bullet from the new paragraph, press Enter again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072B				0	en-ZA	To change the hierarchical level of a bullet in a list, click in front of the paragraph, then press the Tab key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072F				0	en-ZA	To change the bullets or numbering format for the current paragraph only, select a character or word in the paragraph, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</item\>, and then click a new format. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN10733				0	en-ZA	To change the bullet or numbering format for all paragraphs in the list, ensure that the cursor is in the list, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</item\>, and then click a new format. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN10737				0	en-ZA	To apply the same bullet or numbering format to all paragraphs in the list, select all paragraphs, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</item\>, and then click a format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073A				0	en-ZA	You can also use the commands on the \<link href=\"text/swriter/main0206.xhp\" name=\"Numbering Object Bar\"\>Bullets and Numbering\</link\> toolbar to edit a numbered or bulleted list. To change the numbering or bullet format, click the \<emph\>Bullets and Numbering\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153123				0	en-ZA	To Apply Numbering With a Paragraph Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3153137				0	en-ZA	Paragraph Styles give you greater control over numbering that you apply in a document. When you change the numbering format of the style, all paragraphs using the style are automatically updated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149646				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paragraph Styles\</item\>               \<emph/\>icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149599				0	en-ZA	Right-click the paragraph style that you want to apply numbering to, and then choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149850				0	en-ZA	Click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Outline & Numbering\</item\>               \<emph/\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149874				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering Style\</item\> box, select the type of numbering that you want to use.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3145113				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149589				0	en-ZA	Apply the style to the paragraphs that you want to add numbering to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Hiding Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148856				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>text; hiding\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sections;hiding\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs;hiding\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hiding;text, with conditions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>variables;for hiding text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148856	1			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"hidden_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hidden_text.xhp\" name=\"Hiding Text\"\>Hiding Text\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103				0	en-ZA	You can use fields and sections to hide or display text in your document if a condition is met.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153409				0	en-ZA	Before you can hide text, you must first create a variable to use in the condition for hiding the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id5174108				0	en-ZA	To Create a Variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153131				0	en-ZA	Click in your document and choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149640	21			0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Variables \</emph\>tab and click "Set Variable" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149970	22			0	en-ZA	Click "General" in the \<emph\>Format \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149620				0	en-ZA	Type a name for the variable in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Name\</item\> box, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>Hide\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149869				0	en-ZA	Enter a value for the variable in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145108				0	en-ZA	To hide the variable in your document, select \<emph\>Invisible\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149585				0	en-ZA	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156245				0	en-ZA	To Hide Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145391				0	en-ZA	Click in the document where you want to add the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145409	5			0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Functions \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155325	29			0	en-ZA	Click "Hidden Text" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154404				0	en-ZA	Enter a statement in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>Hide==1\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153371	31			0	en-ZA	Type the text that you want to hide in the \<emph\>Hidden text \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	en-ZA	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154256				0	en-ZA	To Hide a Paragraph				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154853				0	en-ZA	Click in the paragraph where you want to add the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154872	35			0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Functions \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155902	6			0	en-ZA	Click "Hidden Paragraph" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155947				0	en-ZA	Enter a statement in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>Hide==1\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149991				0	en-ZA	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3793450				0	en-ZA	You must enable this feature by removing the check mark from menu \<emph\>View - Hidden Paragraphs\</emph\>. When the check mark is set, you cannot hide any paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148675				0	en-ZA	To Hide a Section				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3148697				0	en-ZA	Select the text that you want to hide in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153019				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3148950				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Hide\</item\> area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Hide\</item\>, and then enter an expression in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>Hide==1\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153636				0	en-ZA	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
