helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149963				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>formats; resetting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>font attributes; resetting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>fonts; resetting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>resetting; fonts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>direct formatting;exiting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;exiting direct formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>exiting;direct formatting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149963				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"reset_format\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/reset_format.xhp\" name=\"Resetting Font Attributes\"\>Resetting Font Attributes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3154091				0	en-ZA	You can quickly exit manual formatting by pressing the right-arrow key. For example, if you have pressed Ctrl+B to apply the bold typeface to the text that you type, press the right arrow to return to the default character format of the paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	en-ZA	To reset all direct formatting of existing text, select that text, then choose the menu command \<emph\>Format - Default Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
