helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id5589159				0	en-ZA	To change the measurement units, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - General\</item\>, and then select a new measurement unit in the Settings area. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id9936216				0	en-ZA	You can change the indents for the current paragraph, or for all selected paragraphs, or for a Paragraph Style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id7953123				0	en-ZA	You can also \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/ruler.xhp\" name=\"ruler\"\>set indents using the ruler\</link\>. To display the ruler, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Ruler\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id4013794				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\</item\> to change the indents for the current paragraph or for all selected paragraphs. You can also \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/ruler.xhp\" name=\"ruler\"\>set indents using the ruler\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id1631824				0	en-ZA	Right-click a paragraph and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit Paragraph Style - Indents & Spacing\</item\> to change the indents for all paragraphs that have the same Paragraph Style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id7271645				0	en-ZA	Indents are calculated with respect to the left and right page margins. If you want the paragraph to extend into the page margin, enter a negative number. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id2136295				0	en-ZA	The indents are different regarding the writing direction. For example, look at the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Before text \</item\>indent value in left-to-right languages. The left edge of the paragraph is indented with respect to the left page margin. In right-to-left languages, the right edge of the paragraph is indented with respect to the right page margin.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id4186223				0	en-ZA	For a hanging indent, enter a positive value for \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Before text\</item\> and a negative value for \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>First line\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id1491134				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030100.xhp\"\>Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Checking Spelling and Grammar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149684				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>spellcheck; checking text documents manually\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>checking spelling;manually\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>grammar checker\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149684				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"spellcheck_dialog\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/spellcheck_dialog.xhp\" name=\"Checking Spelling and Grammar\"\>Checking Spelling and Grammar\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3149814				0	en-ZA	You can manually check the spelling and grammar of a text selection or the entire document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id0525200902184476				0	en-ZA	To check the spelling and the grammar of a text, the appropriate dictionaries must be installed. For many languages three different dictionaries exist: a spellchecker, a hyphenation dictionary, and a thesaurus. Each dictionary covers one language only. Grammar checkers can be downloaded and installed as extensions. See the \<link href=\"http://extensions.services.openoffice.org/dictionary\"\>extensions web page\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3149828				0	en-ZA	The spellcheck starts at the current cursor position, or at the beginning of the text selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3155859				0	en-ZA	Click in the document, or select the text that you want to check.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3149836				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Spelling and Grammar\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3156104				0	en-ZA	When a possible spelling error is encountered, the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Spellcheck\</item\>               \<emph/\>dialogue opens and $[officename] offers some suggested corrections.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3149861				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3145099				0	en-ZA	To accept a correction, click the suggestion, and then click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3156241				0	en-ZA	Edit the sentence in the upper text box, and then click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3155886				0	en-ZA	To add the unknown word to a user-defined dictionary, click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3147107				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06010000.xhp\" name=\"Spellcheck dialogue\"\>Spelling and Grammar dialogue\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id9625843				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Adding_More_Languages\"\>Wiki page: Adding more languages\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id1683706				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Spellchecking_in_More_Languages\"\>Wiki page: Multiple language spellchecking\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	User-Defined Indexes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154896				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>indexes; creating user-defined indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>user-defined indexes\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154896				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"indices_userdef\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_userdef.xhp\" name=\"User-Defined Indexes\"\>User-Defined Indexes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3155184				0	en-ZA	You can create as many user-defined indexes as you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155915				0	en-ZA	To Create a User-Defined Index				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3155867				0	en-ZA	Select a word or words that you want to add to a user-defined index.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3153410				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Entry\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3154248				0	en-ZA	Click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>New User-defined Index\</item\> button next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Index\</item\>               \<emph/\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3155886				0	en-ZA	Type a name for the index in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Name\</item\>               \<emph/\>box and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3147114	52			0	en-ZA	Click\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> to add the selected word(s) to the new index. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3147139				0	en-ZA	Click\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150231				0	en-ZA	To Insert a User-Defined Index				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150933				0	en-ZA	Click in the document where you want to insert the index.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150952				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150509				0	en-ZA	On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Index/Table\</item\> tab, select the name of the user-defined index that you created in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\>               \<emph/\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146881				0	en-ZA	Select any options that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146897				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150720				0	en-ZA	If you want to use a different paragraph style as a table of contents entry, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Styles\</item\>, and then click the (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) button next to the box. Click the style in the list, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>>>\</item\>         \<emph/\>or the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\><<\</item\>         \<emph/\>button to define the outline level for the paragraph style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Changing the Case of Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155182				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>characters; uppercase or lowercase\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; uppercase or lowercase\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lowercase letters; text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>uppercase; formatting text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>capital letters;changing to small letters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;cases of text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>initial capitals in titles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>small capitals (guide)\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155182				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"text_capital\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_capital.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Case of Text\"\>Changing the Case of Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3155916				0	en-ZA	You can change the case of text, format text with small capitals, or capitalise the first letter of each word in a selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_idN10728				0	en-ZA	When you apply a formatting to your text by \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>, the text stays the same, it is only displayed in another way. On the other hand, when you choose \<emph\>Format - Change Case\</emph\>, the text is permanently changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155861				0	en-ZA	To Capitalize Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3147420				0	en-ZA	Select the text that you want to capitalise.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149841				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910485778				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Change Case - Uppercase\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910485775				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Character\</item\>, click the Font Effects tab, then select the type of capitalisation in the Effects box. "Capitals" capitalises all letters. "Title" capitalises the first letter of each word. "Small capitals" capitalises all letters, but in a reduced font size.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149644				0	en-ZA	To Change Text to Lowercase				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149964				0	en-ZA	Select the text that you want to change to lowercase.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149606				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id112020091049000				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Change Case - Lowercase\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910490034				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Character\</item\>, click the Font Effects tab, then select "Lowercase" in the Effects box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Inserting and Deleting Page Breaks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155183				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>page breaks; inserting and deleting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; page breaks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;page breaks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages; inserting/deleting page breaks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>manual page breaks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;deleting page breaks before\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155183				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"page_break\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/page_break.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Deleting Page Breaks\"\>Inserting and Deleting Page Breaks\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149833				0	en-ZA	To Insert a Manual Page Break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3153402				0	en-ZA	Click in your document where you want the new page to begin.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3153119				0	en-ZA	Press Ctrl+Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153135				0	en-ZA	To Delete a Manual Page Break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3149641				0	en-ZA	Click in front of the first character on the page that follows the manual page break.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3149608				0	en-ZA	Press Backspace.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149624				0	en-ZA	To Delete a Manual Page Break That Occurs Before a Table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3145111				0	en-ZA	Right-click in the table, and choose \<emph\>Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3156254				0	en-ZA	Click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05090300.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>\<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3153380				0	en-ZA	Clear the \<emph\>Break\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3154249				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04010000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Break dialogue\"\>Insert Break dialogue\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Inserting Sections				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>sections; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>HTML documents;inserting linked sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating;linked sections, manually\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>links;inserting sections\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"section_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/section_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Sections\"\>Inserting Sections\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155917				0	en-ZA	You can insert new sections, or links to sections in other documents into the current document. If you insert a section as a link, the content of the link changes when you modify the source document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155863				0	en-ZA	To Insert a New Section				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149843				0	en-ZA	Click in your document where you want to insert a new section, or select the text that you want to convert to a section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156103				0	en-ZA	If you select a text that occurs within a paragraph, the text is automatically converted into a new paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153404				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>New Section\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, type a name for the section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	en-ZA	Set the options for the section, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149635				0	en-ZA	To Insert a Section as a Link				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149648				0	en-ZA	Before you can insert a section as link, you must first create sections in the source document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149611				0	en-ZA	When you open a document that contains linked sections, $[officename] prompts you to update the contents of the sections. To manually update a link, choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - Links\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149860				0	en-ZA	You can also insert linked sections in HTML documents. When you view the page in a web browser, the content of the sections corresponds to the content of the sections at the time the HTML document was last saved.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145104				0	en-ZA	Click in your document where you want to insert the linked section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156241				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>New Section\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, type a name for the section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153387				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link\</item\>               \<emph/\>area, select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link\</item\>               \<emph/\>check box. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>Under Windows, you can also select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>DDE\</item\> check box to automatically update the contents of the section when the section in the source document is changed. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154852				0	en-ZA	Click the browse button (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File name\</item\>               \<emph/\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155882				0	en-ZA	Locate the document containing the section that you want to link to, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149978				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Section\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, select the section that you want to insert.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150003				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
