helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147135	46			0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Styles \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150229	47			0	en-ZA	Click an index level in the \<emph\>Levels \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150934	48			0	en-ZA	Click the style that you want to apply in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150960				0	en-ZA	Click the assign button \<emph\><\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150516				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146878				0	en-ZA	To Assign Hyperlinks to Entries in a Table of Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3146890				0	en-ZA	You can assign a cross-reference as a hyperlink to entries in a table of contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150712				0	en-ZA	Right-click in the table of contents, and then choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150738				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Entries\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3148399				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Level\</item\> list click the heading level that you want to assign hyperlinks to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3148424	53			0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Structure \</emph\>area, click in the box in front of \<emph\>E#\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3153171				0	en-ZA	Click in the box behind the \<emph\>E\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147060				0	en-ZA	Repeat for each heading level that you want to create hyperlinks for, or click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>All\</item\> button to apply the formatting to all levels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\field_convert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Converting a Field into Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
