helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9836115				0	en-ZA	A black line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6485793				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id1237525\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_6.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1237525\"\>solid line for border\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1454512				0	en-ZA	A black line sets the corresponding line of the selected cells. The line is shown as a dotted line when you choose the 0.05 pt line style. Double lines are shown when you select a double line style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4618671				0	en-ZA	A grey line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1239356				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id2688680\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_7.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2688680\"\>grey line for border\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9474166				0	en-ZA	A grey line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will not be changed. No line will be set or removed at this position.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1545457				0	en-ZA	A white line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1681875				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id7340617\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_8.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7340617\"\>white line for border\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2316660				0	en-ZA	A white line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will be removed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id5908688				0	en-ZA	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5118564				0	en-ZA	Select a single cell in a Writer table, then choose \<emph\>Table - Table properties - Borders\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id244758				0	en-ZA	Select a thick line style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7741325				0	en-ZA	To set a lower border, click the lower edge repeatedly until you see a thick line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id542313				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id4273506\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_6.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4273506\"\>setting thick lower border\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2210760				0	en-ZA	All cells in a Writer table have at least a left and a lower line by default. Most cells on the table perimeter have more lines applied by default. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5400860				0	en-ZA	All lines that are shown in white in the preview will be removed from the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Emphasising Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149820				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>text; emphasising\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>emphasising text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149820				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"text_emphasize\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_emphasize.xhp\" name=\"Emphasizing Text\"\>Emphasising Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	en-ZA	Here are a few examples of how to emphasise text in a document:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	en-ZA	Select the text and apply a different font style or effect, such as \<emph\>bold\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3149840	68			0	en-ZA	Right-click in a paragraph, choose \<emph\>Paragraph, \</emph\>set the options that you want, for example, the background colour, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	en-ZA	Select the text, and then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Frame\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id6924649				0	en-ZA	Use the Text tool on the Drawing toolbar. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E7				0	en-ZA	Use Fontwork. To open the Fontwork window, click the Fontwork Gallery icon on the Drawing bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Using a Frame to Centre Text on a Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155177				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>text frames; centering on pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>centering;text frames on pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>title pages; centering text on\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155177				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"text_centervert\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_centervert.xhp\" name=\"Using a Frame to Center Text on a Page\"\>Using a Frame to Center Text on a Page\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155920				0	en-ZA	Select the text that you want to centre on the page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155868				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Frame\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3152765				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Anchor\</item\>               \<emph/\>area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>To page\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149844				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Size\</item\>               \<emph/\>area, set the dimensions of the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156114				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Position\</item\>               \<emph/\>area, select "Center" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Horizontal\</item\>               \<emph/\>and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Vertical\</item\>               \<emph/\>boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153410				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149615				0	en-ZA	To hide the borders of the frame, select the frame, and then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Frame/Object\</item\>. Click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Borders\</item\> tab, and then click in the\<emph/\>         \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Set No Border\</item\> box in the\<emph/\>         \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Line Arrangement\</item\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145098				0	en-ZA	To resize the frame, drag the edges of the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Calculating Complex Formulae in Text Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147406				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>formulae; complex formulae in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>calculating;formulae/mean values\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147406				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"calculate_intext\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_intext.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Complex Formulas in Text Documents\"\>Calculating Complex Formulas in Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145245				0	en-ZA	You can use predefined functions in a formula, and then insert the result of the calculation into a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152901				0	en-ZA	For example, to calculate the mean value of three numbers, do the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145078				0	en-ZA	Click in the document where you want to insert the formula, and then press F2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	en-ZA	Click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula\</item\>               \<emph/\>icon, and choose "Mean" from the Statistical Functions list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149692				0	en-ZA	Type the three numbers, separated by vertical slashes (|).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481				0	en-ZA	Press \<emph\>Enter\</emph\>. The result is inserted as a field into the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149823				0	en-ZA	To edit the formula, double-click the field in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Calculating in Text Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149909				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulae; calculating in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>references;in Writer tables\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149909				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"calculate\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate.xhp\" name=\"Calculating in Text Documents\"\>Calculating in Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149949				0	en-ZA	You can insert a calculation directly into a text document or into a text table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149972				0	en-ZA	Click in the document where you want to insert the calculation, and then press F2. If you are in a table cell, type an equals sign =.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155547				0	en-ZA	Type the calculation that you want to insert, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=10000/12\</item\>, and then press Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155565				0	en-ZA	You can also click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula\</item\>         \<emph/\>icon on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula Bar\</item\>, and then choose a function for your formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id8316904				0	en-ZA	To reference cells in a Writer text table, enclose the cell address or the cell range in angle brackets. For example, to reference cell A1 from another cell, enter =<A1> into the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149487				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>text frames; inserting/editing/linking\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>resizing;text frames, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scaling; text frames, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>links;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text flow; from frame to frame\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames; linking\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing;hiding text frames from printing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149487				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"text_frame\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_frame.xhp\" name=\"Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\"\>Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149842				0	en-ZA	A text frame is a container for text and graphics that you can place anywhere on a page. You can also use a frame to apply a column layout to text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156104				0	en-ZA	To Insert a Text Frame				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149961				0	en-ZA	Select the text that you want to include in the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149602				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Frame\</emph\>, and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145115				0	en-ZA	To Edit a Text Frame				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	en-ZA	To edit the contents of a text frame, click in the frame, and make the changes that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156239				0	en-ZA	To edit a frame, select the frame, right-click, and then choose a formatting option. You can also right-click the selected frame, and choose \<emph\>Frame\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156261				0	en-ZA	To resize a text frame, click an edge of the frame, and drag one of the edges or corners of the frame. Hold down Shift while you drag to maintain the proportion of the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153386				0	en-ZA	To Hide Text From Printing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154262				0	en-ZA	Any Writer text frame can be set to a mode which allows viewing the text on screen, but hides the text from printing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154858				0	en-ZA	Select the text frame (you see the eight handles).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155875				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Frame/Object - Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155899				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> area, unmark the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> check box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148701				0	en-ZA	To Link Text Frames				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149986				0	en-ZA	You can link Writer text frames so that their contents automatically flow from one frame to another.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3153025				0	en-ZA	Click the edge of a frame that you want to link. Selection handles appear on the edges of the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150223	87			0	en-ZA	On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Frame\</item\> Bar, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link Frames\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3148968\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_chainframes.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148968\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150930				0	en-ZA	Click the frame that you want to link to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150947				0	en-ZA	You can only link frames if:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150969				0	en-ZA	The target frame is empty.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	en-ZA	The target frame is not linked to another frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154383				0	en-ZA	The source and the target frames are in the same section. For example, you cannot link a header frame to a footer frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145559				0	en-ZA	The source frame does not have a next link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145577				0	en-ZA	The target or the source frame are not contained in each other.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3151083				0	en-ZA	When you select a linked frame, a line is displayed that connects the linked frames.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id5853144				0	en-ZA	The AutoSize feature is available only for the last frame in a chain of linked frames.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Using Rulers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	bm_id8186284				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>rulers;using rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>horizontal rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>vertical rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>indents; setting on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page margins on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table cells;adjusting the width on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adjusting page margins and cell widths\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"ruler\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/ruler.xhp\"\>Using Rulers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067D				0	en-ZA	To show or hide rulers, choose \<emph\>View - Ruler\</emph\>. To show the vertical ruler, choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040200.xhp\" name=\"Writer - View\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - View\</emph\>\</link\>, and then select \<emph\>Vertical ruler\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Ruler\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149686				0	en-ZA	Adjusting Page Margins				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3155175				0	en-ZA	The margins of a page are indicated by the filled areas at the ends of the rulers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149038				0	en-ZA	Changing Indents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3153631				0	en-ZA	Indents are adjusted with the three small triangles on the horizontal ruler.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3152776	26			0	en-ZA	To change the left or the right paragraph indent, select the paragraph(s) that you want change the indent for, drag the bottom left or the bottom right triangle on the horizontal ruler to a new location. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3145769				0	en-ZA	To change the first line indent of a selected paragraph, drag the top left triangle on the horizontal ruler to a new location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	en-ZA	You can also double-click anywhere on the horizontal ruler, and adjust the indents in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030000.xhp\" name=\"Paragraph\"\>\<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Inserting Graphics				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154922				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>text; inserting pictures in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images; inserting in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; inserting options\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154922				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Graphics\"\>Inserting Graphics\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149695				0	en-ZA	There are several ways to insert a graphic object in a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Calculating Cell Totals in Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147400				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;sums in text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>totals in text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;calculating sums\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;calculating sums\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>table cells;calculating sums\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sums of table cell series\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147400				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"calculate_intable\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_intable.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Cell Totals in Tables\"\>Calculating the Sum of a Series of Table Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154243				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Table\</emph\>, and insert a table with one column and more than one row into a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154203				0	en-ZA	Type a number in each cell of the column, but leave the last cell in the column empty.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154222				0	en-ZA	Place the cursor in the last cell of the column, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Sum\</item\> icon on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table Bar\</item\>.\<br/\>The\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula Bar\</item\> appears with the entry "=sum".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147775				0	en-ZA	Click in the first cell of the series you want to sum up, drag to the final cell, and then release.\<br/\>$[officename] inserts a formula for calculating the sum of the values in the current column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150507	8			0	en-ZA	Press Enter, or click \<emph\>Apply\</emph\> in the Formula bar. \<br/\>The sum of the values in the current column is entered in the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150533				0	en-ZA	If you enter a different number anywhere in the column, the sum is updated as soon as you click in the last column cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3155533				0	en-ZA	Similarly, you can also quickly calculate the sum of a row of numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146875				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>headers; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page styles; changing from selection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>new page styles from selection\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146875				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"change_header\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/change_header.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page\"\>Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153584				0	en-ZA	You can design a page layout and then create a page style based on it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3154245				0	en-ZA	For example, you can create a page style that displays a particular header, and another page style that displays a different header.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	en-ZA	Open a new text document, choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3150532				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon and select \<emph\>New Styles from Selection\</emph\> from the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153153				0	en-ZA	Type a name for the page in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style name\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153184	32			0	en-ZA	Double-click the name in the list to apply the style to the current page. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155541				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Header\</emph\>, and choose the new page style from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155572				0	en-ZA	Type the text that you want in the header. Position the cursor into the main text area outside of the header.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155592				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3147771				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\>               \<emph/\>area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page break\</item\> and then select “Default” from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\>               \<emph/\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3147810				0	en-ZA	Repeat steps 2-6 to create a second custom page style with a different header.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Turning Number Recognition On or Off in Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156383				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>numbers; automatic recognition in text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; number recognition\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>dates;formatting automatically in tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>recognition;numbers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156383				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"number_date_conv\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/number_date_conv.xhp\" name=\"Turning Number Recognition On or Off in Tables\"\>Turning Number Recognition On or Off in Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3155179				0	en-ZA	$[officename] can automatically format dates that you have entered into a table, according to the regional settings specified in your operating system.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3149966				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3155919				0	en-ZA	Right-click in a table cell and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Number recognition\</item\>. When this feature is on, a check mark is displayed in front of the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Number recognition\</item\> command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3155527				0	en-ZA	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Table\</item\>, and select or clear the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Number recognition\</item\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040500.xhp\" name=\"Text Document - Table\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Table\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_preview.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Previewing a Page Before Printing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_preview.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155179				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>printing; previews\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>previews; print layouts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>print layout checks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>book view\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages;previews\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_preview.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155179				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"print_preview\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/print_preview.xhp\" name=\"Previewing a Page Before Printing\"\>Previewing a Page Before Printing\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_preview.xhp	0	help	par_id3149847	34			0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File\</emph\> - \<emph\>Page Preview\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_preview.xhp	0	help	par_id3155055				0	en-ZA	Use the zoom icons on the \<emph\>Page Preview\</emph\> bar to reduce or enlarge the view of the page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_preview.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067F				0	en-ZA	To print your document scaled down, set the print options on the \<emph\>Page Layout\</emph\> tab page of the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Print\</item\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_preview.xhp	0	help	par_id3145093				0	en-ZA	Use the arrow keys or the arrow icons on the \<emph\>Page Preview\</emph\> bar to scroll through the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_preview.xhp	0	help	par_id3154265				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/01120000.xhp\" name=\"File - Page Preview\"\>File - Page Preview\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Editing or Deleting Index and Table Entries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155186				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>indexes; editing or deleting entries\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; editing or deleting entries\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;entries of indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;table/index entries\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155186				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"indices_delete\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_delete.xhp\" name=\"Editing or Deleting Index and Table Entries\"\>Editing or Deleting Index and Table Entries\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855	12			0	en-ZA	Index entries are inserted as fields into your document. To view fields in your document, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View\</item\>         \<emph/\>and ensure that \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Field Shadings\</item\>         \<emph/\>is selected. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155507				0	en-ZA	Place the cursor immediately in front of the index entry in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155526	16			0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Index Entry\</emph\>, and do one of the following: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155893				0	en-ZA	To cycle through the index entries in your document, click the next or the previous arrows in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02160000.xhp\" name=\"Edit Index Entry dialogue\"\>\<emph\>Edit Index Entry\</emph\> dialogue\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Making Text Superscript or Subscript				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155174				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>text; subscript and superscript\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>superscript text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>subscript text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>characters;subscript and superscript\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155174				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"subscript\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/subscript.xhp\" name=\"Making Text Superscript or Subscript\"\>Making Text Superscript or Subscript\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3155917				0	en-ZA	Select the text that you want to make superscript or subscript.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3155865				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3153416				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020500.xhp\" name=\"Format - Character - Position\"\>Format - Character - Position\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3154705				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"Tools - AutoCorrect - Replace\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect - Replace\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Creating New Styles From Selections				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155911				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>styles; creating from selections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>drag and drop;creating new styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying;styles, from selections\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155911				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"stylist_fromselect\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/stylist_fromselect.xhp\" name=\"Creating New Styles From Selections\"\>Creating New Styles From Selections\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149829				0	en-ZA	To Create a New Style From a Manually Formatted Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3156097				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153402				0	en-ZA	Click the icon of the style category that you want to create.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153119				0	en-ZA	Click in the document where you want to copy the style from, for example, in a paragraph that you applied manual formatting to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153138				0	en-ZA	Click the arrow next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>New Style from Selection\</item\> icon and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>New Style from Selection\</item\>               \<emph/\>from the submenu				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3156260				0	en-ZA	Type a name in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style Name\</item\>               \<emph/\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154411				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153373				0	en-ZA	To Create a New Style by Drag-And-Drop				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	en-ZA	Click the icon of the style category that you want to create.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154851				0	en-ZA	Select at least one character, or object, in the style that you want to copy. For page and frame styles, select at least one character or object in the page or frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154871				0	en-ZA	Drag the character or object to the Styles and Formatting window and release.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B2				0	en-ZA	For paragraph and character styles, you can drag-and-drop onto the respective icon in the Styles and Formatting window. You do not need to open that style category in advance.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B5				0	en-ZA	You can also drag-and-drop a frame into the Styles and Formatting window to create a new frame style: Click the frame, wait a moment with the mouse button pressed down, but without moving the mouse, then drag to the Styles and Formatting window and drop the frame onto the Frame Styles icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149988				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05140000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Adding Line Numbers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150101				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>line numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; line numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs;line numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines of text; numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbering; lines\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; line numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>marginal numbers on text pages\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150101				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"numbering_lines\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/numbering_lines.xhp\" name=\"Adding Line Numbers\"\>Adding Line Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3149842				0	en-ZA	$[officename] can insert line numbers in an entire document or to selected paragraphs in your document. Line numbers are included when you print your document. You can specify the line numbering interval, the starting line number, and whether to count blank lines or lines in frames. You can also add a separator between line numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id7184972				0	en-ZA	Line numbers are not available in HTML format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153410				0	en-ZA	To Add Line Numbers to an Entire Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3149640				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Line Numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>Show numbering\</emph\>, and then select the options that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3145101				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156241				0	en-ZA	To Add Line Numbers to Specific Paragraphs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3156264				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Line Numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153385				0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>Show numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3154248				0	en-ZA	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+T\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>F11\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> to open the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, and then click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3154853				0	en-ZA	Right-click the "Default" paragraph style and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150222				0	en-ZA	All paragraph styles are based on the "Default" style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150931				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Numbering\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150956				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Line Numbering\</item\>               \<emph/\>area, clear the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Include this paragraph in line numbering\</item\>               \<emph/\>check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150520				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3151077				0	en-ZA	Select the paragraph(s) where you want to add the line numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3151096				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Paragraph\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\>               \<emph/\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153733				0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>Include this paragraph in line numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153758				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3146864				0	en-ZA	You can also create a paragraph style that includes line numbering, and apply it to the paragraphs that you want to add line numbers to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146880				0	en-ZA	To Specify the Starting Line Number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150703				0	en-ZA	Click in a paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150721				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Paragraph\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\>               \<emph/\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3148389				0	en-ZA	Select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Include this paragraph in line numbering\</item\>               \<emph/\>check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3148414				0	en-ZA	Select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Restart at the paragraph\</item\>               \<emph/\>check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153779				0	en-ZA	Enter a line number in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Start with\</item\>               \<emph/\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153804				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153934				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06180000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Line Numbering\"\>Tools - Line Numbering\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153960				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030800.xhp\" name=\"Format - Paragraph - Numbering\"\>Format - Paragraph - Numbering\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id2212591				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Setting_up_a_Style_for_Numbering_Lines_in_Code_Listings\"\>Wiki page about numbering paragraphs by styles\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Finding and Replacing in Writer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	bm_id1163670				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>finding; text/text formats/styles/objects\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>replacing; text and text formats\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>styles;finding\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>searching, see also finding\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>text formats; finding\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>formats; finding and replacing\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>searching; formats\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>objects;finding by Navigator\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Asian languages;search options\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id8568681				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"finding\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/finding.xhp\"\>Finding and Replacing in Writer\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id611285				0	en-ZA	In text documents you can find words, formatting, styles, and more. You can navigate from one result to the next, or you can highlight all results at once, then apply another format or replace the words by other text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id6226081				0	en-ZA	The Find & Replace dialogue				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6702780				0	en-ZA	To find text within the whole document, open the Find & Replace dialogue without any active text selection. If you want to search only a part of your document, first select that part of text, then open the Find & Replace dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158970				0	en-ZA	To Find Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6957304				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2164677				0	en-ZA	Enter the text to find in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id5684072				0	en-ZA	Either click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4377269				0	en-ZA	When you click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>, Writer will show you the next text that is equal to your entry. You can watch and edit the text, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again to advance to the next found text. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1371807				0	en-ZA	If you closed the dialogue, you can press a key combination (Ctrl+Shift+F) to find the next text without opening the dialogue. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id924100				0	en-ZA	Alternatively, you can use the icons at the lower right of the document to navigate to the next text or to any other object in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9359416				0	en-ZA	When you click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find All\</item\>, Writer selects all text that is equal to your entry. Now you can for example set all found text to bold, or apply a character style to all at once.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id5891598				0	en-ZA	To Replace Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1780755				0	en-ZA	Unlike searching text, replacing text cannot be restricted to the current selection only.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2467421				0	en-ZA	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4286935				0	en-ZA	Enter the text to search in the \<emph\>Search for \</emph\>text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9959410				0	en-ZA	Enter the text to replace the found text in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id24109				0	en-ZA	Either click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> or \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id703451				0	en-ZA	When you click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>, Writer will search the whole document for the text in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, starting at the current cursor position. When text is found, Writer highlights the text and waits for your response. Click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> to replace the highlighted text in the document with the text in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box. Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> to advance to the next found text without replacing the current selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7540818				0	en-ZA	When you click \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>, Writer replaces all text that matches your entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id9908444				0	en-ZA	To Find Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8413953				0	en-ZA	You want to find all text in your document to which a certain Paragraph Style is assigned, for example the "Heading 2" style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2696920				0	en-ZA	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id896938				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9147007				0	en-ZA	Check \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for Styles\</item\>.\<br/\>The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for\</item\> text box now is a list box, where you can select any of the Paragraph Styles that are applied in the current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id679342				0	en-ZA	Select the style to search for, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3231299				0	en-ZA	To Find Formats				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8087405				0	en-ZA	You want to find all text in your document to which a certain direct character formatting is assigned. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3406170				0	en-ZA	Finding formats only finds direct character attributes, it does not find attributes applied as part of a style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2448805				0	en-ZA	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4542985				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4679403				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7783745				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id5597094				0	en-ZA	More options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9919431				0	en-ZA	The similarity search can find text that is almost the same as your search text. You can set the number of characters that are allowed to differ.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8533280				0	en-ZA	Check the \<emph\>Similarity search\</emph\> option and optionally click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to change the settings. (Setting all three numbers to 1 works fine for English text.)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4646748				0	en-ZA	When you have enabled Asian language support under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</emph\>, the Find & Replace dialogue offers options to search Asian text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id2489394				0	en-ZA	The Navigator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9934385				0	en-ZA	The Navigator is the main tool for finding and selecting objects. You can also use the Navigator to move and arrange chapters, providing an outline view to your document. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4159062				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Navigator\</emph\> to open the Navigator window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7421796				0	en-ZA	Use the Navigator for inserting objects, links and references within the same document or from other open documents. See the \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/navigator.xhp\"\>Navigator\</link\> guide for more information.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6417432				0	en-ZA	Click the icon with the blue circle at the bottom right part of your document to open the small \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4639728				0	en-ZA	Use the small Navigation window to quickly jump to the next object or find the next text in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Indexes Covering Several Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153418				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>indexes;multiple documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>multiple documents;indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>merging;indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>master documents;indexes\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153418				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"indices_multidoc\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_multidoc.xhp\" name=\"Indexes Covering Several Documents\"\>Indexes Covering Several Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155872				0	en-ZA	There are several ways to create an index that spans several documents:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	en-ZA	Create an \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120210.xhp\" name=\"index in each individual document\"\>index in each individual document\</link\>, copy and paste the indexes into a single document, and then edit them.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3147118				0	en-ZA	Select each index, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Section\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Section\</item\>\</link\>, and then enter a name for the index. In a separate document, choose\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Section\</item\>, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link\</item\>, click the browse button (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>), and then locate and insert a named index section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150230				0	en-ZA	Create a \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010001.xhp\" name=\"master document\"\>master document\</link\>, add as subdocuments the files that you want to include in the index, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Index and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Inserting Page Numbers in Footers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155624				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>footers; with page numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages; numbers and count of\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page numbers; footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbering;pages\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155624				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"footer_pagenumber\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footer_pagenumber.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Page Numbers in Footers\"\>Inserting Page Numbers in Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id8230842				0	en-ZA	You can easily insert a page number field in the footer of your document. You can also add a page count to the footer, for example, in the form "Page 9 of 12"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	hd_id7867366				0	en-ZA	To Insert a Page Number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3150508				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\> and select the page style that you want to add the footer to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Page Number\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3153155				0	en-ZA	If you want, you can align the page number field as you would text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	hd_id2988677				0	en-ZA	To Additionally Add a Page Count				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3155532				0	en-ZA	Click in front of the page number field, type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Page\</item\> and enter a space; click after the field, enter a space and then type \<item type=\"literal\"\>of\</item\> and enter another space.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3155554				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Page Count\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Inserting a Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155919				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>running titles in headers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>floating titles in headers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>headers; chapter information\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>chapter names in headers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>names; chapter names in headers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155919				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"header_with_chapter\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_with_chapter.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer\"\>Inserting a Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	en-ZA	Before you can insert chapter information into a header or footer, you must first set the outline numbering options for the paragraph style that you want to use for chapter titles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154244				0	en-ZA	To Create a Paragraph Style for Chapter Titles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155874				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155898				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, select the paragraph style that you want to use for chapter titles, for example, "Heading 1".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147124				0	en-ZA	Select the numbering style for the chapter titles in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Number\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, for example, "1,2,3...".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150219				0	en-ZA	Type "Chapter" followed by a space in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Before\</item\>               \<emph/\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150245				0	en-ZA	Enter a space in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>After\</item\>               \<emph/\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150949				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150505				0	en-ZA	To Insert the Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150527				0	en-ZA	Apply the paragraph style that you defined for chapter titles to the chapter headings in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153729				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Header\</item\>               \<emph/\>or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Footer\</item\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153762				0	en-ZA	Click in the header or footer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3146863				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\> and click the\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Document\</item\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153175				0	en-ZA	Click "Chapter" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\>               \<emph/\>list and "Chapter number and name" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\>               \<emph/\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147065				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147095				0	en-ZA	The header on every page that uses the current page style automatically displays the chapter name and number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Navigating and Selecting With the Keyboard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159260				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>text; navigating and selecting with keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>navigating; in text, with keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>selecting;text, with keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>keyboard; navigating and selecting in text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159260				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"text_nav_keyb\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_nav_keyb.xhp\" name=\"Navigating and Selecting With the Keyboard\"\>Navigating and Selecting With the Keyboard\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3155179				0	en-ZA	You can navigate through a document and make selections with the keyboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id1031200810571916				0	en-ZA	To move the cursor, press the key or key combination given in the following table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id1031200810571929				0	en-ZA	To select the characters under the moving cursor, additionally hold down the Shift key when you move the cursor.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3155918				0	en-ZA	Key				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3155870				0	en-ZA	Function				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3156220	25			0	en-ZA	                  \<emph\>+\</emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\<emph\>Command key\</emph\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>Ctrl key\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	en-ZA	Right, left arrow keys				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	en-ZA	Moves the cursor one character to the left or to the right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418				0	en-ZA	Moves the cursor one word to the left or to the right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3149629				0	en-ZA	Up, down arrow keys				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3149949				0	en-ZA	Moves the cursor up or down one line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3149972				0	en-ZA	(\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>) Moves the current paragraph up or down.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3149624				0	en-ZA	Home				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3149871				0	en-ZA	Moves the cursor to the beginning of the current line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3145108				0	en-ZA	Moves the cursor to the beginning of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3149586				0	en-ZA	Home				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3156237				0	en-ZA	In a table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3156260				0	en-ZA	Moves the cursor to the beginning of the contents in the current cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3145409				0	en-ZA	Moves the cursor to the beginning of the contents of the current cell. Press again to move the cursor to the first cell in the table. Press again to move the cursor to the beginning of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3154410				0	en-ZA	End				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3153372				0	en-ZA	Moves the cursor to the end of the current line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3154235				0	en-ZA	Moves the cursor to the end of the document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3154262				0	en-ZA	End				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3154850				0	en-ZA	In a table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3154873				0	en-ZA	Moves to the end of the contents in the current cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3155894				0	en-ZA	Moves the cursor to the end of the contents of the current cell. Press again to move the cursor to the last cell in the table. Press again to move the cursor to the end of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3155944				0	en-ZA	PgUp				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3148678				0	en-ZA	Scrolls up one page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3148701				0	en-ZA	Moves the cursor to the header.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3149998				0	en-ZA	PgDn				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3153018				0	en-ZA	Scroll down one page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3148949				0	en-ZA	Moves the cursor to the footer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Inserting Cross-References				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145087				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>references; inserting cross-references\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cross-references; inserting and updating\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>OLE objects;cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>draw objects;cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145087				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"references\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/references.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Cross-References\"\>Inserting Cross-References\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3159263				0	en-ZA	Cross-references allow you to jump to specific text passages and objects in a single document. A cross-reference consists of a target and a reference that are inserted as \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields.xhp\" name=\"fields\"\>fields\</link\> in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3155860				0	en-ZA	Objects with captions and bookmarks can be used as targets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149833				0	en-ZA	Cross-Referencing Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149846				0	en-ZA	Before you can insert a cross-reference, you must first specify the targets in your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156105				0	en-ZA	To Insert a Target				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153408				0	en-ZA	Select the text that you want to use as a target for the cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153125				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149634				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list, select “Set Reference”.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149614				0	en-ZA	Type a name for the target in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box. The selected text is displayed in the \<emph\>Value\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3145110				0	en-ZA	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>. The name of the target is added to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Selection\</item\>               \<emph/\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257				0	en-ZA	Leave the dialogue open and proceed to the next section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153370				0	en-ZA	To Create a Cross-Reference to a Target				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id7032074				0	en-ZA	Position the cursor in the text where you want to insert a cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id7796868				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\> to open the dialogue, if it is not open already.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153392				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, select "Insert Reference".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list, select the target that you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3154856				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Insert reference to\</emph\> list, select the format for the cross-reference. The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"format\"\>format\</link\> specifies the type of information that is displayed as the cross-reference. For example, "Reference" inserts the target text, and "Page" inserts the page number where the target is located. For footnotes the footnote number is inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\> when finished.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149980				0	en-ZA	Cross-Referencing an Object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149992				0	en-ZA	You can cross-reference most objects in your document, such as graphics, drawing objects, OLE objects, and tables, so long as they have a caption. To add a caption to an object, select the object, and then choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Caption\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Caption\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3147123				0	en-ZA	Click in the document where you want to insert the cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150212				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150236				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, select the caption category of the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150942				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list, select the caption number of the object that you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150968				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Insert reference to\</emph\> list, select the format of the cross-reference. The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"format\"\>format\</link\> specifies the type of information that is displayed as the cross-reference. For example, "Reference" inserts the caption category and caption text of the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150535				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3151092				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\> when finished.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151115				0	en-ZA	Updating Cross-References				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153594				0	en-ZA	To manually update the cross-references in a document, press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id7321390				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>View - Fields\</emph\> to switch between viewing the reference names and the reference contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153407				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>page styles; left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>blank pages with alternating page styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>empty page with alternating page styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages; left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; even/odd pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>title pages; page styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>First Page page style\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Left Page page style\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>even/odd pages;formatting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153407				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"even_odd_sdw\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/even_odd_sdw.xhp\" name=\"Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages\"\>Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3154265				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3155876\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_designerdialog.png\" width=\"0.1862in\" height=\"0.1862in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155876\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147126				0	en-ZA	$[officename] can automatically apply alternating page styles on even (left) and odd pages (right) in your document. For example, you can use page styles to display different headers and footers on even and odd pages. The current page style is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\> at the bottom of the workplace.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id8194219				0	en-ZA	To Set Up Alternating Page Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150526				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\>               \<emph/\>icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153153				0	en-ZA	In the list of page styles, right-click "Left Page" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153179				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145267				0	en-ZA	Select "Right Page" in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145299				0	en-ZA	In the list of page styles, right-click "Right Page" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	en-ZA	Select "Left Page" in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155561				0	en-ZA	Go to the first page in your document, and double-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles in the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155588				0	en-ZA	To add a header to one of the page styles, choose\<emph/\>         \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Header\</item\>, and choose the page style that you want to add the header to. In the header frame, type the text that you want to use as the header.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147772				0	en-ZA	To add a footer to one of the page styles, choose\<emph/\>         \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Footer\</item\>, and choose the page style that you want to add the footer to. In the footer frame, type the text that you want to use as a footer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	en-ZA	If you do not want to have a header or a footer on the title page of your document, apply the "First Page" style to the title page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id888698				0	en-ZA	To Suppress the Printout of Empty Pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3394573				0	en-ZA	If two even or two odd pages directly follow each other in your document, Writer will insert an empty page by default. You can suppress those automatically generated empty pages from printing and from exporting to PDF.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id7594225				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id8147221				0	en-ZA	Remove the check mark from \<emph\>Print automatically inserted blank pages\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145596				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04010000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Break dialogue\"\>Insert Break dialogue\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\jump2statusbar.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Going to Specific Bookmark				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\jump2statusbar.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145778				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>bookmarks; positioning cursor\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>jumping;to bookmarks\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\jump2statusbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145778				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"jump2statusbar\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/jump2statusbar.xhp\" name=\"Going to Specific Bookmark\"\>Going to Specific Bookmark\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\jump2statusbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178	31			0	en-ZA	To go to a specific bookmark in your document, \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>hold down Ctrl and click \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>right-click\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> in the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> field on the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\>, and then choose the bookmark.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\jump2statusbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04040000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Bookmark\"\>Insert Bookmark\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Word Completion for Text Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148882				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>automatic word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>completion of words\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>word completion;using/disabling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>disabling;word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>switching off;word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deactivating;word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>refusing word completions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rejecting word completions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"word_completion\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/word_completion.xhp\"\>Word Completion for Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076F				0	en-ZA	$[officename] collects words that you frequently use in the current session. When you later type the first three letters of a collected word, $[officename] automatically completes the word. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346	91			0	en-ZA	If there is more than one word in the AutoCorrect memory that matches the three letters that you type, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to cycle through the available words. To cycle in the opposite direction, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+Tab. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078D				0	en-ZA	 To Accept/Reject a Word Completion				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN10794				0	en-ZA	By default, you accept the word completion by pressing the Enter key. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079B				0	en-ZA	 To reject the word completion, continue typing with any other key. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079E				0	en-ZA	 To Switch off the Word Completion 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A5				0	en-ZA	 Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options - Word Completion\</item\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AD				0	en-ZA	 Clear \<emph\>Enable word completion\</emph\> . 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_id7504806				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/word_completion_adjust.xhp\"\>Fine-Tuning the Word Completion\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Modifying Numbering in a Numbered List				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149637				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>numbering; removing/interrupting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>bullet lists; interrupting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lists;removing/interrupting numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;numbers in lists\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>interrupting numbered lists\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;starting numbers in lists\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149637				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"numbering_paras\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/numbering_paras.xhp\" name=\"Modifying Numbering in a Numbered List\"\>Modifying Numbering in a Numbered List\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3145092				0	en-ZA	You can remove the numbering from a paragraph in a numbered list or change the number that a numbered list starts with.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id2172612				0	en-ZA	If you want numbered headings, use the \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\> menu command to assign a numbering to a paragraph style. Do not use the Numbering icon on the Formatting toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145107				0	en-ZA	To Remove the Number From a Paragraph in a Numbered List				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3156248				0	en-ZA	Click in front of the first character of the paragraph that you want to remove the numbering from.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3153366				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154856				0	en-ZA	To Change the Number That a Numbered List Starts With				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3155877				0	en-ZA	Click anywhere in the numbered list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3148691	22			0	en-ZA	Enter the number you want the list to start with in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Start \</item\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>at\</item\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3147116				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id6943571				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Setting_up_a_Style_for_Numbering_Lines_in_Code_Listings\"\>Wiki page about numbering paragraphs by styles\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Printing Register-true				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	bm_id4825891				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>rows; register-true text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines of text; register-true\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages;register-true\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs;register-true\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>register-true;pages and paragraphs\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>spacing;register-true text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;register-true text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10652				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"registertrue\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/registertrue.xhp\"\>Printing Register-true\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065E				0	en-ZA	To Set a Document to Register-True Printing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10665				0	en-ZA	Select the whole document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10669				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page - Page\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10671				0	en-ZA	Select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Register-true\</item\> checkbox and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10678				0	en-ZA	All the paragraphs in the document will be printed register-true, unless otherwise specified.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067B				0	en-ZA	To Exempt Paragraphs From Register-True Printing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10685				0	en-ZA	Select all the paragraphs you want to exempt, then choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068C				0	en-ZA	Open the Styles and Formatting window, click the Paragraph Style you want to exempt, right-click that style, choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>. In the dialogue, click the \<emph\>Indents & Spacing\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10698				0	en-ZA	Clear the \<emph\>Register-true\</emph\> checkbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AA				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030100.xhp\"\>Register-true\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_small.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Printing Multiple Pages on One Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_small.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149694				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>multi-page view of documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages;printing multiple on one sheet\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>overviews;printing multi-page view\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing;multiple pages per sheet\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>reduced printing of multiple pages\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_small.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149694				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"print_small\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/print_small.xhp\" name=\"Printing Multiple Pages on One Sheet\"\>Printing Multiple Pages on One Sheet\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_small.xhp	0	help	par_id3149829				0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Page Layout\</emph\> tab page of the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Print\</item\> dialogue, you have the option to print multiple pages on one sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_small.xhp	0	help	par_id3156098				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Page Layout\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_small.xhp	0	help	par_id3155055				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_small.xhp	0	help	par_id3149603				0	en-ZA	To print two pages side by side on the same sheet, select "2" in the \<emph\>Pages per sheet\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_small.xhp	0	help	par_id3153388	22			0	en-ZA	To print multiple pages on the same sheet, select the number of pages per sheet and optionally set the order of pages. The small preview shows the arrangement of pages. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_small.xhp	0	help	par_id3154841				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_small.xhp	0	help	par_id3150004				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/main0210.xhp\" name=\"File - Page Preview\"\>File - Page Preview\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
