helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149832				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>multi-column text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; multi-column\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns; on text pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text columns\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sections; columns in/use of\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149832				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"sections\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/sections.xhp\" name=\"Using Sections\"\>Using Sections\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3153128				0	en-ZA	Sections are named blocks of text, including graphics or objects, that you can use in a number of ways:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149284				0	en-ZA	To prevent text from being edited.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149630				0	en-ZA	To show or hide text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149647				0	en-ZA	To reuse text and graphics from other $[officename] documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	en-ZA	To insert sections of text that uses a different column layout than the current page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149855				0	en-ZA	A section contains at least one paragraph. When you select a text and create a section, a paragraph break is automatically inserted at the end of the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	en-ZA	You can insert sections from a text document, or an entire text document as a section into another text document. You can also insert sections from a text document as links in another text document, or in the same document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3153367	39			0	en-ZA	To insert a new paragraph immediately before or after a section, click in front or behind the section, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154242				0	en-ZA	Sections and Columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	en-ZA	You can insert sections into an existing section. For example, you can insert a section containing two columns into a section that contains one column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3154845				0	en-ZA	A section layout, for example on the number of columns, has priority over the page layout defined in a page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3155883				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#dde\" name=\"DDE\"\>DDE\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Removing Words From a User-Defined Dictionary				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147688				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>user-defined dictionaries; removing words from\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>custom dictionaries; removing words from\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;words in user-defined dictionaries\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147688				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"delete_from_dict\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/delete_from_dict.xhp\" name=\"Removing Words From a User-Defined Dictionary\"\>Removing Words From a User-Defined Dictionary\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	par_id3153417				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Writing Aids\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	par_id3151391				0	en-ZA	Select the user-defined dictionary that you want to edit in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>User-defined\</item\>               \<emph/\>list, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	en-ZA	Select the word that you want to delete in the \<emph\>Word\</emph\> list, and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145084				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>fill format mode\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying; styles, by fill format mode\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>brush for copying styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles; transferring\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text formats; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145084				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"stylist_fillformat\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/stylist_fillformat.xhp\" name=\"Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode\"\>Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	en-ZA	You can quickly apply styles, such as paragraph and character styles, in your document by using the Fill Format Mode in the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3156114				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153128				0	en-ZA	Click the icon of the style category that you want to apply.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090	17			0	en-ZA	Click the style, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Fill Format Mode\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149644\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fillstyle.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149644\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Styles and Formatting\</item\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153371				0	en-ZA	Move the mouse pointer to where you want to apply the style in the document, and click. To apply the style to more than one item, drag to select the items, and then release.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3154263				0	en-ZA	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Esc\</item\> when finished.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3159259				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05140000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Creating a Bibliography				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149687				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>indexes;creating bibliographies\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>databases;creating bibliographies\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>bibliographies\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>entries;bibliographies\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>storing bibliographic information\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149687				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"indices_literature\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_literature.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Bibliography\"\>Creating a Bibliography\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3155864				0	en-ZA	A bibliography is a list of works that you reference in a document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153402				0	en-ZA	Storing Bibliographic Information				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	en-ZA	$[officename] stores bibliographic information in a bibliography database, or in an individual document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154244				0	en-ZA	To Store Information in the Bibliography Database				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3155872				0	en-ZA	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02250000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Bibliography Database\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Bibliography Database\</emph\>\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3155900				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Record\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3147123				0	en-ZA	Type a name for the bibliography entry in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Short name\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, and then add additional information to the record in the remaining boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3150219	66			0	en-ZA	Close the\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Bibliography Database\</item\> window. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150242				0	en-ZA	To Store Bibliographic Information in an Individual Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3150945				0	en-ZA	Click in your document where you want to add the bibliography entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3150964				0	en-ZA	Choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120300.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Indexes and Tables - Bibliography Entry\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Bibliography Entry\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3150525				0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>From document content\</emph\> and click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3153738				0	en-ZA	Type a name for the bibliography entry in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Short name\</item\>               \<emph/\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3153763				0	en-ZA	Select the publication source for the record in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, and then add additional information in the remaining boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3146873				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3146897				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert Bibliography Entry\</item\>               \<emph/\>dialogue, click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>, and then \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150741				0	en-ZA	Inserting Bibliography Entries From the Bibliography Database				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3148402				0	en-ZA	Click in your document where you want to add the bibliography entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3148421				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Bibliography Entry\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3153231				0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>From bibliography database\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3147059				0	en-ZA	Select the name of the bibliography entry that you want to insert in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Short name\</item\>               \<emph/\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3147085				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120300.xhp\" name=\"Bibliography Database\"\>Bibliography Database\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id6367076				0	en-ZA	Some external tools exist that can interact with %PRODUCTNAME. One example is called \<link href=\"http://bibus-biblio.sourceforge.net/wiki/index.php/Main_Page\"\>Bibus\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Thesaurus				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145576				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>thesaurus; related words\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>related words in thesaurus\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>spelling in thesaurus\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>dictionaries; thesaurus\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lexicon, see thesaurus\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>synonyms in thesaurus\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>searching;synonyms\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145576				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"using_thesaurus\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_thesaurus.xhp\" name=\"Thesaurus\"\>Thesaurus\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3149820				0	en-ZA	You can use the thesaurus to look up synonyms or related terms.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3155920				0	en-ZA	Click in the word that you want to look up or replace.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3155867				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Language - Thesaurus\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F7.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3149848				0	en-ZA	In the Alternatives list, click an entry to copy that related term to the "Replace with" text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3153136				0	en-ZA	Optionally double-click an entry to look up related terms for that entry. On your keyboard, you can also press the arrow up or down keys to select an entry. Then press Return to replace, or press the spacebar to look up.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3149644				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3156263				0	en-ZA	Initially, the thesaurus uses the language of the selected word in the document, if a thesaurus library for that language is installed. The title bar of the Thesaurus dialogue displays the language in use.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3145113				0	en-ZA	To look up the word in a different language, click the Language button, and select one of the installed thesaurus languages. A thesaurus library may not be available for all installed languages. You can install languages with a thesaurus library from the \<link href=\"http://extensions.services.openoffice.org/\"\>Extensions\</link\> web page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3196263				0	en-ZA	If a thesaurus library is installed for the language of a word, the context menu of the word shows a Synonyms submenu. Select any of the terms from the submenu to replace the word.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3154392				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06020000.xhp\" name=\"Thesaurus\"\>Thesaurus\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Resizing Rows and Columns in a Text Table 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156108				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"table_sizing\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_sizing.xhp\" name=\"Resizing Rows and Columns in a Text Table\"\>Resizing Rows and Columns in a Text Table\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3153140				0	en-ZA	You can resize the width of table cells and columns, as well as change the height of table rows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145109				0	en-ZA	Changing the Width of Columns and Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149574				0	en-ZA	To Change the Width of a Column				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3156246				0	en-ZA	Rest the mouse pointer over the column dividing line until the pointer becomes a separator icon, and then drag the line to a new location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3145390				0	en-ZA	Rest the mouse pointer over the column dividing line on the ruler until the pointer becomes a separator icon, and then drag the line to a new location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149993				0	en-ZA	To Change the Width of a Cell				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153014				0	en-ZA	Changing the Height of a Row				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id8478041				0	en-ZA	Resizing a Whole Table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3358867				0	en-ZA	To change the width and height of a table, do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id5366679				0	en-ZA	Click inside the table. In the rulers, drag the border between the white and the grey area to resize the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id1279030				0	en-ZA	Click inside the table. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table - Table Properties\</item\> to open a dialogue and set the properties to the numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id4190496				0	en-ZA	Tables within HTML pages do not offer the full range of properties and commands as tables in OpenDocument format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Inserting and Editing Footnotes or Endnotes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145819				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>endnotes;inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;footnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>organising;footnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footnotes; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145819				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"footnote_usage\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footnote_usage.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Footnotes or Endnotes\"\>Inserting and Editing Footnotes or Endnotes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	en-ZA	Footnotes reference more information about a topic at the bottom of a page and endnotes reference information at the end of the document. $[officename] automatically numbers the footnotes and endnotes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155881				0	en-ZA	To Insert a Footnote or Endnote				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3155903				0	en-ZA	Click in your document where you want to place the anchor of the note.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147120				0	en-ZA	Choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04030000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Footnote\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Footnote/Endnote\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150937				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\>               \<emph/\>area, select the format that you want to use. If you select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Character\</item\>, click the browse button (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) and select the character that you want to use for the footnote.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150508				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\>               \<emph/\>area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Footnote\</item\>               \<emph/\>or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Endnote\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150704				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150729				0	en-ZA	Type the note.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3148843				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3148857\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_insertfootnote.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148857\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3153176				0	en-ZA	You can also insert footnotes by clicking the \<emph\>Insert Footnote Directly\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155543				0	en-ZA	To Edit a Footnote or Endnote				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150167				0	en-ZA	The mouse pointer changes to a hand when you rest it over a footnote or endnote anchor in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3155563				0	en-ZA	To edit the text of a footnote or endnote, click in the note, or click the anchor for the note in the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145029				0	en-ZA	To change the format of a footnote, click in the footnote, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+T\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>F11\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> to open the Styles and Formatting window, right-click "Footnote" in the list, and then choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145062				0	en-ZA	To jump from the footnote or endnote text to the note anchor in the text, press PageUp.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145081				0	en-ZA	To edit the numbering properties of a footnote or endnote anchor, click in front of the anchor, and choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02150000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Footnote\"\>\<emph\>Edit - Footnote/Endnote\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147776				0	en-ZA	To change the formatting that $[officename] applies to footnotes and endnotes, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Footnotes\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Footnotes/Endnotes\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147813				0	en-ZA	To edit the properties of the text area for footnotes or endnotes, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, and then click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05040600.xhp\" name=\"Footnote\"\>\<emph\>Footnote\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147232				0	en-ZA	To remove a footnote, delete the footnote anchor in the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Adding Bullets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155186				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>bullet lists;turning on and off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; bulleted\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>bullets;adding and editing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;bullets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>removing;bullets in text documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;bulleting symbols\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155186				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"using_numbered_lists\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_numbered_lists.xhp\" name=\"Adding Bullets\"\>Adding Bullets\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	hd_id3291116				0	en-ZA	To Add Bullets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3149829				0	en-ZA	Select the paragraph(s) that you want to add bullets to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635	16			0	en-ZA	On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> Bar, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Bullets On/Off\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156108\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_defaultbullet.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156108\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3145403				0	en-ZA	To remove bullets, select the bulleted paragraphs, and then click the \<emph\>Bullets On/Off\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154403				0	en-ZA	To Format Bullets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3154416				0	en-ZA	To change the formatting of a bulleted list, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3153390				0	en-ZA	For example, to change the bulleting symbol, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Options\</item\> tab, click the browse button (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) next to \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Character\</item\>, and then select a special character. You can also click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Graphics\</item\> tab, and then click a symbol style in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Selection\</item\>         \<emph/\>area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Using AutoText				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155521				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>AutoText\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>networks and AutoText directories\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lists;AutoText shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing;AutoText shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;text blocks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text blocks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>blocks of text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155521				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"autotext\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/autotext.xhp\" name=\"Using AutoText\"\>Using AutoText\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	en-ZA	In $[officename] Writer, you can store text - also containing graphics, tables, and fields - as AutoText, so that you can quickly insert the text later on. If you want, you can also store formatted text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155539				0	en-ZA	To To Create an AutoText Entry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155560				0	en-ZA	Select the text, text with graphics, table, or field that you want to save as an AutoText entry. A graphic can only be stored if it is anchored as a character and is preceded and followed by at least one text character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155581				0	en-ZA	Choose\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - AutoText\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147761				0	en-ZA	Select the category where you want to store the AutoText.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147779				0	en-ZA	Type a name that is longer than four characters. This allows you to use the \<emph\>Display remainder of name as suggestion while typing\</emph\> AutoText option. If you want, you can modify the proposed shortcut.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147807	60			0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>AutoText\</emph\> button, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_idN10732				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Close\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147282				0	en-ZA	To Insert an AutoText Entry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145597				0	en-ZA	Click in your document where you want to insert an AutoText entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145615				0	en-ZA	Choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02120000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - AutoText\"\>\<emph\>Edit - AutoText\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145644				0	en-ZA	Select the AutoText that you want to insert, and then click\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145668	30			0	en-ZA	You can also type the shortcut for an AutoText entry, and then press F3, or click the arrow next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>AutoText\</item\>         \<emph/\>icon on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> bar, and then choose an AutoText entry. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155090	43			0	en-ZA	To quickly enter a %PRODUCTNAME Math formula, type \<item type=\"literal\"\>fn\</item\>, and then press F3. If you insert more than one formula, the formulae are sequentially numbered. To insert dummy text, type \<item type=\"literal\"\>dt\</item\>, and then press F3. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155115				0	en-ZA	To Print a List of AutoText Entries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155160				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> list, double-click "%PRODUCTNAME Macros - Gimmicks".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277				0	en-ZA	Select "AutoText" and then click \<emph\>Run\</emph\>. A list of the current AutoText entries is generated in a separate text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151304				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151327				0	en-ZA	Using AutoText in Network Installations				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151355				0	en-ZA	You can store AutoText entries in different directories on a network.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151370				0	en-ZA	For example, you can store "read-only" AutoText entries for your company on a central server, and user-defined AutoText entries in a local directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390				0	en-ZA	The paths for the AutoText directories can be edited in the configuration.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154960				0	en-ZA	Two directories are listed here. The first entry is on the server installation and the second entry is in the user directory. If there are two AutoText entries with the same name in both directories, the entry from the user directory is used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154995				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02120000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - AutoText\"\>Edit - AutoText\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155012				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040600.xhp\" name=\"Word Completion\"\>Word Completion\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Calculating and Pasting the Result of a Formula in a Text Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147692				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>pasting;results of formulae\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>clipboard;calculating in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulae;pasting results in text documents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147692				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"calculate_clipboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_clipboard.xhp\" name=\" Calculating and Pasting the Result of a Formula in a Text Document\"\> Calculating and Pasting the Result of a Formula in a Text Document\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156366				0	en-ZA	If your text already contains a formula, for example "12+24*2", $[officename] can calculate, and then paste the result of the formula in your document, without using the \<emph\>Formula Bar\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154250				0	en-ZA	Select the formula in the text. The formula can only contain numbers and operators and cannot contain spaces.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155496	38			0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Calculate\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Plus Sign (+).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id5172582				0	en-ZA	Place the cursor where you want to insert the result of the formula, and then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Paste\</item\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.\<br/\>The selected formula is replaced by the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Inserting a Horizontal Line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151178				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>horizontal lines\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines; inserting horizontal lines\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rules\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; horizontal lines\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151178				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"insert_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_line.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Horizontal Line\"\>Inserting a Horizontal Line\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2165898				0	en-ZA	This guide is about inserting graphical rules. You can also insert other lines, see \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/line_intext.xhp\"\>Drawing Lines in Text\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3149691				0	en-ZA	Click in the document where you want to insert the line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155186				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Horizontal Rule\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155902	83			0	en-ZA	Click the line that you want to insert in the \<emph\>Selection \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147124				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id5338602				0	en-ZA	The "Plain" type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5342265				0	en-ZA	If you select the "Plain" type of rules, an empty paragraph is inserted at the position of the cursor. This paragraph has the style "Horizontal Line", with a line as the lower border of the paragraph. You can edit that Paragraph Style to change the properties of all "Plain" rules in your document. For example you can set the left indent to 3 inches, or you can change the line style, thickness, and colour.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id707113				0	en-ZA	To edit the "Plain" rule style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5267494				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\> to open the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5074922				0	en-ZA	In the listbox at the bottom, select to display "All Styles".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8491470				0	en-ZA	Right-click the "Horizontal Line" paragraph style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3253883				0	en-ZA	Choose Modify.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3196203				0	en-ZA	For example, open the Borders tab page to set the thickness and style of the lines. Open the Indents & Spacing tab page to set the indents of the line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id8385265				0	en-ZA	The graphical type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2582476				0	en-ZA	Select any rule type below of the "Plain" rule type. This inserts a new paragraph at the position of the cursor. A picture showing a graphical horizontal line is inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150217				0	en-ZA	The inserted line is anchored to the current paragraph and centred between the page margins.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2111575				0	en-ZA	To edit the graphical line, right-click the line and choose \<emph\>Picture\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150231				0	en-ZA	You can also insert one of these lines by dragging it from the \<emph\>Rulers\</emph\> folder in the \<emph\>Gallery\</emph\> into the current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150944				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/gallery.xhp\" name=\"Gallery\"\>Gallery\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Wrapping Text Around Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154486				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>text wrap around objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>contour editor\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>contour wrap\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; formatting around objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; contour wrap\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects; contour wrap\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>wrapping text;editing contours\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editors;contour editor\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154486				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"wrap\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/wrap.xhp\" name=\"Wrapping Text Around Objects\"\>Wrapping Text Around Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	hd_id4792321				0	en-ZA	To Wrap Text Around an Object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3149696				0	en-ZA	Select the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Wrap\</emph\>, and then choose the wrapping style that you want to apply.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3155859				0	en-ZA	The current wrapping style is indicated by a bullet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149834				0	en-ZA	To Specify the Wrapping Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154079				0	en-ZA	Select the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Graphics\</emph\>, and then click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05060200.xhp\" name=\"Wrap\"\>\<emph\>Wrap\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153370				0	en-ZA	Set the options that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153386				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154247				0	en-ZA	To Change the Wrapping Contour of a Graphic				2002-02-02 02:02:02
