helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3156228				0	en-ZA	You can create a conditional text field that displays the word "pages" instead of "page" in conjunction with a page count field if your document contains more than one page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257				0	en-ZA	Place the cursor in your document where you want to insert the page count.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150513				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Page Count\</item\>, and then enter a space.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Functions\</item\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3153166				0	en-ZA	Click "Conditional text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\>               \<emph/\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
