helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromdraw.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155917				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>text; inserting pictures from Draw\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; inserting from Draw\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromdraw.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155917				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_fromdraw\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic_fromdraw.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Graphics From $[officename] Draw or Impress\"\>Inserting Graphics From $[officename] Draw or Impress\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromdraw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	en-ZA	Open the document where you want to insert the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromdraw.xhp	0	help	par_id3149640				0	en-ZA	Open the Draw or Impress document containing the object that you want to copy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromdraw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145098				0	en-ZA	Hold down \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl\</item\> and click and hold the object for a moment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromdraw.xhp	0	help	par_id3156250				0	en-ZA	Drag to the document where you want to insert the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Updating, Editing and Deleting Indexes and Tables of Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>indexes; editing/updating/deleting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; editing and deleting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating;indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"indices_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_edit.xhp\" name=\"Updating, Editing and Deleting Indexes and Tables of Contents\"\>Updating, Editing and Deleting Indexes and Tables of Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155856				0	en-ZA	Place the cursor in the index or table of contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155871				0	en-ZA	If you cannot place your cursor in the index or table of contents, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</item\>, and then select\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Enable\</item\> in the\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Cursor in protected areas\</item\> section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154248				0	en-ZA	Right-click and choose an editing option from the menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155872				0	en-ZA	You can also make changes directly to an index or table of contents. Right-click in the index or table of contents, choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Index/Table\</emph\> tab, and then clear the \<emph\>Protected from manual changes\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Outline Numbering				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147682				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>outlines;numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;heading numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>chapter numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>headings; numbering/paragraph styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbering;headings\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147682				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"chapter_numbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/chapter_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Outline Numbering\"\>Outline Numbering\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155605				0	en-ZA	You can modify the heading hierarchy or assign a level in the hierarchy to a custom paragraph style. You can also add chapter and section numbering to heading paragraph styles. By default, the "Heading 1" paragraph style is at the top of the outline hierarchy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155626				0	en-ZA	To Add Automatic Numbering to a Heading Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\>               \<emph/\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155891				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paragraph Style\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, select the heading style that you want to add chapter numbers to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3150513				0	en-ZA	In the\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbers\</item\> box, select the numbering style that you want to use, and then click\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CE				0	en-ZA	To Remove Automatic Outline Numbering From a Heading Paragraph				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D5				0	en-ZA	Click at the beginning of the text in the heading paragraph, after the number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D9				0	en-ZA	Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Backspace\</item\> key to delete the number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155552				0	en-ZA	To Use a Custom Paragraph Style as a Heading				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155571				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\>               \<emph/\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147758				0	en-ZA	Select the custom style in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147782	39			0	en-ZA	Click the heading level that you want to assign to the custom paragraph style in the\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Level\</item\> list. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147808				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Using Wildcards in Text Searches				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150099				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>wildcards, see regular expressions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>searching; with wildcards\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>regular expressions;searching\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>examples for regular expressions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>characters;finding all\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>invisible characters;finding\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraph marks;searching\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150099				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"search_regexp\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/search_regexp.xhp\"\>Using Wildcards in Text Searches\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200916345516				0	en-ZA	Wildcards or placeholders can be used to search for some unspecified or even invisible characters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155182				0	en-ZA	You can use wildcards when you find and replace text in a document. For example, "s.n" finds "sun" and "son".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Find & Replace\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id2142399				0	en-ZA	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>More Options\</item\> to expand the dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155861				0	en-ZA	Select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Regular expressions\</item\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149843				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for\</item\> box, type the search term and the wildcard(s) that you want to use in your search.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	en-ZA	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find All\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153401				0	en-ZA	Regular Expression Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149641				0	en-ZA	The wildcard for a single character is a period (.).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3153136				0	en-ZA	The wildcard for zero or more occurrences of the previous character is an asterisk. For example: "123*" finds "12" "123", and "1233".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149609				0	en-ZA	The wildcard combination to search for zero or more occurrences of any character is a period and asterisk (.*).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149854				0	en-ZA	The wildcard for the end of a paragraph is a dollar sign ($). The wildcard character combination for the start of a paragraph is a caret and a period (^.).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200916345545				0	en-ZA	The wildcard for a tab character is \\t.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	en-ZA	A search using a regular expression will work only within one paragraph. To search using a regular expression in more than one paragraph, do a separate search in each paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149875				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100001.xhp\" name=\"List of Wildcards\"\>List of Wildcards\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Adding or Deleting a Row or Column to a Table Using the Keyboard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156377				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>rows; inserting/deleting in tables by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns; inserting/deleting in tables by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; editing by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>keyboard;adding or deleting rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>splitting cells;by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>merging;cells, by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;rows/columns, by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;rows/columns, by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156377				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"table_cells\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_cells.xhp\" name=\"Adding or Deleting a Row or Column to a Table Using the Keyboard\"\>Adding or Deleting a Row or Column to a Table Using the Keyboard\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149487				0	en-ZA	You can add or delete rows or columns in tables as well as split or merge table cells using the keyboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155906				0	en-ZA	To insert a new row in a table, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Insert, and then press the up or down arrow key. You can also move the cursor to the last cell in the table, and then press Tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	en-ZA	To insert a new column, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Insert, and then press the left or right arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3156096				0	en-ZA	To split a table cell instead of adding a column, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Insert, and then hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while you press the left or right arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3153408				0	en-ZA	To delete a row, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Delete, and then press the up or down arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149626				0	en-ZA	To delete a column, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Delete, and then press the left or the right arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	en-ZA	To merge a table into an adjacent cell, place the cursor in the cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Delete, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, and then press the left or the right arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Editing Sections				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	en-ZA	You can protect, hide, and convert sections to normal text in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154224				0	en-ZA	Choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02170000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Sections\"\>\<emph\>Format - Sections\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153397				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3156255				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02170000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Sections\"\>Format - Sections\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id973540				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/protection.xhp\"\>Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME Writer\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text_display.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Displaying Hidden Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text_display.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148856				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>hidden text; displaying\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>displaying;hidden text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text_display.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148856				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"hidden_text_display\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hidden_text_display.xhp\" name=\"Displaying Hidden Text\"\>Displaying Hidden Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text_display.xhp	0	help	par_id5659962				0	en-ZA	If you have a text that was hidden by defining a condition with a variable, you have several options to display the hidden text. Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text_display.xhp	0	help	par_id3152777				0	en-ZA	Enable the check mark at \<emph\>View - Hidden Paragraphs\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text_display.xhp	0	help	par_id3153902				0	en-ZA	Double-click in front of the variable that you used to define the condition for hiding the text, and enter a different value for the variable.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text_display.xhp	0	help	par_id3147114				0	en-ZA	Double-click in front of the hidden text field or the hidden paragraph field, and change the condition statement.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text_display.xhp	0	help	par_id1865901				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hidden_text.xhp\" name=\"Hiding Text\"\>Hiding Text\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text_display.xhp	0	help	par_id3147029				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14020000.xhp\" name=\"List of Operators\"\>List of Operators\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Defining Borders for Objects 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146957				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>objects; defining borders\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>borders; for objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames; around objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>charts;borders\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures;borders\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>OLE objects;borders\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;object borders\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"border_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/border_object.xhp\" name=\"Defining Borders for Objects\"\>Defining Borders for Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	en-ZA	In Writer, you can define borders around OLE objects, plug-ins, diagrams/charts, graphics and frames. The name of the menu to be used depends on the object selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145673				0	en-ZA	To Set a Predefined Border Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	en-ZA	Select the object for which you want to define a border.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	4			0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>OLE-Object\</emph\> toolbar or \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> toolbar to open the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3159176				0	en-ZA	Click one of the predefined border styles. This replaces the current border style of the object with the selected style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152474				0	en-ZA	To Set a Customized Border Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	en-ZA	Select the table cells that you want to modify.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3156344	9			0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - (object name) – Borders\</item\>.\<br/\>Replace (object name) with the actual name of the object type you selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area select the edge(s) that you want to appear in a common layout. Click on an edge in the preview to toggle the selection of an edge.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	en-ZA	Select a line style and colour for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3125865				0	en-ZA	Repeat the last two steps for every border edge.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3150447				0	en-ZA	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to Contents\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Positioning Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147828				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>objects;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>positioning;objects (guide)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>anchors;options\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>centering;images on HTML pages\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147828				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"anchor_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/anchor_object.xhp\" name=\"Positioning Objects\"\>Positioning Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3147251				0	en-ZA	You can use anchors to position an object, graphic, or frame in a document. An anchored item remains in place, or moves when you modify the document. The following anchoring options are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145599				0	en-ZA	Anchoring				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145622				0	en-ZA	Effect				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145650				0	en-ZA	As character				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151181				0	en-ZA	Anchors the selected item as a character in the current text. If the height of the selected item is greater than the current font size, the height of the line containing the item is increased.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_idN10674				0	en-ZA	To centre an image on an HTML page, insert the image, anchor it "as character", then centre the paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151212				0	en-ZA	To character				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151235				0	en-ZA	Anchors the selected item to a character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155071				0	en-ZA	To paragraph				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155094				0	en-ZA	Anchors the selected item to the current paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155122				0	en-ZA	To page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155144				0	en-ZA	Anchors the selected item to the current page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	en-ZA	To frame				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145697				0	en-ZA	Anchors the selected item to the surrounding frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145715				0	en-ZA	When you insert an object, graphic, or frame, an anchor icon appears where the item is anchored. You can position an anchored item by dragging the item to another location. To change the anchoring options of an item, right-click the item, and then choose an option from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Anchor\</item\>         \<emph/\>submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Changing the Outline Level of Numbered and Bulleted Lists				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145078				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>tab stops; inserting in lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbering; changing the level of\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists;changing levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>levels;changing outline levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bullet lists;changing levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lowering outline levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rising outline levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;outline levels\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145078				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"insert_tab_innumbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_tab_innumbering.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Outline Level of Numbered and Bulleted Lists\"\>Changing the Outline Level of Numbered and Bulleted Lists\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155909				0	en-ZA	To move a numbered or bulleted paragraph down one outline level, click at the beginning of the paragraph, and then press Tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155859				0	en-ZA	To move a numbered or bulleted paragraph up one outline level, click at the beginning of the paragraph, and then press Shift+Tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3153403	8			0	en-ZA	To insert a tab between the number or bullet and the paragraph text, click at the beginning of the paragraph, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Changing the Default Template				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155913				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>default templates;defining/resetting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defaults; templates\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>templates; default templates\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text documents;default templates\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155913				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"template_default\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/template_default.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Default Template\"\>Changing the Default Template\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3145569				0	en-ZA	The default template contains the default formatting information for new text documents. If you want, you can create a new template and use it as the default template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	hd_id6414990				0	en-ZA	To Create a Default Template				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149838				0	en-ZA	Create a document and the content and formatting styles that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3156101				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149283				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>New Template\</emph\> box, type a name for the new template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3153409				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Categories\</item\> list, select "My Templates", and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3153140				0	en-ZA	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"File - Templates - Organize\"\>\<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149952				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Templates\</item\> list, double-click the "My Templates" folder.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149970				0	en-ZA	Right-click the template that you created, and choose \<emph\>Set as Default Template\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149620				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149867				0	en-ZA	To Reset the Default Template				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3145102				0	en-ZA	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"File - Templates - Organize\"\>\<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149582				0	en-ZA	Right-click a text file in any of the two lists, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Reset Default Template - Text Document\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3156245				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Creating Numbered or Bulleted Lists as You Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147407				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>numbering; lists, while typing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>bullet lists;creating while typing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lists;automatic numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers;lists\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic bullets/numbers; AutoCorrect function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>bullets; using automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; automatic numbering\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147407				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"auto_numbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/auto_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Creating Numbered or Bulleted Lists as You Type\"\>Creating Numbered or Bulleted Lists as You Type\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155525				0	en-ZA	$[officename] can automatically apply numbering or bullets as you type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154243				0	en-ZA	To Enable Automatic Numbering and Bulleting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3152830	29			0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Options\</item\> tab, and then select “Apply numbering – symbol”.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3152867				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - AutoCorrect\</emph\>, and ensure that \<emph\>While Typing\</emph\> is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id2357860				0	en-ZA	The automatic numbering option is only applied to paragraphs that are formatted with the "Default", "Text body", or "Text body indent" paragraph style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152897				0	en-ZA	To Create a Numbered or Bulleted List While You Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147773				0	en-ZA	Type 1., i., or I. to start a numbered list. Type * or - to start a bulleted list. You can also type a right parenthesis after the number instead of a period , for example, 1) or i).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147794				0	en-ZA	Enter a space, type your text, and then press Enter. The new paragraph automatically receives the next number or bullet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147814				0	en-ZA	Press Enter again to finish the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147287				0	en-ZA	You can start a numbered list with any number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3154083				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06050000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Numbering/Bullets\"\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Defining Number Ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>numbering;quotations/similar items\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"number_sequence\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/number_sequence.xhp\" name=\"Defining Number Ranges\"\>Defining Number Ranges\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	par_id3155918				0	en-ZA	You can automatically number similar items, such as quotations, in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	par_id3149829				0	en-ZA	Type the text that you want to assign numbering to, for example, "Quotation Number ".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	par_id3155048				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Variables\</item\>               \<emph/\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	par_id3156240				0	en-ZA	Click "Number range" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\>               \<emph/\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	en-ZA	Type "Quotation" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Name\</item\>               \<emph/\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	par_id3153387				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	par_id3155886				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Creating and Applying Page Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	bm_id7071138				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>page styles;creating and applying\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;page styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles;for pages\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155182	1			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"pagestyles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Creating and Applying Page Styles\"\>Creating and Applying Page Styles\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149846				0	en-ZA	$[officename] uses page styles to specify the layout of a page, including the page orientation, background, margins, headers, footers, and text columns. To change the layout of an individual page in a document, you must create and apply a custom page style to the page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071A				0	en-ZA	         \<embedvar href=\"text/swriter/guide/pageorientation.xhp#pageorientation\"/\>      				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_idN10722				0	en-ZA	         \<embedvar href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagebackground.xhp#pagebackground\"/\>      				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156109				0	en-ZA	To Define a New Page Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153411	3			0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>               \<emph\>.\</emph\>            				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153133				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149641				0	en-ZA	In the list of page styles, right-click an item, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149614				0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab, type a name in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145110				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154252				0	en-ZA	Use the tabs in the dialogue to set the layout options for the page style, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154851				0	en-ZA	To Apply a Page Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154873				0	en-ZA	Click in the page that you want to apply the page style to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3155888				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>, and then click the\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Style\</item\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	en-ZA	Double-click a name in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148701				0	en-ZA	To Apply a Page Style to a New Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147122				0	en-ZA	Click in the document where you want a new page to start.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150235				0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>Page break\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150939				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, select the page style that you want to apply to the page that follows the manual break.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150965				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Using the Direct Cursor				2002-02-02 02:02:02
