helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_id3155908				0	en-ZA	The direct cursor allows you to enter text anywhere on a page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_id3155921				0	en-ZA	To set the behaviour of the direct cursor, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A3				0	en-ZA	On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools\</item\> bar, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Direct Cursor\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149846\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_shadowcursor.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149846\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	en-ZA	Click in a free space in the text document. The mouse pointer changes to reflect the alignment that will be applied to the text that you type:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C8				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id5471987\" src=\"res/helpimg/dircursleft.png\" width=\"0.1457in\" height=\"0.3228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5471987\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> Align left				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E4				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id5730253\" src=\"res/helpimg/dircurscent.png\" width=\"0.2398in\" height=\"0.3228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5730253\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> Centered				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN10700				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id6953622\" src=\"res/helpimg/dircursright.png\" width=\"0.1563in\" height=\"0.3228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6953622\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> Align right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071D				0	en-ZA	Type your text. %PRODUCTNAME automatically inserts the required number of blank lines, and, if the options are enabled, tabs and spaces.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Creating Alphabetical Indexes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155911				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>concordance files;indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>indexes; alphabetical indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>alphabetical indexes\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155911				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"indices_index\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_index.xhp\" name=\"Creating Alphabetical Indexes\"\>Creating Alphabetical Indexes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	en-ZA	Click in your document where you want to insert the index.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3154252				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3155884				0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Index/Table\</emph\> tab, select "Alphabetical Index" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3147114				0	en-ZA	If you want to use a concordance file, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Concordance file\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Options\</item\>               \<emph/\>area, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File\</item\> button, and then locate an existing file or create a new concordance file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3150223	28			0	en-ZA	Set the formatting options for the index, either on the current tab, or on any of the other tabs of this dialogue. For example, if you want to use single letter headings in your index, click the \<emph\>Entries\</emph\> tab, and then select \<emph\>Alphabetical delimiter\</emph\>. To change the formatting of levels in the index, click the \<emph\>Styles\</emph\> tab. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3150946				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3150502				0	en-ZA	To update the index, right-click in the index, and then choose \<emph\>Update Index/Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3152760				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120250.xhp\" name=\"Creating a concordance file\"\>Creating a concordance file\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Printing a Brochure				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	bm_id6743064				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>printing; individual brochures\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>booklet printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>brochures; printing individual\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F6				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"print_brochure\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/print_brochure.xhp\"\>Printing a Brochure\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	en-ZA	You can print a Writer document as a brochure or a booklet. That is, Writer prints two pages on each side of the paper, so that when you fold the paper, you can read the document as a book.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DE				0	en-ZA	When you create a document that you want to print as a brochure, use portrait orientation for the pages. Writer applies the brochure layout when you print the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	en-ZA	To Print a Brochure				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10621				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B6				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialogue, click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070E				0	en-ZA	In the properties dialogue for your printer, set the paper orientation to landscape.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_id8947416				0	en-ZA	If your printer prints duplex, and because brochures always print in landscape mode, you should use the "duplex - short edge" setting in your printer setup dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10628				0	en-ZA	Return to \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialogue, and click the \<emph\>Page Layout\</emph\> tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN1062C				0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>Brochure\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10740				0	en-ZA	For a printer that automatically prints on both sides of a page, specify to include "All pages".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10630				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EA				0	en-ZA	If %PRODUCTNAME prints the pages in the wrong order, open the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab page, select \<emph\>Print in reverse page order\</emph\>, and then print the document again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Page Numbers 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id5918759				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>page numbers;inserting/defining/formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page styles;page numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>starting page numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;page numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;starting page numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;page numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles;page numbers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id413830				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"pagenumbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagenumbers.xhp\" name=\"Page Numbers\"\>Page Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1617175				0	en-ZA	In Writer, a page number is a field that you can insert into your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id6091494				0	en-ZA	To Insert Page Numbers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id8611102				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Page Number\</emph\> to insert a page number at the current cursor position.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6604510				0	en-ZA	If you see the text "Page number" instead of the number, choose \<emph\>View - Field names\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2678914				0	en-ZA	However, these fields will change position when you add or remove text. So it is best to insert the page number field into a header or footer that has the same position and that is repeated on every page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id614642				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Header - (name of page style)\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Footer - (name of page style)\</item\> to add a header or footer to all pages with the current page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id2551652				0	en-ZA	To Start With a Defined Page Number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6111941				0	en-ZA	Now you want some more control on page numbers. You are writing a text document that should start with page number 12.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id5757621				0	en-ZA	Click into the first paragraph of your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2632831				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Text flow\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4395275				0	en-ZA	In the Breaks area, enable \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. Enable \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\> just to be able to set the new \<emph\>Page number\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1654408				0	en-ZA	The new page number is an attribute of the first paragraph of the page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id7519150				0	en-ZA	To Format the Page Number Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id9029206				0	en-ZA	You want roman page numbers running i, ii, iii, iv, and so on.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3032319				0	en-ZA	Double-click directly before the page number field. You see the \<emph\>Edit Fields\</emph\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id9139378				0	en-ZA	Select a number format and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id5051728				0	en-ZA	Using Different Page Number Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1558885				0	en-ZA	You need some pages with the roman numbering style, followed by the remaining pages in another style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1541184				0	en-ZA	In Writer, you will need different page styles. The first page style has a footer with a page number field formatted for roman numbers. The following page style has a footer with a page number field formatted in another look.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id18616				0	en-ZA	Both page styles must be separated by a page break. In Writer, you can have automatic page breaks and manually inserted page breaks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6138492				0	en-ZA	An \<emph\>automatic page break\</emph\> appears at the end of a page when the page style has a different "next style".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4569231				0	en-ZA	For example, the "First Page" page style has "Default" as the next style. To see this, you may press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+T\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>F11\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> to open the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Styles and Formatting\</item\> window, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> icon, right-click the First Page entry. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify\</item\> from the context menu. On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Organizer\</item\> tab, you can see the "next style".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id291451				0	en-ZA	A \<emph\>manually inserted page break\</emph\> can be applied without or with a change of page styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3341776				0	en-ZA	If you just press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\>, you apply a page break without a change of styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id5947141				0	en-ZA	If you choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual break\</emph\>, you can insert a page break without or with a change of style or with a change of page number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1911679				0	en-ZA	It depends on your document what is best: to use a manually inserted page break between page styles, or to use an automatic change. If you just need one title page with a different style than the other pages, you can use the automatic method:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id9364909				0	en-ZA	To Apply a Different Page Style to the First Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4473403				0	en-ZA	Click into the first page of your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4313791				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4331797				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4191717				0	en-ZA	Double-click the "First Page" style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2318796				0	en-ZA	Now your title page has the style "First Page", and the next pages automatically have the "Default" style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id399182				0	en-ZA	You can now for example insert a footer for the "Default" page atyle only, or insert footers in both page styles, but with differently formatted page number fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id5298318				0	en-ZA	To Apply a Manually Inserted Page Style Change				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id7588732				0	en-ZA	Click at the start of the first paragraph on the page where a different page style will be applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id95828				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>. You see the \<emph\>Insert Break\</emph\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3496200				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\> list box, select a page style. You may set a new page number, too. Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id7599108				0	en-ZA	The selected page style will be used from the current paragraph to the next page break with style. You may need to create the new page style first.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Animating Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151182				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>text animation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>effects; text animation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>animations;text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151182				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"text_animation\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_animation.xhp\" name=\"Animating Text\"\>Animating Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3145080				0	en-ZA	You can only animate text that is contained in a drawing object, such as rectangles, lines, or text objects. For example, draw a rectangle, then double-click the rectangle and enter your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	en-ZA	Select the drawing object containing the text that you want to animate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Object - Text Attributes\</item\>, and then click the\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Animation\</item\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149819				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Effect\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, select the animation that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	en-ZA	Set the properties of the effect, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Selecting Tables, Rows, and Columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	bm_id7693411				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>selecting;tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables;selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns;selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows;selecting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F0				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"table_select\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_select.xhp\"\>Selecting Tables, Rows, and Columns\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN1060E				0	en-ZA	You can select a table in a text document with a keyboard or with a mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	en-ZA	To select a table with the keyboard, move the cursor into the table, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+A until all the cells are selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10633				0	en-ZA	To select a table with the mouse, move the mouse pointer to a position just above and left of the table. The mouse pointer becomes a diagonal arrow. Click to select the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10637				0	en-ZA	To select a row or column with the mouse, point to a position just left of the row or above the column. The mouse pointer becomes an arrow. Click to select the row or column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Calculating Across Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154248				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; across multiple text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;calculating across\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154248				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"calculate_multitable\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_multitable.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Across Tables\"\>Calculating Across Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147773				0	en-ZA	You can perform calculations that span across more than one table in a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147795				0	en-ZA	Open a text document, insert two tables, and type numbers in a few cells in both tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147815				0	en-ZA	Place your cursor in an empty cell in one of the tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147833				0	en-ZA	Press F2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula Bar\</item\>, enter the function that you want to perform, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=SUM\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	en-ZA	Click in a cell containing a number, press the plus sign (+), and then click in a different cell containing a number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
