helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155916	1			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"fields_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields_enter.xhp\" name=\"Adding Input Fields\"\>Adding Input Fields\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153409				0	en-ZA	An input field is a variable that you can click in a document to open a dialogue where you can edit the variable.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145776				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>               \<emph/\>and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Functions\</item\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155620				0	en-ZA	Click “Input field”\<emph/\>in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154257				0	en-ZA	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>               \<emph/\>and type the text for the variable.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155888				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150708				0	en-ZA	To quickly open all input fields in a document for editing, press Ctrl+Shift+F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_delete.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Deleting Tables or the Contents of a Table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_delete.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149489				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>deleting; tables or table contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; deleting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_delete.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149489				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"table_delete\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_delete.xhp\" name=\"Deleting Tables or the Contents of a Table\"\>Deleting Tables or the Contents of a Table\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155918				0	en-ZA	You can delete a table from your document, or delete the contents of the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155863				0	en-ZA	To delete a whole table, click in the table, and then choose \<emph\>Table - Delete - Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	en-ZA	To delete the contents of a table, click in the table, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+A until all cells are selected, and then press Delete or Backspace.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Adding Exceptions to the AutoCorrect List				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152887				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; adding exceptions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>exceptions; AutoCorrect function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>abbreviations\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>capital letters;avoiding after specific abbreviations\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152887				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"autocorr_except\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/autocorr_except.xhp\" name=\"Adding Exceptions to the AutoCorrect List\"\>Adding Exceptions to the AutoCorrect List\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3154254	11			0	en-ZA	You can prevent AutoCorrect from correcting specific abbreviations or words that have mixed capital letters and lowercase letters. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3155576				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Exceptions\</item\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3147762				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3147786	19			0	en-ZA	Type the abbreviation followed by a period in the \<emph\>Abbreviations (no subsequent capital) \</emph\>box and click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3147812	20			0	en-ZA	Type the word in the \<emph\>Words with TWo INitial CApitals \</emph\>box and click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3144875	17			0	en-ZA	To quickly undo an AutoCorrect replacement, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z. This also adds the word or abbreviation that you typed to the AutoCorrect exceptions list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Adding Numbering				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147418				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>numbering;paragraphs, on and off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; numbering on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;numbered lists\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;numbering\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147418	15			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"using_numbered_lists2\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_numbered_lists2.xhp\" name=\"Adding Numbering\"\>Adding Numbering\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	hd_id4188970				0	en-ZA	To Add Numbering to a List				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	en-ZA	Select the paragraph(s) that you want to add numbering to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149968	24			0	en-ZA	On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> Bar, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering On/Off\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3153125\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_defaultnumbering.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153125\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149573				0	en-ZA	To change the formatting and the hierarchy of a numbered list, click in the list, and then open the \<emph\>Bullets and Numbering\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	par_id3153365				0	en-ZA	To remove numbering, select the numbered paragraphs, and then click the \<emph\>Numbering On/Off\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154233				0	en-ZA	To Format a Numbered List				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	par_id3154246				0	en-ZA	To change the formatting of a numbered list, click in the list, then choose \<emph\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Moving and Copying Text in Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155919				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>sections;moving and copying\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>moving; text sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying; text sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pasting;cut/copied text sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>mouse;moving and copying text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155919				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"dragdroptext\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/dragdroptext.xhp\" name=\"Moving and Copying Text in Documents\"\>Moving and Copying Text in Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152994				0	en-ZA	Select the text that you want to move or copy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155606				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154236				0	en-ZA	To move the selected text, drag the text to a different location in the document and release. While you drag, the mouse pointer changes to include a grey box.\<br/\>\<image id=\"img_id3153148\" src=\"res/helpimg/movedata.png\" width=\"0.3335in\" height=\"0.3335in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153148\"\>Mouse cursor moving data\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154257	14			0	en-ZA	To copy the selected text, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while you drag. The mouse pointer changes to include a plus sign (+).\<br/\>\<image id=\"img_id3152868\" src=\"res/helpimg/copydata.png\" width=\"0.3335in\" height=\"0.3335in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152868\"\>Mouse cursor copying data\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Working with Master Documents and Subdocuments				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145246				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>Navigator;master documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>master documents;creating/editing/exporting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>subdocuments;creating/editing/removing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>removing;subdocuments\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>indexes; master documents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145246				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"globaldoc_howtos\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/globaldoc_howtos.xhp\"\>Working with Master Documents and Subdocuments\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id1522873				0	en-ZA	A master document lets you manage large documents, such as a book with many chapters. The master document can be seen as a container for individual \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer files. The individual files are called subdocuments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153127				0	en-ZA	To Create a Master Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149634				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149873				0	en-ZA	If you are creating a new master document, the first entry in the Navigator should be a \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text\</item\>               \<emph/\>entry. Type an introduction or enter some text. This ensures that after having edited an existing style in the master document, you see the changed style when viewing the subdocuments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145114				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Navigator\</item\> for master documents (should open automatically, else press F5 to open), click and hold the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>               \<emph/\>icon, and do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153382				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154242				0	en-ZA	To Edit a Master Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	en-ZA	Use the Navigator for rearranging and editing the subdocuments in a master document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3155879				0	en-ZA	To open a subdocument for editing, double-click the name of the subdocument in the Navigator.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3155931				0	en-ZA	To remove a subdocument from the master document, right-click the subdocument in the Navigator list and choose \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>. The subdocument file is not deleted, only the entry in the Navigator is removed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148677				0	en-ZA	To add text to a master document, right-click an item in the Navigator list, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Text\</emph\>. A text section is inserted before the selected item in the master document where you can type the text that you want. You cannot insert text next to an existing text entry in the Navigator.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149982				0	en-ZA	To reorder the subdocuments in a master document, drag a subdocument to a new location in the Navigator list. You can also select a subdocument in the list, and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Move down\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Move up\</item\>               \<emph/\>icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153022				0	en-ZA	To add an index, such as a table of contents, right-click in the Navigator list, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Index\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148949				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3148959\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20246.png\" width=\"0.1862in\" height=\"0.1862in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148959\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153632				0	en-ZA	To update an index in a master document, select the index in the Navigator, and then click the \<emph\>Update\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C40				0	en-ZA	When you insert an object like a frame or a picture into a master document, do not anchor the object "to page". Instead, set the anchor "to paragraph" on the \<emph\>Format - (Object type) - Type\</emph\> tab page, and then set the object's position relative to "Entire Page" in the \<emph\>Horizontal\</emph\> and \<emph\>Vertical\</emph\> list boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153656				0	en-ZA	To Start Each Subdocument on a New Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3152760				0	en-ZA	Ensure that each subdocument starts with a heading that uses the same paragraph style, for example "Heading 1".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	en-ZA	In the master document, choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153907				0	en-ZA	Right-click "Heading 1" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3147124				0	en-ZA	Click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Flow\</item\>               \<emph/\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149770				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Breaks\</item\>               \<emph/\>area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>, and then select “Page”\<emph/\>in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\>               \<emph/\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	en-ZA	If you want each subdocument to start on an odd page, select \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>, and select "Right page" in the box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145205				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145228				0	en-ZA	To Export a Master Document as a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Text Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3150315				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Export\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148580				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> list, select a text document file format and click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id8371227				0	en-ZA	The subdocuments will be exported as sections. Use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Sections\</item\> to unprotect and remove sections, if you prefer a plain text document without sections.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3154382				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator in master mode\"\>Navigator in master mode\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	About Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145576				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>fields;updating/viewing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating;fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Help tips;fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>properties;fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>disabling;field highlighting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;field shadings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>viewing;fields\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145576				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"fields\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields.xhp\" name=\"About Fields\"\>About Fields\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154246				0	en-ZA	Fields are used for data that changes in a document, such as the current date or the total number of pages in a document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154262				0	en-ZA	Viewing Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3150509				0	en-ZA	Fields consist of a field name and the field content. To switch the field display between the field name or the field content, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03090000.xhp\" name=\"View - Fields\"\>\<emph\>View - Field Names\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3150536				0	en-ZA	To display or hide field highlighting in a document, choose \<emph\>View - Field Shadings\</emph\>. To permanently disable this feature, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - Appearance\</emph\>, and clear the check box in front of \<emph\>Field shadings\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3152885				0	en-ZA	To change the colour of field shadings, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01012000.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - Appearance\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>$[officename] - Appearance\</item\>\</link\>\</emph\>, locate the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Field shadings\</item\> option, and then select a different colour in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Color setting\</item\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153166				0	en-ZA	Field Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3153180				0	en-ZA	Most field types in a document, including database fields, store and display variable values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155533				0	en-ZA	The following field types execute an action when you click the field:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155582				0	en-ZA	Field Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147760				0	en-ZA	Property				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147789				0	en-ZA	Placeholder				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147812				0	en-ZA	Opens a dialogue to insert the object for which the placeholder was set.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147216				0	en-ZA	Insert Reference				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147239				0	en-ZA	Moves the mouse pointer to the reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147267				0	en-ZA	Run macro				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147290				0	en-ZA	Runs a macro.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145614				0	en-ZA	Input Field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145637				0	en-ZA	Opens a dialogue to edit the contents of the field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3151244				0	en-ZA	Placeholder, hidden text, insert reference, variable, database, and user-defined fields display a help tip when you rest the mouse pointer over the field in a document. To enable this feature, ensure that the Extended Tips\<emph/\>option (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>What's This?\</item\>) is selected in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Help\</item\> menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155937				0	en-ZA	Updating Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155963				0	en-ZA	To update all of the fields in a document, press F9, or choose \<emph\>Edit - Select All\</emph\>, and then press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155984				0	en-ZA	To update a field that was inserted from a database, select the field, and then press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155845				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; inserting from Navigator\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; hyperlinks from Navigator\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cross-references; inserting with Navigator\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Navigator;inserting hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155845				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"hyperlinks\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hyperlinks.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator\"\>Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	en-ZA	You can insert a cross-reference as a hyperlink in your document using the Navigator. You can even cross-reference items from other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> documents. If you click the hyperlink when the document is opened in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>, you are taken to the cross-referenced item.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149833				0	en-ZA	Open the document(s) containing the items you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3148846				0	en-ZA	On the Standard bar, click the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3156108				0	en-ZA	Click the arrow next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Drag Mode\</item\> icon, and ensure that \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert as Hyperlink\</item\>               \<emph/\>is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	en-ZA	In the list at the bottom of the Navigator, select the document containing the item that you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153416				0	en-ZA	In the Navigator list, click the plus sign next to the item that you want to insert as a hyperlink.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153133				0	en-ZA	Drag the item to where you want to insert the hyperlink in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635				0	en-ZA	The name of the item is inserted in the document as an underlined hyperlink.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Updating Styles From Selections				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155915				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>Stylist, see Styles and Formatting window\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles; updating from selections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>templates; updating from selections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Styles and Formatting window; updating from selections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating; styles, from selections\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155915				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"stylist_update\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/stylist_update.xhp\" name=\"Updating Styles From Selections\"\>Updating Styles From Selections\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3149838				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3156107				0	en-ZA	Click the icon of the style category that you want to update.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3149283				0	en-ZA	In the document, click from where you want to copy the updated style. For example, click a paragraph to which you applied some manual formatting that you want to copy now.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3153402				0	en-ZA	In the Styles and Formatting window, click the style that you want to update.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3153119				0	en-ZA	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon and choose \<emph\>Update Style\</emph\> from the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id0310200910360780				0	en-ZA	Only the manually formatted attributes of the text at the cursor position in the document will be added to the style that is selected in the Styles and Formatting window. Any attributes that were applied as part of a style will not be added to the updated style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3155498				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05140000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Modifying Rows and Columns by Keyboard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155856				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>table mode selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>proportional distribution of tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative distribution of table cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; adapting the width by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; adapting the width by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>keyboard;modifying the behaviour of rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>behaviour of rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155856				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"tablemode\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/tablemode.xhp\" name=\"Modifying the Behavior of Rows and Columns for Table\"\>Modifying Rows and Columns by Keyboard\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149835				0	en-ZA	When you insert or delete cells, rows or columns in a table, the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Behavior of rows/columns\</item\> options determine how the neighbouring elements are affected. For example, you can only insert new rows and columns into a table with fixed row and column dimensions if space permits.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id7344279				0	en-ZA	Note that these properties are valid only for changes to the column width that are made using the keyboard. Using the mouse, you are free to make any column width changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3156110				0	en-ZA	To set the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Behavior of rows/columns\</item\> options for tables in text documents, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Table\</item\>, or use the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Fixed\</item\>, \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Fixed/Proportional\</item\>, and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Variable\</item\> icons on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table\</item\> Bar. There are three display modes for tables:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149638				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Fixed\</emph\> - changes only affect the adjacent cell, and not the entire table. For example, when you widen a cell, the adjacent cell becomes narrower, but the width of the table remains constant.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149613				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Fixed, proportional\</emph\> - changes affect the entire table, and wide cells shrink more than narrow cells. For example, when you widen a cell, the adjacent cells become proportionally narrower, but the width of the table remains constant.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149864				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Variable\</emph\> - changes affect the table size. For example, when you widen a cell, the width of the table increases.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Inserting a Graphic From a File				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154896				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>pictures; inserting by dialogue\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; pictures, by dialogue\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154896				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_dialog\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic_dialog.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Graphic From a File\"\>Inserting a Graphic From a File\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3155914				0	en-ZA	Click in the document where you want to insert the graphic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3155864				0	en-ZA	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/04140000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Picture - From File\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3156021				0	en-ZA	Locate the graphic file that you want to insert, and then click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	en-ZA	By default, the inserted graphic is centred above the paragraph that you clicked in.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\nonprintable_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Creating Non-printing Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\nonprintable_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148856				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>non-printing text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; non-printable\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\nonprintable_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148856				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"nonprintable_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/nonprintable_text.xhp\" name=\"Creating Non-printing Text\"\>Creating Non-printing Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\nonprintable_text.xhp	0	help	par_id4685201				0	en-ZA	To create text that is not to be printed do the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\nonprintable_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149789				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Frame\</item\> and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\nonprintable_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	en-ZA	Enter text in the frame and if you want, resize the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\nonprintable_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150242				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Frame/Object\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Options\</item\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\nonprintable_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145227				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> area, clear the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\nonprintable_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150320				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\nonprintable_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3138828				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hidden_text.xhp\" name=\"Hiding Text\"\>Hiding Text\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Using Smart Tags				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155622				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>options;smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>disabling;smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;smart tags\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3563951				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"smarttags\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/smarttags.xhp\"\>Using Smart Tags\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id368358				0	en-ZA	Smart Tags provide additional information and functionality to specified words in a Writer document. The available features can be different for different Smart Tags extensions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id9298379				0	en-ZA	Installing Smart Tags				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1827448				0	en-ZA	Smart Tags can be supplied as \<link href=\"text/shared/01/packagemanager.xhp\"\>extensions\</link\> to %PRODUCTNAME Writer. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id2508621				0	en-ZA	To install a Smart Tag, do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id3856013				0	en-ZA	Save the *.oxt extension file to your harddrive, then double-click the *.oxt file in your file manager. Alternatively, in %PRODUCTNAME choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Extension Manager\</item\> to open the Extension Manager, click Add and browse to the file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id7814264				0	en-ZA	Click a Smart Tag *.oxt file link on a web page and open the link with the default application. This requires a properly configured Web browser.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id8142338				0	en-ZA	Smart Tags Menu				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1917477				0	en-ZA	Any text in a Writer document can be marked with a Smart Tag, by default a magenta coloured underline. You can change the colour in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Appearance\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id192266				0	en-ZA	When you point to a Smart Tag, a tip help informs you to Ctrl-click to open the Smart Tags menu. If you don't use a mouse, position the cursor inside the marked text and open the context menu by Shift+F10.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1998962				0	en-ZA	In the Smart Tags menu you see the available actions that are defined for this Smart Tag. Choose an option from the menu. The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Smart Tags Options\</item\> command opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040700.xhp\"\>Smart Tags\</link\> page of Tools - Autocorrect Options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id2376476				0	en-ZA	To Enable and Disable Smart Tags				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id349131				0	en-ZA	When you have installed at least one Smart Tags extension, you see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040700.xhp\"\>Smart Tags\</link\> page in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Autocorrect Options\</item\>. Use this dialogue to enable or disable Smart Tags and to manage the installed tags.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1216467				0	en-ZA	Text that is recognised as a Smart Tag is not checked by the automatic spellcheck.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Selecting printer paper trays				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	bm_id6609088				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>selecting;paper trays\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paper tray selection\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155909				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"printer_tray\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/printer_tray.xhp\" name=\"Selecting printer paper trays\"\>Selecting Printer Paper Trays\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	en-ZA	Use page styles to specify different paper sources for different pages in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3149841				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3156108				0	en-ZA	Click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\>               \<emph/\>icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3155066				0	en-ZA	Right-click the page style in the list that you want to specify the paper source for, and then choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3153416				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paper tray\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, select the paper tray that you want to use.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3153140				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3149649				0	en-ZA	Repeat steps 1-5 for each page style that you want to specify the paper for.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3149616				0	en-ZA	Apply the page style to the pages that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3154260				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Creating and applying page styles\"\>Creating and applying page styles\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Spacing Between Footnotes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147683				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>spacing; endnotes/footnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>endnotes; spacing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footnotes; spacing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>borders;for footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines;footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147683				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"footnote_with_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footnote_with_line.xhp\" name=\"Spacing Between Footnotes\"\>Spacing Between Footnotes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3145808				0	en-ZA	If you want to increase the spacing between footnote or endnote texts, you can add a top and bottom border to the corresponding paragraph style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603				0	en-ZA	Click in a footnote or endnote.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155620				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3154251				0	en-ZA	Right-click the Paragraph Style that you want to modify, for example, "Footnote", and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155884				0	en-ZA	Click the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"Borders\"\>\<emph\>Borders\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147110				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Default\</item\>               \<emph/\>area, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Set Top and Bottom Borders Only\</item\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150931				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Line\</item\> area, click a line in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\>               \<emph/\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150961				0	en-ZA	Select "White" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Colour\</item\>               \<emph/\>box. If the background of the page is not white, select the colour that best matches the background colour.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150519				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area, clear the \<emph\>Synchronize\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150709				0	en-ZA	Enter a value in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Top\</item\>               \<emph/\>and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Bottom\</item\>               \<emph/\>boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150740				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3148846				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"Format - Paragraph - Borders\"\>Format - Paragraph - Borders\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Removing Line Breaks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149687				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>hard returns in pasted text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>line breaks;removing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting; line breaks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copies;removing line breaks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraph marks;removing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155916				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"removing_line_breaks\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/removing_line_breaks.xhp\"\>Removing Line Breaks\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	en-ZA	Use the AutoCorrect feature to remove line breaks that occur within sentences. Unwanted line breaks can occur when you copy text from another source and paste it into a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153413	3			0	en-ZA	This AutoCorrect feature only works on text that is formatted with the "Default" paragraph style. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153138	5			0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>               \<emph\>.\</emph\>            				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149645				0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab, ensure that \<emph\>Combine single line paragraphs if length greater than 50%\</emph\> is selected. To change the minimum percentage for the line length, double-click the option in the list, and then enter a new percentage.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3145093				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	en-ZA	Select the text containing the line breaks that you want to remove.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3156253				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Apply Style\</item\> box on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> bar, choose “Default”.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153388				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - AutoCorrect - Apply\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Defining Borders for Pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156136				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>pages;defining borders\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>borders; for pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames; around pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;page borders\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156136	15			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"border_page\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/border_page.xhp\" name=\"Defining Borders for Pages\"\>Defining Borders for Pages\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473				0	en-ZA	In Writer, you define borders for \<emph\>page styles\</emph\>, not individual pages. All changes made to borders apply to all pages that use the same page style. Note that page style changes cannot be undone by the Undo function in $[officename].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150503				0	en-ZA	To Set a Predefined Border Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page - Borders\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	en-ZA	Select one of the default border styles in the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3154046				0	en-ZA	Select a line style and colour for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472				0	en-ZA	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3156023				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	en-ZA	To Set a Customized Border Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3148663				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page - Borders\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area select the edge(s) that you want to appear in a common layout. Click on an edge in the preview to toggle the selection of an edge.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149				0	en-ZA	Select a line style and colour for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3156282				0	en-ZA	Repeat the last two steps for every border edge.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	en-ZA	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3145606				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Inserting Page Numbers of Continuation Pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145819				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>pages; continuation pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>next page number in footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>continuation pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page numbers; continuation pages\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145819				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"footer_nextpage\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footer_nextpage.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Page Numbers of Continuation Pages\"\>Inserting Page Numbers of Continuation Pages\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154242				0	en-ZA	You can easily insert the page number of the next page in a footer by using a field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	en-ZA	The page number is only displayed if the following page exists.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3155886				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\> and select the page style that you want to add the footer to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147109				0	en-ZA	Place the cursor in the footer and choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147134				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Fields\</emph\> dialogue, click the \<emph\>Document\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150955				0	en-ZA	Click 'Page' in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list and 'Next page' in the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150517				0	en-ZA	Click a numbering style in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\>               \<emph/\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537				0	en-ZA	If you select 'Text' in the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list, only the text that you enter in the \<emph\>Value\</emph\> box is displayed in the field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150727				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> to insert the field with the page number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_beforetable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Inserting Text Before a Table at the Top of Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_beforetable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149688				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>tables;start/end of document\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs;inserting before/after tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;paragraphs before/after tables\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_beforetable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149688				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"insert_beforetable\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_beforetable.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Text Before a Table at the Top of Page\"\>Inserting Text Before a Table at the Top of Page\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_beforetable.xhp	0	help	par_id3155923				0	en-ZA	If you want to insert text before a table that is at the top of a page, click in the first cell of the table, in front of any contents of that cell, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_beforetable.xhp	0	help	par_idN10612				0	en-ZA	To insert text after a table at the end of the document, go to the last cell of the table and press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Displaying the Result of a Table Calculation in a Different Table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153899				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;in text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; performing calculations in\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153899				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"calculate_intext2\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_intext2.xhp\" name=\"Displaying the Result of a Table Calculation in a Different Table\"\>Displaying the Result of a Table Calculation in a Different Table\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3154250				0	en-ZA	You can perform a calculation on cells in one table and display the result in a different table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150508				0	en-ZA	Open a text document, insert a table with multiple columns and rows, and then insert another table consisting of one cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150528				0	en-ZA	Enter numbers into some of the cells of the large table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155532				0	en-ZA	Place the cursor in the table with the single cell, and then press F2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155551				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula Bar\</item\>, enter the function that you want to perform, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=SUM\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155577				0	en-ZA	Click in a cell in the larger table that contains a number, press the plus sign (+), and then click in a different cell containing a number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155598				0	en-ZA	Press \<emph\>Enter\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3147776				0	en-ZA	If you want, you can format the table to behave as normal text. Insert the table into a frame, and then anchor the frame as a character. The frame remains anchored to the adjacent text when you insert or delete text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Automatically Check Spelling				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154265				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>spellcheck;AutoSpellcheck on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic spellcheck\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>checking spelling;while typing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>words;disabling spellcheck\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154265				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"auto_spellcheck\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/auto_spellcheck.xhp\" name=\"Automatically Check Spelling\"\>Automatically Check Spelling\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3154664				0	en-ZA	You can have $[officename] automatically check spelling while you type and underline possible misspelt words with a red wavy line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154678				0	en-ZA	To Check Spelling Automatically While You Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3155531	42			0	en-ZA	Activate the \<emph\>AutoSpellcheck \</emph\>icon on the Standard bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3155569	33			0	en-ZA	Right-click a word with a red wavy underline, and then choose a suggested replacement word from the list, or from the \<emph\>AutoCorrect \</emph\>submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147759	6			0	en-ZA	If you choose a word from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>AutoCorrect\</item\> submenu, the underlined word and the replacement word are automatically added to the AutoCorrect list for the current language. To view the AutoCorrect list, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools – AutoCorrect Options\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Replace\</item\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147819				0	en-ZA	You can also add the underlined word to your custom dictionary by choosing \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147220				0	en-ZA	To Exclude Words From the Spellcheck				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147263				0	en-ZA	Select the words that you want to exclude.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147282				0	en-ZA	Click the Language control on the Status bar to open a menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3145602				0	en-ZA	Choose “None (Do not check spelling)”.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3145648				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010401.xhp\" name=\"Creating a new dictionary.\"\>Creating a new dictionary.\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
