helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	HTML compatibility				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155132				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>$[officename] Basic scripts in HTML documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML;compatibility settings\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153821				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01030500.xhp\" name=\"HTML compatibility\"\>HTML compatibility\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156326				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:TABPAGE:RID_OFAPAGE_HTMLOPT\"\>Defines settings for HTML pages.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154897				0	en-ZA	Font sizes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3145673				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:NUMERICFIELD:RID_OFAPAGE_HTMLOPT:NF_SIZE7\"\>Use the spin buttons \<emph\>Size 1\</emph\> to \<emph\>Size 7\</emph\> to define the respective font sizes for the HTML <font size=1> to <font size=7> tags.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148943				0	en-ZA	Import				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385				0	en-ZA	Defines the settings for importing HTML documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id6065248				0	en-ZA	Use 'English (USA)' locale for numbers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id8023926				0	en-ZA	When importing numbers from an HTML page, the decimal separator and the thousands separator characters differ according to the locale of the HTML page. The clipboard however contains no information about the locale. For example, the characters "1.000" copied from a German Web page most possibly mean "one thousand" because the period is the thousands separator in a German locale. If copied from an English Web page, the same characters stand for the number 1 as in "one dot zero zero zero".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id7658314				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If not checked, numbers will be interpreted according to the setting in \<emph\>Language Settings - Language of - Locale setting\</emph\> in the Options dialogue box. If checked, numbers will be interpreted as 'English (USA)' locale.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	en-ZA	Import unknown HTML tags as fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149295				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:CHECKBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_HTMLOPT:CB_UNKNOWN_TAGS\"\>Mark this check box if you want \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#tags\" name=\"tags\"\>tags\</link\> that are not recognised by $[officename] to be imported as fields.\</ahelp\> For an opening tag, an HTML_ON field will be created with the value of the tag name. For a closing tag, an HTML_OFF will be created. These fields will be converted to tags in the HTML export.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148797				0	en-ZA	Ignore font settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149202	44			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:CHECKBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_HTMLOPT:CB_IGNORE_FONTNAMES\"\>Mark this check box to ignore all font settings when importing. The fonts that were defined in the HTML Page Style will be the fonts that will be used. \</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151177				0	en-ZA	Export				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:LISTBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_HTMLOPT:LB_EXPORT\"\>Defines the settings for exporting HTML documents.\</ahelp\> To export in HTML format select the \<emph\>HTML Document\</emph\> file type in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"Save As\"\>\<emph\>Save As\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue. You can find further instructions in the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000020.xhp\" name=\"Import and export filters\"\>Import and export filters\</link\> description.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3145606				0	en-ZA	To optimise the HTML export, select a browser or HTML standard from the Export box. If "$[officename] Writer" is selected, specific $[officename] Writer instructions are exported.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155132				0	en-ZA	$[officename] Basic				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:CHECKBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_HTMLOPT:CB_STARBASIC\"\>Mark this check box to include the $[officename] Basic instructions when exporting to HTML format.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150872				0	en-ZA	You must activate this option before you create the $[officename] Basic Script, since otherwise it will not be inserted. $[officename] Basic Scripts must be located in the header of the HTML document. Once you have created the macro in the $[officename] Basic IDE, it appears in the source text of the HTML document in the header.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149664				0	en-ZA	Display warning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150420				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:CHECKBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_HTMLOPT:CB_STARBASIC_WARNING\"\>If this field is marked, when exporting to HTML a warning is shown that %PRODUCTNAME Basic macros will be lost.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154729				0	en-ZA	Print layout				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156276				0	en-ZA	The HTML filter supports CSS2 (Cascading Style Sheets Level 2) for printing documents. These capabilities are only effective if print layout export is activated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144764				0	en-ZA	Copy local graphics to Internet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:CHECKBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_HTMLOPT:CB_LOCAL_GRF\"\>Mark this check box to automatically upload the embedded pictures to the Internet server when uploading using FTP. Use the \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> dialogue to save the document and enter a complete FTP URL as the file name in the Internet.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152960				0	en-ZA	Character set				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR_LISTBOX_RID_OFAPAGE_HTMLOPT_LB_CHARSET\"\>Select the appropriate character set for the export\</ahelp\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060600.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
