helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:OptionsTreeDialog\"\>This command opens a dialogue for a customised program configuration.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156344				0	en-ZA	All your settings are saved automatically. To expand an entry either double click this entry or click the plus sign. To collapse the entry, click the minus sign or double click the entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01000000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10607				0	en-ZA	You see only the entries that are applicable to the current document. If the current document is a text document, you see the %PRODUCTNAME Writer entry, and so on for all modules of %PRODUCTNAME. %PRODUCTNAME Impress and %PRODUCTNAME Draw are treated as the same in this dialogue. The common entries are always visible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OFADLG_TREELISTBOX\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select an entry to edit.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01000000.xhp	0	help	par_id1013200911280529				0	en-ZA	Note for Mac OS X users: The Help mentions the menu path Tools - Options at numerous places. Replace this path with %PRODUCTNAME - Preferences on your Mac OS X main menu. Both menu entries open the Options dialogue box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
