helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460	68			0	en-ZA	If \<emph\>Load user-specific settings with the document \</emph\>is not selected, the following user-specific settings still apply:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	en-ZA	Settings available in \<emph\>File - Print - Options\</emph\>,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153348				0	en-ZA	Name of Fax,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276				0	en-ZA	Spacing options for paragraphs before text tables,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148686				0	en-ZA	Information about automatic updating for links, field functions and charts,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153254				0	en-ZA	Information about working with Asian character formats.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153666				0	en-ZA	The following settings are \<emph\>always\</emph\> loaded with a document, whether or not this option is marked:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148946				0	en-ZA	Data source linked to the document and its view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id927152				0	en-ZA	Load printer settings with the document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id5684987				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If enabled, the printer settings will be loaded with the document. This can cause a document to be printed on a distant printer, if you do not change the printer manually in the Print dialogue. If disabled, your standard printer will be used to print this document. The current printer settings will be stored with the document whether or not this option is checked.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146794				0	en-ZA	Save				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154071				0	en-ZA	Edit document properties before saving				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SFXPAGE_SAVE_BTN_DOCINFO\"\>Specifies that the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialogue will appear every time you select the \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> command.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145606				0	en-ZA	Always create backup copy				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SFXPAGE_SAVE_BTN_BACKUP\"\>Saves the previous version of a document as a backup copy whenever you save a document. Every time \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> creates a backup copy, the previous backup copy is replaced. The backup copy gets the extension .BAK.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	en-ZA	To change the location of the backup copy, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\>, and then enter a new path for the backup file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154908				0	en-ZA	Save AutoRecovery information every				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149560				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SFXPAGE_SAVE_BTN_AUTOSAVE\"\>Specifies that \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> saves the information needed to restore all open documents in case of a crash. You can specify the saving time interval.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146147				0	en-ZA	Minutes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152460				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_NUMERICFIELD_RID_SFXPAGE_SAVE_ED_AUTOSAVE\"\>Specifies the time interval in minutes for the automatic recovery option.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153575				0	en-ZA	Save URLs relative to file system				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149484				0	en-ZA	This option allows you to select the default for \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#speichern\" name=\"relative\"\>relative\</link\> addressing of URLs in the file system and on the Internet. Relative addressing is only possible if the source document and the referenced document are both on the same drive.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	en-ZA	A relative address always starts from the directory in which the current document is located. In contrast, absolute addressing always starts from a root directory. The following table demonstrates the difference in syntax between relative and absolute referencing:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149413				0	en-ZA	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148455				0	en-ZA	File system				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	en-ZA	Internet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	en-ZA	relative				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147176				0	en-ZA	../images/img.jpg				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145652				0	en-ZA	../images/img.jpg				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	en-ZA	absolute				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154361				0	en-ZA	file:///c|/work/images/img.jpg				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148408				0	en-ZA	http://myserver.com/work/images/img.jpg				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145148				0	en-ZA	The Help tip always displays an absolute path. However, if a document is saved in HTML format, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> will enter a relative path if the appropriate check box is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155176				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SFXPAGE_SAVE_BTN_RELATIVE_FSYS\"\>Select this box for \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#speichern\" name=\"relative saving\"\>relative saving\</link\> of URLs in the file system.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155334				0	en-ZA	Save URLs relative to internet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155608				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SFXPAGE_SAVE_BTN_RELATIVE_INET\"\>Select this box for \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#speichern\" name=\"relative saving\"\>relative saving\</link\> of URLs to the Internet.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id2016968				0	en-ZA	Default file format and ODF settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id2659077				0	en-ZA	ODF format version				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id6944181				0	en-ZA	OpenOffice.org 3 and StarOffice 9 introduce new features which have to be saved using the \<link href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenDocument\"\>OpenDocument\</link\> format (ODF) version 1.2. The prior versions of OpenOffice.org 2 and StarOffice 8 support the file formats ODF 1.0/1.1. Those prior file formats cannot store all new features of the new software.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id886257				0	en-ZA	Current versions can open documents in ODF formats 1.0/1.1 and 1.2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id8892483				0	en-ZA	When you save a document, you can select whether to save the document in the format ODF 1.2, ODF 1.2 (Extended), or in the prior format ODF 1.0/1.1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id0915200911205367				0	en-ZA	Currently, the ODF 1.2 (Extended) format enables files of Draw and Impress to contain comments. Those comments can be inserted by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Comment\</item\> in the latest software version. The comments get lost when loading files into prior software versions that were saved by the latest software version.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id7198400				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Some companies or organizations may require ODF documents in the ODF 1.0/1.1 format. You can select that format to save in the listbox. This older format cannot store all new features, so the new format ODF 1.2 (Extended) is recommended where possible.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154920				0	en-ZA	Size optimisation for ODF format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150488				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SFXPAGE_SAVE_BTN_NOPRETTYPRINTING\"\>When saving the document, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> writes the XML data without indents and extra line breaks.\</ahelp\> This allows documents to be saved and opened more quickly, and the file size is smaller.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091E				0	en-ZA	Warn when not saving in ODF or default format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10922				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>You can choose to get a warning message when you save a document in a format that is not OpenDocument or which you did not set as default format in \<emph\>Load/Save - General\</emph\> in the Options dialogue box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3158444				0	en-ZA	You can choose which file format will be applied as the default when saving documents of various document types. If you always exchange your documents with other persons who use Microsoft Office, for example, you may specify here that %PRODUCTNAME only uses the Microsoft Office file formats as a default.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153270				0	en-ZA	Document type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150828				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SFXPAGE_SAVE_LB_APP\"\>Specifies the document type for which you want to define the default file format.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149527				0	en-ZA	Always save as				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149035				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SFXPAGE_SAVE_LB_FILTER\"\>Specifies how documents of the type selected on the left will always be saved as this file type. You may select another file type for the current document in the \<emph\>Save as\</emph\> dialogue.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\online_update.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Online Update				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\online_update.xhp	0	help	bm_id7657094				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>update options\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>online update options\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>options;online update\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>online updates; checking automatically\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>updates; checking automatically\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Internet; checking for updates\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\online_update.xhp	0	help	hd_id29297				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/online_update.xhp\"\>Online Update\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id8754844				0	en-ZA	Specifies some options for the automatic notification and downloading of online updates to %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\online_update.xhp	0	help	hd_id2189397				0	en-ZA	Check for updates automatically				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id7523728				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Mark to check for online updates periodically, then select the time interval how often %PRODUCTNAME will check for online updates.\</ahelp\> %PRODUCTNAME will check once a day, week, or month, as soon as a working Internet connection is detected. If you connect to the Internet by a proxy server, set the proxy on \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Internet - Proxy\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id8994109				0	en-ZA	When an update is available, an icon in the menu bar displays some explaining text. Click the icon to proceed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id476699				0	en-ZA	If you disable the check, the icon is removed from the menu bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id4057130				0	en-ZA	Online Update is a module that can be selected or deselected to be installed. Choose the customised installation in the Setup of %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
