helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	en-ZA	When you choose \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06050000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Numbering/Bullets\"\>\<emph\>Format - Numbering/Bullets\</emph\>\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>Format - Numbering/Bullets\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> to format a paragraph with numbers or bullets in a text document, the program assigns these Paragraph Styles automatically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154918				0	en-ZA	Caption				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_COMBOBOX_TP_STD_FONT_LB_LABEL\"\>Specifies the font used for the captions of images and tables.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152463				0	en-ZA	Index				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3146923				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_COMBOBOX_TP_STD_FONT_LB_IDX\"\>Specifies the font used for indexes, alphabetical indexes, and tables of contents.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150103				0	en-ZA	Current document only				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3083444				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_STD_FONT_CB_DOCONLY\"\>Specifies that the settings apply to the current document only.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01090000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Formula				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150040				0	en-ZA	%PRODUCTNAME Math Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"druckentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SmEditOptions\"\>Defines the print format and print options for all new formula documents. These options apply when you print a formula directly from \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Math.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> You can also call the dialogue by clicking the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> button in the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialogue. The settings you define in the \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\</emph\> dialogue will be permanent settings, whereas the settings in the Print dialogue are only valid for the current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154143				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01090100.xhp\" name=\"Options\"\>Options\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Calculate				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149399				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>references; iterative (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>calculating;iterative references (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>iterative references in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>recursions in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>dates; default (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>dates; start 1900/01/01 (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>dates; start 1904/01/01 (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>case sensitivity;comparing cell contents (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>decimal places displayed (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>precision as shown (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>values; rounded as shown (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>rounding precision (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>search criteria for database functions in cells\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Excel; search criteria\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145071				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060500.xhp\" name=\"Calculate\"\>Calculate\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149399				0	en-ZA	Iterative references				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	en-ZA	In this section you can delimit the number of approximation steps carried out during iterative calculations. In addition, you can specify the degree of precision of the answer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154142				0	en-ZA	Iterations				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149795	6			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_ITERATE\"\>Specifies whether formulae with iterative references (formulae that are continuously repeated until the problem is solved) are calculated after a specific number of repetitions.\</ahelp\> If the\<emph\> Iterations \</emph\>box is not marked, an iterative reference in the table will cause an error message.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148686	7			0	en-ZA	         \<emph\>Example:\</emph\> calculating the cost of an item without the value-added tax.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155				0	en-ZA	Type the text 'Selling price' in cell A5, the text 'Net' in cell A6, and the text 'Value-added tax' in cell A7.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147530	61			0	en-ZA	Now type a selling price (for example, 100) in cell B5. The net price should be shown in cell B6 and the value-added tax should be shown in cell B7. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153061				0	en-ZA	You know that the value-added tax is calculated as 'net price times 15%' and that you arrive at the net price by deducting the value-added tax from the selling price. Type the formula \<item type=\"literal\"\>=B5-B7\</item\> in B6 to calculate the net price, and type the formula \<item type=\"literal\"\>=B6*0.15\</item\> in cell B7 to calculate the value-added tax.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	en-ZA	Switch on the iterations to correctly calculate the formulae, otherwise a 'Circular reference' error message appears in the \<emph\>Status\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	en-ZA	A				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3145606				0	en-ZA	B				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149202				0	en-ZA	5				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	en-ZA	Selling Price				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149				0	en-ZA	100				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3159254				0	en-ZA	6				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147317				0	en-ZA	Net				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147348				0	en-ZA	=B5-B7				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154918				0	en-ZA	7				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153573				0	en-ZA	Tax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	en-ZA	=B6*0,15				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145750				0	en-ZA	Steps				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:NUMERICFIELD:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:ED_STEPS\"\>Sets the maximum number of iteration steps.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153728				0	en-ZA	Minimum Change				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153139				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:ED_EPS\"\>Specifies the difference between two consecutive iteration step results. If the result of the iteration is lower than the minimum change value, then the iteration will stop.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147125				0	en-ZA	Date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3155416				0	en-ZA	Select the start date for the internal conversion from days to numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147396				0	en-ZA	12/30/1899 (default)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3145646				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_DATESTD\"\>Sets 12/30/1899 as day zero.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156283				0	en-ZA	01/01/1900 (StarCalc 1.0)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_DATESC10\"\>Sets 1/1/1900 as day zero. Use this setting for StarCalc 1.0 spreadsheets containing date entries.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156181				0	en-ZA	01/01/1904				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153948				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_DATE1904\"\>Sets 1/1/1904 as day zero. Use this setting for spreadsheets that are imported in a foreign format.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153838				0	en-ZA	Case sensitive				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3146793				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_CASE\"\>Specifies whether to distinguish between upper and lower case in texts when comparing cell contents.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707	28			0	en-ZA	         \<emph\>Example:\</emph\> Type the text 'Test' in cell A1; and the text 'test' in B1. Then type the formula "=A1=B1" in cell C1. If the \<emph\>Case sensitive\</emph\> box is marked, FALSE will appear in the cell; otherwise, TRUE will appear in the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965				0	en-ZA	The EXACT text function is always case-sensitive, independent of the settings in this dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145231				0	en-ZA	Decimal places				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:NUMERICFIELD:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:ED_PREC\"\>Defines the number of decimals to be displayed for numbers with the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> number format. The numbers are displayed as rounded numbers, but are not saved as rounded numbers.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145150				0	en-ZA	Precision as shown				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150644				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_CALC\"\>Specifies whether to make calculations using the rounded values displayed in the sheet. Charts will be shown with the displayed values. If the \<emph\>Precision as shown\</emph\> option is not marked, the displayed numbers are rounded, but they are calculated internally using the non-rounded number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152581				0	en-ZA	Search criteria = and <> must apply to whole cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149211				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_MATCH\"\>Specifies that the search criteria you set for the Calc database functions must match the whole cell exactly. When the \<emph\>Search criteria = and <> must apply to whole cells\</emph\> box is marked, $[officename] Calc behaves exactly as MS Excel when searching cells in the database functions.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148422				0	en-ZA	.* in following position:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156139				0	en-ZA	Search result:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150979				0	en-ZA	win				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3159239				0	en-ZA	Finds win, but not win95, os2win, or upwind				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153782				0	en-ZA	win.*				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151278				0	en-ZA	Finds win and win95, but not os2win or upwind				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3155506				0	en-ZA	.*win				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150886				0	en-ZA	Finds win and os2win, but not win95 or upwind				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147167				0	en-ZA	.*win.*				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	en-ZA	Finds win, win95, os2win, and upwind				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148814	44			0	en-ZA	If \<emph\>Search criteria = and <> must apply to whole cells \</emph\>is not enabled, the "win" search pattern acts like ".*win.*". The search pattern can be at any position within the cell when searching with the Calc database functions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156448				0	en-ZA	Enable regular expressions in formulae				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156199				0	en-ZA	Automatically find column and row labels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_LOOKUP\"\>Specifies that you can use the text in any cell as a label for the column below the text or the row to the right of the text. The text must consist of at least one word and must not contain any operators.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242	57			0	en-ZA	         \<emph\>Example\</emph\>: Cell E5 contains the text "Europe". Below, in cell E6, is the value 100 and in cell E7 the value 200. If the \<emph\>Automatically find column and row labels\</emph\> box is marked, you can write the following formula in cell A1: =SUM(Europe).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
