helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3157898				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SD_OPTIONS_CONTENTS\"\>Specifies the available display modes.\</ahelp\> By selecting an alternative display, you can speed up the screen display while editing your presentation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148920				0	en-ZA	Display				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155430				0	en-ZA	Rulers visible				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147443				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SD_CHECKBOX_TP_OPTIONS_CONTENTS_CBX_RULER\"\>Specifies whether to display the rulers at the top and to the left of the work area.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145364				0	en-ZA	Guides when moving				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154147				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"verschieb\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SD_CHECKBOX_TP_OPTIONS_CONTENTS_CBX_HELPLINES\"\>Specifies whether to display guides when moving an object.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150488	29			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"vertext\"\>\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> creates dotted guides that extend beyond the box containing the selected object and which cover the entire work area, helping you position the object. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153365				0	en-ZA	You also can use this function through the \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"IMPRESS\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01171400.xhp\" name=\"Icon\"\>icon\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01171400.xhp\" name=\"Icon\"\>icon\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>icon\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> with the same name in the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> bar if a presentation or a drawing document is opened.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155306				0	en-ZA	All control points in Bézier editor				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153877				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SD_CHECKBOX_TP_OPTIONS_CONTENTS_CBX_HANDLES_BEZIER\"\>Displays the control points of all Bézier points if you have previously selected a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#bezierobjekt\" name=\"Bézier curve\"\>Bézier curve\</link\>. If the \<emph\>All control points in Bézier\</emph\> editor option is not marked, only the control points of the selected Bézier points will be visible.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149418				0	en-ZA	Contour of each individual object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284	34			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SD_CHECKBOX_TP_OPTIONS_CONTENTS_CBX_MOVE_OUTLINE\"\>\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> displays the contour line of each individual object when moving this object.\</ahelp\> The \<emph\>Contour of each individual object \</emph\>option enables you to see if single objects conflict with other objects in the target position. If you do not mark the \<emph\>Contour of each individual object \</emph\>option, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> only displays a square contour that includes all selected objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Search				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154515				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>search engines; selecting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155892				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01020200.xhp\" name=\"Search\"\>Search\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153662				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OPTIONS_SEARCH\"\>Use this tab page to define the settings for searching in the Internet.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154306				0	en-ZA	Search in				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3157909				0	en-ZA	Specifies the search engine and its corresponding configuration.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154515				0	en-ZA	Search engines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:LB_SEARCH\"\>Displays the available search engines.\</ahelp\> Select a search engine to display its configuration in the adjacent text and option boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150276				0	en-ZA	Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155449	12			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:ED_SEARCH_NAME\"\>Displays the name of the selected search engine.\</ahelp\> This is the name that will be shown in the sub-menu of the \<emph\>Search\</emph\> icon on the Hyperlink bar. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151245				0	en-ZA	Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:RB_EXACT\"\>Sets the advanced search preferences (and, or, exact) as well as the way the results are defined and displayed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148663				0	en-ZA	The links \<emph\>And, Or\</emph\> and \<emph\>Exactly\</emph\> are available.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150358				0	en-ZA	Prefix				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:ED_URL\"\>This text box displays the URL and the first part of the query command for a search machine. A URL can also be typed directly.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153193				0	en-ZA	Suffix				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153970				0	en-ZA	The search terms are passed between the prefix and the suffix.\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:ED_POSTFIX\"\>The suffix provides the command sequence, sent at the end of a search.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147086				0	en-ZA	Separator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:ED_SEPARATOR\"\>If you type more than one word while running a search, these words will be separated by the character specified here.\</ahelp\> Most search engines require the "+" character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149560				0	en-ZA	To determine which prefixes, separators and suffixes to use when defining a new search engine:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159255				0	en-ZA	Activate the search engine and perform a search with at least two words.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	en-ZA	Copy the URL from your browser's \<emph\>URL\</emph\> field and paste it into a blank document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148647				0	en-ZA	Change the conditions for the search in the search engine, if it offers you the choice.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147317				0	en-ZA	Again, copy the contents of the \<emph\>URL\</emph\> field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147213				0	en-ZA	Compare the URLs with the sample URLs in the fields of this dialogue and make a note of the prefixes, suffixes and separators used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147348				0	en-ZA	Case match				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154918				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:ED_CASE\"\>Determines the case match for running a search.\</ahelp\> The list contains the following entries: \<emph\>None\</emph\>, \<emph\>Upper\</emph\> and \<emph\>Lower\</emph\>. The search terms entered are converted according to your selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	en-ZA	Search engines handle queries differently according to the way they are constructed. For example, some are case sensitive and some are not. Because of this, it is best to select \<emph\>None\</emph\> as the case match option.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156283				0	en-ZA	New				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149413				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:PB_NEW\"\>Use this button to include a new search engine.\</ahelp\>\<emph\>New\</emph\> deletes all important entries of the entry mask such as "Name" and "Suffix". Enter the new search engine together with all of the necessary details. As soon as you accept your entries with \<emph\>Add\</emph\>, the new search engine will appear in the search engine list under \<emph\>Search in\</emph\>. Close the dialogue with the \<emph\>OK\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145254				0	en-ZA	Add				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3144767				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:PB_ADD\"\>Click this button to add a new configuration to the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155603				0	en-ZA	Modify				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151320				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:PB_CHANGE\"\>Click this button to apply the modifications made to an existing configuration.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149122				0	en-ZA	Delete				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154270				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:PB_DELETE\"\>Click this button to delete the selected search engine from the list. There will be no security response.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010700.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Fonts				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010700.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150715				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>HTML;fonts for source display\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Basic; fonts for source display\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fonts;for HTML and Basic\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149398				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010700.xhp\" name=\"Fonts\"\>Fonts\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010700.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OFA_FONT_SUBSTITUTION\"\>Substitutes a font with a font of your choice. The substitution replaces a font only when it is displayed on screen, or on screen and when printing. The replacement does not change the font settings that are saved in the document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010700.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	en-ZA	If you want, you can override the default substitution font that your operating system uses when it encounters an unavailable font in a document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010700.xhp	0	help	par_id3145610				0	en-ZA	Font replacement also affects the display of fonts on the $[officename] user interface.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149295				0	en-ZA	Apply replacement table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010700.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:CHECKBOX:RID_SVX_FONT_SUBSTITUTION:CB_USETABLE\"\>Enables the font replacement settings that you define.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148664				0	en-ZA	Replacement table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154073	14			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OFA_FONT_SUBST_CLB\"\>Lists the original font and the font that will replace it. Select \<emph\>Always\</emph\> to replace the font, even if the original font is installed on your system. Select \<emph\>Screen only \</emph\>to replace the screen font only and never replace the font for printing.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
