helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3158407				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_RADIOBUTTON_TP_COMMONPRINTOPTIONS_RB_PRINTFILEOUTPUT\"\>Specifies whether the print settings apply to direct printing or to printing to a file.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145786				0	en-ZA	Reduce transparency				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3159154				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_CHECKBOX_TP_COMMONPRINTOPTIONS_CB_REDUCETRANSPARENCY\"\>If you mark this field the transparent objects will be printed like normal, non-transparent objects, depending on your selection in the following two option buttons.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3156444				0	en-ZA	Transparency cannot be output directly to a printer. The areas of the document in which transparency is to be visible must therefore always be calculated as bitmaps and sent to the printer. Depending on the size of the bitmaps and the print resolution a large amount of data may result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147441				0	en-ZA	Automatically				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3150488				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_RADIOBUTTON_TP_COMMONPRINTOPTIONS_RB_REDUCETRANSPARENCY_AUTO\"\>Specifies that the transparency is only printed if the transparent area covers less than a quarter of the entire page.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149417				0	en-ZA	No transparency				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_RADIOBUTTON_TP_COMMONPRINTOPTIONS_RB_REDUCETRANSPARENCY_NONE\"\>With this option transparency is never printed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149960				0	en-ZA	Reduce bitmaps				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3148455				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_CHECKBOX_TP_COMMONPRINTOPTIONS_CB_REDUCEBITMAPS\"\>Specifies that bitmaps are printed with reduced quality. The resolution can only be reduced and not increased.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149400				0	en-ZA	High/normal print quality				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510	76			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_RADIOBUTTON_TP_COMMONPRINTOPTIONS_RB_REDUCEBITMAPS_NORMAL\"\>High print quality corresponds to a resolution of 300dpi. Normal print quality corresponds to a resolution of 200dpi. \</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146969				0	en-ZA	Resolution				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3154270				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_LISTBOX_TP_COMMONPRINTOPTIONS_LB_REDUCEBITMAPS_RESOLUTION\"\>Specifies the maximum print quality in dpi. The resolution can only be reduced and not increased.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146789				0	en-ZA	Include transparent objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_CHECKBOX_TP_COMMONPRINTOPTIONS_CB_REDUCEBITMAPS_TRANSPARENCY\"\>If this field is marked, the reduction in print quality for bitmaps also applies to the transparent areas of objects.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154362				0	en-ZA	Reduce gradients				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3148914				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_CHECKBOX_TP_COMMONPRINTOPTIONS_CB_REDUCEGRADIENTS\"\>If this field is marked, gradients are printed with reduced quality.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766				0	en-ZA	Gradient stripes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_NUMERICFIELD_TP_COMMONPRINTOPTIONS_NF_REDUCEGRADIENTS_STEPCOUNT\"\>Specifies the maximum number of gradient stripes for printing.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146313				0	en-ZA	Intermediate colour				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3145230				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_RADIOBUTTON_TP_COMMONPRINTOPTIONS_RB_REDUCEGRADIENTS_COLOR\"\>Specifies that gradients are only printed in a single intermediate colour.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147323				0	en-ZA	Convert colours to greyscale				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3145150				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_CHECKBOX_TP_COMMONPRINTOPTIONS_CB_CONVERTTOGREYSCALES\"\>Specifies that all colours are printed only as greyscale.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150646				0	en-ZA	Printer warnings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_CHECKBOX_TP_COMMONPRINTOPTIONS_CB_CONVERTTOGREYSCALES\"\>Defines which warnings appear before printing begins.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147003				0	en-ZA	Paper size				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3150206				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_CHECKBOX_TP_COMMONPRINTOPTIONS_CB_PAPERSIZE\"\>Mark this check box if a certain paper size is needed for printing the current document.\</ahelp\> If the paper size used in the document is not provided by the current printer, you will receive an error message.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155581				0	en-ZA	Paper orientation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3153231				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_CHECKBOX_TP_COMMONPRINTOPTIONS_CB_PAPERORIENTATION\"\>Mark this check box if you need a certain paper orientation for printing the current document.\</ahelp\> If the format used by the current document is not available from the printer, an error message will appear.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149531				0	en-ZA	Transparency				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3152778				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_CHECKBOX_TP_COMMONPRINTOPTIONS_CB_TRANSPARENCY\"\>Mark this check box if you always want to be warned if transparent objects are contained in the document.\</ahelp\> If you print such a document, a dialogue appears in which you can select if the transparency is to be printed in this print instruction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	VBA Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155805				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>Microsoft Office; importing/exporting VBA code\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>importing; Microsoft Office documents with VBA code\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>exporting; Microsoft Office documents with VBA code\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>loading; Microsoft Office documents with VBA code\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>saving; VBA code in Microsoft Office documents\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>VBA code; loading/saving documents with VBA code\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Visual Basic for Applications; loading/saving documents with VBA code\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01130100.xhp\" name=\"VBA Properties\"\>VBA Properties\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the general properties for loading and saving Microsoft Office documents with VBA (Visual Basic for Applications) code.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145582				0	en-ZA	Microsoft Word 97/2000/XP				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	en-ZA	Select the settings for Microsoft Word documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155420				0	en-ZA	Load Basic code				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159399	6			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"codetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:CHECKBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_MSFILTEROPT:CB_WBAS_CODE\"\>Loads and saves the Basic code from a Microsoft document as a special $[officename] Basic module with the document. The disabled Microsoft Basic code is visible in the $[officename] Basic IDE between \<emph\>Sub\</emph\> and \<emph\>End Sub\</emph\>.\</ahelp\> You can edit the code. When saving the document in $[officename] format, the Basic code is saved as well. When saving in another format, the Basic code from the $[officename] Basic IDE is not saved. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153824				0	en-ZA	Save original Basic code				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:CHECKBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_MSFILTEROPT:CB_WBAS_STG\"\>Specifies that the original Microsoft Basic code contained in the document is held in a special internal memory for as long as the document remains loaded in $[officename]. When saving the document in Microsoft format the Microsoft Basic is saved again with the code in an unchanged form.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153088				0	en-ZA	When saving in another format than Microsoft Format, the Microsoft Basic Code is not saved. For example, if the document contains Microsoft Basic Code and you save it in $[officename] format, you will be warned that the Microsoft Basic Code will not be saved.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151246				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Save original Basic code\</emph\> checkbox takes precedence over the \<emph\>Load Basic code\</emph\> check box. If both boxes are marked and you edit the disabled Basic Code in the $[officename] Basic IDE, the original Microsoft Basic code will be saved when saving in the Microsoft format. A message appears to inform you of this.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148946	19			0	en-ZA	To remove any possible Microsoft Basic macro viruses from the Microsoft document, unmark the \<emph\>Save Original Basic Code \</emph\>check box and save the document in Microsoft format. The document will be saved without the Microsoft Basic code.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154924				0	en-ZA	Microsoft Excel 97/2000/XP				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149457				0	en-ZA	Specifies the settings for documents in Microsoft Excel.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154072				0	en-ZA	Load Basic code				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id0523200811475727				0	en-ZA	Executable code				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id0523200811475733				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The VBA (Visual Basic for Applications) code will be loaded ready to be executed. If this checkbox is not checked, the VBA code will be commented out so it can be inspected, but will not run.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151211				0	en-ZA	Save original Basic code				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149202				0	en-ZA	Microsoft PowerPoint 97/2000/XP				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148922				0	en-ZA	Specifies the settings for documents in Microsoft PowerPoint.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148451				0	en-ZA	Load Basic code				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145419				0	en-ZA	Save original Basic code				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010200.xhp\" name=\"Setting the default file format\"\>Setting the default file format\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01160200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Registered Databases				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01160200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10551				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01160200.xhp\"\>Databases\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01160200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10561				0	en-ZA	Add, modify, or remove entries to the list of registered databases. You must register a database within %PRODUCTNAME in order to see it in the \<emph\>View - Data sources\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01160200.xhp	0	help	par_idN1058E				0	en-ZA	Registered Databases				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01160200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10592				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"35535\"\>Lists the registered name and database file of all registered databases. Double-click an entry to edit.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01160200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10595				0	en-ZA	New				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01160200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10599				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"809226765\"\>Opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01160201.xhp\"\>Database Link\</link\> dialogue to create a new entry.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01160200.xhp	0	help	par_idN105AA				0	en-ZA	Delete				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01160200.xhp	0	help	par_idN105AE				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"809226770\"\>Removes the selected entry from the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01160200.xhp	0	help	par_idN105B1				0	en-ZA	Edit				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01160200.xhp	0	help	par_idN105B5				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"809226766\"\>Opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01160201.xhp\"\>Database Link\</link\> dialogue to edit the selected entry.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Compatibility				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3577990				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>Word documents;compatibility\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>importing;compatibility settings for text import\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>options;compatibility (Writer)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>compatibility settings for MS Word import\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Microsoft Office;importing Word documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>layout;importing Word documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;printer metrics (Writer)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>metrics;document formatting (Writer)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printer metrics for document formatting (Writer)\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10607				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"compatibility_var\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01041000.xhp\"\>Compatibility\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10625				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"53251\"\>Specifies compatibility settings for text documents. These options help in fine-tuning %PRODUCTNAME when importing Microsoft Word documents.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	en-ZA	Some of the settings defined here are only valid for the current document and must be defined separately for each document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149400				0	en-ZA	Use printer metrics for document formatting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE_CB_PRINTER_METRICS\"\>Specifies that printer metrics are applied for printing and also for formatting the display on the screen.\</ahelp\> If this box is not checked, a printer independent layout will be used for screen display and printing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155768				0	en-ZA	If you set this option for the current document and then save the document, for example, in an older binary format, this option will not be saved. If you later open the file from the older format, this option will be set by default.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145640				0	en-ZA	Add spacing between paragraphs and tables (in current document)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147339				0	en-ZA	In $[officename] Writer, paragraph spacing is defined differently than in MS Word documents. If you have defined spacing between two paragraphs or tables, spacing is also added in the corresponding MS Word documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151250				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE:CB_MERGE_PARA_DIST\"\>Specifies whether to add MS Word-compatible spacing between paragraphs and tables in $[officename] Writer text documents.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146317				0	en-ZA	Add paragraph and table spacing at tops of pages (in current document)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE:CB_MERGE_PARA_DIST_PAGESTART\"\>Specifies whether paragraph spacing at the top of a page will also be effective at the beginning of a page or column if the paragraph is positioned on the first page of the document.\</ahelp\> The same applies for a page break.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145789				0	en-ZA	If you import an MS Word document, the spaces are automatically added during the conversion.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149964				0	en-ZA	Use StarOffice 6.0/7 tab stop formatting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152777				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE_CB_TAB_ALIGNMENT\"\>Specifies how to align text at tab stops beyond the right margin, how to handle decimal tab stops, and how to handle tab stops close to a line break.\</ahelp\> If this check box is not selected, tab stops are handled in the same way as in other Office applications.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10810				0	en-ZA	In text documents created by your current version of Writer, the new tab stop handling is used by default. In text documents created by Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0, the old tab stop handling is applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F9				0	en-ZA	Do not add leading (extra space) between lines of text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10806				0	en-ZA	Specifies that additional leading (extra space) between lines of text is not added, even if the font in use contains the additional leading attribute.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10809				0	en-ZA	In text documents created by your current version of Writer, the additional leading is used by default. In text documents created by Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0, the additional leading is not used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FF				0	en-ZA	Use StarOffice 6.0/7 line spacing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10815				0	en-ZA	If the option is off, a new process for formatting text lines with proportional line spacing will be applied. If the option is on, the previous method of formatting of text lines with proportional line spacing will be applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10818				0	en-ZA	In text documents created by your current version of Writer and in Microsoft Word documents of recent versions, the new process is used. In text documents created by Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0, the previous process is used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081B				0	en-ZA	Add paragraph and table spacing at bottom of table cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10846				0	en-ZA	Specifies that the bottom spacing is added to a paragraph, even when it is the last paragraph in a table cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10849				0	en-ZA	If the option is off, table cells will be formatted as in Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0. If the option is on, an alternative method of formatting table cells will be applied. The option is on by default for new documents created with %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION and for documents imported from Microsoft Word format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084C				0	en-ZA	Use StarOffice 6.0/7 object positioning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10864				0	en-ZA	Specifies how to calculate the position of floating objects anchored to a character or paragraph with respect to the top and bottom paragraph spacing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10867				0	en-ZA	If the option is on, the floating objects are positioned as in Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0. If the option is off, the floating objects are positioned using an alternative method that is similar to the method used by Microsoft Word. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1086A				0	en-ZA	The option will be set to off for new documents. For Writer documents created by a version prior to %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION the option is on.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10821				0	en-ZA	Use StarOffice 6.0/7 text wrapping around objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id4016541				0	en-ZA	MS Word and Writer have different approaches on wrapping text around floating screen objects. Floating screen object are Writer frames and drawing objects, and the objects 'text box', 'graphic', 'frame', 'picture' etc. in MS Word.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id7280190				0	en-ZA	In MS Word and in current versions of Writer, page header/footer content and footnote/endnote content does not wrap around floating screen objects. Text body content wraps around floating screen objects which are anchored in the page header. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id2782982				0	en-ZA	In Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0, the opposite was true.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10892				0	en-ZA	If the option is off, which is the default setting, the new text wrapping will be applied. If the option is on, the former text wrapping will be applied. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1092A				0	en-ZA	Consider wrapping style when positioning objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	en-ZA	Specifies how the complex process of positioning floating objects that are anchored to a character or paragraph should work. In Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0, an iterative process was used, while in current versions a straightforward process is used, which is similar to the same process in Microsoft Word.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10943				0	en-ZA	If the option is off, the old %PRODUCTNAME iterative process of object positioning is used. If the option is on, the new straightforward process is used to ensure compatibility with Microsoft Word documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id5240028				0	en-ZA	Expand word space on lines with manual line breaks in justified paragraphs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id8599810				0	en-ZA	If enabled, Writer adds spacing between words, in lines that end with Shift+Enter in justified paragraphs. If disabled, spacing between words will not be expanded to justify the lines.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id8012634				0	en-ZA	This setting is on by default for .odt text documents. It will be saved and loaded with the document in the .odt text document format. This setting cannot be saved in old .sxw text documents, so this setting is off for .sxw text documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10845				0	en-ZA	Use as Default				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10848				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"879350288\"\>Click to use the current settings on this tab page as the default for further sessions with %PRODUCTNAME.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10977				0	en-ZA	The factory defaults are set as follows. Enabled are the following options, while all other options are disabled:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1097D				0	en-ZA	Add spacing between paragraphs and tables (in current document)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10981				0	en-ZA	Add paragraph and table spacing at tops of pages (in current document)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10985				0	en-ZA	Add paragraph and table spacing at bottom of table cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id4653767				0	en-ZA	Expand word space on lines with manual line breaks in justified paragraphs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153823				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040700.xhp\" name=\"Changes\"\>Changes\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149416				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_REDLINE_OPT\"\>Defines the appearance of changes in the document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3156153				0	en-ZA	To record or show changes in your text or spreadsheet document, choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02230000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Changes\"\>\<emph\>Edit - Changes - Record\</emph\>\</link\> or \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Show\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155419				0	en-ZA	Text display				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3144510				0	en-ZA	Defines the settings for displaying recorded changes. Select the type of change and the corresponding display attribute and colour. The preview field shows the effect of the selected display options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148550				0	en-ZA	Insertions / Attributes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_REDLINE_OPT_LB_INS_ATTR\"\>Specifies how changes in the document are displayed when text is inserted.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152812				0	en-ZA	Deletions / Attributes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_REDLINE_OPT_LB_DEL_ATTR\"\>Specifies how changes in the document are displayed when text is deleted. If you record text deletions, the text is displayed with the selected attribute (for example, strikethrough) and is not deleted.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148674				0	en-ZA	Changed attributes / Attributes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3151042				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_REDLINE_OPT_LB_CHG_ATTR\"\>Defines how changes to text attributes are displayed in the document. These changes affect attributes such as bold, italic or underline.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153105				0	en-ZA	Colour				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_REDLINE_OPT_LB_CHG_COL\"\>You can also choose a colour to display each type of recorded change. When you choose the condition "By author" in the list, the colour is automatically determined by $[officename], then modified to match to the author of each change.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145607				0	en-ZA	Lines changed				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149562				0	en-ZA	To indicate which lines of the text have been changed, you can define a mark that appears in the left or right page margin.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145785				0	en-ZA	Mark				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154638				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_REDLINE_OPT:LB_MARKPOS\"\>Defines if and where changed lines in the document are marked.\</ahelp\> You can set the markings so that they always appear on the left or right page margin, or on the outer or inner margin.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163713				0	en-ZA	Colour				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_REDLINE_OPT:LB_LC_COL\"\>Specifies the colour for highlighting the changed lines in the text.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Writing Aids				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	bm_id7986388				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>writing aids options\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom dictionaries; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>user-defined dictionaries; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dictionaries; editing user-defined\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exceptions; user-defined dictionaries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>user-defined dictionaries; dictionary of exceptions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spellcheck; dictionary of exceptions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ignore list for spellcheck\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spellcheck; ignore list\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyphenation; minimal number of characters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145136				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010400.xhp\" name=\"Writing Aids\"\>Writing Aids\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OPTIONS_LINGU\"\>Specifies the properties of the spellcheck, thesaurus and hyphenation.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149096				0	en-ZA	Available Language Modules				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_CLB_LINGU_MODULES\"\>Contains the installed language modules.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153663	35			0	en-ZA	A language module can contain one, two or three submodules: Spellcheck, hyphenation and thesaurus. Each sub-module can be available in one or more languages. If you click in front of the name of the module, you activate all the available sub-modules simultaneously. If you remove a set mark, you deactivate all the available sub-modules simultaneously. If you wish to activate or deactivate individual sub-modules, click the\<emph\> Edit button \</emph\>to open the \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010401.xhp\" name=\"Edit Modules\"\>\<emph\>Edit Modules\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3294778				0	en-ZA	The configuration allows for two different directories: one folder where the user has write permissions, and one without write permissions. The user can only edit and delete the user dictionaries that are located in the writable path. Other dictionaries can be read only.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154307				0	en-ZA	Edit				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145673	37			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SFXPAGE_LINGU_PB_LINGU_MODULES_EDIT\"\>To edit a language module, select it and click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.\</ahelp\> The \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010401.xhp\" name=\"Edit Modules\"\>\<emph\>Edit \</emph\>\<emph\>Modules\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153348				0	en-ZA	User-defined dictionaries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_CLB_EDIT_MODULES_DICS\"\>Lists the available user dictionaries.\</ahelp\> Mark the user dictionaries that you want to use for spellcheck and hyphenation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144511				0	en-ZA	New				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3146794				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SFXPAGE_LINGU_PB_LINGU_DICS_NEW_DIC\"\>Opens the \<emph\>New Dictionary\</emph\> dialogue, in which you can name a new user-defined dictionary or dictionary of exceptions and specify the language.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151054				0	en-ZA	New Dictionary				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Dictionary\</emph\> section you can name a new user-defined dictionary or dictionary of exceptions and specify the language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150398				0	en-ZA	Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SFXDLG_NEWDICT:ED_DICTNAME\"\>Specifies the name of the new custom dictionary.\</ahelp\> The file extension "*.DIC" is automatically appended.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150767				0	en-ZA	Language				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3148920				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SFXDLG_NEWDICT:LB_DICTLANG\"\>By selecting a certain language you can limit the use of the custom dictionary.\</ahelp\> By selecting \<emph\>All\</emph\> the custom dictionary is used independently of the current language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153106				0	en-ZA	Exceptions (-)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149561				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:CHECKBOX:RID_SFXDLG_NEWDICT:BTN_EXCEPT\"\>Specifies whether you wish to avoid certain words in your documents.\</ahelp\> In this way, you can create a custom dictionary of all the words to be avoided. If this exception dictionary is activated, during spellchecking you receive a corresponding note about any words which should be avoided.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145785				0	en-ZA	Edit				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SFXPAGE_LINGU_PB_LINGU_DICS_EDIT_DIC\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Edit custom dictionary\</emph\> dialogue, in which you can add to your custom dictionary or edit existing entries.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147436	75			0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Edit custom dictionary \</emph\>dialogue you have the option to enter new terms or edit existing entries. If you edit an exception dictionary, the dialogue has the added facility of defining an exception for a word. During the spellcheck this exception is then listed as a suggestion.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	76			0	en-ZA	When a dictionary is edited, a check is made on the status of the file. If the file is write-protected, it cannot be changed. The buttons \<emph\>New\</emph\> and \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> are then deactivated. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150116				0	en-ZA	Book				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:LB_ALLDICTS\"\>Specifies the book to be edited.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730	79			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"ignore\"\>The \<emph\>IgnoreAllList (All) \</emph\>includes all words that have been marked with \<emph\>Ignore\</emph\> during spellcheck. This list is valid only for the current spellcheck. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>IgnoreAllList\</emph\> entry cannot be selected and cannot be deleted. Only the words included as content can be deleted. This happens automatically each time that $[officename] is closed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	en-ZA	Language				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:LB_DICTLANG\"\>Assigns a new language to the current custom dictionary.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151189				0	en-ZA	Word				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3151252				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:ED_WORD\"\>You can type a new word for inclusion in the dictionary. In the list below you will see the contents of the current custom dictionary.\</ahelp\> If you select a word from this list it is displayed in the text field. If you type a word with a trailing = character, such as "AutoComplete=", the word is never automatically hyphenated and no hyphenation is suggested. Typing "Auto=Complete" results in the word being hyphenated, or a hyphenation suggested, where you insert the = sign.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155175				0	en-ZA	Suggestion				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147323				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:ED_REPLACE\"\>This input field is only available if you are editing an exception dictionary. The field shows the alternative suggestion for the current word in the "Word" text box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147361				0	en-ZA	New				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3163808	89			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:PB_NEW_REPLACE\"\>Adds the word in the \<emph\>Word \</emph\>text field to your current custom dictionary. The word in the \<emph\>Suggestion \</emph\>field is also added when working with exception dictionaries.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145790				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Removes the marked word from the current custom dictionary.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Deletes the selected dictionary after a confirmation, provided it is not write-protected.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149032				0	en-ZA	Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145259				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_CLB_LINGU_OPTIONS\"\>Defines the options for the spellcheck and hyphenation.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149965				0	en-ZA	Edit				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153231				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SFXPAGE_LINGU_PB_LINGU_OPTIONS_EDIT\"\>If you want to change a value, select the entry and then click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.\</ahelp\> You will see a dialogue for entering a new value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150983				0	en-ZA	Check uppercase words				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3152582				0	en-ZA	Specifies that capitalisation is checked during spellcheck.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150826				0	en-ZA	Check words with numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150208				0	en-ZA	Specifies that words that contain numbers as well as letters are to be checked.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147509				0	en-ZA	Check capitalisation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154200				0	en-ZA	Checks for the correct use of capitals at the start of words during spellcheck.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166424				0	en-ZA	Check special regions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150345				0	en-ZA	Specifies that special regions, such as drawing text, are checked during spellcheck.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166429				0	en-ZA	Check spelling as you type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155531				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"automatisch\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SpellOnline\"\>Automatically checks spelling as you type, and underlines errors.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3156291				0	en-ZA	Typing errors are highlighted in the document with a red underline. If you place the cursor over a word marked in this way, you can open the context menu to obtain a list of corrections. Select a correction to replace the word. If you make the same mistake again while editing the document, it will be marked as an error again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153815				0	en-ZA	To place the word pair in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"AutoCorrect replacement table\"\>AutoCorrect replacement table\</link\>, open the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040500.xhp\" name=\"AutoCorrect context menu\"\>AutoCorrect context menu\</link\> and choose \<emph\>AutoCorrect\</emph\>. Make your selection from the submenu. The word is replaced and at the same time the word pair is placed in the replacement table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150111	53			0	en-ZA	Minimal number of characters for hyphenation 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150316				0	en-ZA	Specifies the minimum number of characters required for automatic hyphenation to be applied. \<ahelp hid=\"HID_LNGDLG_NUM_PREBREAK\" visibility=\"hidden\"\> Type the minimum number of characters that must come before or after the hyphen.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148823				0	en-ZA	Characters before line break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3156029				0	en-ZA	Sets the minimum number of characters of the word to be hyphenated that must remain at the end of the line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154956				0	en-ZA	Characters after line break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149439				0	en-ZA	Specifies the minimum number of characters of a hyphenated word required at the next line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156337				0	en-ZA	Hyphenate without enquiry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3151130				0	en-ZA	Specifies that you will never be asked for a manual hyphenation. If the field is not marked, when a word is not recognised you will be presented with a dialogue for entering hyphens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155900				0	en-ZA	Hyphenate special regions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155098				0	en-ZA	Specifies that hyphenation will also be carried out in footnotes, headers and footers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Proxy				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147577				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>settings; proxies\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>proxy settings\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156414				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01020100.xhp\" name=\"Proxy\"\>Proxy\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#proxy\" name=\"Proxy servers\"\>Proxy servers\</link\> for accessing the Internet can be set up manually as needed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147577				0	en-ZA	Settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	en-ZA	Defines the settings for the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#proxy\" name=\"proxy server\"\>proxy server\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151110				0	en-ZA	Proxy server				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_PROXY:LB_PROXYMODE\"\>Specifies the type of proxy definition.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147574				0	en-ZA	None				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	en-ZA	Accesses the Internet without a proxy server. Allows you to set up a connection directly on your computer to an Internet provider that does not use a proxy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150984				0	en-ZA	Manual				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155				0	en-ZA	Lets you enter the proxy server manually. Specify the proxy servers in accordance with your Internet service. Ask your system administrator for the proxies and ports to enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	en-ZA	Type server names without the protocol prefix. For example, type www.example.com, not http://www.example.com.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10684				0	en-ZA	System				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10688				0	en-ZA	On Windows or UNIX systems using GNOME or KDE, this option tells %PRODUCTNAME to use the system settings. You must restart %PRODUCTNAME to initiate this setting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148948				0	en-ZA	HTTP proxy				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154923				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_PROXY:ED_HTTP_PROXY\"\>Type the name of the proxy server for \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#http\" name=\"HTTP\"\>HTTP\</link\>.\</ahelp\> Type the port in the right-hand field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id9971922				0	en-ZA	HTTPS proxy				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id5319071				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Type the name of the proxy server for HTTPS. Type the port in the right-hand field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150543				0	en-ZA	FTP proxy				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_EDIT_RID_SVXPAGE_INET_PROXY_ED_FTP_PROXY\"\>Type the name of the proxy server for \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#ftp\" name=\"FTP\"\>FTP\</link\>.\</ahelp\> Type the port in the right-hand field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	en-ZA	No proxy for				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151178				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_PROXY:ED_NOPROXYFOR\"\>Specifies the names of the servers that do not require any proxy servers, separated by semicolons.\</ahelp\> These are servers addressed in your local network, and servers used for video and audio streaming, for example.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	en-ZA	You can also use placeholders for the names of hosts and domains. For example, type *.sun.com to address all the hosts in the sun.com domain without proxy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149808				0	en-ZA	Port				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153666				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_PROXY:ED_SOCKS_PORT\"\>Type the port for the corresponding proxy server.\</ahelp\> The maximum value of a port number is fixed at 65535.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	View				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147242				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>cells; showing grid lines (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>borders; cells on screen (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>grids; displaying lines (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>colours; grid lines and cells (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>page breaks; displaying (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>guides; showing (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>handles; showing simple/large handles (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>displaying; zero values (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>zero values; displaying (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>tables in spreadsheets; value highlighting\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>cells; formatting without effect (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>cells; colouring (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>anchors; displaying (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>colours;restriction (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>text overflow in spreadsheet cells\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>references; displaying in colour (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>objects; displaying in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>pictures; displaying in Calc\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>charts; displaying (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>draw objects; displaying (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>row headers; displaying (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>column headers; displaying (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>scrollbars; displaying (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>sheet tabs; displaying\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>tabs; displaying sheet tabs\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>outlines;outline symbols\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150445				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"View\"\>View\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153988				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCPAGE_CONTENT\"\>Defines which elements of the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc main window are displayed. You can also show or hide highlighting of values in tables.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153682				0	en-ZA	Visual aids				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153311				0	en-ZA	Specifies which lines are displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147242				0	en-ZA	Grid lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153088				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_CB_GRID\"\>Specifies whether to display grid lines between the cells.\</ahelp\>\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>For printing, choose \<emph\>Format - Page - \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05070500.xhp\" name=\"Sheet\"\>\<emph\>Sheet\</emph\>\</link\> and mark the \<emph\>Grid\</emph\> check box.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156326				0	en-ZA	Colour				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154286				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_LISTBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_LB_COLOR\"\>Specifies a colour for the grid lines in the current document.\</ahelp\> To see the grid line colour that was saved with the document, go to \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Appearance\</emph\>, under \<emph\>Scheme\</emph\> find the entry \<emph\>Spreadsheet - Grid lines\</emph\> and set the colour to "Automatic".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152349				0	en-ZA	Page breaks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151245				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_CB_PAGEBREAKS\"\>Specifies whether to view the page breaks within a defined print area.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149669				0	en-ZA	Guides while moving				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_CB_GUIDELINE\"\>Specifies whether to view guides when moving drawings, frames, graphics and other objects.\</ahelp\> These guides help you align objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150358	38			0	en-ZA	Simple handles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154140	39			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_CB_HANDLES\"\>Specifies whether to display the handles (the eight points on a selection box) as simple squares without 3D effect.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149202				0	en-ZA	Large handles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_CB_BIGHANDLES\"\>Specifies that larger than normal handles (the eight points on a selection box) are displayed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152920				0	en-ZA	Display				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864				0	en-ZA	Select various options for the screen display.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154218				0	en-ZA	Formulae				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150440				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_CB_FORMULA\"\>Specifies whether to show formulae instead of results in the cells.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155132				0	en-ZA	Zero values				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147318				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_CB_NIL\"\>Specifies whether to show numbers with the value of 0.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147348				0	en-ZA	Comment indicator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_CB_ANNOT\"\>Specifies that a small rectangle in the top right corner of the cell indicates that a comment exists. The comment will be shown only when you enable tips under \<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME - General\</emph\> in the Options dialogue box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150487				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:NoteVisible\"\>To display a comment permanently, select the \<emph\>Show comment\</emph\> command from the cell's context menu.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667				0	en-ZA	You can type and edit comments with the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Comment\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Comment\</emph\>\</link\> command. Comments that are permanently displayed can be edited by clicking the comment box. Click the Navigator and under the \<emph\>Comments\</emph\> entry you can view all comments in the current document. By double clicking a comment in Navigator, the cursor will jump to the corresponding cell containing the comment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150872				0	en-ZA	Value highlighting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154792				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_CB_VALUE\"\>Mark the \<emph\>Value highlighting\</emph\> box to show the cell contents in different colours, depending on type. Text cells are formatted in black, formulae in green, and number cells in blue, no matter how their display is formatted.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151319				0	en-ZA	When this command is active, any colours assigned in the document will not be displayed until the function is deactivated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157846				0	en-ZA	Anchor				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147494				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_CB_ANCHOR\"\>Specifies whether the anchor icon is displayed when an inserted object, such as a graphic, is selected.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146898				0	en-ZA	Text overflow				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_CB_CLIP\"\>If a cell contains text that is wider than the width of the cell, the text is displayed over empty neighbouring cells in the same row. If there is no empty neighbouring cell, a small triangle at the cell border indicates that the text continues.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150327				0	en-ZA	Show references in colour				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153766				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_CB_RFIND\"\>Specifies that each reference is highlighted in colour in the formula. The cell range is also enclosed by a coloured border as soon as the cell containing the reference is selected for editing.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155444				0	en-ZA	Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148405				0	en-ZA	Defines whether to display or hide objects for up to three object groups.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150043				0	en-ZA	Objects/Graphics				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3163549				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_LISTBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_LB_OBJGRF\"\>Defines if objects and graphics are shown or hidden.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151249				0	en-ZA	Charts				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149106				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_LISTBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_LB_DIAGRAM\"\>Defines if charts in your document are shown or hidden.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154703				0	en-ZA	Drawing objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155959				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_LISTBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_LB_DRAW\"\>Defines if drawing objects in your document are shown or hidden.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id0909200810585828				0	en-ZA	Zoom				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id0909200810585881				0	en-ZA	Synchronize sheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810585870				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If checked, all sheets are shown with the same zoom factor. If not checked, each sheet can have its own zoom factor.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153920				0	en-ZA	Window				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154661				0	en-ZA	Specifies whether some Help elements will or will not appear in the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149923				0	en-ZA	Column/Row headers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149816				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_CB_ROWCOLHEADER\"\>Specifies whether to display row and column headers.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154205				0	en-ZA	Horizontal scrollbar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155578				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_CB_HSCROLL\"\>Specifies whether to display a horizontal scrollbar at the bottom of the document window.\</ahelp\> Note that there is a slider between the horizontal scrollbar and the sheet tabs that may be set to one end.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148422				0	en-ZA	Vertical scrollbar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147128				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_CB_VSCROLL\"\>Specifies whether to display a vertical scrollbar at the right of the document window.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150826				0	en-ZA	Sheet tabs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154658				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_CB_TBLREG\"\>Specifies whether to display the sheet tabs at the bottom of the spreadsheet document.\</ahelp\> If this box is not checked, you will only be able to switch between the sheets through the \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Navigator\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>. Note that there is a slider between the horizontal scrollbar and the sheet tabs that may be set to one end.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152584				0	en-ZA	Outline symbols				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145135				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CONTENT_CB_OUTLINE\"\>If you have defined an \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080000.xhp\" name=\"outline\"\>outline\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>outline\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, the \<emph\>Outline symbols\</emph\> option specifies whether to view the outline symbols at the border of the sheet.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
