helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update_dialog.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Check for Updates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update_dialog.xhp	0	help	hd_id4959257				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/online_update_dialog.xhp\"\>Check for Updates\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id1906491				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Checks for available updates to your version of %PRODUCTNAME. If a newer version is available, you can choose to download the update. After downloading, if you have write permissions for the installation directory, you can install the update.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id4799340				0	en-ZA	Once the download starts, you see a progress bar and three buttons on the dialogue. You can pause and resume the download by clicking the Pause and Resume buttons. Click Cancel to abort the download and delete the partly downloaded file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id1502121				0	en-ZA	By default, downloads will be stored to your desktop. You can change the folder where the downloaded file will be stored in \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Online Update.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id8266853				0	en-ZA	After the download is complete, you can click Install to start the installation of the update. You see a confirmation dialogue, where you can choose to close %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id2871181				0	en-ZA	Under some operation systems, it may be required to manually go to the download folder, unzip the download file, and start the setup script.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id2733542				0	en-ZA	After installation of the update you can delete the download file to save space.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id4238715				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Downloads and saves the update files to the desktop or a folder of your choice. Select the folder in %PRODUCTNAME - Online Update in the Options dialogue box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id8277230				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Installs the downloaded update.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id4086428				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Pauses the download. Later click Resume to continue downloading.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id9024628				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Continues a paused download.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3067110				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Aborts the download and deletes the partly downloaded file.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
