helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149119				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"litdattext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"HID_BIB_DB_TBX\"\>Insert, delete, edit, and organise records in the bibliography database.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346				0	en-ZA	If the fields in your database are read-only, ensure that the data source view is closed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150506				0	en-ZA	The supplied bibliography database contains sample records of books.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155356				0	en-ZA	Use the toolbar to select a table in the bibliography database, to search for records, or to sort the records using filters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Lists the available tables in the current database. Click a name in the list to display the records for that table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3158432				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Go to the first record in the table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149192				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Go to the previous record in the table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146795				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Go to the next record in the table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144760				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Go to the last record in the table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3157960				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Type the number of the record that you want to display, and then press Enter.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150868				0	en-ZA	Inserting a New Record				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149168	6			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_GRID_TRAVEL_NEW\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts a new record into the current table.\</ahelp\>To create a record, click the asterisk (*) button at the bottom of the table view. An empty row is added at the end of the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152920				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the type of record that you want to create. $[officename] inserts a number in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> column of the record that corresponds to the type that you select here.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a short name for the record. The short name appears in the \<emph\>Identifier\</emph\> column in the list of records.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155994				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter additional information for the selected record. If you want, you can also enter the information in the corresponding field in the table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163716				0	en-ZA	Finding and Filtering Records				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147478				0	en-ZA	You can search for records by matching a keyword to a field entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159181				0	en-ZA	Entering Search key				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159125	11			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Bib/query\"\>Type the information that you want to search for, and then press Enter. To change the filter options for the search, long-click the \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> icon, and then select a different data field. You can use wildcards such as % or * for any number of characters, and _ or ? for one character in your search. To display all of the records in the table, clear this box, and then press Enter. \</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155511				0	en-ZA	AutoFilter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Bib/autoFilter\"\>Long-click to select the data field that you want to search using the term that you entered in the \<emph\>Search Key\</emph\> box. You can only search one data field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	en-ZA	The list of table records is automatically updated to match the new filter settings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145590	30			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Use the \<emph\>Standard Filter\</emph\> to refine and to combine \<emph\>AutoFilter \</emph\>search options.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155311				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>To display all of the records in a table, click the \<emph\>Remove Filter\</emph\> icon.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147580				0	en-ZA	Deleting a Record				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154471				0	en-ZA	To delete a record in the current table, right-click the row header of the record, and then select \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>. \<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_DELETEROWS\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Deletes the selected record.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152941				0	en-ZA	Changing the data source				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147214				0	en-ZA	Data Source				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151118				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Bib/sdbsource\"\>Select the data source for the bibliography database.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145645				0	en-ZA	Column Arrangement				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151282	36			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Bib/Mapping\"\>Lets you map the column headings to data fields from a different data source. To define a different data source for your bibliography, click the\<emph\> Data Source\</emph\> button on the record\<emph\> Object Bar\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144767				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"BIB_LISTBOX_RID_DLG_MAPPING_LB_CUSTOM4\"\>Select the data field that you want to map to the current \<emph\>Column name\</emph\>. To change the available data fields, select a different data source for your bibliography.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153947				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Deletes the current record.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151019				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Lets you choose a different data source for your bibliography.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153730				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts a new record into the current table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02210101.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Floating Frame Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02210101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150347				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02210101.xhp\" name=\"Floating Frame Properties\"\>Floating Frame Properties\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02210101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149031				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2:TABPAGE:TP_FRAMEPROPERTIES\"\>Changes the properties of the selected floating frame. Floating frames work best when they contain an html document, and when they are inserted in another html document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02210101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	en-ZA	Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02210101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149511				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2:EDIT:TP_FRAMEPROPERTIES:ED_FRAMENAME\"\>Enter a name for the floating frame. The name cannot contain spaces, special characters, or begin with an underscore ( _ ).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02210101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	en-ZA	Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02210101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156414				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2:EDIT:TP_FRAMEPROPERTIES:ED_URL\"\>Enter the path and the name of the file that you want to display in the floating frame. You can also click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button and locate the file that you want to display.\</ahelp\> For example, you can enter:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02210101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	en-ZA	http://www.example.com				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02210101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153683	8			0	en-ZA	file:///c|/Readme.txt 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02210101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147088				0	en-ZA	...				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02210101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155355				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2:PUSHBUTTON:TP_FRAMEPROPERTIES:BT_FILEOPEN\"\>Locate the file that you want to display in the selected floating frame, and then click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
