helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05230500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149760				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_CAPTION_CTL_TYPE\"\>Click the \<emph\>Callout\</emph\> style that you want to apply to the selected callout.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05230500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149798				0	en-ZA	Spacing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05230500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:METRICFIELD:RID_SVXPAGE_CAPTION:MF_ABSTAND\"\>Enter the amount of space that you want to leave between the end of the callout line, and the callout box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05230500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151226				0	en-ZA	Extension				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05230500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148620				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_CAPTION:LB_ANSATZ_REL\"\>Select where you want to extend the callout line from, in relation to the callout box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05230500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153311				0	en-ZA	Length				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05230500.xhp	0	help	par_id3145313				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:METRICFIELD:RID_SVXPAGE_CAPTION:MF_LAENGE\"\>Enter the length of the callout line segment that extends from the callout box to the inflection point of the line.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05230500.xhp	0	help	par_id3159269	11			0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Length \</emph\>box is only available if you select the \<emph\>Angled connector line\</emph\> callout style, and leave the \<emph\>Optimal \</emph\>checkbox cleared.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05230500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149820				0	en-ZA	Optimal				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05230500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147210				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:CHECKBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_CAPTION:CB_LAENGE\"\>Click here to display a single-angled line in an optimal way.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05260600.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	As Character				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05260600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154621				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05260600.xhp\" name=\"As Character\"\>As Character\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05260600.xhp	0	help	par_id3146946				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Anchors the selected item as a character in the current text. If the height of the selected item is greater than the current font size, the height of the line containing the item is increased.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05280000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Fontwork				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05280000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146959				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"fntwrk\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05280000.xhp\" name=\"FontWork\"\>Fontwork Dialog (Previous Version)\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05280000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151097				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FontWork\"\>Edits Fontwork effects of the selected object that has been created with the previous Fontwork dialogue.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05280000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155934				0	en-ZA	This \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> dialogue is only available for Fontwork in old Writer text documents that were created prior to %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION. You must first call \<emph\>Tools - Customize\</emph\> to add a menu command or an icon to open this dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05280000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154497				0	en-ZA	You can change the shape of the text baseline to match semicircles, arcs, circles, and freeform lines.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05280000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152372				0	en-ZA	Alignment icons				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05280000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149760				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FONTWORK_CTL_FORMS\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click the shape of the baseline that you want to use for the text.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05280000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152542				0	en-ZA	The top row contains the following baseline shapes: \<emph\>Upper Semicircle\</emph\>, \<emph\>Lower Semicircle\</emph\>, \<emph\>Left Semicircle\</emph\> and \<emph\>Right Semicircle\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05280000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	en-ZA	The middle row contains the following baseline shapes: \<emph\>Upper Arc\</emph\>, \<emph\>Lower Arc, Left Arc\</emph\> and \<emph\>Right Arc\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05280000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159158				0	en-ZA	The bottom row contains the following baseline shapes: \<emph\>Open Circle, Closed Circle, Closed Circle II\</emph\>, and \<emph\>Open Circle Vertical\</emph\>. For the best results, the drawing object must contain more than two lines of text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05280000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149237				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FONTWORK_TBI_STYLE_OFF\"\>Removes baseline formatting.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
