helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145416				0	en-ZA	The default currency format for a cell is determined by the regional settings of your operating system.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155342				0	en-ZA	Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NUMBERFORMAT_LB_FORMAT\"\>Select how you want the contents of the selected cell(s) to be displayed.\</ahelp\> The code for the selected option is displayed in the \<emph\>Format Code\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154811				0	en-ZA	Currency category list boxes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3148563				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_NUMBERFORMAT:LB_CURRENCY\"\>Select a currency, and then scroll to the top of the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list to view the formatting options for the currency.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150866	99			0	en-ZA	The format code for currencies uses the form [$xxx-nnn], where xxx is the currency symbol, and nnn the country code. Special banking symbols, such as EUR (for Euro), do not require the country code. The currency format is not dependent on the language that you select in the\<emph\> Language\</emph\> box. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154071				0	en-ZA	Language				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_NUMBERFORMAT:LB_LANGUAGE\"\>Specifies the language setting for the selected \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>cells \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>fields\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>. With the language set to \<emph\>Automatic\</emph\>, $[officename] automatically applies the number formats associated with the system default language. Select any language to fix the settings for the selected \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>cells \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>fields\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3157320				0	en-ZA	The language setting ensures that date and currency formats are preserved even when the document is opened in an operating system that uses a different default language setting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
