helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Media Player				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	bm_id8659321				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>Media Player window\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN10550				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"mediaplayertitle\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/mediaplayer.xhp\"\>Media Player\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN10560				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the Media Player window where you can preview movie and sound files as well as insert these files into the current document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN10577				0	en-ZA	The Media Player supports many different media formats. You can also insert media files from the Media Player into your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN105EF				0	en-ZA	On Linux or Solaris systems, the Media Player requires the Java Media Framework API (JMF). Download and install the JMF files from http://java.sun.com/javase/technologies/desktop/media/jmf/index.jsp and add the path to the installed jmf.jar to the class path in the Options dialogue box in %PRODUCTNAME - Java.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064F				0	en-ZA	On Windows systems, the Media Player uses DirectShow, which should be installed on your system by default.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057A				0	en-ZA	Open				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057E				0	en-ZA	Opens a movie file or a sound file that you want to preview.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN10581				0	en-ZA	Apply				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN10585				0	en-ZA	Inserts the current movie file or sound file as a media object into the current document. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN10588				0	en-ZA	Play				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN1058C				0	en-ZA	Plays the current file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN1058F				0	en-ZA	Pause				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN10593				0	en-ZA	Pauses or resumes the playback of the current file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN10596				0	en-ZA	Stop				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN1059A				0	en-ZA	Stops the playback of the current file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN1059D				0	en-ZA	Repeat				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A1				0	en-ZA	Plays the file repeatedly.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A4				0	en-ZA	Mute				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A8				0	en-ZA	Turns sound off and on.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN105AB				0	en-ZA	Volume slider				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN105AF				0	en-ZA	Adjusts the volume.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN105B2				0	en-ZA	View				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN105B6				0	en-ZA	Adjusts the size of the movie playback.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN105B9				0	en-ZA	Position slider				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\mediaplayer.xhp	0	help	par_idN105BD				0	en-ZA	Moves to a different position in the file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Paragraph				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150467				0	en-ZA	Paragraph				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148668				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"absatztext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:EditStyle\"\>Modifies the format of the current paragraph, such as indents and alignment.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> To modify the font of the current paragraph, select the entire paragraph, choose Format - Character, and then click on the Font tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156042	3			0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>The paragraph style for the current paragraph is displayed at the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> toolbar, and is highlighted in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05140000.xhp\" name=\"Styles\"\>Styles and Formatting window\</link\>. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Position				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150467				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06050600.xhp\" name=\"Position\"\>Position\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	par_id3158397				0	en-ZA	Sets the indent, spacing, and alignment options for the numbered or bulleted list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	par_id5004119				0	en-ZA	The Position tab page looks different for documents using the new position and spacing attributes introduced with OpenOffice.org 3.0, or documents using the old attributes from versions before 3.0. The new version of this tab page shows the controls "Numbering followed by", "Numbering alignment", "Aligned at", and "Indent at". The old version of this tab page that can be seen in an old numbered or bulleted list shows the controls "Indent", "Width of numbering", "Minimum space numbering <-> text", and "Numbering alignment".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149031				0	en-ZA	Level				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155755				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:MULTILISTBOX:TP_NUM_POSITION:LB_LEVEL\"\>Select the level(s) that you want to modify.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	hd_id6561784				0	en-ZA	Numbering followed by				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	par_id423291				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select the element that will follow the numbering: a tab stop, a space, or nothing.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	hd_id7809686				0	en-ZA	at				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	par_id8177434				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you select a tab stop to follow the numbering, you can enter a non-negative value as the tab stop position.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155583				0	en-ZA	Numbering alignment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153063				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_NUM_POSITION:LB_ALIGN\"\>Set the alignment of the numbering symbols. Select "Left" to align the numbering symbol to start directly at the "Aligned at" position. Select "Right" to align the symbol to end directly before the "Aligned at" position. Select "Centered" to centre the symbol around the "Aligned at" position.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147422				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Numbering alignment\</emph\> option does not set the alignment of the paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	hd_id1619617				0	en-ZA	Aligned at				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	par_id1015655				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the distance from the left page margin at which the numbering symbol will be aligned.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	hd_id2336191				0	en-ZA	Indent at				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	par_id6081728				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the distance from the left page margin to the start of all lines in the numbered paragraph that follow the first line.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154422				0	en-ZA	Indent				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	par_id3144438				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:METRICFIELD:TP_NUM_POSITION:MF_BORDERDIST\"\>Enter the amount of space to leave between the left page margin (or the left edge of the text object) and the left edge of the numbering symbol. If the current paragraph style uses an indent, the amount you enter here is added to the indent.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155179				0	en-ZA	Relative				2002-02-02 02:02:02
