helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149205	2			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_IMAPDLG_UNDO\"\>Reverses the last command or the last entry you typed. To select the command that you want to reverse, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Undo \</emph\>icon on the Standard bar.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02010000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10630				0	en-ZA	To change the number of commands that you can undo, choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - Memory, and enter a new value in the number of steps box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3163803				0	en-ZA	Some commands (for example, editing Styles) cannot be undone.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
