helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156027				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AUTOCORR_LANGUAGE\"\>Select the language for which you want to create or edit the replacement rules.\</ahelp\> $[officename] first searches for exceptions that are defined for the language at the current cursor position in the document, and then searches the remaining languages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153681				0	en-ZA	Abbreviations (no subsequent capital)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:EDIT:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:ED_ABBREV\"\>Type an abbreviation followed by a period, and then click \<emph\>New\</emph\>. This prevents $[officename] from automatically capitalizing the first letter of the word that comes after the period at the end of the abbreviation.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149751				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:LISTBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:LB_ABBREV\"\>Lists the abbreviations that are not automatically corrected.\</ahelp\> To remove an item from the list, select the item, and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151110				0	en-ZA	Words with TWo INitial CApitals				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:EDIT:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:ED_DOUBLE_CAPS\"\>Type the word or abbreviation that starts with two capital letters that you do not want $[officename] to change to one initial capital. For example, enter PC to prevent $[officename] from changing PC to Pc.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:LISTBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:LB_DOUBLE_CAPS\"\>Lists the words or abbreviations that start with two initial capitals that are not automatically corrected. All words which start with two capital letters are listed in the field.\</ahelp\> To remove an item from the list, select the item, and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155503				0	en-ZA	New				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147573				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:PUSHBUTTON:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:PB_NEWDOUBLECAPS\"\>Adds the current entry to the list of exceptions.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149762				0	en-ZA	AutoInclude				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155829	11			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:CHECKBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:CB_AUTOCAPS\"\>Automatically adds abbreviations or words that start with two capital letters to the corresponding list of exceptions. This feature only works if the \<emph\>Correct TWo INitial CApitals\</emph\> option or the Capitalize\<emph\> first letter of every sentence\</emph\> option are selected in the \<emph\>[T]\</emph\> column on\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040100.xhp\" name=\"Options\"\>\<emph\>Options\</emph\>\</link\> tab of this dialogue. \</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Spelling and Grammar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149047				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>dictionaries; spellcheck\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>spellcheck; dialogue\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>languages; spellcheck\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153882				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06010000.xhp\" name=\"Spellcheck\"\>Spelling and Grammar\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154682				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"recht\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Spelling\"\>Checks the document or the current selection for spelling errors. If a grammar checking extension is installed, the dialogue also checks for grammar errors.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064B				0	en-ZA	The spellcheck starts at the current cursor position and advances to the end of the document or selection. You can then choose to continue the spellcheck from the beginning of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166445				0	en-ZA	Spellcheck looks for misspelled words and gives you the option of adding an unknown word to a user dictionary. When the first misspelled word is found, the \<emph\>Spellcheck\</emph\> dialogue opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id1022200801300654				0	en-ZA	If a grammar checking extension is installed, this dialogue is called \<emph\>Spelling and Grammar\</emph\>. Spelling errors are underlined in red, grammar errors in blue. First the dialogue presents all spelling errors, then all grammar errors.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id1022200801354366				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enable \<emph\>Check grammar\</emph\> to work first on all spellcheck errors, then on all grammar errors.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149511				0	en-ZA	Not in dictionary				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149798				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Displays the sentence with the misspelled word highlighted. Edit the word or the sentence, or click one of the suggestions in the text box below.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149885				0	en-ZA	Suggestions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXDLG_SPELLCHECK_LB_NEWWORD\"\>Lists suggested words to replace the misspelled word. Select the word that you want to use, and then click \<emph\>Change\</emph\> or \<emph\>Change All\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145087				0	en-ZA	Text Language				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144422				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXDLG_SPELLCHECK_LB_LANGUAGE\"\>Specifies the language to use to check the spelling.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154071				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>AutoCorrect\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153798				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SPELLCHECK_BTN_AUTOCORR\"\>Adds the current combination of the incorrect word and the replacement word to the AutoCorrect replacements table.\</ahelp\>\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151382				0	en-ZA	Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SPELLCHECK_BTN_OPTIONS\"\>Opens a dialogue, where you can select the user-defined dictionaries, and set the rules for the spellchecking.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153353				0	en-ZA	Add				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144432				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SPELLCHECK_BTN_ADD\"\>Adds the unknown word to a user-defined dictionary.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155994				0	en-ZA	Ignore Once				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148920				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SVXDLG_SPELLCHECK:BTN_IGNORE\"\>Skips the unknown word and continues with the spellcheck.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CB				0	en-ZA	This label of this button changes to \<emph\>Resume\</emph\> if you leave the Spellcheck dialogue open when you return to your document. To continue the spellcheck from the current position of the cursor, click \<emph\>Resume\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id1024200804091149				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>While performing a grammar check, click Ignore Rule to ignore the rule that is currently flagged as a grammar error.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150740				0	en-ZA	Ignore All				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145318				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SVXDLG_SPELLCHECK:BTN_IGNOREALL\"\>Skips all occurrences of the unknown word in the entire document and continues with the spellcheck.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153056				0	en-ZA	Change				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148559				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SVXDLG_SPELLCHECK:BTN_CHANGE\"\>Replaces the unknown word with the current suggestion. If you changed more than just the misspelled word, the entire sentence is replaced.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145787				0	en-ZA	Change All				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144446				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SVXDLG_SPELLCHECK:BTN_CHANGEALL\"\>Replaces all occurrences of the unknown word with the current suggestion.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10850				0	en-ZA	Undo				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10854				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click to undo the last change in the current sentence. Click again to undo the previous change in the same sentence.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06020000.xhp\" name=\"Thesaurus\"\>Thesaurus\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Bullets and Numbering				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149551				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06050000.xhp\" name=\"Numbering/Bullets\"\>Bullets and Numbering\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150146				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"numauftext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BulletsAndNumberingDial\"\>Adds numbering or bullets to the current paragraph, and lets you edit format of the numbering or bullets.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145211				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Bullets and Numbering\</emph\> dialogue has the following tabs:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154984	27			0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>Remove \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NUM_RESET\"\>Removes the numbering or bullets from the current paragraph or from the selected paragraphs.\</ahelp\>\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\extensionupdate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Extension Update				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\extensionupdate.xhp	0	help	hd_id9688100				0	en-ZA	Extension Update				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\extensionupdate.xhp	0	help	par_id5084688				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click the \<emph\>Check for Updates\</emph\> button in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/packagemanager.xhp\"\>Extension Manager\</link\> to check for online updates for all installed extensions. To check for online updates for only the selected extension, right-click to open the context menu, then choose \<emph\>Update\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\extensionupdate.xhp	0	help	par_id5841242				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>While checking for updates, you see a progress indicator. Wait for some messages to show up in the dialogue, or click Cancel to abort the update check.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\extensionupdate.xhp	0	help	par_id6794030				0	en-ZA	If no updates are available, the message in the dialogue tells you there are no updates. Close the dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\extensionupdate.xhp	0	help	par_id7096774				0	en-ZA	If updates are available, the updates can either be installed automatically, or you must respond with some action:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\extensionupdate.xhp	0	help	par_id6420484				0	en-ZA	The Extension Update dialogue may contain entries which are not selectable and hence no automatic update can be performed. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\extensionupdate.xhp	0	help	par_id6986602				0	en-ZA	Dependencies are not fulfilled (the update needs some more or newer files to be installed).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\extensionupdate.xhp	0	help	par_id616779				0	en-ZA	Insufficient user rights (the Extension Manager was started from the menu, but shared extensions can only be modified when %PRODUCTNAME does not run, and only by a user with appropriate rights). See \<link href=\"text/shared/01/packagemanager.xhp\"\>Extension Manager\</link\> for details.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\extensionupdate.xhp	0	help	par_id791039				0	en-ZA	A manual update is necessary.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\extensionupdate.xhp	0	help	par_id757469				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>When you click the Install button the Download and Installation dialogue is displayed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\extensionupdate.xhp	0	help	par_id5189062				0	en-ZA	All extensions which can be directly downloaded are downloaded now. The progress is shown in the Download and Installation dialogue. If an extension cannot be downloaded, a message is displayed. The operation continues for the remaining extensions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\extensionupdate.xhp	0	help	par_id3949095				0	en-ZA	Some extensions may be marked with the phrase "browser based update". These extensions cannot be downloaded by the Extension Manager. A web browser must be opened to download the extension update from a particular web site. That site may require several more user interaction to download the extension. After downloading you must install the extension manually, for example by double-clicking the extension's icon in a file browser.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\extensionupdate.xhp	0	help	par_id3729056				0	en-ZA	For extensions marked as "browser based update", the Extension Manager will open your web browser on the respective web site. This happens when you close the dialogue, after downloading any other extension updates. If there are no extensions which can be directly downloaded then the web browser is started immediately.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\extensionupdate.xhp	0	help	par_id6854457				0	en-ZA	After the last extension has been downloaded, the installation begins. First all installed extensions for which an update could be downloaded successfully, are removed. Then the updated extensions are installed. If an error occurs, a message that the installation failed is displayed, but the operation proceeds.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\extensionupdate.xhp	0	help	par_id3372295				0	en-ZA	If all updates have been processed the Download and Installation dialogue shows that it has finished. You can abort the download and installation process by clicking the \<emph\>Abort Update\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\extensionupdate.xhp	0	help	hd_id5699942				0	en-ZA	Show all Updates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\extensionupdate.xhp	0	help	par_id7634510				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/packagemanager.xhp\"\>Extension Manager\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Data Sources				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153116				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>data source browser\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables in databases;browsing and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases; editing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; database tables and queries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>queries; editing in data source view\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153323				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340400.xhp\" name=\"Data Sources\"\>Data Sources\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149511				0	en-ZA	This section contains information on browsing and editing database tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149150				0	en-ZA	You cannot use the data source browser on a database table that is open in Design view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149235				0	en-ZA	Data source browser				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The commands for the data source browser are found on the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340400.xhp\" name=\"Database Bar\"\>Table Data bar\</link\> and in \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340400.xhp\" name=\"context menus\"\>context menus\</link\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154514				0	en-ZA	Selecting records				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149514				0	en-ZA	To select a record in a database table, click the row header, or click a row header, and then use the Up or Down arrow keys.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id7812433001				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select database records. Drag-and-drop rows or cells to the document to insert contents. Drag-and-drop column headers to insert fields.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	en-ZA	The following table describes how to select individual elements in the data source browser:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3158432				0	en-ZA	Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150670				0	en-ZA	Action				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153332				0	en-ZA	Record				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153700				0	en-ZA	Click the row header				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149575				0	en-ZA	Several records or removing a selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149295				0	en-ZA	Hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>and click the row header				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3152360				0	en-ZA	Column				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153960				0	en-ZA	Click the column header				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	en-ZA	Data field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150358				0	en-ZA	Click in the data field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	en-ZA	Entire table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	en-ZA	Click the row header of the column headings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154822				0	en-ZA	Table Data toolbar (editing table data)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3150740\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_editdoc.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150740\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3158410				0	en-ZA	Allows you to edit, add, or delete records from the database table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152463				0	en-ZA	Cutting, copying and pasting data				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149287				0	en-ZA	You can cut, copy, and paste records in \<emph\>Data Source\</emph\> view. The Data Source browser also supports the dragging and dropping of records, or text and numbers from other $[officename] files.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
