helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148643				0	en-ZA	If you are in a table or spreadsheet, you can also add or remove predefined borders. Use the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Table Bar\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149575				0	en-ZA	Line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3152360				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_BORDER:LB_LINESTYLE\"\>Click the border style that you want to apply. The style is applied to the borders selected in the preview.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_BORDER:LB_LINECOLOR\"\>Select the line colour that you want to use for the selected border(s).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150359				0	en-ZA	Spacing to contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	en-ZA	Specify the amount of space that you want to leave between the border and the contents of the selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
