helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152924				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Organizer\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Template Management\</emph\> dialogue where you can organise templates and define default templates.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801				0	en-ZA	Left and Right Selection List (Templates / Documents)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_CTL_ORGANIZER_RIGHT\"\>Displays the available template categories or opened $[officename] files. To change the contents of the list, select \<emph\>Templates\</emph\> or \<emph\>Documents\</emph\> in the box below.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	en-ZA	To change the default template path, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010300.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - Paths\"\>$[officename] - Paths\</link\>\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154810				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2:LISTBOX:DLG_ORGANIZE:LB_RIGHT_TYP\"\>Select \<emph\>Templates\</emph\> or \<emph\>Documents\</emph\> to change the contents that are displayed in the list above.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149191				0	en-ZA	Template categories are represented by folder icons. To view the template files for a category, double-click a folder.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159166				0	en-ZA	To view the styles that are used in a file, double-click the file name, and then double-click the \<emph\>Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155504				0	en-ZA	To copy a style, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>and drag the style from one file to another file. To move a style, drag the style from one file to another file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149578				0	en-ZA	Commands				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149514				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2:MENUBUTTON:DLG_ORGANIZE:BTN_EDIT\"\>Contains commands for managing and editing your templates and documents.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149575				0	en-ZA	Depending on the type of file you select in the list, the following commands are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153062				0	en-ZA	New				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_ORGANIZE_NEW\"\>Creates a new template category.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146794				0	en-ZA	Delete				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_ORGANIZE_DELETE\"\>Deletes the current selection.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154388				0	en-ZA	Edit				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156435				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_ORGANIZE_EDIT\"\>Opens the selected template for editing.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151106				0	en-ZA	Import Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_ORGANIZE_COPY_FROM\"\>Imports an additional template. To import a template, select a template folder in the list, click the \<emph\>Command\</emph\> button, and then select \<emph\>Import template\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154821				0	en-ZA	Export Template				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153104				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_ORGANIZE_COPY_TO\"\>Exports the selected template.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150651				0	en-ZA	Print				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154946				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_ORGANIZE_PRINT\"\>Prints the name and properties of the styles that are used in the file.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150767				0	en-ZA	Printer Setup				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147086				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_ORGANIZE_PRINTER_SETUP\"\>Changes the printer and its settings for the selected document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143231				0	en-ZA	Update				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_ORGANIZE_RESCAN\"\>Updates the contents of the lists.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145607				0	en-ZA	Set As Default Template				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147353				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_ORGANIZE_STDTEMPLATE_ADD\"\>Uses the selected template as the default template when you create a new $[officename] document of the same type.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153768				0	en-ZA	Reset Default Template				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155432				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_ORGANIZE_STDTEMPLATE_DEL\"\>Select a $[officename] document type to reset the default template to the original template.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159196				0	en-ZA	Address Book				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154472				0	en-ZA	Edit the field assignments and the data source for the address book.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154151				0	en-ZA	File				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156005	33			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2:PUSHBUTTON:DLG_ORGANIZE:BTN_FILES\"\>Locate a file that you want to add to the document list, and then click\<emph\> Open\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153095				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Printer setup\"\>Printer setup\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110101.xhp\" name=\"Templates: Address Book Assignment\"\>Templates: Address Book Assignment\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	List of Regular Expressions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146765				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>regular expressions; list of\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lists;regular expressions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>replacing;tab stops (regular expressions)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tab stops;regular expressions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>concatenation, see ampersand symbol\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>ampersand symbol, see also operators\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146765				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"02100001\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100001.xhp\"\>List of Regular Expressions\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149741				0	en-ZA	Character				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155577				0	en-ZA	Result/Use				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id6600543				0	en-ZA	Any character				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id9824518.00000001				0	en-ZA	Represents the given character unless otherwise specified.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3152427				0	en-ZA	.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149031				0	en-ZA	Represents any single character except for a line break or paragraph break. For example, the search term "sh.rt" returns both "shirt" and "short".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154682				0	en-ZA	^				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155351				0	en-ZA	Only finds the search term if the term is at the beginning of a paragraph. Special objects such as empty fields or character-anchored frames, at the beginning of a paragraph are ignored. Example: "^Peter".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3159194				0	en-ZA	$				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3152542				0	en-ZA	Only finds the search term if the term appears at the end of a paragraph. Special objects such as empty fields or character-anchored frames at the end of a paragraph are ignored. Example: "Peter$".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156414				0	en-ZA	*				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	en-ZA	Finds zero or more of the characters in front of the "*". For example, "Ab*c" finds "Ac", "Abc", "Abbc", "Abbbc", and so on.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	en-ZA	+				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958				0	en-ZA	Finds one or more of the characters in front of the "+". For example, "AX.+4" finds "AXx4", but not "AX4".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145313				0	en-ZA	The longest possible string that matches this search pattern in a paragraph is always found. If the paragraph contains the string "AX 4 AX4", the entire passage is highlighted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	en-ZA	?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153684				0	en-ZA	Finds zero or one of the characters in front of the "?". For example, "Texts?" finds "Text" and "Texts" and "x(ab|c)?y" finds "xy", "xaby", or "xcy".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	en-ZA	\\				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	en-ZA	Search interprets the special character that follows the "\\" as a normal character and not as a regular expression (except for the combinations \\n, \\t, \\>, and \\<). For example, "tree\\." finds "tree.", not "treed" or "trees".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3152945				0	en-ZA	\\n				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153700				0	en-ZA	Represents a line break that was inserted with the Shift+Enter key combination. To change a line break into a paragraph break, enter \<emph\>\\n\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> and \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> boxes, and then perform a search and replace.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id9262672				0	en-ZA	\\n in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box stands for a line break that was inserted with the Shift+Enter key combination.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id2366100				0	en-ZA	\\n in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box stands for a paragraph break that can be entered with the Enter or Return key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153258				0	en-ZA	\\t				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3157809				0	en-ZA	Represents a tab. You can also use this expression in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3146775	33			0	en-ZA	\\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148644	34			0	en-ZA	Only finds the search term if it appears at the end of a word. For example, "book\\>" finds "checkbook", but not "bookmark".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150670				0	en-ZA	\\<				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153666				0	en-ZA	Only finds the search term if it appears at the beginning of a word. For example, "\\<book" finds "bookmark", but not "checkbook".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149576				0	en-ZA	^$				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3151245				0	en-ZA	Finds an empty paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	en-ZA	^.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	en-ZA	Finds the first character of a paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147282				0	en-ZA	& or $0				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153961				0	en-ZA	Adds the string that was found by the search criteria in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box to the term in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box when you make a replacement.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149650				0	en-ZA	For example, if you enter "window" in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box and "&frame" in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box, the word "window" is replaced with "windowframe".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150543				0	en-ZA	You can also enter an "&" in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box to modify the \<emph\>Attributes\</emph\> or the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> of the string found by the search criteria.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	en-ZA	[abc123]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154630				0	en-ZA	Represents one of the characters that are between the brackets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156293				0	en-ZA	[a-e]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149167				0	en-ZA	Represents any of the characters that are between a and e, including both start and end characters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id100520090232005				0	en-ZA	The characters are ordered by their code numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155994				0	en-ZA	[a-eh-x]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148676				0	en-ZA	Represents any of the characters that are between a-e and h-x.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145318				0	en-ZA	[^a-s]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153351				0	en-ZA	Represents everything that is not between a and s.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156543				0	en-ZA	\\xXXXX				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	en-ZA	Represents a special character based on its four-digit hexadecimal code (XXXX).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3159252				0	en-ZA	The code for the special character depends on the font used. You can view the codes by choosing \<emph\>Insert - Special Character\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	en-ZA	|				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154985				0	en-ZA	Finds the terms that occur before the "|" and also finds the terms that occur after the "|". For example, "this|that" finds "this" and "that".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147376				0	en-ZA	{2}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103				0	en-ZA	Defines the number of times that the character in front of the opening bracket occurs. For example, "tre{2}" finds and selects "tree".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3151289				0	en-ZA	{1,2}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147317				0	en-ZA	Defines the minimum and maximum number of times that the character in front of the opening bracket can occur. For example, "tre{1,2}" finds and selects "tre" and "tree".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id4870754				0	en-ZA	{1,}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id843836				0	en-ZA	Defines the minimum number of times that the character in front of the opening bracket can occur. For example, "tre{2,}" finds "tree", "treee", and "treeeee".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148616				0	en-ZA	( )				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id2701803				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153573				0	en-ZA	Defines the characters inside the parentheses as a reference. You can then refer to the first reference in the current expression with "\\1", to the second reference with "\\2", and so on.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156061				0	en-ZA	For example, if your text contains the number 13487889 and you search using the regular expression (8)7\\1\\1, "8788" is found.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id2367931				0	en-ZA	You can also use () to group terms, for example, "a(bc)?d" finds "ad" or "abcd".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id9200109				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id5766472				0	en-ZA	Use $ (dollar) instead of \\ (backslash) to replace references. Use $0 to replace the whole found string.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154790				0	en-ZA	[:alpha:]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147397				0	en-ZA	Represents an alphabetic character. Use [:alpha:]+ to find one of them.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3152885				0	en-ZA	[:digit:]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	en-ZA	Represents a decimal digit. Use [:digit:]+ to find one of them.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153743				0	en-ZA	[:alnum:]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153281				0	en-ZA	Represents an alphanumeric character ([:alpha:] and [:digit:]).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	en-ZA	[:space:]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150961				0	en-ZA	Represents a space character (but not other whitespace characters).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150486				0	en-ZA	[:print:]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150872				0	en-ZA	Represents a printable character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	en-ZA	[:cntrl:]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	en-ZA	Represents a nonprinting character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	en-ZA	[:lower:]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145730				0	en-ZA	Represents a lowercase character if \<emph\>Match case\</emph\> is selected in \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148455				0	en-ZA	[:upper:]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150092	231			0	en-ZA	Represents an uppercase character if \<emph\>Match case\</emph\> is selected in \<emph\>Options.\</emph\>               				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	hd_id5311441				0	en-ZA	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id9568773				0	en-ZA	You can combine the search terms to form complex searches.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	hd_id71413				0	en-ZA	To find three-digit numbers alone in a paragraph				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id2924283				0	en-ZA	^[:digit:]{3}$				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id5781731				0	en-ZA	^ means the match has to be at the start of a paragraph, 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id6942045				0	en-ZA	[:digit:] matches any decimal digit, 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id4721823				0	en-ZA	{3} means there must be exactly 3 copies of "digit", 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
