helpcontent2	source\text\shared\autopi\01100200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Report Wizard - Grouping				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\autopi\01100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147000				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01100200.xhp\" name=\"Report Wizard - Grouping\"\>Report Wizard - Grouping\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\autopi\01100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3163829				0	en-ZA	You can group records in a report based on the values in one or more fields. \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select the fields by which the resulting report will be grouped. You can group up to four fields in a report.\</ahelp\> When you group more than one field, $[officename] nests the groups according to their group level.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\autopi\01100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149760				0	en-ZA	Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\autopi\01100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155805				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLGREPORT_2_GROUPING\"\>Lists the fields from your selection on the previous page of the Wizard. To group the report by a field, select the field name, then click the \<emph\>>\</emph\> button. You may select up to four levels of grouping.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\autopi\01100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155552				0	en-ZA	Groupings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\autopi\01100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLGREPORT_2_PREGROUPINGDEST\"\>Lists the fields by which the report will be grouped. To remove one level of grouping, select the field name, then click the \<emph\><\</emph\> button. You may select up to four levels of grouping.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\autopi\01100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154289				0	en-ZA	>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
