helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151110				0	en-ZA	File type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_HYPERLINK_NEWDOCUMENT:LB_DOCUMENT_TYPES\"\>Specifies the file type for the new document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20100000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146902				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/20100000.xhp\" name=\"Date\"\>Date\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154926				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:CurrentDate\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Displays the current date.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	HTML Filters and Forms				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163829				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>forms; HTML filters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163829				0	en-ZA	HTML Filters and Forms				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3147285				0	en-ZA	You can use all control elements and form events in HTML documents. There have been numerous events to date (for example, focus events), which have not been changed. They will continue to be imported and exported as ONFOCUS, ONBLUR, and so on for JavaScript and as SDONFOCUS, SDONBLUR, and so on for $[officename] Basic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3150616				0	en-ZA	Generic names that consist of the Listener interface and the method name of the event are used for all other events: An event registered as XListener::method is exported as				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	en-ZA	SDEvent-XListener-method = "/* event-code */"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3152425				0	en-ZA	Note that the XListener- and method components of this option are case sensitive.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3153683				0	en-ZA	Event handling of controls is performed using the $[officename] API. If you assign an event to a control, an object registers itself internally as a "Listener" for a specific control event. To do this, the object must use a specific interface, for example the XFocusListener Interface, so that it can react to focus events. When the event occurs, the control then invokes a special method of the Listener interface when the control receives the focus. The internally registered object then invokes the JavaScript or $[officename] Basic code, which was assigned to the event.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	en-ZA	The HTML filter now uses precisely these listener interfaces and method names so that it can import and export events as desired. You can register a focus event through				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3150506				0	en-ZA	<INPUT TYPE=text ONFOCUS="/* code */"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154289				0	en-ZA	rather than through the				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3155391				0	en-ZA	<INPUT TYPE=text SDEvent-XFocusListener-focusGained="/* code */"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	en-ZA	register. Events can therefore be registered as desired, including those not offered in the list boxes. To define the script language of events, you can write the following line in the document header:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	en-ZA	<META HTTP-EQUIV="content-script-type" CONTENT="...">				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	en-ZA	As CONTENT you can, for example, use "text/x-StarBasic" for $[officename] Basic or a "text/JavaScript" for JavaScript. If no entry is made, JavaScript is assumed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	en-ZA	During exporting, the default script language will be defined based on the first module found in macro management. For events, only one language can be used per document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\05110000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Alignment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\05110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154228				0	en-ZA	Alignment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159201				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ObjectAlign\"\>Modifies the alignment of selected objects.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3153577\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_objectalign.png\" width=\"0.2228inch\" height=\"0.2228inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153577\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143268				0	en-ZA	Alignment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149991				0	en-ZA	Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149987				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>database contents; inserting as fields\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149987	8			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_RADIOBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_RB_AS_FIELD\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts data selected from the data source browser into the document as fields.\</ahelp\>In the \<emph\>Insert Database Columns\</emph\> dialogue, select the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Fields\</link\> to insert the selected data into the document as fields. These \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090006.xhp\" name=\"database fields\"\>database fields\</link\> work as wildcards for the individual database columns and can be used for form letters. Click the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12080000.xhp\" name=\"Data to Fields\"\>\<emph\>Data to Fields\</emph\>\</link\> icon to match the contents of the fields to the currently selected record.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153114				0	en-ZA	If several records are selected when you choose the \<emph\>Data to Text\</emph\> function, the mail merge fields will be inserted according to the number of records. Also, a field command such as "Next record" will be inserted automatically between individual field command blocks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Insert Database Columns\</emph\> dialogue lets you define which database fields to insert into the document and how to format the paragraphs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156136				0	en-ZA	Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Fields\</emph\> area, use the arrow button to select the database table columns into which you want to insert field contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	en-ZA	Database columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	en-ZA	Lists all columns of the database table, which can be accepted in the selection list box to insert them into the document. \<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_LB_TXT_DB_COLUMN\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Select the database columns that you want to insert it in the document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152551				0	en-ZA	>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp visibility=\"visible\" hid=\"SW_IMAGEBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_IB_DBCOL_TOEDIT\"\>Moves the fields that you selected in the \<emph\>Database columns\</emph\> list box into the selection field.\</ahelp\> You can also double-click the entry to select it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166411				0	en-ZA	Select				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_MULTILINEEDIT_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_ED_DB_TEXT\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Lists the database columns that you selected to be inserted into the document. You can also enter text here. This text will be also inserted into the document.\</ahelp\> The entries' order in the selection field corresponds to the data order in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153257				0	en-ZA	Paragraph Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430				0	en-ZA	By default, the inserted paragraphs are formatted with the current Paragraph Styles. This format corresponds to the "none" entry in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> list box. \<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_LB_DB_PARA_COLL\" visibility=\"visible\"\>This is where you can select other Paragraph Styles to apply to the paragraph you want to insert into the document.\</ahelp\> The list box displays the available Paragraph Styles defined in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> and managed in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"Style Catalog\"\>Style Catalog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Special Tips for Table Controls				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	bm_id3109850				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>table controls; properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; properties of table controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table controls;keyboard-only edit mode\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109850				0	en-ZA	Special Tips for Table Controls				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153539				0	en-ZA	You can define a table control to display the records as you like. In other words you can define data fields for displaying or editing data like in a database form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3152372				0	en-ZA	The following fields are possible in a table control: text, date, time and currency field, numeric field, pattern field, check box and combo box. In the case of combined date/time fields, two columns are created automatically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159194				0	en-ZA	The number of selected lines, if any are selected, is in parentheses after the total number of records.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155616				0	en-ZA	To insert columns into the table control, click in the column heads and bring up the context menu. The following commands are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	en-ZA	Insert Column				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_INSERTCOL\"\>Calls a submenu to select a data field to adopt it in the table control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552				0	en-ZA	Configure the table control using drag and drop: Open the data source browser and drag the desired fields out of the data source browser and on to the column heads of the table control. A pre-configured column is created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149827				0	en-ZA	Replace with				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_CHANGECOL\"\>Opens a submenu to select a data field to replace the data field selected in the table control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267				0	en-ZA	Delete Column				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_DELETECOL\"\>Deletes the currently selected column.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275				0	en-ZA	Column				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	en-ZA	Opens the properties dialogue of the selected column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148539				0	en-ZA	Hide Columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_HIDECOL\"\>Hides the selected column.\</ahelp\> Its properties are not changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150771				0	en-ZA	Show columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159400				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWCOLS\"\>Calls a submenu where you can select the columns to show again.\</ahelp\> To show only one column, click the column name. You see only the first 16 hidden columns. If there are more hidden columns, choose the \<emph\>More\</emph\> command to call the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156193				0	en-ZA	More				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159269				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWCOLS_MORE\"\>Calls the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialogue.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVX_DLG_SHOWGRIDCOLUMNS:1\"\>In the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialogue you can select the columns to be shown. Hold down the Shift or Ctrl (Mac: Command) key to select multiple entries.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153561				0	en-ZA	All				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504	87			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWALLCOLS\"\>Click \<emph\>All \</emph\>if you want to show all columns.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153349				0	en-ZA	Keyboard-only control of Table Controls				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149416				0	en-ZA	If you use the keyboard only to travel through controls in your document, you will find one difference to the other types of controls: the Tab key does not move the cursor to the next control, but moves to the next column inside the table control. Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to move to the next control, or press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to move to the previous control.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153062				0	en-ZA	To enter the special keyboard-only edit mode for Table Controls:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3144510				0	en-ZA	The form document must be in \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170500.xhp\" name=\"design mode\"\>design mode\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	en-ZA	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 to select the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3161657				0	en-ZA	Press Shift+F4 to select the first control. If the Table Control is not the first control, press Tab until it is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056				0	en-ZA	Press Enter to enter the edit mode. The handles are shown farther out from the control border.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938				0	en-ZA	In the edit mode, you can open the edit mode context menu by pressing Shift+F10.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	en-ZA	If you want to edit columns, press Shift+Space to enter column edit mode. Now you can rearrange the order of columns with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Arrow keys. The Delete key deletes the current column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	en-ZA	Press the Escape key to exit the edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Special Tips for Date Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150445				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>date fields; properties\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150445				0	en-ZA	Special Tips for Date Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154230				0	en-ZA	When you enter a year using two digits, the corresponding four digit value is determined by a setting in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - General\</emph\>. For example, if 1935 is set as the lower limiting value and you enter 34 as a date value, then the result is 2034 instead of 1934.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149205				0	en-ZA	The pre-set limit value will be saved for each document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02040000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Text running from left to right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153255				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/02040000.xhp\" name=\"Text running from left to right\"\>Text running from left to right\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153539				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:TextdirectionLeftToRigh\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Specifies the horizontal direction of the text.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147291				0	en-ZA	\<image src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_textdirectionlefttoright.png\" id=\"img_id3155805\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155805\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153749				0	en-ZA	Text direction from left to right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	AutoSpellcheck On/Off				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155599				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/18030000.xhp\" name=\"AutoSpellcheck On/Off\"\>AutoSpellcheck On/Off\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150040				0	en-ZA	\<image src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_spellonline.png\" id=\"img_id3150808\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150808\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	en-ZA	AutoSpellcheck On/Off				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01171100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Wizards On/Off				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01171100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155934				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01171100.xhp\" name=\"Wizards On/Off\"\>Wizards On/Off\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01171100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147143				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:UseWizards\"\>Specifies whether to start the wizard automatically when inserting a new control.\</ahelp\> This setting applies globally to all documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01171100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159201				0	en-ZA	There are wizards for inserting a list box or combo box, a table element and group boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Combo Box / List Box Wizard: Table Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154228				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170901.xhp\" name=\"Combo Box / List Box Wizard: Table Selection\"\>Combo Box / List Box Wizard: Table Selection\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	par_id3149716				0	en-ZA	Specifies a table from the available database tables that contains the data field whose content should be displayed as a list entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	par_id3153114				0	en-ZA	For list boxes, a table that can be linked with the current form table is indicated. The link table must have at least one field in common with the table of the current form. This makes it possible to establish an unambiguous reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	en-ZA	For combo boxes, there must be a relationship between the form table and the table containing the data to be displayed in the combo box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147226				0	en-ZA	Table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338	7			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_LISTBOX_RID_PAGE_LCW_CONTENTSELECTION_TABLE_LB_SELECTTABLE\"\>In the\<emph\> Table \</emph\>field, select the table containing the data field whose content should be displayed in the control field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	en-ZA	The table given here appears in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\"Control properties\"\>Control properties\</link\> as an element of an SQL statement in the \<emph\>List Contents\</emph\> field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24090000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Transparency				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159411				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/24090000.xhp\" name=\"Transparency\"\>Transparency\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150445				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:GrafTransparence\"\>Specifies the transparency in the graphic object.\</ahelp\> Values from 0% (fully opaque) to +100% (fully transparent) are possible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
