helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01230000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Styles and Formatting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01230000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154228				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01230000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01230000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144436				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DesignerDialog\"\>Specifies whether to show or hide the Styles and Formatting window, which is where you can assign and organise Styles.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01230000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153894				0	en-ZA	Each $[officename] application has its own Styles and Formatting window. Hence there are separate windows for \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05140000.xhp\" name=\"text documents\"\>text documents\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>text documents\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, for \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05100000.xhp\" name=\"spreadsheets\"\>spreadsheets\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>spreadsheets\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and for \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"IMPRESS\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/05100000.xhp\" name=\"presentations/drawing documents\"\>presentations/drawing documents\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/05100000.xhp\" name=\"presentations/drawing documents\"\>presentations/drawing documents\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>presentations/drawing documents\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01230000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3149999\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_designerdialog.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149999\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01230000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154750				0	en-ZA	Styles and Formatting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24100000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Crop				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154044				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/24100000.xhp\" name=\"Crop\"\>Crop\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154863				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:GrafAttrCrop\"\>Allows to crop the display of an inserted picture. Only the display gets cropped, the inserted picture is not changed.\</ahelp\> A picture must be selected to enable cropping.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24100000.xhp	0	help	par_id0514200804261097				0	en-ZA	In Impress and Draw no dialogue is shown when you click the icon, but you see eight cropping handles. Open the context menu of a selected picture and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Crop Picture\</item\>, if you want to use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030800.xhp\"\>dialogue\</link\> for cropping.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24100000.xhp	0	help	par_id0514200804261043				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Drag any of the eight cropping handles to crop the picture.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24100000.xhp	0	help	par_id0522200809440491				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id0522200809434429\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_crop.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id0522200809434429\"\>icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154927				0	en-ZA	Crop				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Print File Directly				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153539				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>printing; directly\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153539				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01110000.xhp\" name=\"Print File Directly\"\>Print File Directly\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154398				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:PrintDefault\"\>Click the \<emph\>Print File Directly\</emph\> icon to print the active document with the current default print settings.\</ahelp\> These can be found in the \<emph\>Printer Setup\</emph\> dialogue, which you can call with the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Printer Settings\"\>\<emph\>Printer Settings\</emph\>\</link\> menu command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275	3			0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>If you select text or a graphic and click the \<emph\>Print File Direct\</emph\> icon, you are prompted to print the selection or the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_id9547105				0	en-ZA	If the current document uses a printer that is not the default printer for your operating system, the \<emph\>Print File Direct \</emph\>icon opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Print\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10679				0	en-ZA	If the current document uses a printer that is not the default printer that was specified in the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/spadmin.xhp\"\>spadmin\</link\>, printer administration program, the \<emph\>Print File Direct \</emph\>icon opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Print\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Setting Indents, Margins, and Columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148668				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>margins; setting with the mouse\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; setting with the mouse\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; indents, margins and columns\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148668				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/13020000.xhp\" name=\"Setting Indents, Margins, and Columns\"\>Setting Indents, Margins, and Columns\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155364				0	en-ZA	You can define the indents and margins for the current paragraph, or for all selected paragraphs, using the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152594				0	en-ZA	If you split the page into columns, or the cursor is placed in a multiple-column text frame, you can change the column width and the column spacing by dragging them on the ruler with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154398				0	en-ZA	When an object, an image, or a draw object is selected, you will see the borders of the object in the ruler. You can change the borders by dragging them on the ruler with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146130				0	en-ZA	If the cursor is placed in a table cell, you can change the indents for the contents of the cell by dragging them with the mouse on the ruler. You can change the boundary lines of the table on the ruler or by dragging the actual boundary line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156136				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3153750\" src=\"res/helpimg/linleft.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.2291inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153750\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150693				0	en-ZA	These icons mark the left indent for the first line of the current paragraph (top triangle) and the left indent for the other lines of the paragraph (bottom triangle).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3145071\" src=\"res/helpimg/linright.png\" width=\"0.3646inch\" height=\"0.2602inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145071\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	en-ZA	This icon on the right of the ruler marks the right indent of the current paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146949				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Task\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153087				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Procedure\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154143				0	en-ZA	Set left indent				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154307				0	en-ZA	Drag the bottom left mark to the right while pressing the mouse button				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155449				0	en-ZA	Set left indent of first line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145673				0	en-ZA	Drag the top left mark to the right while pressing the mouse button				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156156				0	en-ZA	Set right indent				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153761				0	en-ZA	Drag the mark on the right to the left while pressing the mouse button				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	en-ZA	In order to change the left indent starting with the second line of a paragraph, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, click the triangle on the bottom left, and drag it to the right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148453				0	en-ZA	Tabs that have been set are not changed when indenting a paragraph. If the set tabs end up outside the margins of the paragraph, they are no longer displayed, but they still exist.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Form Navigator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143284				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>controls;arranging in forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms;Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Form Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subforms; creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; hidden\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hidden controls in Form Navigator\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143284				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigator\"\>Form Navigator\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149760				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowFmExplorer\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> displays all forms and subforms of the current document with their respective controls.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	en-ZA	When using several forms, the Form Navigator gives an overview of all forms, and also provides various functions for editing them.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FORM_NAVIGATOR\"\>The \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> contains a list of all created (logical) forms with the corresponding control fields.\</ahelp\> You can see whether a form contains control fields by the plus sign displayed before the entry. Click the plus sign to open the list of the form elements.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	en-ZA	You can change how the different controls are arranged by dragging and dropping them in the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\>. Select one or more controls and drag them into another form. Alternatively use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+X or the context menu command \<emph\>Cut\</emph\> to move a control to the clipboard and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V or the command \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> to insert the control into another position.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	en-ZA	To edit the name in the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\>, click on the name and enter a new name, or use the command in the context menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156347				0	en-ZA	If you select a control in the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\>, the corresponding element is selected in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153662				0	en-ZA	If you call the context menu of a selected entry, the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> offers the following functions:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153252				0	en-ZA	New				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561	8			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_NEW\"\>Adds new elements to the form. The\<emph\> Add \</emph\>function can only be called if a form is selected in the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149763				0	en-ZA	Form				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156117	10			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_NEW_FORM\"\>Creates a new form in the document. \</ahelp\> To create a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"subform\"\>subform\</link\>, add the new form under the desired parent form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155342				0	en-ZA	Hidden Control				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_NEW_HIDDEN\"\>Creates a hidden control in the selected form that is not displayed on the screen. A hidden control serves to include data that is transmitted together with the form.\</ahelp\> It contains additional information or clarifying text that you can specify when creating the form through the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"Special Properties\"\>Special Properties\</link\> of the control. Select the entry of the hidden control in the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> and select the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3159147				0	en-ZA	You can copy controls in the document through the clipboard (shortcut keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C for copying and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V for inserting). You can copy hidden controls in the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> by using drag-and-drop while keeping the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key pressed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068				0	en-ZA	Drag and drop to copy controls within the same document or between documents. Open another form document and drag the hidden control from the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> into the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> of the target document. Click a visible control directly in the document, rest the mouse for a moment so that a copy of the control is added to the drag-and-drop clipboard, then drag the copy into the other document. If you want a copy in the same document, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>while dragging.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152812				0	en-ZA	Delete				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_DELETE\"\>Deletes the selected entry.\</ahelp\> This allows you to delete individual form components as well as whole forms with one mouse click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153799				0	en-ZA	Tab order				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156282				0	en-ZA	When a form is selected, it opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170300.xhp\" name=\"Tab Order\"\>\<emph\>Tab Order\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue, where the indices for focusing the control elements on the Tab key are defined.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150869				0	en-ZA	Rename				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3145607				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_RENAME_OBJECT\"\>Renames the selected object.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153194				0	en-ZA	Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149766				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowPropertyBrowser\"\>Starts the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialogue for the selected entry.\</ahelp\> If a form is selected, the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170200.xhp\" name=\"Form Properties\"\>Form Properties\</link\> dialogue opens. If a control is selected, the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170100.xhp\" name=\"Control Properties\"\>Control Properties\</link\> dialogue opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Format Paintbrush				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1056A				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/paintbrush.xhp\"\>Format Paintbrush\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057A				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>First select some text or an object, then click this icon. Then click on or drag across other text or click an object to apply the same formatting.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3610034\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatpaintbrush.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3610034\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> toolbar. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10639				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id5406964\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatpaintbrush.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5406964\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10657				0	en-ZA	Format Paintbrush				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\07080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Stop Loading				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\07080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154228				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/07080000.xhp\" name=\"Stop Loading\"\>Stop Loading\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\07080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149495				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Stop\"\>Click to interrupt the current loading process, Ctrl-click (Mac: Command-click) to interrupt all loading processes.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\callouts.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Callouts				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\callouts.xhp	0	help	bm_id9298379				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>callouts; drawings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>speech bubbles\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\callouts.xhp	0	help	par_idN1055A				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/callouts.xhp\"\>Callouts\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\callouts.xhp	0	help	par_idN1056A				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the Callouts toolbar from which you can insert graphics into your document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\callouts.xhp	0	help	par_idN10594				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click an icon from the Callouts toolbar, then drag in the document to draw the shape.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\callouts.xhp	0	help	par_idN10597				0	en-ZA	Some shapes have a special handle which you can drag to change properties of the shape. The mouse pointer changes to a hand symbol over these special handles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Sort Descending				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154689				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12020000.xhp\" name=\"Sort Descending\"\>Sort Descending\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149987	2			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SortDown\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sorts the data of the selected field in descending order.\</ahelp\>Text fields are sorted alphabetically, number fields are sorted by number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149496				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3153255\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_sortdescending.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153255\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144436				0	en-ZA	Sort Descending				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154873				0	en-ZA	Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070300.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143284				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>database contents; inserting as text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3143284	3			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:RB_AS_TEXT\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts data selected from the data source browser into the document as text.\</ahelp\>If you select the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> option in the \<emph\>Insert Database Columns\</emph\> dialogue, the content of the data selected in the data source browser is inserted into the document as text. In the dialogue, you can decide which database fields or columns are transferred, and how the text is formatted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154289				0	en-ZA	If several records are selected when you choose the \<emph\>Data to Text\</emph\> function, the mail merge fields will be inserted according to the number of records.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155392				0	en-ZA	Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> area, use the arrow button to select the database table columns into which you want to insert field contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Events				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148643				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>controls; events\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>events; controls\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>macros; assigning to events in forms\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148643				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170103.xhp\" name=\"Events\"\>Events\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152350	2			0	en-ZA	On the\<emph\> Events \</emph\>tab page you can link macros to events that occur in a form's control fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	en-ZA	When the event occurs, the linked macro will be called. To assign a macro to an event, press the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button. An \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05060700.xhp\" name=\"Assign Macro\"\>Assign Macro\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>dialogue\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149732				0	en-ZA	Depending on the control, different events are available. Only the available events for the selected control and context are listed on the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> tab page. The following events are defined:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149191				0	en-ZA	Approve action				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153717				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_APPROVEACTIONPERFORMED\"\>This event takes place before an action is triggered by clicking the control.\</ahelp\> For example, clicking a "Submit" button initiates a send action; however, the actual "send" process is started only when the \<emph\>When initiating\</emph\> event occurs. The \<emph\>Approve action\</emph\> event allows you to kill the process. If the linked method sends back FALSE, \<emph\>When initiating\</emph\> will not be executed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156024				0	en-ZA	Execute action				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_ACTIONPERFORMED\"\>The \<emph\>Execute action\</emph\> event occurs when an action is started.\</ahelp\> For example, if you have a "Submit" button in your form, the send process represents the action to be initiated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156343				0	en-ZA	Changed				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148755	42			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_CHANGED\"\>The\<emph\> Changed \</emph\>event takes place when the control loses the focus and the content of the control has changed since it lost the focus.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153524				0	en-ZA	Text modified				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150495	11			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_TEXTCHANGED\"\>The\<emph\> Text modified \</emph\>event takes place if you enter or modify a text in an input field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154123				0	en-ZA	Item status changed				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870	9			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_ITEMSTATECHANGED\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The\<emph\> Item status changed \</emph\>event takes place if the status of the control field has changed.\</ahelp\>The\<emph\> Item status changed\</emph\> event takes place if he status of the control field has changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151176				0	en-ZA	When receiving focus				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154218	17			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_FOCUSGAINED\"\>The\<emph\> When receiving focus \</emph\>event takes place if a control field receives the focus.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150447				0	en-ZA	When losing focus				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3159252	19			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_FOCUSLOST\"\>The\<emph\> When losing focus \</emph\>event takes place if a control field looses the focus.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147287				0	en-ZA	Key pressed				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152940	21			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_KEYTYPED\"\>The \<emph\>Key pressed \</emph\>event occurs when the user presses any key while the control has the focus.\</ahelp\> This event may be linked to a macro for checking entries.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154127				0	en-ZA	Key released				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154150	44			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_KEYUP\"\>The\<emph\> Key released \</emph\>event occurs when the user releases any key while the control has the focus.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154921				0	en-ZA	Mouse inside				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618	27			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_MOUSEENTERED\"\>The\<emph\> Mouse inside \</emph\>event takes place if the mouse is inside the control field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148576				0	en-ZA	Mouse moved while key pressed				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411	31			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_MOUSEDRAGGED\"\>The\<emph\> Mouse moved while key pressed \</emph\>event takes place when the mouse is dragged while a key is pressed.\</ahelp\> An example is when, during drag-and-drop, an additional key determines the mode (move or copy).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149262				0	en-ZA	Mouse moved				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975	33			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_MOUSEMOVED\"\>The\<emph\> Mouse moved \</emph\>event occurs if the mouse moves over the control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159197				0	en-ZA	Mouse button pressed				2002-02-02 02:02:02
