helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\19090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154788				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/19090000.xhp\" name=\"HTML Source\"\>HTML Source\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\19090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156183				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SourceView\"\>Displays the source text of the current HTML document. To view the HTML source of a new document, you must first save the new document as an HTML document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\19090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149760				0	en-ZA	In HTML Source mode, you can view and edit the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#tags\" name=\"tags\"\>tags\</link\> of \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#html\" name=\"HTML\"\>HTML\</link\>. Save the document as a plain text document. Assign an .html or .htm extension to designate the document as HTML.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151299				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/18010000.xhp\" name=\"Selection\"\>Selection\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148520				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SelectObject\"\>Allows you to select objects in the current document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149511				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3159194\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_drawselect.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159194\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	en-ZA	Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	en-ZA	To select an object, click the object with the arrow. To select more than one object, drag a selection frame around the objects. To add an object to a selection, press Shift, and then click the object. \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CHART\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"MATH\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>The objects selected together can then be defined as a \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05290000.xhp\" name=\"group\"\>group\</link\>, turning them into a single group object.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CHART\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"MATH\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>You can edit individual elements of a group. You can also delete elements from a group with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Shift\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+click.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CHART\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"MATH\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>You can select single objects from a group by double-clicking, if you first disable the \<emph\>Double-click to edit Text\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Option\</emph\> Bar.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Red				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151097				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/24030000.xhp\" name=\"Red\"\>Red\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151100				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:GrafRed\"\>Specifies the proportion of red RGB colour components for the selected graphic object.\</ahelp\> Values from -100% (no red) to +100% (full red) are possible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
