helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Sort Order				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147000				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>sorting; databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases; sorting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147000				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"sortierung\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12100100.xhp\" name=\"Sort Order\"\>Sort Order\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3163829				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"sortierentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:OrderCrit\"\>Specifies the sort criteria for the data display.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149549	12			0	en-ZA	While the functions \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12010000.xhp\" name=\"Sort in Ascending Order\"\>\<emph\>Sort in Ascending Order\</emph\>\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12020000.xhp\" name=\"Sort in Descending Order\"\>\<emph\>Sort in Descending Order\</emph\>\</link\> sort by one criterion only, you can combine several criteria in the\<emph\> Sort Order \</emph\>dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136				0	en-ZA	You can remove a sorting that has been performed with the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12040000.xhp\" name=\"Remove Filter/Sorting\"\>\<emph\>Remove Filter/Sorting\</emph\>\</link\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148548				0	en-ZA	Sorting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155941				0	en-ZA	Use this area to enter sorting criteria. If you enter additional sorting criteria under \<emph\>and then\</emph\>, the data matching the content of the higher-order criterion is ordered according to the next criterion.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148620				0	en-ZA	If you sort the field name "First name" in ascending order and the field name "last name" in descending order, all records will be sorted in ascending order by first name, and then within the first names, in descending order by last name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345				0	en-ZA	Field name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:OrderCrit\"\>Specifies the data field name whose content will determine the sort order.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150774				0	en-ZA	Order				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:OrderCrit\"\>Specifies the sort order (either ascending or descending).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275				0	en-ZA	and then				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	en-ZA	Specifies additional subordinate sort criteria from the other fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\symbolshapes.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Symbol Shapes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\symbolshapes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1055A				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/symbolshapes.xhp\"\>Symbol Shapes\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\symbolshapes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1056A				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the Symbol Shapes toolbar from which you can insert graphics into your document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\symbolshapes.xhp	0	help	par_idN105EB				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click an icon on the Symbol Shapes toolbar, and then drag in the document to draw the shape.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\symbolshapes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1059D				0	en-ZA	Some shapes have a special handle which you can drag to change the properties of the shape. The mouse pointer changes to a hand symbol over these special handles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\10010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Previous Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\10010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154228				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/10010000.xhp\" name=\"Previous Page\"\>Previous Page\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\10010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150445				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:PreviousPage\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Moves back to the previous page in the document.\</ahelp\> This function is only active when you select the \<emph\>Page Preview\</emph\> function on the \<emph\>File\</emph\> menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\10010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552				0	en-ZA	\<image src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_pageup.png\" id=\"img_id3145090\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145090\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\10010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147577				0	en-ZA	Previous Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	General				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153681				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"General\"\>General\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233	2			0	en-ZA	This \<emph\>General \</emph\>tab enables you to define the general properties of a form control. These properties differ, depending on the control type. Not all of the following properties are available for every control.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155342				0	en-ZA	If you export the current form document to HTML format, the default control values are exported, not the current control values. Default values are determined - depending on the type of control - by the properties' Default value (for example, in text fields), Default status (for check boxes and option fields), and Default selection (for list boxes).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149734				0	en-ZA	Enabled				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ENABLED\"\>If a control field has the property "Enabled" (Yes), the form user will be able to use the control field.\</ahelp\> If the property is disabled, it will not be enabled (No) and will be displayed in a grey colour.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153320				0	en-ZA	Line count				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149235	75			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_LINECOUNT\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies how many lines should be displayed in the dropdown list. This setting is only active if you chose "Yes" in the "Dropdown" option.\</ahelp\>For combo boxes with the Dropdown property, you can specify how many lines should be displayed in the dropdown list. With control fields which do not have the Dropdown option, the line's display will be specified by the size of the control field and the font size.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153147				0	en-ZA	Action				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149415	24			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_BUTTONTYPE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The Action property determines the action that occurs when you activate a button.\</ahelp\>You can use navigation actions to design your own database navigation buttons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152474				0	en-ZA	The following table describes the actions that you can assign to a button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147303				0	en-ZA	Action				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154388				0	en-ZA	Description				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154071				0	en-ZA	None				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153797				0	en-ZA	No action occurs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154216				0	en-ZA	Submit form				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228	31			0	en-ZA	Sends the data that is entered in other control fields of the current form to the address that is specified in \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170200.xhp\" name=\"Form Properties\"\>Form Properties\</link\> under \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170201.xhp\" name=\"URL\"\>\<emph\>URL\</emph\>\</link\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F7				0	en-ZA	Enter the URL into the form's data property "URL" text box when you export to a PDF file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	en-ZA	Reset form				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155101				0	en-ZA	Resets the settings in other control fields to the predefined defaults (Default Status, Default Selection, Default Value).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155431				0	en-ZA	Open document / web page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	en-ZA	Opens the URL that is specified under \<emph\>URL\</emph\>. You can use \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> to specify the target frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FE				0	en-ZA	First record				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10803				0	en-ZA	Moves the current form to the first record.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10809				0	en-ZA	Previous record				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1080E				0	en-ZA	Moves the current form to the previous record.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10814				0	en-ZA	Next record				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10819				0	en-ZA	Moves the current form to the next record.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081F				0	en-ZA	Last record				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10824				0	en-ZA	Moves the current form to the last record.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082A				0	en-ZA	Save record				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082F				0	en-ZA	Saves the current record, if necessary.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10835				0	en-ZA	Undo data entry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1083A				0	en-ZA	Reverses the changes in the current record.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10840				0	en-ZA	New record				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10845				0	en-ZA	Moves the current form to the insert row.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084B				0	en-ZA	Delete record				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10850				0	en-ZA	Deletes the current record.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10856				0	en-ZA	Refresh form				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1085B				0	en-ZA	Reloads the most recently saved version of the current form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154638				0	en-ZA	Dropdown				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577	20			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DROPDOWN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether the combo box should dropdown (Yes) or not (No).\</ahelp\>A control field with the dropdown property has an additional arrow button which opens the list of the existing form entries per mouse click. Under \<emph\>Line count\</emph\>, you can specify how many lines (or rows) should be displayed in the dropdown state. Combination fields can have the dropdown property.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159198				0	en-ZA	Combo boxes that were inserted as columns in a table control are always dropdown as the default.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153140				0	en-ZA	Alignment / Graphics alignment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151281	12			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ALIGN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the alignment option for text or graphics that are used on a control.\</ahelp\>The alignment options are left-aligned, right-aligned, and centred. These options are available for the following elements:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN109DD				0	en-ZA	Title of Label fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E1				0	en-ZA	Content of text fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E5				0	en-ZA	Content of table fields in the columns of a table control				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E9				0	en-ZA	Graphics or text that are used in buttons				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN109EC				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> option for buttons is called \<emph\>Graphics alignment\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151073				0	en-ZA	AutoFill				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152375	77			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_AUTOCOMPLETE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Assigns the AutoFill function to a combo box.\</ahelp\>The AutoFill function displays a list of previous entries after you start to type an entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154729				0	en-ZA	Label field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CONTROLLABEL\"\>Specifies the source for the label of the control.\</ahelp\> The text of the label field will be used instead of the name of a database field. For example, in the \<emph\>Filter Navigator\</emph\>, \<emph\>Search\</emph\> dialogue, and as a column name in the table view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153223				0	en-ZA	To define one character of the label as a mnemonic, so that the user can access this control by pressing the character on the keyboard, insert a tilde (~) character in front of the character in the label.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154502				0	en-ZA	Only the text of a group frame can be used as the label field when using radio buttons. This text applies to all of the radio buttons of the same group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148587				0	en-ZA	If you click on the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button next to the text field, you will see the \<emph\>Label Field Selection\</emph\> dialogue. Select a label from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154512	220			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"PCR_CHECKBOX_RID_DLG_SELECTLABELCONTROL_1\"\>Check the \<emph\>No assignment \</emph\>box to remove the link between a control and the assigned label field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148834				0	en-ZA	Width				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148566	143			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_WIDTH\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the column width in the table control field.\</ahelp\>Sets the column width in the table control field in the units that are specified in the %PRODUCTNAME module options. If you want, you can enter a value followed by a valid measurement unit, for example, 2 cm.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id1877803				0	en-ZA	Repeat				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id9863277				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_REPEAT\"\>Specifies if the action of a control such as a spin button repeats when you click the control and hold the mouse button down.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id9827875				0	en-ZA	Delay				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id6092715				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_REPEAT_DELAY\"\>Specifies the delay in milliseconds between repeating events.\</ahelp\> A repeating event occurs when you click an arrow button or the background of a scrollbar, or one of the record navigation buttons of a Navigation Bar, and you keep the mouse button pressed for some time. You can enter a value followed by a valid time unit, for example, 2 s or 500 ms.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145164				0	en-ZA	Record marker				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147257				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_RECORDMARKER\"\>Specifies whether the first column is displayed with row labels, in which the current record is marked by an arrow.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151019				0	en-ZA	Date format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152971	83			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATEFORMAT\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Here, you can determine the format you want for the date readout.\</ahelp\>With date fields you can determine the format for the date readout.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151356				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"hinweis\"\>All format fields (date, time, currency, numeric) are formatted automatically in the selected format as soon as you leave them regardless of how you entered the input.\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156054				0	en-ZA	Spin Button				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154360	88			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SPIN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The "Yes" option transforms the control field into a spin button, where corresponding arrow buttons are added.\</ahelp\>Numerical fields, currency fields, date and time fields can be introduced as spin buttons in the form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159268				0	en-ZA	Tristate				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154254				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TRISTATE\"\>Specifies whether a check box can also represent ZERO values of a linked database apart from the TRUE and FALSE values.\</ahelp\> This function is only available if the database accepts three states: TRUE, FALSE and ZERO.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156712	183			0	en-ZA	The\<emph\> Tristate \</emph\>property is only defined for database forms, not for HTML forms.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147324				0	en-ZA	Printable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154703				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_PRINTABLE\"\>Specifies whether you want the control field to appear in a document's printout.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id0409200921153889				0	en-ZA	PositionX				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200921153823				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Defines the X position of the control, relative to the anchor.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id0409200921153814				0	en-ZA	PositionY				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id040920092115387				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Defines the Y position of the control, relative to the anchor.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id0409200921153833				0	en-ZA	Anchor				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200921153855				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Defines where the control will be anchored.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id0409200921153836				0	en-ZA	Width				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200921153918				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Defines the width of the control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id0409200921153980				0	en-ZA	Height				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200921153919				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Defines the height of the control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155962				0	en-ZA	Edit mask				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150938	92			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_EDITMASK\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Defines the edit mask. By specifying a character code you can determine what the user can enter in the control field.\</ahelp\>By specifying the character code in pattern fields, you can determine what the user can enter in the pattern field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148479				0	en-ZA	The length of the edit mask determines the number of the possible input positions. If the user enters characters that do not correspond to the edit mask, the input is rejected when the user leaves the field. You can enter the following characters to define the edit mask:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147130	93			0	en-ZA	 Character 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149815				0	en-ZA	Meaning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153774				0	en-ZA	L				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154660				0	en-ZA	A text constant. This position cannot be edited. The character is displayed at the corresponding position of the Literal Mask.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151346				0	en-ZA	a				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150829				0	en-ZA	The characters a-z and A-Z can be entered. Capital characters are not converted to lowercase characters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149207				0	en-ZA	A				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156140				0	en-ZA	The characters A-Z can be entered. If a lowercase letter is entered, it is automatically converted to a capital letter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153703				0	en-ZA	c				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148873				0	en-ZA	The characters a-z, A-Z, and 0-9 can be entered. Capital characters are not converted to lowercase characters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153781				0	en-ZA	C				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154574				0	en-ZA	The characters A-Z and 0-9 can be entered. If a lowercase letter is entered, it is automatically converted to a capital letter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153268				0	en-ZA	N				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150979				0	en-ZA	Only the characters 0-9 can be entered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152769				0	en-ZA	x				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156064				0	en-ZA	All printable characters can be entered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150517				0	en-ZA	X				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150429				0	en-ZA	All printable characters can be entered. If a lowercase letter is used, it is automatically converted to a capital letter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155081				0	en-ZA	For the literal mask "__.__.2000", for example, define the "NNLNNLLLLL" edit mask so that the user can only enter four digits when entering a date.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154818				0	en-ZA	Strict format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148750				0	en-ZA	You can have a format check with control fields that accept formatted contents (date, time, and so on). \<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_STRICTFORMAT\"\>If the strict format function is activated (Yes), only the allowed characters are accepted.\</ahelp\> For example, in a date field, only numbers or date delimiters are accepted; all alphabet entries typed with your keyboard are ignored.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147167				0	en-ZA	Frame				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154991	61			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TARGET_FRAME\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the target frame to display the document that is opened by the "Open document / web page" action.\</ahelp\>You can also specify the target frame to display a \<emph\>URL\</emph\> that you open when you click a button that has been assigned the Open document or web page action).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150521				0	en-ZA	If you click the field, you can select an option from the list that specifies into which frame the next document should be loaded. The following possibilities exist:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148814				0	en-ZA	Entry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155500				0	en-ZA	Meaning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149408				0	en-ZA	_blank				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146770				0	en-ZA	The next document is created in a new empty frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149771				0	en-ZA	_parent				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159143				0	en-ZA	The next document is created in a parent frame. If no parent exists, the document is created in the same frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151374				0	en-ZA	_self				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148600				0	en-ZA	The next document is created in the same frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153067				0	en-ZA	_top				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149174				0	en-ZA	The next document is created in a top-level window, that is, in the highest frame of the hierarchy; if the current frame is already a top window, the document is created in the current frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156172				0	en-ZA	The Frame property is relevant for HTML forms, but not for database forms.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146950				0	en-ZA	Graphics				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154344	115			0	en-ZA	An image button has a \<emph\>Graphics \</emph\>property. \<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_IMAGE_URL\"\>The\<emph\> Graphics\</emph\> property specifies the graphic's path and file name that you want to have displayed on the button.\</ahelp\> If you select the graphic file with the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button, the path and file name will be automatically included in the text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150530				0	en-ZA	Help text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156310				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_HELPTEXT\"\>Provides the option of entering a help text that will be displayed as a tip on the control.\</ahelp\> The tip shows the text in user mode when the mouse is moved over the control.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153287				0	en-ZA	For URL type buttons, the help text appears as the extended tip instead of the URL address entered under URL.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145377				0	en-ZA	Help URL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148649				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_HELPURL\"\>Specifies a batch label in URL spelling which refers to a help document and which can be called with the help of the control field.\</ahelp\> The help for the control field help can be opened if the focus is positioned on the control field and the user presses F1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152541				0	en-ZA	Background colour				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155073				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_BACKGROUNDCOLOR\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the background colour of the control field.\</ahelp\>A background colour is available for most control fields. If you click on \<emph\>Background colour\</emph\>, a list will open which enables you to select among various colours. The "Standard" option adopts the system setting. If the desired colour is not listed, click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to define a colour in the \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010501.xhp\" name=\"Color\"\>\<emph\>Color\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148971				0	en-ZA	Scrollbar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3144430				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_HSCROLL\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Adds the scrollbar type that you specify to a text box.\</ahelp\>Adds the scrollbar type that you specify to a text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1110B				0	en-ZA	Incr./decrement value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1110F				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Determines intervals to add or subtract with each activation of the spin button control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146779				0	en-ZA	Value step				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155096	86			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_VALUESTEP\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines spin button intervals.\</ahelp\>You can preset the value intervals for numerical and currency spin buttons. Use the up and down arrows of the spin button to increase or decrease the value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145756				0	en-ZA	List entries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151300				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_STRINGITEMLIST\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Defines the list entries visible in the document. Open this list and type your text. Use Shift+Enter for a new line. With list and combo boxes, you can define the list entries that will be visible in the document. Open the \<emph\>List entries\</emph\> field and type your text.\</ahelp\> Please note the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170100.xhp\" name=\"tips\"\>tips\</link\> referring to the keyboard controls.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152874				0	en-ZA	The predefined default list entry is entered into the \<emph\>Default selection combo\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154610				0	en-ZA	Note that the list entries entered here are only incorporated into the form if, on the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab under \<emph\>List Content Type\</emph\>, the option "Value List" is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154767				0	en-ZA	If you do not want the list entries to be written to the database or transmitted to the recipient of the Web form, but rather assigned values that are not visible in the form, you can assign the list entries to other values in a value list. The value list is determined on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\"Data\"\>\<emph\>Data\</emph\>\</link\> tab. Under \<emph\>Type of List Contents\</emph\>, select the option "Value List". Then enter the values under \<emph\>List Contents\</emph\> that are to be assigned to the corresponding visible list entries of the form. For the correct assignment, the order in the value list is relevant.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150511				0	en-ZA	For HTML documents, a list entry entered on the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab corresponds to the HTML tag <OPTION>; an entry of the value list entered on the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab under \<emph\>List Contents\</emph\> corresponds to the <OPTION VALUE=...> tag.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154290				0	en-ZA	Date maximum				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148637	122			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATEMAX\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines a date which can not be exceeded by another value introduced by the user.\</ahelp\>Determines a date which can not be exceeded by another value introduced by the user.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149804				0	en-ZA	Maximum text length				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150776	124			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_MAXTEXTLEN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Defines the maximum number of characters that the user can enter.\</ahelp\>For text and combo boxes, you can define the maximum number of characters that the user can enter. If this control field property is uncertain, the default setting will be zero.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153813				0	en-ZA	If the control is linked to a database and the text length is to be accepted from the field definition of the database, you must not enter the text length here. The settings are only accepted from the database if the control property was not defined ("Not Defined" state).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145599				0	en-ZA	Value maximum				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154733	126			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_EFFECTIVEMAX\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Defines a value for the control field which can not be exceeded by another value introduced by the user.\</ahelp\>For numerical and currency fields, you can determine the maximum value that the user can enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154835				0	en-ZA	Time maximum				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155762	128			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TIMEMAX\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines a time which can not be exceeded by another value introduced by the user.\</ahelp\>Determines a time which can not be exceeded by another value introduced by the user.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150416				0	en-ZA	Multiselection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3143275				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_MULTISELECTION\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Allows you to select more than one item in a list box.\</ahelp\>Allows you to select more than one item in a list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	bm_id4040955				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>rich text control\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>controls;rich text control\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148527				0	en-ZA	Text type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153724				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"37933\"\>Allows you to use line breaks and formatting in a control field, such as a text box or label. To manually enter a line break, press the Enter key. Select "Multi-line with formatting" to enter formatted text.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN113D2				0	en-ZA	If you select the text type "Multi-line with formatting", you cannot bind this control to a database field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11391				0	en-ZA	This control is named "Multiline input" for a text column inside a table control.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN114EF				0	en-ZA	Word break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11505				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Displays text on more than one line.\</ahelp\> Allows you to use line breaks in a text box, so that you can enter more than one line of text. To manually enter a line break, press the Enter key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11538				0	en-ZA	Toggle				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1154E				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies if a Push Button behaves as a Toggle Button. If you set Toggle to "Yes", you can switch between the "selected" and "not selected" control states when you click the button or press the spacebar while the the control has the focus. A button in the "selected" state appears "pressed in".\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11558				0	en-ZA	Take Focus on Click				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1156E				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you set this option to "Yes", the Push Button receives the focus when you click the button.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11578				0	en-ZA	Hide selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1158E				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"37965\"\>Specifies whether a text selection on a control remains selected when a the focus is no longer on a control.\</ahelp\> If you set \<emph\>Hide selection\</emph\> to "No", the selected text remains selected when the focus is no longer on the control that contains the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11598				0	en-ZA	Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115AE				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"37966\"\>Specifies whether Check boxes and Option buttons are displayed in a 3D look (default) or a flat look.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115B8				0	en-ZA	Border colour				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115CE				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"37967\"\>Specifies the border colour for controls that have the Border property set to "flat".\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115B7				0	en-ZA	Symbol colour				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115BB				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the colour for symbols on controls, for example the arrows on a scrollbar.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149314				0	en-ZA	Date minimum				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155755	132			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATEMIN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines the earliest date that a user can enter.\</ahelp\>Determines the earliest date that a user can enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152866				0	en-ZA	Value minimum				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147505	134			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_EFFECTIVEMIN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can determine here a value for the control field to prevent the user from entering a smaller value.\</ahelp\>For numerical and currency fields you can determine a minimum value to prevent the user from entering a smaller value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153298				0	en-ZA	Time minimum				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148831	136			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TIMEMIN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines the minimum time that a user can enter.\</ahelp\>Determines the minimum time that a user can enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155746				0	en-ZA	Decimal accuracy				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146096	138			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DECIMAL_ACCURACY\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines the number of digits displayed to the right of the decimal point.\</ahelp\>With numerical and currency fields you can determine the number of digits displayed to the right of the decimal point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151340				0	en-ZA	Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149819	10			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_NAME\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>On the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> tab page, this option specifies the name for the control field. On the \<emph\>Form Properties \</emph\>tab page, this option specifies the name for the form.\</ahelp\>Each control field and each form has a \<emph\>Name \</emph\>property through which it can be identified. The name will appear in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigator\"\>Form Navigator\</link\> and, using the name, the control field can be referred to from a macro. The default settings already specify a name which is constructed from using the field's label and number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153025				0	en-ZA	If you work with macros, make sure that the names of the controls are unique.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146325				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>controls; grouping\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>groups;of controls\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>forms; grouping controls\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146325				0	en-ZA	The name is also used to group different controls that belong together functionally, such as radio buttons. To do so, give the same name to all members of the group: controls with identical names form a group. Grouped controls can be represented visually by using a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\" name=\"Group Box\"\>Group Box\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149720				0	en-ZA	Navigation bar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149918	198			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_NAVIGATIONBAR\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether to display the navigation bar on the lower border of the table control.\</ahelp\>Specifies whether to display the navigation bar on the lower border of table controls.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158426				0	en-ZA	Read-only				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153215	43			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_READONLY\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines if the control is read-only (Yes) or if it can be edited (No).\</ahelp\>The\<emph\> Read-only \</emph\>property can be assigned to all controls in which the user can enter text. If you assign the read-only property to an image field which uses graphics from a database, the user will not be able to insert new graphics into the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148912				0	en-ZA	Border				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145637	140			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_BORDER\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines if the field's border should be displayed "Without frame", with a "3-D look" or "Flat".\</ahelp\>With control fields that have a frame, you can determine the border display on the form using the \<emph\>Border \</emph\>property. You can select among the "Without frame", "3-D look" or "Flat" options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149266				0	en-ZA	Tab order				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147483				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TABINDEX\"\>The \<emph\>Tab order\</emph\> property determines the order in which the controls are focused in the form when you press the Tab key.\</ahelp\> In a form that contains more than one control, the focus moves to the next control when you press the Tab key. You can specify the order in which the focus changes with an index under \<emph\>Tab order\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156207				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Tab order\</emph\> property is not available to \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"Hidden Controls\"\>Hidden Controls\</link\>. If you want, you can also set this property for image buttons and image controls, so that you can select these controls with the Tab key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150378				0	en-ZA	When creating a form, an index is automatically assigned to the control fields that are added to this form; every control field added is assigned an index increased by 1. If you change the index of a control, the indices of the other controls are updated automatically. Elements that cannot be focused (Tabstop = No) are also assigned a value. However, these controls are skipped when using the Tab key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150640				0	en-ZA	You can also easily define the indices of the different controls in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170300.xhp\" name=\"Tab Order\"\>\<emph\>Tab Order\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id0509200912114423				0	en-ZA	Mouse wheel scroll				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200912114566				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Sets whether the value changes when the user scrolls a mouse wheel. Never: No change of the value. When focused: (default) The value changes when the control has the focus and the wheel is pointing at the control and gets scrolled. Always: The value changes when the wheel is pointing at the control and gets scrolled, no matter which control has the focus.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154049				0	en-ZA	Default status				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150837				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DEFAULT_CHECKED\"\>Specifies whether an option or a check box is selected by default.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149242				0	en-ZA	For a reset type button, you can define the status of the control if the reset button is activated by the user.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156266				0	en-ZA	For grouped option fields, the status of the group corresponding to the default setting is defined by the \<emph\>Default Status\</emph\> property.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156150				0	en-ZA	Default selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148730	37			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DEFAULT_SELECT_SEQ\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the list box entry to mark as the default entry.\</ahelp\>Specifies the list box entry to mark as the default entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150028	203			0	en-ZA	For a Reset type button, the\<emph\> Default selection\</emph\> entry defines the status of the list box if the reset button is activated by the user.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id919217				0	en-ZA	For a List box that contains a value list, you can click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to open the \<emph\>Default selection\</emph\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id50050				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Default selection\</emph\> dialogue, select the entries that you want to mark as selected when you open the form that contains the list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150460				0	en-ZA	Default value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154222				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_EFFECTIVEDEFAULT\"\>Sets the default value for the control field.\</ahelp\> For example, the default value will be entered when a form is opened.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150740	199			0	en-ZA	For a Reset type button, the\<emph\> Default value entry \</emph\>defines the status of the control if the reset button is activated by the user.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B70				0	en-ZA	Default scroll value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B74				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DEFAULT_SCROLLVALUE\"\>Sets the default value for the scrollbar.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155440				0	en-ZA	Scroll value maximum				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148877				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SCROLLVALUE_MAX\"\>Specify the maximum value of a scrollbar control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN111E4				0	en-ZA	Scroll value minimum				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN111E8				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SCROLLVALUE_MIN\"\>Specify the minimum value of a scrollbar control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B51				0	en-ZA	Small change				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B55				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specify the value to add or subtract when the user clicks the arrow icon on the scrollbar.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B6F				0	en-ZA	Large change				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B73				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specify the value to add or subtract when the user clicks next to the slider on the scrollbar.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id7215491				0	en-ZA	Default time				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id2299874				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Sets the default time.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150482				0	en-ZA	If you do not enter a value, the current time is inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id1727347				0	en-ZA	Default date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id2545548				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Sets the default date.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id2360911				0	en-ZA	If you do not enter a value, the current date is inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id9207434				0	en-ZA	Default text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id4563127				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Sets the default text for a text box or a combo box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145206				0	en-ZA	Default button				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154681	145			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DEFAULT_BUTTON\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The\<emph\> Default button\</emph\> property specifies that the corresponding button will be operated when you press the Return key.\</ahelp\>The\<emph\> Default button\</emph\> property specifies that the corresponding button will be operated when you press the Return key. If you open the dialogue or form and do not carry out any further action, the button with this property is the default button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149750				0	en-ZA	This property should be assigned only to a single button within the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150931				0	en-ZA	When using Web page forms, you might come across this property in search masks. These are edit masks that contain a text field and a Submit type button. The search term is entered in the text field and the search is started by activating the button. If the button is defined as the default button, however, simply hit Enter after entering the search term in order to start the search.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153389				0	en-ZA	Prefix symbol				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150271				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CURRSYM_POSITION\"\>Determines if the currency symbol is displayed before or after the number when using currency fields.\</ahelp\> The default setting is currency symbols are not prefixed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154548				0	en-ZA	Tabstop				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155361	49			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TABSTOP\"\>The \<emph\>Tabstop \</emph\>property determines if a control field can be selected with the tab key.\</ahelp\> The following options are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148627				0	en-ZA	No				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3161673				0	en-ZA	When using the tab key, focusing skips the control.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159323				0	en-ZA	Yes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148584				0	en-ZA	The control can be selected with the Tab key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146909				0	en-ZA	Thousands separator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154936	148			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SHOWTHOUSANDSEP\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts a thousands separator.\</ahelp\>With numerical and currency fields you can determine whether thousands separators are used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156256				0	en-ZA	Label				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156432	8			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_LABEL\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The Label property sets the label of the control field that is displayed in the form.\</ahelp\>The Label property sets the label of the control field that is displayed in the form. This property determines the visible label or the column header of the data field in table control forms.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154568				0	en-ZA	When you create a new control, the description predefined in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> property is used as the default for labelling the control. The label consists of the control field name and an integer numbering the control (for example, CommandButton1). With the \<emph\>Title\</emph\> property, you can assign another description to the control so that the label reflects the function of the control. Change this entry in order to assign an expressive label to the control that is visible to the user.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163820				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>multi-line titles in forms\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>names; multi-line titles\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>controls; multi-line titles\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3163820				0	en-ZA	To create a multi-line title, open the combo box using the arrow button. You can enter a line break by pressing Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159407				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Title\</emph\> property is only used for labelling a form element in the interface visible to the user. If you work with macros, note that at runtime, a control is always addressed through the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> property.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150293				0	en-ZA	URL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154358	57			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TARGET_URL\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the URL address that opens when you click an "Open document / web page" button.\</ahelp\>Enter the URL address for a Open document or web page button type in the \<emph\>URL\</emph\> box. The address opens when you click the button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146074				0	en-ZA	If you move the mouse over the button in User mode, the URL appears as the extended tip, provided that no other Help text was entered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147134				0	en-ZA	Currency symbol				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145160	150			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CURRENCYSYMBOL\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can enter a character or a string for the currency symbol.\</ahelp\>In a currency field, you can pre-define the currency symbol by entering the character or string in the \<emph\>Currency symbol\</emph\> property.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144444				0	en-ZA	Value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152417	155			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_HIDDEN_VALUE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can enter the data that is inherited by the hidden control.\</ahelp\>In a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"hidden control\"\>hidden control\</link\>, under \<emph\>Value\</emph\>, you can enter the data which is inherited by the hidden control. This data will be transferred when sending the form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157315				0	en-ZA	Password characters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155323	157			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ECHO_CHAR\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If the text box is used as a password input, enter the ASCII-code of the display character. This character is displayed instead of the characters typed by the user for the password.\</ahelp\>If the user enters a password, you can determine the characters that will be displayed instead of the characters typed by the user. Under \<emph\>Password character\</emph\>, enter the ASCII code of the desired character. You can use the values from 0 to 255.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152493				0	en-ZA	The characters and their ASCII codes can be seen in the \<emph\>Special Characters\</emph\> dialogue (Insert - Special Character).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157884				0	en-ZA	Literal mask				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3157557	160			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_LITERALMASK\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Defines the literal mask. The literal mask contains the initial values and is always visible after downloading a form.\</ahelp\>With masked fields you can specify a literal mask. A literal mask contains the initial values of a form, and is always visible after downloading a form. Using a character code for the Edit mask, you can determine the entries that the user can type into the masked field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148513				0	en-ZA	The length of the literal mask should always correspond to the length of the edit mask. If this is not the case, the edit mask is either cut off or filled with blanks up to the length of the edit mask.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146762				0	en-ZA	Font				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151037	6			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_FONT\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the font for the text that is in the control field.\</ahelp\>For control fields which have visible text or titles, select the display font that you want to use. To open the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020100.xhp\" name=\"Font\"\>\<emph\>Font\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue, click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button. The selected font is used in control fields names and to display data in table control fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156734				0	en-ZA	Row height				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3160455	163			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ROWHEIGHT\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the row height of a table control field.\</ahelp\>In table controls, enter a value for the row height. If you want, you can enter a value followed by valid measurement unit, for example, 2 cm.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11FB6				0	en-ZA	Text lines end with				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11FBA				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For text fields, select the line end code to be used when writing text into a database column.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160477				0	en-ZA	Time format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145187	169			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TIMEFORMAT\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can define the desired format for the time display.\</ahelp\>You can define the desired format for the time display.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158195				0	en-ZA	Help text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146823	171			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TAG\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies additional information or a descriptive text for the control field.\</ahelp\>In each control field you can specify additional information or a descriptive text for the control field. This property helps the programmer to save additional information that can be used in the program code. This field can be used, for example, for variables or other evaluation parameters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157828				0	en-ZA	Formatting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146843				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_FORMATKEY\"\>Specifies the format code for the control. Click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to select the format code.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN122C4				0	en-ZA	Scale				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN122C8				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SCALEIMAGE\"\>Resizes the image to fit the size of the control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1209F				0	en-ZA	Acting on a record				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN120B1				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"37930\"\>Specifies to show or hide the action items in a selected Navigation Bar control.\</ahelp\> Action items are the following: Save record, Undo, New record, Delete record, Refresh.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN120BE				0	en-ZA	Positioning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN120D9				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"37928\"\>Specifies to show or hide the positioning items in a selected Navigation Bar control.\</ahelp\> Positioning items are the following: Record label, Record position, Record count label, Record count.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN120D7				0	en-ZA	Navigation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN120DB				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"37929\"\>Specifies to show or hide the navigation items in a selected Navigation Bar control.\</ahelp\> Navigation items are the following: First record, Previous record, Next record, Last record.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12156				0	en-ZA	Filtering / Sorting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1215A				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"37931\"\>Specifies to show or hide the filtering and sorting items in a selected Navigation Bar control.\</ahelp\> Filtering and sorting items are the following: Sort ascending, Sort descending, Sort, Automatic filter, Default filter, Apply filter, Remove filter/sort.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12175				0	en-ZA	Icon Size				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12179				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"37927\"\>Specifies whether the icons in a selected Navigation Bar should be small or large.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id0409200920593864				0	en-ZA	Visible				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200920593851				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Defines whether the control will be visible in live mode. In design mode, the control is always visible.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200921154683				0	en-ZA	Note that if this property is set to "Yes" (the default), this does not necessarily mean the control will really appear on the screen. Additional constraints are applied when calculating a control's effective visibility. For instance, a control placed in a hidden section in Writer will never be visible at all, until at least the section itself becomes visible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200921154691				0	en-ZA	If the property is set to "No", then the control will always be hidden in live mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200921154614				0	en-ZA	Older OpenOffice.org versions up to 3.1 will silently ignore this property when reading documents which make use of it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12314				0	en-ZA	Visible size				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12318				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the size of scrollbar thumb in "value units". A value of ("Scroll value max." minus "Scroll value min." ) / 2 would result in a thumb which occupies half of the background area.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12375				0	en-ZA	If set to 0, then the thumb's width will equal its height.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12332				0	en-ZA	Orientation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12336				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the horizontal or vertical orientation for a scrollbar or spin button.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Highlighting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109850				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/02160000.xhp\" name=\"Highlighting\"\>Highlighting\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154927				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"zeichenhintergrundtext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BackColor\"\>Applies the current highlight colour to the background of a text selection. If no text is selected, click the \<emph\>Highlighting\</emph\> icon, select the text that you want to highlight, and then click the \<emph\>Highlighting\</emph\> icon again. To change the highlight colour, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Highlighting\</emph\> icon, and then click the colour that you want.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152551				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3149177\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_backcolor.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149177\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147210				0	en-ZA	Highlighting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	en-ZA	To Apply Highlighting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072B				0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> bar, click the \<emph\>Highlighting\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10736				0	en-ZA	To change the highlighting colour, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Highlighting\</emph\> icon, and then click the colour that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073E				0	en-ZA	Select the text that you want to highlight.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10743				0	en-ZA	To apply highlighting to a single word, double-click the word.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10757				0	en-ZA	To turn off highlighting, press Esc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075A				0	en-ZA	To Remove Highlighting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	en-ZA	Select the highlighted text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149784				0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> bar, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Highlighting\</emph\> icon, and then click \<emph\>No Fill\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\08020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Position in Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\08020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147588				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/08020000.xhp\" name=\"Position in Document\"\>Position in Document\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\08020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143284				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:StatusGetPosition\"\>Displays the current cursor position in the %PRODUCTNAME Basic document. The row number is specified, then the column number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20060000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Document Modification				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147477				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/20060000.xhp\" name=\"Document Modification\"\>Document Modification\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148731				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_MODIFYSTATUS\"\>If changes to the document have not yet been saved, a "*" is displayed in this field on the Status Bar. This also applies to new, not yet saved documents.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\03120000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Decrease Spacing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\03120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155934				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/03120000.xhp\" name=\"Decrease Spacing\"\>Decrease Spacing\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\03120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147143	2			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ParaspaceDecrease\"\>Click the\<emph\> Decrease Spacing \</emph\>icon to decrease the paragraph spacing above the selected paragraph.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\03120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3147834\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_paraspacedecrease.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147834\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\03120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145211				0	en-ZA	Decrease Spacing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\03120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	en-ZA	You can make additional adjustments to the spacing by selecting \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030100.xhp\" name=\"Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\"\>\<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\</emph\>\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\basicshapes.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Basic Shapes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\basicshapes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10557				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/basicshapes.xhp\"\>Basic Shapes\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\basicshapes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10567				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the Basic Shapes toolbar which you can use to insert graphics into your document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\basicshapes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10591				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click an icon on the Basic Shapes toolbar, and then drag in the document to draw the shape.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\basicshapes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10594				0	en-ZA	Some shapes have a handle which you can drag to change the properties of the shape. The mouse pointer changes to a hand symbol over these special handles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Current Page Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3083278				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>page styles;editing/applying with statusbar\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3083278				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/20020000.xhp\" name=\"Current Page Style\"\>Current Page Style\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148731				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:LayoutStatus\"\>Displays the current Page Style. Double-click to edit the style, right-click to select another style.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149283	3			0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>Double-click the\<emph\> Page Style field \</emph\>to open the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05040000.xhp\" name=\"Page Style\"\>Page Style\</link\> dialogue, in which you can edit the style for the current page. In the context menu of this field, you can apply a Page Style. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151234	4			0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>Double-click the \<emph\>Page Style\</emph\> field to open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05070000.xhp\" name=\"Page Style\"\>Page Style\</link\> dialogue, in which you can edit the style for the current page. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346	5			0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"IMPRESS\"\>Double-click this field to open the \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/05120000.xhp\" name=\"Page Style\"\>Slide Design\</link\> dialogue in which you can select the style for the current slide. You can select a different paper format or background. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	6			0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>Double-click this field to open the \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/05120000.xhp\" name=\"Page Style\"\>Slide Design\</link\> dialogue in which you select the style for the current page. You can select a different paper format or background. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\03200000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Change Anchor				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\03200000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153323				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>anchors; changing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\03200000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153323				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/03200000.xhp\" name=\"Change Anchor\"\>Change Anchor\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\03200000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150499	2			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"verankerungtext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToggleAnchorType\"\>Allows you to switch between anchoring options.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> The\<emph\> Change Anchor \</emph\>icon is only visible when an object such as a graphic or control field\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\> or frame\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\> is selected. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\03200000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	en-ZA	Further information about the anchoring is contained in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05260000.xhp\" name=\"Anchoring\"\>\<emph\>Anchoring\</emph\>\</link\> Help section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Standard Filter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151097				0	en-ZA	Standard Filter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149716				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DataFilterStandardFilter\"\>Specifies the logical conditions to filter your table data.\</ahelp\> This dialogue is available for spreadsheet documents, database tables and database forms. The dialogue for databases does not contain the \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_idN105EE				0	en-ZA	         \<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/guide/filters.xhp#filters\"/\>      				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155555				0	en-ZA	Filter criteria				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147834				0	en-ZA	You can define a filter by indicating the type of line, the name of the field, a logical condition and a value or a combination of arguments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149751				0	en-ZA	Operator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_LISTBOX_DLG_FILTERCRIT_LB_WHERECOND3\"\>For the following arguments, you can choose between the logical operators AND / OR.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149182				0	en-ZA	Field name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
