helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN10701				0	en-ZA	Point				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN10704				0	en-ZA	The following formulae convert the units:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070A				0	en-ZA	1 cm = 10 mm				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070E				0	en-ZA	1 inch = 2.54 cm				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN10712				0	en-ZA	1 inch = 6 Pica = 72 Point				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN10715				0	en-ZA	For example, in a text document, open \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\</emph\>. To indent the current paragraph by one inch, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>1 in\</item\> or \<item type=\"literal\"\>1"\</item\> into the "Before text" box. To indent the paragraph by 1 cm, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>1 cm\</item\> into the input box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074C				0	en-ZA	To input the maximum or minimum allowed value respectively, click the current value and then press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Page Up\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Page Down\</item\> key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	ASCII Filter Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146856				0	en-ZA	ASCII Filter Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	par_id3153070				0	en-ZA	You can specify which options, such as basic font, language, character set, or break, are imported or exported with a text document. The dialogue appears when you load an ASCII file with the filter "Text Encoded" or when you save the document the first time, or when you "save as" with another name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159217				0	en-ZA	Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	par_id3155577				0	en-ZA	Defines the settings for importing or exporting your file. When exporting, only the character set and paragraph break can be defined.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146959				0	en-ZA	Character set				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	par_id3143206				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_ASCII_FILTER:LB_CHARSET\"\>Specifies the character set of the file for export or import.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154926				0	en-ZA	Default fonts				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	par_id3151262				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_ASCII_FILTER:LB_FONT\"\>By setting a default font, you specify that the text should be displayed in a specific font. The default fonts can only be selected when importing.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	par_id3153323				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_ASCII_FILTER:LB_LANGUAGE\"\>Specifies the language of the text, if this has not already been defined. This setting is only available when importing.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147143				0	en-ZA	Paragraph break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	par_id3143281				0	en-ZA	Defines the type of paragraph break for a text line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150935				0	en-ZA	CR & LF				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	par_id3145829				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_ASCII_FILTER:RB_CRLF\"\>Produces a "Carriage Return" and a "Linefeed". This option is the default.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153551				0	en-ZA	CR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	par_id3156042				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_ASCII_FILTER:RB_CR\"\>Produces a "Carriage Return" as the paragraph break.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150713				0	en-ZA	LF				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_ASCII_FILTER:RB_LF\"\>Produces a "Linefeed" as the paragraph break.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	XML File Formats				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154408				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>exporting; XML files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>XML file formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>extensions; file formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>suffixes in file formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>document types in $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>file formats; changing $[officename] defaults\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defaults;file formats in $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>file formats;OpenDocument/XML\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>OpenDocument file formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>ODF file formats\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154408				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"xmlformat\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\" name=\"XML File Formats\"\>XML File Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id3148919				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DID_SAVE_PACKED_XML\"\>By default, $[officename] loads and saves files in the OpenDocument file format.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_idN10725				0	en-ZA	The OpenDocument file format (ODF) is a standardised file format used by many software applications. You can find more information at the Wikipedia site: \<link href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenDocument\"\>wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenDocument\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
