helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149403				0	en-ZA	-show {filename.odp}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153838				0	en-ZA	Starts with the Impress file \<emph\>{filename.odp}\</emph\> and starts the presentation. Enters edit mode after the presentation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3156276				0	en-ZA	-minimised				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146080				0	en-ZA	Starts minimised. The splash screen is not displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3641773				0	en-ZA	-maximised				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id8224433				0	en-ZA	Starts maximised.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145641				0	en-ZA	-invisible				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154756				0	en-ZA	Starts in invisible mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148914	17			0	en-ZA	Neither the start-up logo nor the initial program window will be visible. However, the $[officename] software can be controlled and documents and dialogues opened via the \<link href=\"http://api.openoffice.org\" name=\"API\"\>API\</link\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147341	18			0	en-ZA	When the $[officename] software has been started with this parameter, it can only be ended using the taskmanager (Windows) or the \<emph\>kill \</emph\>command (UNIX based systems).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150388				0	en-ZA	It cannot be used in conjunction with \<emph\>-quickstart\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145147				0	en-ZA	More information is found in the \<emph\>$[officename] Developer's Guide\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155334	77			0	en-ZA	-nocrashreport				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149259	78			0	en-ZA	Disables the error report tool.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155903				0	en-ZA	-norestore				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3156374				0	en-ZA	Disables restart and file recovery after a system crash.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id5215918				0	en-ZA	-nofirststartwizard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id5665761				0	en-ZA	Disables the Welcome Wizard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148477				0	en-ZA	-quickstart				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919				0	en-ZA	Activates the Quickstarter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3152479				0	en-ZA	-accept={UNO string}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147130				0	en-ZA	Notifies the $[officename] software that upon the creation of "UNO Acceptor Threads", a "UNO Accept String" will be used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148874				0	en-ZA	More information is found in the \<emph\>$[officename] Developer's Guide\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149964				0	en-ZA	-env				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id2439039				0	en-ZA	Sets another environment for the program start.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id2789086				0	en-ZA	Use soffice -env:UserInstallation=$(URL) where $(URL) is the URL of a folder that contains the "user" folder.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3159238				0	en-ZA	-p {filename1} {filename2} ...				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3163666				0	en-ZA	Prints the files \<emph\>{filename1} {filename2} ...\</emph\> to the default printer and ends. The splash screen does not appear.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150828				0	en-ZA	If the file name contains spaces, then it must be enclosed in quotation marks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150883				0	en-ZA	-pt {Printername} {filename1} {filename2} ...				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155081				0	en-ZA	Prints the files \<emph\>{filename1} {filename2} ...\</emph\> to the printer \<emph\>{Printername}\</emph\> and ends. The splash screen does not appear.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153655				0	en-ZA	If the file name contains spaces, then it must be enclosed in quotation marks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154372				0	en-ZA	-o {filename}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150309				0	en-ZA	Opens \<emph\>{filename}\</emph\> for editing, even if it is a template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151182				0	en-ZA	-view {filename}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145268				0	en-ZA	Creates a temporary copy of \<emph\>{filename}\</emph\> and opens it read-only.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3166421				0	en-ZA	-n {filename}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154259				0	en-ZA	Creates a new document using \<emph\>{filename}\</emph\> as a template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155126				0	en-ZA	-nologo				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151334				0	en-ZA	Disables the splash screen at program start.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3159171				0	en-ZA	-nodefault				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153306				0	en-ZA	Starts without displaying anything except the splash screen.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id2211676				0	en-ZA	-nofirststartwizard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id1641895				0	en-ZA	Add this parameter to the program start command to suppress the Welcome Wizard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153915				0	en-ZA	-display {display}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146786	46			0	en-ZA	Sets the \<emph\>DISPLAY \</emph\>environment variable on UNIX based platforms to the value \<emph\>{display}\</emph\>. This parameter is only supported by the start script for the $[officename] software on UNIX based platforms.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149595				0	en-ZA	-headless				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150530				0	en-ZA	Starts in "headless mode" which allows using the application without user interface.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3156353				0	en-ZA	This special mode can be used when the application is controlled by external clients via the \<link href=\"http://api.openoffice.org\" name=\"API\"\>API\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Registering an Address Book				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152823				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>data sources; registering address books\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>address books; registering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>system address book registration\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>registering; address books\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154228				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"data_addressbook\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_addressbook.xhp\" name=\"Registering an Address Book\"\>Registering an Address Book\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3154927				0	en-ZA	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> you can register different data sources. The contents of the data fields are then available to you for use in various fields and controls. Your system address book is such a data source.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> templates and wizards use fields for the contents of the address book. When activated, the general fields in the templates are automatically replaced with the fields from the data source of your address book.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	en-ZA	In order for the replacement to take place, you must tell \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> which address book you use. The wizard asking for this information appears automatically the first time you activate, for example, a business letter template. You can also call the wizard by following the steps listed below.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id5941648				0	en-ZA	The address book data is read-only in %PRODUCTNAME Base. It is not possible to add, edit, or delete address data from within Base.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149096				0	en-ZA	Address Data Source Wizard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	en-ZA	To call the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01170000.xhp\" name=\"Address Data Source\"\>Address Data Source\</link\> wizard, choose \<emph\>File - Wizards - Address Data Source\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811				0	en-ZA	Registering An Existing Address Book Manually				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Address Book Source\</emph\>. The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110101.xhp\" name=\"Templates: Address Book Assignment\"\>\<emph\>Templates: Address Book Assignment\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Data source\</emph\> combo box, select the system address book or the data source you want to use as an address book.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669	11			0	en-ZA	If you have not yet registered the system address book in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> as the data source, click the \<emph\>Address Data Source ...\</emph\> button. This takes you to the \<emph\>Address Book Data Source Wizard\</emph\>, in which you can register your address book as a new data source in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Table\</emph\> combo box, select the database table you want to use as the address book.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084				0	en-ZA	Under \<emph\>Field assignment\</emph\>, match the fields for first name, company, department, and so on to the actual field names used in your address book.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_idN10784				0	en-ZA	When finished, close the dialogue with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149983				0	en-ZA	Now your data source is registered in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> as the address book. If you now open a template from the \<emph\>Business Correspondence\</emph\> category, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> can automatically insert the correct fields for a form letter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Saving Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147226				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>documents; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backups; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>FTP; saving documents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147226				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"doc_save\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/doc_save.xhp\" name=\"Saving Documents\"\>Saving Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> icon or press the shortcut keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+S.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3155450				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3152349\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_save.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152349\"\>This icon is for tips on how to use the program more effectively.\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	en-ZA	The document is saved under its path and name on the current local data medium or network drive or on the Internet, overwriting any file of the same name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984				0	en-ZA	When you save a new file for the first time, the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"Save As\"\>Save As\</link\> dialogue opens, in which you can enter a name, folder and drive or volume for the file. To open this dialogue, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472				0	en-ZA	You can set the automatic creation of a backup copy under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010200.xhp\" name=\"Load/Save - General\"\>Load/Save - General\</link\>\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	hd_id7146824				0	en-ZA	Automatic extension to the file name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id9359111				0	en-ZA	When saving a file, %PRODUCTNAME always appends an extension to the file name, except when the file name already has an extension that matches the file type. See the list of \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\"\>ODF extensions\</link\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id6709494				0	en-ZA	Some examples for the automatic extensions are listed in the following table:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
