helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\flat_icons.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename]\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\flat_icons.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>View\</emph\> tab page, select the \<emph\>Toolbar icon size\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\flat_icons.xhp	0	help	par_id3157909				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Inserting and Editing Buttons				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149798				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>command buttons, see push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>controls;adding to documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>keys;adding push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>buttons;adding push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>press buttons, see push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>push buttons;adding to documents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149798				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"formfields\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/formfields.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Buttons\"\>Adding a Command Button to a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	en-ZA	You can use the Form Controls toolbar to add checkboxes, buttons, tables showing data records, and other controls to a document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077F				0	en-ZA	To Add a Button to a Document 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Toolbars - Form Controls\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	en-ZA	On the Form Controls toolbar, click the \<emph\>Push Button\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A4				0	en-ZA	The mouse pointer changes to a cross-hair.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	en-ZA	In the document, drag to draw the button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B2				0	en-ZA	Right-click the button and choose \<emph\>Control\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CD				0	en-ZA	Specify the properties of the button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154923				0	en-ZA	To change the button label, click the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab, and edit the text in the \<emph\>Label\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147303	12			0	en-ZA	To attach a macro to the button, click the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> tab, and click the \<emph\>... \</emph\>button beside the button action that you want to run the macro. In the \<emph\>Assign Macro\</emph\> dialogue, locate the macro that you want to use, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10814				0	en-ZA	Close the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147350				0	en-ZA	(Optional) Specify the properties of the form that the button belongs to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10828				0	en-ZA	Right-click the button and choose \<emph\>Form\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082F				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Form Properties\</emph\> dialogue opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	en-ZA	Specify the properties for the form and then close the dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156426				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>faxes; sending\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>faxes;configuring $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sending; documents as faxes \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>configuring;fax icon\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156426				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"fax\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/fax.xhp\" name=\"Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing\"\>Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	en-ZA	To send a fax directly from $[officename], you need a fax modem and a fax driver that allows applications to communicate with the fax modem.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166410				0	en-ZA	Sending a Fax Through the Print Dialogue				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	en-ZA	Open the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialogue by choosing \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\> and select the fax driver in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3155135				0	en-ZA	Clicking \<emph\>OK\</emph\> opens the dialogue for your fax driver, where you can select the fax recipient.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153825				0	en-ZA	Configuring $[officename] a Fax Icon				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3153822				0	en-ZA	You can configure $[officename] so that a single click on an icon automatically sends the current document as a fax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040400.xhp\" name=\"Writer - Print\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</link\>\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3150985				0	en-ZA	Select the fax driver from the \<emph\>Fax\</emph\> list box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EB				0	en-ZA	Click the arrow icon at the end of the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar. In the drop-down menu, choose \<emph\>Customize\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F6				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Toolbar\</emph\>s tab page of the \<emph\>Customize\</emph\> dialogue appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FA				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Add Commands\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10702				0	en-ZA	Select the "Documents" category, then select the "Send Default Fax" command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> and then \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10712				0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Toolbars\</emph\> tab page, click the down arrow button to position the new icon where you want it. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10715				0	en-ZA	Your \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar now has a new icon to send the current document as a fax.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Registering and Deleting a Database 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	bm_id4724570				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>databases;registering (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>registering;databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;deleting (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists;registered databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"data_register\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_register.xhp\"\>Registering and Deleting a Database\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	en-ZA	Data from any \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabadoc.xhp\"\>database file\</link\> can be registered to %PRODUCTNAME. To register means to tell %PRODUCTNAME where the data is located, how it is organised, how to get that data, and more. Once the database is registered, you can use the menu command \<emph\>View - Data source\</emph\> to access the data records from your text documents and spreadsheets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C8				0	en-ZA	To register an existing database file:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CF				0	en-ZA	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01160200.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E1				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\> and select the database file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10700				0	en-ZA	To remove a registered database from %PRODUCTNAME				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10707				0	en-ZA	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01160200.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10719				0	en-ZA	Select the database file and click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F3				0	en-ZA	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp#base\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FB				0	en-ZA	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp#database_main\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
