helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D9				0	en-ZA	Inserting line breaks in $[officename] Calc spreadsheet cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E0				0	en-ZA	To insert a line break in a spreadsheet cell, press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter keys. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E3				0	en-ZA	This will work only with the text edit cursor inside the cell, not at the input line. So first double-click the cell, then single-click at the text position where you want the line break.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200914160968				0	en-ZA	You can search for a newline character in the Find & Replace dialogue by searching for \\n as a regular expression. You can use the text function CHAR(10) to insert a newline character into a text formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E6				0	en-ZA	Formatting $[officename] Calc cells for automatic line wrapping				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106ED				0	en-ZA	Select the cells for which you want an automatic line break.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F1				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Alignment\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F9				0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>Wrap text automatically\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN10700				0	en-ZA	Inserting line breaks in $[officename] Writer text document tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN10707				0	en-ZA	To insert a line break in a text document table cell, press the Enter key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070A				0	en-ZA	An automatic line break will be performed while you type across the end of each cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
