helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\version_number.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144436				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"version_number\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/version_number.xhp\" name=\"Versions and Build Numbers\"\>Versions and Build Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\version_number.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Help - About $[officename]\</emph\>. This opens a dialogue containing information about the program.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\version_number.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	3			0	en-ZA	To obtain further information, keep holding down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>the Command key \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and press the letters S D T in succession. At the beginning you will find information about the version and build number. This is followed by a list of contributors. To stop the information before the end, press Esc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Editing Chart Legends				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147291				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>charts; editing legends\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>legends; charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; chart legends\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting; chart legends\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147291				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"chart_legend\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/chart_legend.xhp\" name=\"Editing Chart Legends\"\>Editing Chart Legends\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	en-ZA	To edit a chart legend:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	en-ZA	Double-click on the chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3154824				0	en-ZA	A grey border appears around the chart and the menu bar now contains commands for editing the objects in the chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Legend\</emph\> or double-click on the legend. This opens the \<emph\>Legend\</emph\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3147210				0	en-ZA	Choose from the available tabs to make modifications, then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	en-ZA	To select the legend, first double-click on the chart (see step 1), then click on the legend. You can now move the legend within the chart using the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3154347				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05010000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Object Properties\"\>Format - Object Properties\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Defining Borders for Paragraphs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147571				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>borders, see also frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; defining borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders; for paragraphs\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames; around paragraphs\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;paragraph borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;paragraph borders\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147571	15			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"border_paragraph\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/border_paragraph.xhp\" name=\"Defining Borders for Paragraphs\"\>Defining Borders for Paragraphs\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159233				0	en-ZA	Setting a Predefined Border Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	en-ZA	Place the cursor in the paragraph for which you want to define a border.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Borders\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3156326				0	en-ZA	Select one of the default border styles in the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3154285				0	en-ZA	Select a line style and colour for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	en-ZA	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area. You can only change distances to edges that have a border line defined.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3153543				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149237				0	en-ZA	Setting a Customized Border Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Borders\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area select the edge(s) that you want to appear in a common layout. Click on an edge in the preview to toggle the selection of an edge.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3148948				0	en-ZA	Select a line style and colour for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	en-ZA	Repeat the last two steps for every border edge.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3150793				0	en-ZA	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area. You can only change distances to edges that have a border line defined.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3151178				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Changing the Association of Microsoft Office Document Types				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143267				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>Microsoft Office;reassigning document types\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>file associations for Microsoft Office\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;file associations in Setup program\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"ms_doctypes\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/ms_doctypes.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Association of Microsoft Office Document Types\"\>Changing the Association of Microsoft Office Document Types\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780				0	en-ZA	To change the association of Microsoft Office file name extensions to open the files either in $[officename] or in Microsoft Office, using Microsoft Windows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	par_id0815200803314147				0	en-ZA	In Windows Explorer, right-click a file of the type that you want to assign to another application.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	par_id0815200803314268				0	en-ZA	In the context menu, choose "Open with..."				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	par_id0815200803314245				0	en-ZA	In the list of applications, select the program that should open the current type of files. Make sure that "Always use this program" is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	par_id0815200803314243				0	en-ZA	If these steps do not apply to your brand of Microsoft Windows, search your Microsoft Windows Help for instructions how to change the file associations.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Viewing File Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152594				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>properties;files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files;properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;file properties\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152594				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"viewing_file_properties\"\>\<variable id=\"viewing\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/viewing_file_properties.xhp\" name=\"Viewing File Properties\"\>Viewing File Properties\</link\>\</variable\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	en-ZA	File properties, such as author name, subject, and keywords, help you manage and identify your documents. $[officename] also tracks file statistics, including the number of words and the number of pages in a document, and automatically adds the statistics as part of the file property.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3147834				0	en-ZA	You can view file properties for the current document\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\> or for a document in the Windows File Open dialogue \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159233				0	en-ZA	To view file properties for the current document:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3153311				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150443				0	en-ZA	To view file properties for a document listed in the Windows File Open dialogue				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306				0	en-ZA	Select a file in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3145121				0	en-ZA	Right-click and choose\<emph\> Properties\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Inserting Charts				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153910				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>charts; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>plotting data as charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; inserting charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts; editing data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; chart data\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153910				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"chart_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/chart_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Charts\"\>Inserting Charts\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3139133				0	en-ZA	Different methods exist to start a chart:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6772972				0	en-ZA	Insert a chart based on data from cells in Calc or Writer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6049684				0	en-ZA	These charts update automatically when the source data changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id2356944				0	en-ZA	Insert a chart with a default data set, and then use the Data Table dialogue to enter your own data for that chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id866115				0	en-ZA	These charts can be created in Writer, Impress and Draw. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146763				0	en-ZA	Copy a chart from Calc or Writer into another document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id701315				0	en-ZA	These charts are snapshots of the data at the time of copying. They do not change when the source data changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id4439832				0	en-ZA	In Calc, a chart is an object on a sheet, it cannot be a sheet of its own.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id719931				0	en-ZA	Chart in a Calc spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	en-ZA	Click inside the cell range that you want to present in your chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id7211218				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Insert Chart\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id7549363				0	en-ZA	You see a chart preview and the Chart Wizard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id9091769				0	en-ZA	Follow the instructions in the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> to create the chart. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3761406				0	en-ZA	Chart in a Writer text document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155066	32			0	en-ZA	In a Writer document, you can insert a chart based on the values in a Writer table. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id428479				0	en-ZA	Click inside the Writer table. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id7236243				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Object - Chart\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6171452				0	en-ZA	You see a chart preview and the Chart Wizard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419	7			0	en-ZA	Follow the instructions in the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> to create the chart. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id6436658				0	en-ZA	Chart based on values of its own				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6944792				0	en-ZA	In Writer, if you have not selected any cells, choose \<emph\>Insert - Object - Chart\</emph\> to insert a chart with default data. In Draw or Impress, choose \<emph\>Insert - Chart\</emph\> to insert a chart based on default data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3152960				0	en-ZA	You can change the default data values by double-clicking on the chart and then choosing \<link href=\"text/schart/01/03010000.xhp\" name=\"View - Chart Data Table\"\>\<emph\>View - Chart Data Table\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Fontwork For Graphical Text Art				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	bm_id3696707				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>graphical text art\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>designing; fonts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>TextArt, see Fontwork\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>WordArt, see Fontwork\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Fontwork\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text effects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>effects; Fontwork icons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; Fontwork icons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>3D text creation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rotating;3D text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;Fontwork objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;Fontwork objects\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066D				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"fontwork\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/fontwork.xhp\"\>Fontwork For Graphical Text Art\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068B				0	en-ZA	You can use Fontwork to create graphical text art objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN10691				0	en-ZA	To create a Fontwork object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_id0202200911373965				0	en-ZA	If you don't see the Drawing toolbar or the Fontwork toolbar, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Toolbars\</item\> to enable the toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069C				0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar or on the \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> toolbar, click the \<emph\>Fontwork Gallery\</emph\> icon.\<image id=\"img_id7040009\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fontworkgalleryfloater.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7040009\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_id3149761				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a Fontwork style and click OK to insert the Fontwork into your document. Double-click or Ctrl+double-click the Fontwork in your document to enter text edit mode and change the text.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A0				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Fontwork Gallery\</emph\> dialogue, select a Fontwork style and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN10755				0	en-ZA	The Fontwork object is inserted into your document. Fontwork objects are Custom Shapes. Using the 3D Settings toolbar, you can switch the view at any time from 2D to 3D and back.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A4				0	en-ZA	Double-click the object to enter text edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D5				0	en-ZA	Replace the default Fontwork text with your own text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A8				0	en-ZA	Press Esc to exit text edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AE				0	en-ZA	To edit a Fontwork object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B5				0	en-ZA	Click the Fontwork object. If the Fontwork object is inserted in the background, hold down the Ctrl key while you click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B8				0	en-ZA	The \<link href=\"text/shared/fontwork_toolbar.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\>\</link\> toolbar is displayed. If you do not see the \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> toolbar, choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Fontwork\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BC				0	en-ZA	Click an icon in the \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN10839				0	en-ZA	The following icons are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	en-ZA	Fontwork Gallery - adds another Fontwork object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C9				0	en-ZA	Fontwork Shape - edits the shape				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CD				0	en-ZA	Fontwork Same Letter Heights - changes the height of characters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D5				0	en-ZA	Fontwork Alignment - aligns the text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D9				0	en-ZA	Fontwork Character Spacing - changes the character spacing and kerning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN108CA				0	en-ZA	To edit more Fontwork attributes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D1				0	en-ZA	Click the Fontwork object. If the Fontwork object is inserted in the background, hold down the Ctrl key while you click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D5				0	en-ZA	Select the properties from the \<emph\>Drawing Object Properties\</emph\> toolbar. You can change the line width, line colour, fill colour, fill style, and more.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E7				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/fontwork_toolbar.xhp\"\>Fontwork toolbar\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Editing Graphic Objects 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145136				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>resizing, see also scaling/zooming\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scaling, see also zooming\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>drawings, see also draw objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>graphic objects, see draw objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; drawing pictures\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; drawings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures; drawing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects; copying when moving in presentations\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>draw objects; adding/editing/copying\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>circle drawings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>square drawings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>handles; scaling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scaling; objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects;moving and resizing with mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>resizing;objects, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pasting;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures;scaling/resizing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145136				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_drawit\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_graphic_drawit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Graphic Objects\"\>Editing Graphic Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Drawing\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, if it is not already open.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	en-ZA	Drawing objects can be subsequently edited and modified. Drawing objects created in this way are vector graphics, which you can scale freely without any loss of quality.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	en-ZA	To create a rectangle, click the rectangle icon and move your cursor to the place in the document where you want one corner of the rectangle to be. Press the mouse button and hold it down while dragging to the opposite corner of the rectangle. When you release the mouse button, the rectangle is inserted in the document. It is selected, and you can edit its properties through the context menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id9448225				0	en-ZA	Holding down the Shift key while dragging restricts the created object. For example, instead of a rectangle you get a square, instead of an ellipse you get a circle. When you drag a handle of an existing object with Shift held down, the aspect ratio of the object is retained.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153626				0	en-ZA	To scale the objects, first select them by clicking on them with the selection tool. You then see eight handles around the object. When you drag one of the four corner handles, the opposite corner remains fixed while the other three corners move. When you drag one of the side handles, the opposite side remains fixed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669				0	en-ZA	To move draw objects, first select them. To select more than one object, press the Shift key while clicking. Select text objects by clicking exactly on their edge. While holding down the mouse button, drag the objects to the new location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Information about the individual icons\"\>Information about the individual icons\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Editing Hyperlinks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153910				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links; editing hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text attributes; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>buttons;editing hyperlink buttons\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>URL;changing hyperlink URLs\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153910				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_edit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Hyperlinks\"\>Editing Hyperlinks\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id4124881				0	en-ZA	When you \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>-click a hyperlink in a Writer document, your web browser opens with the requested web address. If you don't use a mouse, position the cursor inside the hyperlink and open the context menu by Shift+F10, then choose Open Hyperlink.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145071				0	en-ZA	Change the text of a hyperlink as follows				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410	12			0	en-ZA	In Writer documents, you can click anywhere into a hyperlink and edit the visible text. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id2690511				0	en-ZA	If you leave the hyperlink by positioning the cursor somewhere else, only the visible text will be changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id1983092				0	en-ZA	If you leave the hyperlink by entering a space character directly following the last character, the AutoCorrect - if enabled - will change the target URL to be the same as the visible text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id333262				0	en-ZA	In all document types, you can open the Hyperlink dialogue to edit a hyperlink. First set the cursor into the hyperlink or directly in front of the hyperlink, then click the Hyperlink icon on the Standard bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158432				0	en-ZA	Change the URL of a hyperlink as follows				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	en-ZA	Option 1: As described above, open \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink Dialog\"\>Hyperlink Dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	en-ZA	Option 2: Open \<link href=\"text/shared/main0209.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink Bar\"\>Hyperlink Bar\</link\> (\<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\>). Click on the hyperlink, do not release the mouse button and drag the hyperlink to the Hyperlink Bar. Edit the URL on the Hyperlink Bar and press the Return key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148686				0	en-ZA	Change the attribute of all hyperlinks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	en-ZA	Open the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN10826				0	en-ZA	Click the Character Styles icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082C				0	en-ZA	Right-click the "Internet Link" or "Visited Internet Link" character style, and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	en-ZA	In the dialogue, select the new attributes, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147530				0	en-ZA	Edit a hyperlink button				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3152361				0	en-ZA	If the hyperlink is a button, click on the border to select it, or press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while clicking. Open the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialogue through the context menu. You can edit the label text under "Caption," and modify the address in the "URL" field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Changing Default Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154285				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>modifying, see changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing, see also editing and replacing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>default templates; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating; templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates;editing and saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resetting;templates\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154285				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"standard_template\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/standard_template.xhp\" name=\"Changing Default Templates\"\>Changing Default Templates\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	en-ZA	When you open a new document with \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, a blank document appears based on a $[officename] template. You can edit, modify, or replace this template so that the new document contains your customised Styles or other contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	en-ZA	Modifying Default Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	en-ZA	First, open either an existing $[officename] template and modify it, or open a new document and edit it as necessary to create the desired template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3159152				0	en-ZA	You can define a document template for each $[officename] module. The following describes how to proceed for text documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145748	8			0	en-ZA	Save the document by choosing\<emph\> File\</emph\> -\<emph\> Templates - Save \</emph\>and saving the document in the \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> category.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	en-ZA	Double-click \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> in the list on the left. You will see the user-defined templates in the user directory specified under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\>. Select the template you have just saved and open the context menu or open the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146901				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Set As Default Template\</emph\>. The next time you open a new text document, the new document will be based on the new default template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153947				0	en-ZA	Resetting Default Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3156276				0	en-ZA	To reset the modified text template to the original default template:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146792				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	en-ZA	Open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reset default template\</emph\>. In the submenu, select the document type whose default setting you want to restore. Thereafter, when you open an empty text document, it will again correspond to the $[officename] default template for text documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153764				0	en-ZA	Using Custom Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3150386	14			0	en-ZA	There are several ways to make your work easier by using your own custom templates. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149109				0	en-ZA	Templates in the Template Folder				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918				0	en-ZA	You can save a new template with \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\> or by selecting "Template" file type in any Save dialogue. Save the template in the user directory specified under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\> to be able to access the template from within the \<emph\>File - New - From Templates and Documents\</emph\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	en-ZA	You may need to update the view of the templates in the dialogue before you can see a newly created template. In this case, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\> and in the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button, choose \<emph\>Update\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	en-ZA	To open the template for editing, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Edit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147315				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110000.xhp\" name=\"Templates\"\>Templates\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Shortcuts (%PRODUCTNAME Accessibility)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158421				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility;general shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>shortcut keys; %PRODUCTNAME accessibility\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158421				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Shortcuts (%PRODUCTNAME Accessibility)\"\>Shortcuts (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Accessibility)\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159201				0	en-ZA	You can control \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> without using a mouse device, using only the keyboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	en-ZA	On each module's main help page (for example, the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer or \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc main help page) there is a link to access the keyboard shortcuts' help for that module.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	en-ZA	In addition, under the keyword "Accessibility" you find step-by-step instructions about how to control the selected module without a mouse device.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166460				0	en-ZA	Working with the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> user interface without mouse				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154749				0	en-ZA	Activating menu bar, toolbars, windows, and document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156329				0	en-ZA	Repeatedly pressing F6 switches the focus and circles through the following objects:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150669				0	en-ZA	menu bar,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149234				0	en-ZA	every toolbar from top to bottom and from left to right,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	en-ZA	every free window from left to right,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154514				0	en-ZA	document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252				0	en-ZA	Press Shift+F6 to switch through objects in the opposite direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152473				0	en-ZA	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 to switch to the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152360				0	en-ZA	Press F10 to switch to the menu bar and back.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	en-ZA	Escape closes an open submenu, a toolbar, or the current free window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3161656				0	en-ZA	Calling a menu command				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056				0	en-ZA	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> or F6 or F10 to select the first menu (the \<emph\>File\</emph\> menu). With right arrow, the next menu to the right is selected; with left arrow, the previous menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153381				0	en-ZA	Arrow down opens a selected menu. Any additional arrow down and up arrow move the selection through the menu commands. With right arrow you open any existing submenus.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	en-ZA	Press Enter to execute the selected menu command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147086				0	en-ZA	Executing an icon command				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148922				0	en-ZA	Press F6 repeatedly until the first icon on the toolbar is selected. Use the right and left arrows to select an icon on a horizontal toolbar. Similarly, use the up and down arrows to select an icon on a vertical toolbar. The Home key selects the first icon on a toolbar and the End key, the last.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3144433				0	en-ZA	Press Enter to execute the selected icon. If the selected icon normally demands a consecutive mouse action, such as inserting a rectangle, then pressing the Enter key is not sufficient: in these cases press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	en-ZA	Pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter on an icon for creating a draw object. A draw object will be placed into the middle of the view, with a predefined size.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449				0	en-ZA	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter on the Selection tool to select the first draw object in the document. If you want to edit, size, or move the selected draw object, first use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 to set the focus into the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	en-ZA	If a toolbar is longer than can be displayed on screen, it shows an icon at the right or lower edge. Select the toolbar and press PageUp or PageDown to display the remaining icons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150440				0	en-ZA	Special hints for toolbars				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149983				0	en-ZA	Press the down arrow or right arrow to open the selected toolbar. This is equivalent to a mouse click. In the toolbar use the right arrow and left arrow keys. The Home and End keys select the first and last icon in the toolbar, respectively.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145365				0	en-ZA	Close the toolbar with Esc. It is not possible to move the toolbar without a mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151119				0	en-ZA	Selection from a combo box				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146986				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3148645\" src=\"res/helpimg/zellvor.png\" width=\"1.15in\" height=\"0.3165in\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148645\"\>Combo box\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666				0	en-ZA	Select the combo box. Press Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366				0	en-ZA	Use the down arrow or Page Down key to scroll down the combo box entries, or the up arrow or Page Up key to scroll upwards. The Home key takes you to the first entry and the End key takes you to the last entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145749				0	en-ZA	Press Enter to execute the selected entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150685				0	en-ZA	Selection in Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154320				0	en-ZA	In several windows, dialogues, and in the table control field, there are tables to select data, for instance, in the right part of the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp\" name=\"Data Source View\"\>Data Source View\</link\>. The following keys are used for selections in these tables:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014				0	en-ZA	Spacebar: switches from selection of the current row and cancellation of any selection, but not if the current cell is in edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+spacebar: switches between selection of the current row and cancellation of this selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149488				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+spacebar: switches between selection of the current column and cancellation of this selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Up Arrow or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Down Arrow: moves the window separator between table and form, for instance in the bibliography database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251				0	en-ZA	In a table control or in the data source view, the Tab key moves to the next column. To move to the next control, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab. To move to the previous control, press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150592				0	en-ZA	Size and Position of Windows and Dialogues				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153221				0	en-ZA	First press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+spacebar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456				0	en-ZA	A system menu opens with menu commands like \<emph\>Move\</emph\>, \<emph\>Resize\</emph\> and \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	en-ZA	Choose a command (down arrow, then Enter).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155083				0	en-ZA	Now you can use the arrow keys to move or resize the dialogue or window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147497				0	en-ZA	Press Enter to accept the change. Press Escape to cancel the changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146988				0	en-ZA	Docking and Undocking Windows and Toolbars				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147176				0	en-ZA	Press F6 until the window or toolbar is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	en-ZA	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+F10.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154479				0	en-ZA	Selecting objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148993				0	en-ZA	Press Shift+F4 to select the first object in the current document. When an object is selected, press Tab to select the next object, or press Esc to go back to the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152962				0	en-ZA	Edit Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156379				0	en-ZA	A selected OLE object can be activated with the Enter key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766				0	en-ZA	Edit Position and Size of Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148405				0	en-ZA	Use the arrow keys to move the selected object by one grid resolution unit.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145619				0	en-ZA	Set the grid resolution unit with \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Grid\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Resolution\</emph\> area. If you enter a number greater than 1 in the \<emph\>Subdivision\</emph\> area, you must press the arrow key as often as the number states to move the selected object by one grid resolution unit.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3166450				0	en-ZA	Use the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and arrow keys to move the selected object by one pixel.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	en-ZA	Use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to enter the handle edit mode. The upper left handle is the active handle, it starts blinking. Use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to select the next handle. Press Escape to exit the handle edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	en-ZA	In the handle edit mode, the arrow keys move the selected handle, which changes the object size.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147361				0	en-ZA	Edit the Anchors of Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148534				0	en-ZA	You can move the anchor of an object with the arrow keys. First enter the handle edit mode and select the anchor. Depending on the type of anchor, you can then move the anchor in different directions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3163808				0	en-ZA	Select the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150646				0	en-ZA	Enter the handle edit mode with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150940				0	en-ZA	The upper left handle starts blinking. Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab several times, until no handle blinks. This signals that now the anchor of the object is activated. \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>In text documents you can press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+A to activate the anchor directly.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919				0	en-ZA	Use the arrow keys to move the anchor. The object follows the anchor as appropriate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152582				0	en-ZA	You can change the anchor of the selected object for example in the object's context menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148393				0	en-ZA	If the object is anchored \<emph\>To Paragraph\</emph\>, the arrow keys move the object to the previous or next paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145615	69			0	en-ZA	If the object is anchored\<emph\> To page\</emph\>, the keys Page Up or Page Down move it to the previous or next page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145135				0	en-ZA	If the object is anchored \<emph\>To character\</emph\>, the Arrow keys move it through the current paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145256	71			0	en-ZA	If the object is anchored\<emph\> As character\</emph\>, no anchor icon exists. You cannot move the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149527				0	en-ZA	If the object is anchored \<emph\>To frame\</emph\>, the Arrow keys move it to the next frame in the respective direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153270				0	en-ZA	Controlling the Dividing Lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3158413	134			0	en-ZA	Documents of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Draw, and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Impress can be split horizontally and vertically into separate views. Each view can show other parts of the document. Using the mouse, you can drag a dividing line from the scrollbar into the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149814				0	en-ZA	Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6: shows the dividing lines at default positions and focus a line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3158444				0	en-ZA	Arrow keys: moves the current dividing line a big step in the arrow direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3163668				0	en-ZA	Shift+Arrow keys: moves the current dividing line a small step in the arrow direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148426				0	en-ZA	Delete: deletes the current dividing line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277				0	en-ZA	Shift+Delete: deletes both dividing lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150383				0	en-ZA	Enter: fixes the current position of the dividing lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150369				0	en-ZA	Escape: resets the current dividing line to its default position				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154492				0	en-ZA	Controlling the Data Source View				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150515				0	en-ZA	F4: opens and closes the data source view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159109				0	en-ZA	F6: switches between document and toolbars.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153229				0	en-ZA	+ (plus key): expands the selected entry in the data source explorer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150312				0	en-ZA	- (minus key): collapses the selected entry in the data source explorer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+E: switches between data source explorer and table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147171				0	en-ZA	Shortcuts in the Query Design Window				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152455				0	en-ZA	F6: switches between object bar, table view, and selection area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151180				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Up arrow or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Down arrow: moves the border between table view and selection area up or down.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156288				0	en-ZA	Keys in the Table View (upper area of the query design) and in the Relations window				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156166				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Arrow key: moves the selected table in the direction of the arrow.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147310				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+Arrow key: resizes the selected table in the table view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152986				0	en-ZA	Del: removes the selected table or connection from the table view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	en-ZA	Tab: switches between tables and connections in the table view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154529				0	en-ZA	Enter: when a connection is selected, the Enter key opens the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialogue of the connection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159624				0	en-ZA	Enter: when a table is selected, the Enter key enters the first data field from the list box into the selection area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153816				0	en-ZA	Keys in the Selection Area (bottom area of the query design)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152896				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Left Arrow or Right Arrow: moves the selected column to the left or to the right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146152				0	en-ZA	Keys in the Table Design Window				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151243				0	en-ZA	F6: switches between toolbar, column view, and properties area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145075				0	en-ZA	Controlling the ImageMap Editor				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159096				0	en-ZA	Press Tab to select an icon. If you selected one of the icons from \<emph\>Rectangle\</emph\> to \<emph\>Freeform Polygon\</emph\> and you press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter, an object of the selected type is created in default size.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156016				0	en-ZA	If you press Enter while the icon \<emph\>Select\</emph\> is selected, the focus is set into the image window of the ImageMap Editor. Press Esc to set the focus back to the icons and input boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149587				0	en-ZA	If the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> icon is selected and you press Ctrl+Enter, the first object in the image window gets selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154343				0	en-ZA	Use the icon \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> to switch into the point edit mode for polygons and back.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147073				0	en-ZA	Use Ctrl+Tab in the image window to select the next point. Use Shift+Ctrl+Tab to select the previous point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153285				0	en-ZA	Use the Delete key with the focus in the image window to delete the selected object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145377				0	en-ZA	Controlling the Help				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149441				0	en-ZA	Press Shift+F1 to display the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0108.xhp\" name=\"Extended Tips\"\>Extended Tips\</link\> for the currently selected command, icon or control.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154960				0	en-ZA	Navigating the main help pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151300				0	en-ZA	In the main help pages, use Tab to jump to the next hyperlink or Shift+Tab to jump to the previous link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155537				0	en-ZA	Press Enter to execute the selected hyperlink.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154912				0	en-ZA	Press Backspace above the Enter key to return to the previous help page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150894				0	en-ZA	Controlling the Text Import dialogue (CSV file import)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153975				0	en-ZA	Ruler				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	en-ZA	Left or Right Arrow: go one position to the left or to the right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151000				0	en-ZA	Ctrl+Left Arrow or Ctrl+Right Arrow: jump to the previous or to the next split				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159203				0	en-ZA	Ctrl+Shift+Left Arrow or Ctrl+Shift+Right Arrow: move a split one position to the left or to the right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154538				0	en-ZA	Home or End: jump to the first or the last possible position				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155382				0	en-ZA	Ctrl+Home or Ctrl+End: jump to the first or the last split				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155894				0	en-ZA	Shift+Ctrl+Home or Shift+Ctrl+End: move split to the first or to the last position				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145195				0	en-ZA	Space key: insert or remove a split				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154647				0	en-ZA	Insert key: insert a split (leave existing splits unchanged)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154765				0	en-ZA	Delete key: delete a split				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154650				0	en-ZA	Shift+Delete: delete all splits				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145368				0	en-ZA	Up Arrow or Down Arrow: scroll table down or up one row				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155914				0	en-ZA	Page Up or Page Down: scroll table down or up one page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147492				0	en-ZA	Escape key (during mouse drag): cancel drag, move split to old position				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145216				0	en-ZA	Preview				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155148				0	en-ZA	Left Arrow or Right Arrow: select left or right column and clear other selections				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150780				0	en-ZA	Ctrl+Left Arrow or Ctrl+Right Arrow: move focus to the left or to the right column (does not change selection)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153811				0	en-ZA	Shift+Left Arrow or Shift+Right Arrow: expand or shrink the selected range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146962				0	en-ZA	Ctrl+Shift+Left Arrow or Ctrl+Shift+Right Arrow: expand or shrink the selected range (does not change other selections)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147512				0	en-ZA	Home or End: select the first or the last column (use Shift or Ctrl as with cursor keys)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
