helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Copying Attributes With the Format Paintbrush				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	bm_id380260				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>Format Paintbrush\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>formatting;copying\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>copying;formatting\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Paintbrush\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1053A				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"formatpaintbrush\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/paintbrush.xhp\"\>Copying Formatting With the Format Paintbrush\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10655				0	en-ZA	You can use the Format Paintbrush tool to copy formatting from a text selection or from an object and apply the formatting to another text selection or object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_id101920091122570				0	en-ZA	In Calc, the Format Paintbrush only applies to cell formatting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DD				0	en-ZA	Select the text or object whose formatting you want to copy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10667				0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Standard Bar\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10660				0	en-ZA	The cursor changes to a paint bucket.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	en-ZA	If you want to apply the formatting to more than one selection, double-click the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id209967\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatpaintbrush.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id209967\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. After you apply all the formatting, click the icon again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066E				0	en-ZA	Select or click the text or object that you want to apply the formatting to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10716				0	en-ZA	To exclude paragraph formatting, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> when you click. To exclude character formatting, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift when you click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10671				0	en-ZA	The following table describes the formatting attributes that the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> can copy:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10691				0	en-ZA	Type of Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10697				0	en-ZA	Comment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069E				0	en-ZA	Nothing selected, but cursor is inside a text passage				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A4				0	en-ZA	Copies the formatting of the current paragraph and the character formatting of the next character in the text flow direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	en-ZA	Text is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B1				0	en-ZA	Copies the formatting of the last selected character and of the paragraph that contains the character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B8				0	en-ZA	Frame is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BE				0	en-ZA	Copies the frame attributes that are defined in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Frame\</item\> dialogue. The contents, size, position, linking, hyperlinks, and macros in the frame are not copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	en-ZA	Object is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CB				0	en-ZA	Copies the object formatting that is defined in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Graphics\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Drawing Object\</item\> dialogues. The contents, size, position, hyperlinks, and macros in the object are not copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D2				0	en-ZA	Form control is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D8				0	en-ZA	Not supported				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DF				0	en-ZA	Drawing object is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E5				0	en-ZA	Copies all formatting attributes. In Impress and Draw, the text contents of the object is also copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EC				0	en-ZA	Text within Calc cells is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F2				0	en-ZA	Not supported				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F9				0	en-ZA	Writer table or cells are selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FF				0	en-ZA	Copies the formatting that is specified in Table, Text Flow, Borders, and Background tab pages in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Table\</item\> dialogue. The paragraph and character formatting are also copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	en-ZA	Calc table or cells are selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070C				0	en-ZA	Copies the formatting that is specified in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells\</item\> dialogue as well as the formatting of the cell contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Viewing a Database				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	bm_id2339854				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>opening;database files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing; databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data sources;viewing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;viewing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A6				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"data_view\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_view.xhp\"\>Viewing a Database\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C4				0	en-ZA	There are two different methods of viewing a database in %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CA				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> to open the database file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D1				0	en-ZA	The \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabadoc.xhp\"\>database file\</link\> gives you full access to tables, queries, reports, and forms. You can edit the structure of your tables and change the contents of the data records.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E3				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>View - Data source\</emph\> to view the registered databases.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105EA				0	en-ZA	The \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp\"\>data source view\</link\> can be used to drag-and-drop table fields from registered databases into your documents and to produce mail merges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN10606				0	en-ZA	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp#base\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN1060E				0	en-ZA	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp#database_main\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Accessibility in %PRODUCTNAME				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150502				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; %PRODUCTNAME features\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150502				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"accessibility\"\>\<link name=\"Accessibility in %PRODUCTNAME\" href=\"text/shared/guide/accessibility.xhp\"\>Accessibility in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3154894				0	en-ZA	The following accessibility features are part of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3153894				0	en-ZA	Support of \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/assistive.xhp\" name=\"external devices and applications\"\>external devices and applications\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552				0	en-ZA	Access to all functions by keyboard. The keys that replace the mouse actions are listed in the \<link name=\"%PRODUCTNAME Help\" href=\"text/shared/guide/keyboard.xhp\"\>\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Help\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	en-ZA	Improved readability of screen contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	en-ZA	Zooming of on-screen user interface for menus, icons, and documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3145071				0	en-ZA	The user interface is scalable through your \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Window Manager\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>operating system\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> settings. The default font size for dialogues is 12pt, corresponding to a scale of 100%. You can also change the font size for dialogues in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> - View\</emph\>. The zoom factor of a document can be changed in \<emph\>View - Zoom\</emph\>, or by double-clicking the zoom factor displayed in the Status Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	en-ZA	Please note that accessibility support relies on Java technology for communications with assistive technology tools. This means that the first program startup may take a few seconds longer, because the Java runtime environment has to be started as well.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link name=\"%PRODUCTNAME - View\" href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010800.xhp\"\>\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> - View\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link name=\"%PRODUCTNAME - Appearance\" href=\"text/shared/optionen/01012000.xhp\"\>\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> - Appearance\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link name=\"%PRODUCTNAME - Accessibility\" href=\"text/shared/optionen/01013000.xhp\"\>\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> - Accessibility\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Recording Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155364				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>changes; recording\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>recording; changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>comments; on changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>review function;tracking changes\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"redlining_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_enter.xhp\" name=\"Recording Changes\"\>Recording Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7271645				0	en-ZA	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145669				0	en-ZA	Not all changes are recorded. For example, the changing of a tab stop from align left to align right is not recorded. However, all usual changes made by a proofreader are recorded, such as additions, deletions, text alterations, and usual formatting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	en-ZA	1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	en-ZA	To start recording changes, open the document to be edited and choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02230000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Changes\"\>\<emph\>Edit - Changes\</emph\>\</link\> and then choose \<emph\>Record\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	en-ZA	2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	en-ZA	Now start making your changes. You will note that all new text passages that you enter are underlined in colour, while all text that you delete remains visible but is crossed out and shown in colour.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	en-ZA	3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	en-ZA	If you move to a marked change with the mouse pointer, you will see a reference to the type of change, the author, date and time of day for the change in the Help Tip. If the Extended Tips are also enabled, you will also see any available comments on this change.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156119				0	en-ZA	Changes in a spreadsheet document are highlighted by a border around the cells; when you point to the cell you can see more detailed information on this change in the Help Tip.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473				0	en-ZA	You can enter a comment on each recorded change by placing the cursor in the area of the change and then choosing \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Comment\</emph\>. In addition to Extended Tips, the comment is also displayed in the list in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02230400.xhp\" name=\"Accept or Reject Changes\"\>\<emph\>Accept or Reject Changes\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153542				0	en-ZA	To stop recording changes, choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Record\</emph\> again. The check mark is removed and you can now save the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153627				0	en-ZA	In a text document, you can highlight all lines that you have changed with an additional coloured marking. This can be in the form of a red line in the margin, for example.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147530				0	en-ZA	To change the settings for tracking changes, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer\</emph\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040700.xhp\" name=\"Changes\"\>\<emph\>Changes\</emph\>\</link\> or on the \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060600.xhp\" name=\"Changes\"\>\<emph\>Changes\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Version Management				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154230				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>versions; of a document\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; version management\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>version management\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154230				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"redlining_versions\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_versions.xhp\" name=\"Version Management\"\>Version Management\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>File\</emph\> menu contains a \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01190000.xhp\" name=\"Versions\"\>\<emph\>Versions\</emph\>\</link\> command that enables you to save multiple versions of a document in the same file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	par_id3149399				0	en-ZA	You can choose to view individual versions of a document, or you can display the differences between versions with colour markings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	en-ZA	In the dialogue to open a document, you can select from a combo box which version of this document you want to open.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143267				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ActiveX control\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;ActiveX control\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Internet; Internet Explorer for displaying $[officename] documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>$[officename] documents;viewing and editing in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;%PRODUCTNAME documents in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;%PRODUCTNAME documents in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"activex\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/activex.xhp\" name=\"ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer\"\>ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	en-ZA	Under Windows only, you can view any $[officename] document in a window of the Microsoft Internet Explorer. Install the ActiveX control in the $[officename] Setup program.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156346				0	en-ZA	Installing the ActiveX control				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821				0	en-ZA	Close $[officename] and the Quickstarter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	en-ZA	Click the Start button on the Windows taskbar. Choose \<emph\>Control Panel\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E8				0	en-ZA	In the Control Panel, click \<emph\>Add or Remove Programs\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155				0	en-ZA	In the list, click %PRODUCTNAME, then click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	en-ZA	In the Installation Wizard, select \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3159399				0	en-ZA	Open the \<emph\>Optional Components\</emph\> entry and find the \<emph\>ActiveX Control\</emph\> entry. Open the sub menu of the icon and select to install the feature.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561	8			0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\> and \<emph\>Install\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151384				0	en-ZA	Viewing $[officename] documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669				0	en-ZA	In Internet Explorer, browse to a web page that contains a link to a $[officename] Writer document, for example.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	en-ZA	Click the link to view the document in the Internet Explorer window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3154072				0	en-ZA	You may still right-click the link to save the file on your harddisk.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153361				0	en-ZA	Editing $[officename] documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3154367				0	en-ZA	The $[officename] document inside the Internet Explorer shows a set of read-only toolbar icons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3148451				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Edit file\</emph\> icon in the document's toolbar to open a copy of the document in a new $[officename] window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3144760				0	en-ZA	Edit the copy of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Recording a Macro				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	bm_id3093440				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>macros; recording\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recording; macros\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Basic; recording macros\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	hd_id3093440				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"macro_recording\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/macro_recording.xhp\" name=\"Recording a Macro\"\>Recording a Macro\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	en-ZA	Open the document for which you want to record a macro.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Record Macro\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	en-ZA	You see the small \<emph\>Recording\</emph\> dialogue with just one button called \<emph\>Stop Recording\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3153087				0	en-ZA	Perform the actions you want to be recorded in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504				0	en-ZA	Press the Escape key to deselect an object, as the macro recorder currently does not record this action by mouse click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3148492				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Stop Recording\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3148686				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Macro\</emph\> dialogue appears, in which you can save and run the macro.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3159158				0	en-ZA	If you want to abort the recording without saving a macro, click the \<emph\>Close\</emph\> button of the \<emph\>Recording\</emph\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3144510				0	en-ZA	To save the macro, first select the object where you want the macro to be saved in the \<emph\>Save macro in\</emph\> list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550	12			0	en-ZA	If you want the macro to be saved into a new library or module, click the \<emph\>New Library \</emph\>or \<emph\>New Module \</emph\>button and enter a name for the library or module.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	en-ZA	Enter a name for the new macro in the \<emph\>Macro name\</emph\> text box. Do not use Basic keywords as a name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	hd_id2486342				0	en-ZA	Limitations of the macro recorder				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3608508				0	en-ZA	The following actions are \<emph\>not\</emph\> recorded:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id921353				0	en-ZA	Opening of windows is not recorded.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id9296243				0	en-ZA	Actions carried out in another window than where the recorder was started are not recorded.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id4269234				0	en-ZA	Window switching is not recorded.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id8014465				0	en-ZA	Actions that are not related to the document contents are not recorded. For example, changes made in the Options dialogue, macro organiser, customising.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id2814416				0	en-ZA	Selections are recorded only if they are done by using the keyboard (cursor travelling), but not when the mouse is used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id2522354				0	en-ZA	The macro recorder works only in Calc and Writer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Macro\"\>Macro\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0600.xhp\" name=\"macro programming in $[officename]\"\>Programming in %PRODUCTNAME\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id7797242				0	en-ZA	The macro recording functionality is only available for text documents in %PRODUCTNAME Writer and for spreadsheets in %PRODUCTNAME Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Using and Editing Database Reports 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147834				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>database reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data sources;reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reports;opening and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening;reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates;database reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reports;templates\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149178				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"data_report\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_report.xhp\" name=\"Create, Use, and Edit Database Reports\"\>Using and Editing Database Reports\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145609				0	en-ZA	Using a Report				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147265				0	en-ZA	%PRODUCTNAME stores the information about the created reports in the database file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> and select the database file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054				0	en-ZA	In the database file window, click the \<emph\>Reports\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	en-ZA	Double-click one of the report names to open the report.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077D				0	en-ZA	These links are added automatically when you create a new report by the Report Wizard or in the Report Builder window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id1695608				0	en-ZA	Editing a Report Created in the Report Builder Window				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id7510910				0	en-ZA	Right-click the name of a report in the database file window, then choose Edit.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id8138065				0	en-ZA	The Report Builder window opens with the report's information loaded. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id5086825				0	en-ZA	Use the toolbars and menu commands and drag-and-drop to edit the report as stated in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Builder\</link\> guide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id4747154				0	en-ZA	Execute the report to see the resulting report document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153104				0	en-ZA	Editing a Report Created by the Report Wizard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863				0	en-ZA	On the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01100500.xhp\" name=\"last dialogue page of the Report AutoPilot\"\>last dialogue page of the Report Wizard\</link\>, you can choose to edit the report template before you use the report.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3155431				0	en-ZA	You can edit the page styles for the first page and the following pages of the report as well as the paragraph styles, the number formats, the printed field labels, and more.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D7				0	en-ZA	Unless you have a thorough understanding of the database the report accesses, do not edit the SQL statement, database name, the hidden form controls, or the related information on the report.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Copying Graphics Between Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159201				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; drag and drop between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;pictures, between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;pictures from other documents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159201				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_graphic\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_graphic.xhp\" name=\"Copying Graphics Between Documents\"\>Copying Graphics Between Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155805				0	en-ZA	You can copy a graphic from one document to another by drag-and-drop. If you plan to publish your document, please observe copyright laws and obtain the consent of the authors.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	en-ZA	Open the document in which you want to insert the graphic object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	en-ZA	Open the document from which you want to copy the graphic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	en-ZA	Click the graphic while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, to select it without executing any hyperlinks it may refer to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110				0	en-ZA	Keep the mouse button pressed and wait a moment while the object is copied to an internal memory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763	21			0	en-ZA	Drag the graphic into the other document. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the documents are not visible side by side, first move the mouse pointer to the button of the target document while keeping the mouse button pressed. The document in question is then displayed and you can move the mouse pointer into the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628				0	en-ZA	Release the mouse button as soon as the grey text cursor indicates the position where you want to insert a copy of the picture.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276				0	en-ZA	If the graphic is connected with a hyperlink, the hyperlink and not the graphic is inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150502				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ImageMap; editor\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editors; ImageMap editor\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>images; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hotspots;adding to images\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>URL;in pictures\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10631				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"imagemap\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/imagemap.xhp\"\>Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064F				0	en-ZA	An ImageMap allows you to attach URLs to specific areas, called hotspots, on a picture in your document. An image map is a group of one or more hotspots.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066C				0	en-ZA	You can draw three types of hotspots: rectangles, ellipses, and polygons. When you click a hotspot, the URL is opened in the browser window or frame that you specify. You can also specify the text that appears when your mouse rests on the hotspot.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10677				0	en-ZA	To add a clickable hotspot to an image				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067E				0	en-ZA	Position the cursor where you want the ImageMap in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>, select and insert a bitmap picture.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068A				0	en-ZA	With the picture selected, choose \<emph\>Edit - ImageMap\</emph\>. You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02220000.xhp\"\>ImageMap Editor\</link\>, which displays the picture at the background.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A0				0	en-ZA	Use the icons in the ImageMap Editor to draw a hotspot shape, for example a rectangle, over the image at the background.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A3				0	en-ZA	You can see an extended help text on the functions of each icon when you enable Extended Help in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	en-ZA	Enter the "Address" URL that will be shown in a Web browser when the user clicks the hotspot.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AF				0	en-ZA	Optionally, enter the "Text" that will be shown as a tip when the user points the mouse to the hotspot.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B3				0	en-ZA	Click the Apply button to apply your changes, and close the ImageMap Editor.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	en-ZA	Save the document in the %PRODUCTNAME or HTML format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BA				0	en-ZA	You may save the ImageMap as a file and upload that file to a Web server, for example.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Adding Graphics to the Gallery				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154927				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop;to Gallery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;to Gallery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Gallery; adding pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures;adding to Gallery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;pictures in Gallery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;to Gallery\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927	49			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_gallery\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_gallery.xhp\" name=\"Adding Graphics to the Gallery\"\>Adding Graphics to the Gallery\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	en-ZA	You can place a graphic from a document such as an HTML page in the Gallery by drag-and-drop.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	en-ZA	Display the Gallery theme to which you want to add the graphic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	en-ZA	Position the mouse pointer above the graphic, without clicking.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	en-ZA	If the mouse pointer changes to a hand symbol, the graphic refers to a hyperlink. In this case, click the graphic while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key to select it without executing the respective link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	en-ZA	If the mouse pointer does not change to a hand symbol, you can simply click the graphic to select it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3145120				0	en-ZA	Once the graphic is selected, release the mouse button. Click again on the graphic image, keeping the mouse button pressed for more than two seconds. The graphic image is copied to the internal memory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3150772				0	en-ZA	Without releasing the mouse button, drag the graphic into the Gallery.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Copying Graphics From the Gallery				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145345				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>Gallery;dragging pictures to draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;dropping Gallery pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop;from Gallery to draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_fromgallery\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp\" name=\"Copying Graphics From the Gallery\"\>Copying Graphics From the Gallery\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	en-ZA	If you drag a graphic from the Gallery into a text, spreadsheet or presentation document, the graphic will be inserted there.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	en-ZA	If you release the graphic \<emph\>directly on a draw object\</emph\>, please note the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153825				0	en-ZA	If you move the graphic (drag it without pressing any key, in which case no additional symbol appears next to the mouse pointer), only the attributes are copied from the graphic and applied to the draw object on which you release the mouse button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	en-ZA	If you copy the graphic (drag it while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, in which case a plus sign appears next to the mouse pointer), the graphic will be inserted as an object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154514				0	en-ZA	If you create a hyperlink (drag while holding down Shift and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, in which case a linking arrow appears next to the mouse pointer), the drawing object is replaced by the graphic from the Gallery, but the position and size of the replaced draw object are retained.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Opening documents saved in other formats				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153988				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>Microsoft Office;opening Microsoft documents\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>documents; importing\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>importing; documents in other formats\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>opening; documents from other formats\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>loading; documents from other formats\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>converting;Microsoft documents\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>saving; default file formats\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>defaults;document formats in file dialogue\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>file formats; saving always in other formats\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Microsoft Office; as default file format\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>files;importing\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>XML converters\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>converters; XML\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Document Converter Wizard\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>wizards; document converter\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>converters; document converter\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>files, see also documents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145313				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"import_ms\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/import_ms.xhp\" name=\"Opening documents saved in other formats\"\>Opening documents saved in other formats\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	en-ZA	You can open a document saved in another format by using the following procedure:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780	5			0	en-ZA	Select a format from the\<emph\> Files of type\</emph\> list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	en-ZA	Select a file name and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3159399				0	en-ZA	If you always want the file dialogue to show another format by default, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - General\</emph\> and select that format as \<emph\>Default file format\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154898				0	en-ZA	Converting all documents of a folder				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336				0	en-ZA	Open the wizard, which guides you through the operation, to copy and convert all documents from Microsoft Word, Microsoft Excel or Microsoft PowerPoint into OpenDocument file format documents. You can select a source and target directory, specify whether to convert documents and/or templates, and more besides.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	en-ZA	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01130000.xhp\" name=\"File - AutoPilot - Document Converter\"\>\<emph\>File - Wizards - Document Converter\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	hd_id4563127				0	en-ZA	Opening HTML files in Writer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id9207434				0	en-ZA	Choose the file type "HTML Document" to open in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer/Web. This is the default for HTML documents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id7215491				0	en-ZA	All the options of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer/Web are now available to you, such as \<emph\>Show HTML source\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id2299874				0	en-ZA	Choose "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer)" to open in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id1727347				0	en-ZA	All the options of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer are now available to you. Not all options that \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer offers for editing of documents can be saved in HTML format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3148944				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01130100.xhp\" name=\"Working with VBA code\"\>Working with VBA code\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
