helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\aaa_start.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156324				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>samples and templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates; new documents from templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>business cards; using templates\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\aaa_start.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156324				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"aaa_start\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/aaa_start.xhp\" name=\"First Steps\"\>First Steps\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\aaa_start.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156211				0	en-ZA	How to simplify your work using samples and templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\aaa_start.xhp	0	help	par_id3144436				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> includes many sample documents and ready-to-use templates. You can access these by choosing \<emph\>File - New - \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010100.xhp\" name=\"Templates and Documents\"\>\<emph\>Templates and Documents\</emph\>\</link\>, or press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+N.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\aaa_start.xhp	0	help	par_id3147291				0	en-ZA	When you open one of the templates, a new document is created based on this template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\aaa_start.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803563860				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Get more templates online\</emph\> link in the dialogue to select and download more templates.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\aaa_start.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803563974				0	en-ZA	You can also use the various wizards (under the \<emph\>File - Wizards\</emph\> menu) to create your own templates, which you can use as a basis for further documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\aaa_start.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/main.xhp\" name=\"Working with %PRODUCTNAME\"\>Working with \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\aaa_start.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/main.xhp\" name=\"Working with Text Documents\"\>Working with Text Documents\</link\>\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\aaa_start.xhp	0	help	par_id3152997				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/main.xhp\" name=\"Working with Spreadsheets\"\>Working with Spreadsheets\</link\>\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\aaa_start.xhp	0	help	par_id3147243				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"IMPRESS\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/main.xhp\" name=\"Working with Presentations\"\>Working with Presentations\</link\>\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\aaa_start.xhp	0	help	par_id3154047				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/main.xhp\" name=\"Working with Drawings\"\>Working with Drawings\</link\>\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\aaa_start.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MATH\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/main.xhp\" name=\"Working with Formulas\"\>Working with Formulas\</link\>\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Defining Borders for Tables and Table Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155805				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>tables in text; defining borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables in spreadsheets;defining borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders; for tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames; around tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;table borders\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155805				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"border_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/border_table.xhp\" name=\"Defining Borders for Tables and Table Cells\"\>Defining Borders for Tables and Table Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147008				0	en-ZA	Setting a Predefined Border Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	en-ZA	Select the table cells that you want to modify.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346	3			0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Table \</emph\>toolbar (Writer) or on the \<emph\>Line and Filling\</emph\> bar to open the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3143270				0	en-ZA	Click one of the predefined border styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156156				0	en-ZA	This \<emph\>adds\</emph\> the selected style to the current border style of the table cells. Select the blank border style at the top left of the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window to clear all border styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153666				0	en-ZA	Setting a Customized Border Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472				0	en-ZA	Select the table cells that you want to modify.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3147265				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Table - Table Properties - Borders\</emph\> (Writer) or \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\> (Calc).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area select the edge(s) that you want to appear in a common layout. Click on an edge in the preview to toggle the selection of an edge.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id31594132				0	en-ZA	If you select more than one row or column, you can change the middle lines between rows or columns. Select the middle markers in the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526				0	en-ZA	Select a line style and colour for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145606				0	en-ZA	Repeat the last two steps for every border edge.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	en-ZA	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149807				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Adding Texture to Chart Bars				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149798				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>charts; bars with textures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>textures;on chart bars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;textures on chart bars\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3156136				0	en-ZA	You can add texture to the bars in a graph or chart (instead of the default colours) via bitmap graphics:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	en-ZA	Enter edit mode by double-clicking on the chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	en-ZA	In the context menu choose \<emph\>Object Properties\</emph\>. Then choose the \<emph\>Area\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	en-ZA	Click on \<emph\>Bitmap\</emph\>. In the list box select a bitmap as a texture for the currently selected bars. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to accept the setting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Working with Groups 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	bm_id6888027				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>groups;entering/exiting/ungrouping\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames; selection frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exiting;groups\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entering groups\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ungrouping groups\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selection frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multiple selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>marking, see selecting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id2454298				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"groups\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/groups.xhp\"\>Working with Groups\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id2307199				0	en-ZA	You can combine several graphic objects into a group so that you can use them like a single object. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id9983825				0	en-ZA	You can move, transform, resize, distort, or convert all objects in a group together, and you can enter the group any time to change the individual objects. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id5734733				0	en-ZA	You can change the properties (line size, fill colour, and more) of all objects in a group together, and you can enter the group and change the individual objects. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id561540				0	en-ZA	Groups can also be nested to form groups within other groups. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id7705618				0	en-ZA	To group objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id607013				0	en-ZA	Select the objects together that you want to group. Hold down Shift while you click the individual objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1399578				0	en-ZA	Right-click any of the selected objects to open the context menu. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id598162				0	en-ZA	In Impress or Draw, choose Group. In Calc or Writer, choose Group – Group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id6738792				0	en-ZA	To select the objects, you can also drag a selection frame around the objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id7309793				0	en-ZA	For example, you can group all of the objects in a company logo to move and resize the logo as a single object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1227759				0	en-ZA	After you have grouped objects, selecting any part of the group selects the entire group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id7424237				0	en-ZA	To enter a group				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1388592				0	en-ZA	Right-click any object of the group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id343943				0	en-ZA	In Impress or Draw, choose Enter Group. In Calc or Writer, choose Group - Edit Group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id8726767				0	en-ZA	Now you can select and edit a single object in the group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id691549				0	en-ZA	You can add or delete objects to and from a group in this mode. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	en-ZA	The objects that are not part of the group are shown with dimmed colours.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id9141819				0	en-ZA	To exit a group				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id6354869				0	en-ZA	Right-click any object of the group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id2685323				0	en-ZA	In Impress or Draw, choose Exit Group. In Calc or Writer, choose Group - Exit Group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id6042664				0	en-ZA	To exit a group in Draw or Impress, you can also double-click anywhere outside the group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id7889950				0	en-ZA	To ungroup a group				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3236182				0	en-ZA	Right-click any object of the group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1251258				0	en-ZA	In Impress or Draw, choose Ungroup. In Calc or Writer, choose Group - Ungroup.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id8111819				0	en-ZA	Now you can select and edit all objects as individual objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Distributing an XML filter as package 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	bm_id7007583				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>distributing XML filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;XML filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XML filters;saving as package/installing/deleting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;XML filters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10ABC				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"xsltfilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter_distribute.xhp\"\>Distributing An XML Filter As Package\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AC0				0	en-ZA	You can distribute an XML filter to multiple users using a special package format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AC3				0	en-ZA	To Save an XML Filter as a Package				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10ACD				0	en-ZA	The XML Filter Settings dialogue is only available when a text document is open.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10ACA				0	en-ZA	In Writer, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - XML Filter Settings\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AD9				0	en-ZA	Select the filter that you want to distribute and click \<emph\>Save As Package\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AE0				0	en-ZA	To Install an XML Filter from a Package				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AEA				0	en-ZA	The XML Filter Settings dialogue is only available when a text document is opened.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AE7				0	en-ZA	In Writer, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - XML Filter Settings\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AF6				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Open Package\</emph\> and select the package file with the filter you want to install.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10535				0	en-ZA	To Delete an Installed XML Filter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B0A				0	en-ZA	In Writer, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - XML Filter Settings\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B19				0	en-ZA	Select the filter you want to delete and click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_id6011841				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter.xhp\"\>About XML Filters\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Configuring $[officename]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152801				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>configuring; $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>customising; $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"configure_overview\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/configure_overview.xhp\" name=\"Configuring $[officename]\"\>Configuring $[officename]\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	en-ZA	You can customise your $[officename] to suit your needs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3145071				0	en-ZA	You are free to change the items on the menu bar. You can delete items, add new ones, copy items from one menu to another, rename them, and so on.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	en-ZA	The toolbars may be freely configured.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	en-ZA	You can change the shortcut keys.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	en-ZA	To change these, choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06140000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Customize\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Customize\</emph\>\</link\> to open the \<emph\>Customize\</emph\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06140000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Customize\"\>Tools - Customize\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Working with Forms				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	bm_id5762199				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>opening;forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms;creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>design view;creating forms\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F9				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"data_forms\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_forms.xhp\"\>Working with Forms\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	en-ZA	Using forms, you can define how to present the data. Open a text document or a spreadsheet and insert the controls such as push buttons and list boxes. In the properties dialogues of the controls, you can define what data the forms should display.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	en-ZA	Creating a New Form With the Form Wizard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061E				0	en-ZA	In %PRODUCTNAME, you can create a new form using the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01090000.xhp\"\>Form Wizard\</link\>:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	en-ZA	Open the database file where you want to create the new form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10636				0	en-ZA	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Forms\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063E				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Form\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	en-ZA	Creating a New Form Manually				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064C				0	en-ZA	Open the database file where you want to create the new form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10650				0	en-ZA	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Forms\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10658				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Create Form in Design View\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	en-ZA	A new text document opens. Use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\"\>Form Controls\</link\> to insert form controls.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10670				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Forms\</emph\> icon to access all forms that were created from within the current database window. In addition, you can use the \<emph\>Form Controls\</emph\> icons to add database form controls to any Writer or Calc document, but these documents will not be listed in the database window. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Printing Address Labels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>address labels from databases\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>labels; from databases\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>stickers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>databases;creating labels\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"labels_database\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/labels_database.xhp\" name=\"Printing Address Labels\"\>Printing Address Labels\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Labels\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084	37			0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab page, select the format of the label sheets you want to print on. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id0130200903370863				0	en-ZA	Choose the database and table from which to get the data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id013020090337089				0	en-ZA	Select a database field of which you want to print the contents. Click the button that shows a left arrow to insert the database field into the Label Text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id0130200903370930				0	en-ZA	Continue to select and insert database fields if you want more fields on every label. You can press Enter to insert a new line, and you can type any character to insert fixed text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id0130200903370924				0	en-ZA	Optionally, if you want to type more text, apply formatting, or insert images and line art, you should enable \<emph\>Synchronize contents\</emph\> on the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab. If you enable this, once you leave the Labels dialogue box a small window opens with a Synchronize button. Now you only need to work on the first label on the labels document, then click the Synchronize button to copy your work to every label of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_idN10687				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	en-ZA	When you see the label document, you might want to temporarily enable \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Field Names\</item\>. This displays the fields in a more visible manner, so that you can arrange and edit label contents more easily.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3148484				0	en-ZA	You can save and/or print the label document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id8476821				0	en-ZA	When you choose to print the document, you will be asked if you want to print a form letter. Answer Yes to open the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/01150000.xhp\"\>Mail Merge\</link\> dialogue. In the Mail Merge dialogue, you can select the records for which you want to print labels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Inserting Protected Spaces, Hyphens and Conditional Separators				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155364				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>protected spaces;inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spaces; inserting protected spaces\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyphens;inserting custom\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>conditional separators\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>separators; conditional\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dashes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>non-breaking dashes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing;dashes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>protected dashes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exchanging, see also replacing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"space_hyphen\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/space_hyphen.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Protected Spaces, Hyphens and Conditional Separators\"\>Inserting Protected Spaces, Hyphens and Conditional Separators\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156136				0	en-ZA	Non-breaking spaces				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	31			0	en-ZA	To prevent two words from being separated at the end of a line, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command key \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl key\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and the Shift key when you type a space between the words.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id5749687				0	en-ZA	In Calc, you cannot insert non-breaking spaces.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	en-ZA	Non-breaking dash				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3148538				0	en-ZA	An example of a non-breaking dash is a company name such as A-Z. Obviously you would not want A- to appear at the end of a line and Z at the beginning of the next line. To solve this problem, press Shift+Ctrl+ minus sign. In other words, hold down the Shift and Ctrl keys and press the minus key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163802				0	en-ZA	Hyphen, dash				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749	66			0	en-ZA	In order to enter longer dashes, you can find under \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</emph\>\<emph\>- Options\</emph\> the \<emph\>Replace dashes\</emph\> option. This option replaces one or two minus signs under certain conditions with an en-dash or an em-dash (see \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040100.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Help\"\>$[officename] Help\</link\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561	67			0	en-ZA	For additional replacements see the replacements table under \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</emph\>\<emph\>- \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"Replace\"\>\<emph\>Replace\</emph\>\</link\>. Here you can, among other things, replace a shortcut automatically by a dash, even in another font.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153825				0	en-ZA	Definite separator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306	60			0	en-ZA	To support automatic hyphenation by entering a separator inside a word yourself, use the keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+minus sign. The word is separated at this position when it is at the end of the line, even if automatic hyphenation for this paragraph is switched off.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3151245				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04100000.xhp\" name=\"Special characters\"\>Special characters\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Web Pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156014				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/07/09000000.xhp\" name=\"Web Pages\"\>Web Pages\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146946				0	en-ZA	To create a new web page for the Internet, open a new \<emph\>HTML Document\</emph\> by choosing \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143284				0	en-ZA	A tool for creating new web pages is the Web Layout mode, which you enable with \<emph\>View - Web Layout\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147285				0	en-ZA	Creating a New Web Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150808				0	en-ZA	Switch to the web layout mode by choosing \<emph\>View - Web Layout\</emph\> or by opening a new HTML document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136				0	en-ZA	To create an HTML page from your $[officename] document, save the page using one of the "HTML Document" file types.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
