helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02ado.xhp	0	help	par_idN10550				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the options for adding an ADO (Microsoft ActiveX Data Objects) database.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02ado.xhp	0	help	par_idN10565				0	en-ZA	The ADO interface is a Microsoft Windows proprietary container for connecting to databases.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02ado.xhp	0	help	par_idN10568				0	en-ZA	$[officename] requires the Microsoft Data Access Components (MDAC) to use the ADO interface. Microsoft Windows 2000 and XP include these components by default. For earlier visions of Windows, you need to install MDAC separately. You can download MDAC from the Microsoft web site.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02ado.xhp	0	help	par_idN1056B				0	en-ZA	Data source URL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02ado.xhp	0	help	par_idN1056F				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the data source URL.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02ado.xhp	0	help	par_idN10572				0	en-ZA	Example URLs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02ado.xhp	0	help	par_idN10576				0	en-ZA	To connect to an Access 2000 file, use the format:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02ado.xhp	0	help	par_idN10579				0	en-ZA	PROVIDER=Microsoft.Jet.OLEDB.4.0;DATA SOURCE=c:\\Access\\nwind2000.mdb				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02ado.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057C				0	en-ZA	To connect with a name to a catalogue on a Microsoft SQL server that has a name turner, enter:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02ado.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057F				0	en-ZA	PROVIDER=sqloledb;DATA SOURCE=turner;INITIAL CATALOG=First				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02ado.xhp	0	help	par_idN10582				0	en-ZA	To access an ODBC driver as a provider:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02ado.xhp	0	help	par_idN10585				0	en-ZA	DSN=SQLSERVER				2002-02-02 02:02:02
