helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151100				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/05030400.xhp\" name=\"Assign columns\"\>Assign columns\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3156027	2			0	en-ZA	In the data source explorer, you can copy a table by dragging and dropping the table onto the table container. If you select the \<emph\>Attach data \</emph\>check box on the first page of the \<emph\>Copy table \</emph\>dialogue, the \<emph\>Assign columns \</emph\>dialogue opens as the second window. You can use this dialogue to map the contents of a data field in the source table to a different data field in the destination table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157958				0	en-ZA	Source table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145071				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_TAB_NAMEMATCHING_COLS_AVAIL\"\>Lists the data fields in the source table. To include a data field from the source table in the destination table, select the check box in front of the data field name. To map the contents of a data field in the source table to a different data field in the destination table, click the data field in the source table list, and then click the up or down arrow.\</ahelp\> To include all of the source data fields in the destination table, click \<emph\>All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166410				0	en-ZA	Destination table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_TAB_NAMEMATCHING_COLS_ASSIGN\"\>Lists the possible data fields in the destination table. Only the data fields that are selected in the source table list will be included the destination table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
