helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN105BD				0	en-ZA	Oracle database				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	en-ZA	You can use a JDBC driver to access an Oracle database from Solaris or Linux. To access the database from Windows, you need an ODBC driver.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D4				0	en-ZA	On UNIX, ensure that the Oracle database client is installed with JDBC support. The JDBC driver class for the Solaris Oracle client version 8.x is located in the <Oracle client>/product/jdbc/lib/classes111.zip directory. You can also download the latest version of the driver from the Oracle web site:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D7				0	en-ZA	http://otn.oracle.com/tech/java/sqlj_jdbc/content.html				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN105EA				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>In the \<emph\>Data source URL\</emph\> box, enter the location of the Oracle database server. The syntax of the URL depends on the database type. See the documentation that came with the JDBC driver for more information.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F1				0	en-ZA	For an Oracle database, the syntax of the URL is:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F4				0	en-ZA	oracle:thin:@hostname:port:database_name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FD				0	en-ZA	hostname is the name of the machine that runs the Oracle database. You can also replace hostname with the IP address of the server.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN10601				0	en-ZA	port is the port where the Oracle database listens. Ask your database administrator for the correct port address.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN10605				0	en-ZA	database_name is the name of the Oracle database. Ask your database administrator for the correct name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN10608				0	en-ZA	Name of the Oracle database				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN1060C				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the name of the Oracle database.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN1060F				0	en-ZA	Server URL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN10613				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the URL for the database server. \</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN10616				0	en-ZA	Port number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the port number for the database server.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061D				0	en-ZA	Oracle JDBC Driver Class				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN10621				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DSADMIN_DRIVERCLASS\"\>Enter the name of the JDBC driver.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN10630				0	en-ZA	Test Class				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN10634				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Tests the connection with the current settings.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN10637				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabawiz03auth.xhp\"\>Authentication\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN10646				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabawiz00.xhp\"\>Database Wizard\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Queries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150445				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>queries;overview (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables in databases; printing queries (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing; queries (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>queries; printing (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150445				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02000000.xhp\" name=\"Queries\"\>Queries\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150499				0	en-ZA	A "query" is a special view of a table. A query can display chosen records or chosen fields within records; it can also sort those records. A query can apply to one table to multiple tables, if they are linked by common data fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	en-ZA	Use queries to find records from data tables based on certain criteria. All queries created for a database are listed under the \<emph\>Queries\</emph\> entry. Since this entry contains the database queries, it is also called the "query container".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153750				0	en-ZA	Printing Queries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149183				0	en-ZA	To print a query or table:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	en-ZA	Open a text document (or a spreadsheet document if you prefer the specific printing functions of this type of document).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149827				0	en-ZA	Open the database file and click the Table icon if you want to print a table, or click the Query icon if you want to print a query.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	en-ZA	Drag the name of the table or query into the open text document or spreadsheet. The dialogue \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Database Columns\"\>Insert Database Columns\</link\> opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	en-ZA	Decide which columns = data fields you want to include. You can also click the \<emph\>AutoFormat\</emph\> button and select a corresponding formatting type. Close the dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561				0	en-ZA	The query or table will be inserted into your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	en-ZA	Print the document by choosing \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153146				0	en-ZA	You can also open the data source view (F4), select the entire database table in the data source view (button in the top left corner of the table), and then drag the selection to a text document or spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148946				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0212.xhp\" name=\"Sorting and Filtering Data\"\>Sorting and Filtering Data\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149655				0	en-ZA	Allows you to sort and filter the data in a query table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153379				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Design\"\>Query Design\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211				0	en-ZA	With the \<emph\>Query Design\</emph\>, you can create and edit a query or view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153968				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Through Several Tables\"\>Query Through Several Tables\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151043				0	en-ZA	The query result can contain data from several tables if these are linked to each other by suitable data fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159149				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Formulating Query Criteria\"\>Formulating Query Criteria\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154910				0	en-ZA	You can find out which operators and commands can be used to formulate the filter conditions for a query.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156212				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Executing Functions\"\>Executing Functions\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762				0	en-ZA	You can perform calculations with the data of a table and store the results as a query result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11170000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Adabas D Statistics				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150445				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/11170000.xhp\" name=\"Adabas D Statistics\"\>Adabas D Statistics\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3157898				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the access options for the Adabas database.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153750				0	en-ZA	Data Buffer Size				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_NUMERICFIELD_TAB_PAG_ADABAS_SETTINGS_NF_CACHE_SIZE\"\>Enter the size of the data buffer for the database.\</ahelp\> The setting takes effect after you restart the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149095				0	en-ZA	Increment size				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_NUMERICFIELD_TAB_PAG_ADABAS_SETTINGS_NF_DATA_INCREMENT\"\>Enter the size by which you want to automatically increment the database. The maximum increment size is 100 MB.\</ahelp\> The setting takes effect after you restart the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156346				0	en-ZA	Control User Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150355				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_EDIT_TAB_PAG_ADABAS_SETTINGS_ET_CTRLUSERNAME\"\>Enter the name of a user that you want to give limited control to modify some parameters of the database.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153146				0	en-ZA	Control Password				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_EDIT_TAB_PAG_ADABAS_SETTINGS_ET_CTRLPASSWORD\"\>Enter the password of the Control User.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149235				0	en-ZA	Shut down the service when closing $[officename]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153254				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_CHECKBOX_TAB_PAG_ADABAS_SETTINGS_CB_SHUTDB\"\>Exits the Adabas database server when you exit $[officename].\</ahelp\> This option is only available if you start the database server from $[officename] with a control user and password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146948				0	en-ZA	Extended				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156002				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_PUSHBUTTON_TAB_PAG_ADABAS_SETTINGS_PB_STAT\"\>Opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/11170100.xhp\" name=\"Database Statistics\"\>Database Statistics\</link\> dialogue, where you can view statistics about the Adabas database.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Type formatting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163829				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/05030300.xhp\" name=\"Type formatting\"\>Type formatting\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150247	2			0	en-ZA	In the data source explorer, you can copy a table by dragging and dropping the table onto the table container. The\<emph\> Type formatting \</emph\>dialogue is the third window of the \<emph\>Copy table\</emph\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801				0	en-ZA	List box				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145313				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_MULTILISTBOX_TAB_WIZ_TYPE_SELECT_LB_NEW_COLUMN_NAMES\"\>Lists the data fields that will be included in to the copied table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155535				0	en-ZA	Column information				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156426				0	en-ZA	Field name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_TAB_ENT_COLUMNNAME\"\>Displays the name of the selected data field. If you want, you can enter a new name.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156113				0	en-ZA	Field type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_TAB_ENT_TYPE\"\>Select a field type.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149763				0	en-ZA	Length				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155449				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_TAB_ENT_LEN\"\>Enter the number of characters for the data field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159176				0	en-ZA	Decimal places				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153666				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_TAB_ENT_SCALE\"\>Enter the number of decimal places for the data field. This option is only available for numerical or decimal data fields.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150276				0	en-ZA	Default value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147620				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_TAB_ENT_BOOL_DEFAULT\"\>Select the default value for a Yes/No field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153087				0	en-ZA	Automatic type recognition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561				0	en-ZA	$[officename] can automatically recognise field contents when you copy database tables by drag and drop.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156023				0	en-ZA	(maximum) lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155923				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_NUMERICFIELD_TAB_WIZ_TYPE_SELECT_ET_AUTO\"\>Enter the number of lines to use for automatic type recognition.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154347				0	en-ZA	Auto				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3152361				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_PUSHBUTTON_TAB_WIZ_TYPE_SELECT_PB_AUTO\"\>Enables automatic type recognition.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Relations				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153323				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/05020000.xhp\" name=\"Relations\"\>Relations\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146957				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>relational databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957	2			0	en-ZA	This command opens the \<emph\>Relation Design \</emph\>window, which allows you to define relationships between various database tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_CTL_RELATIONTAB\"\>Here you can link together tables from the current database through common data fields.\</ahelp\> Click the \<emph\>New Relation\</emph\> icon to create the relationships, or simply drag-and-drop with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145316				0	en-ZA	This function is only available if you are working with a relational database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149235				0	en-ZA	When you choose \<emph\>Tools - Relationships\</emph\>, a window opens in which all the existing relationships between the tables of the current database are shown. If no relationships have been defined, or if you want to relate other tables of the database to each other, then click the \<emph\>Add Tables\</emph\> icon. The \<link href=\"text/shared/02/14020100.xhp\" name=\"Add Tables\"\>Add Tables\</link\> dialogue opens in which you can select the tables that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152812				0	en-ZA	If the \<emph\>Relation Design\</emph\> window is open, the selected tables cannot be modified, even in Table Design mode. This ensures that tables are not changed while the relations are being created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	en-ZA	The selected tables are shown in the top area of the design view. You can close a table window through the context menu or with the Delete key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148922				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>primary keys;inserting (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>keys;primary keys (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>external keys (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148922				0	en-ZA	Primary key and other key				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149168				0	en-ZA	If you want to define a relation among the different tables, you should enter a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#primaerschluessel\" name=\"primary key\"\>primary key\</link\> that clearly identifies a data field of the existing table. You can refer to the primary key from other tables to access the data of this table. All data fields referring to this primary key will be identified as an external key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147085				0	en-ZA	All data fields referring to a primary key will be identified in the table window by a small key symbol.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153193				0	en-ZA	Define relations				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155430				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>relations; creating and deleting (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155430				0	en-ZA	All existing relations are shown in the relations windows by a line that connects the primary and other key fields. You can add a relation by using drag-and-drop to drop the field of one table onto the field of the other table. A relation is removed again by selecting it and pressing the Delete key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149984				0	en-ZA	Alternatively, you can also click the \<emph\>New Relation\</emph\> icon in the top area of the relation field and define the relation between two tables in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/05020100.xhp\" name=\"Relations\"\>\<emph\>Relations\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153093				0	en-ZA	If you use $[officename] as the front-end for a relational database, the creation and deletion of relationships is not placed in an intermediate memory by $[officename], but is forwarded directly to the external database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155856	15			0	en-ZA	By double-clicking a connection line, you can assign certain properties to the relation. The \<emph\>Relations \</emph\>dialogue opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
