helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\03130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155066				0	en-ZA	You can specify settings for running a slide show in \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Slide Show - Slide Show Settings\"\>\<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show Settings\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\03130000.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CF				0	en-ZA	Specify whether a slide show starts with the current slide or with the first slide on \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - General\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\03130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	en-ZA	To start a slide show, do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\03130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155337				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Slide Show\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Presentation\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\03130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150343				0	en-ZA	Right-click a slide in \<emph\>Normal\</emph\> view and choose \<emph\>Slide Show.\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\03130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156445				0	en-ZA	Press F5.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\03130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153912				0	en-ZA	Under Windows, right-click the *.sxi or *.odp file in the Windows Explorer, then choose \<emph\>Show\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
