helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3145354				0	en-ZA	Select a locked layer, and then choose \<emph\>Format - Layer\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3148393	35			0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> area, clear the \<emph\>Locked \</emph\>check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3150467				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Drawing Curves				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149377				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>lines; drawing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>curves; drawing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>control points definition\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>corner points\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawing;lines\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149377				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"line_draw\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/line_draw.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Curves\"\>Drawing Curves\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868	4			0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Curve\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3150205\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_linetoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150205\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar opens a toolbar to draw Bézier curves. Bézier curves are defined by a start point and an end point, which are called "anchors". The curvature of the Bézier curve is defined by control points ("handles"). Moving a control point changes the shape of the Bézier curve.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id8532364				0	en-ZA	Control points are only visible in "Edit Points" mode. Control points are represented by circles, anchor points are represented by squares. The start point is a little bit larger than the other anchor points.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210				0	en-ZA	Bézier curve segments and straight line segments can be joined to form more complex Bézier curves. Three different transitions can be applied to join adjacent segments:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3154766				0	en-ZA	A \<emph\>symmetrical\</emph\> anchor point has the same line curvature on either side, and two control lines that move together as a straight line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3149874				0	en-ZA	A \<emph\>smooth\</emph\> anchor point may have different line curvatures on either side.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150435				0	en-ZA	A \<emph\>corner\</emph\> anchor point has one or two independent control lines. Changing one side has no effect on the other side.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	hd_id46388				0	en-ZA	How to use the Curve tool				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155262	5			0	en-ZA	On the Drawing toolbar, open the \<emph\>Curves\</emph\> toolbar \<image id=\"img_id3145829\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_linetoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145829\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and select the \<emph\>Curve\</emph\>\<image id=\"Graphic1\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezier_unfilled.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> tool.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155928	6			0	en-ZA	Click where you want the curve to start, and drag in the direction where you want the curve to go. The control line will indicate the direction. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id8174687				0	en-ZA	Hold down \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift\</item\> while you drag to restrict the direction to a 45 degree grid.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3148390				0	en-ZA	Release the mouse where the first control point should be.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3154865	22			0	en-ZA	Move the pointer to where you want the curve segment to end. The curve follows the pointer. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id1556443				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3151172	9			0	en-ZA	Double-click on the position of the end point to finish drawing the line. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id5377056				0	en-ZA	To create a closed shape, double-click the starting point of the line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919				0	en-ZA	Click and release the mouse button to add an anchor point. Move the mouse to draw the next segment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3149451				0	en-ZA	Click and drag in any direction to add a smooth anchor point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	hd_id2071596				0	en-ZA	How to use the Freeform Line tool				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id4907681				0	en-ZA	On the Drawing toolbar, open the \<emph\>Curves\</emph\> toolbar \<image id=\"Graphic2\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_linetoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and select the \<emph\>Freeform Line\</emph\>\<image id=\"Graphic3\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_freeline_unfilled.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> tool.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id1122165				0	en-ZA	Click where you want the curve to start, and keep holding the mouse button down.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id5792107				0	en-ZA	Draw the freeform line as you would do with a pencil.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id7734916				0	en-ZA	Release the mouse button to finish the line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Animating Slide Transitions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153820				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>cross-fading; slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide transitions; applying effects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>animated slide transitions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>transition effects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting; slide transition effects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>effects;animated slide transitions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153820				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"animated_slidechange\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/animated_slidechange.xhp\" name=\"Animating Slide Transitions\"\>Animating Slide Transitions\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150049				0	en-ZA	You can apply a special effect that plays when you display a slide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153811				0	en-ZA	To apply a transition effect to a slide				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3145086				0	en-ZA	In \<emph\>Normal\</emph\> view, select the slide that you want to add the transition effect to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150655	70			0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Tasks\</emph\> pane, click \<emph\>Slide Transition\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154554				0	en-ZA	Select a slide transition from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3149022				0	en-ZA	You can preview the transition effect in the document window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147562				0	en-ZA	To apply the same transition effect to more than one slide				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150263				0	en-ZA	In \<emph\>Slide Sorter\</emph\> view, select the slides that you want to add the transition effect to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3148826	49			0	en-ZA	If you want, you can use the \<emph\>Zoom\</emph\> toolbar \<image id=\"img_id3151172\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_zoom.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151172\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to change the view magnification for the slides.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154269	78			0	en-ZA	On the Tasks pane, click Slide Transition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154102				0	en-ZA	Select a slide transition from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3153785				0	en-ZA	To preview the transition effect for a slide, click the small icon underneath the slide on the \<emph\>Slides Pane\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149341				0	en-ZA	To remove a transition effect				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3151287				0	en-ZA	In \<emph\>Slide Sorter\</emph\> View, select the slides that you want to remove the transition effect from.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3146930	85			0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>No Transition \</emph\>in the listbox on the \<emph\>Tasks\</emph\> pane.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3149300				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/06040000.xhp\" name=\"Slide Transition\"\>Slide Transition\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
