helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\main.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154560				0	en-ZA	Miscellaneous				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Printing a Slide to Fit a Paper Size				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155067				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>fitting to pages; individual slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pages; fitting to printed pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing; fitting to paper\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155067				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"print_tofit\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/print_tofit.xhp\" name=\"Printing a Slide to Fit a Paper Size\"\>Printing a Slide to Fit a Paper Size\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704				0	en-ZA	You can reduce the size of a slide when you print, so that the slide can fit on a printed page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154658				0	en-ZA	Open the document that you want to print.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	en-ZA	In \<emph\>Normal View\</emph\>, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148871	6			0	en-ZA	In \<emph\>Layout settings \</emph\>area, select the \<emph\>Fit object to paper format\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153811				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Paper format\</emph\> area, select a \<emph\>Format\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150431				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The slide is resized to fit the printed page, while maintaining the relative positions of the objects on the slide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Loading Line and Arrow Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145253				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>line styles;loading\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines;about line ends\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>arrows;loading arrow styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles;arrow and line styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>loading;arrow and line styles\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145253				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"line_arrow_styles\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/line_arrow_styles.xhp\" name=\"Loading Line and Arrow Styles\"\>Loading Line and Arrow Styles\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017				0	en-ZA	You can use styles to organise similar line and arrow types. $[officename] provides a few standard style files that you can load and use in your document. If you want, you can add or delete elements from a style file, or even create a custom style file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154485				0	en-ZA	To load a line styles file:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Line Styles\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154705				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Load Line Styles\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145588				0	en-ZA	Locate the file containing the line styles that you want to load, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The file has the format [filename].sod.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3151240				0	en-ZA	To save a line styles file, click the \<emph\>Save Line Styles\</emph\> button, enter a filename, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154765				0	en-ZA	To load an arrow styles file:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153070				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Arrow Styles\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149054				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Load Arrow Styles\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	en-ZA	Locate the file containing the arrow styles that you want to load, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The file has the format [filename].soe.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3166465				0	en-ZA	To save an arrow styles file, click the \<emph\>Save Arrow Styles\</emph\> button, enter a filename, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145822				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05200000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Line\"\>Format - Line\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150207				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>3D rotation objects; generating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>3D objects; generating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>3D scenes; creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; to curves, polygons, 3D\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>extrusion objects\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150207				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"3d_create\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/3d_create.xhp\" name=\"Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects\"\>Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914				0	en-ZA	You can convert two dimensional (2D) objects to create different shapes. $[officename] can convert 2D objects to the following object types:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210				0	en-ZA	Curved object based on Bézier curves				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762				0	en-ZA	Polygon object consisting of straight line segments				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150051				0	en-ZA	3D object with shading and a light source				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149873				0	en-ZA	3D rotation object with shading and a light source				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id31490481				0	en-ZA	Two types of 3D objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id31472951				0	en-ZA	The Status bar displays "3D scene selected". The 3D scenes are built from objects which have dimensions in x, y, and z coordinates. Examples are the objects inserted by the 3D Objects toolbar, and rectangles, ellipses, or text that got created by the Rectangle, Ellipse, or Text icons left on the Drawing toolbar, or any Custom Shapes, and that got converted to 3D by using the context menu "Convert - To 3D". These 3D scenes can be entered (for example, by pressing F3), and the objects can be rotated in 3D. Microsoft Office doesn't know these real 3D objects. When exporting these 3D scenes to Microsoft Office formats, a snapshot of the current view will be exported as a bitmap. 3D bars in charts are of this type, too.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id31506541				0	en-ZA	The Status bar displays "Shape selected". The Custom Shapes can be viewed in a 2D mode or in a 3D mode. At any time, you can switch the view between the two modes. You use the Basic Shapes, Symbol Shapes, and the following icons on the Drawing toolbar to create Custom Shapes. The Custom Shapes can be changed using the 3D Settings toolbar. They do not form a 3D scene, they cannot be illuminated by more than one light source, they show no reflections, and there are some more limitations. You can convert them to a 3D scene, but then they are no longer Custom Shapes. Custom Shapes in 2D or 3D mode can be exported to and imported from Microsoft Office formats.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149048				0	en-ZA	To convert an object to a curved shape:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295				0	en-ZA	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150654				0	en-ZA	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145828				0	en-ZA	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id1027558\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1027558\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object. You can also drag the control points of a handle to modify the shape of the curve.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153738				0	en-ZA	To convert a 2D object to a polygon:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	en-ZA	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774				0	en-ZA	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To Polygon.\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3155368				0	en-ZA	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id7219458\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.2201inch\" height=\"0.2201inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7219458\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153919				0	en-ZA	To convert a 2D object to a 3D object:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147172				0	en-ZA	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN1088B				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Extrusion On/Off\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id2490920\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_extrusiontoggle.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2490920\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar, or right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To 3D\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148828				0	en-ZA	To edit the properties of the 3D object, use the \<emph\>Line and Filling\</emph\> toolbar and the \<emph\>3D Settings\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C5				0	en-ZA	To convert a text object to 3D, use the \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id3821222\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fontworkgalleryfloater.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3821222\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145410				0	en-ZA	To convert a 2D object to a 3D rotation object:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154260				0	en-ZA	A 3D rotation object is created by rotating the selected object around its vertical axis.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147506				0	en-ZA	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151318				0	en-ZA	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To 3D Rotation Object\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3146125				0	en-ZA	To edit the properties of the 3D object, use the Line and Filling toolbar and the 3D Settings toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149336				0	en-ZA	You can rotate the 2D object before converting it to create a more complex shape.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\move_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Moving Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\move_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146121				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>objects;moving in slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;objects in slides\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\move_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146121				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"move_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/move_object.xhp\" name=\"Moving Objects\"\>Moving Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\move_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667				0	en-ZA	You can move selected objects in your slide by dragging them, using the arrow keys, or by copying the objects and pasting them in another location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\move_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	en-ZA	The arrow keys let you move objects more precisely than with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Converting Bitmap Images into Vector Graphics				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153415				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>vectorizing bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; bitmaps to polygons\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bitmaps; converting to vector graphics\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>vector graphics;converting bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153415				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"vectorize\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/vectorize.xhp\" name=\"Converting Bitmap Images into Vector Graphics\"\>Converting Bitmap Images into Vector Graphics\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3155633				0	en-ZA	A vector graphic can be resized without losing the quality of the graphic. In $[officename] Draw and Impress, you can convert a bitmap image into a vector graphic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241				0	en-ZA	Select the bitmap image that you want to convert.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3153812				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	en-ZA	In $[officename] Draw, choose \<emph\>Modify - Convert - To Polygon\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3151387				0	en-ZA	In $[officename] Impress, right-click the object, and then choose \<emph\>Convert - To Polygon\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3149349				0	en-ZA	Set the conversion options for the image, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. See \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/13050200.xhp\" name=\"Convert to Polygon\"\>\<emph\>Convert to Polygon\</emph\>\</link\> for a description of the conversion options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3147371				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/13050200.xhp\" name=\"Convert to Polygon\"\>Convert to Polygon\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Adding a Header or a Footer to All Slides				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153191				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>footers;slide masters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide masters; headers and footers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers and footers; slide masters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;headers/footers in all slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide numbers on all slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page numbers on all slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>date on all slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>time and date on all slides\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153191	1			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"footer\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/footer.xhp\" name=\"Adding a Header or a Footer to All Slides\"\>Adding a Header or a Footer to All Slides\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1356547				0	en-ZA	Every slide is based on a slide master. The text, pictures, tables, fields or other objects that you place on the slide master are visible as a background on all slides that are based on that slide master.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id704672				0	en-ZA	Masters exist for slides, notes, and handouts. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8403576				0	en-ZA	To edit a slide master, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>. Click the Close Master View icon on the Master View toolbar, or choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>, to leave the slide master.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id5641651				0	en-ZA	To edit a notes master, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Notes Master\</emph\>. Click the Close Master View icon on the Master View toolbar, or choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>, to leave the notes master.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1583300				0	en-ZA	To edit a handout master, click the Handout tab above the slide. Click the Normal tab to leave the handout master.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id7251808				0	en-ZA	Adding predefined header or footer objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id5015411				0	en-ZA	Every type of master has some predefined areas to hold the date, footer, and slide numbers. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8217413				0	en-ZA	When you switch to the master view, you can move that areas to any position on the master. You can enter additional text and resize the areas. You can select the contents of the areas and apply text formats. For example, you can change the font size or colour.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id7549668				0	en-ZA	A predefined Header Area is available only for notes and handouts. If you want a header on all slides, you can move the Footer Area on the slide master to the top.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1829889				0	en-ZA	Objects that you insert on a slide master are visible on all slides that are based on that slide master.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8843043				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>View - Header and Footer\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1876583				0	en-ZA	You see a dialogue with two tab pages: \<emph\>Slide\</emph\> and \<emph\>Notes and Handouts\</emph\> where you can enter contents to the predefined areas. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id4101077				0	en-ZA	By default, the \<emph\>Date and Time\</emph\> checkbox is enabled, but the format is set to Fixed and the text input box is empty, so no date and time is visible on the slides.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id204779				0	en-ZA	By default, the \<emph\>Footer\</emph\> checkbox is enabled, but the text input box is empty, so no footer is visible on the slides.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1453901				0	en-ZA	By default, the \<emph\>Slide number\</emph\> checkbox is cleared, so no slide numbers are visible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1445966				0	en-ZA	Enter or select the contents that should be visible on all slides.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1956236				0	en-ZA	If you want to change the position and formatting of the master objects, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id5259559				0	en-ZA	You see the slide master with areas near the bottom. You can move the areas , and you can select the fields and apply some formatting. You can also enter some text here which will be shown next to the fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id2521439				0	en-ZA	Click the Date Area and move the time and date field. Select the <date/time> field and apply some formatting to change the format for the date and time on all slides. The same applies to the Footer Area and the Slide Number Area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id4712057				0	en-ZA	Adding text objects as header or footer objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	en-ZA	You can add a text object anywhere on the slide master.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3148866				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295	12			0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar, select the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3154654\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_texttoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154654\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149947				0	en-ZA	Drag in the slide master to draw a text object, and then type or paste your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155441				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\> when you are finished.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150476				0	en-ZA	You can also add fields, such as the date or page number, to a header or footer by choosing \<emph\>Insert - Fields\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3156320	18			0	en-ZA	You can hide the header or footer on the current slide by choosing \<emph\>Format\</emph\> - \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"Modify Layout\"\>Slide\<emph\> Layout\</emph\>\</link\>, and clearing the \<emph\>Objects on background\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155848				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/04990000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Fields\"\>Insert Fields\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Creating a Flowchart				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150439				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>connectors; using\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>flowcharts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>organisation charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hot spots in flowcharts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>interactions; hot spots\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150439				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"orgchart\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/orgchart.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Flowchart\"\>Creating a Flowchart\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159153				0	en-ZA	To create a flowchart:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3152482				0	en-ZA	Select a tool from the \<emph\>Flowchart\</emph\> toolbar on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	en-ZA	Drag a shape in your slide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3154486				0	en-ZA	To add more shapes, repeat the last steps.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3146967	43			0	en-ZA	Open the \<emph\>Connectors \</emph\>toolbar on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar, and select a connector line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3149945				0	en-ZA	Move the pointer over the edge of a shape so that the connection sites appear.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3146871				0	en-ZA	Click a connection site, drag to a connection site on another shape, and then release.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3145824				0	en-ZA	To add more connectors, repeat the last steps.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3153036				0	en-ZA	You now have the basic outline for your flowchart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155255				0	en-ZA	To add text to the shapes on your flowchart				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3150865				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3145592				0	en-ZA	Double-click the shape, and type or paste your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3154504				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar, and drag a text object over the shape. Type or paste your text into the text object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153730				0	en-ZA	To add a colour fill to a shape:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3155930				0	en-ZA	Select the shape, and choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3145348				0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>Colour\</emph\>, and then click a colour in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150934				0	en-ZA	To add some hot spots that call other slides:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3145300	57			0	en-ZA	Assign \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/06070000.xhp\" name=\"interactions\"\>interactions\</link\> to some objects on your slide. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_idN10898				0	en-ZA	Select the object, then choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Interaction\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A0				0	en-ZA	Select an interaction in the dialogue. For example, select to go to the next slide when the user clicks the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3153922				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/simpress/02/10100000.xhp\" name=\"Connectors\"\>Connectors\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/simpress/02/10030200.xhp\" name=\"Glue points\"\>Glue points\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Loading Colour, Gradient, and Hatching Lists				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154510				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>colours;loading lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>gradients;loading lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hatching;loading lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>loading;colours/gradients/hatchings\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154510				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"palette_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/palette_files.xhp\" name=\"Loading Color, Gradient, and Hatching Lists\"\>Loading Colour, Gradient, and Hatching Lists\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3156385	73			0	en-ZA	You can use lists to organise colours, gradients, or hatching patterns. $[officename] provides several lists that you can load and use in your document. If you want, you can add or delete elements from a list, or even create custom lists. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155961				0	en-ZA	To load a colour list:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Colours\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3152896				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Load Colour List\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3151239				0	en-ZA	Locate the colour list that you want to load, and then click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. A colour list file has the format [filename].soc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762				0	en-ZA	To save a colour list, click the \<emph\>Save Colour List\</emph\> button, enter a filename, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149871				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>colours; default colours\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3149871				0	en-ZA	The CMYK list is optimised for print colours, whereas the colours in the Web and the HTML lists are optimised for displays using a resolution of 256 colours.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150435				0	en-ZA	To load a gradient list:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3150393				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Gradients\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3146322				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Load Gradients List\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3149946				0	en-ZA	Locate the gradient list that you want to load, and then click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. A gradient list file has the format [filename].sog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3150740				0	en-ZA	To save a gradients list, click the \<emph\>Save Gradients List\</emph\> button, enter a filename, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153036				0	en-ZA	To load a hatching list:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3155255				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Hatching\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3153004				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Load Hatches List\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3154505				0	en-ZA	Locate the hatches list that you want to load, and then click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. A hatches list file has the format [filename].soh.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3149881				0	en-ZA	To save a hatches list, click the \<emph\>Save Hatches List\</emph\> button, enter a filename, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3155437				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05210000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Area\"\>Format - Area\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Rehearse Timings of Slide Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145253				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>presentations;rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>timings; rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic slide changes;rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recording;display times for slides\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145253				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"rehearse_timings\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/rehearse_timings.xhp\" name=\"Rehearse Timings of Slide Changes\"\>Rehearse Timings of Slide Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446	1			0	en-ZA	$[officename] assists you in defining the right rehearse timings for automatic slide changes. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	en-ZA	Prepare the slides, start the show using a special icon, tell your imaginary audience what you want to tell for the first slide, then advance to the next slide and so on. $[officename] records the display time for each slide, so the next time you play the show with automatic slide changes, the timing will be as recorded.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146317				0	en-ZA	To record a show with rehearse timings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3149874				0	en-ZA	Open a presentation, and switch to \<emph\>Slide Sorter\</emph\> View.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150651	6			0	en-ZA	Start the show with the \<emph\>Rehearse Timings\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156396\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_rehearsetimings.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156396\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the Slide View bar. You see the first slide, and a timer in the bottom corner.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3145590				0	en-ZA	When it's time to advance to the next slide, click the timer. To keep the default setting for this slide, click the slide, but not the timer. Continue for all slides in your presentation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150333				0	en-ZA	$[officename] has recorded the display time for each slide. Save your presentation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3145248				0	en-ZA	If you want the whole presentation to auto-repeat, open the menu \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show Settings\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Auto\</emph\> and \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150935				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Slide Show Settings\"\>Slide Show Settings\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Editing Curves				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150441				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>curves; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>splitting;curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>closing;shapes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;points\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting;points\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>points;adding/converting/deleting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150441				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"line_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/line_edit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Curves\"\>Editing Curves\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	en-ZA	A curved line segment consists of two data points (endpoints) and two control points (handles). A control line connects a control point to a data point. You can change the shape of a curve by converting a data point to a different type, or by dragging the control points to a different location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	en-ZA	You can also modify the properties of the line by selecting the line and choosing \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3149018\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleobjectbeziermode.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149018\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155959				0	en-ZA	To view the data points and control points of a curved line, select the line, and then click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the Drawing bar. The data points are represented by squares and the control points by circles. A control point might overlay a data point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145587				0	en-ZA	To adjust a curved line segment:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241	51			0	en-ZA	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810				0	en-ZA	Drag a data point to resize the line. If a control point overlies the data point, drag the control point until you can see the data point, and then drag the data point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	en-ZA	Drag a control point. The curve pulls in the direction that you drag the control point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150431				0	en-ZA	To split a curved line:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150395				0	en-ZA	You can only split a curved line that has three or more data points.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3151392	59			0	en-ZA	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149941	60			0	en-ZA	Select a data point, and then click the \<emph\>Split Curve \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150655				0	en-ZA	To create a closed shape:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150743	62			0	en-ZA	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153080	63			0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar, click the\<emph\> Close Bézier\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145162				0	en-ZA	To convert a data point on a curved line:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150336	64			0	en-ZA	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155925				0	en-ZA	Click the data point you want to convert, and do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	en-ZA	To convert the data point to a smooth point, click the \<emph\>Smooth Transition\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145299				0	en-ZA	To convert the data point to a symmetrical point, click the \<emph\>Symmetric Transition\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145348				0	en-ZA	To convert the data point to a corner point, click the \<emph\>Corner Point\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150471				0	en-ZA	To add a data point:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155373	69			0	en-ZA	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3156256	70			0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar, click the\<emph\> Insert Points\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3083280				0	en-ZA	Click the line where you want to add the point, and drag a short distance.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154643				0	en-ZA	If a data point does not have a control point, select the data point, and then click the \<emph\>Convert to Curve\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151186				0	en-ZA	To delete a data point:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153624	74			0	en-ZA	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150261				0	en-ZA	Click the point you want to delete.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3143230	76			0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar, click the\<emph\> Delete Points\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3151174				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0227.xhp\" name=\"Edit Points bar\"\>Edit Points bar\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Changing the Slide Order				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149499				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>slides; arranging\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; arranging slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;order of slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arranging;slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ordering;slides\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149499				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"arrange_slides\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/arrange_slides.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Slide Order\"\>Changing the Slide Order\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	par_id3143233				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>View - Slide Sorter\</emph\>, select one or more slides, and then drag the slides to another location. To select multiple slides, hold down shift and click on the slides. To create a copy of a selected slide, hold down Ctrl while you drag. The mouse pointer changes to a plus sign. You can also drag a copy of a slide into another open $[officename] Impress document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	par_id3153072				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>View - Outline\</emph\>, select a slide, and then drag the slide to another location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\> or \<emph\>Notes\</emph\>, select the slide preview on the \<emph\>Slides Pane\</emph\>, and then drag the slide preview to another location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	par_id3153079				0	en-ZA	To temporarily remove a slide from your presentation, go to \<emph\>Slide Sorter\</emph\>, right-click the slide, and then choose \<emph\>Show/Hide Slide\</emph\>. The number of the hidden slide is crossed out. To show the slide, right-click the slide, and then choose \<emph\>Show/Hide Slide\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Including Spreadsheets in Slides				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154022				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;in presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations;inserting spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>including spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154022				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"table_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/table_insert.xhp\" name=\"Including Spreadsheets in Slides\"\>Including Spreadsheets in Slides\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id4231086				0	en-ZA	You can apply different methods to insert spreadsheet cells into your Impress slides or Draw pages:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id9209875				0	en-ZA	Insert a native table - you enter the data into the cells and apply fancy formatting using the Table Design section on the Tasks pane.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3044526				0	en-ZA	Insert a new table as an OLE object or insert an existing file as an OLE object - you can specify the link to a file to be a live link to the latest data saved in a spreadsheet file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id137333				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the number of columns for the new table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id8626667				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the number of rows for the new table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551581				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Define the vertical alignment of selected or all cell contents. Split or merge cells.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551553				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>All selected cells are merged into one cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551535				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The selected cell is split into several cells. You see the Split Cells dialogue box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551651				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The cell contents are align at the top of the cells.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551697				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The cell contents are aligned vertically centred in the cells.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551632				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The cell contents are aligned at the bottom of the cells.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551734				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Choose commands for the selected or all rows.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804080035				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Distributes the height of the selected or all rows to the same size. The height of the table is not changed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804080063				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, all rows will be selected. If currently cells are selected, all rows containing the selected cells will be selected.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id091620080408008				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, a new row will be inserted at the bottom of the table. If currently cells are selected, as many new rows as the selection has will be inserted below the selection.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804080050				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>All rows of the current selection will be deleted.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163012				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Choose commands for the selected or all columns.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163092				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Distributes the width of the selected or all columns to the same size. The width of the table is not changed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163046				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, all columns will be selected. If currently cells are selected, all columns containing the selected cells will be selected.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163128				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, a new column will be inserted at the right border of the table. If currently cells are selected, as many new columns as the selection has will be inserted right of the selection.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163127				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>All columns of the current selection will be deleted.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163151				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Align the table within the page or slide.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id8594317				0	en-ZA	Inserting a native table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id7184972				0	en-ZA	Go to the Impress slide or Draw page where you want to insert the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id248115				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Table\</item\> or use the Table icon on the Standard toolbar to insert a table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id2748496				0	en-ZA	Double-click the table and enter or paste the data into the cells. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id8270210				0	en-ZA	Select some cell contents and right-click to open the context menu. Choose commands to change the cell's contents, like font size and line spacing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6820276				0	en-ZA	Right-click the table border to open the table's context menu. Use the table's context menu to enter a name and description for the table, or to distribute the rows or columns equally, among other commands.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551725				0	en-ZA	Select some cells and right-click to open a context menu, where you can insert or delete rows and columns, among other commands. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id091620080355171				0	en-ZA	To select a rectangular area of cells, point to a cell in one corner of the rectangle, hold down the mouse button, and drag the mouse to the opposite corner of the rectangle, then release the mouse button. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551880				0	en-ZA	To select one cell, point to that cell, hold down the mouse button, and drag the mouse to the next cell and back, then release the mouse button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151075				0	en-ZA	Inserting a new spreadsheet as an OLE object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	en-ZA	You can add a blank $[officename] Calc spreadsheet to a slide as an OLE object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	en-ZA	Go to the slide where you want to insert the spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313	18			0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - OLE- Object\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Create new\</emph\> and select the %PRODUCTNAME Spreadsheet. Click OK. Click in the spreadsheet to enter your data. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id2466505				0	en-ZA	Click outside the spreadsheet to view the slide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3148870				0	en-ZA	To resize the spreadsheet without resizing the cells, double-click the spreadsheet, and then drag a corner handle. To resize the cells of the spreadsheet, click the spreadsheet, and then drag a corner handle.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150215				0	en-ZA	Inserting a spreadsheet from a file				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154765				0	en-ZA	When you insert an existing spreadsheet into your slide, changes that are made to the original spreadsheet file are not updated on your slide. You can, however, make changes to the spreadsheet in your slide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145112				0	en-ZA	Go to the slide where you want to insert the spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153075				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Object - OLE Object\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>Create from file\</emph\>, and click \<emph\>Search\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537	20			0	en-ZA	Locate the file you want to insert, and then click\<emph\> OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id1616565				0	en-ZA	Enable the \<emph\>Link to file\</emph\> checkbox to insert the file as a live link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155256				0	en-ZA	The entire spreadsheet is inserted into your slide. If you want to change the sheet that is displayed, double-click the spreadsheet, and then select a different sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154505				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Slide Layout\"\>Format - Slide Layout\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150335				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04150100.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Object - OLE Object\"\>Insert - Object - OLE Object\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_save.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Exporting Animations in GIF Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_save.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149666				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>animations; saving as GIFs\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; animations to GIF format\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_save.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149666				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"animated_gif_save\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/animated_gif_save.xhp\" name=\"Exporting Animations in GIF Format\"\>Exporting Animations in GIF Format\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3150202				0	en-ZA	Select an animated object on your slide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3145802				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Export\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064	79			0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>GIF - Graphics Interchange Format (.gif)\</emph\> in the \<emph\>File type \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> check box to export the selected object, and not the entire slide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3150206				0	en-ZA	Locate where you want to save the animated GIF, enter a name, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Creating a Custom Slide Show				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146119				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>slide shows; custom\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>starting; always with the current slide\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>starting;custom slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;hidden slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hidden pages;showing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"individual\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/individual.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Custom Slide Show\"\>Creating a Custom Slide Show\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150344				0	en-ZA	You can create custom slide shows to meet the needs of your audience using slides within the current presentation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715				0	en-ZA	To create a custom slide show:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3153712				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Custom Slide Shows\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3153966	62			0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\> and enter a name for your slide show in the \<emph\>Name \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150249				0	en-ZA	Under \<emph\>Existing Slides\</emph\>, select the slides you want to add to your slide show, and click the \<emph\>>>\</emph\> button. Hold down Shift to select a range of slides, or Ctrl to select multiple slides.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3153916				0	en-ZA	You can change the order of the slides in your custom slide show, by dragging and dropping the slides under \<emph\>Selected Slides\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151387				0	en-ZA	To start a custom slide show:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3147403				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Custom Slide Show\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150538				0	en-ZA	Select the show you want to start from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3149943				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Start\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3145593	56			0	en-ZA	If you want the selected custom slide show to start when you click the \<emph\>Slide Show\</emph\> icon on the\<emph\> Presentation\</emph\> toolbar, or when you press F5, select \<emph\>Use Custom Slide Show\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145169				0	en-ZA	Options for Running a Slide Show				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150335				0	en-ZA	To always start a slide show from the current slide:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150014				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - General\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3155932				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Start presentation\</emph\> area, select the \<emph\>Always with current page\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3155372				0	en-ZA	Do not select this option if you want to run a custom slide show.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153922				0	en-ZA	To hide a slide:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3083278				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Show/Hide Slide\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3151264				0	en-ZA	The slide is not removed from your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147570				0	en-ZA	To show a hidden slide:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3145210				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>View - Slide Sorter\</emph\>, and then select the hidden slide(s) that you want to show.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150260				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Show/Hide Slide\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Saving a Presentation in HTML Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155067				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>exporting;presentations to HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;as HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; exporting to HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML; exporting from presentations\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155067				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"html_export\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/html_export.xhp\" name=\"Saving a Presentation in HTML Format\"\>Saving a Presentation in HTML Format\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3153246				0	en-ZA	Open the presentation that you want to save in HTML format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3149502				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Export\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3148842				0	en-ZA	Set the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> to \<emph\>HTML Document ($[officename] Impress) (.html;.htm)\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3143228				0	en-ZA	Enter a \<emph\>File name\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3153808				0	en-ZA	Follow the instructions in the \<emph\>HTML Export\</emph\> Wizard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3151391				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01110000.xhp\" name=\"HTML Export AutoPilot\"\>HTML Export Wizard\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3150394				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/01170000.xhp\" name=\"File - Export\"\>File - Export\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Zooming With the Keypad				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149018				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>zooming;keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>keyboard; zooming\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"change_scale\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/change_scale.xhp\" name=\"Zooming With the Keypad\"\>Zooming With the Keypad\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	par_id3148487				0	en-ZA	You can use the keypad to quickly enlarge or reduce the view on your slide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	par_id3149501				0	en-ZA	To zoom in, press the Plus Sign.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	par_id3148837				0	en-ZA	To zoom out, press the Minus Sign.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	par_id7954954				0	en-ZA	If you are using a mouse with a scroll wheel, you can hold down Ctrl and turn the wheel to change the zoom factor in all main modules of %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/simpress/04/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Shortcut keys for presentations\"\>Shortcut keys for presentations\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Using Gluepoints				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	bm_id0919200803534995				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>glue points;using\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"gluepoints\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/gluepoints.xhp\"\>Using Gluepoints\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803040964				0	en-ZA	In Impress and Draw, you can connect each two shapes with a line called a \<link href=\"text/simpress/02/10100000.xhp\"\>connector\</link\>. When you draw a connector between shapes, the connector will be attached to a gluepoint on each shape. Each shape has some default gluepoints, and the positions of the default gluepoints depend on the specific shape. You can add your own custom gluepoints to a shape and then attach connectors to the custom gluepoints.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041099				0	en-ZA	To add and edit gluepoints				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id091920080304108				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041082				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Glue Point\</emph\> icon on the Drawing toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041186				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Glue Points\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041160				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Insert Glue Point\</emph\> icon on the Gluepoints toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041115				0	en-ZA	Click inside the shape where you want to add the new gluepoint.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041133				0	en-ZA	If the shape is filled, you can click anywhere inside the shape. If the shape is unfilled, you can click the border to insert a glue point. Once inserted, you can drag the glue point to another position inside the shape.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041250				0	en-ZA	With the four icons next to the \<emph\>Insert Glue Point\</emph\> icon, you choose the directions which will be permitted for a connector at this gluepoint. You can choose one or more directions for a particular gluepoint.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041298				0	en-ZA	If the \<emph\>Glue Point Relative\</emph\> icon is active, the gluepoint moves when you resize the object to keep its position relative to the object borders.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041223				0	en-ZA	If the \<emph\>Glue Point Relative\</emph\> icon is not active, the icons next to it are no longer greyed out. With these icons you can decide where a gluepoint will be placed when the size of the object is changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Showing a Slide Show				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	bm_id5592516				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>running slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide shows; starting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; starting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>starting; slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide transitions;automatic\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic slide transition\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id4901272				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"show\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/show.xhp\" name=\"Showing a Slide Show\"\>Showing a Slide Show\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9636829				0	en-ZA	Different ways exist to start a slide show. Once a slide show is running, you can take control pressing keys or clicking the mouse buttons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id7076937				0	en-ZA	By default, a slide show always starts with the first slide. You advance manually through slides up to the last slide. You can change these settings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id9954527				0	en-ZA	Running a Slide Show				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id6860255				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show\</emph\> to run the show.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4199957				0	en-ZA	If you want all shows to start from the current slide instead of the first slide, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - General\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Always with current page\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3209936				0	en-ZA	Click to advance to the next effect or to the next slide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id8702658				0	en-ZA	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Esc\</item\> to abort the show before the end.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3741264				0	en-ZA	Many more keys are available to \<link href=\"text/simpress/04/01020000.xhp\"\>control a slide show\</link\>. You can also right-click to open a context menu with useful commands.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id5694143				0	en-ZA	Showing an automatic slide show (kiosk mode)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id5829645				0	en-ZA	For an automatic change to the next slide, you must assign a slide transition to each slide. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id2361522				0	en-ZA	On the Task Pane, click \<emph\>Slide Transition\</emph\> to open that tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9168980				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Advance slide\</emph\> area, click \<emph\>Automatically after\</emph\>, and select a time duration.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9766533				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Apply to All Slides\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id6081728				0	en-ZA	You can assign a different time for every slide to advance to the next slide. The \<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/rehearse_timings.xhp\"\>rehearse timings\</link\> feature can assist you to get the timing right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9219641				0	en-ZA	To advance to the first slide, after all slides have been shown, you must set the slide show to repeat automatically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3174230				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show Settings\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id1336405				0	en-ZA	In the Type area, click \<emph\>Auto\</emph\> and select a pause time between shows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4959257				0	en-ZA	When you create a new slide show using the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01050000.xhp\"\>Presentation Wizard\</link\>, you can select the duration of slides and of the pause, on the third wizard page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id1906491				0	en-ZA	Running a slide show from a file				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4799340				0	en-ZA	You can start %PRODUCTNAME from a command prompt, followed by the parameter \<item type=\"literal\"\>-show\</item\> and an Impress filename. For example, to start the file \<item type=\"literal\"\>filename.odp\</item\> from the command prompt, enter the following command:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id1502121				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"literal\"\>soffice -show filename.odp\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id8266853				0	en-ZA	This assumes that soffice is in the program path of your system, and that \<item type=\"literal\"\>filename.odp\</item\> is located in the current directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Animating Objects in Presentation Slides				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150251				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>objects; moving along paths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>connecting; paths and objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paths; moving objects along\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>motion paths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;animation effects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>effects;applying to/removing from objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>animation effects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>animations;editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom animation\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150251	31			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"animated_objects\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/animated_objects.xhp\" name=\"Animating Objects in Slides\"\>Animating Objects in Presentation Slides\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3150214	32			0	en-ZA	You can apply preset animation effects to objects on your slide. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154762	70			0	en-ZA	To apply an animation effect to an object: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3146964				0	en-ZA	On a slide in \<emph\>Normal\</emph\> view, select the object you want to animate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3149875				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Custom Animation\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>, and then select an animation effect.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3166462				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Custom Animation\</emph\> dialogue, click a tab page to choose from a category of effects. Click an effect, then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060				0	en-ZA	To preview the animation, click the \<emph\>Play\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	hd_id2476577				0	en-ZA	To apply and edit a motion path effect:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id4217047				0	en-ZA	An object can be animated to move along a motion path. You can use predefined or your own motion paths.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id2629474				0	en-ZA	If you select "Curve", "Polygon", or "Freeform Line", the dialogue closes and you can draw your own path. If the drawing is finished and not cancelled, the created path is removed from the document and inserted as a motion path effect.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id8069704				0	en-ZA	 \<emph\>Editing motion paths\</emph\> 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id4524674				0	en-ZA	If the Custom Animation Panel is visible, the motion paths of all effects of the current slide are drawn as a transparent overlay on the slide. All paths are visible all the time, therefore animations with consecutive paths can be created easily. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id4396801				0	en-ZA	A motion path can be selected by clicking on the path. A selected path will support handles, it can be moved and resized like a shape. A double click on a path starts the point edit mode. The point edit mode can also be started by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Points\</item\> or by pressing \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F8\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148387				0	en-ZA	To remove an animation effect from an object:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774				0	en-ZA	On a slide in \<emph\>Normal\</emph\> view, select the object from which to remove the effect.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3155372				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Custom Animation\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3153718				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Remove\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Applying a Slide Design to a Slide Master 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152596				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>slide designs\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide masters; designing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds; slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slides; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>master pages, see slide masters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"masterpage\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/masterpage.xhp\" name=\"Applying a Slide Design to a Slide Master\"\>Applying a Slide Design to a Slide Master\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017				0	en-ZA	Every slide in a presentation has exactly one slide master, also known as master page. A slide master determines the text formatting style for the title and outline and the background design for all slides that use this slide master.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	en-ZA	To apply a new slide master				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>Format - Slide Design\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Load\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	en-ZA	Under \<emph\>Categories\</emph\>, select a slide design category.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3153915	26			0	en-ZA	Under \<emph\>Templates\</emph\>, select a template with the design that you want to apply. To preview the template, click \<emph\>More\</emph\>, and then select the \<emph\>Preview \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154652				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145115				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150436				0	en-ZA	To apply the slide design to all of the slides in your presentation, select the \<emph\>Exchange background page\</emph\> check box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3151387				0	en-ZA	To apply the slide design to the current slide only, clear the \<emph\>Exchange background page\</emph\> check box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3149941				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/05100000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Copying Slides From Other Presentations				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146971				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>copying; slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slides; copying between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pages; copying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; slides from files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;slides from other presentations\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146971				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"page_copy\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/page_copy.xhp\" name=\"Copying Slides From Other Presentations\"\>Copying Slides From Other Presentations\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149378				0	en-ZA	You can insert slides from another presentation into the current presentation. You can also copy and paste slides between presentations.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153418				0	en-ZA	To insert a slide from another presentation:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	en-ZA	Open a presentation, and choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - File\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3159238				0	en-ZA	Locate the presentation file containing the slide that you want to insert, and click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3148837				0	en-ZA	Click the plus sign next to the icon for the presentation file, and then select the slide(s) that you want to insert.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3148869				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154651				0	en-ZA	To copy and paste slides between presentations:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3153812				0	en-ZA	Open the presentations that you want to copy and paste between.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3153073	14			0	en-ZA	In the presentation containing the slide(s) that you want to copy, choose\<emph\> View - Slide Sorter\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3147401	5			0	en-ZA	Select the slide(s), and then choose\<emph\> Edit - Copy\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3147298				0	en-ZA	Change to the presentation where you want to paste the slide(s), and then choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3156401				0	en-ZA	Select the slide that you want the copied slide to follow, and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150655				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/04110000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - File\"\>Insert - File\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Inserting Layers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148797				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>layers; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; layers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;layer properties\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148797				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"layer_new\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/layer_new.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Layers\"\>Inserting Layers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	en-ZA	Drawings in %PRODUCTNAME Draw support layers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_idN10643				0	en-ZA	Right-click the layer tab area at the bottom.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert Layer\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3155068	12			0	en-ZA	Type a name for the layer in the \<emph\>Name \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382	15			0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Properties \</emph\>area, set the options for the layer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3153964				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The new layer automatically becomes the active layer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3154658				0	en-ZA	To change the properties of a layer, click the name tab of the layer, and then choose \<emph\>Format - Layer\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3153814				0	en-ZA	You cannot change the name of or delete a predefined \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Draw layer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150717				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>text; converting to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>characters; converting to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sign conversion to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; text to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;converting text to\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>curves;converting text to\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150717				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"text2curve\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/text2curve.xhp\" name=\"Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects\"\>Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	en-ZA	You can convert text characters into curves that you can edit and resize as you would any drawing object. Once you convert text into a drawing object, you can no longer edit the content of the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153965				0	en-ZA	To convert text into a drawing object:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3146963				0	en-ZA	Select the text that you want to convert, and do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3149053				0	en-ZA	In $[officename] Draw, choose \<emph\>Modify - Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150395				0	en-ZA	In $[officename] Impress, right-click the border of the text object, and then choose \<emph\>Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150746				0	en-ZA	If your text contains more than one character, the converted text becomes a grouped object. Double-click the group to edit individual objects. Press Esc when finished.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150336				0	en-ZA	Now, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar. Click the object. You can see all the Bézier points of the object. On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> bar, you can find various icons for editing, inserting and deleting points.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Changing the Slide Background Fill				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150199				0	en-ZA	            \<bookmark_value\>backgrounds; changing\</bookmark_value\>            \<bookmark_value\>slide masters; changing backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>            \<bookmark_value\>slides;changing backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>        				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150199	33			0	en-ZA	            \<variable id=\"background\"\>                \<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/background.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Slide Background Fill\"\>Changing the Slide Background Fill\</link\>            \</variable\>        				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3155067				0	en-ZA	You can change the background colour or the background fill of the current slide or all of the slides in your document. For a background fill, you can use hatching, a gradient, or a bitmap image.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3148701				0	en-ZA	If you want to change the background fill for all of the slides, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>. To change the background fill of a single slide, choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id624713				0	en-ZA	            \<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click Set Background Picture for Slide in the context menu of a slide in Normal view to select a bitmap file. This file is used as a background picture.\</ahelp\>        				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150534				0	en-ZA	To use a colour, gradient, or hatching pattern for the slide background				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149942				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, and then click on the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3148725	51			0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Fill \</emph\>area, do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3153040				0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>Colour\</emph\>, and then click a colour in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150866				0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>Gradient\</emph\>, and then click a gradient style in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150338				0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>Hatching\</emph\>, and then click a hatching style in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150021				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145244				0	en-ZA	To use an image for the slide background				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3148394				0	en-ZA	You can display an entire image as a slide background, or you can tile the image to produce a patterned background.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3156064				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, and then click on the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3145356	59			0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Fill \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>Bitmap\</emph\>, and then click an image in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150757	60			0	en-ZA	If you want to use a custom image for the slide background, close the \<emph\>Page Setup \</emph\>dialogue, and then choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\>. Click the \<emph\>Bitmaps \</emph\>tab, and then click \<emph\>Import\</emph\>. Locate the image you want to import and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. When you return to the \<emph\>Background \</emph\>tab, the image you imported will be in the \<emph\>Bitmap \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3153151				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150263	62			0	en-ZA	To display the entire image as the background, clear the \<emph\>Tile \</emph\>check box in the \<emph\>Position \</emph\>area, and then select \<emph\>AutoFit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149756				0	en-ZA	To tile the image on the background, select \<emph\>Tile\</emph\>, and set the \<emph\>Size\</emph\>, \<emph\>Position\</emph\>, and \<emph\>Offset\</emph\> options for the image.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3154934				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3158403				0	en-ZA	This modification is only valid for the current presentation document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10820				0	en-ZA	To save a new slide master as a template				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10827				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\> to change to the slide master.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082F				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\> to change the slide background, or choose other formatting commands. Objects that you add here will be visible on all slides that are based on this slide master.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\> to close the master view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN1083F				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\> to save the document as a template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10847				0	en-ZA	Enter a name for the template. Do not change the category from "My Templates". Click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084A				0	en-ZA	Now you can use the Presentation Wizard to open a new presentation based on your new template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Printing Presentations				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153726				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>printing; presentations\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>slides; printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>notes; printing in presentations\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>outlines; printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>presentations; printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tiled printing of slides\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;layout for handouts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>handout printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>layout;printing handouts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"printing\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/printing.xhp\" name=\"Printing Presentations\"\>Printing Presentations\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154486				0	en-ZA	Default printer settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3156385				0	en-ZA	To set the default printing options for $[officename] Impress, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153914				0	en-ZA	Setting printer options for the current presentation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3154651				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3149870				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Impress\</emph\> or the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab page, and then select the printer options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3150431				0	en-ZA	These settings override the default printer options in \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - Print\</emph\> for the current print job only.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id4555192				0	en-ZA	Choosing a print layout for handouts				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id7197790				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Print\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id1104159				0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab page of the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialogue, select the "Handouts" entry from the Document listbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id9354533				0	en-ZA	Select the number of slides to print per page of paper.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id6556596				0	en-ZA	Defining print options for handouts				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id6744285				0	en-ZA	Click the Handout tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id996734				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Page Number\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Header and Footer\</emph\> dialogue box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id6752220				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Notes and Handouts\</emph\> to enter the header and footer text for handouts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id5703909				0	en-ZA	You see four areas on this dialogue with check boxes for Header, Date and time, Footer, and Page number. These four areas correspond to the four areas in the corners of the handout master view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id4984282				0	en-ZA	Enter text for header, footer, and date. Check the \<emph\>Page number\</emph\> box, if you want to number the handout pages. Ensure the \<emph\>Header\</emph\> check box is enabled if you want your header text to be printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id816064				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Apply to All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id863063				0	en-ZA	The fields in the handout master view on screen are not updated, but the text that you entered will be printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id5036164				0	en-ZA	Printing handouts or notes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id2901394				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Print\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id5674611				0	en-ZA	Click the Document listbox and select the type of contents to print.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id1308023				0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>Handouts\</emph\> or \<emph\>Notes\</emph\> and select the number of slides to print on each page of paper.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id6821192				0	en-ZA	If you want another layout of the slides on the printed paper pages, use the mouse to move the slides around on the Handout view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151389				0	en-ZA	Printing a range of slides				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3146318				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>View - Slide Sorter\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3166465				0	en-ZA	Hold down Shift, and click the range of slides that you want to print.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3157875				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3150746				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Range and copies\</emph\> area, click \<emph\>Slides\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3154561				0	en-ZA	Enter the slide numbers you want to print, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Creating Animated GIF Images				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153188				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>cross-fading; creating cross-fades\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>GIF images; animating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>animated GIFs\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153188				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"animated_gif_create\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/animated_gif_create.xhp\" name=\"Creating Animated GIF Images\"\>Creating Animated GIF Images\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	en-ZA	You can animate drawing objects, text objects, and graphic objects (images) on your slides to make your presentation more interesting. $[officename] Impress provides you with a simple animation editor where you can create animation images (frames) by assembling objects from your slide. The animation effect is achieved by rotating through the static frames that you create.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154657				0	en-ZA	If you create a bitmap animation (animated GIF), you can assign a delay time to each frame, and specify the number of times the animation is played.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150250				0	en-ZA	To create an animated GIF:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148703	59			0	en-ZA	Select an object or group of objects that you want to include in your animation and choose\<emph\> Insert - Animated Image\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149601				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145086	97			0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Apply Object \</emph\>button \<image id=\"img_id3148489\" src=\"sd/res/get1obj.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148489\"\>Note Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to add a single object or a group of objects to the current animation frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150860	98			0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Apply Objects Individually \</emph\>button \<image id=\"img_id3149355\" src=\"sd/res/getallob.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149355\"\>Tip Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to create a separate animation frame for each of the selected objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148391	61			0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Animation Group \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>Bitmap object\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154871				0	en-ZA	Use the animation timeline to specify the duration for displaying a frame and the number of times an animation sequence is presented (looping).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154644				0	en-ZA	Enter a frame number in the \<emph\>Image Number\</emph\> box (left box).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150756	63			0	en-ZA	Enter the number of seconds you want the frame to display in the \<emph\>Duration \</emph\>box (middle box).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151182				0	en-ZA	Repeat the last two steps for each frame in your animation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177	100			0	en-ZA	You can preview your animation by using the controls to the left of the \<emph\>Image Number \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154939	65			0	en-ZA	Select the number of times you want the animation sequence to repeat in the \<emph\>Loop count \</emph\>box (right box).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145421				0	en-ZA	Select an alignment option for the objects in the \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154285				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Create\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	About Layers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149018				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>layers; definition\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"layers\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/layers.xhp\" name=\"About Layers\"\>About Layers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313	3			0	en-ZA	Layers are available in $[officename] Draw, not in $[officename] Impress. Layers allow you to assemble elements on a page that are related. Think of layers as individual workspaces that you can hide from view, hide from printing, or lock. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id7036957				0	en-ZA	Layers do not determine the stacking order of objects on your page, except for the \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer which is always in front of other layers. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id1614734				0	en-ZA	The stacking order of objects on your page is determined by the sequence in which you add the objects. You can rearrange the stacking order by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id398876				0	en-ZA	The areas on a layer that do not contain objects are transparent.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146962				0	en-ZA	$[officename] Draw provides three default layers:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153073				0	en-ZA	Layout				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3149053				0	en-ZA	Controls				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	en-ZA	Dimension Lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156397				0	en-ZA	You cannot delete or rename the default layers. You can add your own layers by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Layer\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Layout\</emph\> layer is the default workspace. The \<emph\>Layout\</emph\> layer determines the location of title, text, and object placeholders on your page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150742				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer can be used for buttons that have been assigned an action, but that should not be printed. Set the layer's properties to not printable. Objects on the \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer are always in front of objects on other layers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153085				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Dimension Lines\</emph\> layer is where you draw, for example, the dimension lines. By switching the layer to show or hide, you can easily switch these lines on and off.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154507				0	en-ZA	You can lock a layer to protect its contents, or hide a layer and its contents from view or from printing. When you add a new layer to a page, the layer is added to all of the pages in your document. However, when you add an object to a layer, it is only added to the current page. If you want the object to appear on all of the pages, add the object to the master page (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Master\</item\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Selecting Underlying Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154492				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>objects; selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting; hidden objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>covered objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>underlying objects\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154492				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"select_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/select_object.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Underlying Objects\"\>Selecting Underlying Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3159238				0	en-ZA	To select an object that is covered by other objects, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and click through the objects until you reach the underlying object. To cycle through the objects in reverse order, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift when you click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	en-ZA	To select an object that is covered by another object using the keyboard, press Tab to cycle through the objects on the slide. To cycle through the objects in reverse order, press Shift+Tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Insert Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150202				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sdraw/01/04010000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Page\"\>Insert Page\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152988				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"seitetext\"\>Inserts a blank page after the selected page.\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
