helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150217				0	en-ZA	33				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150312				0	en-ZA	Select a single column range in which to enter the frequency according to the class limits. You must select one field more than the class ceiling. In this example, select the range C1:C6. Call up the FREQUENCY function in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>. Select the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> range in (A1:A11), and then the \<emph\>Classes\</emph\> range in which you entered the class limits (B1:B6). Select the \<emph\>Array\</emph\> check box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You will see the frequency count in the range C1:C6.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN11269				0	en-ZA	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#moreontop\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151030				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>MDETERM function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>determinants\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151030				0	en-ZA	MDETERM				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154073				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MDET\"\>Returns the array determinant of an array.\</ahelp\> This function returns a value in the current cell; it is not necessary to define a range for the results.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156366				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3156380				0	en-ZA	MDETERM(Array)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150290				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Array\</emph\> represents a square array in which the determinants are defined.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN11035				0	en-ZA	You can find a general introduction to using Array functions on top of this page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN11333				0	en-ZA	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#moreontop\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151348				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>MINVERSE function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inverse arrays\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151348				0	en-ZA	MINVERSE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3145569				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MINV\"\>Returns the inverse array.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156072				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3156085				0	en-ZA	MINVERSE(Array)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3157849				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Array\</emph\> represents a square array that is to be inverted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN113EE				0	en-ZA	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#moreontop\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157868				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3149638				0	en-ZA	Select a square range and select MINVERSE. Select the output array, select the \<emph\>Array\</emph\> field and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148546				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>MMULT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148546				0	en-ZA	MMULT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3148518				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MMULT\"\>Calculates the array product of two arrays.\</ahelp\> The number of columns for array 1 must match the number of rows for array 2. The square array has an equal number of rows and columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146767				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150798				0	en-ZA	MMULT(Array; Array)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150812				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Array\</emph\> at first place represents the first array used in the array product.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3152553				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Array\</emph\> at second place represents the second array with the same number of rows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN114C3				0	en-ZA	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#moreontop\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152574				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3146826				0	en-ZA	Select a square range. Choose the MMULT function. Select the first \<emph\>Array\</emph\>, then select the second \<emph\>Array\</emph\>. Using \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Array\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The output array will appear in the first selected range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154970				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>TRANSPOSE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154970				0	en-ZA	TRANSPOSE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3155276				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MTRANS\"\>Transposes the rows and columns of an array.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155294				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3153843				0	en-ZA	TRANSPOSE(Array)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3153857				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Array\</emph\> represents the array in the spreadsheet that is to be transposed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN115A5				0	en-ZA	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#moreontop\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159352				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3159366				0	en-ZA	In the spreadsheet, select the range in which the transposed array can appear. If the original array has n rows and m columns, your selected range must have at least m rows and n columns. Then enter the formula directly, select the original array and press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Shift+Command+Enter\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Shift+Ctrl+Enter\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>. Or, if you are using the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Array\</emph\> check box. The transposed array appears in the selected target range and is protected automatically against changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3109846				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>LINEST function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109846				0	en-ZA	LINEST				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3144733				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_RGP\"\>Returns a table of statistics for a straight line that best fits a data set.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152825				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3152839				0	en-ZA	LINEST(data_Y; data_X; linearType; stats)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3152853				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>data_Y\</emph\> is a single row or column range specifying the y coordinates in a set of data points.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154428				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>data_X\</emph\> is a corresponding single row or column range specifying the x coordinates. If \<emph\>data_X\</emph\> is omitted it defaults to \<item type=\"literal\"\>1, 2, 3, ..., n\</item\>. If there is more than one set of variables \<emph\>data_X\</emph\> may be a range with corresponding multiple rows or columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id0811200804502119				0	en-ZA	LINEST finds a straight line \<item type=\"literal\"\>y = a + bx\</item\> that best fits the data, using linear regression (the "least squares" method). With more than one set of variables the straight line is of the form \<item type=\"literal\"\>y = a + b1x1 + b2x2 ... + bnxn\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154448				0	en-ZA	 if\<emph\>linearType\</emph\> is FALSE the straight line found is forced to pass through the origin (the constant a is zero; y = bx). If omitted, \<emph\>linearType\</emph\> defaults to TRUE (the line is not forced through the origin).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154142				0	en-ZA	if\<emph\>stats\</emph\> is omitted or FALSE only the top line of the statistics table is returned. If TRUE the entire table is returned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id0811200804502261				0	en-ZA	LINEST returns a table (array) of statistics as below and must be entered as an array formula (for example by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+Return rather than just Return).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN11416				0	en-ZA	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN116C6				0	en-ZA	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#moreontop\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154162				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154176				0	en-ZA	This function returns an array and is handled in the same way as the other array functions. Select a range for the answers and then the function. Select \<emph\>data_Y\</emph\>. If you want, you can enter other parameters. Select \<emph\>Array\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3155468				0	en-ZA	The results returned by the system (if \<emph\>stats\</emph\> = 0), will at least show the slope of the regression line and its intersection with the Y axis. If \<emph\>stats\</emph\> does not equal 0, other results are to be displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155491				0	en-ZA	Other LINEST Results:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3159291				0	en-ZA	Examine the following examples:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
