helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3143277				0	en-ZA	Each unit of measure can be preceded by a prefix character from the following list:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3148422				0	en-ZA	Permitted prefix characters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3149490				0	en-ZA	10^(<0)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3149931				0	en-ZA	d, c, m, u, n, p, f, a, z, y				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3149589				0	en-ZA	10^(>0)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3151248				0	en-ZA	e, h, k, M, G, T, P, E, Z, Y				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200903061174				0	en-ZA	Information units "bit" and "byte" may also be prefixed by one of the following IEC 60027-2 / IEEE 1541 prefixes:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200903090966				0	en-ZA	ki kibi 1024				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200903090958				0	en-ZA	Mi mebi 1048576				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200903090936				0	en-ZA	Gi gibi 1073741824				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200903090975				0	en-ZA	Ti tebi 1099511627776				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200903090930				0	en-ZA	Pi pebi 1125899906842620				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200903091070				0	en-ZA	Ei exbi 1152921504606850000				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200903091097				0	en-ZA	Zi zebi 1180591620717410000000				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200903091010				0	en-ZA	Yi yobi 1208925819614630000000000				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146125				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3153695				0	en-ZA	CONVERT_ADD(Number; "FromUnit"; "ToUnit")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3147522	211			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number to be converted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3154472	212			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>FromUnit\</emph\> is the unit from which conversion is taking place.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3153790	213			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>ToUnit\</emph\> is the unit to which conversion is taking place. Both units must be of the same type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id09022809540918				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Calc:_CONVERT_ADD_function\"\>Current list of CONVERT_ADD units in the OpenOffice.org Wiki.\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156270				0	en-ZA	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3156336	215			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=CONVERT_ADD(10;"HP";"PS") \</item\>returns, rounded to two decimal places, 10.14. 10 HP equal 10.14 PS.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3154834	216			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=CONVERT_ADD(10;"km";"mi") \</item\>returns, rounded to two decimal places, 6.21. 10 kilometers equal 6.21 miles. The k is the permitted prefix character for the factor 10^3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147096				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>FACTDOUBLE function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>factorials;numbers with increments of two\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147096				0	en-ZA	FACTDOUBLE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3151309				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_FACTDOUBLE\"\>Returns the double factorial of a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154666				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3155121				0	en-ZA	FACTDOUBLE(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3158440	40			0	en-ZA	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\>            \<emph\>!!\</emph\>, the double factorial of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, where \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is an integer greater than or equal to zero.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id2480849				0	en-ZA	For even numbers FACTDOUBLE(n) returns:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id4181951				0	en-ZA	2*4*6*8* ... *n				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id2927335				0	en-ZA	For odd numbers FACTDOUBLE(n) returns:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id2107303				0	en-ZA	1*3*5*7* ... *n				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id4071779				0	en-ZA	FACTDOUBLE(0) returns 1 by definition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154622				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id7844477				0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=FACTDOUBLE(5)\</item\> returns 15.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3154116	43			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=FACTDOUBLE(6)\</item\> returns 48.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id6478469				0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=FACTDOUBLE(0)\</item\> returns 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Add-in Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150870				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>add-ins; functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>functions; add-in functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Function Wizard; add-ins\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150870				0	en-ZA	Add-in Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427	2			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"addintext\"\>The following describes and lists some of the available add-in functions. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3163713				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp#addinconcept\"\>Add-in concept\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120	5			0	en-ZA	You will also find a \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\"\>description of the $[officename] Calc add-in interface\</link\> in the Help. In addition, important functions and their parameters are described in the Help for the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Shared Library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>$[officename] Calc add-in DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151075				0	en-ZA	Add-ins supplied				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3156285				0	en-ZA	$[officename] contains examples for the add-in interface of $[officename] Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3159267				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060115.xhp\"\>Analysis Functions Part One\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3154703				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060116.xhp\"\>Analysis Functions Part Two\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149566				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ISLEAPYEAR function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>leap year determination\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149566				0	en-ZA	ISLEAPYEAR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3150297				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Determines whether a year is a leap year.\</ahelp\> If yes, the function will return the value 1 (TRUE); if not, it will return 0 (FALSE).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148487				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3150205				0	en-ZA	ISLEAPYEAR("Date")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3159239				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Date\</emph\> specifies whether a given date falls within a leap year. The Date parameter must be a valid date according to the locale settings of %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149817				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3150786				0	en-ZA	=ISLEAPYEAR(A1) returns 1, if A1 contains 1968-02-29, the valid date 29th of February 1968 in your locale setting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E7				0	en-ZA	You may also use =ISLEAPYEAR("1968-02-29") or =ISLEAPYEAR("2/29/68").				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_idN107EA				0	en-ZA	Never use =ISLEAPYEAR(2/29/68), because this would first evaluate 2 divided by 29 divided by 68, and then calculate the ISLEAPYEAR function from this small number as a serial date number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154656				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>YEARS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of years between two dates\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154656				0	en-ZA	YEARS				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3150886				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DAI_FUNC_DIFFYEARS\"\>Calculates the difference in years between two dates.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154370				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3146114				0	en-ZA	YEARS(StartDate; EndDate; Type)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3145387				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>StartDate\</emph\> is the first date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3156290				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>EndDate\</emph\> is the second date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3152893				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> calculates the type of difference. Possible values are 0 (interval) and 1 (in calendar years).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152898				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>MONTHS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of months between two dates\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152898				0	en-ZA	MONTHS				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3153066				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DAI_FUNC_DIFFMONTHS\"\>Calculates the difference in months between two dates.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151240				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3146869				0	en-ZA	MONTHS(StartDate; EndDate; Type)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3145075				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>StartDate\</emph\> is the first date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3157981				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>EndDate\</emph\> is the second date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3150111				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> calculates the type of difference. Possible values include 0 (interval) and 1 (in calendar months).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159094				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ROT13 function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>encrypting text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159094				0	en-ZA	ROT13				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3146781				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DAI_FUNC_ROT13\"\>Encrypts a character string by moving the characters 13 positions in the alphabet.\</ahelp\> After the letter Z, the alphabet begins again (Rotation). By applying the encryption function again to the resulting code, you can decrypt the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150893				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3159205				0	en-ZA	ROT13(Text)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3153249				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Text\</emph\> is the character string to be encrypted. ROT13(ROT13(Text)) decrypts the code.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151300				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>DAYSINYEAR function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of days; in a specific year\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151300				0	en-ZA	DAYSINYEAR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3143220				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DAI_FUNC_DAYSINYEAR\"\>Calculates the number of days of the year in which the date entered occurs.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145358				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3154651				0	en-ZA	DAYSINYEAR(Date)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3153803				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Date\</emph\> is any date in the respective year. The Date parameter must be a valid date according to the locale settings of %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153487				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3153811				0	en-ZA	=DAYSINYEAR(A1) returns 366 days if A1 contains 1968-02-29, a valid date for the year 1968.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154737				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>DAYSINMONTH function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of days;in a specific month of a year\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154737				0	en-ZA	DAYSINMONTH				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3149316				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DAI_FUNC_DAYSINMONTH\"\>Calculates the number of days of the month in which the date entered occurs.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145114				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3150955				0	en-ZA	DAYSINMONTH(Date)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3147501				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Date\</emph\> is any date in the respective month of the desired year. The Date parameter must be a valid date according to the locale settings of %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149871				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3155742				0	en-ZA	=DAYSINMONTH(A1) returns 29 days if A1 contains 1968-02-17, a valid date for February 1968.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149048				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>WEEKS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of weeks;between two dates\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149048				0	en-ZA	WEEKS				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3153340				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DAI_FUNC_DIFFWEEKS\"\>Calculates the difference in weeks between two dates.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150393				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3147402				0	en-ZA	WEEKS(StartDate; EndDate; Type)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3151387				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>StartDate\</emph\> is the first date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3146324				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>EndDate\</emph\> is the second date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3166467				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> calculates the type of difference. The possible values are 0 (interval) and 1 (in numbers of weeks).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145237				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>WEEKSINYEAR function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of weeks;in a specific year\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145237				0	en-ZA	WEEKSINYEAR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3147410				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DAI_FUNC_WEEKSINYEAR\"\>Calculates the number of weeks of the year in which the date entered occurs.\</ahelp\> The number of weeks is defined as follows: a week that spans two years is added to the year in which most days of that week occur.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149719				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3145638				0	en-ZA	WEEKSINYEAR(Date)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3149946				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Date\</emph\> is any date in the respective year. The Date parameter must be a valid date according to the locale settings of %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150037				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3147614				0	en-ZA	WEEKSINYEAR(A1) returns 53 if A1 contains 1970-02-17, a valid date for the year 1970.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157901				0	en-ZA	Add-ins through %PRODUCTNAME API				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3149351				0	en-ZA	Add-ins can also be implemented through the %PRODUCTNAME \<link href=\"http://api.openoffice.org/\"\>API\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Fill Series				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148664				0	en-ZA	Fill Series				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"reihenfuellentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FillSeries\"\>Automatically generate series with the options in this dialogue. Determine direction, increment, time unit and series type.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3146976				0	en-ZA	Before filling a series, first select the cell range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3145748				0	en-ZA	To automatically continue a series using the assumed completion rules, choose the \<emph\>AutoFill\</emph\> option after opening the \<emph\>Fill Series\</emph\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147435				0	en-ZA	Direction				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	en-ZA	Determines the direction of series creation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145253				0	en-ZA	Down				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155418				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_BOTTOM\"\>Creates a downward series in the selected cell range for the column using the defined increment to the end value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155738				0	en-ZA	Right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149402				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_RIGHT\"\>Creates a series running from left to right within the selected cell range using the defined increment to the end value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146972				0	en-ZA	Up				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_TOP\"\>Creates an upward series in the cell range of the column using the defined increment to the end value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153764				0	en-ZA	Left				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_LEFT\"\>Creates a series running from right to left in the selected cell range using the defined increment to the end value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147344				0	en-ZA	Series Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149257	15			0	en-ZA	Defines the series type. Choose between \<emph\>Linear, Growth, Date \</emph\>and \<emph\>AutoFill\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148488				0	en-ZA	Linear				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3159238				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_ARITHMETIC\"\>Creates a linear number series using the defined increment and end value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149210				0	en-ZA	Growth				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150364				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_GEOMETRIC\"\>Creates a growth series using the defined increment and end value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149528				0	en-ZA	Date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150887				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_DATE\"\>Creates a date series using the defined increment and end date.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150202				0	en-ZA	AutoFill				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156288				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_AUTOFILL\"\>Forms a series directly in the sheet.\</ahelp\> The AutoFill function takes account of customised lists. For example, by entering \<emph\>January\</emph\> in the first cell, the series is completed using the list defined under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155811				0	en-ZA	AutoFill tries to complete a value series by using a defined pattern. The series 1,3,5 is automatically completed with 7,9,11,13, and so on. Date and time series are completed accordingly; for example, after 01.01.99 and 15.01.99, an interval of 14 days is used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148700				0	en-ZA	Unit of Time				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153308				0	en-ZA	In this area you can specify the desired unit of time. This area is only active if the \<emph\>Date\</emph\> option has been chosen in the \<emph\>Series type\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148868				0	en-ZA	Day				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3148605				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_DAY\"\>Use the \<emph\>Date\</emph\> series type and this option to create a series using seven days.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144771				0	en-ZA	Weekday				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150108				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_DAY_OF_WEEK\"\>Use the \<emph\>Date\</emph\> series type and this option to create a series of five day sets.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154957				0	en-ZA	Month				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_MONTH\"\>Use the \<emph\>Date\</emph\> series type and this option to form a series from the names or abbreviations of the months.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152870				0	en-ZA	Year				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3151300				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_YEAR\"\>Use the \<emph\>Date\</emph\> series type and this option to create a series of years.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154762				0	en-ZA	Start Value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149381				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:ED_START_VALUES\"\>Determines the start value for the series.\</ahelp\> Use numbers, dates or times.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153013				0	en-ZA	End Value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153487				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:ED_END_VALUES\"\>Determines the end value for the series.\</ahelp\> Use numbers, dates or times.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149312				0	en-ZA	Increment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154739				0	en-ZA	The term "increment" denotes the amount by which a given value increases.\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:ED_INCREMENT\"\> Determines the value by which the series of the selected type increases by each step.\</ahelp\> Entries can only be made if the linear, growth or date series types have been selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060199.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Operators in $[officename] Calc				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060199.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156445				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>formulae; operators\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>operators; formula functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>division sign, see also operators\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multiplication sign, see also operators\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>minus sign, see also operators\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>plus sign, see also operators\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text operators\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comparisons;operators in Calc\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arithmetical operators\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reference operators\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060199.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156445				0	en-ZA	Operators in $[officename] Calc				2002-02-02 02:02:02
