helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	SECOND 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159390				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>SECOND function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159390				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"second\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_second.xhp\"\>SECOND\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3148974				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SEKUNDE\"\>Returns the second for the given time value.\</ahelp\> The second is given as an integer between 0 and 59.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154362				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3148407				0	en-ZA	SECOND(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3155904				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number\</emph\>, as a time value, is a decimal, for which the second is to be returned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149992				0	en-ZA	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3153350				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SECOND(NOW())\</item\> returns the current second				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3150831				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SECOND(C4)\</item\> returns 17 if contents of C4 = \<item type=\"input\"\>12:20:17\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Subtotals				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153822				0	en-ZA	Subtotals				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"teilergebnisse\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DataSubTotals\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Calculates subtotals for the columns that you select.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> $[officename] uses the SUM function to automatically calculate the subtotal and grand total values in a labelled range. You can also use other functions to perform the calculation. $[officename] automatically recognises a defined database area when you place the cursor in it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	en-ZA	For example, you can generate a sales summary for a certain postal code based on data from a client database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163708				0	en-ZA	Delete				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154125				0	en-ZA	Deletes the subtotal rows in the selected area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Mathematical Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147124				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>mathematical functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Function Wizard; mathematical\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>functions; mathematical functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>trigonometric functions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147124				0	en-ZA	Mathematical Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154943				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"mathematiktext\"\>This category contains the \<emph\>Mathematical\</emph\> functions for Calc.\</variable\> To open the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>, choose \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Function\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Function\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146944				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ABS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>absolute values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>values;absolute\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146944				0	en-ZA	ABS				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154546				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ABS\"\>Returns the absolute value of a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154843				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3147475				0	en-ZA	ABS(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148438				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number whose absolute value is to be calculated. The absolute value of a number is its value without the +/- sign.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155823				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152787				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ABS(-56)\</item\> returns 56.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148752				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ABS(12)\</item\> returns 12.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id320139				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ABS(0)\</item\> returns 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150896				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>COUNTBLANK function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>counting;empty cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>empty cells;counting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150896				0	en-ZA	COUNTBLANK				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155260				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ANZAHLLEEREZELLEN\"\>Returns the number of empty cells.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145144				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153931				0	en-ZA	COUNTBLANK(Range)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3149512				0	en-ZA	 Returns the number of empty cells in the cell range \<emph\>Range\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146139				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148586				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTBLANK(A1:B2)\</item\> returns 4 if cells A1, A2, B1, and B2 are all empty.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153114				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ACOS function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153114				0	en-ZA	ACOS				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145163				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARCCOS\"\>Returns the inverse trigonometric cosine of a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153565				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150020				0	en-ZA	ACOS(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159134				0	en-ZA	 This function returns the inverse trigonometric cosine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the angle (in radians) whose cosine is Number. The angle returned is between 0 and PI.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id679647				0	en-ZA	To return the angle in degrees, use the DEGREES function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149882				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150128				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ACOS(-1)\</item\> returns 3.14159265358979 (PI radians)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8792382				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DEGREES(ACOS(0.5))\</item\> returns 60. The cosine of 60 degrees is 0.5.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145355				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ACOSH function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145355				0	en-ZA	ACOSH				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157993				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARCOSHYP\"\>Returns the inverse hyperbolic cosine of a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145295				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151017				0	en-ZA	ACOSH(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3149000	64			0	en-ZA	 This function returns the inverse hyperbolic cosine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the number whose hyperbolic cosine is Number. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6393932				0	en-ZA	 Number must be greater than or equal to 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150566				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145629				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ACOSH(1)\</item\> returns 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id951567				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ACOSH(COSH(4))\</item\> returns 4.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149027				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ACOT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149027				0	en-ZA	ACOT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155818				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARCCOT\"\>Returns the inverse cotangent (the arccotangent) of the given number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153225				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158419				0	en-ZA	ACOT(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154948				0	en-ZA	 This function returns the inverse trigonometric cotangent of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the angle (in radians) whose cotangent is Number. The angle returned is between 0 and PI.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5834528				0	en-ZA	To return the angle in degrees, use the DEGREES function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147538				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155375				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ACOT(1)\</item\> returns 0.785398163397448 (PI/4 radians).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8589434				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DEGREES(ACOT(1))\</item\> returns 45. The tangent of 45 degrees is 1. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148426				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ACOTH function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148426				0	en-ZA	ACOTH				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3147478				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARCOTHYP\"\>Returns the inverse hyperbolic cotangent of the given number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152585				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3147172				0	en-ZA	ACOTH(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146155				0	en-ZA	 This function returns the inverse hyperbolic cotangent of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the number whose hyperbolic cotangent is Number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5818659				0	en-ZA	An error results if Number is between -1 and 1 inclusive.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3083452				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150608				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ACOTH(1.1)\</item\> returns inverse hyperbolic cotangent of 1.1, approximately 1.52226.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145084				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ASIN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145084				0	en-ZA	ASIN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3156296				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARCSIN\"\>Returns the inverse trigonometric sine of a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149716				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3156305				0	en-ZA	ASIN(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150964				0	en-ZA	 This function returns the inverse trigonometric sine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the angle (in radians) whose sine is Number. The angle returned is between -PI/2 and +PI/2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id203863				0	en-ZA	To return the angle in degrees, use the DEGREES function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149448				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3156100				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ASIN(0)\</item\> returns 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6853846				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ASIN(1)\</item\> returns 1.5707963267949 (PI/2 radians). 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8772240				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DEGREES(ASIN(0.5))\</item\> returns 30. The sine of 30 degrees is 0.5.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151266				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ASINH function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151266				0	en-ZA	ASINH				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3147077				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARSINHYP\"\>Returns the inverse hyperbolic sine of a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150763				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150882				0	en-ZA	ASINH(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3147621	104			0	en-ZA	 This function returns the inverse hyperbolic sine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the number whose hyperbolic sine is Number. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153212				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3156120				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ASINH(-90)\</item\> returns approximately -5.1929877.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id4808496				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ASINH(SINH(4))\</item\> returns 4.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155996				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ATAN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155996				0	en-ZA	ATAN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3149985				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARCTAN\"\>Returns the inverse trigonometric tangent of a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151294				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150261				0	en-ZA	ATAN(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3147267				0	en-ZA	 This function returns the inverse trigonometric tangent of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the angle (in radians) whose tangent is Number. The angle returned is between -PI/2 and PI/2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6293527				0	en-ZA	To return the angle in degrees, use the DEGREES function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154054				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143229				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ATAN(1)\</item\> returns 0.785398163397448 (PI/4 radians).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8746299				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DEGREES(ATAN(1))\</item\> returns 45. The tangent of 45 degrees is 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153983				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ATAN2 function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153983				0	en-ZA	ATAN2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154297				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARCTAN2\"\>Returns the inverse trigonometric tangent of the specified x and y coordinates.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149758				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3156013				0	en-ZA	ATAN2(NumberX; NumberY)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151168				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>NumberX\</emph\> is the value of the x coordinate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152798				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>NumberY\</emph\> is the value of the y coordinate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5036164				0	en-ZA	ATAN2 returns the inverse trigonometric tangent, that is, the angle (in radians) between the x-axis and a line from point NumberX, NumberY to the origin. The angle returned is between -PI and PI.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3001800				0	en-ZA	To return the angle in degrees, use the DEGREES function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145663				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154692				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ATAN2(20;20)\</item\> returns 0.785398163397448 (PI/4 radians).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1477095				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DEGREES(ATAN2(12.3;12.3))\</item\> returns 45. The tangent of 45 degrees is 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155398				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ATANH function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
