helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3149484				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the angle in radians to be converted to degrees.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3669545				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3459578				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DEGREES(PI())\</item\> returns 180 degrees.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148698				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>EXP function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148698				0	en-ZA	EXP				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150592				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_EXP\"\>Returns e raised to the power of a number.\</ahelp\> The constant e has a value of approximately 2.71828182845904.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150351				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146786				0	en-ZA	EXP(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155608				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the power to which e is to be raised.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154418				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3156340				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=EXP(1)\</item\> returns 2.71828182845904, the mathematical constant e to Calc's accuracy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145781				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>FACT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>factorials;numbers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
