helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03070000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Column & Row Headers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03070000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156024				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; displaying headers of columns/rows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>displaying; headers of columns/rows\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156024				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03070000.xhp\" name=\"Column & Row Headers\"\>Column & Row Headers\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147230				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ViewRowColumnHeaders\"\>Shows column headers and row headers.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	en-ZA	To hide the column and row headers unmark this menu entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	en-ZA	You can also set the view of the column and row headers in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_hour.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	HOUR 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_hour.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154725				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>HOUR function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_hour.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154725				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"hour\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_hour.xhp\"\>HOUR\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_hour.xhp	0	help	par_id3149747				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_STUNDE\"\>Returns the hour for a given time value.\</ahelp\> The hour is returned as an integer between 0 and 23.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_hour.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149338				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_hour.xhp	0	help	par_id3150637				0	en-ZA	HOUR(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_hour.xhp	0	help	par_id3147547				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number\</emph\>, as a time value, is a decimal, for which the hour is to be returned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_hour.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153264				0	en-ZA	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_hour.xhp	0	help	par_id3159215				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=HOUR(NOW())\</item\> returns the current hour				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_hour.xhp	0	help	par_id3145152				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=HOUR(C4)\</item\> returns 17 if the contents of C4 = \<item type=\"input\"\>17:20:00\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_hour.xhp	0	help	par_id3154188				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060102.xhp\" name=\"YEAR\"\>YEAR\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060102.xhp\" name=\"NOW\"\>NOW\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060102.xhp\" name=\"MINUTE\"\>MINUTE\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060102.xhp\" name=\"MONTH\"\>MONTH\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060102.xhp\" name=\"DAY\"\>DAY\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060102.xhp\" name=\"WEEKDAY\"\>WEEKDAY\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Conditional Formatting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155132				0	en-ZA	Conditional Formatting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"bedingtetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConditionalFormatDialog\"\>Choose \<emph\>Conditional Formatting\</emph\> to define format styles depending on certain conditions.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> If a style was already assigned to a cell, it remains unchanged. The style entered here is then evaluated. You can enter three conditions that query the contents of cell values or formulae. The conditions are evaluated from 1 to 3. If the condition 1 matches the condition, the defined style will be used. Otherwise, condition 2 is evaluated, and its defined style used. If this style does not match, condition 3 is evaluated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id2414014				0	en-ZA	To apply conditional formatting, AutoCalculate must be enabled. Choose Tools - Cell Contents - AutoCalculate (you see a check mark next to the command when AutoCalculate is enabled).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153189				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>conditional formatting; conditions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153189				0	en-ZA	Condition 1/2/3				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149413				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_CONDFORMAT:CBX_COND3\"\>Mark the boxes corresponding to each condition and enter the corresponding condition.\</ahelp\> To close the dialogue, click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147394				0	en-ZA	Cell Value / Formula				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_CONDFORMAT:LB_COND3_1\"\>Specifies if conditional formatting is dependent on a cell value or a formula.\</ahelp\> If you select a formula as a reference, the \<emph\>Cell Value Condition\</emph\> box is displayed to the right of the \<emph\>Cell value/Formula\</emph\> field. If the condition is "Formula is", enter a cell reference. If the cell reference is a value other than zero, the condition matches.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153709				0	en-ZA	Cell Value Condition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153764				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_CONDFORMAT:LB_COND3_2\"\>Choose a condition for the format to be applied to the selected cells.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156384				0	en-ZA	Cell Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145228				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_CONDFORMAT:LB_COND3_TEMPLATE\"\>Choose the style to be applied if the specified condition matches.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0509200913175331				0	en-ZA	New Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200913175368				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you haven't already defined a style to be used, you can click New Style to open the Organizer tab page of the Cell Style dialogue. Define a new style there and click OK.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146316				0	en-ZA	Parameter field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_CONDFORMAT:EDT_COND3_2\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a reference, value or formula.\</ahelp\> Enter a reference, value or formula in the parameter field, or in both parameter fields if you have selected a condition that requires two parameters. You can also enter formulae containing relative references.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145257				0	en-ZA	Once the parameters have been defined, the condition is complete. It may appear as:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150784				0	en-ZA	Cell value is equal 0: Cell style Null value (You must have already defined a cell style with this name before assigning it to a condition).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150365				0	en-ZA	Cell value is between $B$20 and $B$21: Cell style Result (The corresponding value limits must already exist in cells B20 and B21).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152992				0	en-ZA	Formula is SUM($A$1:$A$5)=10: Cell style Result (The selected cells are formatted with the Result style if the sum of the contents in cells A1 to A5 is equal to 10).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E1				0	en-ZA	            \<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellstyle_conditional.xhp#cellstyle_conditional\"/\>         				2002-02-02 02:02:02
