helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02200000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146794				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02200000.xhp\" name=\"Sheet\"\>Sheet\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02200000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Edit commands for entire sheets.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02200000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02180000.xhp\" name=\"Move/Copy\"\>Move/Copy\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02200000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153968				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02210000.xhp\" name=\"Select\"\>Select\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02200000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163708				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02170000.xhp\" name=\"Delete\"\>Delete\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	DAYS 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151328				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>DAYS function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151328				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"days\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_days.xhp\"\>DAYS\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	par_id3155139				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TAGE\"\>Calculates the difference between two date values.\</ahelp\> The result returns the number of days between the two days.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155184				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	en-ZA	DAYS(Date2; Date1)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	par_id3151376				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Date1\</emph\> is the start date, \<emph\>Date2\</emph\> is the end date. If \<emph\>Date2\</emph\> is an earlier date than \<emph\>Date1\</emph\> the result is a negative number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151001				0	en-ZA	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	par_id3159101				0	en-ZA	=DAYS("2010-01-01"; NOW()) returns the number of days from today until January 1, 2010.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	par_id3163720				0	en-ZA	=DAYS("1990-10-10";"1980-10-10") returns 3652 days.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Edit Print Ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153088				0	en-ZA	Edit Print Ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3159488				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"druckbereichetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:EditPrintArea\"\>Opens a dialogue where you can specify the print range.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> You can also set the rows or columns which are to be repeated in every page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_idN105AE				0	en-ZA	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/guide/printranges.xhp#printranges\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156281				0	en-ZA	Print range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_AREAS:ED_PRINTAREA\"\>Allows you to modify a defined print range.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145174				0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>-none-\</emph\> to remove a print range definition for the current spreadsheet. Select \<emph\>-entire sheet-\</emph\> to set the current sheet as a print range. Select \<emph\>-selection-\</emph\> to define the selected area of a spreadsheet as the print range. By selecting \<emph\>-user-defined-\</emph\>, you can define a print range that you have already defined using the \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Define\</emph\> command. If you have given a name to a range using the \<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\> command, this name will be displayed and can be selected from the list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	en-ZA	In the right-hand text box, you can enter a print range by reference or by name. If the cursor is in the \<emph\>Print range\</emph\> text box, you can also select the print range in the spreadsheet with your mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149260				0	en-ZA	Rows to repeat				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_AREAS:ED_REPEATROW\"\>Choose one or more rows to print on every page. In the right text box enter the row reference, for example, "1" or "$1" or "$2:$3".\</ahelp\> The list box displays \<emph\>-user defined-\</emph\>. You can also select \<emph\>-none-\</emph\> to remove a defined repeating row.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155418				0	en-ZA	You can also define repeating rows by dragging the mouse in the spreadsheet, if the cursor is in the \<emph\>Rows to repeat\</emph\> text field in the dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149581				0	en-ZA	Columns to repeat				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_AREAS:ED_REPEATCOL\"\>Choose one or more columns to print on every page. In the right text box enter the column reference, for example, "A" or "AB" or "$C:$E".\</ahelp\> The list box then displays \<emph\>-user defined-\</emph\>. You can also select \<emph\>-none-\</emph\> to remove a defined repeating column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	en-ZA	You can also define repeating columns by dragging the mouse in the spreadsheet, if the cursor is in the \<emph\>Columns to repeat\</emph\> text field in the dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Page Break Preview				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151384				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"Page Break Preview\"\>Page Break Preview\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150792				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:PagebreakMode\"\>Display the page breaks and print ranges in the sheet. Choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\> to switch this mode off.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153877				0	en-ZA	The context menu of the page break preview contains functions for editing page breaks, including the following options:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154731				0	en-ZA	Delete All Manual Breaks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DeleteAllBreaks\"\>Deletes all manual breaks in the current sheet.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155067				0	en-ZA	Add Print Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764				0	en-ZA	Adds the selected cells to print ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050000.xhp	0	help	bm_id1245460				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>CTL;right-to-left sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets;right-to-left\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>right-to-left text;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155923				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05050000.xhp\" name=\"Sheet\"\>Sheet\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Sets the sheet name and hides or shows selected sheets.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156280				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05050100.xhp\" name=\"Rename\"\>Rename\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145787				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05050300.xhp\" name=\"Show\"\>Show\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150542				0	en-ZA	If a sheet has been hidden, the Show Sheet dialogue opens, which allows you to select a sheet to be shown again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10656				0	en-ZA	Right-To-Left				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065A				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SheetRightToLeft\"\>Changes the orientation of the current sheet to Right-To-Left if \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01150300.xhp\"\>CTL\</link\> support is enabled.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	WORKDAY				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149012				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>WORKDAY function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149012				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"workday\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_workday.xhp\"\>WORKDAY\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3149893				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_WORKDAY\"\> The result is a date number that can be formatted as a date. You then see the date of a day that is a certain number of \<emph\>workdays\</emph\> away from the \<emph\>start date\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146944				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154844				0	en-ZA	WORKDAY(StartDate; Days; Holidays)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3147469				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>StartDate\</emph\> is the date from when the calculation is carried out. If the start date is a workday, the day is included in the calculation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3153038				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Days\</emph\> is the number of workdays. Positive value for a result after the start date, negative value for a result before the start date.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150693				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Holidays\</emph\> is a list of optional holidays. These are non-working days. Enter a cell range in which the holidays are listed individually.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150141				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3152782				0	en-ZA	What date came 17 workdays after 1 December 2001? Enter the start date "2001-12-01" in C3 and the number of workdays in D3. Cells F3 to J3 contain the following Christmas and New Year holidays: "2001-12-24", "2001-12-25", "2001-12-26", "2001-12-31", "2002-01-01".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3146142				0	en-ZA	=WORKDAY(C3;D3;F3:J3) returns 2001-12-28. Format the serial date number as a date, for example in the format YYYY-MM-DD.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	YEAR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153982				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>YEAR function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153982				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"year\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_year.xhp\"\>YEAR\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	par_id3147496				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_JAHR\"\>Returns the year as a number according to the internal calculation rules.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146090				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	par_id3154304				0	en-ZA	YEAR(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	par_id3156013				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> shows the internal date value for which the year is to be returned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152797				0	en-ZA	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	par_id3145668				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=YEAR(1)\</item\> returns 1899				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	par_id3151168				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=YEAR(2)\</item\> returns 1900				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	par_id3150115				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=YEAR(33333.33)\</item\> returns 1991				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Move or Copy a Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153360				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; moving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; copying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153360				0	en-ZA	Move or Copy a Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154686				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"tabelleverschiebenkopierentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Move\"\>Moves or copies a sheet to a new location in the document or to a different document.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	par_id2282479				0	en-ZA	When you copy and paste cells containing \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060102.xhp\"\>date values\</link\> between different spreadsheets, both spreadsheet documents must be set to the same date base. If date bases differ, the displayed date values will change!				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163710				0	en-ZA	To Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_MOVETAB:LB_DEST\"\>Indicates where the current sheet is to be moved or copied to.\</ahelp\> Select \<emph\>new document\</emph\> if you want to create a new location for the sheet to be moved or copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154012				0	en-ZA	Insert Before				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_MOVETAB:LB_INSERT\"\>The current sheet is moved or copied in front of the selected sheet.\</ahelp\> The \<emph\>move to end position\</emph\> option places the current sheet at the end.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726				0	en-ZA	Copy				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_MOVETAB:BTN_COPY\"\>Specifies that the sheet is to be copied. If the option is unmarked, the sheet is moved.\</ahelp\> Moving sheets is the default.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Criteria				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	bm_id1464278				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>selection lists;validity\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153032				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12120100.xhp\" name=\"Criteria\"\>Criteria\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156327				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:TABPAGE:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES\"\>Specify the validation rules for the selected cell(s).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155923				0	en-ZA	For example, you can define criteria such as: "Numbers between 1 and 10" or "Texts that are no more than 20 characters".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896				0	en-ZA	Allow				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES:LB_ALLOW\"\>Click a validation option for the selected cell(s).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	en-ZA	The following conditions are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150447				0	en-ZA	Condition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	en-ZA	Effect				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153092				0	en-ZA	All values				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411				0	en-ZA	No limitation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	en-ZA	Whole number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	en-ZA	Only whole numbers corresponding to the condition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145802				0	en-ZA	Decimal				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153160				0	en-ZA	All numbers corresponding to the condition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	en-ZA	Date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150718				0	en-ZA	All numbers corresponding to the condition. The entered values are formatted accordingly the next time the dialogue is called up.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	en-ZA	Time				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155066				0	en-ZA	All numbers corresponding to the condition. The entered values are formatted accordingly the next time the dialogue is called up.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A0				0	en-ZA	Cell range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A5				0	en-ZA	Allow only values that are given in a cell range. The cell range can be specified explicitly, or as a named database range, or as a named range. The range may consist of one column or one row of cells. If you specify a range of columns and rows, only the first column is used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	en-ZA	List				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B0				0	en-ZA	Allow only values or strings specified in a list. Strings and values can be mixed. Numbers evaluate to their value, so if you enter the number 1 in the list, the entry 100% is also valid.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154756				0	en-ZA	Text length				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147339				0	en-ZA	Entries whose length corresponds to the condition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154704				0	en-ZA	Allow blank cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153967				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:TRISTATEBOX:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES:TSB_ALLOW_BLANKS\"\>In conjunction with \<emph\>Tools - Detective - Mark invalid Data\</emph\>, this defines that blank cells are shown as invalid data (disabled) or not (enabled).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10709				0	en-ZA	Show selection list				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070D				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:CheckBox:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES:CB_SHOWLIST\"\>Shows a list of all valid strings or values to select from. The list can also be opened by selecting the cell and pressing Ctrl+D (Mac: Command+D).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10724				0	en-ZA	Sort entries ascending				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10728				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:CheckBox:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES:CB_SORTLIST\"\>Sorts the selection list in ascending order and filters duplicates from the list. If not checked, the order from the data source is taken.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073F				0	en-ZA	Source				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10743				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:Edit:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES:EDT_MIN\"\>Enter the cell range that contains the valid values or text.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075A				0	en-ZA	Entries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075E				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:MultiLineEdit:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES:EDT_LIST\"\>Enter the entries that will be valid values or text strings.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163807				0	en-ZA	Data				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3144502	10			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES:LB_VALUE\"\>Select the comparative operator that you want to use.\</ahelp\> The available operators depend on what you selected in the \<emph\>Allow \</emph\>box. If you select "between" or "not between", the \<emph\>Minimum\</emph\> and \<emph\>Maximum\</emph\> input boxes appear. Otherwise, only the \<emph\>Minimum\</emph\>, the \<emph\>Maximum, or the Value\</emph\> input boxes appear.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153782				0	en-ZA	Value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153266	12			0	en-ZA	Enter the value for the data validation option that you selected in the \<emph\>Allow \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149814				0	en-ZA	Minimum				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153199	14			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES:EDT_MIN\"\>Enter the minimum value for the data validation option that you selected in the \<emph\>Allow \</emph\>box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149035				0	en-ZA	Maximum				2002-02-02 02:02:02
