helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3149202	111			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Data1\</emph\> is the dependent array or range of data for the first record.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3145666	112			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Data2\</emph\> is the dependent array or range of data for the second record.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153903	113			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Mode\</emph\> = 1 calculates the one-tailed test, \<emph\>Mode\</emph\> = 2 the two- tailed test.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3155327	114			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Type\</emph\> is the kind of t-test to perform. Type 1 means paired. Type 2 means two samples, equal variance (homoscedastic). Type 3 means two samples, unequal variance (heteroscedastic).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159342				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
