helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145598				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3149298				0	en-ZA	PERMUTATIONA(Count1; Count2)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3156139	157			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Count1\</emph\> is the total number of objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3149519	158			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Count2\</emph\> is the number of objects in each permutation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151382				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153949				0	en-ZA	How often can 2 objects be selected from a total of 11 objects?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233	161			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=PERMUTATIONA(11;2)\</item\> returns 121.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3150622	162			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=PERMUTATIONA(6;3)\</item\> returns 216. There are 216 different possibilities to put a sequence of 3 playing cards together out of six playing cards if every card is returned before the next one is drawn.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152952				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>PROB function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152952				0	en-ZA	PROB				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154110				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WAHRSCHBEREICH\"\>Returns the probability that values in a range are between two limits.\</ahelp\> If there is no \<item type=\"literal\"\>End\</item\> value, this function calculates the probability based on the principle that the Data values are equal to the value of \<item type=\"literal\"\>Start\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146810				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3147330				0	en-ZA	PROB(Data; Probability; Start; End)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154573	168			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Data\</emph\> is the array or range of data in the sample.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3156334	169			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Probability\</emph\> is the array or range of the corresponding probabilities.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3151107	170			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Start\</emph\> is the start value of the interval whose probabilities are to be summed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153694	171			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>End\</emph\> (optional) is the end value of the interval whose probabilities are to be summed. If this parameter is missing, the probability for the \<emph\>Start \</emph\>value is calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147574				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153666	173			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=PROB(A1:A50;B1:B50;50;60)\</item\> returns the probability with which a value within the range of A1:A50 is also within the limits between 50 and 60. Every value within the range of A1:A50 has a probability within the range of B1:B50.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150941				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>WEIBULL function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150941				0	en-ZA	WEIBULL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154916				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WEIBULL\"\>Returns the values of the Weibull distribution.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372767				0	en-ZA	The Weibull distribution is a continuous probability distribution, with parameters Alpha > 0 (shape) and Beta > 0 (scale). 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372777				0	en-ZA	If C is 0, WEIBULL calculates the probability density function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372743				0	en-ZA	If C is 1, WEIBULL calculates the cumulative distribution function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159393				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154478				0	en-ZA	WEIBULL(Number; Alpha; Beta; C)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3151317	179			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value at which to calculate the Weibull distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3158436	180			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Alpha \</emph\>is the shape parameter of the Weibull distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154668	181			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Beta\</emph\> is the scale parameter of the Weibull distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154825	182			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>C\</emph\> indicates the type of function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153794				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3146077	184			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=WEIBULL(2;1;1;1)\</item\> returns 0.86.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372899				0	en-ZA	See also the \<link href=\"http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Calc:_WEIBULL_function\"\>Wiki page\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030600.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Trace Error				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030600.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153561				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>cells; tracing errors\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tracing errors\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error tracing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153561				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030600.xhp\" name=\"Trace Error\"\>Trace Error\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030600.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowErrors\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Draws tracer arrows to all precedent cells which cause an error value in a selected cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Hide AutoFilter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040500.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150276				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; hiding AutoFilter\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150276				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12040500.xhp\" name=\"Hide AutoFilter\"\>Hide AutoFilter\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156326				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DataFilterHideAutoFilter\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Hides the AutoFilter buttons in the selected cell range.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Sort				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150275				0	en-ZA	Sort				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"sorttext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DataSort\"\>Sorts the selected rows according to the conditions that you specify.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> $[officename] automatically recognises and selects database ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428				0	en-ZA	You cannot sort data if the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02230000.xhp\" name=\"Record changes\"\>Record changes\</link\> options is enabled.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Create Scenario				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156023				0	en-ZA	Create Scenario				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"szenariotext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ScenarioManager\"\>Defines a scenario for the selected sheet area.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10637				0	en-ZA	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/guide/scenario.xhp#scenario\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156280				0	en-ZA	Name of scenario				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041	13			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_SCENWIN_TOP\"\>Defines the name for the scenario. Use a clear and unique name so you can easily identify the scenario.\</ahelp\> You can also modify a scenario name in the Navigator through the \<emph\>Properties \</emph\>context menu command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153954				0	en-ZA	Comment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411	15			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_SCENWIN_BOTTOM\"\>Specifies additional information about the scenario. This information will be displayed in the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\> when you click the \<emph\>Scenarios\</emph\> icon and select the desired scenario.\</ahelp\> You can also modify this information in the Navigator through the \<emph\>Properties \</emph\>context menu command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145273				0	en-ZA	Settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153364				0	en-ZA	This section is used to define some of the settings used in the scenario display.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145367				0	en-ZA	Display border				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_NEWSCENARIO:LB_COLOR\"\>Highlights the scenario in your table with a border. The colour for the border is specified in the field to the right of this option.\</ahelp\> The border will have a title bar displaying the name of the last scenario. The button on the right of the scenario border offers you an overview of all the scenarios in this area, if several have been defined. You can choose any of the scenarios from this list without restrictions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149582				0	en-ZA	Copy back				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154942				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_NEWSCENARIO:CB_TWOWAY\"\>Copies the values of cells that you change into the active scenario. If you do not select this option, the scenario is not changed when you change cell values. The behaviour of the \<emph\>Copy back\</emph\> setting depends on the cell protection, the sheet protection, and the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> settings.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149402				0	en-ZA	Copy entire sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969	23			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_NEWSCENARIO:CB_COPYALL\"\>Copies the entire sheet into an additional scenario sheet. \</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075A				0	en-ZA	Prevent changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075E				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:CheckBox:RID_SCDLG_NEWSCENARIO:CB_PROTECT\"\>Prevents changes to the active scenario. The behaviour of the \<emph\>Copy back\</emph\> setting depends on the cell protection, the sheet protection, and the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> settings.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10778				0	en-ZA	You can only change the scenario properties if the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> option is not selected and if the sheet is not protected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10780				0	en-ZA	You can only edit cell values if the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> option is selected, if the \<emph\>Copy back\</emph\> is option is not selected, and if the cells are not protected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078C				0	en-ZA	You can only change scenario cell values and write them back into the scenario if the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> option is not selected, if the \<emph\>Copy back\</emph\> option is selected, and if the cells are not protected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12070000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Consolidate				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148946				0	en-ZA	Consolidate				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"konsolidieren\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DataConsolidate\"\>Combines data from one or more independent cell ranges and calculates a new range using the function that you specify.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150010				0	en-ZA	Function				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_CONSOLIDATE:LB_FUNC\"\>Select the function that you want to use to consolidate the data.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147127				0	en-ZA	Consolidation ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151075				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:MULTILISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_CONSOLIDATE:LB_CONSAREAS\"\>Displays the cell ranges that you want to consolidate.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147397				0	en-ZA	Source data range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153836	13			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_CONSOLIDATE:ED_DATA_AREA\"\>Specifies the cell range that you want to consolidate with the cell ranges listed in the \<emph\>Consolidation ranges \</emph\>box. Select a cell range in a sheet, and then click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>. You can also select a the name of a predefined cell from the \<emph\>Source data range \</emph\>list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155768				0	en-ZA	Copy results to				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147341				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_CONSOLIDATE:ED_DEST_AREA\"\>Displays the first cell in the range where the consolidation results will be displayed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147345				0	en-ZA	Add				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335	18			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_CONSOLIDATE:BTN_ADD\"\>Adds the cell range specified in the \<emph\>Source data range\</emph\> box to the \<emph\>Consolidation ranges \</emph\>box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148630				0	en-ZA	More >>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159239				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:MOREBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_CONSOLIDATE:BTN_MORE\"\>Shows additional \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12070100.xhp\" name=\"options\"\>options\</link\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	AutoOutline				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150275				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080500.xhp\" name=\"AutoOutline\"\>AutoOutline\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080500.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:AutoOutline\"\>If the selected cell range contains formulae or references, $[officename] automatically outlines the selection.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	en-ZA	For example, consider the following table:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123				0	en-ZA	January				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	en-ZA	February				2002-02-02 02:02:02
