helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147363				0	en-ZA	The cells for the 1st and 2nd quarters each contain a sum formula for the three cells to their left. If you apply the \<emph\>AutoOutline\</emph\> command, the table is grouped into two quarters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080500.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918				0	en-ZA	To remove the outline, select the table, and then choose \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080600.xhp\" name=\"Data - Group and Outline - Remove\"\>Data - Group and Outline - Remove\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Remove				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153562				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080200.xhp\" name=\"Remove\"\>Remove\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DeletePrintArea\"\>Removes the defined print area.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Rename Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147336				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>worksheet names\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing; sheet names\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; renaming\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147336				0	en-ZA	Rename Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150792				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"umbenennentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:RenameTable\"\>This command opens a dialogue where you can assign a different name to the current sheet.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153968				0	en-ZA	Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_APPEND_NAME\"\>Enter a new name for the sheet here.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153092	5			0	en-ZA	You can also open the\<emph\> Rename Sheet \</emph\>dialogue through the context menu by positioning the mouse pointer over a sheet tab at the bottom of the window and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>clicking while pressing Control\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>clicking the right mouse button\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	en-ZA	Alternatively, click the sheet tab while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key. Now you can change the name directly. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/00/00000099.xhp#winmanager\"/\>\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Optimal Column Width				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155628				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; optimal column widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; optimal widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>optimal column widths\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155628				0	en-ZA	Optimal Column Width				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"optitext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SetOptimalColumnWidthDi\"\>Defines the optimal column width for selected columns.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> The optimal column width depends on the longest entry within a column. You can choose from the available \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000003.xhp#metrik\" name=\"measurement units\"\>measurement units\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150767				0	en-ZA	Add				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:METRICFIELD:RID_SCDLG_COL_OPT:ED_VALUE\"\>Defines additional spacing between the longest entry in a column and the vertical column borders.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145785				0	en-ZA	Default value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_COL_OPT:BTN_DEFVAL\"\>Defines the optimal column width in order to display the entire contents of the column.\</ahelp\> The additional spacing for the optimal column width is preset to 0.1 in.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Solver				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	bm_id7654652				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>goal seeking;solver\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>what if operations;solver\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>back-solving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>solver\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	hd_id9216284				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"solver\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/solver.xhp\"\>Solver\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id9210486				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the Solver dialogue. A solver allows to solve equations with multiple unknown variables by goal seeking methods.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id8538773				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter or click the cell reference of the target cell. This field takes the address of the cell whose value is to be optimised.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id7564012				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Try to solve the equation for a maximum value of the target cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id1186254				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Try to solve the equation for a minimum value of the target cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id7432477				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Try to solve the equation to approach a given value of the target cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id7141026				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the value or a cell reference.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id8531449				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the cell range that can be changed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id9183935				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a cell reference.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id946684				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select an operator from the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id9607226				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a value or a cell reference.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id1939451				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to shrink or restore the dialogue. You can click or select cells in the sheet. You can enter a cell reference manually in the input box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id9038972				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to remove the row from the list. Any rows from below this row move up.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id2423780				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Options dialogue.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to solve the equation with the current settings. The dialogue settings are retained until you close the current document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id5474410				0	en-ZA	To solve equations with the solver				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id2216559				0	en-ZA	The goal of the solver process is to find those variable values of an equation that result in an optimised value in the \<emph\>target cell\</emph\>, also named the "objective". You can choose whether the value in the target cell should be a maximum, a minimum, or approaching a given value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id7869502				0	en-ZA	The initial variable values are inserted in a rectangular cell range that you enter in the \<emph\>By changing cells\</emph\> box. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id9852900				0	en-ZA	You can define a series of limiting conditions that set constraints for some cells. For example, you can set the constraint that one of the variables or cells must not be bigger than another variable, or not bigger than a given value. You can also define the constraint that one or more variables must be integers (values without decimals), or binary values (where only 0 and 1 are allowed).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id5323953				0	en-ZA	The default solver engine supports only linear equations.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Column Break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151384				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;deleting column breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;manual column breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>column breaks;deleting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151384				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02190200.xhp\" name=\"Column Break\"\>Column Break\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DeleteColumnbreak\"\>Removes a manual column break to the left of the active cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145173				0	en-ZA	Position the cursor in the cell to the right of the column break indicated by a vertical line and choose \<emph\>Edit - Delete Manual Break - Column Break\</emph\>. The manual column break is removed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	WEEKDAY 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154925				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>WEEKDAY function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154925				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"weekday\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_weekday.xhp\"\>WEEKDAY\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154228				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WOCHENTAG\"\>Returns the day of the week for the given date value.\</ahelp\> The day is returned as an integer between 1 (Sunday) and 7 (Saturday) if no type or type=1 is specified. If type=2, numbering begins at Monday=1; and if type=3 numbering begins at Monday=0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147217				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3149033				0	en-ZA	WEEKDAY(Number; Type)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3149046				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number\</emph\>, as a date value, is a decimal for which the weekday is to be returned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154394				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> determines the type of calculation. For Type=1, the weekdays are counted starting from Sunday (this is the default even when the Type parameter is missing). For Type=2, the weekdays are counted starting from Monday=1. For Type=3, the weekdays are counted starting from Monday=0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3156188				0	en-ZA	These values apply only to the standard date format that you select under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Calculate\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153836				0	en-ZA	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150317				0	en-ZA	=WEEKDAY("2000-06-14") returns 4 (the Type parameter is missing, therefore the standard count is used. The standard count starts with Sunday as day number 1. June 14, 2000 was a Wednesday and therefore day number 4).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3153174				0	en-ZA	=WEEKDAY("1996-07-24";2) returns 3 (the Type parameter is 2, therefore Monday is day number 1. July 24, 1996 was a Wednesday and therefore day number 3).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3153525				0	en-ZA	=WEEKDAY("1996-07-24";1) returns 4 (the Type parameter is 1, therefore Sunday is day number 1. July 24, 1996 was a Wednesday and therefore day number 4).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150575				0	en-ZA	=WEEKDAY(NOW()) returns the number of the current day.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150588	171			0	en-ZA	To obtain a function indicating whether a day in A1 is a business day, use the IF and WEEKDAY functions as follows: \<br/\>IF(WEEKDAY(A1;2)<6;"Business day";"Weekend")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Validity				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156347				0	en-ZA	Validity				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"gueltigkeit\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Validation\"\>Defines what data is valid for a selected cell or cell range.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120000.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D1				0	en-ZA	You can also insert a list box from the Controls toolbar and link the list box to a cell. This way you can specify the valid values on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\"\>Data\</link\> page of the list box properties window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Sheet from file				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04050100.xhp\"\>Sheet from file\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D1				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"26275\"\>Inserts a sheet from a different spreadsheet file.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F7				0	en-ZA	Use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File - Open\</link\> dialogue to locate the spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10609				0	en-ZA	In the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04050000.xhp\"\>Insert Sheet\</link\> dialogue, select the sheet that you want to insert.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Down				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02140100.xhp\" name=\"Down\"\>Down\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153969				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FillDown\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Fills a selected range of at least two rows with the contents of the top cell of the range.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145787				0	en-ZA	If a selected range has only one column, the contents of the top cell are copied to all others. If several columns are selected, the contents of the corresponding top cell will be copied down.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04010100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Row Break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04010100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153821				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; inserting row breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>row breaks; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; manual row breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>manual row breaks\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153821				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04010100.xhp\" name=\"Row Break\"\>Row Break\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertRowBreak\"\>Inserts a row break (horizontal page break) above the selected cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	en-ZA	The manual row break is indicated by a dark blue horizontal line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
