helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156198				0	en-ZA	Fill Format Mode				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148870				0	en-ZA	How to apply a new style with the paint can:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145078				0	en-ZA	Select the desired style from the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159098				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Fill Format Mode\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148609				0	en-ZA	Click a cell to format it, or drag your mouse over a certain range to format the whole range. Repeat this action for other cells and ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149438				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Fill Format Mode\</emph\> again to exit this mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153975				0	en-ZA	New Style from Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149499				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_TEMPLDLG_NEWBYEXAMPLE\"\>Creates a new style based on the formatting of a selected object.\</ahelp\> Assign a name for the style in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05140100.xhp\" name=\"Create Style\"\>Create Style\</link\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150050				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3154649\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_stylenewbyexample.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154649\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146963				0	en-ZA	New Style from Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153813				0	en-ZA	Update Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154707				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_TEMPLDLG_UPDATEBYEXAMPLE\"\>Updates the Style selected in the Styles and Formatting window with the current formatting of the selected object.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3155754\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_styleupdatebyexample.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155754\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147501				0	en-ZA	Update Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05100000.xhp	0	help	par_idN109BE				0	en-ZA	Style List				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05100000.xhp	0	help	par_idN109C2				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_TEMPLATE_FMT\"\>Displays the list of the styles from the selected style category.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05100000.xhp	0	help	par_idN109D1				0	en-ZA	In the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#kontextmenue\" name=\"context menu\"\>context menu\</link\> you can choose commands to create a new style, delete a user-defined style, or change the selected style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149053				0	en-ZA	Style Groups				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147299				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_TEMPLATE_FILTER\"\>Lists the available style groups.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Formula Bar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147264				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>formula bar;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; formula bar\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147264				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03090000.xhp\" name=\"Formula Bar\"\>Formula Bar\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InputLineVisible\"\>Shows or hides the Formula Bar, which is used for entering and editing formulae.\</ahelp\> The Formula Bar is the most important tool when working with spreadsheets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154686				0	en-ZA	To hide the Formula Bar, unmark the menu item.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145787				0	en-ZA	If the Formula Bar is hidden, you can still edit cells by activating the edit mode with F2. After editing cells, accept the changes by pressing Enter, or discard entries by pressing Esc. Esc is also used to exit the edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Date & Time Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154536				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>date and time functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>functions; date & time\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Function Wizard; date & time\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154536				0	en-ZA	Date & Time Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153973	2			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"datumzeittext\"\>These spreadsheet functions are used for inserting and editing dates and times. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	par_idN10600				0	en-ZA	The functions whose names end with _ADD return the same results as the corresponding Microsoft Excel functions. Use the functions without _ADD to get results based on international standards. For example, the WEEKNUM function calculates the week number of a given date based on international standard ISO 8601, while WEEKNUM_ADD returns the same week number as Microsoft Excel.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150437				0	en-ZA	$[officename] internally handles a date/time value as a numerical value. If you assign the numbering format "Number" to a date or time value, it is converted to a number. For example, 01/01/2000 12:00 PM, converts to 36526.5. The value preceding the decimal point corresponds to the date; the value following the decimal point corresponds to the time. If you do not want to see this type of numerical date or time representation, change the number format (date or time) accordingly. To do this, select the cell containing the date or time value, call its context menu and select \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab page contains the functions for defining the number format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	hd_id2408825				0	en-ZA	Date base for day zero				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	par_id9988402				0	en-ZA	Dates are calculated as offsets from a starting day zero. You can set the day zero to be one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	par_id6401257				0	en-ZA	Date base				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	par_id5841242				0	en-ZA	Use				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	par_id6794030				0	en-ZA	'12/30/1899'				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	par_id7096774				0	en-ZA	(default)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	par_id5699942				0	en-ZA	'01/01/1900'				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	par_id6420484				0	en-ZA	(used in former StarCalc 1.0)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	par_id6986602				0	en-ZA	'01/01/1904'				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	par_id616779				0	en-ZA	(used in Apple software)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	par_id791039				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Calculate\</emph\> to select the date base.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	par_id1953489				0	en-ZA	When you copy and paste cells containing date values between different spreadsheets, both spreadsheet documents must be set to the same date base. If date bases differ, the displayed date values will change!				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	hd_id757469				0	en-ZA	Two digits years				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	par_id3149720				0	en-ZA	In \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - General\</emph\> you find the area \<emph\>Year (two digits)\</emph\>. This sets the period for which two-digit information applies. Note that changes made here have an effect on some of the following functions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150654				0	en-ZA	When entering dates, slashes or dashes used as date separators may be interpreted as arithmetic operators. Therefore, dates entered in this format are not always recognised as dates and result in erroneous calculations. To keep dates from being interpreted as parts of formulae, place them in quotation marks, for example, "07/20/54".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
