helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12030100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163808				0	en-ZA	Ascending				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155336				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCPAGE_SORT_FIELDS:BTN_UP3\"\>Sorts the selection from the lowest value to the highest value. You can define the sort rules on Data - Sort - Options.\</ahelp\> You define the default on \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language settings - Languages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12030100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147364				0	en-ZA	Descending				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149258				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCPAGE_SORT_FIELDS:BTN_DOWN3\"\>Sorts the selection from the highest value to the lowest value. You can define the sort rules on Data - Sort - Options.\</ahelp\> You define the default on \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language settings - Languages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12030100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150300				0	en-ZA	Sort Ascending/Descending				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3158212				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SortDescending\"\>\<variable id=\"sytext\"\>Sorts the selection from the highest to the lowest value, or from the lowest to the highest value. Number fields are sorted by size and text fields by the order of the characters. You can define the sort rules on Data - Sort - Options.\</variable\>\</ahelp\> You define the default on \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language settings - Languages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159236				0	en-ZA	Icons on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> toolbar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Logical Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153484				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>logical functions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Function Wizard; logical\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>functions; logical functions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153484				0	en-ZA	Logical Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149312				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"logischtext\"\>This category contains the \<emph\>Logical\</emph\> functions. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147505				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>AND function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147505				0	en-ZA	AND				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3153959				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_UND\"\>Returns TRUE if all arguments are TRUE.\</ahelp\> If one of the elements is FALSE, this function returns the FALSE value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3146100				0	en-ZA	The arguments are either logical expressions themselves (TRUE, 1<5, 2+3=7, B8<10) that return logical values, or arrays (A1:C3) containing logical values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150538				0	en-ZA	When a function expects a single value, but you entered a cell range, then the value from the cell range is taken that is in the same column or row as the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149128				0	en-ZA	If the entered range is outside of the current column or row of the formula, the function returns the error value #VALUE!				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150374				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3159123				0	en-ZA	AND(LogicalValue1; LogicalValue2 ...LogicalValue30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150038	33			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>LogicalValue1; LogicalValue2 ...LogicalValue30\</emph\> are conditions to be checked. All conditions can be either TRUE or FALSE. If a range is entered as a parameter, the function uses the value from the range that is in the current column or row. The result is TRUE if the logical value in all cells within the cell range is TRUE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149143				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3153123				0	en-ZA	The logical values of entries 12<13; 14>12, and 7<6 are to be checked:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3145632	36			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=AND(12<13;14>12;7<6)\</item\> returns FALSE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149946	60			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=AND (FALSE;TRUE)\</item\> returns FALSE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149015				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>FALSE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149015				0	en-ZA	FALSE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149890				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_FALSCH\"\>Returns the logical value FALSE.\</ahelp\> The FALSE() function does not require any arguments, and always returns the logical value FALSE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146939				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150030				0	en-ZA	FALSE()				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150697				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3154842	8			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=FALSE()\</item\> returns FALSE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3147468	9			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=NOT(FALSE())\</item\> returns TRUE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150141				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>IF function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150141				0	en-ZA	IF				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3148740				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WENN\"\>Specifies a logical test to be performed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153325				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3154558				0	en-ZA	IF(Test; ThenValue; OtherwiseValue)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149727	52			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Test\</emph\> is any value or expression that can be TRUE or FALSE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155828	53			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>ThenValue\</emph\> (optional) is the value that is returned if the logical test is TRUE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3154811	54			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>OtherwiseValue\</emph\> (optional) is the value that is returned if the logical test is FALSE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FA				0	en-ZA	            \<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>         				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149507				0	en-ZA	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150867	57			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=IF(A1>5;100;"too small")\</item\> If the value in A1 is higher than 5, the value 100 is entered in the current cell; otherwise, the text “too small” (without quotes) is entered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155954				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>NOT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155954				0	en-ZA	NOT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3153570				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_NICHT\"\>Complements (inverts) a logical value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147372				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3157996				0	en-ZA	NOT(LogicalValue)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3148766	16			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>LogicalValue\</emph\> is any value to be complemented.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149884				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150132	18			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=NOT(A)\</item\>. If A=TRUE then NOT(A) will evaluate FALSE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148394				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>OR function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148394				0	en-ZA	OR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ODER\"\>Returns TRUE if at least one argument is TRUE.\</ahelp\> This function returns the value FALSE, if all the arguments have the logical value FALSE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3148771				0	en-ZA	The arguments are either logical expressions themselves (TRUE, 1<5, 2+3=7, B8<10) that return logical values, or arrays (A1:C3) containing logical values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3153546				0	en-ZA	When a function expects a single value, but you entered a cell range, then the value from the cell range is taken that is in the same column or row as the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149027				0	en-ZA	If the entered range is outside of the current column or row of the formula, the function returns the error value #VALUE!				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155517				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150468				0	en-ZA	OR(LogicalValue1; LogicalValue2 ...LogicalValue30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155819	24			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>LogicalValue1; LogicalValue2 ...LogicalValue30\</emph\> are conditions to be checked. All conditions can be either TRUE or FALSE. If a range is entered as a parameter, the function uses the value from the range that is in the current column or row.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153228				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3154870				0	en-ZA	The logical values of entries 12<11; 13>22, and 45=45 are to be checked.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155371	27			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=OR(12<11;13>22;45=45)\</item\> returns TRUE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3158412	59			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=OR(FALSE;TRUE)\</item\> returns TRUE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156256				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>TRUE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156256				0	en-ZA	TRUE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155985				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WAHR\"\>The logical value is set to TRUE.\</ahelp\> The TRUE() function does not require any arguments, and always returns the logical value TRUE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153717				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3152590				0	en-ZA	TRUE()				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147175				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3146148				0	en-ZA	If A=TRUE and B=FALSE the following examples appear:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3083285	44			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=AND(A;B)\</item\> returns FALSE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3083444	45			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=OR(A;B)\</item\> returns TRUE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3154314	46			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=NOT(AND(A;B))\</item\> returns TRUE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Define				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145673				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080100.xhp\" name=\"Define\"\>Define\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DefinePrintArea\"\>Defines an active cell or selected cell area as the print range.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_edate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	EDATE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_edate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151184				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>EDATE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_edate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151184				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"edate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_edate.xhp\"\>EDATE\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_edate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150880	214			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_EDATE\"\>The result is a date which is a number of m\<emph\>onths\</emph\> away from the \<emph\>start date\</emph\>. Only months are considered; days are not used for calculation.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_edate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154647				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_edate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153212				0	en-ZA	EDATE(StartDate; Months)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_edate.xhp	0	help	par_id3146860				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>StartDate\</emph\> is a date.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_edate.xhp	0	help	par_id3152929				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Months\</emph\> is the number of months before (negative) or after (positive) the start date.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_edate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151289				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_edate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155845				0	en-ZA	What date is one month prior to 3.31.2001?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_edate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155999				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=EDATE(3.31.2001;-1)\</item\> returns 2.28.2001.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Show				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030400.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147264				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; showing columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing; columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing; rows\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147264				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05030400.xhp\" name=\"Show\"\>Show\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150447				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowColumn\"\>Choose this command to show previously hidden rows or columns.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	en-ZA	To show a column or row, select the range of rows or columns containing the hidden elements, then choose \<emph\>Format - Row - Show\</emph\> or \<emph\>Format - Column - Show\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145748				0	en-ZA	To show all hidden cells, first click in the field in the upper left corner. This selects all cells of the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04010200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Column Break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04010200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155923				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; inserting column breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>column breaks; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; manual column breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>manual column breaks\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155923				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04010200.xhp\" name=\"Column Break\"\>Column Break\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150447				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertColumnBreak\"\>Inserts a column break (vertical page break) to the left of the active cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	en-ZA	The manual column break is indicated by a dark blue vertical line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154908				0	en-ZA	Layout				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3147229	20			0	en-ZA	$[officename] automatically adds a caption to buttons that are dragged into the \<emph\>Data Fields \</emph\>area. The caption contains the name of the data field as well as the formula that created the data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145749				0	en-ZA	To change the function that is used by a data field, double-click a button in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area to open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>Data Field\</link\> dialogue. You can also double-click buttons in the \<emph\>Row Fields\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column Fields\</emph\> areas.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149260				0	en-ZA	Remove				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SCDLG_PIVOT_LAYOUT_BTN_REMOVE\"\>Removes the selected data field from the table layout.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145273				0	en-ZA	Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SCDLG_PIVOT_LAYOUT_BTN_OPTIONS\"\>Opens the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue where you can change the function that is associated with the selected field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154944				0	en-ZA	More				2002-02-02 02:02:02
