helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	hd_id0509200913025625				0	en-ZA	Selection from				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155603				0	en-ZA	Results to				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147364				0	en-ZA	Ignore empty rows				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_PIVOT_LAYOUT:BTN_IGNEMPTYROWS\"\>Ignores empty fields in the data source.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155114				0	en-ZA	Identify categories				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145257				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_PIVOT_LAYOUT:BTN_DETECTCAT\"\>Automatically assigns rows without labels to the category of the row above.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149207				0	en-ZA	Total columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_PIVOT_LAYOUT:BTN_TOTALCOL\"\>Calculates and displays the grand total of the column calculation.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150364				0	en-ZA	Total rows				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3152583				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_PIVOT_LAYOUT:BTN_TOTALROW\"\>Calculates and displays the grand total of the row calculation.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN10897				0	en-ZA	Add filter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108B2				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the Filter dialogue.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C9				0	en-ZA	Enable drill to details				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108CD				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select this check box and double-click an item label in the table to show or hide details for the item. Clear this check box and double-click a cell in the table to edit the contents of the cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E0				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E6				0	en-ZA	Select a range of cells and choose \<emph\>Data - Group and Outline - Show Details\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108EE				0	en-ZA	Double-click a field in the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108F1				0	en-ZA	If you double-click a field which has adjacent fields at the same level, the \<emph\>Show Detail\</emph\> dialogue opens:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN10900				0	en-ZA	Show Detail				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN10904				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Choose the field that you want to view the details for.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02140200.xhp\" name=\"Right\"\>Right\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FillRight\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Fills a selected range of at least two columns with the contents of the left most cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	en-ZA	If a range of only one row is selected, the contents of the far left cell are copied to all the other selected cells. If you have selected several rows, each of the far left cells is copied into those cells to the right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Statistical Functions Part Four				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153415				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"mq\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060184.xhp\" name=\"Statistical Functions Part Four\"\>Statistical Functions Part Four\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154511				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>MAX function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154511				0	en-ZA	MAX				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153709				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MAX\"\>Returns the maximum value in a list of arguments.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id9282509				0	en-ZA	Returns 0 if no numeric value and no error was encountered in the cell range(s) passed as cell reference(s). Text cells are ignored by MIN() and MAX(). The functions MINA() and MAXA() return 0 if no value (numeric or text) and no error was encountered. Passing a literal string argument to MIN() or MAX(), e.g. MIN("string"), still results in an error.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154256				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147340				0	en-ZA	MAX(Number1; Number2; ...Number30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568	6			0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number1; Number2;...Number30\</emph\> are numerical values or ranges. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153963				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MAX(A1;A2;A3;50;100;200)\</item\> returns the largest value from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MAX(A1:B100)\</item\> returns the largest value from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3166426				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>MAXA function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166426				0	en-ZA	MAXA				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150363				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MAXA\"\>Returns the maximum value in a list of arguments. In opposite to MAX, here you can enter text. The value of the text is 0.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id7689443				0	en-ZA	The functions MINA() and MAXA() return 0 if no value (numeric or text) and no error was encountered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150516				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3166431				0	en-ZA	MAXA(Value1; Value2; ... Value30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150202				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Value1; Value2;...Value30\</emph\> are values or ranges. Text has the value of 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156290				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3156446				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MAXA(A1;A2;A3;50;100;200;"Text")\</item\> returns the largest value from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149404				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MAXA(A1:B100)\</item\> returns the largest value from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153820				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>MEDIAN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153820				0	en-ZA	MEDIAN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MEDIAN\"\>Returns the median of a set of numbers. In a set containing an uneven number of values, the median will be the number in the middle of the set and in a set containing an even number of values, it will be the mean of the two values in the middle of the set.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148871				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155264				0	en-ZA	MEDIAN(Number1; Number2; ...Number30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150109				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number1; Number2;...Number30\</emph\> are values or ranges, which represent a sample. Each number can also be replaced by a reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144506				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145078				0	en-ZA	for an odd number: \<item type=\"input\"\>=MEDIAN(1;5;9;20;21)\</item\> returns 9 as the median value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	en-ZA	for an even number: \<item type=\"input\"\>=MEDIAN(1;5;9;20)\</item\> returns the average of the two middle values 5 and 9, thus 7.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154541				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>MIN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154541				0	en-ZA	MIN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3143222				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MIN\"\>Returns the minimum value in a list of arguments.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id2301400				0	en-ZA	Returns 0 if no numeric value and no error was encountered in the cell range(s) passed as cell reference(s). Text cells are ignored by MIN() and MAX(). The functions MINA() and MAXA() return 0 if no value (numeric or text) and no error was encountered. Passing a literal string argument to MIN() or MAX(), e.g. MIN("string"), still results in an error.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154651				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3146964				0	en-ZA	MIN(Number1; Number2; ...Number30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153486				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number1; Number2;...Number30\</emph\> are numerical values or ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155523				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154734				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MIN(A1:B100)\</item\> returns the smallest value in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147504				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>MINA function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147504				0	en-ZA	MINA				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147249				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MINA\"\>Returns the minimum value in a list of arguments. Here you can also enter text. The value of the text is 0.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id4294564				0	en-ZA	The functions MINA() and MAXA() return 0 if no value (numeric or text) and no error was encountered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150435				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153336				0	en-ZA	MINA(Value1; Value2; ... Value30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3146098				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Value1; Value2;...Value30\</emph\> are values or ranges. Text has the value of 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148743				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147401				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MINA(1;"Text";20)\</item\> returns 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MINA(A1:B100)\</item\> returns the smallest value in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3166465				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>AVEDEV function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>averages;statistical functions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166465				0	en-ZA	AVEDEV				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150373				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MITTELABW\"\>Returns the average of the absolute deviations of data points from their mean.\</ahelp\> Displays the diffusion in a data set.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150038				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145636				0	en-ZA	AVEDEV(Number1; Number2; ...Number30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number1, Number2,...Number30\</emph\> are values or ranges that represent a sample. Each number can also be replaced by a reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149725				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153122				0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=AVEDEV(A1:A50)\</item\>         				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145824				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>AVERAGE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145824				0	en-ZA	AVERAGE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150482				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MITTELWERT\"\>Returns the average of the arguments.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146943				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154679				0	en-ZA	AVERAGE(Number1; Number2; ...Number30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150741				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number1; Number2;...Number 0\</emph\> are numerical values or ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153039				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151232				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=AVERAGE(A1:A50)\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148754				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>AVERAGEA function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148754				0	en-ZA	AVERAGEA				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145138				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MITTELWERTA\"\>Returns the average of the arguments. The value of a text is 0.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153326				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149734				0	en-ZA	AVERAGEA(Value1; Value2; ... Value30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155260				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Value1; Value2;...Value30\</emph\> are values or ranges. Text has the value of 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149504				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150864				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=AVERAGEA(A1:A50)\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153933				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>MODE function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>most common value\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153933				0	en-ZA	MODE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153085				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MODALWERT\"\>Returns the most common value in a data set.\</ahelp\> If there are several values with the same frequency, it returns the smallest value. An error occurs when a value doesn't appear twice.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153003				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155950				0	en-ZA	MODE(Number1; Number2; ...Number30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150337				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number1; Number2;...Number30\</emph\> are numerical values or ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153571				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153733				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MODE(A1:A50)\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149879				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>NEGBINOMDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>negative binomial distribution\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149879				0	en-ZA	NEGBINOMDIST				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155437				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_NEGBINOMVERT\"\>Returns the negative binomial distribution.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145351				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150935				0	en-ZA	NEGBINOMDIST(X; R; SP)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153044				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>X\</emph\> represents the value returned for unsuccessful tests.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151018				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>R\</emph\> represents the value returned for successful tests.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148878				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>SP\</emph\> is the probability of the success of an attempt.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149539				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148770				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NEGBINOMDIST(1;1;0.5)\</item\> returns 0.25.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155516				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>NORMINV function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>normal distribution;inverse of\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155516				0	en-ZA	NORMINV				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154634				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_NORMINV\"\>Returns the inverse of the normal cumulative distribution.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153227				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147534				0	en-ZA	NORMINV(Number; Mean; StDev)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154950				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> represents the probability value used to determine the inverse normal distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150690				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Mean\</emph\> represents the mean value in the normal distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148594				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>StDev\</emph\> represents the standard deviation of the normal distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155822				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153921				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NORMINV(0.9;63;5)\</item\> returns 69.41. If the average egg weighs 63 grams with a standard deviation of 5, then there will be 90% probability that the egg will not be heavier than 69.41g grams.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153722				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>NORMDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>density function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153722				0	en-ZA	NORMDIST				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150386				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_NORMVERT\"\>Returns the density function or the normal cumulative distribution.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3083282				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150613				0	en-ZA	NORMDIST(Number; Mean; StDev; C)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149820				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value of the distribution based on which the normal distribution is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3146063				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Mean\</emph\> is the mean value of the distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3156295				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>StDev\</emph\> is the standard deviation of the distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145080				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>C\</emph\> is optional. \<emph\>C\</emph\> = 0 calculates the density function, \<emph\>C\</emph\> = 1 calculates the distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152972				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149283				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NORMDIST(70;63;5;0)\</item\> returns 0.03.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149448				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NORMDIST(70;63;5;1)\</item\> returns 0.92.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152934				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>PEARSON function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152934				0	en-ZA	PEARSON				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153216				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_PEARSON\"\>Returns the Pearson product moment correlation coefficient r.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147081				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3156133				0	en-ZA	PEARSON(Data1; Data2)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151272				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Data1\</emph\> represents the array of the first data set.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153279				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Data2\</emph\> represents the array of the second data set.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147567				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151187				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PEARSON(A1:A30;B1:B30)\</item\> returns the Pearson correlation coefficient of both data sets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152806				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>PHI function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152806				0	en-ZA	PHI				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150254				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_PHI\"\>Returns the values of the distribution function for a standard normal distribution.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154748				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149976				0	en-ZA	PHI(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3156108				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> represents the value based on which the standard normal distribution is calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153621				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155849				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PHI(2.25) \</item\>= 0.03				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3143236				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PHI(-2.25)\</item\> = 0.03				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149286				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PHI(0)\</item\> = 0.4				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153985				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>POISSON function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153985				0	en-ZA	POISSON				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154298				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_POISSON\"\>Returns the Poisson distribution.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159183				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3146093				0	en-ZA	POISSON(Number; Mean; C)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147253				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> represents the value based on which the Poisson distribution is calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Mean\</emph\> represents the middle value of the Poisson distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149200				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>C\</emph\> (optional) = 0 or False calculates the density function; \<emph\>C\</emph\> = 1 or True calculates the distribution. When omitted, the default value True is inserted when you save the document, for best compatibility with other programs and older versions of %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159347				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150113				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=POISSON(60;50;1)\</item\> returns 0.93.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153100				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>PERCENTILE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153100				0	en-ZA	PERCENTILE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154940				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_QUANTIL\"\>Returns the alpha-percentile of data values in an array.\</ahelp\> A percentile returns the scale value for a data series which goes from the smallest (Alpha=0) to the largest value (alpha=1) of a data series. For \<item type=\"literal\"\>Alpha\</item\> = 25%, the percentile means the first quartile; \<item type=\"literal\"\>Alpha\</item\> = 50% is the MEDIAN.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150531				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148813				0	en-ZA	PERCENTILE(Data; Alpha)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153054				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Data\</emph\> represents the array of data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154212				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Alpha\</emph\> represents the percentage of the scale between 0 and 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154290				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3159147				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PERCENTILE(A1:A50;0.1)\</item\> represents the value in the data set, which equals 10% of the total data scale in A1:A50.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148807				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>PERCENTRANK function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148807				0	en-ZA	PERCENTRANK				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153573				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_QUANTILSRANG\"\>Returns the percentage rank of a value in a sample.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147512				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147238				0	en-ZA	PERCENTRANK(Data; Value)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154266				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Data\</emph\> represents the array of data in the sample.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148475				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> represents the value whose percentile rank must be determined.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149163				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PERCENTRANK(A1:A50;50)\</item\> returns the percentage rank of the value 50 from the total range of all values found in A1:A50. If 50 falls outside the total range, an error message will appear.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3166442				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>QUARTILE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166442				0	en-ZA	QUARTILE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3146958				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_QUARTILE\"\>Returns the quartile of a data set.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152942				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153684				0	en-ZA	QUARTILE(Data; Type)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153387				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Data\</emph\> represents the array of data in the sample.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155589				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> represents the type of quartile. (0 = MIN, 1 = 25%, 2 = 50% (MEDIAN), 3 = 75% and 4 = MAX.)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149103				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3159276				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=QUARTILE(A1:A50;2)\</item\> returns the value of which 50% of the scale corresponds to the lowest to highest values in the range A1:A50.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Error Alert				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153821				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12120300.xhp\" name=\"Error Alert\"\>Error Alert\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:TABPAGE:TP_VALIDATION_ERROR\"\>Define the error message that is displayed when invalid data is entered in a cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	en-ZA	You can also start a macro with an error message. A sample macro is provided at the end of this page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156280				0	en-ZA	Show error message when invalid values are entered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150768				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Displays the error message that you enter in the \<emph\>Contents\</emph\> area when invalid data is entered in a cell.\</ahelp\> If enabled, the message is displayed to prevent an invalid entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3146984	5			0	en-ZA	In both cases, if you select "Stop", the invalid entry is deleted and the previous value is reentered in the cell. The same applies if you close the "Warning" and "Information" dialogues by clicking the \<emph\>Cancel \</emph\>button. If you close the dialogues with the \<emph\>OK\</emph\> button, the invalid entry is not deleted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152460				0	en-ZA	Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148646				0	en-ZA	Action				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3151115				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:TP_VALIDATION_ERROR:LB_ACTION\"\>Select the action that you want to occur when invalid data is entered in a cell.\</ahelp\> The "Stop" action rejects the invalid entry and displays a dialogue that you have to close by clicking \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The "Warning" and "Information" actions display a dialogue that can be closed by clicking \<emph\>OK\</emph\> or \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>. The invalid entry is only rejected when you click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156441				0	en-ZA	Browse				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153160				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:PUSHBUTTON:TP_VALIDATION_ERROR:BTN_SEARCH\"\>Opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Macro\"\>Macro\</link\> dialogue where you can select the macro that is executed when invalid data is entered in a cell. The macro is executed after the error message is displayed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153876				0	en-ZA	Title				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149410				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:TP_VALIDATION_ERROR:EDT_TITLE\"\>Enter the title of the macro or the error message that you want to display when invalid data is entered in a cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154510				0	en-ZA	Error message				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149122				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:MULTILINEEDIT:TP_VALIDATION_ERROR:EDT_ERROR\"\>Enter the message that you want to display when invalid data is entered in a cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Sample macro:\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Statistical Functions Part Three				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166425				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"kl\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060183.xhp\" name=\"Statistical Functions Part Three\"\>Statistical Functions Part Three\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149530				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>LARGE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149530				0	en-ZA	LARGE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3150518				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KGROESSTE\"\>Returns the Rank_c-th largest value in a data set.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152990				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3154372				0	en-ZA	LARGE(Data; RankC)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3152986				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Data\</emph\> is the cell range of data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3156448				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>RankC\</emph\> is the ranking of the value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152889				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3148702				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LARGE(A1:C50;2)\</item\> gives the second largest value in A1:C50.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154532				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>SMALL function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154532				0	en-ZA	SMALL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3157981				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KKLEINSTE\"\>Returns the Rank_c-th smallest value in a data set.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154957				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3153974				0	en-ZA	SMALL(Data; RankC)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3154540				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Data\</emph\> is the cell range of data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3155094				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>RankC\</emph\> is the rank of the value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153247				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3149897				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SMALL(A1:C50;2)\</item\> gives the second smallest value in A1:C50.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153559				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>CONFIDENCE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153559				0	en-ZA	CONFIDENCE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3153814				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KONFIDENZ\"\>Returns the (1-alpha) confidence interval for a normal distribution.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149315				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3147501				0	en-ZA	CONFIDENCE(Alpha; StDev; Size)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Alpha\</emph\> is the level of the confidence interval.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3145324				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>StDev\</emph\> is the standard deviation for the total population.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3153075				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Size\</emph\> is the size of the total population.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150435				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3153335				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CONFIDENCE(0.05;1.5;100)\</item\> gives 0.29.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148746				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>CORREL function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>coefficient of correlation\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148746				0	en-ZA	CORREL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3147299				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KORREL\"\>Returns the correlation coefficient between two data sets.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156397				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3153023				0	en-ZA	CORREL(Data1; Data2)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3150036				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Data1\</emph\> is the first data set.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3153021				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Data2\</emph\> is the second data set.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149720				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3149941				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CORREL(A1:A50;B1:B50)\</item\> calculates the correlation coefficient as a measure of the linear correlation of the two data sets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150652				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>COVAR function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150652				0	en-ZA	COVAR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3146875				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KOVAR\"\>Returns the covariance of the product of paired deviations.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149013				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3150740				0	en-ZA	COVAR(Data1; Data2)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3145827				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Data1\</emph\> is the first data set.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3150465				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Data2\</emph\> is the second data set.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154677				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3144748				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COVAR(A1:A30;B1:B30)\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147472				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>CRITBINOM function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147472				0	en-ZA	CRITBINOM				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3149254				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KRITBINOM\"\>Returns the smallest value for which the cumulative binomial distribution is less than or equal to a criterion value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153930				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3148586				0	en-ZA	CRITBINOM(Trials; SP; Alpha)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3145593				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Trials\</emph\> is the total number of trials.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3153084				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>SP\</emph\> is the probability of success for one trial.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3149726				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Alpha\</emph\> is the threshold probability to be reached or exceeded.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148752				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3148740				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CRITBINOM(100;0.5;0.1)\</item\> yields 44.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155956				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>KURT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155956				0	en-ZA	KURT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3153108				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KURT\"\>Returns the kurtosis of a data set (at least 4 values required).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150334				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3154508				0	en-ZA	KURT(Number1; Number2; ...Number30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3145167				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number1,Number2,...Number30\</emph\> are numeric arguments or ranges representing a random sample of distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158000				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3150016				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=KURT(A1;A2;A3;A4;A5;A6)\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150928				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>LOGINV function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inverse of lognormal distribution\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150928				0	en-ZA	LOGINV				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3145297				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LOGINV\"\>Returns the inverse of the lognormal distribution.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151016				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3153049				0	en-ZA	LOGINV(Number; Mean; StDev)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3148390				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the probability value for which the inverse standard logarithmic distribution is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3149538				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Mean\</emph\> is the arithmetic mean of the standard logarithmic distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3145355				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>StDev\</emph\> is the standard deviation of the standard logarithmic distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148768				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3155623				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LOGINV(0.05;0;1)\</item\> returns 0.19.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158417				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>LOGNORMDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cumulative lognormal distribution\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158417				0	en-ZA	LOGNORMDIST				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3154953				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LOGNORMVERT\"\>Returns the cumulative lognormal distribution.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150474				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3150686				0	en-ZA	LOGNORMDIST(Number; Mean; StDev; Cumulative)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3154871				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the probability value for which the standard logarithmic distribution is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3155820				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Mean\</emph\> (optional) is the mean value of the standard logarithmic distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3155991				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>StDev\</emph\> (optional) is the standard deviation of the standard logarithmic distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3155992				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Cumulative\</emph\> (optional) = 0 calculates the density function, Cumulative = 1 calculates the distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153178				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3149778				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LOGNORMDIST(0.1;0;1)\</item\> returns 0.01.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Define Label Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; defining label ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>label ranges in sheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"define_label_range\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04070400.xhp\"\>Define Label Range\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"beschtext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DefineLabelRange\"\>Opens a dialogue in which you can define a label range.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411				0	en-ZA	The cell contents of a label range can be used like names in formulae - $[officename] recognises these names in the same manner that it does the predefined names of the weekdays and months. These names are automatically completed when typed into a formula. In addition, the names defined by label ranges will have priority over names defined by automatically generated ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435				0	en-ZA	You can set label ranges that contain the same labels on different sheets. $[officename] first searches the label ranges of the current sheet and, following a failed search, the ranges of other sheets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145801				0	en-ZA	Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_COLROWNAMERANGES:ED_AREA\"\>Displays the cell reference of each label range.\</ahelp\> In order to remove a label range from the list box, select it and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149121				0	en-ZA	Contains column labels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150330				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_COLROWNAMERANGES:BTN_COLHEAD\"\>Includes column labels in the current label range.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149020				0	en-ZA	Contains row labels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_COLROWNAMERANGES:BTN_ROWHEAD\"\>Includes row labels in the current label range.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159264				0	en-ZA	For data range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154703				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_COLROWNAMERANGES:ED_DATA\"\>Sets the data range for which the selected label range is valid. To modify it, click in the sheet and select another range with the mouse.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145789				0	en-ZA	Add				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147005				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_COLROWNAMERANGES:BTN_ADD\"\>Adds the current label range to the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Data field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150871				0	en-ZA	Data field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	en-ZA	Subtotals				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_id3151113				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_PIVOTSUBT\"\>Specify the subtotals that you want to calculate.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145366				0	en-ZA	None				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_PIVOTSUBT:BTN_NONE\"\>Does not calculate subtotals.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154012				0	en-ZA	Automatic				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155856				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_PIVOTSUBT:BTN_AUTO\"\>Automatically calculates subtotals.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411				0	en-ZA	User-defined				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149581				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_PIVOTSUBT:BTN_USER\"\>Select this option, and then click the type of subtotal that you want to calculate in the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147124				0	en-ZA	Function				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:MULTILISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_PIVOTSUBT:LB_FUNC\"\>Click the type of subtotal that you want to calculate. This option is only available if the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> option is selected.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154944				0	en-ZA	Show elements without data				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149403				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_PIVOTSUBT:CB_SHOWALL\"\>Includes empty columns and rows in the results table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149122				0	en-ZA	Name:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	en-ZA	Lists the name of the selected data field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EC				0	en-ZA	More				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F0				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Expands or reduces the dialogue. The \<emph\>More\</emph\> button is visible for data fields only.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F3				0	en-ZA	Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F7				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090106.xhp\"\>Data Field Options\</link\> dialogue. The \<emph\>Options\</emph\> button is visible for column, row, or page fields only.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN10708				0	en-ZA	If the dialogue is expanded by the \<emph\>More\</emph\> button, the following items are added to the dialogue:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070B				0	en-ZA	Displayed value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070F				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For each data field, you can select the type of display.\</ahelp\> For some types you can select additional information for a base field and a base item.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN10712				0	en-ZA	Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN10716				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"1495371266\"\>Select the type of calculating of the displayed value for the data field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN10724				0	en-ZA	Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072A				0	en-ZA	Displayed value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	en-ZA	Normal				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN10737				0	en-ZA	Results are shown unchanged				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073E				0	en-ZA	Difference from				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN10744				0	en-ZA	From each result, its reference value (see below) is subtracted, and the difference is shown. Totals outside of the base field are shown as empty results.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN10747				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Named item\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074C				0	en-ZA	If a base item name is specified, the reference value for a combination of field items is the result where the item in the base field is replaced by the specified base item.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074F				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Previous item or Next item\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN10754				0	en-ZA	If "previous item" or "next item" is specified as the base item, the reference value is the result for the next visible member of the base field, in the base field's sort order.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075B				0	en-ZA	% Of				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN10761				0	en-ZA	Each result is divided by its reference value. The reference value is determined in the same way as for "Difference from". Totals outside of the base field are shown as empty results. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076A				0	en-ZA	% Difference from				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN10770				0	en-ZA	From each result, its reference value is subtracted, and the difference is divided by the reference value. The reference value is determined in the same way as for "Difference from". Totals outside of the base field are shown as empty results.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN10777				0	en-ZA	Running total in				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077D				0	en-ZA	Each result is added to the sum of the results for preceding items in the base field, in the base field's sort order, and the total sum is shown.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN10780				0	en-ZA	Results are always summed, even if a different summary function was used to get each result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN10787				0	en-ZA	% of row				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN10794				0	en-ZA	% of column				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079A				0	en-ZA	Same as "% of row", but the total for the result's column is used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A1				0	en-ZA	% of total				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A7				0	en-ZA	Same as "% of row", but the grand total for the result's data field is used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AE				0	en-ZA	Index				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B4				0	en-ZA	The row and column totals and the grand total, following the same rules as above, are used to calculate the following expression:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B7				0	en-ZA	( original result * grand total ) / ( row total * column total )				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BA				0	en-ZA	Base field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BE				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"1495371267\"\>Select the field from which the respective value is taken as base for the calculation.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C1				0	en-ZA	Base item				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C5				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"1495371268\"\>Select the item of the base field from which the respective value is taken as base for the calculation.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Row Break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156326				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; deleting row breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;manual row breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>row breaks; deleting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156326				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02190100.xhp\" name=\"Row Break\"\>Row Break\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DeleteRowbreak\"\>Removes the manual row break above the active cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	en-ZA	Position the cursor in a cell directly below the row break indicated by a horizontal line and choose \<emph\>Edit - Delete Manual Break - Row Break\</emph\>. The manual row break is removed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Value Highlighting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151384				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03080000.xhp\" name=\"Value Highlighting\"\>Value Highlighting\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ViewValueHighlighting\"\>Displays cell contents in different colours, depending on type.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863				0	en-ZA	To remove the highlighting, unmark the menu entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785				0	en-ZA	Text cells are formatted in black, formulae in green, and number cells in blue, no matter how their display is formatted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	en-ZA	If this function is active, colours that you define in the document will not be displayed. When you deactivate the function, the user-defined colours are displayed again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Mark Invalid Data				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153821				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>cells; invalid data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; showing invalid data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>invalid data;marking\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153821				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030800.xhp\" name=\"Mark Invalid Data\"\>Mark Invalid Data\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowInvalid\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Marks all cells in the sheet that contain values outside the validation rules.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211				0	en-ZA	The \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12120000.xhp\" name=\"validity rules\"\>validity rules\</link\> restrict the input of numbers, dates, time values and text to certain values. However, it is possible to enter invalid values or copy invalid values into the cells if the \<emph\>Stop\</emph\> option is not selected. When you assign a validity rule, existing values in a cell will not be modified.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	AutoFormat				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149666				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"autoformat\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05110000.xhp\" name=\"AutoFormat\"\>AutoFormat\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145367				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"autoformattext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Use this command to apply an AutoFormat to a selected sheet area or to define your own AutoFormats.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148455				0	en-ZA	Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_AUTOFORMAT:LB_FORMAT\"\>Choose a predefined AutoFormat to apply to a selected area in your sheet.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149410				0	en-ZA	Add				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_AUTOFORMAT:BTN_ADD\"\>Allows you to add the current formatting of a range of at least 4 x 4 cells to the list of predefined AutoFormats.\</ahelp\> The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05150101.xhp\" name=\"Add AutoFormat\"\>Add AutoFormat\</link\> dialogue then appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153708	29			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_AUTOFMT_NAME\"\>Enter a name and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. \</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150044				0	en-ZA	More				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:MOREBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_AUTOFORMAT:BTN_MORE\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> section, which displays the formatting overrides that can be applied to the spreadsheet. Deselecting an option keeps the format of the current spreadsheet for that format type.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155961				0	en-ZA	Formatting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965				0	en-ZA	In this section you can select or deselect the available formatting options. If you want to keep any of the settings currently in your spreadsheet, deselect the corresponding option.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154021				0	en-ZA	Number format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159239				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_AUTOFORMAT:BTN_NUMFORMAT\"\>When marked, specifies that you want to retain the number format of the selected format.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149530				0	en-ZA	Borders				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145259				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_AUTOFORMAT:BTN_BORDER\"\>When marked, specifies that you want to retain the border of the selected format.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154657				0	en-ZA	Font				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_AUTOFORMAT:BTN_FONT\"\>When marked, specifies that you want to retain the font of the selected format.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155379				0	en-ZA	Pattern				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150368				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_AUTOFORMAT:BTN_PATTERN\"\>When marked, specifies that you want to retain the pattern of the selected format.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146115				0	en-ZA	Alignment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156445				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_AUTOFORMAT:BTN_ALIGNMENT\"\>When marked, specifies that you want to retain the alignment of the selected format.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155811				0	en-ZA	AutoFit width and height				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148703				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_AUTOFORMAT:BTN_ADJUST\"\>When marked, specifies that you want to retain the width and height of the selected cells of the selected format.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159223				0	en-ZA	Rename				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153064				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_RENAME_AUTOFMT\"\>Opens a dialogue where you can change the specification of the selected AutoFormat.\</ahelp\> The button is only visible if you clicked the \<emph\>More\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153912				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Rename AutoFormat\</emph\> dialogue opens.\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_REN_AFMT_NAME\"\> Enter the new name of the AutoFormat here.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155264				0	en-ZA	More				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159094				0	en-ZA	Closes the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> options section, if it is currently open.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Add-in for Programming in $[officename] Calc				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151076				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>programming; add-ins\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>shared libraries; programming\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>external DLL functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>functions; $[officename] Calc add-in DLL\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>add-ins; for programming\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151076				0	en-ZA	Add-in for Programming in $[officename] Calc				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	en-ZA	The method of extending Calc by Add-Ins that is described in the following is outdated. The interfaces are still valid and supported, to ensure compatibility with existing Add-Ins, but for programming new Add-Ins you should use the new \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/integratinguno.xhp\" name=\"API functions\"\>API functions\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150361	2			0	en-ZA	$[officename] Calc can be expanded by Add-Ins, which are external programming modules providing additional functions for working with spreadsheets. These are listed in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Add-In\</emph\> category. If you would like to program an Add-In yourself, you can learn here which functions must be exported by the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>shared library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>external DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> so that the Add-In can be successfully attached.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149211	3			0	en-ZA	$[officename] searches the Add-in folder defined in the configuration for a suitable \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>shared library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>. To be recognised by $[officename], the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>shared library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> must have certain properties, as explained in the following. This information allows you to program your own Add-In for \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\> of $[officename] Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146981				0	en-ZA	The Add-In Concept				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3156292				0	en-ZA	Each Add-In library provides several functions. Some functions are used for administrative purposes. You can choose almost any name for your own functions. However, they must also follow certain rules regarding parameter passing. The exact naming and calling conventions vary for different platforms.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152890	6			0	en-ZA	Functions of \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Shared Library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>AddIn DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148837				0	en-ZA	At a minimum, the administrative functions \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"GetFunctionCount\"\>GetFunctionCount\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"GetFunctionData\"\>GetFunctionData\</link\> must exist. Using these, the functions as well as parameter types and return values can be determined. As return values, the Double and String types are supported. As parameters, additionally the cell areas \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"Double Array\"\>Double Array\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"String Array\"\>String Array\</link\>, and \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"Cell Array\"\>Cell Array\</link\> are supported.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148604				0	en-ZA	Parameters are passed using references. Therefore, a change of these values is basically possible. However, this is not supported in $[officename] Calc because it does not make sense within spreadsheets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150112				0	en-ZA	Libraries can be reloaded during runtime and their contents can be analyzed by the administrative functions. For each function, information is available about count and type of parameters, internal and external function names and an administrative number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3155269				0	en-ZA	The functions are called synchronously and return their results immediately. Real time functions (asynchronous functions) are also possible; however, they are not explained in detail because of their complexity.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145077				0	en-ZA	General information about the interface				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3146776				0	en-ZA	The maximum number of parameters in an Add-In function attached to $[officename] Calc is 16: one return value and a maximum of 15 function input parameters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149899				0	en-ZA	The data types are defined as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3151302				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Data types\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3143222				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Definition\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149384				0	en-ZA	CALLTYPE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3146963				0	en-ZA	Under Windows: FAR PASCAL (_far _pascal)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153809				0	en-ZA	Other: default (operating system specific default)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154734				0	en-ZA	USHORT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3155760				0	en-ZA	2 Byte unsigned Integer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3145320				0	en-ZA	DOUBLE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150956				0	en-ZA	8 byte platform-dependent format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3146097				0	en-ZA	Paramtype				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150432				0	en-ZA	Platform-dependent like int				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153955				0	en-ZA	PTR_DOUBLE =0 pointer to a double				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3159262				0	en-ZA	PTR_STRING =1 pointer to a zero-terminated string				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148747				0	en-ZA	PTR_DOUBLE_ARR =2 pointer to a double array				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3147406				0	en-ZA	PTR_STRING_ARR =3 pointer to a string array				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3151392				0	en-ZA	PTR_CELL_ARR =4 pointer to a cell array				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153028				0	en-ZA	NONE =5				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156396	31			0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Shared Library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153019	32			0	en-ZA	Following you will find a description of those functions, which are called at the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Shared Library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>external DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150038	33			0	en-ZA	For all \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Shared Library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> functions, the following applies:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3157876				0	en-ZA	void CALLTYPE fn(out, in1, in2, ...)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3147616				0	en-ZA	Output: Resulting value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3159119				0	en-ZA	Input: Any number of types (double&, char*, double*, char**, Cell area), where the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"Cell area\"\>Cell area\</link\> is an array of types double array, string array, or cell array.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150653				0	en-ZA	GetFunctionCount()				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3152981				0	en-ZA	Returns the number of functions without the management functions of the reference parameter. Each function has a unique number between 0 and nCount-1. This number will be needed for the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"GetFunctionData\"\>GetFunctionData\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"GetParameterDescription\"\>GetParameterDescription\</link\> functions later.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150742				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Syntax\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148728				0	en-ZA	void CALLTYPE GetFunctionCount(USHORT& nCount)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154677				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Parameter\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3146940				0	en-ZA	USHORT &nCount:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149893				0	en-ZA	Output: Reference to a variable, which is supposed to contain the number of Add-In functions. For example: If the Add-In provides 5 functions for $[officename] Calc, then nCount=5.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147476				0	en-ZA	GetFunctionData()				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154841				0	en-ZA	Determines all the important information about an Add-In function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148888				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Syntax\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148434				0	en-ZA	void CALLTYPE GetFunctionData(USHORT& nNo, char* pFuncName, USHORT& nParamCount, Paramtype* peType, char* pInternalName)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149253				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Parameter\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149686				0	en-ZA	USHORT& nNo:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149949				0	en-ZA	Input: Function number between 0 and nCount-1, inclusively.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149546				0	en-ZA	char* pFuncName:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148579	52			0	en-ZA	Output: Function name as seen by the programmer, as it is named in the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Shared Library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>. This name does not determine the name used in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153935				0	en-ZA	USHORT& nParamCount:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150142				0	en-ZA	Output: Number of parameters in AddIn function. This number must be greater than 0, because there is always a result value; the maximum value is 16.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3145143				0	en-ZA	Paramtype* peType:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148750				0	en-ZA	Output: Pointer to an array of exactly 16 variables of type Paramtype. The first nParamCount entries are filled with the suitable type of parameter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153078				0	en-ZA	char* pInternalName:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3155261				0	en-ZA	Output: Function name as seen by the user, as it appears in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>. May contain umlauts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153327				0	en-ZA	The pFuncName and pInternalName parameters are char arrays, which are implemented with size 256 in $[officename] Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148567				0	en-ZA	GetParameterDescription()				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153000				0	en-ZA	Provides a brief description of the Add-In function and its parameters. As an option, this function can be used to show a function and parameter description in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154501				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Syntax\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153564				0	en-ZA	void CALLTYPE GetParameterDescription(USHORT& nNo, USHORT& nParam, char* pName, char* pDesc)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3157995				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Parameter\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3155925				0	en-ZA	USHORT& nNo:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149883				0	en-ZA	Input: Number of the function in the library; between 0 and nCount-1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154326				0	en-ZA	USHORT& nParam:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3159139				0	en-ZA	Input: Indicates, for which parameter the description is provided; parameters start at 1. If nParam is 0, the description itself is supposed to be provided in pDesc; in this case, pName does not have any meaning.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3147374				0	en-ZA	char* pName:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3145245				0	en-ZA	Output: Takes up the parameter name or type, for example, the word "Number" or "String" or "Date", and so on. Implemented in $[officename] Calc as char[256].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3151020				0	en-ZA	char* pDesc:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148389				0	en-ZA	Output: Takes up the description of the parameter, for example, "Value, at which the universe is to be calculated." Implemented in $[officename] Calc as char[256].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3145303				0	en-ZA	pName and pDesc are char arrays; implemented in $[officename] Calc with size 256. Please note that the space available in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\> is limited and that the 256 characters cannot be fully used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148874				0	en-ZA	Cell areas				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150265				0	en-ZA	The following tables contain information about which data structures must be provided by an external program module in order to pass cell areas. $[officename] Calc distinguishes between three different arrays, depending on the data type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156060				0	en-ZA	Double Array				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149540				0	en-ZA	As a parameter, a cell area with values of the Number/Double type can be passed. A double array in $[officename] Calc is defined as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149388				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Offset\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
