helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156068				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>8\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3691824				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>INFO function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id5787224				0	en-ZA	INFO				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id1507309				0	en-ZA	Returns specific information about the current working environment. The function receives a single text argument and returns data depending on that parameter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id7693411				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3928952				0	en-ZA	INFO("Type")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id5206762				0	en-ZA	The following table lists the values for the text parameter \<item type=\"literal\"\>Type\</item\> and the return values of the INFO function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id5735953				0	en-ZA	Value for "Type"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id8360850				0	en-ZA	Return value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id9648731				0	en-ZA	"osversion"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id908841				0	en-ZA	Always "Windows (32-bit) NT 5.01", for compatibility reasons				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id8193914				0	en-ZA	"system"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id9841608				0	en-ZA	The type of the operating system. \<br/\>"WNT" for Microsoft Windows \<br/\>"LINUX" for Linux \<br/\>"SOLARIS" for Solaris				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id2701803				0	en-ZA	"release"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id2136295				0	en-ZA	The product release identifier, for example "300m25(Build:9876)"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id9200109				0	en-ZA	"numfile"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id4186223				0	en-ZA	Always 1, for compatibility reasons				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id5766472				0	en-ZA	"recalc"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id1491134				0	en-ZA	Current formula recalculation mode, either "Automatic" or "Manual" (localised into %PRODUCTNAME language)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id1161534				0	en-ZA	Other spreadsheet applications may accept localised values for the \<item type=\"literal\"\>Type\</item\> parameter, but %PRODUCTNAME Calc will only accept the English values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id5459456				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3994567				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=INFO("release")\</item\> returns the product release number of the %PRODUCTNAME in use.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id2873622				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=INFO(D5)\</item\> with cell \<item type=\"literal\"\>D5\</item\> containing a text string \<item type=\"literal\"\>system\</item\> returns the operation system type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155625				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>CURRENT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155625				0	en-ZA	CURRENT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3157975				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_AKTUELL\"\>This function returns the result to date of evaluating the formula of which it is a part (in other words the result as far as that evaluation has got). Its main use is together with the STYLE() function to apply selected styles to a cell depending on the cell contents.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148880				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150930				0	en-ZA	CURRENT()				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145629				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id5919064				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=1+2+CURRENT()\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id8751792				0	en-ZA	The example returns 6. The formula is calculated from left to right as: 1 + 2 equals 3, giving the result to date when CURRENT() is encountered; CURRENT() therefore yields 3, which is added to the original 3 to give 6.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id5863826				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=A2+B2+STYLE(IF(CURRENT()>10;”Red”;”Default”))\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id7463911				0	en-ZA	The example returns A2 + B2 (STYLE returns 0 here). If this sum is greater than 10, the style Red is applied to the cell. See the \<emph\>STYLE\</emph\> function for more explanation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id7318643				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>="choo"&CURRENT()\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id6019165				0	en-ZA	The example returns choochoo.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150688				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>FORMULA function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formula cells;displaying formulae in other cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>displaying;formulae at any position\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150688				0	en-ZA	FORMULA				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3158417				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_FORMEL\"\>Displays the formula of a formula cell as a text string.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154954				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3147535				0	en-ZA	FORMULA(Reference)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3014313				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Reference\</emph\> is a reference to a cell containing a formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id8857081				0	en-ZA	An invalid reference or a reference to a cell with no formula results in the error value #N/A.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152820				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153179				0	en-ZA	If cell A8 contains the formula \<item type=\"input\"\>=SUM(1;2;3)\</item\> then				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153923				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FORMULA(A8)\</item\> returns the text =SUM(1;2;3).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155409				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ISREF function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references;testing cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell contents;testing for references\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155409				0	en-ZA	ISREF				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153723				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ISTBEZUG\"\>Tests if the argument is a reference.\</ahelp\> Returns TRUE if the argument is a reference, returns FALSE otherwise. When given a reference this function does not examine the value being referenced.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147175				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149821				0	en-ZA	ISREF(Value)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3146152				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> is the value to be tested, to determine whether it is a reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3083448				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154317				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISREF(C5)\</item\> returns the result TRUE because C5 is a valid reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id9728072				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISREF("abcdef")\</item\> returns always FALSE because a text can never be a reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id2131544				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISREF(4)\</item\> returns FALSE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id4295480				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISREF(INDIRECT("A6"))\</item\> returns TRUE, because INDIRECT is a function that returns a reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3626819				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISREF(ADDRESS(1; 1; 2;"Sheet2"))\</item\> returns FALSE, because ADDRESS is a function that returns a text, although it looks like a reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154812				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ISERR function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error codes;controlling\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154812				0	en-ZA	ISERR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149282				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ISTFEHL\"\>Tests for error conditions, except the #N/A error value, and returns TRUE or FALSE.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149450				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156312				0	en-ZA	ISERR(Value)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3146857				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> is any value or expression which is tested to see whether an error value other than #N/A is present.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153212				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153276				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISERR(C8)\</item\> where cell C8 contains \<item type=\"input\"\>=1/0\</item\> returns TRUE, because 1/0 is an error.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id8456984				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISERR(C9)\</item\> where cell C9 contains \<item type=\"input\"\>=NA()\</item\> returns FALSE, because ISERR() ignores the #N/A error.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147081				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ISERROR function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recognising;general errors\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147081				0	en-ZA	ISERROR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156316				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ISTFEHLER\"\>Tests for error conditions, including the #N/A error value, and returns TRUE or FALSE.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147569				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153155				0	en-ZA	ISERROR(Value)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154047				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> is or refers to the value to be tested. ISERROR() returns TRUE if there is an error and FALSE if not.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155994				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150256				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISERROR(C8)\</item\> where cell C8 contains \<item type=\"input\"\>=1/0\</item\> returns TRUE, because 1/0 is an error.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id1889095				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISERROR(C9)\</item\> where cell C9 contains \<item type=\"input\"\>=NA()\</item\> returns TRUE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153618				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ISFORMULA function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recognising formula cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formula cells;recognising\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153618				0	en-ZA	ISFORMULA				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149138				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ISTFORMEL\"\>Returns TRUE if a cell is a formula cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155100				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3143230				0	en-ZA	ISFORMULA(Reference)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150150				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Reference\</emph\> indicates the reference to a cell in which a test will be performed to determine if it contains a formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147491				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3159182				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISFORMULA(C4)\</item\> returns FALSE if the cell C4 contains the number \<item type=\"input\"\>5\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149760				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ISEVEN_ADD function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149760				0	en-ZA	ISEVEN_ADD				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3147253				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_ISEVEN\"\>Tests for even numbers. Returns 1 if the number divided by 2 returns a whole number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152799				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149202				0	en-ZA	ISEVEN_ADD(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3151168				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number to be tested.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150115				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153904				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISEVEN_ADD(5)\</item\> returns 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id6238308				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISEVEN_ADD(A1)\</item\> returns 1 if cell A1 contains the number \<item type=\"input\"\>2\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154692				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ISNONTEXT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell contents;no text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154692				0	en-ZA	ISNONTEXT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3155330				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ISTKTEXT\"\>Tests if the cell contents are text or numbers, and returns FALSE if the contents are text.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id5719779				0	en-ZA	If an error occurs, the function returns TRUE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154931				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3148829				0	en-ZA	ISNONTEXT(Value)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3146992				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> is any value or expression where a test is performed to determine whether it is a text or numbers or a Boolean value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150525				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149906				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISNONTEXT(D2)\</item\> returns FALSE if cell D2 contains the text \<item type=\"input\"\>abcdef\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150777				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISNONTEXT(D9)\</item\> returns TRUE if cell D9 contains the number \<item type=\"input\"\>8\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159148				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ISBLANK function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>blank cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>empty cells; recognising\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159148				0	en-ZA	ISBLANK				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3148800	78			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ISTLEER\"\>Returns TRUE if the reference to a cell is blank.\</ahelp\> This function is used to determine if the content of a cell is empty. A cell with a formula inside is not empty. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159162				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3158406				0	en-ZA	ISBLANK(Value)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154212				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> is the content to be tested.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147508				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3147234				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISBLANK(D2)\</item\> returns FALSE as a result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155356				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ISLOGICAL function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number formats;logical\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>logical number formats\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155356				0	en-ZA	ISLOGICAL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3148926				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ISTLOG\"\>Tests for a logical value (TRUE or FALSE).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3541062				0	en-ZA	If an error occurs, the function returns FALSE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149162				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3148918				0	en-ZA	ISLOGICAL(Value)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3146946				0	en-ZA	Returns TRUE if \<emph\>Value\</emph\> is a logical value (TRUE or FALSE), and returns FALSE otherwise.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150709				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3166442				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISLOGICAL(99)\</item\> returns FALSE, because 99 is a number, not a logical value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3556016				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISLOGICAL(ISNA(D4))\</item\> returns TRUE whatever the contents of cell D4, because ISNA() returns a logical value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153685				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ISNA function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>#N/A error;recognising\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153685				0	en-ZA	ISNA				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149105				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ISTNV\"\>Returns TRUE if a cell contains the #N/A (value not available) error value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id6018860				0	en-ZA	If an error occurs, the function returns FALSE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152947				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	en-ZA	ISNA(Value)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3152884				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> is the value or expression to be tested.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149964				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154852				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISNA(D3)\</item\> returns FALSE as a result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149426				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ISTEXT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell contents;text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149426				0	en-ZA	ISTEXT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3145368				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ISTTEXT\"\>Returns TRUE if the cell contents refer to text.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id6779686				0	en-ZA	If an error occurs, the function returns FALSE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154332				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3148649				0	en-ZA	ISTEXT(Value)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150417				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> is a value, number, Boolean value, or an error value to be tested.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149239				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3144756				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISTEXT(D9)\</item\> returns TRUE if cell D9 contains the text \<item type=\"input\"\>abcdef\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3148416				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISTEXT(C3)\</item\> returns FALSE if cell C3 contains the number \<item type=\"input\"\>3\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153939				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ISODD_ADD function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153939				0	en-ZA	ISODD_ADD				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153538				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_ISODD\"\>Returns TRUE (1) if the number does not return a whole number when divided by 2.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145601				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149485				0	en-ZA	ISODD_ADD(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153315				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number to be tested.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143274				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154793				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISODD_ADD(5)\</item\> returns 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148688				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ISNUMBER function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell contents;numbers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148688				0	en-ZA	ISNUMBER				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154618				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ISTZAHL\"\>Returns TRUE if the value refers to a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152769				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150595				0	en-ZA	ISNUMBER(Value)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150351				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> is any expression to be tested to determine whether it is a number or text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146793				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3155614				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISNUMBER(C3)\</item\> returns TRUE if the cell C3 contains the number \<item type=\"input\"\>4\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154417				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISNUMBER(C2)\</item\> returns FALSE if the cell C2 contains the text \<item type=\"input\"\>abcdef\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153694				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>N function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153694				0	en-ZA	N				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150405				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_N\"\>Returns the numeric value of the given parameter. Returns 0 if parameter is text, FALSE or #NA.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id9115573				0	en-ZA	If an error occurs, other than #NA, the function returns the error value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145774				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153883				0	en-ZA	N(Value)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3151101				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> is the parameter to be converted into a number. N() returns the numeric value if it can. It returns the logical values TRUE and FALSE as 1 and 0 respectively. It returns text and errors as 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147097				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154117				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=N(123)\</item\> returns 123				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id2337717				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=N(TRUE)\</item\> returns 1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153781				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=N(FALSE)\</item\> returns 0				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154670				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=N("abc")\</item\> returns 0				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3519089				0	en-ZA	=N(1/0) returns #DIV/0!				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156275				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>NA function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>#N/A error;assigning to a cell\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156275				0	en-ZA	NA				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156161				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_NV\"\>Returns the error value #N/A.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147532				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149563				0	en-ZA	NA()				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155128				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154481				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NA()\</item\> converts the contents of the cell into #N/A.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151255				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>TYPE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151255				0	en-ZA	TYPE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3155900				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TYP\"\>Returns the type of value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149992				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3148400				0	en-ZA	TYPE(Value)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150830				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> is a specific value for which the data type is determined. Value 1 = number, value 2 = text, value 4 = Boolean value, value 8 = formula, value 16 = error value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154363				0	en-ZA	Example (see example table above)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153357				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TYPE(C2)\</item\> returns 2 as a result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3148980				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TYPE(D9)\</item\> returns 1 as a result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155509				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>CELL function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell information\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>information on cells\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155509				0	en-ZA	CELL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153196				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZELLE\"\>Returns information on address, formatting or contents of a cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149323				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3147355				0	en-ZA	CELL("InfoType"; Reference)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154716				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>InfoType\</emph\> is the character string that specifies the type of information. The character string is always in English. Upper or lower case is optional.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150636				0	en-ZA	InfoType				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149344				0	en-ZA	Meaning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153266				0	en-ZA	COL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156204				0	en-ZA	Returns the number of the referenced column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150094				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CELL("COL";D2)\</item\> returns 4.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3151276				0	en-ZA	ROW				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3147583				0	en-ZA	Returns the number of the referenced row.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3151222				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CELL("ROW";D2)\</item\> returns 2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3159217				0	en-ZA	SHEET				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3151201				0	en-ZA	Returns the number of the referenced sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149169				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CELL("Sheet";Sheet3.D2)\</item\> returns 3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149431				0	en-ZA	ADDRESS				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156054				0	en-ZA	Returns the absolute address of the referenced cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154136				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CELL("ADDRESS";D2)\</item\> returns $D$2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3159198				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CELL("ADDRESS";Sheet3.D2)\</item\> returns $Sheet3.$D$2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150245				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CELL("ADDRESS";'X:\\dr\\test.sxc'#$Sheet1.D2)\</item\> returns 'file:///X:/dr/test.sxc'#$Sheet1.$D$2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3146811				0	en-ZA	FILENAME				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3151328				0	en-ZA	Returns the file name and the sheet number of the referenced cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3148896				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CELL("FILENAME";D2)\</item\> returns 'file:///X:/dr/own.sxc'#$Sheet1, if the formula in the current document X:\\dr\\own.sxc is located in Sheet1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3155144				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CELL("FILENAME";'X:\\dr\\test.sxc'#$Sheet1.D2)\</item\> returns 'file:///X:/dr/test.sxc'#$Sheet1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3151381				0	en-ZA	COORD				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3151004				0	en-ZA	Returns the complete cell address in Lotus(TM) notation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3159104				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CELL("COORD"; D2)\</item\> returns $A:$D$2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3163720				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CELL("COORD"; Sheet3.D2)\</item\> returns $C:$D$2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3155910				0	en-ZA	CONTENTS				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156041				0	en-ZA	Returns the contents of the referenced cell, without any formatting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3151069				0	en-ZA	TYPE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3155344				0	en-ZA	Returns the type of cell contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3145217				0	en-ZA	b = blank. empty cell				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3155176				0	en-ZA	l = label. Text, result of a formula as text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3147280				0	en-ZA	v = value. Value, result of a formula as a number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156348				0	en-ZA	WIDTH				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154920				0	en-ZA	Returns the width of the referenced column. The unit is the number of zeros (0) that fit into the column in the default text and the default size.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3152355				0	en-ZA	PREFIX				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154230				0	en-ZA	Returns the alignment of the referenced cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3155946				0	en-ZA	' = align left or left-justified				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3147220				0	en-ZA	" = align right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149038				0	en-ZA	^ = centred				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153129				0	en-ZA	\\ = repeating (currently inactive)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154406				0	en-ZA	PROTECT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3145127				0	en-ZA	Returns the status of the cell protection for the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3155794				0	en-ZA	1 = cell is protected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3155072				0	en-ZA	0 = cell is not protected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156178				0	en-ZA	FORMAT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150220				0	en-ZA	Returns a character string that indicates the number format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	en-ZA	, = number with thousands separator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153837				0	en-ZA	F = number without thousands separator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150318				0	en-ZA	C = currency format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153168				0	en-ZA	S = exponential representation, for example, 1.234+E56				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153515				0	en-ZA	P = percentage				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154375				0	en-ZA	In the above formats, the number of decimal places after the decimal separator is given as a number. Example: the number format #,##0.0 returns ,1 and the number format 00.000% returns P3				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150575				0	en-ZA	D1 = MMM-D-YY, MM-D-YY and similar formats				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150589				0	en-ZA	D2 = DD-MM				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3151034				0	en-ZA	D3 = MM-YY				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156371				0	en-ZA	D4 = DD-MM-YYYY HH:MM:SS				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3157881				0	en-ZA	D5 = MM-DD				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3157894				0	en-ZA	D6 = HH:MM:SS AM/PM				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154068				0	en-ZA	D7 = HH:MM AM/PM				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150286				0	en-ZA	D8 = HH:MM:SS				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3145756				0	en-ZA	D9 = HH:MM				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3145768				0	en-ZA	G = All other formats				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153375				0	en-ZA	- (Minus) at the end = negative numbers are formatted in colour				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3155545				0	en-ZA	() (brackets) at the end = there is an opening bracket in the format code				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154594				0	en-ZA	COLOR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3152922				0	en-ZA	Returns 1, if negative values have been formatted in colour, otherwise 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3145563				0	en-ZA	PARENTHESES				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156072				0	en-ZA	Returns 1 if the format code contains an opening bracket (, otherwise 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156090				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Reference\</emph\> (list of options) is the position of the cell to be examined. If \<emph\>Reference\</emph\> is a range, the cell moves to the top left of the range. If \<emph\>Reference\</emph\> is missing, $[officename] Calc uses the position of the cell in which this formula is located. Microsoft Excel uses the reference of the cell in which the cursor is positioned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Column				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155628				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05040000.xhp\" name=\"Column\"\>Column\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148946				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Sets the column width and hides or shows selected columns.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150398				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340200.xhp\" name=\"Width\"\>Width\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145171				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05040200.xhp\" name=\"Optimal Width\"\>Optimal Width\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06990000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Cell Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06990000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153087				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06990000.xhp\" name=\"Cell Contents\"\>Cell Contents\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06990000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	en-ZA	Opens a submenu with commands to calculate tables and activate AutoInput.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	TIMEVALUE 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146755				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>TIMEVALUE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146755				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"timevalue\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_timevalue.xhp\"\>TIMEVALUE\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3148502				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZEITWERT\"\>TIMEVALUE returns the internal time number from a text enclosed by quotes and which may show a possible time entry format.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3150794				0	en-ZA	The internal number indicated as a decimal is the result of the date system used under $[officename] to calculate date entries.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id011920090347118				0	en-ZA	If the text string also includes a year, month, or day, TIMEVALUE only returns the fractional part of the conversion.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150810				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3150823				0	en-ZA	TIMEVALUE("Text")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3152556	165			0	en-ZA	         \<emph\>Text\</emph\> is a valid time expression and must be entered in quotation marks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146815				0	en-ZA	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3146829	167			0	en-ZA	         \<item type=\"input\"\>=TIMEVALUE("4PM")\</item\> returns 0.67. When formatting in time format HH:MM:SS, you then get 16:00:00.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3153632	168			0	en-ZA	         \<item type=\"input\"\>=TIMEVALUE("24:00")\</item\> returns 1. If you use the HH:MM:SS time format, the value is 00:00:00.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Financial Functions Part One				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143284				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>financial functions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>functions; financial functions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Function Wizard; financial\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>amortizations, see also depreciations\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143284				0	en-ZA	Financial Functions Part One				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"finanztext\"\>This category contains the mathematical finance functions of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153366				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>AMORDEGRC function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>depreciations;degressive amortizations\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153366				0	en-ZA	AMORDEGRC				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_AMORDEGRC\"\>Calculates the amount of depreciation for a settlement period as degressive amortization.\</ahelp\> Unlike AMORLINC, a depreciation coefficient that is independent of the depreciable life is used here.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155855				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427				0	en-ZA	AMORDEGRC(Cost; DatePurchased; FirstPeriod; Salvage; Period; Rate; Basis)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3147125	363			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Cost\</emph\> is the acquisition costs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3151074	364			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>DatePurchased\</emph\> is the date of acquisition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3144765	365			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>FirstPeriod \</emph\>is the end date of the first settlement period.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286	366			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Salvage\</emph\> is the salvage value of the capital asset at the end of the depreciable life.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415	367			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Period\</emph\> is the settlement period to be considered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064	368			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the rate of depreciation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153765				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>AMORLINC function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>depreciations;linear amortizations\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153765				0	en-ZA	AMORLINC				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3159264				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_AMORLINC\"\>Calculates the amount of depreciation for a settlement period as linear amortization. If the capital asset is purchased during the settlement period, the proportional amount of depreciation is considered.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150044				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3147363				0	en-ZA	AMORLINC(Cost; DatePurchased; FirstPeriod; Salvage; Period; Rate; Basis)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920	373			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Cost\</emph\> means the acquisition costs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3163807	374			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>DatePurchased\</emph\> is the date of acquisition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488	375			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>FirstPeriod \</emph\>is the end date of the first settlement period.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149530	376			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Salvage\</emph\> is the salvage value of the capital asset at the end of the depreciable life.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148633	377			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Period\</emph\> is the settlement period to be considered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150982	378			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the rate of depreciation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145257				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ACCRINT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145257				0	en-ZA	ACCRINT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151276				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>accrued interests;periodic payments\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3151276				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_ACCRINT\"\>Calculates the accrued interest of a security in the case of periodic payments.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152581				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3159092				0	en-ZA	ACCRINT(Issue; FirstInterest; Settlement; Rate; Par; Frequency; Basis)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150519	339			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Issue\</emph\> is the issue date of the security.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155376	340			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>FirstInterest\</emph\> is the first interest date of the security.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3166431	341			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date at which the interest accrued up until then is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154486	342			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the annual nominal rate of interest (coupon interest rate)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3156445	343			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Par\</emph\> is the par value of the security.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149406	344			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is the number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148699				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148599				0	en-ZA	A security is issued on 2001-02-28. First interest is set for 2001-08-31. The settlement date is 2001-05-01. The Rate is 0.1 or 10% and Par is 1000 currency units. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). The basis is the US method (0). How much interest has accrued?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148840	347			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=ACCRINT("2001-02-28";"2001-08-31";"2001-05-01";0.1;1000;2;0)\</item\> returns 16.94444.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151240				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>ACCRINTM function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>accrued interests;one-off payments\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151240				0	en-ZA	ACCRINTM				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3157981				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_ACCRINTM\"\>Calculates the accrued interest of a security in the case of one-off payment at the settlement date.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159097				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3147074				0	en-ZA	ACCRINTM(Issue; Settlement; Rate; Par; Basis)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3144773	352			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Issue\</emph\> is the issue date of the security.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154956	353			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date at which the interest accrued up until then is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153972	354			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the annual nominal rate of interest (coupon interest rate).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3159204	355			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Par\</emph\> is the par value of the security.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155384				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154541				0	en-ZA	A security is issued on 2001-04-01. The maturity date is set for 2001-06-15. The Rate is 0.1 or 10% and Par is 1000 currency units. The basis of the daily/annual calculation is the daily balance (3). How much interest has accrued?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149128	358			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=ACCRINTM("2001-04-01";"2001-06-15";0.1;1000;3)\</item\> returns 20.54795.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145753				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>RECEIVED function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>amount received for fixed-interest securities\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145753				0	en-ZA	RECEIVED				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150051				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_RECEIVED\"\>Calculates the amount received that is paid for a fixed-interest security at a given point in time.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149385				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145362				0	en-ZA	RECEIVED("Settlement"; "Maturity"; Investment; Discount; Basis)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154654	394			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153011	395			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155525	396			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Investment\</emph\> is the purchase sum.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155760	397			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Discount\</emph\> is the percentage discount on acquisition of the security.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154710				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154735				0	en-ZA	Settlement date: February 15 1999, maturity date: May 15 1999, investment sum: 1000 currency units, discount: 5.75 per cent, basis: Daily balance/360 = 2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146108				0	en-ZA	The amount received on the maturity date is calculated as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3147246	401			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=RECEIVED("1999-02-15";"1999-05-15";1000;0.0575;2)\</item\> returns 1014.420266.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147556				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>PV function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>present values\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>calculating; present values\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147556				0	en-ZA	PV				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153301				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_BW\"\>Returns the present value of an investment resulting from a series of regular payments.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146099				0	en-ZA	Use this function to calculate the amount of money needed to be invested at a fixed rate today, to receive a specific amount, an annuity, over a specified number of periods. You can also determine how much money is to remain after the elapse of the period. Specify as well if the amount is to be paid out at the beginning or at the end of each period.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153334				0	en-ZA	Enter these values either as numbers, expressions or references. If, for example, interest is paid annually at 8%, but you want to use month as your period, enter 8%/12 under \<emph\>Rate\</emph\> and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc with automatically calculate the correct factor.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147407				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150395				0	en-ZA	PV(Rate; NPer; Pmt; FV; Type)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3151341	9			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Rate\</emph\> defines the interest rate per period.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153023	10			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the total number of periods (payment period).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146323	11			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Pmt\</emph\> is the regular payment made per period.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150536	12			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>FV\</emph\> (optional) defines the future value remaining after the final installment has been made.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146883	13			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Type\</emph\> (optional) denotes due date for payments. Type = 1 means due at the beginning of a period and Type = 0 (default) means due at the end of the period.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B13				0	en-ZA	            \<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>         				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150037				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145225				0	en-ZA	What is the present value of an investment, if 500 currency units are paid out monthly and the annual interest rate is 8%? The payment period is 48 months and 20,000 currency units are to remain at the end of the payment period.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907	16			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=PV(8%/12;48;500;20000)\</item\> = -35,019.37 currency units. Under the named conditions, you must deposit 35,019.37 currency units today, if you want to receive 500 currency units per month for 48 months and have 20,000 currency units left over at the end. Cross-checking shows that 48 x 500 currency units + 20,000 currency units = 44,000 currency units. The difference between this amount and the 35,000 currency units deposited represents the interest paid.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149150				0	en-ZA	If you enter references instead of these values into the formula, you can calculate any number of "If-then" scenarios. Please note: references to constants must be defined as absolute references. Examples of this type of application are found under the depreciation functions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152978				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; depreciations\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>SYD function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>depreciations; arithmetic declining\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>arithmetic declining depreciations\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152978				0	en-ZA	SYD				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148732				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DIA\"\>Returns the arithmetic-declining depreciation rate.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149886				0	en-ZA	Use this function to calculate the depreciation amount for one period of the total depreciation span of an object. Arithmetic declining depreciation reduces the depreciation amount from period to period by a fixed sum.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149431				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150483				0	en-ZA	SYD(Cost; Salvage; Life; Period)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146879	24			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Cost\</emph\> is the initial cost of an asset.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3147423	25			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Salvage\</emph\> is the value of an asset after depreciation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3151229	26			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Life\</emph\> is the period fixing the time span over which an asset is depreciated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3147473	27			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Period\</emph\> defines the period for which the depreciation is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148434				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149688				0	en-ZA	A video system initially costing 50,000 currency units is to be depreciated annually for the next 5 years. The salvage value is to be 10,000 currency units. You want to calculate depreciation for the first year.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150900	30			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=SYD(50000;10000;5;1)\</item\>=13,333.33 currency units. The depreciation amount for the first year is 13,333.33 currency units.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146142				0	en-ZA	To have an overview of depreciation rates per period, it is best to define a depreciation table. By entering the different depreciation formulae available in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc next to each other, you can see which depreciation form is the most appropriate. Enter the table as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
