helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155397	406			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148558	407			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153096	408			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Coupon\</emph\> is the annual coupon interest rate (nominal rate of interest)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154594	409			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Yield\</emph\> is the annual yield of the security.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149906	410			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is the number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146995				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148834				0	en-ZA	A security is purchased on 2001-01-01; the maturity date is 2006-01-01. The Coupon rate of interest is 8%. The yield is 9.0%. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) how long is the duration?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154902	413			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=DURATION_ADD("2001-01-01";"2006-01-01";0.08;0.09;2;3)\</item\>         				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159147				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>annual net interest rates\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>calculating; annual net interest rates\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>net annual interest rates\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>EFFECTIVE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159147				0	en-ZA	EFFECTIVE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154204				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_EFFEKTIV\"\>Returns the net annual interest rate for a nominal interest rate.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145417				0	en-ZA	Nominal interest refers to the amount of interest due at the end of a calculation period. Effective interest increases with the number of payments made. In other words, interest is often paid in installments (for example, monthly or quarterly) before the end of the calculation period.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150510				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148805				0	en-ZA	EFFECTIVE(Nom; P)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149768	93			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Nom\</emph\> is the nominal interest.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149334	94			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>P\</emph\> is the number of interest payment periods per year.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154223				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3144499				0	en-ZA	If the annual nominal interest rate is 9.75% and four interest calculation periods are defined, what is the actual interest rate (effective rate)?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150772	97			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=EFFECTIVE(9.75%;4)\</item\> = 10.11% The annual effective rate is therefore 10.11%.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147241				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>effective interest rates\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>EFFECT_ADD function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147241				0	en-ZA	EFFECT_ADD				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3147524				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_EFFECT\"\>Calculates the effective annual rate of interest on the basis of the nominal interest rate and the number of interest payments per annum.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155118				0	en-ZA	EFFECT_ADD(NominalRate; NPerY)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148907	418			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>NominalRate\</emph\> is the annual nominal rate of interest.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154274	419			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>NPerY \</emph\>is the number of interest payments per year.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149156				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3158426				0	en-ZA	What is the effective annual rate of interest for a 5.25% nominal rate and quarterly payment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148927	422			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=EFFECT_ADD(0.0525;4)\</item\> returns 0.053543 or 5.3543%.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149998				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; arithmetic-degressive depreciations\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>arithmetic-degressive depreciations\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>depreciations;arithmetic-degressive\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>DDB function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149998				0	en-ZA	DDB				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3159190				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_GDA\"\>Returns the depreciation of an asset for a specified period using the arithmetic-declining method.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152361				0	en-ZA	Use this form of depreciation if you require a higher initial depreciation value as opposed to linear depreciation. The depreciation value gets less with each period and is usually used for assets whose value loss is higher shortly after purchase (for example, vehicles, computers). Please note that the book value will never reach zero under this calculation type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156038				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3166452				0	en-ZA	DDB(Cost; Salvage; Life; Period; Factor)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153237	104			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Cost\</emph\> fixes the initial cost of an asset.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149787	105			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Salvage\</emph\> fixes the value of an asset at the end of its life.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152945	106			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Life\</emph\> is the number of periods (for example, years or months) defining how long the asset is to be used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149736	107			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Period\</emph\> states the period for which the value is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150243	108			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Factor\</emph\> (optional) is the factor by which depreciation decreases. If a value is not entered, the default is factor 2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159274				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152882				0	en-ZA	A computer system with an initial cost of 75,000 currency units is to be depreciated monthly over 5 years. The value at the end of the depreciation is to be 1 currency unit. The factor is 2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154106	111			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=DDB(75000;1;60;12;2) \</item\>= 1,721.81 currency units. Therefore, the double-declining depreciation in the twelfth month after purchase is 1,721.81 currency units.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149962				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; geometric-degressive depreciations\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>geometric-degressive depreciations\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>depreciations;geometric-degressive\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>DB function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149962				0	en-ZA	DB				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148989				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_GDA2\"\>Returns the depreciation of an asset for a specified period using the double-declining balance method.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3156213				0	en-ZA	This form of depreciation is used if you want to get a higher depreciation value at the beginning of the depreciation (as opposed to linear depreciation). The depreciation value is reduced with every depreciation period by the depreciation already deducted from the initial cost.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149807				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153349				0	en-ZA	DB(Cost; Salvage; Life; Period; Month)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148462	118			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Cost\</emph\> is the initial cost of an asset.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148658	119			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Salvage\</emph\> is the value of an asset at the end of the depreciation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145371	120			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Life\</emph\> defines the period over which an asset is depreciated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154608	121			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Period\</emph\> is the length of each period. The length must be entered in the same date unit as the depreciation period.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150829	122			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Month\</emph\> (optional) denotes the number of months for the first year of depreciation. If an entry is not defined, 12 is used as the default.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151130				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3156147				0	en-ZA	A computer system with an initial cost of 25,000 currency units is to be depreciated over a three year period. The salvage value is to be 1,000 currency units. One period is 30 days.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149513	125			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=DB(25000;1000;36;1;6)\</item\> = 1,075.00 currency units				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3159242				0	en-ZA	The fixed-declining depreciation of the computer system is 1,075.00 currency units.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153948				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>IRR function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>calculating;internal rates of return, regular payments\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>internal rates of return;regular payments\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153948				0	en-ZA	IRR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3143282				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_IKV\"\>Calculates the internal rate of return for an investment.\</ahelp\> The values represent cash flow values at regular intervals, at least one value must be negative (payments), and at least one value must be positive (income).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150599				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155427				0	en-ZA	IRR(Values; Guess)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3144758	132			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Values\</emph\> represents an array containing the values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233	133			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Guess\</emph\> (optional) is the estimated value. An iterative method is used to calculate the internal rate of return. If you can provide only few values, you should provide an initial guess to enable the iteration.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151258				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150630				0	en-ZA	Under the assumption that cell contents are A1=\<item type=\"input\"\>-10000\</item\>, A2=\<item type=\"input\"\>3500\</item\>, A3=\<item type=\"input\"\>7600\</item\> and A4=\<item type=\"input\"\>1000\</item\>, the formula \<item type=\"input\"\>=IRR(A1:A4)\</item\> gives a result of 11,33%.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151012				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; interests for unchanged amortization installments\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>interests for unchanged amortization installments\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>ISPMT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151012				0	en-ZA	ISPMT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148693				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ISPMT\"\>Calculates the level of interest for unchanged amortization installments.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154661				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146070				0	en-ZA	ISPMT(Rate; Period; TotalPeriods; Invest)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672	318			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Rate\</emph\> sets the periodic interest rate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145777	319			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Period\</emph\> is the number of installments for calculation of interest.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153678	320			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>TotalPeriods\</emph\> is the total number of installment periods.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3159390	321			0	en-ZA	            \<emph\>Invest\</emph\> is the amount of the investment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156162				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149558				0	en-ZA	For a credit amount of 120,000 currency units with a two-year term and monthly installments, at a yearly interest rate of 12% the level of interest after 1.5 years is required.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150949	324			0	en-ZA	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=ISPMT(1%;18;24;120000)\</item\> = -300 currency units. The monthly interest after 1.5 years amounts to 300 currency units.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146812				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060119.xhp\" name=\"Forward to Financial Functions Part Two\"\>Financial Functions Part Two\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154411				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060118.xhp\" name=\"Forward to Financial Functions Part Three\"\>Financial Functions Part Three\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_minute.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	MINUTE 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_minute.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149803				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>MINUTE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_minute.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149803				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"minute\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_minute.xhp\"\>MINUTE\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_minute.xhp	0	help	par_id3148988				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MINUTE\"\>Calculates the minute for an internal time value.\</ahelp\> The minute is returned as a number between 0 and 59.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_minute.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154343				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_minute.xhp	0	help	par_id3148660				0	en-ZA	MINUTE(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_minute.xhp	0	help	par_id3154611				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number\</emph\>, as a time value, is a decimal number where the number of the minute is to be returned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_minute.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145374				0	en-ZA	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_minute.xhp	0	help	par_id3148463				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MINUTE(8.999)\</item\> returns 58				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_minute.xhp	0	help	par_id3149419				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MINUTE(8.9999)\</item\> returns 59				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_minute.xhp	0	help	par_id3144755				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MINUTE(NOW())\</item\> returns the current minute value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05020600.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Cell Protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05020600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145119				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05020600.xhp\" name=\"Cell Protection\"\>Cell Protection\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05020600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150398				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCPAGE_PROTECTION\"\>Defines protection options for selected cells.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05020600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150447				0	en-ZA	Protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05020600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125864				0	en-ZA	Hide all				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05020600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:TRISTATEBOX:RID_SCPAGE_PROTECTION:BTN_HIDE_ALL\"\>Hides formulae and contents of the selected cells.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05020600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153190				0	en-ZA	Protected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05020600.xhp	0	help	par_id3151119				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:TRISTATEBOX:RID_SCPAGE_PROTECTION:BTN_PROTECTED\"\>Prevents the selected cells from being modified.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05020600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	en-ZA	This cell protection only takes effect if you also protect the sheet (\<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05020600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149377				0	en-ZA	Hide formula				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05020600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:TRISTATEBOX:RID_SCPAGE_PROTECTION:BTN_HIDE_FORMULAR\"\>Hides formulae in the selected cells.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05020600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155602				0	en-ZA	Print				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05020600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153836				0	en-ZA	Defines print options for the sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05020600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155065				0	en-ZA	Hide when printing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05020600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:TRISTATEBOX:RID_SCPAGE_PROTECTION:BTN_HIDE_PRINT\"\>Keeps the selected cells from being printed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150542				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>pages; order when printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing; page order\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156329				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05070500.xhp\" name=\"Sheet\"\>Sheet\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCPAGE_TABLE\"\>Specifies the elements to be included in the printout of all sheets with the current Page Style. Additionally, you can set the print order, the first page number, and the page scale.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150542				0	en-ZA	Print				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863				0	en-ZA	Defines which elements of the spreadsheet are to be printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151041				0	en-ZA	Column and row headers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_HEADER\"\>Specifies whether you want the column and row headers to be printed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150439				0	en-ZA	Grid				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147436				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_GRID\"\>Prints out the borders of the individual cells as a grid.\</ahelp\> For the view on screen, make your choice under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"View\"\>\<emph\>View\</emph\>\</link\> - \<emph\>Grid lines\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145750				0	en-ZA	Comments				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_NOTES\"\>Prints the comments defined in your spreadsheet.\</ahelp\> They will be printed on a separate page, along with the corresponding cell reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154944				0	en-ZA	Objects/graphics				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149581				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_OBJECTS\"\>Includes all inserted objects (if printable) and graphics with the printed document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149377				0	en-ZA	Charts				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148455				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_CHARTS\"\>Prints the charts that have been inserted into your spreadsheet.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153418				0	en-ZA	Drawing Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149122				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_DRAWINGS\"\>Includes all drawing objects in the printed document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150330				0	en-ZA	Formulas				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153715				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_FORMULAS\"\>Prints the formulae contained in the cells, instead of the results.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156385				0	en-ZA	Zero Values				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149258				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_NULLVALS\"\>Specifies that cells with a zero value are printed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154022				0	en-ZA	Page Order				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3166423				0	en-ZA	Defines the order in which data in a sheet is numbered and printed when it does not fit on one printed page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152580				0	en-ZA	Top to bottom, then right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150205				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_TOPDOWN\"\>Prints vertically from the left column to the bottom of the sheet.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150786				0	en-ZA	Left to right, then down				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154657				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_LEFTRIGHT\"\>Prints horizontally from the top row of the sheet to the right column.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150887				0	en-ZA	First page number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3155378				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_PAGENO\"\>Select this option if you want the first page to start with a number other than 1.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3145389				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:NUMERICFIELD:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:ED_PAGENO\"\>Enter the number of the first page.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146978				0	en-ZA	Scale				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149408				0	en-ZA	Defines a page scale for the printed spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN1096D				0	en-ZA	Scaling mode				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN10971				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:ListBox:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:LB_SCALEMODE\"\>Select a scaling mode from the list box. Appropriate controls will be shown at the side of the list box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155089				0	en-ZA	Reduce/enlarge printout				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3159171				0	en-ZA	Specifies a scaling factor to scale all printed pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN1099A				0	en-ZA	Scaling factor				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3152899				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_METRICFIELD_RID_SCPAGE_TABLE_ED_SCALEALL\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a scaling factor. Factors less than 100 reduce the pages, higher factors enlarge the pages.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109B2				0	en-ZA	Fit print range(s) to width/height				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109B5				0	en-ZA	Specifies the maximum number of pages horizontally (width) and vertically (height) on which every sheet with the current Page Style is to be printed. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109BB				0	en-ZA	The print ranges are always scaled proportionally, so the resulting number of pages may be less than specified.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109BF				0	en-ZA	You may clear one of the boxes, then the unspecified dimension will use as many pages as necessary.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109C3				0	en-ZA	If you clear both boxes, this will result in a scaling factor of 100%.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109CE				0	en-ZA	Width in pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109D1				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:NumericField:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:ED_SCALEPAGEWIDTH\"\>Enter the maximum number of pages to be printed horizontally across.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E8				0	en-ZA	Height in pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109EB				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:NumericField:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:ED_SCALEPAGEHEIGHT\"\>Enter the maximum number of pages to be printed vertically stacked.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148868				0	en-ZA	Fit print range(s) on number of pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3145074				0	en-ZA	Specifies the maximum number of pages on which every sheet with the current Page Style is to be printed. The scale will be reduced as necessary to fit the defined number of pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A26				0	en-ZA	Number of pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3144507				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:NUMERICFIELD:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:ED_SCALEPAGENUM\"\>Enter the maximum number of pages to be printed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Print Ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154013				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080000.xhp\" name=\"Print Ranges\"\>Print Ranges\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Manages print ranges. Only cells within the print ranges will be printed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	en-ZA	If you do not define any print range manually, Calc assigns an automatic print range to include all the cells that are not empty.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154729				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\" name=\"Edit\"\>Edit\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Deleting Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143284				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>deleting; cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; deleting contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; deleting cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell contents; deleting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143284				0	en-ZA	Deleting Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"inhalteloeschentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Delete\"\>Specifies the contents to be deleted from the active cell or from a selected cell range.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> If several sheets are selected, all selected sheets will be affected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159154				0	en-ZA	This dialogue is also called by pressing Del after the cell cursor has been activated on the sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145367				0	en-ZA	Pressing Backspace deletes content without calling the dialogue or changing formats.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	en-ZA	Use \<emph\>Cut\</emph\> on the Standard bar to delete contents and formats without the dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148575				0	en-ZA	Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149665				0	en-ZA	This area lists the options for deleting contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146975				0	en-ZA	Delete All				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCDLG_DELCONT_BTN_DELALL\"\>Deletes all content from the selected cell range.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156286				0	en-ZA	Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154015				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCDLG_DELCONT_BTN_DELSTRINGS\"\>Deletes text only. Formats, formulae, numbers and dates are not affected.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153840				0	en-ZA	Numbers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148405				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCDLG_DELCONT_BTN_DELNUMBERS\"\>Deletes numbers only. Formats and formulae remain unchanged.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155764				0	en-ZA	Date & time				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149567				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCDLG_DELCONT_BTN_DELDATETIME\"\>Deletes date and time values. Formats, text, numbers and formulae remain unchanged.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154703				0	en-ZA	Formulas				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCDLG_DELCONT_BTN_DELFORMULAS\"\>Deletes formulae. Text, numbers, formats, dates and times remain unchanged.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150300				0	en-ZA	Comments				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154658				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCDLG_DELCONT_BTN_DELNOTES\"\>Deletes comments added to cells. All other elements remain unchanged.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155112				0	en-ZA	Formats				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146134				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCDLG_DELCONT_BTN_DELATTRS\"\>Deletes format attributes applied to cells. All cell content remains unchanged.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150088				0	en-ZA	Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02150000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCDLG_DELCONT_BTN_DELOBJECTS\"\>Deletes objects. All cell content remains unchanged.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
