helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Function List				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04080000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154126				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>formula list window\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>function list window\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting functions; function list window\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154126				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04080000.xhp\" name=\"Function List\"\>Function List\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151118				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"funktionslistetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_FUNCTIONLIST\"\>This command opens the \<emph\>Function List\</emph\> window, which displays all functions that can be inserted into your document.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> The \<emph\>Function List\</emph\> window is similar to the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> tab page of the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"Function Wizard\"\>Function Wizard\</link\>. The functions are inserted with placeholders to be replaced with your own values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Function List\</emph\> window is a resizable \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#andocken\" name=\"dockable window\"\>dockable window\</link\>. Use it to quickly enter functions in the spreadsheet. By double-clicking an entry in the functions list, the respective function is directly inserted with all parameters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145799				0	en-ZA	Category List				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153160				0	en-ZA	Function List				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149412				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:FID_FUNCTION_BOX:LB_FUNC\"\>Displays the available functions.\</ahelp\> When you select a function, the area below the list box displays a short description. To insert the selected function double-click it or click the \<emph\>Insert Function into calculation sheet\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146971				0	en-ZA	Insert Function into calculation sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150043				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3159267\" src=\"sc/res/fx.png\" width=\"0.1945inch\" height=\"0.1945inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159267\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:IMAGEBUTTON:FID_FUNCTION_BOX:IMB_INSERT\"\>Inserts the selected function into the document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030900.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Refresh Traces				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030900.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152349				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>cells; refreshing traces\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>traces; refreshing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;traces\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152349				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030900.xhp\" name=\"Refresh Traces\"\>Refresh Traces\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030900.xhp	0	help	par_id3148947				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:RefreshArrows\"\>Redraws all traces in the sheet. Formulas modified when traces are redrawn are taken into account.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030900.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	en-ZA	Detective arrows in the document are updated under the following circumstances:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030900.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	en-ZA	Starting \<emph\>Tools - Detective - Update Refresh Traces\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030900.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	en-ZA	If \<emph\>Tools - Detective - Update Automatically\</emph\> is turned on, every time formulae are changed in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eomonth.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	EOMONTH				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eomonth.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150991				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>EOMONTH function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eomonth.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150991				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"eomonth\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_eomonth.xhp\"\>EOMONTH\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eomonth.xhp	0	help	par_id3152766	232			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_EOMONTH\"\>Returns the date of the last day of a month which falls m\<emph\>onths\</emph\> away from the s\<emph\>tart date\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eomonth.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150597				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eomonth.xhp	0	help	par_id3150351				0	en-ZA	EOMONTH(StartDate; Months)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eomonth.xhp	0	help	par_id3146787				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>StartDate\</emph\> is a date (the starting point of the calculation).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eomonth.xhp	0	help	par_id3155615				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Months\</emph\> is the number of months before (negative) or after (positive) the start date.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eomonth.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156335				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eomonth.xhp	0	help	par_id3154829				0	en-ZA	What is the last day of the month that falls 6 months after September 14 2001?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eomonth.xhp	0	help	par_id3156143				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=EOMONTH(DATE(2001;9;14);6)\</item\> returns the serial number 37346. Formatted as a date, this is 2002-03-31.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eomonth.xhp	0	help	par_id3156144				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"input\"\>=EOMONTH("2001-09-14";6)\</item\> works as well. If the date is given as string, it has to be in ISO format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\07080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Split				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\07080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163800				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07080000.xhp\" name=\"Split\"\>Split\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\07080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SplitWindow\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Divides the current window at the top left corner of the active cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\07080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154910				0	en-ZA	You can also use the mouse to split the window horizontally or vertically. To do this, drag the thick black line located directly above the vertical scrollbar or directly to the right of the horizontal scrollbar into the window. A thick black line will show where the window is split.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\07080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149263				0	en-ZA	A split window has its own scrollbars in each partial section; by contrast, \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07090000.xhp\" name=\"fixed window sections\"\>fixed window sections\</link\> are not scrollable.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
