helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Handling of Empty Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146799				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>empty cells;handling of\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id1502121				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"empty_cells\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/05/empty_cells.xhp\"\>Handling of Empty Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id8266853				0	en-ZA	In older versions of the software, empty cells were forced to numeric 0 in some contexts and to empty string in others, except in direct comparison where =A1=0 and =A1="" both resulted in TRUE if A1 was empty. Emptiness now is inherited until used, so both =VLOOKUP(...)=0 and =VLOOKUP(...)="" give TRUE if the lookup resulted in an empty cell being returned. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id2733542				0	en-ZA	A simple reference to an empty cell is still displayed as numeric 0 but is not necessarily of type numeric anymore, so also comparisons with the referencing cell work as expected. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4238715				0	en-ZA	For the following examples, A1 contains a number, B1 is empty, C1 contains the reference to B1:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id8277230				0	en-ZA	A1: 1 B1: <empty> C1: =B1 (displays 0)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4086428				0	en-ZA	=B1=0 => TRUE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id9024628				0	en-ZA	=B1="" => TRUE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3067110				0	en-ZA	=C1=0 => TRUE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id8841822				0	en-ZA	=C1="" => TRUE (previously was FALSE)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4077578				0	en-ZA	=ISNUMBER(B1) => FALSE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id9094515				0	en-ZA	=ISNUMBER(C1) => FALSE (previously was TRUE)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id396740				0	en-ZA	=ISNUMBER(VLOOKUP(1;A1:C1;2)) => FALSE (B1)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3859675				0	en-ZA	=ISNUMBER(VLOOKUP(1;A1:C1;3)) => FALSE (C1, previously was TRUE)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id402233				0	en-ZA	=ISTEXT(B1) => FALSE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id1623889				0	en-ZA	=ISTEXT(C1) => FALSE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id7781914				0	en-ZA	=ISTEXT(VLOOKUP(1;A1:C1;2)) => FALSE (B1, previously was TRUE)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id300912				0	en-ZA	=ISTEXT(VLOOKUP(1;A1:C1;3)) => FALSE (C1)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id9534592				0	en-ZA	=ISBLANK(B1) => TRUE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4969328				0	en-ZA	=ISBLANK(C1) => FALSE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id9635914				0	en-ZA	=ISBLANK(VLOOKUP(1;A1:C1;2)) => TRUE (B1, previously was FALSE)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id2476577				0	en-ZA	=ISBLANK(VLOOKUP(1;A1:C1;3)) => FALSE (C1)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4217047				0	en-ZA	Note that Microsoft Excel behaves different and always returns a number as the result of a reference to an empty cell or a formula cell with the result of an empty cell. For example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id2629474				0	en-ZA	A1: <empty>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id8069704				0	en-ZA	B1: =A1 => displays 0, but is just a reference to an empty cell				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4524674				0	en-ZA	=ISNUMBER(A1) => FALSE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
