helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\00\00000402.xhp	0	help	par_id3153191				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"bzeilum\"\>Choose \<emph\>Edit - Delete Manual Break - Row Break\</emph\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\00\00000402.xhp	0	help	par_id3145645				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"bspaum\"\>Choose \<emph\>Edit - Delete Manual Break - Column Break\</emph\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Consolidating Data				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>consolidating data\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>ranges; combining\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>combining;cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; combining\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>data; merging cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>merging;data ranges\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"consolidate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/consolidate.xhp\" name=\"Consolidating Data\"\>Consolidating Data\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153191				0	en-ZA	During consolidation, the contents of the cells from several sheets will be combined in one place.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	hd_id892056				0	en-ZA	To Combine Cell Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	en-ZA	Open the document that contains the cell ranges to be consolidated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154513				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Consolidate\</item\> to open the \<emph\>Consolidate\</emph\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	en-ZA	From the \<emph\>Source data area\</emph\> box select a source cell range to consolidate with other areas.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149209				0	en-ZA	If the range is not named, click in the field next to the \<emph\>Source data area\</emph\>. A blinking text cursor appears. Type a reference for the first source data range or select the range with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> to insert the selected range in the \<emph\>Consolidation areas\</emph\> field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153816				0	en-ZA	Select additional ranges and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> after each selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3157983				0	en-ZA	Specify where you want to display the result by selecting a target range from the \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150215				0	en-ZA	If the target range is not named, click in the field next to \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> and enter the reference of the target range. Alternatively, you can select the range using the mouse or position the cursor in the top left cell of the target range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153813				0	en-ZA	Select a function from the \<emph\>Function\</emph\> box. The function specifies how the values of the consolidation ranges are linked. The "Sum" function is the default setting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149315				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to consolidate the ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DE				0	en-ZA	Additional Settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147250				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>More\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Consolidate\</emph\> dialogue to display additional settings:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3156400				0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>Link to source data\</emph\> to insert the formulae that generate the results in the target range, rather than the actual results. If you link the data, any values modified in the source range are automatically updated in the target range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150538				0	en-ZA	The corresponding cell references in the target range are inserted in consecutive rows, which are automatically ordered and then hidden from view. Only the final result, based on the selected function, is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149945				0	en-ZA	Under \<emph\>Consolidate by\</emph\>, select either \<emph\>Row labels\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column labels\</emph\> if the cells of the source data range are not to be consolidated corresponding to the identical position of the cell in the range, but instead according to a matching row label or column label.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871				0	en-ZA	To consolidate by row labels or column labels, the label must be contained in the selected source ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150478				0	en-ZA	The text in the labels must be identical, so that rows or columns can be accurately matched. If the row or column label does not match any that exist in the target range, it will be appended as a new row or column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147468				0	en-ZA	The data from the consolidation ranges and target range will be saved when you save the document. If you later open a document in which consolidation has been defined, this data will again be available.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153039				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12070000.xhp\" name=\"Data - Consolidate\"\>Data - Consolidate\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Applying Multiple Operations				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147559				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>multiple operations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>what if operations;two variables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; multiple operations in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data tables; multiple operations in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-classified tables\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147559				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"multioperation\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multioperation.xhp\" name=\"Applying Multiple Operations\"\>Applying Multiple Operations\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145171				0	en-ZA	Multiple Operations in Columns or Rows				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id4123966				0	en-ZA	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Multiple Operations\</item\> command provides a planning tool for "what if" questions. In your spreadsheet, you enter a formula to calculate a result from values that are stored in other cells. Then, you set up a cell range where you enter some fixed values, and the Multiple Operations command will calculate the results depending on the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159153				0	en-ZA	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153189				0	en-ZA	You produce toys which you sell for $10 each. Each toy costs $2 to make, in addition to which you have fixed costs of $10,000 per year. How much profit will you make in a year if you sell a particular number of toys?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id6478774				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id1621753\" src=\"res/helpimg/what-if.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1621753\"\>what-if sheet area\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145239				0	en-ZA	Calculating With One Formula and One Variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3146888				0	en-ZA	To calculate the profit, first enter any number as the quantity (items sold) - in this example 2000. The profit is found from the formula Profit=Quantity * (Selling price - Direct costs) - Fixed costs. Enter this formula in B5.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3157875				0	en-ZA	In column D enter given annual sales, one below the other; for example, 500 to 5000, in steps of 500.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3159115				0	en-ZA	Select the range D2:E11, and thus the values in column D and the empty cells alongside in column E.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149723				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple operations\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149355				0	en-ZA	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> field and click cell B4. This means that B4, the quantity, is the variable in the formula, which is replaced by the selected column values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149009				0	en-ZA	Close the dialogue with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You see the profits for the different quantities in column E.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148725				0	en-ZA	Calculating with Several Formulae Simultaneously				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3146880				0	en-ZA	Delete column E.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154675				0	en-ZA	Enter the following formula in C5: = B5 / B4. You are now calculating the annual profit per item sold.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3148885				0	en-ZA	Select the range D2:F11, thus three columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3147474				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple Operations\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154846				0	en-ZA	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field, select cells B5 thru C5.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153931				0	en-ZA	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> field and click cell B4.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3150862				0	en-ZA	Close the dialogue with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You will now see the profits in column E and the annual profit per item in column F.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146139				0	en-ZA	Multiple Operations Across Rows and Columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149949				0	en-ZA	Calculating with Two Variables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154808				0	en-ZA	Consider columns A and B of the sample table above. You now want to vary not just the quantity produced annually, but also the selling price, and you are interested in the profit in each case.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149731				0	en-ZA	Expand the table shown above. D2 thru D11 contain the numbers 500, 1000 and so on, up to 5000. In E1 through H1 enter the numbers 8, 10, 15 and 20.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3152810				0	en-ZA	Select the range D1:H11.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153620				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple Operations\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	en-ZA	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Row input cell\</emph\> field and click cell B1. This means that B1, the selling price, is the horizontally entered variable (with the values 8, 10, 15 and 20).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154049				0	en-ZA	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> field and click in B4. This means that B4, the quantity, is the vertically entered variable.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149141				0	en-ZA	Close the dialogue with OK. You see the profits for the different selling prices in the range E2:H11.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3155104				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12060000.xhp\" name=\"Multiple operations\"\>Multiple operations\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Applying AutoFilter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156423				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>filters, see also AutoFilter function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoFilter function;applying\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; filter values\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; filter sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns; AutoFilter function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>drop-down menus in sheet columns\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>database ranges; AutoFilter function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"autofilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/autofilter.xhp\" name=\"Applying AutoFilter\"\>Applying AutoFilter\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> function inserts a combo box on one or more data columns that lets you select the records (rows) to be displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	en-ZA	Select the columns you want to use AutoFilter on.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</emph\>. The combo box arrows are visible in the first row of the range selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	en-ZA	Run the filter by clicking the drop-down arrow in the column heading and choosing an item.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	en-ZA	Only those rows whose contents meet the filter criteria are displayed. The other rows are filtered. You can see if rows have been filtered from the discontinuous row numbers. The column that has been used for the filter is identified by a different colour for the arrow button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id9216589				0	en-ZA	When you apply an additional AutoFilter on another column of a filtered data range, then the other combo boxes list only the filtered data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714	12			0	en-ZA	To display all records again, select the "all\<emph\>"\</emph\> entry in the AutoFilter combo box. If you choose "Standard\<emph\>"\</emph\>, the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Standard Filter\</item\> dialogue appears, allowing you to set up a standard filter. Choose "Top 10" to display the highest 10 values only. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147340				0	en-ZA	To stop using AutoFilter, reselect all cells selected in step 1 and once again choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id4303415				0	en-ZA	To assign different AutoFilters to different sheets, you must first define a database range on each sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3159236				0	en-ZA	The arithmetic functions also take account of the cells that are not visible due to an applied filter. For example, a sum of an entire column will also total the values in the filtered cells. Apply the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060106.xhp\" name=\"SUBTOTAL\"\>SUBTOTAL\</link\> function if only the cells visible after the application of a filter are to be taken into account.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12040100.xhp\" name=\"Data - Filter - AutoFilter\"\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060106.xhp\" name=\"SUBTOTAL\"\>SUBTOTAL\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	User Defined Borders in Cells 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	bm_id3457441				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>cells;borders\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>line arrangements with cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>borders;cells\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id4544816				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"borders\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/borders.xhp\"\>User Defined Borders in Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2320017				0	en-ZA	You can apply a variety of different lines to selected cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8055665				0	en-ZA	Select the cell or a block of cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9181188				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9947508				0	en-ZA	In the dialogue, click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7907956				0	en-ZA	Choose the border options you want to apply and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1342204				0	en-ZA	The options in the \<emph\>Line arrangement\</emph\> area can be used to apply multiple border styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id4454481				0	en-ZA	Selection of cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7251503				0	en-ZA	Depending on the selection of cells, the area looks different.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8716696				0	en-ZA	Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4677877				0	en-ZA	Line arrangement area				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id807824				0	en-ZA	One cell				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8473464				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id1737113\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_1.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.5937in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1737113\"\>borders with one cell selected\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id3509933				0	en-ZA	Cells in a column				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6635639				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id1680959\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_2.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.5937in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1680959\"\>borders with a column selected\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8073366				0	en-ZA	Cells in a row				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6054567				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id9623096\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_3.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.5937in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id9623096\"\>borders with a row selected\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id466322				0	en-ZA	Cells in a block of 2x2 or more				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4511551				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id8139591\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_4.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.5937in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id8139591\"\>borders with a block selected\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5383465				0	en-ZA	You cannot apply borders to multiple selections.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id7790154				0	en-ZA	Default Settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2918485				0	en-ZA	Click one of the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> icons to set or reset multiple borders.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1836909				0	en-ZA	The thin grey lines inside an icon show the borders that will be reset or cleared.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5212561				0	en-ZA	The dark lines inside an icon show the lines that will be set using the selected line style and colour.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4818872				0	en-ZA	The thick grey lines inside an icon show the lines that will not be changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id8989226				0	en-ZA	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id622577				0	en-ZA	Select a block of about 8x8 cells, then choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8119754				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id7261268\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_5.png\" width=\"1.0937in\" height=\"0.2189in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7261268\"\>default icon row of Borders tab page\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8964201				0	en-ZA	Click the left icon to clear all lines. This removes all outer borders, all inner lines, and all diagonal lines.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6048463				0	en-ZA	Click the second icon from the left to set an outer border and to remove all other lines.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1495406				0	en-ZA	Click the rightmost icon to set an outer border. The inner lines are not changed, except the diagonal lines, which will be removed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9269386				0	en-ZA	Now you can continue to see which lines the other icons will set or remove.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id3593554				0	en-ZA	User Defined Settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4018066				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>User defined\</emph\> area, you can click to set or remove individual lines. The preview shows lines in three different states. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8004699				0	en-ZA	Repeatedly click an edge or a corner to switch through the three different states.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8037659				0	en-ZA	Line types				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2305978				0	en-ZA	Image				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8716086				0	en-ZA	Meaning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id3978087				0	en-ZA	A black line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4065065				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id9379863\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_7.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id9379863\"\>solid line for user defined border\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6987823				0	en-ZA	A black line sets the corresponding line of the selected cells. The line is shown as a dotted line when you choose the 0.05 pt line style. Double lines are shown when you select a double line style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1209143				0	en-ZA	A grey line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6653340				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id6972563\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_gray.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6972563\"\>grey line for user defined border\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2278817				0	en-ZA	A grey line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will not be changed. No line will be set or removed at this position.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5374919				0	en-ZA	A white line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id52491				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3801080\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_white.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3801080\"\>white line for user defined border\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id372325				0	en-ZA	A white line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will be removed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id7282937				0	en-ZA	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4230780				0	en-ZA	Select a single cell, then choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1712393				0	en-ZA	Click the lower edge to set a very thin line as a lower border. All other lines will be removed from the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5149693				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id9467452\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_6.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id9467452\"\>setting a thin lower border\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5759453				0	en-ZA	Choose a thicker line style and click the lower edge. This sets a thicker line as a lower border.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6342051				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id7431562\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_7.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7431562\"\>setting a thick line as a border\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5775322				0	en-ZA	Click the second \<emph\>Default\</emph\> icon from the left to set all four borders. Then repeatedly click the lower edge until a white line is shown. This removes the lower border.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2882778				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id8155766.00000001\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_8.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id8155766.00000001\"\>removing lower border\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8102053				0	en-ZA	You can combine several line types and styles. The last image shows how to set thick outer borders (the thick black lines), while any diagonal lines inside the cell will not be touched (grey lines).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2102420				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id5380718\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_9.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5380718\"\>advanced example for cell borders\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	19xx/20xx Years				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150439				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>years; 2-digits\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dates; 19xx/20xx\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150439				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"year2000\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/year2000.xhp\" name=\"19xx/20xx Years\"\>19xx/20xx Years\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151116				0	en-ZA	The year in a date entry is often entered as two digits. Internally, the year is managed by $[officename] as four digits, so that in the calculation of the difference from 1/1/99 to 1/1/01, the result will correctly be two years.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	en-ZA	Under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - General\</emph\> you can define the century that is used when you enter a year with only two digits. The default is 1930 to 2029.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	en-ZA	This means that if you enter a date of 1/1/30 or higher, it will be treated internally as 1/1/1930 or higher. All lower two-digit years apply to the 20xx century. So, for example, 1/1/20 is converted into 1/1/2020.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Filter: Applying Advanced Filters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148798				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>filters;defining advanced filters \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>advanced filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining; advanced filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; advanced filters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148798	18			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"specialfilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/specialfilter.xhp\" name=\"Filter: Applying Advanced Filters\"\>Filter: Applying Advanced Filters\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785				0	en-ZA	Copy the column headers of the sheet ranges to be filtered into an empty area of the sheet, and then enter the criteria for the filter in a row beneath the headers. Horizontally arranged data in a row will always be logically connected with AND, and vertically arranged data in a column will always be logically connected with OR.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	en-ZA	Once you have created a filter matrix, select the sheet ranges to be filtered. Open the \<emph\>Advanced Filter\</emph\> dialogue by choosing \<emph\>Data - Filter - Advanced Filter\</emph\>, and define the filter conditions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726	21			0	en-ZA	Then click OK, and you will see that only the rows from the original sheet whose contents have met the search criteria are still visible. All other rows are temporarily hidden and can be made to reappear with the \<emph\>Format - Row - Show \</emph\>command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664	22			0	en-ZA	 \<emph\>Example\</emph\> 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427				0	en-ZA	Load a spreadsheet with a large number of records. We are using a fictional \<emph\>Turnover\</emph\> document, but you can just as easily use any other document. The document has the following layout:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
