helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153566				0	en-ZA	Specify that only rows which either have the value \<item type=\"literal\"\>January\</item\> in the \<emph\>Month\</emph\> cells OR a value of under 160000 in the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> cells will be displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147372				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - Advanced Filter\</emph\>, and then select the range A20:E22. After you click OK, only the filtered rows will be displayed. The other rows will be hidden from view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Cells in Currency Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156329				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>currency formats; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>international currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; currency formats in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>currencies; default currencies\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;currency formats\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156329				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"currency_format\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/currency_format.xhp\" name=\"Cells in Currency Format\"\>Cells in Currency Format\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	en-ZA	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can give numbers any currency format. When you click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Currency\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3150791\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_currencyfield.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150791\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> bar to format a number, the cell is given the default currency format set under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	en-ZA	Exchanging of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc documents can lead to misunderstandings, if your \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc document is loaded by a user who uses a different default currency format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	en-ZA	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can define that a number that you have formatted as "1,234.50 €", still remains in euros in another country and does not become dollars.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3151075				0	en-ZA	You can change the currency format in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format Cells\</item\> dialogue (choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</item\> tab) by two country settings. In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Language\</item\> combo box select the basic setting for decimal and thousands separators. In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list box you can select the currency symbol and its position.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	en-ZA	For example, if the language is set to "Default" and you are using a german locale setting, the currency format will be "1.234,00 €". A point is used before the thousand digits and a comma before the decimal places. If you now select the subordinate currency format "$ English (US)" from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list box , you will get the following format: "$ 1.234,00". As you can see, the separators have remained the same. Only the currency symbol has been changed and converted, but the underlying format of the notation remains the same as in the locale setting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	en-ZA	If, under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Language\</item\>, you convert the cells to "English (US)", the English-language locale setting is also transferred and the default currency format is now "$ 1,234.00".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Numbers\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	User-defined Number Formats				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143268				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>numbers;user-defined formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; user-defined numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number formats; millions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>format codes; user-defined number formats\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143268				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"format_value_userdef\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_value_userdef.xhp\" name=\"User-defined Number Formats\"\>User-defined Number Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400				0	en-ZA	You can define your own number formats to display numbers in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	en-ZA	As an example, to display the number 10,200,000 as 10.2 Million:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	en-ZA	Select the cells to which you want to apply a new, user-defined format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Categories\</emph\> list box select "User-defined".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3148646				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Format code\</emph\> text box enter the following code:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596				0	en-ZA	0.0,, "Million"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	en-ZA	Click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3155417				0	en-ZA	The following table shows the effects of rounding, thousands delimiters (,), decimal delimiters (.) and the placeholders # and 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146971				0	en-ZA	Number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	en-ZA	.#,, "Million"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	en-ZA	0.0,, "Million"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920				0	en-ZA	#,, "Million"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3147344				0	en-ZA	10200000				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3147003				0	en-ZA	10.2 Million				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	en-ZA	10.2 Million				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3155113				0	en-ZA	10 Million				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150369				0	en-ZA	500000				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3145585				0	en-ZA	.5 Million				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3154486				0	en-ZA	0.5 Million				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146114				0	en-ZA	1 Million				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3155810				0	en-ZA	100000000				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	en-ZA	100. Million				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241				0	en-ZA	100.0 Million				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3144771				0	en-ZA	100 Million				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Renaming Sheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150398				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>renaming;sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheet tabs;renaming\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;renaming\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>names; sheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150398				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"rename_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rename_table.xhp\" name=\"Renaming Sheets\"\>Renaming Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	en-ZA	Click the name of the sheet that you want to change.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	en-ZA	Enter a new name for the sheet and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667				0	en-ZA	Alternatively, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option key\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt key\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and click on any sheet name and enter the new name directly.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502833				0	en-ZA	Sheet names can contain almost any character. Some naming restrictions apply when you want to save the spreadsheet to Microsoft Excel format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050283				0	en-ZA	When saving to Microsoft Excel format, the following characters are not allowed in sheet names:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050281				0	en-ZA	colon :				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502897				0	en-ZA	back slash \\				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050299				0	en-ZA	forward slash /				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502913				0	en-ZA	question mark ?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050298				0	en-ZA	asterisk *				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502969				0	en-ZA	left square bracket [				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502910				0	en-ZA	right square bracket ]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502971				0	en-ZA	single quote ' as the first or last character of the name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050307				0	en-ZA	In cell references, a sheet name has to be enclosed in single quotes ' if the name contains other characters than alphanumeric or underscore. A single quote contained within a name has to be escaped by doubling it (two single quotes). For example, you want to reference the cell A1 on a sheet with the following name:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503071				0	en-ZA	This year's sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503054				0	en-ZA	The reference must be enclosed in single quotes, and the one single quote inside the name must be doubled:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503069				0	en-ZA	'This year''s sheet'.A1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155444				0	en-ZA	The name of a sheet is independent of the name of the spreadsheet. You enter the spreadsheet name when you save it for the first time as a file. The document can contain up to 256 individual sheets, which can have different names.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Entering Values				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150868				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>values; inserting in multiple cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;values\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell ranges;selecting for data entries\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>areas, see also cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3405255				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"cell_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_enter.xhp\"\>Entering Values\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7147129				0	en-ZA	Calc can simplify entering data and values into multiple cells. You can change some settings to conform to your preferences.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id5621509				0	en-ZA	To Enter Values Into a Range of Cells Manually				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8200018				0	en-ZA	There are two features that assist you when you enter a block of data manually.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id1867427				0	en-ZA	Area Detection for New Rows				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7908871				0	en-ZA	In the row below a heading row, you can advance from one cell to the next with the Tab key. After you enter the value into the last cell in the current row, press Enter. Calc positions the cursor below the first cell of the current block.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id6196783				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id6473586\" src=\"res/helpimg/area1.png\" width=\"4.8335in\" height=\"1.5937in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6473586\"\>area detection\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8118839				0	en-ZA	In row 3, press Tab to advance from cell B3 to C3, D3, and E3. Then press Enter to advance to B4.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3583788				0	en-ZA	Area Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id2011780				0	en-ZA	Use drag-and-drop to select the area where you want to input values. But start dragging from the last cell of the area and release the mouse button when you have selected the first cell. Now you can start to input values. Always press the Tab key to advance to the next cell. You will not leave the selected area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7044282				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id2811365\" src=\"res/helpimg/area2.png\" width=\"4.8335in\" height=\"1.5937in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2811365\"\>area selection\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3232520				0	en-ZA	Select the area from E7 to B3. Now B3 is waiting for your input. Press Tab to advance to the next cell within the selected area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id8950163				0	en-ZA	To Enter Values to a Range of Cells Automatically				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id633869				0	en-ZA	See \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_series.xhp\"\>Automatically Filling in Data Based on Adjacent Cells\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Rotating Tables (Transposing)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>tables; transposing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>transposing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inverting tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>swapping tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; swap with rows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; swapping with columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; rotating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rotating; tables\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"table_rotate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/table_rotate.xhp\" name=\"Rotating Tables (Transposing)\"\>Rotating Tables (Transposing)\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	en-ZA	In $[officename] Calc, there is a way to "rotate" a spreadsheet so that rows become columns and columns become rows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	en-ZA	Select the cell range that you want to transpose.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153191				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Cut\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	en-ZA	Click the cell that is to be the top left cell in the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste Special\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	en-ZA	In the dialogue, mark \<emph\>Paste all\</emph\> and \<emph\>Transpose\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	en-ZA	If you now click OK the columns and rows are transposed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\" name=\"Paste Special\"\>Paste Special\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Importing and Exporting dBASE Files 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id1226844				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>exporting;spreadsheets to dBASE\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>importing;dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>dBASE import/export\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; importing from/exporting to dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables in databases;importing dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10738				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"dbase_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/dbase_files.xhp\"\>Importing and Exporting dBASE Files\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10756				0	en-ZA	You can open and save data in the dBASE file format (*.dbf file extension) in $[officename] Base or a spreadsheet. In %PRODUCTNAME Base, a dBASE database is a folder that contains files with the .dbf file extension. Each file corresponds to a table in the database. Formulas and formatting are lost when you open and save a dBASE file from %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10759				0	en-ZA	To Import a dBASE File Into a Spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071F				0	en-ZA	Locate the *.dbf file that you want to import. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10768				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10730				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Import dBASE files\</emph\> dialogue opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10777				0	en-ZA	The dBASE file opens as a new Calc spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074E				0	en-ZA	If you want to save the spreadsheet as a dBASE file, do not alter or delete the first row in the imported file. This row contains information that is required by a dBASE database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077A				0	en-ZA	To Import a dBASE File Into a Database Table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076C				0	en-ZA	A %PRODUCTNAME Base database table is actually a link to an existing database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10796				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - New - Database\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10786				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> dialogue, enter a name for the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10792				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079A				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Database type \</emph\>box of the \<emph\>Database Properties\</emph\> dialogue, select "dBASE".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A6				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AE				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B6				0	en-ZA	Locate the directory that contains the dBASE file, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BE				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Create\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F1				0	en-ZA	To Save a Spreadsheet as a dBASE File				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F8				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10800				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> box, select "dBASE file".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F9				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, type a name for the dBASE file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10801				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10808				0	en-ZA	Only the data on the current sheet is exported.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Merging and Splitting Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147240				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>cells; merging/unmerging\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; merging cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell merges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>unmerging cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>merging;cells\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id8005005				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"table_cellmerge\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/table_cellmerge.xhp\" name=\"Merging and Unmerging Cells\"\>Merging and Unmerging Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id8049867				0	en-ZA	You can select adjacent cells, then merge them into a single cell. Conversely, you can take a large cell that has been created by merging single cells, and divide it back into individual cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200913480176				0	en-ZA	When you copy cells into a target range containing merged cells, the target range gets unmerged first, then the copied cells are pasted in. If the copied cells are merged cells, they retain their merge state.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id235602				0	en-ZA	Merging Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id1272927				0	en-ZA	Select the adjacent cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id6424146				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Merge Cells\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id451368				0	en-ZA	Canceling the merging of cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id7116611				0	en-ZA	Place the cursor in the cell to be split.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id9493087				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Merge Cells\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Selecting Multiple Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153361				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>cells; selecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>marking cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>selecting;cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>multiple cells selection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>selection modes in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; selecting ranges\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153361				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"mark_cells\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/mark_cells.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Multiple Cells\"\>Selecting Multiple Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145272				0	en-ZA	Select a rectangular range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149261				0	en-ZA	With the mouse button pressed, drag from one corner to the diagonally opposed corner of the range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151119				0	en-ZA	Mark a single cell				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	en-ZA	Click, then Shift-click the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	en-ZA	Pressing the mouse button, drag a range across two cells, do not release the mouse button, and then drag back to the first cell. Release the mouse button. You can now move the individual cell by drag and drop.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154942				0	en-ZA	Select various dispersed cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id1001200901072060				0	en-ZA	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284				0	en-ZA	Mark at least one cell. Then while pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, click each of the additional cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id1001200901072023				0	en-ZA	Click the STD / EXT / ADD area in the status bar until it shows ADD. Now click all cells that you want to select.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146971				0	en-ZA	Switch marking mode				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	en-ZA	On the status bar, click the box with the legend STD / EXT / ADD to switch the marking mode:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3159264				0	en-ZA	Field contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155337				0	en-ZA	Effect of clicking the mouse				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568				0	en-ZA	STD				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3148486				0	en-ZA	A mouse click selects the cell you have clicked on. Unmarks all marked cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090				0	en-ZA	EXT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3150305				0	en-ZA	A mouse click marks a rectangular range from the current cell to the cell you clicked. Alternatively, Shift-click a cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3145587				0	en-ZA	ADD				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	en-ZA	A mouse click in a cell adds it to the already marked cells. A mouse click in a marked cell unmarks it. Alternatively, \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>-click the cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3154487				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/main0208.xhp\" name=\"Status bar\"\>Status bar\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Writing Multi-line Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>text in cells; multi-line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; text breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>breaks in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multi-line text in cells\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"text_wrap\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/text_wrap.xhp\" name=\"Writing Multi-line Text\"\>Writing Multi-line Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	en-ZA	Pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter keys inserts a manual line break. This shortcut only works directly in the cell, not in the input line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	en-ZA	If you want the text to automatically break at the right border of the cell, proceed as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	en-ZA	Select all the cells where you want the text to break at the right border.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	en-ZA	In \<emph\>Format - Cells - Alignment\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Wrap text automatically\</emph\> option and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05020000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cell\"\>Format - Cell\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156023				0	en-ZA	Position the cursor within a range of cells containing values, row and column headings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	en-ZA	Drag the desired buttons into one of the four areas.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	en-ZA	If the button is dropped in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area it will be given a caption that also shows the formula that will be used to calculate the data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	en-ZA	By double-clicking on one of the fields in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area you can call up the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	en-ZA	The order of the buttons can be changed at any time by moving them to a different position in the area with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	en-ZA	Remove a button by dragging it back to the area of the other buttons at the right of the dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	en-ZA	To open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialogue, double-click one of the buttons in the \<emph\>Row\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column\</emph\> area. Use the dialogue to select if and to what extent \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> calculates display subtotals.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Referencing a Cell in Another Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147436				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>sheet references\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>references; to cells in other sheets/documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; operating in another document\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents;references\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"cellreferences\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreferences.xhp\" name=\"Referencing Other Sheets\"\>Referencing Other Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id9663075				0	en-ZA	In a sheet cell you can show a reference to a cell in another sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id1879329				0	en-ZA	In the same way, a reference can also be made to a cell from another document provided that this document has already been saved as a file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id7122409				0	en-ZA	To Reference a Cell in the Same Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id2078005				0	en-ZA	Open a new, empty spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id4943693				0	en-ZA	By way of example, enter the following formula in cell A1 of Sheet1:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id9064302				0	en-ZA	               \<item type=\"literal\"\>=Sheet2.A1\</item\>            				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7609790				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Sheet 2\</emph\> tab at the bottom of the spreadsheet. Set the cursor in cell A1 there and enter text or a number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id809961				0	en-ZA	If you switch back to Sheet1, you will see the same content in cell A1 there. If the contents of Sheet2.A1 change, then the contents of Sheet1.A1 also change.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id9209570				0	en-ZA	To Reference a Cell in Another Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5949278				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>, to load an existing spreadsheet document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8001953				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, to open a new spreadsheet document. Set the cursor in the cell where you want to insert the external data and enter an equals sign to indicate that you want to begin a formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8571123				0	en-ZA	Now switch to the document you have just loaded. Click the cell with the data that you want to insert in the new document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8261665				0	en-ZA	Switch back to the new spreadsheet. In the input line you will now see how $[officename] Calc has added the reference to the formula for you. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5888241				0	en-ZA	The reference to a cell of another document contains the name of the other document in single inverted commas, then a hash #, then the name of the sheet of the other document, followed by a point and the name of the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7697683				0	en-ZA	Confirm the formula by clicking the green tick.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7099826				0	en-ZA	If you drag the box in the lower right corner of the active cell to select a range of cells, $[officename] automatically inserts the corresponding references in the adjacent cells. As a result, the sheet name is preceded with a "$" sign to designate it as an absolute reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id674459				0	en-ZA	If you examine the name of the other document in this formula, you will notice that it is written as a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#url\" name=\"URL\"\>URL\</link\>. This means that you can also enter a URL from the Internet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Recognizing Names as Addressing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148797				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>automatic addressing in tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>natural language addressing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulae; using row/column labels\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text in cells; as addressing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>addressing; automatic\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>name recognition on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>row headers;using in formulae\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>column headers;using in formulae\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns; finding labels automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rows; finding labels automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>recognising; column and row labels\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148797				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"address_auto\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/address_auto.xhp\" name=\"Recognizing Names as Addressing\"\>Recognizing Names as Addressing\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	par_id3152597				0	en-ZA	You can use cells with text to refer to the rows or to the columns that contain the cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3154942\" src=\"res/helpimg/names_as_addressing.png\" width=\"2.1291in\" height=\"0.8709in\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154942\"\>Example spreadsheet\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	par_id3154512				0	en-ZA	In the example spreadsheet, you can use the string \<item type=\"literal\"\>'Column One'\</item\> in a formula to refer to the cell range \<item type=\"literal\"\>B3\</item\> to \<item type=\"literal\"\>B5\</item\>, or \<item type=\"literal\"\>'Column Two'\</item\> for the cell range \<item type=\"literal\"\>C2\</item\> to \<item type=\"literal\"\>C5\</item\>. You can also use \<item type=\"literal\"\>'Row One'\</item\> for the cell range \<item type=\"literal\"\>B3\</item\> to \<item type=\"literal\"\>D3\</item\>, or \<item type=\"literal\"\>'Row Two'\</item\> for the cell range \<item type=\"literal\"\>B4\</item\> to \<item type=\"literal\"\>D4\</item\>. The result of a formula that uses a cell name, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>SUM('Column One')\</item\>, is 600.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	en-ZA	This function is active by default. To turn this function off, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Calculate\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Automatically find column and row labels\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	par_id3149210				0	en-ZA	If you want a name to be automatically recognised by Calc, the name must start with a letter and be composed of alphanumeric characters. If you enter the name in the formula yourself, enclose the name in single quotation marks ('). If a single quotation mark appears in a name, you must enter a backslash in front of the quotation mark, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>'Harry\\'s Bar'.\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Defining Background Colours or Background Graphics				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149346				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>backgrounds;cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rows, see also cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns, see also cells\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"background\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/background.xhp\" name=\"Defining Background Colors or Background Graphics\"\>Defining Background Colours or Background Graphics\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id9520249				0	en-ZA	You can define a background colour or use a graphic as a background for cell ranges in $[officename] Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144760				0	en-ZA	Applying a Background Colour to a $[officename] Calc Spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3155429				0	en-ZA	Select the cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> (or \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> from the context menu).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3152938				0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab page, select the background colour.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146974				0	en-ZA	Graphics in the Background of Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3155414				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	en-ZA	Select the graphic and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3153575				0	en-ZA	The graphic is inserted anchored to the current cell. You can move and scale the graphic as you want. In your context menu you can use the \<emph\>Arrange - To Background\</emph\> command to place this in the background. To select a graphic that has been placed in the background, use the \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Navigator\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id51576				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/background.xhp\"\>Watermarks\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3156180				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030600.xhp\" name=\"Background tab page\"\>\<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab page\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id7601245				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_table.xhp\"\>Formatting Spreadsheets\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Changing Row Height or Column Width				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145748				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>heights of cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell heights\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; heights and widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>widths of cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>column widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; heights\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;row heights/column widths\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145748				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"row_height\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/row_height.xhp\" name=\"Changing Row Height or Column Width\"\>Changing Row Height or Column Width\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017				0	en-ZA	You can change the height of the rows with the mouse or through the dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	en-ZA	What is described here for rows and row height applies accordingly for columns and column width.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153963				0	en-ZA	Using the mouse to change the row height or column width				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	en-ZA	Click the area of the headers on the separator below the current row, keep the mouse button pressed and drag up or down in order to change the row height.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3159237				0	en-ZA	Select the optimal row height by double-clicking the separator below the row.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154659				0	en-ZA	Using the dialogue to change the row height or column width				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3150367				0	en-ZA	Click the row so that you achieve the focus.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3166432				0	en-ZA	Start the context menu on the header at the left-hand side.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154487				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340100.xhp\" name=\"Row height\"\>Row height\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3149408				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Optimal row height\"\>Optimal row height\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3153305				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340200.xhp\" name=\"Column width\"\>Column width\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3153815				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05040200.xhp\" name=\"Optimal column width\"\>Optimal column width\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Deactivating Automatic Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149456				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>deactivating; automatic changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; deactivating automatic changes in\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoInput function on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text in cells;AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; AutoInput function of text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>input support in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing; input in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function;cell contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell input;AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lowercase letters;AutoInput function (in cells)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>capital letters;AutoInput function (in cells)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>date formats;avoiding conversion to\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>word completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"auto_off\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/auto_off.xhp\" name=\"Deactivating Automatic Changes\"\>Deactivating Automatic Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	en-ZA	By default, $[officename] automatically corrects many common typing errors and applies formatting while you type. You can immediately undo any automatic changes with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	en-ZA	The following shows you how to deactivate and reactivate the automatic changes in $[officename] Calc:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145748				0	en-ZA	Automatic Text or Number Completion				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730				0	en-ZA	When making an entry in a cell, $[officename] Calc automatically suggests matching input found in the same column. This function is known as \<emph\>AutoInput\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	en-ZA	To turn the AutoInput on and off, set or remove the check mark in front of \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146972				0	en-ZA	Automatic Conversion to Date Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	en-ZA	$[officename] Calc automatically converts certain entries to dates. For example, the entry \<emph\>1.1\</emph\> may be interpreted as January 1 of the current year, according to the locale settings of your operating system, and then displayed according to the date format applied to the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3159267				0	en-ZA	To ensure that an entry is interpreted as text, add an apostrophe at the beginning of the entry. The apostrophe is not displayed in the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150043				0	en-ZA	Quotation Marks Replaced by Custom Quotes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</emph\>. Go to the \<emph\>Localized Options\</emph\> tab and unmark \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149565				0	en-ZA	Cell Content Always Begins With Uppercase				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>. Go to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Options\</item\> tab. Unmark \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Capitalize first letter of every sentence\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150345				0	en-ZA	Replace Word With Another Word				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3166425				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>. Go to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Replace\</item\> tab. Select the word pair and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Delete\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3152992				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\"\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - AutoCorrect\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Applying Filters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153896				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>filters; applying/removing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rows;removing/redisplaying with filters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>removing;filters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"filters\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/filters.xhp\" name=\"Applying Filters\"\>Applying Filters\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	en-ZA	Filters and advanced filters allow you to work on certain filtered rows (records) of a data range. In the spreadsheets in $[officename] there are various possibilities for applying filters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	en-ZA	One use for the \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> function is to quickly restrict the display to records with identical entries in a data field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Standard Filter\</emph\> dialogue, you can also define ranges which contain the values in particular data fields. You can use the standard filter to connect the conditions with either a logical AND or a logical OR operator.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Advanced filter\</emph\> allows up to a total of eight filter conditions. With advanced filters you enter the conditions directly into the sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id9384746				0	en-ZA	To remove a filter, so that you see all cells again, click inside the area where the filter was applied, then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - Remove Filter\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	en-ZA	When you select multiple rows from an area where a filter was applied, then this selection can include rows that are visible and rows that are hidden by the filter. If you then apply formatting, or delete the selected rows, this action then applies only to the visible rows. The hidden rows are not affected. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id218817				0	en-ZA	This is the opposite to rows that you have hidden manually by the \<emph\>Format - Rows - Hide Rows\</emph\> command. Manually hidden rows are deleted when you delete a selection that contains them.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Shortcut Keys (%PRODUCTNAME Calc Accessibility)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145120				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; %PRODUCTNAME Calc shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>shortcut keys;%PRODUCTNAME Calc accessibility\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145120				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Shortcut Keys (%PRODUCTNAME Calc Accessibility)\"\>Shortcut Keys (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc Accessibility)\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	en-ZA	Refer also to the lists of shortcut keys for \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> in general.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153360				0	en-ZA	Cell Selection Mode				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3150439\" src=\"formula/res/refinp1.png\" width=\"0.1327inch\" height=\"0.1327inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150439\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	en-ZA	In a text box that has a button to minimise the dialogue, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F2\</item\> to enter the cell selection mode. Select any number of cells, then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F2\</item\> again to show the dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	en-ZA	In the cell selection mode, you can use the common navigation keys to select cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148646				0	en-ZA	Controlling the Outline				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	en-ZA	You can use the keyboard in \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080000.xhp\" name=\"Outline\"\>Outline\</link\>:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	en-ZA	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+F6\</item\> until the vertical or horizontal outline window has the focus.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> - cycle through all visible buttons from top to bottom or from left to right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> - cycle through all visible buttons in the opposite direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149403				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+1 to Command+8\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+1 to Ctrl+8\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - show all levels up to the specified number; hide all higher levels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	en-ZA	Use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>+\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>-\</item\> to show or hide the focused outline group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446				0	en-ZA	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> to activate the focused button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	en-ZA	Use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Up\</item\>, \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Down\</item\>, \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Left\</item\>, or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Right\</item\> arrow to cycle through all buttons in the current level.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147343				0	en-ZA	Selecting a Drawing Object or a Graphic				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AA				0	en-ZA	Choose View - Toolbars - Drawing to open the Drawing toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	en-ZA	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> until the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150345				0	en-ZA	If the selection tool is active, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter. This selects the first drawing object or graphic in the sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159240				0	en-ZA	With \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 you set the focus to the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155379				0	en-ZA	Now you can use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> to select the next drawing object or graphic and \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> to select the previous one.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Validity of Cell Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156442				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>values; limiting on input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>limits; specifying value limits on input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>permitted cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error messages; defining for incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>actions in case of incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Help tips; defining text for cell input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comments;help text for cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; defining input help\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>macros; running when incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; validity check\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156442				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"validity\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/validity.xhp\" name=\"Validity of Cell Contents\"\>Validity of Cell Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	en-ZA	For each cell, you can define entries to be valid. Invalid entries to a cell will be rejected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	en-ZA	The validity rule is activated when a new value is entered. If an invalid value has already been inserted into the cell, or if you insert a value in the cell either with drag-and-drop or by copying and pasting, the validity rule will not take effect.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id5174718				0	en-ZA	You can choose \<emph\>Tools - Detective\</emph\> at any time and choose the command \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030800.xhp\" name=\"Mark Invalid Data\"\>\<emph\>Mark Invalid Data\</emph\>\</link\> to display which cells contain invalid values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155603				0	en-ZA	Using Cell Contents Validity				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3155959				0	en-ZA	Select the cells for which you want to define a new validity rule.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3148837	8			0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Validity\</item\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156020	9			0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> tab page, enter the conditions for new values entered into cells. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3159208				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Allow\</emph\> field, select an option.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3153011				0	en-ZA	If you select "Whole Numbers", values such as "12.5" are not allowed. Choosing "Date" allows date information both in the local date format as well as in the form of a \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030101.xhp\" name=\"serial date\"\>serial date\</link\>. Similarly, the "Time" condition permits time values such as "12:00" or serial time numbers. "Text Length" stipulates that cells are allowed to contain text only.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id9224829				0	en-ZA	Select "List" to enter a list of valid entries.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149317				0	en-ZA	Select the next condition under \<emph\>Data\</emph\>. According to what you choose, additional options will be selectable.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3151389				0	en-ZA	After you have determined the conditions for cell validity, you can use the other two tab pages to create message boxes:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3159261				0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Input Help\</emph\> tab page, enter the title and the text of the tip, which will then be displayed if the cell is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156396				0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Error Alert\</emph\> tab page, select the action to be carried out in the event of an error.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3147416				0	en-ZA	If you select "Stop" as the action, invalid entries are not accepted, and the previous cell contents are retained.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3150033				0	en-ZA	Select "Warning" or "Information" to display a dialogue in which the entry can either be cancelled or accepted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149947				0	en-ZA	If you select "Macro", then by using the \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> button you can specify a macro to be run in the event of an error.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149011	35			0	en-ZA	To display the error message, select \<emph\>Show error message when invalid values are entered\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3148586				0	en-ZA	After changing the action for a cell on the \<emph\>Error Alert\</emph\> tab page and closing the dialogue with OK, you must first select another cell before the change takes effect.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3154805				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12120000.xhp\" name=\"Data - Validity\"\>Data - Validity\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Using Print Ranges on a Spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	bm_id14648				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>exporting;cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing; cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ranges;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PDF export of print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell ranges; printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>clearing, see also deleting/removing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>extending print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D7				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"printranges\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/printranges.xhp\"\>Defining Print Ranges on a Sheet\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108F5				0	en-ZA	You can define which range of cells on a spreadsheet to print.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FB				0	en-ZA	The cells on the sheet that are not part of the defined print range are not printed or exported. Sheets without a defined print range are not printed and not exported to a PDF file, unless the document uses the Excel file format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077A				0	en-ZA	For files opened in Excel format, all sheets that do not contain a defined print range are printed. The same behaviour occurs when you export the Excel formatted spreadsheet to a PDF file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FE				0	en-ZA	To Define a Print Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10905				0	en-ZA	Select the cells that you want to print.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10909				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Define\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10910				0	en-ZA	To Add Cells to a Print Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10917				0	en-ZA	Select the cells that you want to add to the existing print range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091B				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Add\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10922				0	en-ZA	To Clear a Print Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10929				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Remove\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10953				0	en-ZA	Using the Page Break Preview to Edit Print Ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093E				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, print ranges as well as page break regions are outlined by a blue border and contain a centred page number in grey. Nonprinting areas have a grey background.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143				0	en-ZA	To define a new page break region, drag the border to a new location. When you define a new page break region, an automatic page break is replaced by a manual page break.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10930				0	en-ZA	To View and Edit Print Ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10937				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082A				0	en-ZA	To change the default zoom factor of the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, double click the percentage value on the \<emph\>Status\</emph\> bar, and select a new zoom factor.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10836				0	en-ZA	Edit the print range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10944				0	en-ZA	To change the size of a print range, drag a border of the range to a new location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_id3151075				0	en-ZA	To delete a manual page break that is contained in a print range, drag the border of the page break outside of the print range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10948				0	en-ZA	To clear a print range, drag a border of the range onto the opposite border of the range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10862				0	en-ZA	To exit the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN109CF				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\"\>Editing Print Ranges\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Using Rounded Off Numbers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153361				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>numbers; rounded off\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounded off numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exact numbers in $[officename] Calc\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal places; showing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;number of decimal places\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>values;rounded in calculations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;rounded off values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; decimal places\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>precision as shown\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounding precision\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; values as shown\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156422				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"rounding_numbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rounding_numbers.xhp\" name=\"Using Rounded Off Numbers\"\>Using Rounded Off Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	en-ZA	In $[officename] Calc, all decimal numbers are displayed rounded off to two decimal places.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	en-ZA	To change this for selected cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154321				0	en-ZA	Mark all the cells you want to modify.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> and go to the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> field, select \<emph\>Number\</emph\>. Under \<emph\>Options\</emph\>, change the number of \<emph\>Decimal places\</emph\> and exit the dialogue with OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155415				0	en-ZA	To change this everywhere				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	en-ZA	Go to the \<emph\>Calculate\</emph\> page. Modify the number of \<emph\>Decimal places\</emph\> and exit the dialogue with OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154755				0	en-ZA	To calculate with the rounded off numbers instead of the internal exact values				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150045				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920				0	en-ZA	Go to the \<emph\>Calculate\</emph\> page. Mark the \<emph\>Precision as shown\</emph\> field and exit the dialogue with OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3145790				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Numbers\"\>Numbers\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147005				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060500.xhp\" name=\"Calculate\"\>Calculate\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	References to Other Sheets and Referencing URLs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150441				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>HTML; in sheet cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; URL in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; Internet references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>URL; in Calc\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150441				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"cellreferences_url\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreferences_url.xhp\" name=\"Referencing URLs\"\>Referencing URLs\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id1955626				0	en-ZA	For example, if you found an Internet page containing current stock exchange information in spreadsheet cells, you can load this page in $[officename] Calc by using the following procedure:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3152993				0	en-ZA	In a $[officename] Calc document, position the cursor in the cell into which you want to insert the external data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Link to External Data\</item\>. The \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"External Data\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>External Data\</item\>\</link\> dialogue appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3152892				0	en-ZA	Enter the URL of the document or Web page in the dialogue. The URL must be in the format: http://www.my-bank.com/table.html. The URL for local or local area network files is the path seen in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153068				0	en-ZA	$[officename] loads the Web page or file in the "background", that is, without displaying it. In the large list box of the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>External Data\</item\> dialogue, you can see the name of all the sheets or named ranges you can choose from.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914				0	en-ZA	Select one or more sheets or named ranges. You can also activate the automatic update function every "n" seconds and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3157979				0	en-ZA	The contents will be inserted as a link in the $[officename] Calc document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768				0	en-ZA	Save your spreadsheet. When you open it again later, $[officename] Calc will update the linked cells following an enquiry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3159204				0	en-ZA	Under \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040900.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - General\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - General\</item\>\</link\> you can choose to have the update, when opened, automatically carried out either always, upon request or never. The update can be started manually in the dialogue under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Links\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Highlighting Negative Numbers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147434				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; highlighting negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>highlighting;negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>colours;negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number formats;colours for negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"cellstyle_minusvalue\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp\" name=\"Highlighting Negative Numbers\"\>Highlighting Negative Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	en-ZA	You can format cells with a number format that highlights negative numbers in red. Alternatively, you can define your own number format in which negative numbers are highlighted in other colours.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	en-ZA	Select the cells and choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab, select a number format and mark \<emph\>Negative numbers red\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	en-ZA	The cell number format is defined in two parts. The format for positive numbers and zero is defined in front of the semicolon; after the semicolon the formula for negative numbers is defined. You can change the code (RED) under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format code\</item\>. For example, instead of RED, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>YELLOW\</item\>. If the new code appears in the list after clicking the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Add\</item\> icon, this is a valid entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Copying to Multiple Sheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149456				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>copying;values, to multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;values in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data;inserting in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>sheets; simultaneous multiple filling\</bookmark_value\> 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456	3			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"edit_multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/edit_multitables.xhp\" name=\"Copying to Multiple Sheets\"\>Copying to Multiple Sheets\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	en-ZA	In $[officename] Calc, you can insert values, text or formulae that are simultaneously copied to other selected sheets of your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	en-ZA	Select all desired sheets by holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key and clicking the corresponding register tabs that are still grey at the bottom margin of the workspace. All selected register tabs are now white.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	en-ZA	You can use Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Up or Page Down to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435				0	en-ZA	Now when you insert values, text or formulae into the active sheet, they will also appear in the identical positions in the other selected sheets. For example, data entered in cell A1 of the active sheet is automatically entered into cell A1 of any other seleted sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Referencing Cells by Drag-and-Drop				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154686				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; referencing cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; referencing by drag and drop \</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>references;inserting by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;references, by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154686				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"cellreference_dragdrop\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreference_dragdrop.xhp\" name=\"Referencing Cells by Drag-and-Drop\"\>Referencing Cells by Drag-and-Drop\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3156444				0	en-ZA	With the help of the Navigator you can reference cells from one sheet to another sheet in the same document or in a different document. The cells can be inserted as a copy, link, or hyperlink. The range to be inserted must be defined with a name in the original file so that it can be inserted in the target file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	en-ZA	Open the document that contains the source cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	en-ZA	To set the source range as the range, select the cells and choose \<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>. Save the source document, and do not close it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	en-ZA	Open the sheet in which you want to insert something.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154732				0	en-ZA	Open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\>. In the lower box of the Navigator select the source file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752				0	en-ZA	In the Navigator, the source file object appears under "Range names".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	en-ZA	Using the \<emph\>Drag Mode\</emph\> icon in Navigator, choose whether you want the reference to be a hyperlink, link, or copy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	en-ZA	Click the name under "Range names" in the Navigator, and drag into the cell of the current sheet where you want to insert the reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	en-ZA	This method can also be used to insert a range from another sheet of the same document into the current sheet. Select the active document as source in step 4 above.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Importing and Exporting Text Files				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153726				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>csv files;formulae\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulae; importing/exporting as csv files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>exporting;formulae as csv files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>importing;csv files with formulae\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"csv_formula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/csv_formula.xhp\" name=\"Importing and Exporting Text Files\"\>Importing and Exporting CSV Text Files with Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149402				0	en-ZA	Comma separated values (CSV) files are text files that contain the cell contents of a single sheet. Commas, semicolons, or other characters can be used as the field delimiters between the cells. Text strings are put in quotation marks, numbers are written without quotation marks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715				0	en-ZA	To Import a CSV File				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153709				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155445				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> field, select the format "Text CSV". Select the file and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. When a file has the .csv extension, the file type is automatically recognised.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	en-ZA	You will see the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Import\</item\> dialogue. Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149255				0	en-ZA	If the csv file contains formulae, but you want to import the results of those formulae, then choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154022				0	en-ZA	To Export Formulas and Values as CSV Files				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	en-ZA	Click the sheet to be written as a csv file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3166423				0	en-ZA	If you want to export the formulae as formulae, for example, in the form =SUM(A1:B5), proceed as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155111				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150200				0	en-ZA	Under \<emph\>Display\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	en-ZA	If you want to export the calculation results instead of the formulae, do not mark \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3148702				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Save as\</emph\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153912				0	en-ZA	In the\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File type\</item\> field select the format "Text CSV".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3157978				0	en-ZA	Enter a name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	en-ZA	From the \<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\> dialogue that appears, select the character set and the field and text delimiters for the data to be exported, and confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3146781				0	en-ZA	If the numbers use commas as decimal separators or thousands separators, do not select the comma as the field delimiter. If the text contains double quotation marks, you must select the single quotation mark as separator.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150050				0	en-ZA	If necessary, after you have saved, clear the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box to see the calculated results in the table again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153487				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153008				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000207.xhp\" name=\"Export text files\"\>Export text files\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155595				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000208.xhp\" name=\"Import text files\"\>Import text files\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Unprotecting Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153252				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>cell protection; unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>protecting; unprotecting cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>unprotecting cells\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153252	14			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"cell_unprotect\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_unprotect.xhp\" name=\"Unprotecting Cells\"\>Unprotecting Cells\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3151112				0	en-ZA	Click the sheet for which you want to cancel the protection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document\</emph\>, then choose \<emph\>Sheet\</emph\> or \<emph\>Document\</emph\> to remove the check mark indicating the protected status.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	en-ZA	If you have assigned a password, enter it in this dialogue and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771				0	en-ZA	The cells can now be edited, the formulae can be viewed, and all cells can be printed until you reactivate the protection for the sheet or document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Filtering Cell Ranges 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153541				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>cell ranges;applying/removing filters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>filtering;cell ranges/database ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>database ranges;applying/removing filters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>removing;cell range filters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153541				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"database_filter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_filter.xhp\" name=\"Filtering Cell Ranges\"\>Filtering Cell Ranges\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069				0	en-ZA	You can use several filters to filter cell ranges in spreadsheets. A standard filter uses the options that you specify to filter the data. An AutoFilter filters data according to a specific value or string. An advanced filter uses filter criteria from specified cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	en-ZA	To Apply a Standard Filter to a Cell Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150398				0	en-ZA	Click in a cell range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10693				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - Standard Filter\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Standard Filter\</emph\> dialogue, specify the filter options that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A5				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143				0	en-ZA	The records that match the filter options that you specified are shown.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	en-ZA	To Apply an AutoFilter to a Cell Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	en-ZA	Click in a cell range or a database range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id9303872				0	en-ZA	If you want to apply multiple AutoFilters to the same sheet, you must first define database ranges, then apply the AutoFilters to the database ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DB				0	en-ZA	An arrow button is added to the head of each column in the database range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	en-ZA	Click the arrow button in the column that contains the value or string that you want to set as the filter criteria.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	en-ZA	Select the value or string that you want to use as the filter criteria.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074C				0	en-ZA	The records that match the filter criteria that you selected are shown.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E8				0	en-ZA	To Remove a Filter From a Cell Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075C				0	en-ZA	Click in a filtered cell range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EC				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - Remove Filter\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id4525284				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Defining_a_Data_Range\"\>Wiki page about defining a data range\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Applying Sort Lists				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150870				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>filling;customised lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sort lists;applying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;sort lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>geometric lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arithmetic lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>series;sort lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists; user-defined\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>customised lists\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150870	3			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"sorted_list\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/sorted_list.xhp\" name=\"Applying Sort Lists\"\>Applying Sort Lists\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3159154				0	en-ZA	Sort lists allow you to type one piece of information in a cell, then drag it to fill in a consecutive list of items.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	en-ZA	For example, enter the text "Jan" or "January" in an empty cell. Select the cell and click the mouse on the lower right corner of the cell border. Then drag the selected cell a few cells to the right or downwards. When you release the mouse button, the highlighted cells will be filled with the names of the months.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id2367931				0	en-ZA	Hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>if you do not want to fill the cells with different values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577				0	en-ZA	The predefined series can be found under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists\</emph\>. You can also create your own lists of text strings tailored to your needs, such as a list of your company's branch offices. When you use the information in these lists later (for example, as headings), just enter the first name in the list and expand the entry by dragging it with your mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060400.xhp\" name=\"Sort lists\"\>Sort lists\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Automatically Calculating Series				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150769				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>series; calculating\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>calculating; series\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>linear series\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>growth series\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>date series\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>powers of 2 calculations\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; filling automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic cell filling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoFill function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>filling;cells, automatically\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150769				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"calc_series\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_series.xhp\" name=\"Automatically Calculating Series\"\>Automatically Filling in Data Based on Adjacent Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A8				0	en-ZA	You can automatically fill cells with data with the AutoFill command or the Series command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D3				0	en-ZA	Using AutoFill				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D7				0	en-ZA	AutoFill automatically generates a data series based on a defined pattern.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	en-ZA	On a sheet, click in a cell, and type a number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CB				0	en-ZA	Click in another cell and then click back in the cell where you typed the number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	en-ZA	Drag the fill handle in the bottom right corner of the cell across the cells that you want to fill, and release the mouse button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801				0	en-ZA	The cells are filled with ascending numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EE				0	en-ZA	To quickly create a list of consecutive days, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>Monday\</item\> in a cell, and drag the fill handle.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9720145				0	en-ZA	Hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>if you do not want to fill the cells with different values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	en-ZA	If you select two or more adjacent cells that contain different numbers, and drag, the remaining cells are filled with the arithmetic pattern that is recognised in the numbers. The AutoFill function also recognises customised lists that are defined under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10737				0	en-ZA	You can double-click the fill handle to automatically fill all empty columns of the current data block. For example, first enter Jan into A1 and drag the fill handle down to A12 to get the twelve months in the first column. Now enter some values into B1 and C1. Select those two cells, and double-click the fill handle. This fills automatically the data block B1:C12.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10713				0	en-ZA	Using a Defined Series				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	en-ZA	Select the cell range in the sheet that you want to fill.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Fill - Series\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10716				0	en-ZA	Select the parameters for the series. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	en-ZA	If you select a \<emph\>linear\</emph\> series, the increment that you enter is \<emph\>added\</emph\> to each consecutive number in the series to create the next value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073C				0	en-ZA	If you select a \<emph\>growth\</emph\> series, the increment that you enter is \<emph\>multiplied\</emph\> by each consecutive number to create the next value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10747				0	en-ZA	If you select a \<emph\>date\</emph\> series, the increment that you enter is added to the time unit that you specify.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3159173				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060400.xhp\" name=\"Sort lists\"\>Sort lists\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	 Importing and Exporting CSV Files 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id892361				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>number series import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data series import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; tables as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; tables as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>delimited values and files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comma separated files and values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text file import and export\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>csv files;importing and exporting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; importing/exporting as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents; importing to spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening;text csv files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;as text csv\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10862				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"csv_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/csv_files.xhp\"\>Opening and Saving Text CSV Files\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10880				0	en-ZA	Comma Separated Values (CSV) is a text file format that you can use to exchange data from a database or a spreadsheet between applications. Each line in a Text CSV file represents a record in the database, or a row in a spreadsheet. Each field in a database record or cell in a spreadsheet row is usually separated by a comma. However, you can use other characters to delimit a field, such as a tabulator character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10886				0	en-ZA	If the field or cell contains a comma, the field or cell \<emph\>must\</emph\> be enclosed by single quotes (') or double quotes (").				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10890				0	en-ZA	To Open a Text CSV File in Calc				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10897				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1089F				0	en-ZA	Locate the CSV file that you want to open.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A2				0	en-ZA	If the file has a *.csv extension, select the file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A5				0	en-ZA	If the CSV file has another extension, select the file, and then select "Text CSV" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File type\</item\> box				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082D				0	en-ZA	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Open\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	en-ZA	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Import\</item\> dialogue opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108B1				0	en-ZA	Specify the options to divide the text in the file into columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108BB				0	en-ZA	You can preview the layout of the imported data at the bottom of the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Import\</item\> dialogue. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_id8444166				0	en-ZA	Right-click a column in the preview to set the format or to hide the column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E2				0	en-ZA	Check the text delimiter box that matches the character used as text delimiter in the file. In case of an unlisted delimiter, type the character into the input box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C5				0	en-ZA	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FA				0	en-ZA	To Save a Sheet as a Text CSV File				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FC				0	en-ZA	When you export a spreadsheet to CSV format, only the data on the current sheet is saved. All other information, including formulae and formatting, is lost.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10901				0	en-ZA	Open the Calc sheet that you want to save as a Text CSV file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AF				0	en-ZA	Only the current sheet can be exported.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10905				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Save as\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10915				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File name\</item\> box, enter a name for the file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1090D				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File type\</item\> box, select "Text CSV".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DD				0	en-ZA	(Optional) Set the field options for the Text CSV file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091C				0	en-ZA	Select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit filter settings\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107ED				0	en-ZA	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Export of text files\</item\> dialogue, select the options that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F4				0	en-ZA	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FC				0	en-ZA	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Save\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3153487				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3153008				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000207.xhp\" name=\"Export text files\"\>Export text files\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3155595				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000208.xhp\" name=\"Import text files\"\>Import text files\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Rotating Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151112				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>cells; rotating text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rotating; text in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text in cells; writing vertically\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151112				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"text_rotate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/text_rotate.xhp\" name=\"Rotating Text\"\>Rotating Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	en-ZA	Select the cells whose text you want to rotate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155133				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05020000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells\"\>Format - Cells\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Alignment\"\>Format - Cells - Alignment\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Moving Cells by Drag-and-Drop 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155686				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; moving cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; moving by drag and drop \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns;moving by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;cells by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;cells, by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	hd_id986358				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"move_dragdrop\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/move_dragdrop.xhp\"\>Moving Cells by Drag-and-Drop\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2760093				0	en-ZA	When you drag-and-drop a selection of cells on a Calc sheet, the cells normally overwrite the existing cells in the area where you drop. This is the normal \<emph\>overwrite mode\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9527268				0	en-ZA	When you hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while releasing the mouse button, you enter the \<emph\>insert mode\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id79653				0	en-ZA	In insert mode, the existing cells where you drop will be shifted to the right or to the bottom, and the dropped cells are inserted into the now empty positions without overwriting. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8676717				0	en-ZA	The surrounding box of the moved cells looks different in insert mode. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3968932				0	en-ZA	In overwrite mode you see all four borders around the selected area. In insert mode you see only the left border when target cells will be shifted to the right. You see only the upper border when target cells will be shifted down. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id7399517				0	en-ZA	Whether the target area will be shifted to the right or to the bottom depends on the distance between source and target cells, if you move within the same sheet. It depends on the number of horizontal or vertical cells in the moved area, if you move to a different sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8040406				0	en-ZA	If you move cells in insert mode within the same row (only horizontally), then after insertion of the cells, all cells will be shifted to the left to fill the source area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2586748				0	en-ZA	In both modes, you can hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key, or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys while you release the mouse button to insert a copy or a link, respectively.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5814081				0	en-ZA	Keys pressed while releasing the mouse button				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6581316				0	en-ZA	Result				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9906613				0	en-ZA	No key				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2815637				0	en-ZA	Cells are moved and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells are emptied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6161687				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4278389				0	en-ZA	Cells are copied and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2805566				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5369121				0	en-ZA	Links to the source cells are inserted and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9518723				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2926419				0	en-ZA	Cells are moved and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells are emptied, except if you move within the same rows on the same sheet. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4021423				0	en-ZA	If you move within the same rows on the same sheet, the cells in the target area shift to the right, and then the whole row shifts to fill the source area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2783898				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>keys				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2785119				0	en-ZA	Cells are copied and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells stay as they are.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id584124				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5590990				0	en-ZA	Links to the source cells are inserted and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells stay as they are.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Changing Table Views				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147304				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>row headers; hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>column headers; hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; views\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>views; tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>grids;hiding lines in sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;headers/grid lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;table views\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147304				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"table_view\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/table_view.xhp\" name=\"Changing Table Views\"\>Changing Table Views\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	en-ZA	To hide column and line headers in a table:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	en-ZA	Under the menu item \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc,\</emph\> go to the \<emph\>View\</emph\> tab page. Unmark\<emph\> Column/row headers\</emph\>. Confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3147436				0	en-ZA	To hide grid lines:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	en-ZA	Under the menu item \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\>\<emph\>,\</emph\> go to the \<emph\>View\</emph\> tab page. Unmark \<emph\>Grid lines\</emph\>. Confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Finding and Replacing in Calc				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	bm_id3769341				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>searching, see also finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>finding;formulae/values/text/objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing; cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;multiple cell texts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149204				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"finding\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/finding.xhp\"\>Finding and Replacing in Calc\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9363689				0	en-ZA	In spreadsheet documents you can find words, formulae, and styles. You can navigate from one result to the next, or you can highlight all matching cells at once, then apply another format or replace the cell content by other content.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3610644				0	en-ZA	The Find & Replace dialogue				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2224494				0	en-ZA	Cells can contain text or numbers that were entered directly as in a text document. But cells can also contain text or numbers as the result of a calculation. For example, if a cell contains the formula =1+2 it displays the result 3. You must decide whether to search for the 1 respective 2, or to search the 3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id2423780				0	en-ZA	To find formulae or values				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	en-ZA	You can specify in the Find & Replace dialogue either to find the parts of a formula or the results of a calculation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6394238				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7214270				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2186346				0	en-ZA	Select "Formulas" or "Values" in the \<emph\>Search in\</emph\> list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1331217				0	en-ZA	With "Formulas" you will find all parts of the formulae. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id393993				0	en-ZA	With "Values" you will find the results of the calculations. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	en-ZA	Cell contents can be formatted in different ways. For example, a number can be formatted as a currency, to be displayed with a currency symbol. You see the currency symbol in the cell, but you cannot search for it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id7359233				0	en-ZA	Finding text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6549272				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6529740				0	en-ZA	Enter the text to find in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9121982				0	en-ZA	Either click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3808404				0	en-ZA	When you click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>, Calc will select the next cell that contains your text. You can watch and edit the text, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again to advance to the next found cell. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2394482				0	en-ZA	If you closed the dialogue, you can press a key combination (\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+F) to find the next cell without opening the dialogue. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id631733				0	en-ZA	By default, Calc searches the current sheet. Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\>, then enable \<emph\>Search in all sheets\</emph\> to search through all sheets of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7811822				0	en-ZA	When you click \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>, Calc selects all cells that contain your entry. Now you can for example set all found cells to bold, or apply a Cell Style to all at once.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id8531449				0	en-ZA	The Navigator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9183935				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>View - Navigator\</emph\> to open the Navigator window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id946684				0	en-ZA	The Navigator is the main tool for finding and selecting objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9607226				0	en-ZA	Use the Navigator for inserting objects and links within the same document or from other open documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Inserting External Data in Table (WebQuery)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>HTML WebQuery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ranges; inserting in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>external data; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; inserting external data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>web pages; importing data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>WebQuery filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; external data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data sources; external data\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"webquery\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/webquery.xhp\" name=\"Inserting External Data in Table (WebQuery)\"\>Inserting External Data in Table (WebQuery)\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	en-ZA	With the help of the \<emph\>Web Page Query ($[officename] Calc)\</emph\> import filter, you can insert tables from HTML documents in a Calc spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	en-ZA	You can use the same method to insert ranges defined by name from a Calc or Microsoft Excel spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	en-ZA	The following insert methods are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146976				0	en-ZA	Inserting by Dialogue				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	en-ZA	Set the cell cursor at the cell where the new content will be inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Link to External Data\</emph\>. This opens the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\"\>External Data\</link\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	en-ZA	Enter the URL of the HTML document or the name of the spreadsheet. Press Enter when finished. Click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to open a file selection dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	en-ZA	In the large list box of the dialogue, select the named ranges or tables you want to insert.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	en-ZA	You can also specify that the ranges or tables are updated every n seconds.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	en-ZA	The import filter can create names for cell ranges on the fly. As much formatting as possible is retained, while the filter intentionally does not load any images.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149021				0	en-ZA	Inserting by Navigator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965				0	en-ZA	Open two documents: the $[officename] Calc spreadsheet in which the external data is to be inserted (target document) and the document from which the external data derives (source document).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3150205				0	en-ZA	In the target document open the Navigator.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	en-ZA	In the lower combo box of the Navigator select the source document. The Navigator now shows the range names and database ranges or the tables contained in the source document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3148842	20			0	en-ZA	In the Navigator select the \<emph\>Insert as link\</emph\> drag mode \<image id=\"img_id3152985\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20238.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152985\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3157978				0	en-ZA	Drag the desired external data from the Navigator into the target document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768				0	en-ZA	If you have loaded an HTML document with the \<emph\>Web Page Query\</emph\> filter as the source document, you will find the tables in the Navigator, named continuously from "HTML_table1" onwards, and also two range names that have been created:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3152873				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"literal\"\>HTML_all\</item\> - designates the entire document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149897				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"literal\"\>HTML_tables\</item\> - designates all HTML tables in the document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149126				0	en-ZA	Editing the external data				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3159228				0	en-ZA	Open \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\>. Here you can edit the link to the external data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154650				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"External data dialogue\"\>External data dialogue\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Formatting Spreadsheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154125				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>text in cells; formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds;cells and pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders;cells and pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; formatting options for selected cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>currencies;formats\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154125				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"format_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_table.xhp\" name=\"Designing Spreadsheets\"\>Formatting Spreadsheets\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153912	13			0	en-ZA	Formatting Text in a Spreadsheet 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3144772				0	en-ZA	Select the text you want to format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155268	15			0	en-ZA	Choose the desired text attributes from the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>Bar. You can also choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialogue will appear in which you can choose various text attributes on the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149899				0	en-ZA	Formatting Numbers in a Spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3159226				0	en-ZA	Select the cells containing the numbers you want to format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3150046	18			0	en-ZA	To format numbers in the default currency format or as percentages, use the icons on the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>Bar. For other formats, choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. You can choose from the preset formats or define your own on the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153483				0	en-ZA	Formatting Borders and Backgrounds for Cells and Pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154733				0	en-ZA	You can assign a format to any group of cells by first selecting the cells (for multiple selection, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key when clicking), and then activating the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialogue in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cell\</item\>. In this dialogue, you can select attributes such as shadows and backgrounds.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116				0	en-ZA	To apply formatting attributes to an entire sheet, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>. You can define headers and footers, for example, to appear on each printed page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145389				0	en-ZA	An image that you have loaded with \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Background\</item\> is only visible in print or in the page preview. To display a background image on screen as well, insert the graphic image by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Picture - From File\</item\> and arrange the image behind the cells by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Arrange - To Background\</item\>. Use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\> to select the background image.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id2837916				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\"\>Number Formatting Options\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id2614215				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/background.xhp\"\>Backgrounds for Cells\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154684				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>tables; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>title rows; freezing during table split\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>freezing rows or columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers; freezing during table split\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scrolling prevention in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>windows; splitting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; splitting windows\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154684				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"line_fix\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/line_fix.xhp\" name=\"Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers\"\>Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	en-ZA	If you have long rows or columns of data that extend beyond the viewable area of the sheet, you can freeze some rows or columns, which allows you to see the frozen columns or rows as you scroll through the rest of the data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	en-ZA	Select the row below, or the column to the right of the row or column that you want to be in the frozen region. All rows above, or all columns to the left of the selection are frozen.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158				0	en-ZA	To freeze both horizontally and vertically, select the \<emph\>cell\</emph\> that is below the row and to the right of the column that you want to freeze.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Window - Freeze\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073	5			0	en-ZA	To deactivate, choose \<emph\>Window - Freeze \</emph\>again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	en-ZA	If the area defined is to be scrollable, apply the \<emph\>Window - Split\</emph\> command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	en-ZA	If you want to print a certain row on all pages of a document, choose \<emph\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3147004				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07090000.xhp\" name=\"Window - Freeze\"\>Window - Freeze\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07080000.xhp\" name=\"Window - Split\"\>Window - Split\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Print ranges - Edit\"\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Printing Rows or Columns on Every Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151112				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheets on multiple pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing on multiple pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; repeating when printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; repeating when printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>repeating;columns/rows on printed pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>title rows; printing on all sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers; printing on sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footers; printing on sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing; rows/columns as table headings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headings;repeating rows/columns as\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153727				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"print_title_row\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_title_row.xhp\" name=\"Printing Rows or Columns on Every Page\"\>Printing Rows or Columns on Every Page\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014				0	en-ZA	If you have a sheet that is so large that it will be printed multiple pages, you can set up rows or columns to repeat on each printed page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	en-ZA	As an example, If you want to print the top two rows of the sheet as well as the first column (A)on all pages, do the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Edit\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Edit Print Ranges\</emph\> dialogue appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	en-ZA	Click the icon at the far right of the \<emph\>Rows to repeat\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3145800				0	en-ZA	The dialogue shrinks so that you can see more of the sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	en-ZA	Select the first two rows and, for this example, click cell A1 and drag to A2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	en-ZA	In the shrunk dialogue you will see $1:$2. Rows 1 and 2 are now rows to repeat.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	en-ZA	Click the icon at the far right of the \<emph\>Rows to repeat\</emph\> area. The dialogue is restored again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	en-ZA	If you also want column A as a column to repeat, click the icon at the far right of the \<emph\>Columns to repeat\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	en-ZA	Click column A (not in the column header).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704				0	en-ZA	Click the icon again at the far right of the \<emph\>Columns to repeat\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	en-ZA	Rows to repeat are rows from the sheet. You can define headers and footers to be printed on each print page independently of this in \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155380				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154371				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Print ranges - Edit\"\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3146113				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05070000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Page - (Header / Footer)\"\>Format - Page - (Header / Footer)\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Inserting and Editing Comments				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153968				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>comments; on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;comments\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>remarks on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;comments on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>viewing;comments on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>displaying; comments\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153968				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"note_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/note_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Comments\"\>Inserting and Editing Comments\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150440				0	en-ZA	You can assign a comment to each cell by choosing \<link href=\"text/shared/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Comment\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Comment\</emph\>\</link\>. The comment is indicated by a small red square, the comment indicator, in the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	en-ZA	The comment is visible whenever the mouse pointer is over the cell, provided you have activated \<emph\>Help - Tips\</emph\> or - \<emph\>Extended Tips\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	en-ZA	When you select the cell, you can choose \<emph\>Show Comment\</emph\> from the context menu of the cell. Doing so keeps the comment visible until you deactivate the \<emph\>Show Comment\</emph\> command from the same context menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	en-ZA	To edit a permanently visible comment, just click in it. If you delete the entire text of the comment, the comment itself is deleted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN10699				0	en-ZA	Move or resize each comment as you like.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069D				0	en-ZA	Format each comment by specifying background colour, transparency, border style, and text alignment. Choose the commands from the context menu of the comment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	en-ZA	To show or hide the comment indicator, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and mark or unmark the \<emph\>Comment indicator\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	en-ZA	To display a help tip for a selected cell, use \<emph\>Data - Validity - Input Help\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Comment\"\>Insert - Comment\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Converting Text to Numbers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>formats; text as numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>time format conversion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>date formats;conversion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>converting;text, into numbers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id0908200901265171				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"numbers_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/numbers_text.xhp\" name=\"Converting Text to Numbers\"\>Converting Text to Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265127				0	en-ZA	Calc converts text inside cells to the respective numeric values if an unambiguous conversion is possible. If no conversion is possible, Calc returns a #VALUE! error.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265196				0	en-ZA	Only integer numbers including exponent are converted, and ISO 8601 dates and times in their extended formats with separators. Anything else, like fractional numbers with decimal separators or dates other than ISO 8601, is not converted, as the text string would be locale dependent. Leading and trailing blanks are ignored.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265220				0	en-ZA	The following ISO 8601 formats are converted:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265288				0	en-ZA	CCYY-MM-DD				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265267				0	en-ZA	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265248				0	en-ZA	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265374				0	en-ZA	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss,s				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265327				0	en-ZA	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss.s				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265399				0	en-ZA	hh:mm				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265347				0	en-ZA	hh:mm:ss				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265349				0	en-ZA	hh:mm:ss,s				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265342				0	en-ZA	hh:mm:ss.s				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265491				0	en-ZA	The century code CC may not be omitted. Instead of the T date and time separator, exactly one space character may be used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265467				0	en-ZA	If a date is given, it must be a valid Gregorian calendar date. In this case the optional time must be in the range 00:00 to 23:59:59.99999...				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265420				0	en-ZA	If only a time string is given, it may have an hours value of more than 24, while minutes and seconds can have a maximum value of 59.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265448				0	en-ZA	The conversion is done for single arguments only, as in =A1+A2, or ="1E2"+1. Cell range arguments are not affected, so SUM(A1:A2) differs from A1+A2 if at least one of the two cells contain a convertible string.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id090820090126540				0	en-ZA	Strings inside formulae are also converted, such as in ="1999-11-22"+42, which returns the date 42 days after November 22nd, 1999. Calculations involving localised dates as strings inside the formula return an error. For example, the localised date string "11/22/1999" or "22.11.1999" cannot be used for the automatic conversion.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id1005200903485368				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id1005200903485359				0	en-ZA	In A1 enter the text \<item type=\"literal\"\>'1e2\</item\> (which is converted to the number 100 internally).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id1005200903485341				0	en-ZA	In A2 enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>=A1+1\</item\> (which correctly results in 101).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265544				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Numbers\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Selecting Themes for Sheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>theme selection for sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>layout;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell styles; selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;themes for sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;themes for sheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791	6			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"design\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/design.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Themes for Sheets\"\>Selecting Themes for Sheets\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	en-ZA	$[officename] Calc comes with a predefined set of formatting themes that you can apply to your spreadsheets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	en-ZA	It is not possible to add themes to Calc, and they cannot be modified. However, you can modify their styles after you apply them to a spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	en-ZA	Before you format a sheet with a theme, you have to apply at least one custom cell style to the cells on the sheet. You can then change the cell formatting by selecting and applying a theme in the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	en-ZA	To apply a custom cell style to a cell, you can open the Styles and Formatting window and, in its lower list box, set the Custom Styles view. A list of the existing custom defined cell styles will be displayed. Double click a name from the Styles and Formatting window to apply this style to the selected cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	en-ZA	To apply a theme to a spreadsheet:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920	15			0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Choose Themes\</emph\> icon in the \<emph\>Tools\</emph\> bar. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialogue appears. This dialogue lists the available themes for the whole spreadsheet and the Styles and Formatting window lists the custom styles for specific cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114	9			0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Theme Selection \</emph\>dialogue, select the theme that you want to apply to the spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090				0	en-ZA	Click OK				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3150201				0	en-ZA	As soon as you select another theme in the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialogue, some of the properties of the custom style will be applied to the current spreadsheet. The modifications will be immediately visible in your spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3146979				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/02/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Theme selection\"\>Theme selection\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	en-ZA	By dragging the button to a different position in the same row you can alter the order of the columns. If you drag a button to the left edge of the table into the row headings area, you can change a column into a row.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Entering Fractions 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155411				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>fractions; entering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; entering fractions \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;fractions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"fraction_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/fraction_enter.xhp\" name=\"Entering Fractions \"\>Entering Fractions \</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	en-ZA	You can enter a fractional number in a cell and use it for calculation:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155133				0	en-ZA	Enter "0 1/5" in a cell (without the quotation marks) and press the input key. In the input line above the spreadsheet you will see the value 0.2, which is used for the calculation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	en-ZA	If you enter "0 1/2" AutoCorrect causes the three characters 1, / and 2 to be replaced by a single character. The same applies to 1/4 and 3/4. This replacement is defined in \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options - Options\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145367	44			0	en-ZA	If you want to see multi-digit fractions such as "1/10", you must change the cell format to the multi-digit fraction view. Open the context menu of the cell, and choose \<emph\>Format cells. \</emph\>Select "Fraction" from the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> field, and then select "-1234 10/81". You can then enter fractions such as 12/31 or 12/32 - the fractions are, however, automatically reduced, so that in the last example you would see 3/8.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Applying Conditional Formatting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149263				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>conditional formatting; cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; conditional formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; conditional formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles;conditional styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell formats; conditional\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>random numbers;examples\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell styles; copying\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying; cell styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; copying cell styles\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149263				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"cellstyle_conditional\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellstyle_conditional.xhp\" name=\"Applying Conditional Formatting\"\>Applying Conditional Formatting\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3159156				0	en-ZA	Using the menu command \<emph\>Format - Conditional formatting\</emph\>, the dialogue allows you to define up to three conditions per cell, which must be met in order for the selected cells to have a particular format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id8039796				0	en-ZA	To apply conditional formatting, AutoCalculate must be enabled. Choose \<emph\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoCalculate\</emph\> (you see a check mark next to the command when AutoCalculate is enabled).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	en-ZA	With conditional formatting, you can, for example, highlight the totals that exceed the average value of all totals. If the totals change, the formatting changes correspondingly, without having to apply other styles manually.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id4480727				0	en-ZA	To Define the Conditions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	en-ZA	Select the cells to which you want to apply a conditional style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Conditional Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	en-ZA	Enter the condition(s) into the dialogue box. The dialogue is described in detail in \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05120000.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Help\"\>$[officename] Help\</link\>, and an example is provided below:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766				0	en-ZA	Example of Conditional Formatting: Highlighting Totals Above/Under the Average Value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id4341868				0	en-ZA	Step1: Generate Number Values				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3150043				0	en-ZA	You want to give certain values in your tables particular emphasis. For example, in a table of turnovers, you can show all the values above the average in green and all those below the average in red. This is possible with conditional formatting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3155337				0	en-ZA	First of all, write a table in which a few different values occur. For your test you can create tables with any random numbers:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	en-ZA	In one of the cells enter the formula =RAND(), and you will obtain a random number between 0 and 1. If you want integers of between 0 and 50, enter the formula =INT(RAND()*50).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3149258				0	en-ZA	Copy the formula to create a row of random numbers. Click the bottom right corner of the selected cell, and drag to the right until the desired cell range is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3159236				0	en-ZA	In the same way as described above, drag down the corner of the rightmost cell in order to create more rows of random numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149211				0	en-ZA	Step 2: Define Cell Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3154659				0	en-ZA	The next step is to apply a cell style to all values that represent above-average turnover, and one to those that are below the average. Ensure that the Styles and Formatting window is visible before proceeding.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3150883				0	en-ZA	Click in a blank cell and select the command \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> in the context menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialogue on the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab, select a background colour. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	en-ZA	In the Styles and Formatting window, click the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon. Enter the name of the new style. For this example, name the style "Above".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3152889				0	en-ZA	To define a second style, click again in a blank cell and proceed as described above. Assign a different background colour for the cell and assign a name (for this example, "Below").				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148704				0	en-ZA	Step 3: Calculate Average				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3148837				0	en-ZA	In our particular example, we are calculating the average of the random values. The result is placed in a cell:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768				0	en-ZA	Set the cursor in a blank cell, for example, J14, and choose \<emph\>Insert - Function\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3156016				0	en-ZA	Select the AVERAGE function. Use the mouse to select all your random numbers. If you cannot see the entire range, because the Function Wizard is obscuring it, you can temporarily shrink the dialogue using the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#eingabesymbol\" name=\"Shrink or Maximize\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Shrink / Maximize\</item\>\</link\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3153246				0	en-ZA	Close the Function Wizard with \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149898				0	en-ZA	Step 4: Apply Cell Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	en-ZA	Now you can apply the conditional formatting to the sheet:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3150049				0	en-ZA	Select all cells with the random numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3153801				0	en-ZA	Choose the \<emph\>Format - Conditional Formatting\</emph\> command to open the corresponding dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3153013				0	en-ZA	Define the condition as follows: If cell value is less than J14, format with cell style "Below", and if cell value is greater than or equal to J14, format with cell style "Above".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155761				0	en-ZA	Step 5: Copy Cell Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3145320				0	en-ZA	To apply the conditional formatting to other cells later:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3153074				0	en-ZA	Click one of the cells that has been assigned conditional formatting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3149051				0	en-ZA	Copy the cell to the clipboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3150436				0	en-ZA	Select the cells that are to receive this same formatting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3147298				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste Special\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialogue appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3166465				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> area, check only the \<emph\>Formats\</emph\> box. All other boxes must be unchecked. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3159123				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05120000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Conditional formatting\"\>Format - Conditional formatting\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Addresses and References, Absolute and Relative				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156423				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>addressing; relative and absolute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; absolute/relative\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>absolute addresses in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative addresses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>absolute references in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; to cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; references\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"relativ_absolut_ref\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/relativ_absolut_ref.xhp\" name=\"Addresses and References, Absolute and Relative\"\>Addresses and References, Absolute and Relative\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163712				0	en-ZA	Relative Addressing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	en-ZA	The cell in column A, row 1 is addressed as A1. You can address a range of adjacent cells by first entering the coordinates of the upper left cell of the area, then a colon followed by the coordinates of the lower right cell. For example, the square formed by the first four cells in the upper left corner is addressed as A1:B2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730				0	en-ZA	By addressing an area in this way, you are making a relative reference to A1:B2. Relative here means that the reference to this area will be adjusted automatically when you copy the formulae.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149377				0	en-ZA	Absolute Addressing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3154943				0	en-ZA	Absolute references are the opposite of relative addressing. A dollar sign is placed before each letter and number in an absolute reference, for example, $A$1:$B$2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	en-ZA	$[officename] can convert the current reference, in which the cursor is positioned in the input line, from relative to absolute and vice versa by pressing Shift +F4. If you start with a relative address such as A1, the first time you press this key combination, both row and column are set to absolute references ($A$1). The second time, only the row (A$1), and the third time, only the column ($A1). If you press the key combination once more, both column and row references are switched back to relative (A1)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	en-ZA	$[officename] Calc shows the references to a formula. If, for example you click the formula =SUM(A1:C5;D15:D24) in a cell, the two referenced areas in the sheet will be highlighted in colour. For example, the formula component "A1:C5" may be in blue and the cell range in question bordered in the same shade of blue. The next formula component "D15:D24" can be marked in red in the same way.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154704				0	en-ZA	When to Use Relative and Absolute References				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3147346				0	en-ZA	What distinguishes a relative reference? Assume you want to calculate in cell E1 the sum of the cells in range A1:B2. The formula to enter into E1 would be: =SUM(A1:B2). If you later decide to insert a new column in front of column A, the elements you want to add would then be in B1:C2 and the formula would be in F1, not in E1. After inserting the new column, you would therefore have to check and correct all formulae in the sheet, and possibly in other sheets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	en-ZA	Fortunately, $[officename] does this work for you. After having inserted a new column A, the formula =SUM(A1:B2) will be automatically updated to =SUM(B1:C2). Row numbers will also be automatically adjusted when a new row 1 is inserted. Absolute and relative references are always adjusted in $[officename] Calc whenever the referenced area is moved. But be careful if you are copying a formula since in that case only the relative references will be adjusted, not the absolute references.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3145791				0	en-ZA	Absolute references are used when a calculation refers to one specific cell in your sheet. If a formula that refers to exactly this cell is copied relatively to a cell below the original cell, the reference will also be moved down if you did not define the cell coordinates as absolute.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3147005				0	en-ZA	Aside from when new rows and columns are inserted, references can also change when an existing formula referring to particular cells is copied to another area of the sheet. Assume you entered the formula =SUM(A1:A9) in row 10. If you want to calculate the sum for the adjacent column to the right, simply copy this formula to the cell to the right. The copy of the formula in column B will be automatically adjusted to =SUM(B1:B9).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Printing Sheet Details				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>printing;sheet details\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing details\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>grids; printing sheet grids\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulae; printing, instead of results\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comments; printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts;printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheet grids; printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; printing grids\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders; printing cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>zero values; printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>null values; printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;printing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"print_details\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_details.xhp\" name=\"Printing Sheet Details\"\>Printing Sheet Details\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	en-ZA	When printing a sheet you can select which details are to be printed:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	en-ZA	Row and column headers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	en-ZA	Sheet grid				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	en-ZA	Comments				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801				0	en-ZA	Objects and graphics				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491				0	en-ZA	Charts				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731				0	en-ZA	Drawing objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	en-ZA	Formulae				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752				0	en-ZA	To choose the details proceed as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	en-ZA	Select the sheet you want to print.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3150042				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3147340	13			0	en-ZA	The command is not visible if the sheet was opened with write protection on. In that case, click the \<emph\>Edit File \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3146916	14			0	en-ZA	Select the \<emph\>Sheet\</emph\> tab. In the \<emph\>Print \</emph\>area mark the details to be printed and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3145789				0	en-ZA	Print the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3150345				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	User-Defined Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155411				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>functions; user-defined\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>user-defined functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Basic IDE for user-defined functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>IDE; Basic IDE\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>programming;functions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"userdefined_function\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/userdefined_function.xhp\" name=\"Defining Functions Yourself\"\>User-Defined Functions\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3153969				0	en-ZA	You can apply user-defined functions in $[officename] Calc in the following ways:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366				0	en-ZA	You can define your own functions using the Basic-IDE. This method requires a basic knowledge of programming.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	en-ZA	You can program functions as \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060111.xhp\" name=\"add-ins\"\>add-ins\</link\>. This method requires an advanced knowledge of programming.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149260				0	en-ZA	Defining A Function Using %PRODUCTNAME Basic				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> button. You will now see the Basic IDE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327				0	en-ZA	Enter the function code. In this example, we define a \<item type=\"literal\"\>VOL(a; b; c)\</item\> function that calculates the volume of a rectangular solid with side lengths \<item type=\"literal\"\>a\</item\>, \<item type=\"literal\"\>b\</item\> and \<item type=\"literal\"\>c\</item\>:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	en-ZA	Close the Basic-IDE window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150043				0	en-ZA	Your function is automatically saved in the default module and is now available. If you apply the function in a Calc document that is to be used on another computer, you can copy the function to the Calc document as described in the next section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147340				0	en-ZA	Copying a Function To a Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3145232	19			0	en-ZA	In stage 2 of "Defining A Function Using %PRODUCTNAME Basic", in the \<emph\>Macro\</emph\> dialogue you clicked on \<emph\>Edit \</emph\>. As the default, in the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> field the \<emph\>My Macros - Standard - Module1\</emph\> module is selected. The \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> library resides locally in your user directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	en-ZA	If you want to copy the user-defined function to a Calc document:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</item\> .				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150086				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> field select \<emph\>My Macros - Standard - Module1\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3166430				0	en-ZA	In the Basic-IDE, select the source of your user-defined function and copy it to the clipboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081D				0	en-ZA	Close the Basic-IDE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150517				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</item\> .				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> field select \<emph\>(Name of the Calc document) - Standard - Module1\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3148699				0	en-ZA	Paste the clipboard contents in the Basic-IDE of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153305				0	en-ZA	Applying a User-defined Function in $[officename] Calc				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3148869				0	en-ZA	Once you have defined the function \<item type=\"literal\"\>VOL(a; b; c)\</item\> in the Basic-IDE, you can apply it the same way as the built-in functions of $[officename] Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3148606				0	en-ZA	Open a Calc document and enter numbers for the function parameters \<item type=\"literal\"\>a\</item\>, \<item type=\"literal\"\>b\</item\>, and \<item type=\"literal\"\>c\</item\> in cells A1, B1, and C1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3156019				0	en-ZA	Set the cursor in another cell and enter the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3155264				0	en-ZA	=VOL(A1;B1;C1)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3146776				0	en-ZA	The function is evaluated and you will see the result in the selected cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Defining Number of Pages for Printing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153194				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheet counts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing sheet counts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page breaks; spreadsheet preview\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>previews;page breaks for printing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153194				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"print_exact\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_exact.xhp\" name=\"Defining Number of Pages for Printing\"\>Defining Number of Pages for Printing\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771				0	en-ZA	If a sheet is too large for a single printed page, $[officename] Calc will print the current sheet evenly divided over several pages. Since the automatic page break does not always take place in the optimal position, you can define the page distribution yourself.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3159155				0	en-ZA	Go to the sheet to be printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	en-ZA	You will see the automatic distribution of the sheet across the print pages. The automatically created print ranges are indicated by dark blue lines, and the user-defined ones by light blue lines. The page breaks (line breaks and column breaks) are marked as black lines.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578				0	en-ZA	You can move the blue lines with the mouse. You will find further options in the Context menu, including adding an additional print range, removing the scaling and inserting additional manual line and column breaks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Calculating With Dates and Times				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146120				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>dates; in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>times; in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;date and time formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>current date and time values\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146120				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"calc_date\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_date.xhp\" name=\"Calculating With Dates and Times\"\>Calculating With Dates and Times\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3154320				0	en-ZA	In $[officename] Calc, you can perform calculations with current date and time values. As an example, to find out exactly how old you are in seconds or hours, follow the following steps:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3150750				0	en-ZA	In a spreadsheet, enter your birthday in cell A1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3145642	14			0	en-ZA	Enter the following formula in cell A3: \<item type=\"literal\"\>=NOW()-A1\</item\>            				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3149020				0	en-ZA	After pressing the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> key you will see the result in date format. Since the result should show the difference between two dates as a number of days, you must format cell A3 as a number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	en-ZA	Place the cursor in cell A3, right-click to open a context menu and choose \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	en-ZA	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format Cells\</item\> dialogue appears. On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbers\</item\> tab, the "Number" category will appear already highlighted. The format is set to "General", which causes the result of a calculation containing date entries to be displayed as a date. To display the result as a number, set the number format to "-1,234" and close the dialogue with the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	en-ZA	The number of days between today's date and the specified date is displayed in cell A3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	en-ZA	Experiment with some additional formulae: in A4 enter =A3*24 to calculate the hours, in A5 enter =A4*60 for the minutes, and in A6 enter =A5*60 for seconds. Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> key after each formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3149207				0	en-ZA	The time since your date of birth will be calculated and displayed in the various units. The values are calculated as of the exact moment when you entered the last formula and pressed the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> key. This value is not automatically updated, although "Now" continuously changes. In the \<emph\>Tools\</emph\> menu, the menu item \<emph\>Cell Contents - AutoCalculate\</emph\> is normally active; however, automatic calculation does not apply to the function NOW. This ensures that your computer is not solely occupied with updating the sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Entering Formulas 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150868				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>formula bar; input line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>input line in formula bar\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulae; inputting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;formulae\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150868				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"formula_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_enter.xhp\" name=\"Entering Formulas\"\>Entering Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id6848353				0	en-ZA	You can enter formulae in several ways: using the icons, or by typing on the keyboard, or by a mixture of both methods.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364				0	en-ZA	Click the cell in which you want to enter the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Function\</emph\> icon on the Formula Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	en-ZA	You will now see an equals sign in the input line and you can begin to input the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	en-ZA	After entering the required values, press Enter or click \<emph\>Accept\</emph\> to insert the result in the active cell. If you want to clear your entry in the input line, press Escape or click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	en-ZA	You can also enter the values and the formulae directly into the cells, even if you cannot see an input cursor. Formulae must always begin with an equals sign.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id4206976				0	en-ZA	You can also press the + or - key on the numerical keyboard to start a formula. NumLock must be "on". For example, press the following keys in succession:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id1836909				0	en-ZA	+ 5 0 - 8 Enter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8171330				0	en-ZA	You see the result \<item type=\"literal\"\>42\</item\> in the cell. The cell contains the formula \<item type=\"literal\"\>=+50-8\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764				0	en-ZA	If you are editing a formula with references, the references and the associated cells will be highlighted with the same colour. You can now resize the reference border using the mouse, and the reference in the formula displayed in the input line also changes. \<emph\>Show references in colour\</emph\> can be deactivated under \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060300.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149210	7			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"tip\"\>If you would like to view the calculation of individual elements of a formula, select the respective elements and press F9. For example, in the formula =SUM(A1:B12)*SUM(C1:D12) select the section SUM(C1:D12) and press F9 to view the subtotal for this area. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	en-ZA	If an error occurs when creating the formula, an \<link href=\"text/scalc/05/02140000.xhp\" name=\"error message\"\>error message\</link\> appears in the active cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152993				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/main0206.xhp\" name=\"Formula bar\"\>Formula bar\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Calculating Time Differences				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150769				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;time differences\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>time differences\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150769				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"calc_timevalues\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_timevalues.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Time Differences\"\>Calculating Time Differences\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	par_id3149263				0	en-ZA	If you want to calculate time differences, for example, the time between 23:30 and 01:10 in the same night, use the following formula:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	par_id3159153				0	en-ZA	=(B2<A2)+B2-A2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	par_id3152598				0	en-ZA	The later time is B2 and the earlier time is A2. The result of the example is 01:40 or 1 hour and 40 minutes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	par_id3145271				0	en-ZA	In the formula, an entire 24-hour day has a value of 1 and one hour has a value of 1/24. The logical value in parentheses is 0 or 1, corresponding to 0 or 24 hours. The result returned by the formula is automatically issued in time format due to the sequence of the operands.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Applying Multiple Sheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154759				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; selecting multiple\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>appending sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>selecting;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>calculating;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154759				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multitables.xhp\" name=\"Applying Multiple Sheets\"\>Applying Multiple Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148576				0	en-ZA	Inserting a Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Sheet\</item\> to insert a new sheet or an existing sheet from another file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id050920091402035				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to select all sheets in the document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200914020391				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to deselect all sheets in the document, except the current sheet.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154491				0	en-ZA	Selecting Multiple Sheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	en-ZA	You can use Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Up or Page Down to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155600				0	en-ZA	Undoing a Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156382				0	en-ZA	Calculating Across Multiple Sheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	en-ZA	You can refer to a range of sheets in a formula by specifying the first and last sheet of the range, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=SUM(Sheet1.A1:Sheet3.A1) \</item\>sums up all A1 cells on Sheet1 through Sheet3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Copying Formulae				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151113				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>formulae; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;formulae\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151113				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"formula_copy\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_copy.xhp\" name=\"Copying Formulas\"\>Copying Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	en-ZA	There are various ways to copy a formula. One suggested method is:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439				0	en-ZA	Select the cell containing the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Copy\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C to copy it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3159155				0	en-ZA	Select the cell into which you want the formula to be copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V. The formula will be positioned in the new cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149961				0	en-ZA	If you want to copy a formula into multiple cells, there is a quick and easy way to copy into adjacent cell areas:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	en-ZA	Select the cell containing the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	en-ZA	Position the mouse on the bottom right of the highlighted border of the cell, and continue holding down the mouse button until the pointer changes to a cross-hair symbol.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	en-ZA	With the mouse button pressed, drag it down or to the right over all the cells into which you want to copy the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	en-ZA	When you release the mouse button, the formula will be copied into the cells and automatically adjusted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3156385				0	en-ZA	If you do not want values and texts to be automatically adjusted, then hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key when dragging. Formulas, however, are always adjusted accordingly.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Text Superscript / Subscript				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151112				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>superscript text in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subscript text in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; text super/sub\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>characters;superscript/subscript\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151112				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"super_subscript\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/super_subscript.xhp\" name=\"Text Superscript / Subscript\"\>Text Superscript / Subscript\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	en-ZA	In the cell, select the character that you want to put in superscript or subscript.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439				0	en-ZA	If, for example, you want to write H20 with a subscript 2, select the 2 in the cell (not in the input line).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	en-ZA	Open the context menu for the selected character and choose \<emph\>Character\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Character\</emph\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Font Position\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3153954				0	en-ZA	Select the \<emph\>Subscript\</emph\> option and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020500.xhp\" name=\"Context menu - Character - Font Position\"\>Context menu - Character - Font Position\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Assigning Formats by Formula				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145673				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>formats; assigning by formulae\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell formats; assigning by formulae\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>STYLE function example\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell styles;assigning by formulae\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulae;assigning cell formats\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145673	13			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"cellstyle_by_formula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellstyle_by_formula.xhp\" name=\"Assigning Formats by Formula\"\>Assigning Formats by Formula\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	en-ZA	The STYLE() function can be added to an existing formula in a cell. For example, together with the CURRENT function, you can colour a cell depending on its value. The formula =...+STYLE(IF(CURRENT()>3; "Red"; "Green")) applies the cell style "Red" to cells if the value is greater than 3, otherwise the cell style "Green" is applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385				0	en-ZA	If you would like to apply a formula to all cells in a selected area, you can use the\<emph/\>         \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find & Replace\</item\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	en-ZA	Select all the desired cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	en-ZA	Select the menu command \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767	18			0	en-ZA	For the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for\</item\> term, enter: .\<item type=\"literal\"\>*\</item\>            				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153770				0	en-ZA	".*" is a regular expression that designates the contents of the current cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143	20			0	en-ZA	Enter the following formula in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Replace with\</item\> field: \<item type=\"literal\"\>=&+STYLE(IF(CURRENT()>3;"Red";"Green"))\</item\>            				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	en-ZA	The "&" symbol designates the current contents of the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> field. The line must begin with an equal sign, since it is a formula. It is assumed that the cell styles "Red" and "Green" already exist.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	en-ZA	Mark the fields \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\" name=\"Regular expressions\"\>\<emph\>Regular expressions\</emph\>\</link\> and \<emph\>Current selection only\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3144767				0	en-ZA	All cells with contents that were included in the selection are now highlighted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3147127				0	en-ZA	Click\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Replace all\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Naming Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147434				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>cells; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>names; defining for cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>values; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>constants definition\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>variables; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell ranges; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;names for cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulae; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>addressing; by defined names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell names; defining/addressing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>references; by defined names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>allowed cell names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>renaming;cells\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"value_with_name\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/value_with_name.xhp\" name=\"Naming Cells\"\>Naming Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	hd_id4391918				0	en-ZA	Allowed names				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id2129581				0	en-ZA	Names in Calc can contain letters, numeric characters, and some special characters. Names must start with a letter or an underline character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id1120029				0	en-ZA	Allowed special characters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3362224				0	en-ZA	underline (_) 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id4891506				0	en-ZA	period (.) - allowed within a name, but not as first or last character				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id2816553				0	en-ZA	blank ( ) - allowed within a name, but not as first or last character, and not for a cell range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id328989				0	en-ZA	Names must not be the same as cell references. For example, the name A1 is invalid because A1 is a cell reference to the top left cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id4769737				0	en-ZA	Names for cell ranges must not include blanks. Blanks are allowed within names for single cells, sheets and documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	hd_id1226233				0	en-ZA	Naming cells and formulae				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id5489364				0	en-ZA	A good way of making the references to cells and cell ranges in formulae legible is to give the ranges names. For example, you can name the range A1:B2 \<emph\>Start\</emph\>. You can then write a formula such as "=SUM(Start)". Even after you insert or delete rows or columns, $[officename] still correctly assigns the ranges identified by name. Range names must not contain any spaces.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id953398				0	en-ZA	For example, it is much easier to read a formula for sales tax if you can write "= Amount * Tax_rate" instead of "= A5 * B12". In this case, you would name cell A5 "Amount" and cell B12 "Tax_rate."				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id4889675				0	en-ZA	Use the \<emph\>Define Names\</emph\> dialogue to define names for formulae or parts of formulae you need more often. In order to specify range names,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3153954				0	en-ZA	Select a cell or range of cells, then choose \<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Define Names\</emph\> dialogue appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	en-ZA	Type the name of the selected area in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> field. Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>. The newly defined name appears in the list below. Click OK to close the dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id5774101				0	en-ZA	You can also name other cell ranges in this dialogue by entering the name in the field and then selecting the respective cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3154942				0	en-ZA	If you type the name in a formula, after the first few characters entered you will see the entire name as a tip.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	en-ZA	Press the Enter key in order to accept the name from the tip.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	en-ZA	If more than one name starts with the same characters, you can scroll through all the names using the Tab key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04070100.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Names - Define\"\>Insert - Names - Define\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Protecting Cells from Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146119				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>protecting;cells and sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell protection; enabling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; hiding for printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing; sheet protection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hiding;formulae\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulae;hiding\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"cell_protect\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_protect.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Cells from Changes\"\>Protecting Cells from Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153368				0	en-ZA	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can protect sheets and the document as a whole. You can choose whether the cells are protected against accidental changes, whether the formulae can be viewed from within Calc, whether the cells are visible or whether the cells can be printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145261				0	en-ZA	Protection can be provided by means of a password, but it does not have to be. If you have assigned a password, protection can only be removed once the correct password has been entered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id5974303				0	en-ZA	These protection features are just switches to prevent accidental action. The features are not intended to provide any secure protection. For example, by exporting a sheet to another file format, a user may be able to surpass the protection features. There is only one secure protection: the password that you can apply when saving an OpenDocument file. A file that has been saved with a password can be opened only with the same password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	en-ZA	Select the cells that you want to specify the cell protection options for.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149019				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells\</item\> and click the \<emph\>Cell Protection\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152898	10			0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> to prevent changes to the contents and the format of a cell. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069A				0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>Hide formula\</emph\> to hide and to protect formulae from changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A1				0	en-ZA	Select \<emph\>Hide when printing\</emph\> to hide protected cells in the printed document. The cells are not hidden onscreen.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152872				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145362				0	en-ZA	Apply the protection options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C0				0	en-ZA	To protect the cells from being changed / viewed / printed according to your settings in the \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> dialogue, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C7				0	en-ZA	To protect the structure of the document, for example the count, \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rename_table.xhp\"\>names\</link\>, and order of the sheets, from being changed, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CF				0	en-ZA	(Optional) Enter a password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D2				0	en-ZA	If you forget your password, you cannot deactivate the protection. If you only want to protect cells from accidental changes, set the sheet protection, but do not enter a password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810	13			0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B8C				0	en-ZA	            \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp#digital_signatures\"/\>         				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\main.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Instructions for Using $[officename] Calc				2002-02-02 02:02:02
