helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\main.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166464				0	en-ZA	Miscellaneous				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Entering a Number with Leading Zeros				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147560				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>zero values; entering leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; with leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>integers with leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; changing text/number formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; changing text/number\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text in cells; changing to numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>converting;text with leading zeros, into numbers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147560				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"integer_leading_zero\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/integer_leading_zero.xhp\" name=\"Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\"\>Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153194				0	en-ZA	There are various ways to enter integers starting with a zero:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	en-ZA	Enter the number as text. The easiest way is to enter the number starting with an apostrophe (for example, \<item type=\"input\"\>'0987\</item\>). The apostrophe will not appear in the cell, and the number will be formatted as text. Because it is in text format, however, you cannot calculate with this number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	en-ZA	Format a cell with a number format such as \<item type=\"input\"\>\\0000\</item\>. This format can be assigned in the \<emph\>Format code\</emph\> field under the \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\> tab, and defines the cell display as "always put a zero first and then the integer, having at least three places, and filled with zeros at the left if less than three digits".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158				0	en-ZA	If you want to apply a numerical format to a column of numbers in text format (for example, text "000123" becomes number "123"), do the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	en-ZA	Select the column in which the digits are found in text format. Set the cell format in that column as "Number".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944	60			0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>               				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510	61			0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>^[0-9]\</item\>               				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3155068	62			0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>&\</item\>               				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018	63			0	en-ZA	Check \<emph\>Regular expressions\</emph\>               				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382	64			0	en-ZA	Check \<emph\>Current selection only\</emph\>               				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146916	65			0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>               				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Applying Goal Seek				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>goal seeking;example\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>equations in goal seek\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;variables in equations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variables;calculating equations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>examples;goal seek\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"goalseek\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/goalseek.xhp\" name=\"Applying Goal Seek\"\>Applying Goal Seek\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	en-ZA	With the help of Goal Seek you can calculate a value that, as part of a formula, leads to the result you specify for the formula. You thus define the formula with several fixed values and one variable value and the result of the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153966				0	en-ZA	Goal Seek Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150871				0	en-ZA	To calculate annual interest (I), create a table with the values for the capital (C), number of years (n), and interest rate (i). The formula is:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596				0	en-ZA	I = C * n* i				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	en-ZA	Let us assume that the interest rate \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> of 7.5% and the number of years \<item type=\"literal\"\>n\</item\> (1) will remain constant. However, you want to know how much the investment capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> would have to be modified in order to attain a particular return \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\>. For this example, calculate how much capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> would be required if you want an annual return of $15,000.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	en-ZA	Enter each of the values for Capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> (an arbitrary value like \<item type=\"literal\"\>$100,000\</item\>), number of years \<item type=\"literal\"\>n \</item\>(\<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\>), and interest rate \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> (\<item type=\"literal\"\>7.5%\</item\>) in one cell each. Enter the formula to calculate the interest \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\> in another cell. Instead of \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\>, \<item type=\"literal\"\>n\</item\>, and \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/relativ_absolut_ref.xhp\"\>reference to the cell\</link\> with the corresponding value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	en-ZA	Place the cursor in the cell containing the interest \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\>, and choose \<emph\>Tools - Goal Seek\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Goal Seek\</emph\> dialogue appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	en-ZA	The correct cell is already entered in the field \<emph\>Formula Cell\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	en-ZA	Place the cursor in the field \<emph\>Variable Cell\</emph\>. In the sheet, click in the cell that contains the value to be changed, in this example it is the cell with the capital value \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150369				0	en-ZA	Enter the expected result of the formula in the \<emph\>Target Value\</emph\> text box. In this example, the value is 15,000. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3146978				0	en-ZA	A dialogue appears informing you that the Goal Seek was successful. Click \<emph\>Yes\</emph\> to enter the result in the cell with the variable value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3149409				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06040000.xhp\" name=\"Goal Seek\"\>Goal Seek\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Calculating With Formulae				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155411				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>formulae;calculating with\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating; with formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>examples;formula calculation\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"formulae\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formulae.xhp\" name=\"Calculating With Formulae\"\>Calculating With Formulae\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281				0	en-ZA	All formulae begin with an equals sign. The formulae can contain numbers, text, arithmetic operators, logic operators, or functions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	en-ZA	Remember that the basic arithmetic operators (+, -, *, /) can be used in formulae using the "Multiplication and Division before Addition and Subtraction" rule. Instead of writing =SUM(A1:B1) you can write =A1+B1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	en-ZA	Parentheses can also be used. The result of the formula =(1+2)*3 produces a different result than =1+2*3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3156285				0	en-ZA	Here are a few examples of $[officename] Calc formulae:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154015				0	en-ZA	=A1+10				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146972				0	en-ZA	Displays the contents of cell A1 plus 10.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3145643				0	en-ZA	=A1*16%				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	en-ZA	Displays 16% of the contents of A1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146917				0	en-ZA	=A1 * A2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146315				0	en-ZA	Displays the result of the multiplication of A1 and A2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	en-ZA	=ROUND(A1;1)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150363				0	en-ZA	Displays the contents of cell A1 rounded to one decimal place.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150209				0	en-ZA	=EFFECTIVE(5%;12)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150883				0	en-ZA	Calculates the effective interest for 5% annual nominal interest with 12 payments a year.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146114				0	en-ZA	=B8-SUM(B10:B14)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154486				0	en-ZA	Calculates B8 minus the sum of the cells B10 to B14.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3152890				0	en-ZA	=SUM(B8;SUM(B10:B14))				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3159171				0	en-ZA	Calculates the sum of cells B10 to B14 and adds the value to B8.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150109				0	en-ZA	It is also possible to nest functions in formulae, as shown in the example. You can also nest functions within functions. The Function Wizard assists you with nested functions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060100.xhp\" name=\"Functions list\"\>Functions list\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"AutoPilot: Functions\"\>Function Wizard\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Displaying Formulae or Values				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153195				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>formulae; displaying in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>values; displaying in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; displaying formulae/values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>results display vs. formulae display\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>displaying; formulae instead of results\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153195				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"formula_value\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_value.xhp\" name=\"Displaying Formulas or Values\"\>Displaying Formulas or Values\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	en-ZA	If you want to display the formulae in the cells, for example in the form =SUM(A1:B5), proceed as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3151116				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Display\</emph\> area mark the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> box. Click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	en-ZA	If you want to view the calculation results instead of the formula, do not mark the Formulas box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	en-ZA	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Calculating in Spreadsheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"calculate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calculate.xhp\" name=\"Calculating in Spreadsheets\"\>Calculating in Spreadsheets\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	en-ZA	The following is an example of a calculation in $[officename] Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	en-ZA	Click in a cell, and type a number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065D				0	en-ZA	The cursor moves down to the next cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	en-ZA	Enter another number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN10676				0	en-ZA	The cursor moves to the right into the next cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	en-ZA	Type in a formula, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=A3 * A4 / 100.\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	en-ZA	The result of the formula appears in the cell. If you want, you can edit the formula in the input line of the Formula bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155378				0	en-ZA	When you edit a formula, the new result is calculated automatically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Defining Database Ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154758				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>tables; database ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>database ranges; defining\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>ranges; defining database ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;database ranges\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154758				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"database_define\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_define.xhp\" name=\"Defining Database Ranges\"\>Defining a Database Range\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	en-ZA	You can define a range of cells in a spreadsheet to use as a database. Each row in this database range corresponds to a database record and each cell in a row corresponds to a database field. You can sort, group, search, and perform calculations on the range as you would in a database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801	82			0	en-ZA	You can only edit and access a database range in the spreadsheet that contains the range. You cannot access the database range in the %PRODUCTNAME Data Sources view. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10648				0	en-ZA	To define a database range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	en-ZA	Select the range of cells that you want to define as a database range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10654				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Define Range\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153715				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box, enter a name for the database range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066A				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>More\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	en-ZA	Specify the options for the database range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10675				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Data - Group and Outline - Group\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	en-ZA	To remove a grouping, click inside the group, then choose \<emph\>Data - Group and Outline - Ungroup\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Navigating Through Sheets Tabs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150769				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; showing multiple\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheet tabs;using\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>views;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150769	4			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"multi_tables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multi_tables.xhp\" name=\"Navigating Through Sheet Tabs\"\>Navigating Through Sheet Tabs\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771				0	en-ZA	By default $[officename] displays three sheets "Sheet1" to "Sheet3", in each new spreadsheet. You can switch between sheets in a spreadsheet using the sheet tabs at the bottom of the screen.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AF				0	en-ZA	 \<image id=\"img_id4829822\" src=\"res/helpimg/sheettabs.png\" width=\"3.3335inch\" height=\"0.7638inch\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4829822\"\>Sheet Tabs\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	en-ZA	 \<image id=\"img_id3156441\" src=\"res/helpimg/calcnav.png\" width=\"0.6563inch\" height=\"0.1457inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156441\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	en-ZA	Use the navigation buttons to display all the sheets belonging to your document. Clicking the button on the far left or the far right displays, respectively, the first or last sheet tab. The middle buttons allow the user to scroll forward and backward through all sheet tabs. To display the sheet itself click on the sheet tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	en-ZA	If there is insufficient space to display all the sheet tabs, you can increase it by pointing to the separator between the scrollbar and the sheet tabs, pressing the mouse button and, keeping the mouse button pressed, dragging to the right. In doing so you will be sharing the available space between the sheet tabs and horizontal scrollbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Formatting Numbers With Decimals				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145367				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>numbers;formatting decimals\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; numbers in tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; number formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defaults; number formats in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>decimal places;formatting numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;numbers with decimals\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;adding/deleting decimal places\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number formats; adding/deleting decimal places in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting; decimal places\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>decimal places; adding/deleting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145367				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"format_value\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_value.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Numbers With Decimals\"\>Formatting Numbers With Decimals\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	en-ZA	Enter a number into the sheet, for example, 1234.5678. This number will be displayed in the default number format, with two decimal places. You will see 1234.57 when you confirm the entry. Only the display in the document will be rounded off; internally, the number retains all four decimal places after the decimal point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012				0	en-ZA	To format numbers with decimals:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	en-ZA	Set the cursor at the number and choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> to start the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	en-ZA	On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab you will see a selection of predefined number formats. In the bottom right in the dialogue you will see a preview of how your current number would look if you were to give it a particular format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3155766				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3149021\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_numberformatincdecimals.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149021\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3149256				0	en-ZA	If you only want to modify the number of the decimal places displayed, the easiest method is to use the \<emph\>Number Format: Add Decimal Place\</emph\> or \<emph\>Number Format: Delete Decimal Place\</emph\> icons on the Formatting Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Sorting Data 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150767				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; sorting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sorting; database ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>data;sorting in databases\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150767				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"database_sort\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_sort.xhp\" name=\"Sorting Database Ranges\"\>Sorting Data\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3145751				0	en-ZA	Click in a database range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id121020081121549				0	en-ZA	If you select a range of cells, only these cells will get sorted. If you just click one cell without selecting, then the whole database range will get sorted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN10635				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Sort\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id121020081121547				0	en-ZA	The range of cells that will get sorted is shown in inverted colours.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	en-ZA	Select the sort options that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063D				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id1846980				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Defining_a_Data_Range\"\>Wiki page about defining a data range\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Entering Matrix Formulae				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153969				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>matrices; entering matrix formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulae; matrix formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;matrix formulae\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153969				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"matrixformula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/matrixformula.xhp\" name=\"Entering Matrix Formulas\"\>Entering Matrix Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	en-ZA	The following is an example of how you can enter a matrix formula, without going into the details of matrix functions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	en-ZA	Assume you have entered 10 numbers in Columns A and B (A1:A10 and B1:B10), and would like to calculate the sum of each row in Column C.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154321				0	en-ZA	Using the mouse, select the range C1:C10, in which the results are to be displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	en-ZA	Press F2, or click in the input line of the Formula bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	en-ZA	Enter an equal sign (=).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	en-ZA	Select the range A1:A10, which contains the first values for the sum formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3144767				0	en-ZA	Press the (+) key from the numerical keypad.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	en-ZA	Select the numbers in the second column in cells B1:B10.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150716				0	en-ZA	End the input with the matrix key combination: Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	en-ZA	The matrix area is automatically protected against modifications, such as deleting rows or columns. It is, however, possible to edit any formatting, such as the cell background.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Using Scenarios				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149664				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>scenarios; creating/editing/deleting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening;scenarios\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;scenarios in Navigator\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"scenario\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/scenario.xhp\" name=\"Using Scenarios\"\>Using Scenarios\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	en-ZA	A $[officename] Calc scenario is a set of cell values that can be used within your calculations. You assign a name to every scenario on your sheet. Define several scenarios on the same sheet, each with some different values in the cells. Then you can easily switch the sets of cell values by their name and immediately observe the results. Scenarios are a tool to test out "what-if" questions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149255				0	en-ZA	Creating Your Own Scenarios				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704	16			0	en-ZA	To create a scenario, select all the cells that provide the data for the scenario. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	en-ZA	Select the cells that contain the values that will change between scenarios. To select multiple cells, hold down the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\</item\>key as you click each cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3150364				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Scenarios\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Create Scenario\</emph\> dialogue appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	en-ZA	Enter a name for the new scenario and leave the other fields unchanged with their default values. Close the dialogue with OK. Your new scenario is automatically activated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149664				0	en-ZA	Using Scenarios				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	en-ZA	Scenarios can be selected in the Navigator:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752	12			0	en-ZA	Open the Navigator with the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id1593676\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_navigator.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1593676\"\>Navigator icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the Standard bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764	13			0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Scenarios\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id7617114\" src=\"sc/res/imglst/navipi/na07.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7617114\"\>Scenarios icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the Navigator.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	en-ZA	In the Navigator, you see the defined scenarios with the comments that were entered when the scenarios were created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id1243629				0	en-ZA	Double-click a scenario name in the Navigator to apply that scenario to the current sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id9044770				0	en-ZA	To delete a scenario, right-click the name in the Navigator and choose \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3674123				0	en-ZA	To edit a scenario, right-click the name in the Navigator and choose \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3424481				0	en-ZA	To hide the border of a set of cells that are part of a scenario, open the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialogue for each scenario that affects the cells and clear the Display border checkbox. Hiding the border also removes the listbox on the sheet where you can choose the scenarios.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	en-ZA	If you want to know which values in the scenario affect other values, choose \<emph\>Tools - Detective - Trace Dependents\</emph\>. You see arrows to the cells that are directly dependent on the current cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06050000.xhp\" name=\"Creating Scenarios\"\>Creating Scenarios\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Using AutoFormat for Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155132				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>tables; AutoFormat function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;AutoFormat function for tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoFormat function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; automatically formatting spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic formatting in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets;AutoFormat function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155132				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"autoformat\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/autoformat.xhp\" name=\"Using AutoFormat for Tables\"\>Applying Automatic Formatting to a Selected Cell Range\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3149401				0	en-ZA	You can use the AutoFormat feature to quickly apply a format to a sheet or a selected cell range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10702				0	en-ZA	To Apply an AutoFormat to a Sheet or Selected Cell Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CE				0	en-ZA	Select the cells, including the column and row headers, that you want to format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D5				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - AutoFormat\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242				0	en-ZA	To select which properties to include in an AutoFormat, click \<emph\>More\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10715				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075D				0	en-ZA	The format is applied to the selected range of cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3149210				0	en-ZA	If you do not see any change in colour of the cell contents, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Value Highlighting\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3155379				0	en-ZA	To Define an AutoFormat for Spreadsheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868				0	en-ZA	You can define a new AutoFormat that is available to all spreadsheets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	en-ZA	Format a sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Select All\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153815				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - AutoFormat\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A9				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Add AutoFormat\</emph\> dialogue, enter a name for the format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C3				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3159203				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05110000.xhp\" name=\"Format - AutoFormat\"\>Format - AutoFormat\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Formatting Numbers as Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>numbers;entering as text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text formats; for numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; numbers as text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell formats; text/numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;numbers as text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"text_numbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/text_numbers.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Numbers as Text\"\>Formatting Numbers as Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	en-ZA	You can format numbers as text in $[officename] Calc. Open the context menu of a cell or range of cells and choose \<emph\>Format Cells - Numbers\</emph\>, then select "Text" from the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> list. Any numbers subsequently entered into the formatted range are interpreted as text. The display of these "numbers" is left-justified, just as with other text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	en-ZA	If you have already entered normal numbers in cells and have afterwards changed the format of the cells to "Text", the numbers will remain normal numbers. They will not be converted. Only numbers entered afterwards, or numbers which are then edited, will become text numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3144765				0	en-ZA	If you decide to enter a number directly as text, enter an apostrophe (') first. For example, for years in column headings, you can enter '1999, '2000 and '2001. The apostrophe is not visible in the cell, it only indicates that the entry is to be recognised as a text. This is useful if, for example, you enter a telephone number or postal code that begins with a zero (0), because a zero (0) at the start of a sequence of digits is removed in normal number formats.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Numbers\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150542				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>HTML; sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving; sheets in HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening; sheets in HTML\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150542				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"html_doc\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/html_doc.xhp\" name=\"Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML\"\>Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154124				0	en-ZA	Saving Sheets in HTML				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc saves all the sheets of a Calc document together as an HTML document. At the beginning of the HTML document, a heading and a list of hyperlinks are automatically added which lead to the individual sheets within the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	en-ZA	Numbers are shown as written. In addition, in the <SDVAL> HTML tag, the exact internal number value is written so that after opening the HTML document with \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> you know you have the exact values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	en-ZA	To save the current Calc document as HTML, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> list box, in the area with the other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc filters, choose the file type "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc)".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	en-ZA	Enter a \<emph\>File name\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149379				0	en-ZA	Opening Sheets in HTML				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	en-ZA	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> offers various filters for opening HTML files, which you can select under \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Files of type\</emph\> list box:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	en-ZA	Choose the file type "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc)" to open in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446				0	en-ZA	All \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc options are now available to you. However, not all options that \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc offers for editing can be saved in HTML format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"File - Open\"\>File - Open\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"File - Save As\"\>File - Save As\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Only Copy Visible Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150440				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>cells; copying/deleting/formatting/moving\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rows;visible and invisible\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying; visible cells only\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;visible cells only\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>moving;visible cells only\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;visible cells only\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>invisible cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>filters;copying visible cells only\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hidden cells\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150440				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"cellcopy\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellcopy.xhp\" name=\"Only Copy Visible Cells\"\>Only Copy Visible Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3148577				0	en-ZA	Assume you have hidden a few rows in a cell range. Now you want to copy, delete, or format only the remaining visible rows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	en-ZA	$[officename] behaviour depends on how the cells were made invisible, by a filter or manually.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603				0	en-ZA	Method and Action				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150751				0	en-ZA	Result				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	en-ZA	Cells were filtered by AutoFilters, standard filters or advanced filters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150044				0	en-ZA	Copy, delete, move, or format a selection of currently visible cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918				0	en-ZA	Only the visible cells of the selection are copied, deleted, moved, or formatted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3166427				0	en-ZA	Cells were hidden using the \<emph\>Hide\</emph\> command in the context menu of the row or column headers, or through an \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080000.xhp\" name=\"outline\"\>outline\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	en-ZA	Copy, delete, move, or format a selection of currently visible cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154371				0	en-ZA	All cells of the selection, including the hidden cells, are copied, deleted, moved, or formatted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Printing Sheets in Landscape Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153418				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheet selections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing in landscape\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing; landscape\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>landscape printing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153418				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"print_landscape\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_landscape.xhp\" name=\"Printing Sheets in Landscape Format\"\>Printing Sheets in Landscape Format\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3149257				0	en-ZA	In order to print a sheet you have a number of interactive options available under \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>. Drag the delimiter lines to define the range of printed cells on each page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	en-ZA	To print in landscape format, proceed as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	en-ZA	Go to the sheet to be printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150786				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150089	5			0	en-ZA	The command is not visible if the sheet has been opened with write protection on. In that case, click the \<emph\>Edit File \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3166430				0	en-ZA	Select the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab. Select the \<emph\>Landscape\</emph\> paper format and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150885				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3156288				0	en-ZA	Depending on the printer driver and the operating system, it may be necessary to click the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> button and to change your printer to landscape format there.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3149404	9			0	en-ZA	In the \<emph\>Print \</emph\>dialogue in the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab page, select the contents to be printed:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3153305	10			0	en-ZA	               \<emph\>All sheets\</emph\> - All sheets will be printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3148871	12			0	en-ZA	               \<emph\>Selected sheets\</emph\> - Only the selected sheets will be printed. All sheets whose names (at the bottom on the sheet tabs) are selected will be printed. By pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while clicking a sheet name you can change this selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3764763				0	en-ZA	               \<emph\>Selected cells\</emph\> - All selected cells are printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id5538804				0	en-ZA	From all the paper pages that result from the above selection, you can select the range of paper pages to be printed:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id14343				0	en-ZA	               \<emph\>All pages\</emph\> - Print all resulting pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3148699	11			0	en-ZA	               \<emph\>Pages\</emph\> - Enter the pages to be printed. The pages will also be numbered from the first sheet onwards. If you see in the Page Break Preview that Sheet1 will be printed on 4 pages and you want to print the first two pages of Sheet2, enter 5-6 here.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3145076				0	en-ZA	If under \<emph\>Format - Print ranges\</emph\> you have defined one or more print ranges, only the contents of these print ranges will be printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3156019				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id8254646				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/printranges.xhp\"\>Defining Print Ranges on a Sheet\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153150				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>formatting;in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>$[officename] Math; formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>superscripts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>binomials\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>vertical elements\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines; inserting in formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subscripts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>stacks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>vertical arrangement of elements\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>small gaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>alignment; left (Math)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>left-justified alignment (Math)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>alignment; horizontally centred (Math)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>centred horizontally; alignment (Math)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>alignment; right (Math)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>right-justified alignment in %PRODUCTNAME Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>matrices; arranging\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spaces in formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>gaps in formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; gaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arranging;matrices\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulae;aligning\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>aligning formulae\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153150				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03090700.xhp\" name=\"Format\"\>Format\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3147262				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_FORMAT_CAT\"\>You can choose among various options for formatting a $[officename] Math formula. The format options are displayed in the lower half of the Formula Elements window.\</ahelp\> These options are also listed in the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#kontextmenue\" name=\"context menu\"\>context menu\</link\> of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3153536				0	en-ZA	The letter "a" refers to the placeholder in your formula which you would like to assign to the respective formatting. You can substitute this character for any other you like.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151104				0	en-ZA	Formatting options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
