helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_idN10265				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3149220\" src=\"starmath/res/co21906.png\" width=\"0.3335inch\" height=\"0.3335inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149220\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3147116				0	en-ZA	Vertical stack (3 elements)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3146332				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_STACK\"\>Inserts a vertical stack with three placeholders.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>stack {<?>#<?>#<?>}\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_idN102A0				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3149848\" src=\"starmath/res/co21902.png\" width=\"0.3335inch\" height=\"0.3335inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149848\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3155572				0	en-ZA	Small gap				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3147056				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_SBLANK\"\>Inserts a small gap between a placeholder and the next element.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>`\</emph\> directly in the Commands window. The command must appear to the left or right of a symbol, variable, number or complete command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_idN102DC				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3154094\" src=\"starmath/res/co21909.png\" width=\"0.3335inch\" height=\"0.3335inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154094\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154580				0	en-ZA	Align left				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154592				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_ALIGNLX\"\>This icon assigns left-alignment to "a" and inserts a placeholder.\</ahelp\> You can type \<emph\>alignl<?>\</emph\> directly in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_idN10317				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3156130\" src=\"starmath/res/co21910.png\" width=\"0.3335inch\" height=\"0.3335inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156130\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154723				0	en-ZA	Align to horizontal centre				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149319				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_ALIGNCX\"\>Assigns horizontal central alignment to "a" and inserts a placeholder.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>alignc<?>\</emph\> directly in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_idN10352				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3155583\" src=\"starmath/res/co21911.png\" width=\"0.3335inch\" height=\"0.3335inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155583\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149768				0	en-ZA	Align right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149780				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_ALIGNRX\"\>Inserts the command for right alignment and a placeholder.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>alignr<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_idN1038D				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3155085\" src=\"starmath/res/co21907.png\" width=\"0.3335inch\" height=\"0.3335inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155085\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154338				0	en-ZA	Matrix stack				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3146941				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_MATRIX\"\>This icon inserts a matrix with four placeholders.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>matrix{<?>#<?>##<?>#<?>}\</emph\> directly in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window. The position of an element inside this diagram is indicated by two coordinates; the first specifies the line number and the second the column number. You can expand this matrix in any direction in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window by adding characters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_idN103C9				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3150027\" src=\"starmath/res/co21903.png\" width=\"0.3335inch\" height=\"0.3335inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150027\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149358				0	en-ZA	Gap				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149370				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_BLANK\"\>This icon inserts a gap or space between placeholders.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>~\</emph\> directly in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window. The command must appear to the left or right of a symbol, variable, number or complete command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3155394	48			0	en-ZA	For alignment, the \<emph\>alignl, alignc\</emph\> and \<emph\>alignr\</emph\> commands are especially effective, if you are 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3151009				0	en-ZA	aligning numerators and denominators, for example \<emph\>{alignl a}over{b+c}\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3148812				0	en-ZA	constructing binomials or stacks, for example \<emph\>binom{2*n}{alignr k}\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154360				0	en-ZA	aligning the elements in a matrix, for example \<emph\>matrix{alignr a#b+2##c+1/3#alignl d}\</emph\> and				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3155946				0	en-ZA	beginning a new line, for example \<emph\>a+b-c newline alignr x/y\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154621				0	en-ZA	When using the align instructions, note that				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3147382				0	en-ZA	they can only placed at the beginning of expressions and can only occur once. Therefore you can type \<emph\>a+b alignr c\</emph\>, but not \<emph\>a+alignr b\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154004				0	en-ZA	they affect each other, which means that typing \<emph\>{alignl{alignr a}}over{b+c}\</emph\> aligns \<emph\>a\</emph\> on the right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	hd_id8036133				0	en-ZA	To align using the "matrix" command				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_idN10F70				0	en-ZA	Aligning to the left				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149645				0	en-ZA	If a line or an expression begins with text, it is aligned on the left by default. You can change this with any of the \<emph\>align\</emph\> commands. An example is \<emph\>stack{a+b-c*d#alignr "text"}\</emph\>, where "text" appears aligned to the right. Note that text must always be surrounded by quotation marks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149966				0	en-ZA	The standard centralized formulae can be aligned to the left without using the \<emph\>Format - Alignment\</emph\> menu. To do this, place an empty character string, that is, the inverted commas which surround any text "", before the section of formula that you want to align. For example, typing \<emph\>"" a+b newline "" c+d\</emph\> results in both equations being left-aligned instead of centred.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3145654				0	en-ZA	When typing information in the Commands window, note that some formats require spaces for the correct structure. This is especially true when entering values (for example, a lsup{3}) instead of placeholders.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3148708				0	en-ZA	Click \<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091100.xhp\" name=\"Brackets and Grouping\"\>Brackets and Grouping\</link\> for more information about formatting in \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3155340				0	en-ZA	Useful information about \<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091200.xhp\" name=\"Indexes and Exponents\"\>Indexes and Exponents\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091400.xhp\" name=\"Scaling\"\>Scaling\</link\>, helps you organise your document in the best possible way.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090906.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Matrix in Bold Font				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090906.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154704				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03090906.xhp\" name=\"Matrix in Bold Font\"\>Matrix in Bold Font\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090906.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	en-ZA	Here is an example of how to create a bold font matrix in \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\>. You can copy this example to the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window using the clipboard and use it in your own formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090906.xhp	0	help	par_id3148866				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3150210\" src=\"res/helpimg/smzb6.png\" width=\"9.511cm\" height=\"7.99cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150210\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090906.xhp	0	help	par_id3154763				0	en-ZA	bold { f(x", "y) = left [ stack { x + y over z + left lbrace matrix { 2 # 3 # 4 ## 4 # 5 # 6 ## 6 # 7 # 8} right rbrace # {y + sin (x)} over %alpha # z + y over g } right ]}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090901.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Symbols with Indices				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090901.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156382				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03090901.xhp\" name=\"Symbols with Indices\"\>Symbols with Indices\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090901.xhp	0	help	par_id3150301				0	en-ZA	The following example explains how to create symbols with indexes in \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\>. You can copy this example to the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window by using the clipboard and use it in your own formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090901.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3148870\" src=\"res/helpimg/smzb1.png\" width=\"3.217cm\" height=\"2.939cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148870\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Spacing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05030000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154658				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>spacing; formula elements\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulae;element spacing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154658				0	en-ZA	Spacing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"abstaendetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SID_DISTANCE\"\>Use this dialogue to determine the spacing between formula elements. The spacing is specified as a percentage in relation to the base size defined under \<emph\>Format - Font Size\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143228				0	en-ZA	Use the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> button to determine the formula element for which you would like to specify the spacing. The appearance of the dialogue depends on the selected category. A preview window shows you which spacing is modified through the respective boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154653				0	en-ZA	Category				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149873				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:MENUBUTTON:RID_DISTANCEDIALOG:1\"\>This button allows you to select the category for which you would like to change the spacing.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
