helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	par_idN10519				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3149625\" src=\"starmath/res/op21420.png\" width=\"8.47mm\" height=\"8.47mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149625\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	par_id3145663				0	en-ZA	Set of real numbers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	par_id3148709				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_SETR\"\>Use this icon to insert a character for the \<emph\>set of real numbers\</emph\>.\</ahelp\> Instead of this, you can enter \<emph\>setr\</emph\> in the Commands window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	par_idN10552				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3155555\" src=\"starmath/res/op21421.png\" width=\"8.47mm\" height=\"8.47mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155555\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	par_id3149519				0	en-ZA	Set of complex numbers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_SETC\"\>Use this icon to insert a character for the \<emph\>set of complex numbers\</emph\>.\</ahelp\> You can also enter \<emph\>setc\</emph\> in the Commands window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	par_id3154224				0	en-ZA	Be sure to leave spaces (gaps) between values and commands when entering them manually in the Commands window. This ensures that the correct structure is achieved.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Indexes and Exponents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150746				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>indexes and exponents in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exponents and indexes in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150746				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091200.xhp\" name=\"Indexes and Exponents\"\>Indexes and Exponents\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153730				0	en-ZA	Here, you will find basic information about indexes and exponents in \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\>. You can try the examples described here to help you understand the details discussed. (The quotation marks in this text are for emphasis purposes only and are not part of the examples.)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149884				0	en-ZA	The index and exponent for a character are displayed one on top of the other, left-justified to the base character. For example, type \<emph\>a_2^3\</emph\> or \<emph\>a^3_2\</emph\>. This can be in any order. Instead of \<emph\>'_'\</emph\> and \<emph\>'^'\</emph\>, you can use \<emph\>'sub'\</emph\> and \<emph\>'sup'\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148387				0	en-ZA	However, it is no longer possible to use the following patterns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149029				0	en-ZA	a_2_3				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155985				0	en-ZA	a^2^3				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153923				0	en-ZA	a_2^3_4				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153724				0	en-ZA	Each sub-/superscript position of a base character can only be used once. You must use brackets to indicate the desired result. The following examples illustrate this				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151185				0	en-ZA	a_{2_3}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151272				0	en-ZA	a^{2^3}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156316				0	en-ZA	a_2^{3_4}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145207				0	en-ZA	a_{2^3}^{4_5}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151173	13			0	en-ZA	Unlike other formula editors where "\<emph\>_\</emph\>" and " \<emph\>^\</emph\> " only refer to the next character ("a_24" refers only to the "2"), $[officename] Math refers to the entire number(s)/name(s)/text. If you want to put superscripts and subscripts in sequence, the expression can be written as follows: a_2{}^3 or a^3{}_2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154260				0	en-ZA	To write tensors, \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\> provides several options. In addition to the notation "R_i{}^{jk}{}_l", common in other applications, additional notations can be used, namely "R_i{}^jk{}_l" and "{{R_i}^jk}_l."				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147516				0	en-ZA	Super- and subscripts to the left of the base character can also be right-justified. To do this, the new commands "lsub" and "lsup" are used. Both commands have the same effect as "sub" and "sup", except that they are left of the base character. See also "a lsub 2 lsup 3."				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154276				0	en-ZA	The rules governing unambiguity and the necessity of using brackets remain the same. In principle, this can be achieved with \<emph\>{}_2^3 a\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152961				0	en-ZA	The commands "sub" and "sup" are also available as "rsub" and "rsup".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	par_id3158437				0	en-ZA	Using the "csub" and "csup" commands, you can write super- and subscripts directly above or below a character. An example is "a csub y csup x". Combinations of indexes and exponents together are also possible: "abc_1^2 lsub 3 lsup 4 csub 55555 csup 66666."				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154570				0	en-ZA	Super- and subscripts can be attached to most unary and binary operators. Two examples: "a div_2 b a<csub n b +_2 h" and "a toward csub f b x toward csup f y."				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155904				0	en-ZA	Be sure to also enter all spaces between characters when entering these examples into the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Font Sizes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153816				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>font sizes; in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sizes; of fonts in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153816				0	en-ZA	Font Sizes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"schriftgroessentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FONTSIZE\"\>Use this dialogue to specify the font sizes for your formula. Select a base size and all elements of the formula will be scaled in relation to this base.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146968				0	en-ZA	Base size				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145115				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:METRICFIELD:RID_FONTSIZEDIALOG:1\"\>All elements of a formula are proportionally scaled to the base size. To change the base size, select or type in the desired point (pt) size. You can also use other units of measure or other \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#metrik\" name=\"metrics\"\>metrics\</link\>, which are then automatically converted to points.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153005				0	en-ZA	To permanently change the default size (12 pt) used in $[officename] Math, you must first set the size (for example, 11 pt) and then click the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153735				0	en-ZA	Relative Sizes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	en-ZA	In this section, you can determine the relative sizes for each type of element with reference to the base size.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150935				0	en-ZA	Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:METRICFIELD:RID_FONTSIZEDIALOG:4\"\>Select the size for text in a formula relative to the base size.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148392				0	en-ZA	Indexes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
