helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150659				0	en-ZA	toward				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150670				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XTOWARDY\"\>Inserts a \<emph\>toward\</emph\> relation symbol with two placeholders.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\><?> toward <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_idN104E7				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3149969\" src=\"starmath/res/bi21324.png\" width=\"0.847cm\" height=\"0.847cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149969\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147279				0	en-ZA	double arrow pointing left				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149599				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_DLARROW\"\>Inserts the logical relation \<emph\>arrow with double bar pointing left\</emph\>.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>dlarrow\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10525				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3149516\" src=\"starmath/res/bi21325.png\" width=\"0.847cm\" height=\"0.847cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149516\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148707				0	en-ZA	double arrow pointing left and right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148721				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_DLRARROW\"\>Inserts the logical relation \<emph\>arrow with double bar pointing left and right\</emph\> with two operators.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>dlrarrow\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10563				0	en-ZA	\<image id=\"img_id3148697\" src=\"starmath/res/bi21326.png\" width=\"0.847cm\" height=\"0.847cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148697\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150853				0	en-ZA	double arrow pointing right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150866				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_DRARROW\"\>Inserts the logical operator \<emph\>arrow with double bar pointing right\</emph\> with two placeholders.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>drarrow\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153545	74			0	en-ZA	To create the \<emph\>much greater than\</emph\> relation with two placeholders, type \<emph\><?> gg <?> \</emph\>or \<emph\>>>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156000				0	en-ZA	Type \<emph\>ll\</emph\> or \<emph\><<\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window to insert the \<emph\>much less than\</emph\> relation into the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153749				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>is defined as\</emph\> relation with two placeholders is inserted by typing \<emph\><?>def<?>\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154068				0	en-ZA	Insert the \<emph\>picture by\</emph\> correspondence character with two placeholders by typing \<emph\><?> transl <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149592				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\><?>transr<?>\</emph\> command inserts the \<emph\>original by\</emph\> correspondence character with two placeholders.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154735				0	en-ZA	When entering information manually in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window, note that a number of operators require spaces for the correct structure. This is especially true if you are working with values instead of placeholders. For example, for the "is considerably greater" relation, type either \<emph\>10 gg 1\</emph\> or \<emph\>a gg b\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090903.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Symbols with Indices				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090903.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155959				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03090903.xhp\" name=\"Symbols with Indices\"\>Symbols with Indices\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090903.xhp	0	help	par_id3150300				0	en-ZA	A third example of how to use \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\> to create symbols with indexes is shown below. You can copy the example into the clipboard and use it in your own formula in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
