helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Alignment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148730				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>aligning; multi-line formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multi-line formulae; aligning\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148730				0	en-ZA	Alignment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152999				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"ausrichtungtext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SID_ALIGN\" visibility=\"visible\"\>You can define the alignment of multi-line formulae as well as formulae with several elements in one line.\</ahelp\> Create multi-line formulae by entering a \<emph\>NEWLINE\</emph\> command in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153737				0	en-ZA	Horizontal				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148388				0	en-ZA	Specifies the type of horizontal alignment for multi-line formulae.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148768				0	en-ZA	Left				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150566				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:RADIOBUTTON:RID_ALIGNDIALOG:1\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Aligns the selected elements of a formula to the left.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149709	21			0	en-ZA	Text is always aligned left. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154646				0	en-ZA	Centred				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150762				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:RADIOBUTTON:RID_ALIGNDIALOG:2\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Aligns the elements of a formula to the centre.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145204				0	en-ZA	Right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151264				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:RADIOBUTTON:RID_ALIGNDIALOG:3\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Aligns the elements of a formula to the right.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150261				0	en-ZA	Default				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153622				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:PUSHBUTTON:RID_ALIGNDIALOG:1\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Click here to save your changes as the default settings for new formulae.\</ahelp\> A security response will appear before saving.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Scaling				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091400.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153923				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>scaling; in %PRODUCTNAME Math\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153923				0	en-ZA	 \<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091400.xhp\" name=\"Scaling\"\>Scaling\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147173				0	en-ZA	More detailed information about scaling in \<emph\>\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Math\</emph\> as well as some examples can be found here. (The quotation marks in this text are for emphasis purposes only and are not part of the examples.)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091400.xhp	0	help	par_id3156316				0	en-ZA	The factorial is not scaled (example: "fact stack{a#b}" and "fact {a over b}") but is oriented using the baseline or centre of the arguments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150756				0	en-ZA	Brackets always have a fixed size as well. This applies to all symbols that can be used as brackets. Compare "(((a)))", "( stack{a#b#c})", "(a over b)."				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147570				0	en-ZA	Brackets preceded by "left" or "right", however, are always adjusted to the argument. See "left(left(left(a right)right)right)", "left(stack{a#b#c}right)", "left(a over b right)."				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145206				0	en-ZA	Some \<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091300.xhp\" name=\"Attributes\"\>Attributes\</link\> have fixed sizes; do not change these if they are placed above a long symbol.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154694				0	en-ZA	The spaces in the examples are required for the correct structure. You may not delete them when making entries in the Commands window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
