helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151129				0	en-ZA	Concatenate				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156102	39			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XCIRCY\"\>Inserts a \<emph\>concatenation sign\</emph\> with two placeholders. \</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>circ\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150906				0	en-ZA	By typing \<emph\><?>oplus<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window, you insert a \<emph\>circled plus operator\</emph\> in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151197				0	en-ZA	Type \<emph\><?>ominus<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window to insert a \<emph\>circled minus operator\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155082				0	en-ZA	Type \<emph\><?>odot<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window to insert a \<emph\>circled dot operator\</emph\> in the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154331				0	en-ZA	Type \<emph\><?>odivide<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window to insert a \<emph\>circled division operator\</emph\> in the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150089				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XWIDESLASHY\"\>Type \<emph\>a wideslash b\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window to produce two characters with a slash (from lower left to upper right) between them.\</ahelp\> The characters are set such that everything to the left of the slash is up, and everything to the right is down. This command is also available in the context menu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150024				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XWIDEBSLASHY\"\>Type \<emph\>a widebslash b\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window to produce two characters with a slash (from upper left to lower right) between them.\</ahelp\> The characters are set such that everything to the left of the slash is down, and everything to the right is up. This command is also available in the context menu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149376				0	en-ZA	Type \<emph\>sub\</emph\> or \<emph\>sup\</emph\> in the Commands window to add indexes and powers to the characters in your formula; for example, a sub 2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147398				0	en-ZA	When entering information manually in the Commands window, please note that a number of operators require spaces between the elements for the correct structure. This is especially true if you are using values instead of placeholders in your operators, for example, to construct a division 4 div 3 or a div b.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\02100000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Next Error				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\02100000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150299				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>error search; next error\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>finding ;errors in %PRODUCTNAME Math\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\02100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150299				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/02100000.xhp\" name=\"Next Error\"\>Next Error\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\02100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145387				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_NEXTERR\"\>Moves the cursor to the next error (moving right).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Fonts				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156261				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>fonts; in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formula fonts; defining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining; formula fonts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156261				0	en-ZA	Fonts				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153716				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"schriftartentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FONT\"\>Defines the fonts that can be applied to formula elements.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154639				0	en-ZA	Formula Fonts				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151187				0	en-ZA	You can define fonts for the variables, functions, numbers and inserted text that form the elements of your formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156318				0	en-ZA	The list boxes in the \<emph\>Fonts\</emph\> dialogue display a default font for all elements. To change to a different font, click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>, then select the element type. A new dialogue box appears. Select the desired font and check any desired attributes, then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. To set the changes as the default fonts, click the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148831				0	en-ZA	If you want to mark individual text segments with a font other than that used for the whole text, then enter the \<link href=\"text/smath/01/05010000.xhp\" name=\"FONT\"\>Font\</link\> command in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154262				0	en-ZA	Variables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147516				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_LISTBOX_RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG_1\"\>You can select the fonts for the variables in your formula.\</ahelp\> For example, in the formula x=SIN(y), x and y are variables, and will reflect the assigned font.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150708				0	en-ZA	Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152950				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:2\"\>Select the fonts for names and properties of functions.\</ahelp\> For example, the functions in the formula x=SIN(y) are =SIN( ).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149805				0	en-ZA	Numbers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154610				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:3\"\>You can select the fonts for the numbers in your formula.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153529				0	en-ZA	Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153780				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:4\"\>Define the fonts for the text in your formula here.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152963				0	en-ZA	Custom Fonts				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154566				0	en-ZA	In this section of the \<emph\>Fonts\</emph\> dialogue you can define fonts, with which you can format other text components in the formula. The three basic fonts \<emph\>Serif, Sans\</emph\> and \<emph\>Fixed\</emph\> are available. You can add any other font to each standard installed basic font. Every font installed on your system is available for you to use. Select the \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> button to expand the selection offered in the list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151315	17			0	en-ZA	These custom fonts are used if you set a different font with the FONT command in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153670				0	en-ZA	Serif				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151108				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:5\"\>You can specify the font to be used for the \<emph\>font serif\</emph\> format.\</ahelp\> Serifs are the small "guides" that can be seen, for example, at the bottom of a capital A when the Times serif font is used. Using serifs is quite helpful since it guides a reader's eye in a straight line and can speed up reading.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150836				0	en-ZA	Sans				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155900				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:6\"\>You can specify the font to be used for \<emph\>sans\</emph\> font formatting.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149340				0	en-ZA	Fixed				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154198				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:7\"\>You can specify the font to be used for \<emph\>fixed\</emph\> font formatting.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159194				0	en-ZA	Modify				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146932				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:MENUBUTTON:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:1\"\>Click one of the choices from this pop-up menu to access the \<link href=\"text/smath/01/05010100.xhp\" name=\"Fonts\"\>Fonts\</link\> dialogue, where you can define the font and attributes for the respective formula and for custom fonts.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149304				0	en-ZA	Default				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155186				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:PUSHBUTTON:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:2\"\>Click this button to save your changes as the default for all new formulae.\</ahelp\> After confirming the changes, click the \<emph\>Yes\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Text Mode				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05050000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147339				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>text mode in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulae; fit to text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147339				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/05050000.xhp\" name=\"Text Mode\"\>Text Mode\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150206				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_TEXTMODE\"\>Switches the text mode on or off. In text mode, formulae are displayed as the same height as a line of text.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Edit Symbols				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	bm_id2123477				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>new symbols in %PRODUCTNAME Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>symbols; adding in %PRODUCTNAME Math\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151075				0	en-ZA	Edit Symbols				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154513				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_MODALDIALOG_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG\"\>Use this dialogue to add symbols to a symbol set, to edit symbol sets, or to modify symbol notations.\</ahelp\> You can also define new symbol sets, assign names to symbols, or to modify existing symbol sets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146066				0	en-ZA	Old Symbol				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_COMBOBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_1\"\>Select the name of the current symbol.\</ahelp\> The symbol, the name of the symbol, and the set that the symbol belongs to are displayed in the left preview pane at the bottom of the dialogue box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154020				0	en-ZA	Old Symbol Set				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150209				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_COMBOBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_2\"\>This list box contains the name of the current symbol set. If you want, you can also select a different symbol set.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145386				0	en-ZA	Symbol				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148870				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_COMBOBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_4\"\>Lists the names for the symbols in the current symbol set. Select a name from the list or type a name for a newly added symbol.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150215				0	en-ZA	Adding a New Symbol				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3143233				0	en-ZA	To add a symbol to a symbol set, select a font in the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> box, and then click a symbol in symbols pane. In the \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\> box, type a name for the symbol. In the \<emph\>Symbol set\</emph\> list box, select a symbol set, or type a new name to create a new symbol set. The right preview pane displays the symbol that you selected. Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> and then \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151389				0	en-ZA	Modifying the Name of a Symbol				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147296				0	en-ZA	To change the name of a symbol, select the old name in the \<emph\>Old symbol\</emph\> list box. Then enter the new name in the \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\> box. Check whether the desired character is in the preview window before you click the \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> button. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157870				0	en-ZA	Symbol Set				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145825				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_COMBOBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_5\"\>The \<emph\>Symbol set\</emph\> list box contains the names of all existing symbol sets. You can modify a symbol set or create a new one.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154554				0	en-ZA	Creating a New Symbol Set				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145594				0	en-ZA	To create a new symbol set, type a name for it in the \<emph\>Symbol set\</emph\> list box and add at least one symbol. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the dialogue. The new symbol set is now available under the new name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153736				0	en-ZA	Font				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147374				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_LISTBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_1\"\>Displays the name of the current font and enables you to select a different font.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150564				0	en-ZA	Subset				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145295				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_LISTBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_LB_FONTS_SUBSET\"\>If you selected a non-symbol font in the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> list box, you can select a Unicode subset in which to place your new or edited symbol. When a subset has been selected, all symbols belonging to this subset of the current symbol set are displayed in the symbols list above.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148386				0	en-ZA	Typeface				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_COMBOBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_3\"\>The current typeface is displayed. You can change the typeface by selecting one from the list box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156262				0	en-ZA	Add				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153922				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_1\"\>Click this button to add the symbol shown in the right preview window to the current symbol set.\</ahelp\> It will be saved under the name displayed in the \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\> list box. You must specify a name under \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\> or \<emph\>Symbol Set\</emph\> to be able to use this button. Names cannot be used more than once.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150756				0	en-ZA	Modify				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147570				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_2\"\>Click this button to replace the name of the symbol shown in the left preview window (the old name is displayed in the \<emph\>Old symbol\</emph\> list box) with the new name you have entered in the \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\> list box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154640				0	en-ZA	Moving a Symbol to Another Symbol Set				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151174				0	en-ZA	As an example, to transfer the large ALPHA from the "Greek" set to the "Special" set, select the old set (Greek) and then the ALPHA symbol using the two top list boxes. The symbol appears in the left preview window. In the \<emph\>Symbol set\</emph\> list box, select the "Special" set. Click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> and then \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The ALPHA symbol is now only in the "Special" symbol set.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145414				0	en-ZA	Delete				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_3\"\>Click to remove the symbol shown in the left preview window from the current symbol set.\</ahelp\> There will be no security query. Deleting the last remaining symbol of a symbol set also deletes the symbol set.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	en-ZA	You can also click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\> at any time to close the dialogue without saving any of the changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\02090000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Previous Marker				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\02090000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153770				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>markers; previous\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>placeholders; previous marker\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\02090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153770				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/02090000.xhp\" name=\"Previous Marker\"\>Previous Marker\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\02090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_PREVMARK\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Moves the cursor to the previous marker (to the left).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\02090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	en-ZA	"Markers" are placeholders. They take the form of <?> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Zoom Out				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03050000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147338				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>views; zooming out $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formula display sizes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulae; zooming out\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>zooming out on formula display\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
