helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	hd_id5676442				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"text\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/text.xhp\" name=\"Entering Text\"\>Entering Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	hd_id8509170				0	en-ZA	How to enter direct text strings that do not get interpreted?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	par_id337229				0	en-ZA	Some text strings get interpreted as operators automatically. Sometimes this is not what you want. If you want to write W\<emph\>*\</emph\> (a letter with a superscripted asterisk), the asterisk will be interpreted as a multiplication operator. Enclose the direct text within double quotes or add spaceholders.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D0				0	en-ZA	Examples:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	par_id521866				0	en-ZA	An imported MathType formula contains the following string				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	par_id9413739				0	en-ZA	W rSup { size 8{*} }				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	par_id755943				0	en-ZA	If you have set up Math to convert imported MathType formulae (in \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - Microsoft Office), you see the formula with a placeholder instead of the asterisk.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	par_id5988952				0	en-ZA	Change {*} to {} * {} as in the following formula:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	par_id3304544				0	en-ZA	W rSup { size 8{} * {} }				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	par_id4941557				0	en-ZA	You can also use W^"*" to enter the character as direct text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	par_id9961851				0	en-ZA	Some formulae start with an = sign. Use "=" to enter that character as direct text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Manually Aligning Formula Parts				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156384				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>aligning; characters in %PRODUCTNAME Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formula parts; manually aligning\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156384				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"align\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/align.xhp\" name=\"Manually Aligning Formula Parts\"\>Manually Aligning Formula Parts\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154657				0	en-ZA	How do you align characters in $[officename] Math quickly and easily?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	par_id3150249				0	en-ZA	To accomplish this, you must define empty groups and character strings. They do not require any space, but carry information that helps in the alignment process.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	par_id3153912				0	en-ZA	To create empty groups, enter curly brackets \<emph\>{}\</emph\> in the Commands window. In the following example, the goal is to achieve a line break so that the plus signs are beneath one another, even though one less character is entered in the upper line:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	par_id3153246				0	en-ZA	a+a+a+{} newline {}{}{}{}{}a+a+a+a				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	par_id3143229				0	en-ZA	Empty character strings are a simple way to ensure that texts and formulae are left-aligned. They are defined using double inverted commas "" . Make sure you do not use any typographic inverted commas. Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	par_id3153809				0	en-ZA	"A further example." newline a+b newline ""c-d				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\main.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Instructions for Using $[officename] Math				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\main.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147341				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>$[officename] Math;general instructions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>instructions; $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Equation Editor, see $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\main.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147341				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"main\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/main.xhp\" name=\"Instructions for Using $[officename] Math\"\>Instructions for Using $[officename] Math\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\main.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150199				0	en-ZA	Entering and Editing Formulae				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Merging Formula Parts in Brackets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152596				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>brackets; merging formula parts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formula parts; merging\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fractions in formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>merging;formula parts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"brackets\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/brackets.xhp\" name=\"Merging Formula Parts in Brackets\"\>Merging Formula Parts in Brackets\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154511				0	en-ZA	Inserting fractions into formulae				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	par_id3146971				0	en-ZA	In the case of a fraction whose numerator and denominator consist of a product, a sum, and so on, the values that belong together must be bracketed together.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	par_id3149021				0	en-ZA	Use the following syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	par_id3083280				0	en-ZA	{a + c} over 2 = m				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	par_id3154703				0	en-ZA	or				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	par_id3150297				0	en-ZA	m = {a + c} over 2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\attributes.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Changing Default Attributes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\attributes.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145792				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>attributes; changing in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>font attributes;changing defaults\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;changing default attributes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;changing default formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;default formatting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\attributes.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145792				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"attributes\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/attributes.xhp\" name=\"Changing Default Attributes\"\>Changing Default Attributes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\attributes.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154484				0	en-ZA	Can default formats in $[officename] Math be modified?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\attributes.xhp	0	help	par_id3148870				0	en-ZA	Some parts of formulae are always formatted bold or italic by default.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\attributes.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210				0	en-ZA	You can remove these attributes using "nbold" and "nitalic". Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\attributes.xhp	0	help	par_id3143231				0	en-ZA	a + b				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\attributes.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810				0	en-ZA	nitalic a + bold b.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\attributes.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	en-ZA	In the second formula, the a is not italic. The b is bold. You cannot change the plus sign by this method.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\parentheses.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Inserting Brackets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\parentheses.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153415				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>brackets; inserting in %PRODUCTNAME Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;brackets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>distances between brackets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\parentheses.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153415				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"parentheses\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/parentheses.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Brackets\"\>Inserting Brackets\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\parentheses.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150751				0	en-ZA	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Math, can brackets be shown separately so that the distance between them is freely definable?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\parentheses.xhp	0	help	par_id3083281				0	en-ZA	You can set individual brackets using "left" and "right", but the distance between the brackets will not be fixed, as they adapt to the argument. Nevertheless, there is a way to display brackets so that the distance between them is fixed. To accomplish this, place a "\\" (backslash) before the normal brackets. These brackets now behave like any other symbol and the alignment is the same as with other symbols:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\parentheses.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	en-ZA	left lbrace x right none				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\parentheses.xhp	0	help	par_id3148489				0	en-ZA	size *2 langle x rangle				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\parentheses.xhp	0	help	par_id3150344				0	en-ZA	size *2 \\langle x \\rangle				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Shortcuts ($[officename] Math Accessibility)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149018				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; $[officename] Math shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Shortcuts ($[officename] Math Accessibility)\"\>Shortcuts ($[officename] Math Accessibility)\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150298				0	en-ZA	You can control $[officename] Math without a mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150343				0	en-ZA	Inserting a Formula Directly				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154659				0	en-ZA	If you want to insert a formula into a text document, and you already know the correct writing, you can proceed as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	en-ZA	Write the formula into your text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153915				0	en-ZA	Select the formula				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	en-ZA	Choose the command \<emph\>Insert - Object - Formula\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154767				0	en-ZA	Inserting a Formula using a Window				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149875				0	en-ZA	If you want to use the $[officename] Math interface to edit a formula, choose the command \<emph\>Insert - Object - Formula\</emph\> without any text selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	en-ZA	The cursor waits in the Commands window and you can type the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Working with Limits				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	bm_id8404492				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>limits;in sums/integrals\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>integral limits\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	hd_id1892147				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"limits\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/limits.xhp\"\>Working with Limits\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	hd_id9881893				0	en-ZA	How can I define the limits in a Sum or Integral formula?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id6504409				0	en-ZA	You want to insert a summation formula like "summation of s^k from k = 0 to n" at the cursor in a Writer text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id8811304				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Object - Formula\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id9641712				0	en-ZA	To enable lower and upper limits, click additionally the \<emph\>Upper and Lower Limits\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id3304239				0	en-ZA	In the input window, the first placeholder or marker is selected, and you can start to enter the lower limit: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id8679158				0	en-ZA	k = 0				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id8471327				0	en-ZA	Press F4 to advance to the next marker, and enter the upper limit:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id4731894				0	en-ZA	n				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id759300				0	en-ZA	Press F4 to advance to the next marker, and enter the summand:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id651875				0	en-ZA	s^k				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id6756187				0	en-ZA	Now the formula is complete. Click into your text document outside the formula to leave the formula editor.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id5866267				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Object - Formula\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id1965697				0	en-ZA	Click in the input window and enter the following line:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id9004486				0	en-ZA	int from{a} to{b} f(x)`dx				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id3877071				0	en-ZA	If you don't like the font of the letters f and x, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Fonts\</item\> and select other fonts. Click the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> button to use the new fonts as default from now on.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id3021332				0	en-ZA	If you need the formula within a line of text, the limits increase the line height. You can choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Text Mode\</item\> to place the limits besides the Sum or Integral symbol, which reduces the line height.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id260322				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03090909.xhp\"\>Example of Integral and Sum ranges\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\newline.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Entering Line Breaks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\newline.xhp	0	help	bm_id1295205				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>line breaks; in formulae\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulae;line breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wrapping text;in formulae\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\newline.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146970				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"newline\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/newline.xhp\" name=\"Entering Line Breaks\"\>Entering Line Breaks\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\newline.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147339				0	en-ZA	How to write formulae in $[officename] Math over two lines (with manual line break):				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\newline.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	en-ZA	Create a line break by using the "newline" command. Everything coming after the line break is placed on the next line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Entering Comments				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155961				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>comments; entering in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;comments in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155961				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"comment\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/comment.xhp\" name=\"Entering Comments\"\>Entering Comments\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154657				0	en-ZA	How does one attach comments that don't appear in the document to a formula?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	par_id3149499				0	en-ZA	A comment begins with a double percent sign \<emph\>%%\</emph\>, and extends to the next line-end character (Enter key). Everything that lies in between is ignored and is not printed out. If there are percent signs in the text, they are treated as part of the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D0				0	en-ZA	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D3				0	en-ZA	a^2+b^2=c^2 %% Pythagorean theorem.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	InputBox Function [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148932				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>InputBox function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148932				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03010201.xhp\" name=\"InputBox Function [Runtime]\"\>InputBox Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3151262				0	en-ZA	Displays a prompt in a dialogue at which the user can input text. The input is assigned to a variable.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3151100				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>InputBox\</emph\> statement is a convenient method of entering text through a dialogue. Confirm the input by clicking OK or pressing Return. The input is returned as the function return value. If you close the dialogue with Cancel, \<emph\>InputBox\</emph\> returns a zero-length string ("").				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152347				0	en-ZA	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3159201	5			0	en-ZA	InputBox (Msg As String[, Title As String[, Default As String[, x_pos As Integer, y_pos As Integer]]]]) 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150713				0	en-ZA	Return value:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090				0	en-ZA	String				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346				0	en-ZA	Parameter:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153311	9			0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Msg\</emph\>: String expression displayed as the message in the dialogue box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315	10			0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Title\</emph\>: String expression displayed in the title bar of the dialogue box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154307	11			0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Default\</emph\>: String expression displayed in the text box as default if no other input is given.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3147573	12			0	en-ZA	\<emph\>x_pos\</emph\>: Integer expression that specifies the horizontal position of the dialogue. The position is an absolute coordinate and does not refer to the window of the office application.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024	13			0	en-ZA	\<emph\>y_pos\</emph\>: Integer expression that specifies the vertical position of the dialogue. The position is an absolute coordinate and does not refer to the window of the office application.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153897				0	en-ZA	If \<emph\>x_pos\</emph\> and \<emph\>y_pos\</emph\> are omitted, the dialogue is centred on the screen. The position is specified in \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/00000002.xhp#twips\" name=\"twips\"\>twips\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456				0	en-ZA	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
