helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	GetDefaultContext Function [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132500.xhp	0	help	bm_id4761192				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>GetDefaultContext function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132500.xhp	0	help	par_idN10580				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03132500.xhp\"\>GetDefaultContext Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132500.xhp	0	help	par_idN10590				0	en-ZA	Returns the default context of the process service factory, if existent, else returns a null reference. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132500.xhp	0	help	par_idN10593				0	en-ZA	This runtime function returns the default component context to be used, if instantiating services via XmultiServiceFactory. See the \<item type=\"literal\"\>Professional UNO\</item\> chapter in the \<item type=\"literal\"\>Developer's Guide\</item\> on \<link href=\"http://api.openoffice.org\"\>api.openoffice.org\</link\> for more information.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	CBool Function [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150616				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>CBool function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150616				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03100100.xhp\" name=\"CBool Function [Runtime]\"\>CBool Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136				0	en-ZA	Converts a string comparison or numeric comparison to a Boolean expression, or converts a single numeric expression to a Boolean expression.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	en-ZA	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149514				0	en-ZA	CBool (Expression1 {= | <> | < | > | <= | >=} Expression2) or CBool (Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156152				0	en-ZA	Return value:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	en-ZA	Bool				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147530				0	en-ZA	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156344				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Expression1, Expression2:\</emph\> Any string or numeric expressions that you want to compare. If the expressions match, the \<emph\>CBool\</emph\> function returns \<emph\>True\</emph\>, otherwise \<emph\>False\</emph\> is returned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149655				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Any numeric expression that you want to convert. If the expression equals 0, \<emph\>False\</emph\> is returned, otherwise \<emph\>True\</emph\> is returned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	en-ZA	The following example uses the \<emph\>CBool\</emph\> function to evaluate the value that is returned by the \<emph\>Instr\</emph\> function. The function checks if the word "and" is found in the sentence that was entered by the user.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156212				0	en-ZA	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147288				0	en-ZA	Sub ExampleCBool				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	en-ZA	Dim sText As String				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155132				0	en-ZA	sText = InputBox("Please enter a short sentence:")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	en-ZA	REM Proof if the word »and« appears in the sentence.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146984				0	en-ZA	REM Instead of the command line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	en-ZA	REM If Instr(Input, "and")<>0 Then...				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014				0	en-ZA	REM the CBool function is applied as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155413				0	en-ZA	If CBool(Instr(sText, "and")) Then				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152940				0	en-ZA	MsgBox "The word »and« appears in the sentence you entered!"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153954				0	en-ZA	EndIf				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152886				0	en-ZA	End Sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Libraries, Modules and Dialogues				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147317				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/01020500.xhp\" name=\"Libraries, Modules and Dialogs\"\>Libraries, Modules and Dialogs\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427				0	en-ZA	The following describes the basic use of libraries, modules and dialogues in $[officename] Basic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	en-ZA	$[officename] Basic provides tools to help you structuring your projects. It supports various "units" which enable you to group individual SUBS and FUNCTIONS in a Basic project.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148575				0	en-ZA	Libraries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011				0	en-ZA	Libraries serve as a tool for organising modules, and can either be attached to a document or a template. When the document or a template is saved, all modules contained in the library are automatically saved as well.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151112				0	en-ZA	A library can contain up to 16,000 modules.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149262				0	en-ZA	Modules				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	en-ZA	A module contains SUBS and FUNCTIONS along with variable declarations. The length of the program that can be saved in a module is limited to 64 KB. If more space is required you can divide a $[officename] Basic project among several modules, and then save them in a single library.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152577				0	en-ZA	Dialogue Modules				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	en-ZA	Dialogue modules contain dialogue definitions, including the dialogue box properties, the properties of each dialogue element and the events assigned. Since a dialogue module can only contain a single dialogue, they are often referred to as "dialogues".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Time Statement [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145090				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>Time statement\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145090				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030302.xhp\"\>Time Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984				0	en-ZA	This function returns the current system time as a string in the format "HH:MM:SS".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346				0	en-ZA	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	en-ZA	Time				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	en-ZA	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Text:\</emph\> Any string expression that specifies the new time in the format "HH:MM:SS".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145173				0	en-ZA	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281				0	en-ZA	Sub ExampleTime				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	en-ZA	MsgBox Time,0,"The time is"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123				0	en-ZA	end sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Month Function [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153127				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>Month function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153127				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030104.xhp\" name=\"Month Function [Runtime]\"\>Month Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	en-ZA	Returns the month of a year from a serial date that is generated by the DateSerial or the DateValue function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	en-ZA	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150398				0	en-ZA	Month (Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154366				0	en-ZA	Return value:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154125				0	en-ZA	Integer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150768				0	en-ZA	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Numeric expression that contains the serial date number that is used to determine the month of the year.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153770	9			0	en-ZA	This function is the opposite of the \<emph\>DateSerial \</emph\>function. It returns the month in the year that corresponds to the serial date that is generated by \<emph\>DateSerial\</emph\> or \<emph\>DateValue\</emph\>. For example, the expression				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426				0	en-ZA	Print Month(DateSerial(1994, 12, 20))				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366				0	en-ZA	returns the value 12.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146923				0	en-ZA	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	en-ZA	Sub ExampleMonth				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	en-ZA	MsgBox "" & Month(Now) ,64,"The current month"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012				0	en-ZA	End sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Put Statement [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150360				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>Put statement\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150360				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020204.xhp\" name=\"Put Statement [Runtime]\"\>Put Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3154909				0	en-ZA	Writes a record to a relative file or a sequence of bytes to a binary file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281				0	en-ZA	See also: \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020201.xhp\" name=\"Get\"\>\<item type=\"literal\"\>Get\</item\>\</link\> statement				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	en-ZA	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3155132				0	en-ZA	Put [#] FileNumber As Integer, [position], Variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153190				0	en-ZA	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>FileNumber:\</emph\> Any integer expression that defines the file that you want to write to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411	8			0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Position: \</emph\>For relative files (random access files), the number of the record that you want to write.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	en-ZA	For binary files (binary access), the position of the byte in the file where you want to start writing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3153729				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Variable:\</emph\> Name of the variable that you want to write to the file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	en-ZA	Note for relative files: If the contents of this variable does not match the length of the record that is specified in the \<emph\>Len\</emph\> clause of the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> statement, the space between the end of the newly written record and the next record is padded with existing data from the file that you are writing to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	en-ZA	Note for binary files: The contents of the variables are written to the specified position, and the file pointer is inserted directly after the last byte. No space is left between the records.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154491				0	en-ZA	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3149410				0	en-ZA	Sub ExampleRandomAccess				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	en-ZA	Dim iNumber As Integer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	en-ZA	Dim sText As Variant REM Must be a variant type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	en-ZA	Dim aFile As String				2002-02-02 02:02:02
