helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020203.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	en-ZA	Reads strings from a sequential file into a variable.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150447				0	en-ZA	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020203.xhp	0	help	par_id3147229	4			0	en-ZA	Line Input #FileNumber As Integer, Var As String 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145173				0	en-ZA	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020203.xhp	0	help	par_id3161832	6			0	en-ZA	\<emph\>FileNumber: \</emph\>Number of the file that contains the data that you want to read. The file must have been opened in advance with the Open statement using the key word INPUT.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020203.xhp	0	help	par_id3151119				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>var:\</emph\> The name of the variable that stores the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	en-ZA	With the \<emph\>Line Input#\</emph\> statement, you can read strings from an open file into a variable. String variables are read line-by-line up to the first carriage return (Asc=13) or linefeed (Asc=10). Line end marks are not included in the resulting string.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
