helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	en-ZA	DIM sPar3 AS STRING				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	en-ZA	Dim declares local variables within subroutines. Global variables are declared with the PUBLIC or the PRIVATE statement.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156443				0	en-ZA	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149412				0	en-ZA	[ReDim]Dim VarName [(start To end)] [As VarType][, VarName2 [(start To end)] [As VarType][,...]]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147397				0	en-ZA	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>VarName:\</emph\> Any variable or array name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147125				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Start, End:\</emph\> Numerical values or constants that define the number of elements (NumberElements=(end-start)+1) and the index range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153877				0	en-ZA	Start and End can be numerical expressions if ReDim is applied at the procedure level.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153510				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>VarType:\</emph\> Key word that declares the data type of a variable.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154015				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Keyword:\</emph\> Variable type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153949				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Bool:\</emph\> Boolean variable (True, False)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156275				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Currency:\</emph\> Currency-Variable (Currency with 4 Decimal places)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156057				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Date:\</emph\> Date variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148405				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Double:\</emph\> Double-precision floating-point variable (1,79769313486232 x 10E308 - 4,94065645841247 x 10E-324)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148916				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Integer:\</emph\> Integer variable (-32768 - 32767)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150045				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Long:\</emph\> Long integer variable (-2.147.483.648 - 2.147.483.647)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149255				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Object:\</emph\> Object variable (Note: this variable can only subsequently be defined with Set!)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155937				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Single:\</emph\> Single-precision floating-point variable (3,402823 x 10E38 - 1,401298 x 10E-45).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151251				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>String:\</emph\> String variable consisting of a maximum of 64,000 ASCII characters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>[Variant]:\</emph\> Variant variable type (contains all types, specified by definition). If a key word is not specified, variables are automatically defined as Variant Type, unless a statement from DefBool to DefVar is used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146316				0	en-ZA	In $[officename] Basic, you do not need to declare variables explicitly. However, you need to declare an array before you can use them. You can declare a variable with the Dim statement, using commas to separate multiple declarations. To declare a variable type, enter a type-declaration character following the name or use a corresponding key word.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149924				0	en-ZA	$[officename] Basic supports single or multi-dimensional arrays that are defined by a specified variable type. Arrays are suitable if the program contains lists or tables that you want to edit. The advantage of arrays is that it is possible to address individual elements according to indexes, which can be formulated as numeric expressions or variables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	en-ZA	Arrays are declared with the Dim statement. There are two methods to define the index range:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154662				0	en-ZA	DIM text(20) as String REM 21 elements numbered from 0 to 20				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155604				0	en-ZA	DIM text(5 to 25) as String REM 21 elements numbered from 5 to 25				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151274				0	en-ZA	DIM text(-15 to 5) as String REM 21 elements (including 0)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152774				0	en-ZA	REM numbered from -15 to 5				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150829				0	en-ZA	Two-dimensional data field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149529				0	en-ZA	DIM text(20,2) as String REM 63 elements; form 0 to 20 level 1, from 0 to 20 level 2 and from 0 to 20 level 3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159239				0	en-ZA	You can declare an array types as dynamic if a ReDim statement defines the number of dimensions in the subroutine or the function that contains the array. Generally, you can only define an array dimension once, and you cannot modify it. Within a subroutine, you can declare an array with ReDim. You can only define dimensions with numeric expressions. This ensures that the fields are only as large as necessary.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150344				0	en-ZA	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150206				0	en-ZA	Sub ExampleDim1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154201				0	en-ZA	Dim sVar As String				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146134				0	en-ZA	Dim iVar As Integer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154657				0	en-ZA	sVar = "Office"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148459				0	en-ZA	End Sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3166424				0	en-ZA	Sub ExampleDim2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149036				0	en-ZA	REM Two-dimensional data field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149737				0	en-ZA	Dim stext(20,2) as String				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153782				0	en-ZA	Const sDim as String = " Dimension:"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150518				0	en-ZA	for i = 0 to 20				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428				0	en-ZA	for ii = 0 to 2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152994				0	en-ZA	stext(i,ii) = str(i) & sDim & str(ii)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150202				0	en-ZA	next ii				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154370				0	en-ZA	next i				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156166				0	en-ZA	for i = 0 to 20				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148815				0	en-ZA	for ii = 0 to 2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146981				0	en-ZA	msgbox stext(i,ii)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155125				0	en-ZA	next ii				2002-02-02 02:02:02
