helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155087				0	en-ZA	End Sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Shell Function [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150040				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>Shell function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150040				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03130500.xhp\" name=\"Shell Function [Runtime]\"\>Shell Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	en-ZA	Starts another application and defines the respective window style, if necessary.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	en-ZA	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576	5			0	en-ZA	Shell (Pathname As String[, Windowstyle As Integer][, Param As String][, bSync]) 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149235				0	en-ZA	Parameter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154306				0	en-ZA	Pathname				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	en-ZA	Complete path and program name of the program that you want to start.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150771				0	en-ZA	Windowstyle				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609				0	en-ZA	Optional integer expression that specifies the style of the window that the program is executed in. The following values are possible:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148663				0	en-ZA	0				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	en-ZA	The focus is on the hidden program window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123				0	en-ZA	1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3144760				0	en-ZA	The focus is on the program window in standard size.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	en-ZA	2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148451				0	en-ZA	The focus is on the minimised program window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149561				0	en-ZA	3				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3146921				0	en-ZA	focus is on the maximised program window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481				0	en-ZA	4				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	en-ZA	Standard size program window, without focus.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3145271				0	en-ZA	6				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3152938				0	en-ZA	Minimised program window, focus remains on the active window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	en-ZA	10				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151112				0	en-ZA	Full-screen display.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150419				0	en-ZA	Param				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149412				0	en-ZA	Any string expression that specifies the command line that want to pass.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148456				0	en-ZA	bSync				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154096				0	en-ZA	If this value is set to \<emph\>true\</emph\>, the \<emph\>Shell\</emph\> command and all $[officename] tasks wait until the shell process completes. If the value is set to \<emph\>false\</emph\>, the shell returns directly. The default value is \<emph\>false\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154270				0	en-ZA	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153948				0	en-ZA	Sub ExampleShellForWin				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154479				0	en-ZA	 Shell("c:\\windows\\calc.exe",2)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03130500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153709				0	en-ZA	end sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090405.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	FreeLibrary Function [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090405.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143270				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>FreeLibrary function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090405.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143270				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090405.xhp\" name=\"FreeLibrary Function [Runtime]\"\>FreeLibrary Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090405.xhp	0	help	par_id3147559				0	en-ZA	Releases DLLs that were loaded by a Declare statement. A released DLL is automatically reloaded if one of its functions is called. See also: \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090403.xhp\" name=\"Declare\"\>Declare\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090405.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148550				0	en-ZA	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090405.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361				0	en-ZA	FreeLibrary (LibName As String)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090405.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153380				0	en-ZA	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090405.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>LibName:\</emph\> String expression that specifies the name of the DLL.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090405.xhp	0	help	par_id3146923				0	en-ZA	FreeLibrary can only release DLLs that are loaded during Basic runtime.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090405.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153363				0	en-ZA	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090405.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	en-ZA	Declare Sub MyMessageBeep Lib "user32.dll" Alias "MessageBeep" ( long )				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090405.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	en-ZA	Sub ExampleDeclare				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090405.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618				0	en-ZA	Dim lValue As Long				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090405.xhp	0	help	par_id3147350				0	en-ZA	lValue = 5000				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090405.xhp	0	help	par_id3148648				0	en-ZA	MyMessageBeep( lValue )				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090405.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	en-ZA	FreeLibrary("user32.dll" )				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090405.xhp	0	help	par_id3149412				0	en-ZA	End Sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	TimeSerial Function [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143271				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>TimeSerial function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143271				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030205.xhp\" name=\"TimeSerial Function [Runtime]\"\>TimeSerial Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3156344				0	en-ZA	Calculates a serial time value for the specified hour, minute, and second parameters that are passed as numeric value. You can then use this value to calculate the difference between times.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146794				0	en-ZA	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3150792				0	en-ZA	TimeSerial (hour, minute, second)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148797				0	en-ZA	Return value:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	en-ZA	Date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154124				0	en-ZA	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3153193				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>hour:\</emph\> Any integer expression that indicates the hour of the time that is used to determine the serial time value. Valid values: 0-23.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3159252				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>minute:\</emph\> Any integer expression that indicates the minute of the time that is used to determine the serial time value. In general, use values between 0 and 59. However, you can also use values that lie outside of this range, where the number of minutes influence the hour value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3161831				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>second:\</emph\> Any integer expression that indicates the second of the time that is used to determine the serial time value. In general, you can use values between 0 and 59. However, you can also use values that lie outside of this range, where the number seconds influences the minute value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Examples:\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3153952				0	en-ZA	12, -5, 45 corresponds to 11, 55, 45				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3147349				0	en-ZA	12, 61, 45 corresponds to 13, 2, 45				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426				0	en-ZA	12, 20, -2 corresponds to 12, 19, 58				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3153365				0	en-ZA	12, 20, 63 corresponds to 12, 21, 4				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3146985				0	en-ZA	You can use the TimeSerial function to convert any time into a single value that you can use to calculate time differences.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3155308				0	en-ZA	The TimeSerial function returns the type Variant with VarType 7 (Date). This value is stored internally as a double-precision number between 0 and 0.9999999999. As opposed to the DateSerial or DateValue function, where the serial date values are calculated as days relative to a fixed date, you can calculate with values returned by the TimeSerial function, but you cannot evaluate them.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3149482				0	en-ZA	In the TimeValue function, you can pass a string as a parameter containing the time. For the TimeSerial function, however, you can pass the individual parameters (hour, minute, second) as separate numeric expressions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154790				0	en-ZA	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
