helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150359				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Expression:\</emph\> Any string or numeric expression that you want to convert.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100300.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864				0	en-ZA	When you convert a string expression, the date and time must be entered in the format MM.DD.YYYY HH.MM.SS, as defined by the \<emph\>DateValue\</emph\> and \<emph\>TimeValue\</emph\> function conventions. In numeric expressions, values to the left of the decimal represent the date, beginning from December 31, 1899. Values to the right of the decimal represent the time.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156422				0	en-ZA	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
