helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3146781				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Modules\</emph\> tab or the \<emph\>Dialogs\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3159206				0	en-ZA	Select the library where the module will be inserted and click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3152389				0	en-ZA	Enter a name for the module or the dialogue and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152872				0	en-ZA	Renaming a Module or Dialogue				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3159230				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> or click the \<emph\>Select Module\</emph\> icon in the Basic IDE to open the \<emph\>Macro Organizer\</emph\> dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150046				0	en-ZA	Click the module to be renamed twice, with a pause between the clicks. Enter the new name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153801				0	en-ZA	In the Basic IDE, right-click the name of the module or dialogue in the tabs at the bottom of the screen, choose \<emph\>Rename\</emph\> and type in the new name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155526				0	en-ZA	Press Enter to confirm your changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
