helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153527				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03104000.xhp\" name=\"IsMissing function [Runtime]\"\>IsMissing function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153825				0	en-ZA	Tests if a function is called with an optional parameter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150669				0	en-ZA	See also: \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03104100.xhp\" name=\"Optional\"\>Optional\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145611				0	en-ZA	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154924				0	en-ZA	IsMissing( ArgumentName )				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145069				0	en-ZA	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149457				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>ArgumentName:\</emph\> the name of an optional argument.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150398				0	en-ZA	If the IsMissing function is called by the ArgumentName, then True is returned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	en-ZA	See also \<link href=\"text/sbasic/guide/sample_code.xhp\" name=\"Examples\"\>Examples\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	If...Then...Else Statement [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154422				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>If statement\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154422				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090101.xhp\" name=\"If...Then...Else Statement [Runtime]\"\>If...Then...Else Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	en-ZA	Defines one or more statement blocks that you only want to execute if a given condition is True.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	en-ZA	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126				0	en-ZA	If condition=true Then Statement block [ElseIf condition=true Then] Statement block [Else] Statement block EndIf\<br/\>Instead of Else If you can write ElseIf, instead of End If you can write EndIf.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155419				0	en-ZA	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153062				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> statement executes program blocks depending on given conditions. When $[officename] Basic encounters an \<emph\>If\</emph\> statement, the condition is tested. If the condition is True, all subsequent statements up to the next \<emph\>Else\</emph\> or \<emph\>ElseIf\</emph\> statement are executed. If the condition is False, and an \<emph\>ElseIf\</emph\> statement follows, $[officename] Basic tests the next condition and executes the following statements if the condition is True. If False, the program continues either with the next \<emph\>ElseIf\</emph\> or \<emph\>Else\</emph\> statement. Statements following \<emph\>Else\</emph\> are executed only if none of the previously tested conditions were True. After all conditions are evaluated, and the corresponding statements executed, the program continues with the statement following \<emph\>EndIf\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	en-ZA	You can nest multiple \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> statements.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Else\</emph\> and \<emph\>ElseIf\</emph\> statements are optional.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152939				0	en-ZA	You can use \<emph\>GoTo\</emph\> and \<emph\>GoSub\</emph\> to jump out of an \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> block, but not to jump into an \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> structure.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	en-ZA	The following example enables you to enter the expiration date of a product, and determines if the expiration date has passed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152576				0	en-ZA	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011				0	en-ZA	Sub ExampleIfThenDate				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	en-ZA	Dim sDate as String				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	en-ZA	Dim sToday as String				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	en-ZA	sDate = InputBox("Enter the expiration date (MM.DD.YYYY)")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154943				0	en-ZA	sDate = Right$(sDate, 4) + Mid$(sDate, 4, 2) + Left$(sDate, 2)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154098				0	en-ZA	sToday = Date$				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3144765				0	en-ZA	sToday = Right$(sToday, 4)+ Mid$(sToday, 4, 2) + Left$(sToday, 2)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154792				0	en-ZA	If sDate < sToday Then				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155601				0	en-ZA	MsgBox "The expiration date has passed"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146972				0	en-ZA	ElseIf sDate > sToday Then				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146912				0	en-ZA	MsgBox "The expiration date has not yet passed"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153710				0	en-ZA	Else				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	en-ZA	MsgBox "The expiration date is today"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154361				0	en-ZA	End If				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148405				0	en-ZA	End Sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	LSet Statement [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143268				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>LSet statement\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143268				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03120304.xhp\" name=\"LSet Statement [Runtime]\"\>LSet Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	en-ZA	Aligns a string to the left of a string variable, or copies a variable of a user-defined type to another variable of a different user-defined type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145317				0	en-ZA	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984				0	en-ZA	LSet Var As String = Text or LSet Var1 = Var2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143271				0	en-ZA	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3145610				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Var:\</emph\> Any String variable that contains the string that you want align to the left.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3154346				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Text:\</emph\> String that you want to align to the left of the string variable.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Var1:\</emph\> Name of the user-defined type variable that you want to copy to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Var2:\</emph\> Name of the user-defined type variable that you want to copy from.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3154686				0	en-ZA	If the string is shorter than the string variable, \<emph\>LSet\</emph\> left-aligns the string within the string variable. Any remaining positions in the string variable are replaced by spaces. If the string is longer than the string variable, only the leftmost characters up to the length of the string variable are copied. With the \<emph\>LSet\</emph\> statement, you can also copy a user-defined type variable to another variable of the same type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156282				0	en-ZA	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3153193				0	en-ZA	Sub ExampleRLSet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3150768				0	en-ZA	Dim sVar As String				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3150447				0	en-ZA	Dim sExpr As String				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3149561				0	en-ZA	sVar = String(40,"*")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	en-ZA	sExpr = "SBX"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3152940				0	en-ZA	REM Align "SBX" within the 40-character reference string				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3148647				0	en-ZA	REM Replace asterisks with spaces				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	en-ZA	RSet sVar = sExpr				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3153365				0	en-ZA	Print ">"; sVar; "<"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	en-ZA	sVar = String(5,"*")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3147436				0	en-ZA	sExpr = "123457896"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3146923				0	en-ZA	RSet sVar = sExpr				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3151114				0	en-ZA	Print ">"; sVar; "<"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	en-ZA	sVar = String(40,"*")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3145253				0	en-ZA	sExpr = "SBX"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3151075				0	en-ZA	REM Left-align "SBX" within the 40-character reference string				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3147126				0	en-ZA	LSet sVar = sExpr				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3154792				0	en-ZA	Print ">"; sVar; "<"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3154942				0	en-ZA	sVar = String(5,"*")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603				0	en-ZA	sExpr = "123456789"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3150716				0	en-ZA	LSet sVar = sExpr				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	en-ZA	Print ">"; sVar; "<"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	en-ZA	End Sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
