helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150952				0	en-ZA	...if a message was received.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153299				0	en-ZA	Assigning a Macro to an Event				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147244				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146098				0	en-ZA	Select whether you want the assignment to be globally valid or just valid in the current document in the \<emph\>Save In\</emph\> listbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150431				0	en-ZA	Select the event from the \<emph\>Event\</emph\> list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148742				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Macro\</emph\> and select the macro to be assigned to the selected event.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146321				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to assign the macro.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147414				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154581				0	en-ZA	Removing the Assignment of a Macro to an Event				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146883				0	en-ZA	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155909				0	en-ZA	Select whether you want to remove a global assignment or an assignment that is just valid in the current document by selecting the option in the \<emph\>Save In\</emph\> listbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159129				0	en-ZA	Select the event that contains the assignment to be removed from the \<emph\>Event\</emph\> list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149143				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Remove\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149351				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Seek Statement [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159413				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>Seek statement\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159413				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020305.xhp\" name=\"Seek Statement [Runtime]\"\>Seek Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id3153381				0	en-ZA	Sets the position for the next writing or reading in a file that was opened with the Open statement.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id2100589				0	en-ZA	For random access files, the Seek statement sets the number of the next record to be accessed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id5444807				0	en-ZA	For all other files, the Seek statement sets the byte position at which the next operation is to occur.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	en-ZA	See also: \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020103.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>Open\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020304.xhp\" name=\"Seek\"\>Seek\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145785				0	en-ZA	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	en-ZA	Seek[#FileNumber], Position (As Long)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154321				0	en-ZA	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id3153952	9			0	en-ZA	\<emph\>FileNumber: \</emph\>The data channel number used in the Open statement.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366	10			0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Position: \</emph\>Position for the next writing or reading. Position can be a number between 1 and 2,147,483,647. According to the file type, the position indicates the number of the record (files in the Random mode) or the byte position (files in the Binary, Output, Append or Input mode). The first byte in a file is position 1, the second byte is position 2, and so on.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\05060700.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Macro				2002-02-02 02:02:02
