helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3148664				0	en-ZA	Declare {Sub | Function} Name Lib "Libname" [Alias "Aliasname"] [Parameter] [As Type]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153360				0	en-ZA	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3154140				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Name:\</emph\> A different name than defined in the DLL, to call the subroutine from $[officename] Basic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870	9			0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Aliasname\</emph\>: Name of the subroutine as defined in the DLL.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Libname:\</emph\> File or system name of the DLL. This library is automatically loaded the first time the function is used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3148452				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Argumentlist:\</emph\> List of parameters representing arguments that are passed to the procedure when it is called. The type and number of parameters is dependent on the executed procedure.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3147289				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Type:\</emph\> Defines the data type of the value that is returned by a function procedure. You can exclude this parameter if a type-declaration character is entered after the name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3146922				0	en-ZA	To pass a parameter to a subroutine as a value instead of as a reference, the parameter must be indicated by the keyword \<emph\>ByVal\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
