helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090404.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618				0	en-ZA	Print "Number from 6 to 8"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090404.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	en-ZA	Case Is > 8 And iVar < 11				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090404.xhp	0	help	par_id3147436				0	en-ZA	Print "Greater than 8"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090404.xhp	0	help	par_id3155418				0	en-ZA	Case Else				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090404.xhp	0	help	par_id3150418				0	en-ZA	Print "Outside range 1 to 10"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090404.xhp	0	help	par_id3156285				0	en-ZA	End Select				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090404.xhp	0	help	par_id3149582				0	en-ZA	end sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Second Function [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153346				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>Second function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153346				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030204.xhp\" name=\"Second Function [Runtime]\"\>Second Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	par_id3156023				0	en-ZA	Returns an integer that represents the seconds of the serial time number that is generated by the TimeSerial or the TimeValue function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147264				0	en-ZA	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	par_id3146795				0	en-ZA	Second (Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	en-ZA	Return value:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	par_id3154140				0	en-ZA	Integer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156280				0	en-ZA	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Numeric expression that contains the serial time number that is used to calculate the number of seconds.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864	9			0	en-ZA	This function is the opposite of the \<emph\>TimeSerial \</emph\>function. It returns the seconds of a serial time value that is generated by the \<emph\>TimeSerial\</emph\> or \<emph\>TimeValue \</emph\>functions. For example, the expression:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	en-ZA	Print Second(TimeSerial(12,30,41))				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	par_id3151117				0	en-ZA	returns the value 41.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147426				0	en-ZA	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012				0	en-ZA	Sub ExampleSecond				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	en-ZA	MsgBox "The exact second of the current time is "& Second( Now )				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	par_id3151112				0	en-ZA	End sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Xor-Operator [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156024				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>Xor operator (logical)\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156024				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03060600.xhp\" name=\"Xor-Operator [Runtime]\"\>Xor-Operator [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	par_id3159414				0	en-ZA	Performs a logical Exclusive-Or combination of two expressions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153381				0	en-ZA	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400				0	en-ZA	Result = Expression1 Xor Expression2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153968				0	en-ZA	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150448				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Result:\</emph\> Any numeric variable that contains the result of the combination.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Expression1, Expression2:\</emph\> Any numeric expressions that you want to combine.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439				0	en-ZA	A logical Exclusive-Or conjunction of two Boolean expressions returns the value True only if both expressions are different from each other.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153770				0	en-ZA	A bitwise Exclusive-Or conjunction returns a bit if the corresponding bit is set in only one of the two expressions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153366				0	en-ZA	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	par_id3159154				0	en-ZA	Sub ExampleXor				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	en-ZA	Dim vA as Variant, vB as Variant, vC as Variant, vD as Variant				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155856				0	en-ZA	Dim vOut as Variant				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	par_id3152462				0	en-ZA	vA = 10: vB = 8: vC = 6: vD = Null				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	en-ZA	vOut = vA > vB Xor vB > vC REM returns 0				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153191				0	en-ZA	vOut = vB > vA Xor vB > vC REM returns -1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	en-ZA	vOut = vA > vB Xor vB > vD REM returns -1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	en-ZA	vOut = (vB > vD Xor vB > vA) REM returns 0				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	par_id3148455				0	en-ZA	vOut = vB Xor vA REM returns 2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	en-ZA	End Sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
