helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151262				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090300.xhp\" name=\"Jumps\"\>Jumps\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090300.xhp	0	help	par_id3148983				0	en-ZA	The following statements execute jumps.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Numeric Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153127				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03080000.xhp\" name=\"Numeric Functions\"\>Numeric Functions\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	en-ZA	The following numeric functions perform calculations. Mathematical and Boolean operators are described in a separate section. Functions differ from operators in that functions pass arguments and return a result, instead of operators that return a result by combining two numeric expressions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03070500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	"^" Operator [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03070500.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145315				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>"^" operator (mathematical)\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145315				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03070500.xhp\"\>"^" Operator [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	en-ZA	Raises a number to a power.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
