helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020201.xhp\"\>Get Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069				0	en-ZA	Reads a record from a relative file, or a sequence of bytes from a binary file, into a variable.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154346				0	en-ZA	See also: \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020204.xhp\" name=\"PUT\"\>\<item type=\"literal\"\>PUT\</item\>\</link\> Statement				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150358				0	en-ZA	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150792				0	en-ZA	Get [#] FileNumber As Integer, [Position], Variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154138				0	en-ZA	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150448				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>FileNumber:\</emph\> Any integer expression that determines the file number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Position:\</emph\> For files opened in Random mode, \<emph\>Position\</emph\> is the number of the record that you want to read.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	en-ZA	For files opened in Binary mode, \<emph\>Position\</emph\> is the byte position in the file where the reading starts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3147319				0	en-ZA	If \<emph\>Position\</emph\> is omitted, the current position or the current data record of the file is used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149484				0	en-ZA	Variable: Name of the variable to be read. With the exception of object variables, you can use any variable type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
