helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148550				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>Tan function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148550				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03080104.xhp\" name=\"Tan Function [Runtime]\"\>Tan Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3148663				0	en-ZA	Determines the tangent of an angle. The angle is specified in radians.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	en-ZA	Using the angle Alpha, the Tan Function calculates the ratio of the length of the side opposite the angle to the length of the side adjacent to the angle in a right-angled triangle.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	en-ZA	Tan(Alpha) = side opposite the angle/side adjacent to angle				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145174				0	en-ZA	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3151042				0	en-ZA	Tan (Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156214				0	en-ZA	Return value:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281				0	en-ZA	Double				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155132				0	en-ZA	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Any numeric expression that you want to calculate the tangent for (in radians).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	en-ZA	To convert degrees to radians, multiply by Pi/180. To convert radians to degrees, multiply by 180/Pi.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3155414				0	en-ZA	degrees=(radiant*180)/Pi				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	en-ZA	radiant=(degrees*Pi)/180				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	en-ZA	Pi is approximately 3.141593.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149483				0	en-ZA	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3148646				0	en-ZA	REM In this example, the following entry is possible for a right-angled triangle:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012				0	en-ZA	REM The side opposite the angle and the angle (in degrees) to calculate the length of the side adjacent to the angle:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3151115				0	en-ZA	Sub ExampleTangens				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158				0	en-ZA	REM Pi = 3.1415926 is a pre-defined variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3145800				0	en-ZA	Dim d1 as Double				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150417				0	en-ZA	Dim dAlpha as Double				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	en-ZA	d1 = InputBox$ ("Enter the length of the side opposite the angle: ","opposite")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149582				0	en-ZA	dAlpha = InputBox$ ("Enter the Alpha angle (in degrees): ","Alpha")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154016				0	en-ZA	Print "the length of the side adjacent the angle is"; (d1 / tan (dAlpha * Pi / 180))				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731				0	en-ZA	End Sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
