helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Numeric expression that defines the angle in radians that you want to calculate the sine for.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155413				0	en-ZA	To convert degrees to radians, multiply degrees by Pi/180, and to convert radians to degrees, multiply radians by 180/Pi.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	en-ZA	grad=(radiant*180)/pi				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143				0	en-ZA	radiant=(grad*pi)/180				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3151112				0	en-ZA	Pi is approximately 3.141593.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163712				0	en-ZA	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149482				0	en-ZA	REM In this example, the following entry is possible for a right-angled triangle:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148577				0	en-ZA	REM The side opposite the angle and the angle (in degrees) to calculate the length of the hypotenuse:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152941				0	en-ZA	Sub ExampleSine				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011				0	en-ZA	REM Pi = 3.1415926 is a predefined variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153159				0	en-ZA	Dim d1 as Double				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491				0	en-ZA	Dim dAlpha as Double				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251				0	en-ZA	d1 = InputBox$ ("Enter the length of the opposite side: ","Opposite Side")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456				0	en-ZA	dAlpha = InputBox$ ("Enter the angle Alpha (in degrees): ","Alpha")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153877				0	en-ZA	Print "The length of the hypotenuse is"; (d1 / sin (dAlpha * Pi / 180))				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150717				0	en-ZA	End Sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
