helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366	8			0	en-ZA	         \<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Numeric expression that contains the serial time value that is used to return the hour value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154909	9			0	en-ZA	This function is the opposite of the \<emph\>TimeSerial\</emph\> function. It returns an integer value that represents the hour from a time value that is generated by the \<emph\>TimeSerial\</emph\> or the \<emph\>TimeValue \</emph\>function. For example, the expression				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030201.xhp	0	help	par_id3163798				0	en-ZA	Print Hour(TimeSerial(12,30,41))				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030201.xhp	0	help	par_id3155132				0	en-ZA	returns the value 12.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147348				0	en-ZA	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
