helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149670				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030206.xhp\" name=\"TimeValue Function [Runtime]\"\>TimeValue Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361				0	en-ZA	Calculates a serial time value from the specified hour, minute, and second - parameters passed as strings - that represents the time in a single numeric value. This value can be used to calculate the difference between times.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154138				0	en-ZA	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3156282				0	en-ZA	TimeValue (Text As String)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153969				0	en-ZA	Return value:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	en-ZA	Date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145172				0	en-ZA	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Text:\</emph\> Any string expression that contains the time that you want to calculate in the format "HH:MM:SS".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578				0	en-ZA	Use the TimeValue function to convert any time into a single value, so that you can calculate time differences.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	en-ZA	This TimeValue function returns the type Variant with VarType 7 (Date), and stores this value internally as a double-precision number between 0 and 0.9999999999.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3151117				0	en-ZA	As opposed to the DateSerial or the DateValue function, where serial date values result in days relative to a fixed date, you can calculate with the values that are returned by the TimeValue function, but you cannot evaluate them.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426				0	en-ZA	In the TimeSerial function, you can pass individual parameters (hour, minute, second) as separate numeric expressions. For the TimeValue function, however, you can pass a string as a parameter containing the time.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
