helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156024				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03060300.xhp\" name=\"Imp-Operator [Runtime]\"\>Imp Operator [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3148947				0	en-ZA	Performs a logical implication on two expressions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148664				0	en-ZA	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	en-ZA	Result = Expression1 Imp Expression2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151212				0	en-ZA	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154910				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Result:\</emph\> Any numeric variable that contains the result of the implication.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Expression1, Expression2:\</emph\> Any expressions that you want to evaluate with the Imp operator.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150440				0	en-ZA	If you use the Imp operator in Boolean expressions, False is only returned if the first expression evaluates to True and the second expression to False.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	en-ZA	If you use the Imp operator in bit expressions, a bit is deleted from the result if the corresponding bit is set in the first expression and the corresponding bit is deleted in the second expression.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147318				0	en-ZA	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
