helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148887				0	en-ZA	Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154548				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Insert a name for the current control. This name is used to identify the control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148739				0	en-ZA	Order				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149252				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specify the order in which the controls receive the focus when the Tab key is pressed in the dialogue.\</ahelp\> On entering a dialogue, the control with the lowest order (0) receives the focus. Pressing the \<emph\>Tab\</emph\> key the successively focusses the other controls as specified by their order number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155259				0	en-ZA	Initially, the controls receive numbers in the order they are added to the dialogue. You can change the order numbers for controls. $[officename] Basic updates the order numbers automatically to avoid duplicate numbers. Controls that cannot be focused are also assigned a value but these controls are skipped when using the Tab key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149511				0	en-ZA	Orientation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
