helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\insert_control.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Creating Controls in the Dialogue Editor				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\insert_control.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149182				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>controls; creating in the dialogue editor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dialogue editor;creating controls\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\insert_control.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149182				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"insert_control\"\>\<link href=\"text/sbasic/guide/insert_control.xhp\" name=\"Creating Controls in the Dialog Editor\"\>Creating Controls in the Dialog Editor\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\insert_control.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797	2			0	en-ZA	Use the tools on the \<emph\>Toolbox \</emph\>of the BASIC dialogue editor to add controls to your dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\insert_control.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276				0	en-ZA	To open the \<emph\>Toolbox\</emph\>, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Insert Controls\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Macro\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\insert_control.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068				0	en-ZA	Click a tool on the toolbar, for example, \<emph\>Button\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\insert_control.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	en-ZA	On the dialogue, drag the button to the size you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Translation of Controls in the Dialog Editor				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	bm_id8915372				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>dialogues;translating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>localising dialogues\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>translating dialogues\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3574896				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"translation\"\>\<link href=\"text/sbasic/guide/translation.xhp\"\>Translation of Controls in the Dialog Editor\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id4601940				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The Language toolbar in the Basic IDE dialogue editor shows controls to enable and manage localisable dialogues.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id9538560				0	en-ZA	By default, any dialogue that you create only contains string resources for one language. You may want to create dialogues that automatically show localised strings according to the user's language settings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id6998809				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the language for the strings that you want to edit. Click the Manage Languages icon to add languages.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id71413				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click a language, then click Default to set the language as default, or click Delete to remove the language from the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id2924283				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialogue where you can add a language to the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id5781731				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a language in the list and click Delete to remove that language. When you remove all languages, the string resources for localisable dialogues are removed from all dialogues in the current library.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id6942045				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a language in the list and click Default to set the language as default language.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id4721823				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The default language will be used as a source for all other language strings.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id5806756				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Add UI languages for your dialogue strings.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	hd_id6596881				0	en-ZA	To enable localisable dialogues				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id8750572				0	en-ZA	In the Basic IDE dialogue editor, open the Language toolbar choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Toolbars - Language\</item\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id2224494				0	en-ZA	If the current library already contains a localisable dialogue, the Language toolbar is shown automatically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id7359233				0	en-ZA	Click the \<emph\>Manage Languages\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id2526017\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_managelanguage.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2526017\"\>Manage Language icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the Language toolbar or on the Toolbox bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id6549272				0	en-ZA	You see the Manage User Interface Language dialogue. The dialogue manages languages for the current library. The name of the current library is shown on the title bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id6529740				0	en-ZA	Click Add in the dialogue to add a language entry. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id7811822				0	en-ZA	This step enables all new dialogues to contain localisable string resources.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id9121982				0	en-ZA	The first time you click Add, you see the Set Default User Interface Language dialogue. The following times you click Add, this dialogue has the name Add User Interface Language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id3640247				0	en-ZA	You can also change the default language in the Manage User Interface Language dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id3808404				0	en-ZA	Select a language. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id4585100				0	en-ZA	This adds string resources to contain the translated versions of all strings to the dialogue properties. The set of dialogue strings of the default language is copied to the new set of strings. Later, you can switch to the new language and then translate the strings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id2394482				0	en-ZA	Close the dialogue or add additional languages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	hd_id631733				0	en-ZA	To edit localisable controls in your dialogue				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id2334665				0	en-ZA	Once you have added the resources for localisable strings in your dialogues, you can select the current language from the Current Language listbox on the Language toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id8956572				0	en-ZA	Switch the Current Language listbox to display the default language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id500808				0	en-ZA	Insert any number of controls to your dialogue and enter all strings you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id8366649				0	en-ZA	Select another language in the Current Language listbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id476393				0	en-ZA	Using the control's property dialogues, edit all strings to the other language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id2655720				0	en-ZA	Repeat for all languages that you added.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id3682058				0	en-ZA	The user of your dialogue will see the strings of the user interface language of the user's version of %PRODUCTNAME, if you did provide strings in that language. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id5977965				0	en-ZA	If no language matches the user's version, the user will see the default language strings. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id3050325				0	en-ZA	If the user has an older version of %PRODUCTNAME that does not know localisable string resources for Basic dialogues, the user will see the default language strings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
