helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147301				0	en-ZA	Automatic				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3147404				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_AXIS_LABEL:RB_AXIS_LABEL_AUTOORDER\"\>Automatically arranges numbers on the axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149353				0	en-ZA	Problems may arise in displaying labels if the size of your chart is too small. You can avoid this by either enlarging the view or decreasing the font size.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id1106200812235146				0	en-ZA	Text Direction				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id1106200812235271				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specify the text direction for a paragraph that uses complex text layout (CTL). This feature is only available if complex text layout support is enabled.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Chart Type XY				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	bm_id84231				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>scatter charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XY charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;XY (scatter)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error indicators in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error bars in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>averages in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>statistics in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variances in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>standard deviation in charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id9346598				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"type_xy\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_xy.xhp\"\>Chart Type XY (Scatter)\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id2003845				0	en-ZA	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id7757194				0	en-ZA	XY (Scatter)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5977965				0	en-ZA	An XY chart in its basic form is based on one data series consisting of a name, a list of x‑values, and a list of y‑values. Each value pair (x|y) is shown as a point in a coordinate system. The name of the data series is associated with the y‑values and shown in the legend.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4381847				0	en-ZA	Choose an XY chart for the following example tasks:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1336710				0	en-ZA	scale the x‑axis				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1221655				0	en-ZA	generate a parameter curve, for example a spiral				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id3397320				0	en-ZA	draw the graph of a function				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7657399				0	en-ZA	explore the statistical association of quantitative variables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id8925138				0	en-ZA	Your XY chart may have more than one data series.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id5461897				0	en-ZA	XY Chart Variants				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id8919339				0	en-ZA	You can choose an XY chart variant on the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\>, or by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Chart Type \</item\>for a chart in edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4634235				0	en-ZA	The chart is created with default settings. After the chart is finished, you can edit its properties to change the appearance. Line styles and icons can be changed on the \<emph\>Line\</emph\>tab page of the data series properties dialogue.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5482039				0	en-ZA	Double-click any data point to open the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data Series\</item\> dialogue. In this dialogue, you can change many properties of the data series.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id0805200810492449				0	en-ZA	For 2D charts, you can choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Y Error Bars\</item\> to enable the display of error bars.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id6221198				0	en-ZA	You can enable the display of mean value lines and trend lines using commands on the Insert menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id1393475				0	en-ZA	Points only				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id6571550				0	en-ZA	Each data point is shown by an icon. %PRODUCTNAME uses default icons with different forms and colours for each data series. The default colours are set in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Charts - Default Colours\</item\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id5376140				0	en-ZA	Lines Only				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4408093				0	en-ZA	This variant draws straight lines from one data point to the next. The data points are not shown by icons. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7261268				0	en-ZA	The drawing order is the same as the order in the data series. Mark \<emph\>Sort by X Values\</emph\> to draw the lines in the order of the x values. This sorting applies only to the chart, not to the data in the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id6949369				0	en-ZA	Points and Lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id9611499				0	en-ZA	This variant shows points and lines at the same time.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id6765953				0	en-ZA	3D Lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7422711				0	en-ZA	The lines are shown like tapes. The data points are not shown by icons. In the finished chart choose \<link href=\"text/schart/01/three_d_view.xhp\"\>3D View\</link\> to set properties like illumination and angle of view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id239265				0	en-ZA	Smooth Lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7957396				0	en-ZA	Mark \<emph\>Smooth Lines\</emph\> to draw curves instead of straight line segments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1202124				0	en-ZA	Click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> to set details for the curves.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5989562				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Cubic Spline\</emph\> interpolates your data points with polynomials of degree 3. The transitions between the polynomial pieces are smooth, having the same slope and curvature. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id6128421				0	en-ZA	The \<emph\>Resolution\</emph\> determines how many line segments are calculated to draw a piece of polynomial between two data points. You can see the intermediate points if you click any data point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id9280373				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>B-Spline\</emph\> uses the data points as control points to form a B-spline curve. Those curves are built piecewise from polynomials. The \<emph\>Data points order\</emph\> sets the degree k of these polynomials. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Axes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153768				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>axes;formatting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153768				0	en-ZA	Axes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"achsen\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DiagramAxisAll\"\>Opens a dialogue, where you can edit the properties of the selected axis.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> The name of the dialogue depends on the selected axis.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667				0	en-ZA	The \<link href=\"text/schart/01/05040200.xhp\" name=\"Y axis\"\>Y axis\</link\> has an enhanced dialogue. For X-Y charts, the X axis chart is also enhanced by the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/05040201.xhp\" name=\"Scaling\"\>\<emph\>Scaling\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159266				0	en-ZA	Scaling the X axis is only possible in the X-Y chart type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145230				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020100.xhp\" name=\"Character\"\>Character\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Data Series				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150449				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05010200.xhp\" name=\"Data Series\"\>Data Series\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	en-ZA	Use this to change the properties of a selected data series. This dialogue appears when one data series is selected when you choose \<emph\>Format - Format Selection\</emph\>. Some of the menu entries are only available for 2D or 3D charts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154015				0	en-ZA	Any changes made here affect the entire data series. For example, if you change the colour, all elements belonging to this data series will change colour.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146916				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Y Error Bars\"\>Y Error Bars\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Chart Wizard - Data Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	bm_id2429578				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>data ranges in charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	hd_id8313852				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"wiz_data_range\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_data_range.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard - Data Range\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id8829309				0	en-ZA	On this page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can select one single source of data range. This range may consist of more than one rectangular range of cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id6401867				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Data Ranges dialogue where you can edit Data Range and Data Series.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id2025818				0	en-ZA	Use the Chart Wizard - Data Series page if you need more control over the data ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id8466139				0	en-ZA	This dialogue is only available for charts based on a Calc or Writer table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	hd_id1877193				0	en-ZA	To specify a data range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5924863				0	en-ZA	Select the data range. Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id4357432				0	en-ZA	Enter the data range in the text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5626392				0	en-ZA	In Calc, an example data range would be "$Sheet1.$B$3:$B$14". Note that a data range may consist of more than one region in a spreadsheet, e.g. "$Sheet1.A1:A5;$Sheet1.D1:D5" is also a valid data range. In Writer, an example data range would be "Table1.A1:E4".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id1363872				0	en-ZA	In Calc, click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimise the dialogue, then drag over a cell area to select the data range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id6823938				0	en-ZA	If you want a data range of multiple cell areas that are not next to each other, enter the first range, then manually add a semicolon at the end of the text box, then enter the other ranges. Use a semicolon as delimiter between ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id1434369				0	en-ZA	Click one of the options for data series in rows or in columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id7524033				0	en-ZA	Check whether the data range has labels in the first row or in the first column or both.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5256508				0	en-ZA	In the preview you can see how the final chart will look.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id379650				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the data range that you want to include in your chart. To minimise this dialogue while you select the data range in Calc, click the \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> button.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id953703				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Data series get their data from consecutive rows in the selected range. For scatter charts, the first data series will contain x-values for all series. All other data series are used as y-values, one for each series.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id4496597				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Data series get their data from consecutive columns in the selected range. For scatter charts, the first data column will contain x-values for all series. All other data columns are used as y-values, one for each series.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id2898953				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>For data series in columns: The first row in the range is used as names for data series. For data series in rows: The first row in the range is used as categories. The remaining rows comprise the data series. If this check box is not selected, all rows are data series.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id7546311				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>For data series in columns: The first column in the range is used as names for data series. For data series in rows: The first column in the range is used as categories. The remaining columns comprise the data columns. If this check box is not selected, all columns are data columns.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Axis				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05040000.xhp\" name=\"Axis\"\>Axis\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150441				0	en-ZA	This opens a submenu to edit axial properties.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	en-ZA	The tabs in the dialogues depend on the chart type selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153729				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05040100.xhp\" name=\"X axis\"\>X axis\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147394				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05040200.xhp\" name=\"Y axis\"\>Y axis\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153160				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05040100.xhp\" name=\"Secondary X Axis\"\>Secondary X Axis\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149401				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DiagramAxisA\"\>Opens a dialogue where you can edit the properties of the secondary X axis. To insert a secondary X axis, choose \<emph\>Insert - Axes\</emph\> and select \<emph\>X axis\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145640				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05040200.xhp\" name=\"Secondary Y Axis\"\>Secondary Y Axis\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159264				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DiagramAxisB\"\>Opens a dialogue where you can edit the properties of the secondary Y axis. To insert a secondary Y axis, choose \<emph\>Insert - Axes\</emph\> and select \<emph\>Y axis\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145228				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05040100.xhp\" name=\"Z axis\"\>Z axis\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147345				0	en-ZA	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05040100.xhp\" name=\"All axes\"\>All axes\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Chart Area				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149670				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>charts; formatting areas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting; chart areas\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149670				0	en-ZA	Chart Area				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864	2			0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"diagrammflaeche\"\>\<ahelp visibility=\"visible\" hid=\".uno:DiagramArea\"\>Opens the\<emph\> Chart Area\</emph\> dialogue, where you can modify the properties of the chart area. The chart area is the background behind all elements of the chart.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Axes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147428				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>axes; showing axes in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts; showing axes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>X axes; showing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Y axes; showing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Z axes; showing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>axes; better scaling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>secondary axes in charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147428				0	en-ZA	Axes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150330				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"achsen\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertMenuAxes\"\>Specifies the axes to be displayed in the chart.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156385				0	en-ZA	Major axis				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146316				0	en-ZA	X axis				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145230				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_CHECKBOX_DLG_AXIS_CB_X_PRIMARY\"\>Displays the X axis as a line with subdivisions.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147003				0	en-ZA	Y axis				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_AXIS:CB_Y_PRIMARY\"\>Displays the Y axis as a line with subdivisions.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150345				0	en-ZA	Z axis				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155113				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_AXIS:CB_Z_PRIMARY\"\>Displays the Z axis as a line with subdivisions.\</ahelp\> This axis can only be displayed in 3D charts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150206				0	en-ZA	Secondary axis				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428				0	en-ZA	Use this area to assign a second axis to your chart. If a data series is already assigned to this axis, $[officename] automatically displays the axis and the label. You can turn off these settings later on. If no data has been assigned to this axis and you activate this area, the values of the primary Y axis are applied to the secondary axis.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152988				0	en-ZA	X axis				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156445				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_AXIS:CB_X_SECONDARY\"\>Displays a secondary X axis in the chart.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152896				0	en-ZA	Y axis				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_AXIS:CB_Y_SECONDARY\"\>Displays a secondary Y axis in the chart.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762	41			0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_AXIS:CB_Y_SECONDARY\"\>The major axis and the secondary axis can have different scaling. For example, you can scale one axis to 2 in. and the other to 1.5 in. \</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Chart Type Stock				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	bm_id2959990				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>stock charts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>chart types;stock\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>data sources;setting for stock charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id966216				0	en-ZA	\<variable id=\"type_stock\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_stock.xhp\"\>Chart Type Stock\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3516953				0	en-ZA	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id5268410				0	en-ZA	Stock				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id61342				0	en-ZA	A Stock chart illustrates the market trend given by opening price, bottom price, top price and closing price. The transaction volume can also be shown.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2131412				0	en-ZA	For a Stock chart the order of the data series is important. The data should be arranged as shown in the example table below.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
