swext	mediawiki\help\wikiaccount.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	MediaWiki				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiaccount.xhp	0	help	hd_id960722				0	en-ZA	MediaWiki				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiaccount.xhp	0	help	par_id4571672				0	en-ZA	Use the MediaWiki dialogue to add or edit your MediaWiki account settings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiaccount.xhp	0	help	par_id7631458				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the URL of a MediaWiki server, starting with http://\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiaccount.xhp	0	help	par_id7862483				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter your user name on the MediaWiki server. Leave empty for anonymous access.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiaccount.xhp	0	help	par_id1113010				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter your password on the MediaWiki server. Leave empty for anonymous access.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiaccount.xhp	0	help	par_id656758				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enable to store your password between sessions. The master password must be enabled, see \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME - Security\</item\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiaccount.xhp	0	help	par_id3112582				0	en-ZA	Enter the Internet address of a Wiki server in a format like http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki or copy the URL from a web browser.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiaccount.xhp	0	help	par_id628070				0	en-ZA	If the Wiki allows anonymous access, you can leave the account text boxes empty. Else enter your user name and password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiaccount.xhp	0	help	par_id9046601				0	en-ZA	If you have enabled the master password feature on the Security tab page of the Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME dialogue, then the software can store your password and automatically insert the data where necessary. Enable the "Save password" checkbox to store your password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	@WIKIEXTENSIONPRODUCTNAME@				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154408				0	en-ZA	\<bookmark_value\>Wiki;@WIKIEXTENSIONPRODUCTNAME@\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>@WIKIEXTENSIONPRODUCTNAME@\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>extensions;MediaWiki\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	hd_id5993530				0	en-ZA	@WIKIEXTENSIONPRODUCTNAME@				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id9647511				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>By using the @WIKIEXTENSIONPRODUCTNAME@ you can upload your current Writer text document to a MediaWiki server. After uploading, all Wiki users can read your document on the Wiki.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id6468703				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - To MediaWiki\</item\> to upload the current Writer document to a MediaWiki server.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	hd_id4554582				0	en-ZA	System Requirements				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id2597430				0	en-ZA	StarOffice/StarSuite 9				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id8430738				0	en-ZA	OpenOffice.org 3.0				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id9340495				0	en-ZA	Java Runtime Environment 1.4				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id7387615				0	en-ZA	A Wiki account on a supported \<link href=\"http://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/MediaWiki\"\>MediaWiki\</link\> server				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	hd_id8047120				0	en-ZA	Installing @WIKIEXTENSIONPRODUCTNAME@				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id4277169				0	en-ZA	Before you install the @WIKIEXTENSIONPRODUCTNAME@, ensure that %PRODUCTNAME uses a Java Runtime Environment (JRE). To check the status of the JRE, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME - Java\</item\>. Ensure that "Use a Java runtime environment" is marked and that a Java runtime folder is selected in the big listbox. If no JRE was activated, then activate a JRE 1.4 or later and restart %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	hd_id567339				0	en-ZA	To Install the @WIKIEXTENSIONPRODUCTNAME@				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id1732230				0	en-ZA	In a Writer window, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Extension Manager\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id4338511				0	en-ZA	In the Extension Manager dialogue, click Add.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id5882442				0	en-ZA	Locate the @WIKIEXTENSIONFILENAME@.oxt file, click Open, and then click Close. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id4008911				0	en-ZA	Close %PRODUCTNAME, and close also the Quickstarter if enabled.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id265511				0	en-ZA	Restart the software, open a text document, then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Options - Internet - MediaWiki\</item\> to enter your Wiki settings. See "To Connect To a Wiki" below.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	hd_id3569444				0	en-ZA	To Remove the @WIKIEXTENSIONPRODUCTNAME@				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id2655110				0	en-ZA	In a Writer window, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Extension Manager\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id9504379				0	en-ZA	Click the plus sign (+) in front of My Extensions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id8431348				0	en-ZA	Select the extension, click Remove, and then click Close.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	hd_id5316019				0	en-ZA	To Connect to a Wiki				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id2381969				0	en-ZA	Note: You can store your user name and password for all respective dialogues inside %PRODUCTNAME. The password will be stored in a secure way, where access is maintained by a master password. To enable the master password, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME - Security\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id3751640				0	en-ZA	Note: If you connect to the web using a proxy server, enter the proxy information to \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Options - Internet - Proxy\</item\>, and restart the software.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id9533677				0	en-ZA	Open a Writer document, and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Options - Internet - MediaWiki\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id368968				0	en-ZA	In the \<link href=\"@WIKIEXTENSIONID@/wikisettings.xhp\"\>Options\</link\> dialogue, click Add.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id6962187				0	en-ZA	In the \<link href=\"@WIKIEXTENSIONID@/wikiaccount.xhp\"\>MediaWiki\</link\> dialogue, enter the account information for the Wiki.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id5328836				0	en-ZA	In the URL textbox, enter the address of a Wiki that you want to connect to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id389416				0	en-ZA	You can copy the URL from a web browser and paste it into the textbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id5906552				0	en-ZA	In the Username box, enter your user ID for your Wiki account.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id9297158				0	en-ZA	If the Wiki allows anonymous write access, you can leave the Username and Password boxes empty.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id8869594				0	en-ZA	In the Password box, enter the password for your Wiki account, then click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id292062				0	en-ZA	Optionally enable "Save password" to save the password between sessions. A master password is used to maintain access to all saved passwords. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME - Security\</item\> to enable the master password. "Save password" is unavailable when the master password is not enabled.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	hd_id7044892				0	en-ZA	To Create a New Wiki Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id3514206				0	en-ZA	Open a Writer document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id944853				0	en-ZA	Write the content of the Wiki page. You can use formatting like text formats, headings, footnotes, and more. See the \<link href=\"@WIKIEXTENSIONID@/wikiformats.xhp\"\>list of supported formats\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id4566484				0	en-ZA	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - To MediaWiki\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id228278				0	en-ZA	In the \<link href=\"@WIKIEXTENSIONID@/wikisend.xhp\"\>Send to MediaWiki\</link\> dialogue, specify the settings for your entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id2564165				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>MediaWiki server\</emph\>: Select the Wiki.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id5566576				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Title\</emph\>: Type the title of your page. Type the title of an existing page to overwrite the page with your current text document. Type a new title to create a new page on the Wiki.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id9688711				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Summary\</emph\>: Enter an optional short summary of your page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id4123661				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>This is a minor edit\</emph\>: Check this box to mark the uploaded page as a minor edit of the already existing page with the same title.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id452284				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Show in web browser\</emph\>: Check this box to open your system web browser and show the uploaded Wiki page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wiki.xhp	0	help	par_id8346812				0	en-ZA	Click Send.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	MediaWiki Formats				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id3743095				0	en-ZA	MediaWiki Formats				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id8654133				0	en-ZA	The following list gives an overview of the text formats that the @WIKIEXTENSIONPRODUCTNAME@ can upload to the Wiki server.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id5630664				0	en-ZA	The OpenDocument format used by Writer and the WikiMedia format are quite different. Only a subset of all features can be transformed from one format to the other.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id7178868				0	en-ZA	Headings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id508133				0	en-ZA	Apply a heading paragraph style to the headings in your Writer document. The Wiki will show the heading styles of the same outline level, formatted as defined by the Wiki engine.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id7217627				0	en-ZA	Hyperlinks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id3735465				0	en-ZA	Native OpenDocument hyperlinks are transformed into "external" Wiki links. Therefore, the built-in linking facility of OpenDocument should only be used to create links that point to other sites outside the Wiki web. For creating Wiki links that point to other subjects of the same Wiki domain, use Wiki links.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id941190				0	en-ZA	Lists				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id8942838				0	en-ZA	Lists can reliably be exported when the whole list uses a consistent list style. Use the Numbering or Bullets icon to generate a list in Writer. If you need a list without numbering or bullets, use Format - Bullets and Numbering to define and apply the respective list style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id7026886				0	en-ZA	Paragraphs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id4436475				0	en-ZA	Alignment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id376598				0	en-ZA	Explicit text alignment should not be used in Wiki articles. Nevertheless, text alignment is supported for left, centred, and right alignment of text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id7486190				0	en-ZA	Pre-formatted text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id1459395				0	en-ZA	A paragraph style with a fixed-width font is transformed as pre-formatted text. Pre-formatted text is shown on the Wiki with a border around the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id4834131				0	en-ZA	Character styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id6397595				0	en-ZA	Character styles modify the appearance of parts of a paragraph. The transformation supports bold, italics, bold/italics, subscript and superscript. All fixed width fonts are transformed into the Wiki typewriter style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id5152745				0	en-ZA	Footnotes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id5238196				0	en-ZA	Note: The transformation uses the new style of footnotes with <ref> and <references> tags that requires the Cite.php extension to be installed into MediaWiki. If those tags occur as plain text in the transformation result, ask the Wiki administrator to install this extension.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id9405499				0	en-ZA	Images				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id3541673				0	en-ZA	Images cannot be exported by a transformation producing a single file of Wiki text. However, if the image is already uploaded to the target Wiki domain (e. g. WikiMedia Commons), then the transformation produces a valid image tag that includes the image. Image captions are also supported.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id2162236				0	en-ZA	Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id3037202				0	en-ZA	Simple tables are supported well. Table headers are translated into corresponding Wiki style table headers. However, custom formatting of table borders, column sizes and background colours is ignored.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id2954496				0	en-ZA	Joined Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id8253730				0	en-ZA	OpenDocument and especially OpenOffice.org represent tables that have joined cells that span rows as tables with nested tables. In contrast, the wiki model of table is to declare column and row spans for such joined cells. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id8163090				0	en-ZA	If only columns of the same row are joined, the result of the transformation resembles the source document very well.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id425122				0	en-ZA	Borders				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id1831110				0	en-ZA	Irrespective of custom table styles for border and background, a table is always exported as "\<emph\>prettytable"\</emph\>, which renders in the Wiki engine with simple borders and bold header.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id6255073				0	en-ZA	Charset and special characters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id8216193				0	en-ZA	The charset of the transformation result is fixed to UTF-8. Depending on your system, this might not be the default charset. This might cause "special characters" to look broken when viewed with default settings. However, you can switch your editor to UTF-8 encoding to fix this. If your editor does not support switching the encoding, you can display the result of the transformation in the Firefox browser and switch the encoding to UTF-8 there. Now, you can cut and paste the transformation result to your program of choice.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikisettings.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	MediaWiki Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikisettings.xhp	0	help	hd_id6425672				0	en-ZA	MediaWiki Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikisettings.xhp	0	help	par_id1188390				0	en-ZA	You can add, edit and remove MediaWiki servers. Open the dialogue by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Options - Internet - MediaWiki\</item\>. Alternatively, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Extension Manager\</item\>, select the @WIKIEXTENSIONPRODUCTNAME@, and click the Options button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikisettings.xhp	0	help	par_id300607				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click Add to add a new Wiki server.\<br/\>Select an entry and click Edit to edit the account settings.\<br/\>Select an entry and click Remove to remove the entry from the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikisettings.xhp	0	help	par_id9786065				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the MediaWiki dialogue to add a new entry to the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikisettings.xhp	0	help	par_id3386333				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the MediaWiki dialogue to edit the selected entry.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikisettings.xhp	0	help	par_id7285073				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Removes the selected entry from the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikisettings.xhp	0	help	par_id1029084				0	en-ZA	When you click Add or Edit, the \<link href=\"@WIKIEXTENSIONID@/wikiaccount.xhp\"\>MediaWiki\</link\> dialogue opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikisend.xhp	0	help	tit				0	en-ZA	Send to MediaWiki				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikisend.xhp	0	help	hd_id108340				0	en-ZA	Send to MediaWiki				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikisend.xhp	0	help	par_id1743827				0	en-ZA	In the Send to MediaWiki dialogue, specify the settings for your current Wiki upload.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikisend.xhp	0	help	par_id664082				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select the MediaWiki server where you want to publish your document. Click Add to add a new server to the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikisend.xhp	0	help	par_id2794885				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the title of your Wiki entry. This is the top heading of your Wiki entry. For a new entry, the title must be unique on this Wiki. If you enter an existing title, your upload will overwrite the existing Wiki entry.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikisend.xhp	0	help	par_id2486342				0	en-ZA	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter an optional short summary or comment.\</ahelp\> See \<link href=\"http://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Help:Edit_summary\"\>http://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Help:Edit_summary\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikisend.xhp	0	help	par_id823999				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>This is a minor edit\</emph\>: \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Check this box to mark the uploaded page as a minor edit of the already existing page with the same title.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
swext	mediawiki\help\wikisend.xhp	0	help	par_id6592913				0	en-ZA	\<emph\>Show in web browser\</emph\>: \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Check this box to open your system web browser and show the uploaded Wiki page.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
